INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (1,'jsearch','isUkFMozUOdgOqvXAAAAAA==','Solutions Engineer','Guardsman Group',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Solutions-Engineer-Job-227124.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Summary: The Solutions Engineer is responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining innovative software and system solutions that align with the company’s operational and business needs. The role collaborates with developers, IT professionals, and end-users to build, test, and deploy scalable applications, databases, and APIs while ensuring optimal system performance and reliability. Additionally, the Solutions Engineer supports existing deployments and recommends upgrades to enhance efficiency and productivity. Key Responsibilities: Collaborate with other developers to build end-to-end solutions Designing solutions for existing systems to meet the current and expanding business needs Designing, develop and testing programs and scripts to agreed specification Design and development of mobile solutions Design, deploy and maintain required databases Design and construction of REST APIs Maintain and upgrade technical systems or offer recommendations on upgrades Coordinate maintenance with other IT professionals and users Test and demonstrate new software and technology to increase productivity Provide support for all existing deployments Perform any other related duties as assigned Experience and Qualifications: BSc in Computer Science Proficiency with fundamental front-end languages such as HTML, CSS, jQuery, XML and JavaScript. Proficiency with server-side languages such as JAVA, ASP.Net and ASP.NET CORE. Proficiency with mobile languages such as FLUTTER. Familiarity with database technology such as Microsoft SQL and MySQL. Special Conditions: The incumbent may be required to travel out of town and stay overnight to support operational or project related activities. The role also requires flexibility to work on weekends, public holidays, and outside of normal working hours, as well as availability to respond to emergencies or urgent technical issues. Application Deadline: Friday, February 27, 2026 We appreciate all applications of interest, however, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'solutions engineer,solutions,upgrades,deployments,existing deployments,end,designing,languages,professionals,asp,asp net,business needs,existing,productivity,users,mobile,net,proficiency,operational,needs,test,deploy,engineer,technology,databases'),(2,'jsearch','Pdjep9LlG8xcJwovAAAAAA==','Software Engineer, Full-Stack','Grammarly',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/software-engineer-full-stack-at-grammarly-4311805148?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','SUPERHUMAN MAIL ?\n\nAt Superhuman, we’ve built the fastest email experience in the world — one that\'s deeply loved and adored by customers who get through their inboxes twice as fast.\n\n? Superhuman Mail, Grammarly, and Coda are now part of the Superhuman Suite, an AI productivity platform on a mission to unlock the superhuman potential in everyone. The Superhuman suite of apps and agents brings AI wherever people work, integrating with over 1 million applications and websites. Learn more at superhuman.com and about our values here.\n\nBUILD LOVE ?\n\nAt Superhuman, we have a deep understanding of how to build products that people love. We incorporate fun and play, infusing magic and joy to create experiences that amaze and delight. It all starts with the right team — a team that deeply cares about values, customers, and each other.\n\nCREATE MASSIVE IMPACT ?\n\nWe\'re not solving a small problem, nor are we addressing a small market. We\'re reshaping the fundamentals of how people work. We\'re combining premium product craft with enterprise-scale capabilities to rethink how individuals and teams should fundamentally collaborate. We are building a household brand and a worldwide organization. We are here to do our best work, and we hope you are too.\n\nROLE ?????\n• Develop new products and features, improve existing offerings\n• Become an expert in web app development\n• Expand development experience across the stack and to other platforms\n• Contribute to the product development process: thinking through UX, designing beautiful UI, and working with customers to solve their problems\n• Help estimate, plan, and complete projects, features, and integrations\n• Champion code quality, new technologies, and architectural design within the company\n• Technologies we use: React, Typescript, Golang, Postgres, Electron, Google Cloud\n\nSOUND LIKE YOU? ?\n• Experience: 5+ years of professional full-stack web development experience, working from the database to the UI.\n• Expertise: You have a deep understanding of browser JavaScript (including the DOM and platform APIs).\n• AI Enthusiast: You believe AI will revolutionize how we work as well as the experiences that we create for our customers. Driven by passion and curiosity, you leverage AI to dramatically increase your own productivity and the impact of your team.\n• Remarkable Quality: You produce work that is striking, worthy of attention, and a contribution to the state of the art.\n• Asynchronous Communicator: You’re effective across various mediums (especially Slack, Notion, and email) and can produce and consume detailed written materials as needed without sacrificing speed. You respond quickly and thoughtfully to unblock others and speed things up.\n• Start-to-Finish Ownership: Acts with 100% responsibility for their own outcomes as well as the outcomes of the company.\n• Bias to action: Speed matters. Takes rapid and decisive steps forward, even in the face of uncertainty, recognizing action is the catalyst for progress and growth.\n• Growth Mindset: You embrace challenges, welcome feedback, and believe you and others can always grow.\n\nSALARY INFO ?\n\nSuperhuman takes a market-based approach to compensation, which means base pay may vary depending on your location.\n\nBase pay may vary considerably depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The expected salary ranges for this position are outlined below and may be modified in the future.\n• SF/NY/Seattle: $180,000-$306,000\n• Other US geographies: $162,000-$275,000\n• Canada: $128,000-$246,000 CAD\n• Mexico: $1,928,000-$2,762,000 MXN\n• Brazil: R$562,000-R$806,000 BRL\n• Argentina: $103,000-$147,000 USD\n\nCOME JOIN US ?️\n\nWe value our differences, and we encourage all to apply — especially those whose identities are traditionally underrepresented in tech organizations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, ancestry, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, political belief, or any other characteristic protected by law. Superhuman is an equal opportunity employer and a participant in the US federal E-Verify program (US). We also abide by the Employment Equity Act (Canada).',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'000,superhuman,customers,ai,status,people,create,stack,speed,love,action,mail,deeply,pay vary,pay,suite,email,base pay,canada,superhuman suite,people work,depending,superhuman mail,produce,vary'),(3,'jsearch','q1BJCNW1TuH2UrhJAAAAAA==','Public Cloud Software Engineer','Lloyds Banking Group',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/public-cloud-software-engineer-at-lloyds-banking-group-4371896092?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Description\n\nPublic Cloud Senior Software Engineer\n\nSalary: £70,929.00 - £78,810 Location: Manchester, Edinburgh, Bristol, Halifax & Leeds Hours: Full-time Working Pattern: Hybrid - spend at least two days per week (or 40% of your time) at the location above.\n\nCloud Platform DevOps Engineer GCP\n\nJob Description:\n\nAt Lloyds Banking Group, we\'re all driven by our purpose, to Help Britain Prosper. It\'s why we exist - it\'s our reason to get out of bed in the morning. The choices we make, our success and our future really matter.\n\nBut the world is changing, fast. And we\'re changing too. It\'s never been a more exciting time to join us as we transform our business to shape finance as a force for good.\n\nOur team\n\nThe Cloud Platform team is on the journey to create the next generation cloud platform for Lloyds Banking Group that will be at the core of one of the UK\'s biggest financial service transformations. We\'re looking for a Cloud Platform DevOps Engineer to join our Native Cloud team within the Cloud Platform.\n\nThis role provides an outstanding chance to be part of an ambitious team focused on driving technology modernisation. It supports Lloyds Banking Group\'s goal to become the biggest Fintech in the UK.\n\nWe\'re seeking an experienced, motivated and innovative hands-on Cloud focussed Devops Engineer. The ideal candidate will have confirmed experience in a DevOps or Site Reliability Engineer role. You\'ll be a technical inspiring senior engineer and experienced at driving the delivery of new technical platforms.\n\nWhat\'s needed to be considered for this job?\n\n· Expert Engineering experience building, configuring, and optimizing GCP based networking at enterprise scale. Specific networking knowledge (including Dedicated Interconnect, VPC network peering, Cloud Routers, Firewalls, Google DNS, Cloud NAT, IAM and VPC SC), basic knowledge of connected workloads (GKE, Compute Engine, Cloud SQL, Storage buckets, Google Data AI products, etc.) and corresponding ancillary function such as Identity.\n\n· Hands on participation in projects heavily involving GCP networking including sustaining engineering, network deployment/implementation, network scaling, technology refresh and network optimization in both non-production and production environments.\n\n· Significant experience of DevOps concepts and CI/CD pipelines using cloud native and third-party tooling - Git, Terraform Cloud, HashiCorp Vault, Harness, Jenkins\n\n· Manage Incidents and Problems to resolve (and advance) enterprise networking connectivity issues to improve the stability of the platform.\n\n· Review and feedback on code changes for your fellow team members.\n\n· Develop, deploy and own the lifecycle of products and solutions developed within the team.\n\n· Perform all engineering tasks in compliance with the Control and Security requirements\n\nAbout you\n\n· Proficient, validated experience maintaining enterprise scale GCP cloud networking and cross cloud / on-premises connectivity.\n\n· Proven track record working closely with other Networks, Systems, and Software Engineering teams to ensure fast, smooth roll-out of new designs and products, as well as assisting with deployment and maintenance of networking tools.\n\n· Infrastructure development experience in Bash and/or Python.\n\n· Proficient in Terraform\n\n· Engineer the lifecycle of Google Cloud Platform networking products in Infrastructure as Code to enable new products and features\n\n· Able to collaborate with other teams including architecture, business and other engineering teams to create solution and deliver product team artifacts and dependencies\n\n· Continuous curiosity to learn and develop themselves with the latest industry methods and tooling.\n\nWe\'ll be excited if you have\n\n· Bachelor\'s degree in computer programming / computer science / a related field or equivalent experience in cloud engineering / infrastructure engineering\n\n· Certified Google Cloud Platform Professional Cloud Engineer (one of the Professional Cloud DevOps, Network or Security Engineer qualifications)\n\n· Advanced Python development with experience of hosting APIs\n\n· Experience of authoring guardrails / policy in Hashicorp Sentinel\n\n· Awareness of Egress Proxies, IP Management, On premises networking, hardware firewall appliances, Infoblox, cloud proxy, Entra ID\n\n· Experience with high-traffic monitoring systems. Implementing logging telemetry with Dynatrace and Google Cloud Monitoring.\n\n· Effective verbal, written, interpersonal communication.\n\n· Comfortable with ambiguity, changing requirements and changing priorities.\n\n· Creative mindset always coming up with ideas and solutions.\n\nAbout working for us\n\nOur focus is to ensure we\'re inclusive every day, building an organisation that reflects modern society and celebrates diversity in all its forms.\n\nWe want our people to feel that they belong and can be their best, regardless of background, identity, or culture.\n\nIf you\'d like reasonable adjustments to be made to the recruitment process, please let us know.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'cloud,networking,cloud platform,engineer,platform,network,changing,engineering,gcp,banking group,devops engineer,lloyds banking,lloyds,experience,products,team,devops,google,banking,group,infrastructure,team cloud,tooling,experience devops,platform devops'),(4,'jsearch','Z3xkwB3STS3MU_VwAAAAAA==','Internal Software Support Engineer','TheHiveCareers',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/internal-software-support-engineer-at-thehivecareers-4371520056?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Internal Software Support Engineer\n\nLocation: Remote (Carribean)\n\nEmployment Type: Full-time Contract\n\nReports to: Chief Technology Officer\n\nRole Overview\n\nWe are seeking a technically strong, service-oriented Internal Software Support Engineer who will act as the first line of support for internal software systems and websites. This role combines IT and software support, hands-on website development, and solution design, including recommending and implementing software and CRM platforms to improve business processes and internal efficiency.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nInternal Software & Technical Support\n• Provide Level 1–2 technical support for internal software tools, platforms, and web applications\n• Troubleshoot system, website, and application issues; identify root causes and implement fixes\n• Monitor system performance and escalate complex issues when required\n• Install, configure, and maintain internal software, tools, and user access\n• Log, track, and resolve incidents using ticketing systems while meeting defined SLAs\n• Document issues, solutions, and support processes to build internal knowledge bases\n\nWebsite & Application Support\n• Support, maintain, and update company websites and internal web platforms\n• Fix bugs, improve performance, and ensure website functionality and uptime\n• Implement content and feature updates using CMS platforms\n• Collaborate with product, design, and engineering teams on enhancements and new features\n• Ensure websites are secure, responsive, and optimized for performance\n\nSolution Design & Business Process Optimization\n• Analyze existing business processes and daily workflows to identify inefficiencies and technology gaps\n• Creating solutions and recommending software/CRM platforms to optimize business processes and day to day functions\n• Design and recommend technical solutions to improve productivity, automation, and system reliability\n• Research, evaluate, and recommend software tools, SaaS products, and CRM platforms to support business needs\n• Support or lead the implementation, configuration, and optimization of selected tools and platforms\n• Act as a technical advisor to internal teams by translating business requirements into effective system solutions\n• Ensure recommended solutions are scalable, cost-effective, and aligned with company goals\n• Document system configurations, integrations, and best practices for long-term maintainability\n\nCollaboration & Process Improvement\n• Work closely with internal teams to understand system needs and resolve issues efficiently\n• Assist with system testing, deployments, upgrades, and integrations\n• Recommend improvements to tools, workflows, and system architecture\n• Support a culture of continuous improvement and operational excellence\n\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\n• 2–4+ years of experience in technical support, software support, or IT support roles\n• Hands-on experience with website development and maintenance\n• Working knowledge of HTML, CSS, JavaScript (basic to intermediate)\n• Experience with CMS platforms (WordPress, Webflow, or similar)\n• Familiarity with basic backend concepts (APIs, databases, hosting environments)\n• Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills\n• Ability to communicate technical concepts clearly to non-technical users\n\nPreferred / Nice-to-Have\n• Experience with React, PHP, or Node.js\n• Understanding of cloud hosting, DNS, and server environments\n• Exposure to ticketing systems (Jira, Zendesk, Freshdesk, etc.)\n• Experience evaluating or implementing CRM platforms (HubSpot, Salesforce, Zoho, or similar)\n• Knowledge of workflow automation and system integrations\n• Basic knowledge of cybersecurity best practices\n• Experience working in a fast-paced startup or scale-up environment\n\nWhat We Offer\n• Opportunity to work in a growing, impact-driven company\n• Remote working environment\n• Exposure to both support engineering and development work\n• Collaborative and supportive team culture\n• Career growth and learning opportunities',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'support,internal,internal software,website,software support,software,crm platforms,crm,platforms,software tools,technical support,support engineer,business processes,technical,business,issues,basic,websites,tools,integrations,processes,engineer,recommend,experience,solutions'),(5,'jsearch','gJNcvoY-dczKmYr3AAAAAA==','Full Stack Java Developer','HGS',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/full-stack-java-developer-at-hgs-4370443754?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','We are seeking a skilled and motivated Full Stack Java Developer to join our team. The successful candidate will be responsible for end-to-end application development, collaborating closely with cross-functional teams to deliver secure, scalable, and high-quality solutions.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and maintain backend services using Java, Spring Boot, Hibernate, RESTful APIs, and Microservices architecture.\n• Develop and maintain front-end components using JavaScript, CSS, React or Angular.\n• Participate in end-to-end application development, from database design (MySQL) to UI integration.\n• Implement secure authentication and authorization using JWT, OAuth2, and Spring Security.\n• Optimize API performance through caching, pagination, and asynchronous processing.\n• Collaborate with front-end teams to define API contracts and data models for seamless integration.\n• Write and maintain unit, integration, and API tests using JUnit, Mockito, and Postman.\n• Participate in code reviews, refactoring, and design discussions to ensure high code quality and maintainability.\n• Implement and maintain CI/CD pipelines using Jenkins and/or GitHub Actions.\n• Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve production issues using logging and monitoring tools such as Kibana.\n• Contribute to architecture improvements, performance tuning, and modernization initiatives.\n• Work within Agile/Scrum teams, participating in sprint planning, daily stand-ups, reviews, and retrospectives.\n• Collaborate closely with Product Owners and QA teams to ensure timely and high-quality delivery.\n\nQualifications & Experience\n• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• 3–5+ years of hands-on experience in Full Stack Java development (or equivalent).\n• Strong experience with Java, Spring Boot, Hibernate, and Microservices.\n• Proven experience with front-end frameworks such as React or Angular.\n• Experience working with relational databases, preferably MySQL.\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Experience working in Agile development environments.\n\nTechnical Skills\n• Backend: Java, Spring Boot, Hibernate, REST APIs, Microservices\n• Frontend: JavaScript, CSS, React or Angular\n• Security: JWT, OAuth2, Spring Security\n• Database: MySQL\n• Testing: JUnit, Mockito, Postman\n• DevOps/Tools: Jenkins, GitHub Actions, Git, Kibana\n• Methodologies: Agile / Scrum\n\nSoft Skills\n• Strong problem-solving and analytical skills\n• Excellent communication and collaboration abilities\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a team\n• Strong attention to detail and commitment to quality\n• Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'spring,end,java,stack java,java spring,boot hibernate,hibernate,using,spring boot,boot,microservices,stack,junit mockito,oauth2 spring,postman,github,jwt oauth2,javascript css,css react,spring security,mockito,end application,mockito postman,jwt,actions'),(6,'jsearch','4Steyu_NkP_ZHICNAAAAAA==','Software Engineer, Frontend (Latin America)','Grammarly',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/69932a0dda7696de2f53c31c-software-engineer-frontend-latin-america?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nIMPORTANT EMPLOYMENT NOTE ⚠️\n\nWe are only considering candidates based in Latin America. This position will be employed by Deel, our Employer of Record partner, and will support Superhuman\'s product development. Deel is the legal employer and will manage all employment matters, payroll, benefits, and day-to-day supervision in accordance with local labor laws.\n\nSUPERHUMAN MAIL ?\n\nAt Superhuman, we’ve built the fastest email experience in the world — one that\'s deeply loved and adored by customers who get through their inboxes twice as fast.\n\n? Superhuman Mail, Grammarly, and Coda are now part of the Superhuman Suite, an AI productivity platform on a mission to unlock the superhuman potential in everyone. The Superhuman suite of apps and agents brings AI wherever people work, integrating with over 1 million applications and websites. Learn more at superhuman.com and about our values here.\n\nBUILD LOVE ?\n\nAt Superhuman, we have a deep understanding of how to build products that people love. We incorporate fun and play, infusing magic and joy to create experiences that amaze and delight.\n\nIt all starts with the right team — a team that deeply cares about values, customers, and each other.\n\nCREATE MASSIVE IMPACT ?\n\nWe\'re not solving a small problem, nor are we addressing a small market. We\'re reshaping the fundamentals of how people work. We\'re combining premium product craft with enterprise-scale capabilities to rethink how individuals and teams should fundamentally collaborate. We are building a household brand and a worldwide organization. We are here to do our best work, and we hope you are too.\n\nROLE ??‍??‍?\n• Design, build, and maintain our desktop application while keeping resource usage (CPU, memory, threads) minimal and predictable\n• Monitor, profile, and analyze runtime performance (rendering, memory leaks, blocking operations) and implement optimizations to avoid regressions\n• Advocate and evolve the frontend architecture (modularity, dependency boundaries, layering, decoupling) to ensure scalability as features grow\n• Define, enforce, and evangelize best practices in code quality (linting, style guides, code reviews, static analysis, automated checks)\n• Develop robust error-handling, crash-reporting, fallback mechanisms, and recovery paths for critical failures inside the UI\n• Work cross-functionally with backend, QA, and infrastructure teams to define interfaces, API contracts, versioning, and compatibility across releases\n• Instrument and maintain tooling (metrics, logging, telemetry) to gain visibility into app health, user flows, and regressions\n• Mentor other frontend engineers on performance, reliability, and architecture decisions; drive continuous improvements in the app’s frontend codebase\n• Technologies you will be using: React, Typescript, Electron, Google Cloud\n• Other technologies we have in our stack: Golang, Postgres, Swift, Kotlin\n\nSOUND LIKE YOU? ?\n• Experience: 8+ years of professional Frontend web development experience, working from the database to the UI.\n• Expertise: You have a deep understanding of browser JavaScript (including the DOM and platform APIs).\n• AI Enthusiast: You believe AI will revolutionize how we work as well as the experiences that we create for our customers. Driven by passion and curiosity, you leverage AI to dramatically increase your own productivity and the impact of your team.\n• Remarkable Quality: You produce work that is striking, worthy of attention, and a contribution to the state of the art.\n• Asynchronous Communicator: You’re effective across various mediums (especially Slack, Notion, and email) and can produce and consume detailed written materials as needed without sacrificing speed. You respond quickly and thoughtfully to unblock others and speed things up.\n• Start-to-Finish Ownership: Acts with 100% responsibility for their own outcomes as well as the outcomes of the project.\n• Bias to action: Speed matters. Takes rapid and decisive steps forward, even in the face of uncertainty, recognizing action is the catalyst for progress and growth.\n• Growth Mindset: You embrace challenges, welcome feedback, and believe you and others can always grow.\n• Location: This role is open to candidates based in Latin America and will be employed by Deel, our Employer of Record partner.\n\nSALARY INFO ?\n\nCompensation offered by Deel may vary considerably depending on job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and location. The expected salary ranges for this position are outlined below and may be modified in the future. All compensation, benefits, and employment terms will be administered by Deel in accordance with local laws and market practices.\n• Argentina: $124,000 - $147,000 USD\n• Mexico: $2,322,000 - $2,762,000 MXN\n• Brazil: R$677,000 - R$806,000 BRL\n\nCOME COLLABORATE WITH US ?️\n\nWe value our differences, and we encourage all to apply — especially those whose identities are traditionally underrepresented in tech organizations. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, gender expression or identity, sexual orientation, ancestry, national origin, citizenship, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, political belief, or any other characteristic protected by law.\n\nThis offer from \"Grammarly\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 78% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'superhuman,000,deel,ai,frontend,create,work,latin,america,latin america,employment,people,customers,status,employer,employed deel,memory,superhuman suite,local,employed,deep understanding,accordance,outcomes,accordance local,superhuman mail'),(7,'jsearch','V0yHtemgaK52RQ_bAAAAAA==','Full Stack Software Engineer','Newsela',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobs.reachcapital.com/companies/newsela/jobs/68009943-full-stack-software-engineer?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About the Role:\n\nWe are seeking a creative and technically-minded Full Stack Software Engineer (Junior to Mid-Level) to help us build the future of student data analytics. In this role, you won\'t just be moving data—you\'ll be designing how educators interact with it. You will work across our entire stack, from building Python-based APIs to crafting beautiful, responsive frontends. A strong eye for design is essential here; we need someone who cares about user experience and knows how to make complex data look clean, intuitive, and actionable.\n\nWhat You\'ll Be Doing:\n• End-to-End Feature Development: Build and ship new features using Python (Flask) on the backend and React on the frontend.\n• Data Visualization: Create engaging, interactive charts and dashboards using Chart.js and other modern visualization libraries.\n• UI/UX Implementation: Translate product ideas into polished user interfaces, ensuring a high-quality look and feel across the platform.\n• Semantic Layer: Work with Cube (formerly Cube.js) to manage our semantic data layer (we’ll train you on this if you haven\'t used it!).\n• Database Integration: Interface with Postgres (Spanner) and BigQuery to ensure our application has fast, reliable access to student data.\n• Growth & Learning: Actively participate in code reviews and collaborate with senior engineers to level up your technical skills and architectural thinking.\n\nAbout You:\n• 2-4 years of professional experience in full-stack web development.\n• Frontend Proficiency: Strong experience with React and a deep understanding of modern CSS/styling.\n• Design Sensibility: A \"strong eye for design\" and a passion for creating clean, user-friendly interfaces. You should be comfortable making UI decisions that improve the user experience.\n• Backend Fundamentals: Solid experience with Python and web frameworks (like Flask or FastAPI).\n• Data Viz Interest: Experience with Chart.js, D3.js, or similar visualization libraries to tell stories with data.\n• SQL Skills: Comfortable writing and optimizing queries for relational databases (Postgres) or data warehouses (BigQuery).\n• Adaptability: Excited to learn new technologies like Cube and dive into the nuances of K-12 educational data.\n\nWhy you’ll love working at Newsela:\n• Work From Home: We are a fully remote company. We provide a monthly tech stipend to support your WFH needs!\n• Time Off: Flexible PTO plus 10 company holidays plus winter break (Dec 24th - Jan 1st).\n• Make A Difference: No matter your role or department, the work you do each day helps share the future of education and improves the lives of students and teachers.\nAbout Newsela:\n\nNewsela takes authentic, real world content from trusted sources and makes it instruction ready for K-12 classrooms. Each text is published at five reading levels, so content is accessible to every learner. Today, over 3.3 million teachers and 40 million students have registered with Newsela for content that\'s personalized to student interests, accessible to everyone, aligned to instructional standards, and attached to activities and reporting that hold teachers accountable for instruction and students accountable for their work. With over 15,000 texts on our platform and multiple new texts published every day across 20+ genres, Newsela enables educators to go deep on any subject they choose.\n\n#LI-Remote',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'data,newsela,visualization,teachers,cube,students,student,content,ll,js,stack,python,user,experience,chart,strong eye,student data,chart js,eye design,data ll,texts,semantic,educators,flask,accountable'),(8,'jsearch','FLQ24qiarqXi9jNOAAAAAA==','Staff Full Stack Software Engineer (Node.js / Go / React)','Growth Acceleration Partners',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/698b08e192425699427a8ba4-staff-full-stack-software-engineer-node.js-go-react?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nWHAT WE DO\n\nFounded in 2007, Growth Acceleration Partners (GAP) is a consulting and technology services company. We consult, design, build and modernize revenue-generating software and data engineering solutions for clients. With modernization services and AI tools, we help businesses achieve a competitive advantage through technology. GAP’s remote, integrated engineering teams use end-to-end solutions to innovate and align with your business goals. We have 600+ English-speaking engineers based in Latin America and approximately 20 U.S.-based engineers. With some of the highest customer satisfaction scores in the industry, GAP’s focus is customer and employee success.\n\nGAP is a woman-owned company headquartered in Austin Texas. We are a values-based company focused on growing our people by investing in education, onsite English classes and training in the latest technologies, including AI, data analytics and machine learning. Our goal is to provide solutions for our customers that help them achieve critical business outcomes, while enabling our GAPSters and our communities to attain long-term success.\n\nSummary\n\nWe are looking for a Senior Full Stack Software Engineer with strong experience across modern frontend and backend technologies to design, build, and scale robust, user-centric applications. In this role, you will work closely with product managers, designers, and engineering teams to ideate solutions, define architecture, and deliver high-quality software across web and mobile platforms.\n\nThis position is ideal for a senior-level engineer or technical lead who enjoys owning end-to-end solutions—from system design and APIs to responsive UI and deployment—while contributing to technical decisions, mentoring others, and ensuring best practices around performance, security, and scalability.\n\nEducation\n\nBachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n• 8–12 years of professional experience in software development.\n\n• Proven experience as a Full Stack Developer or Senior Software Engineer.\n\n• Strong background working with modern frontend frameworks and backend services.\n\n• Experience contributing to or leading technical design decisions.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Collaborate with development teams and product managers to ideate and design software solutions.\n\n• Design and implement client-side and server-side architectures.\n\n• Build visually appealing, responsive, and high-performance frontend applications.\n\n• Develop and maintain robust APIs and backend services.\n\n• Ensure applications are responsive, efficient, and scalable through testing and optimization.\n\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and enhance existing software solutions.\n\n• Implement security and data protection best practices.\n\n• Build features with mobile-responsive design in mind.\n\n• Produce clear and concise technical documentation.\n\n• Partner with data scientists and analysts to enhance application capabilities and insights.\n\nRequired Skills\n\nBackend Development\n\n• 5+ years of experience with backend technologies such as Node.js and Golang.\n\n• Strong experience designing and building RESTful APIs.\n\n• Familiarity with backend performance tuning and scalability considerations.\n\nFrontend Development\n\n• 5+ years of experience with React.js.\n\n• Solid knowledge of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\n\n• Experience building responsive and user-friendly interfaces.\n\n• Familiarity with UI/UX principles and collaboration with design teams.\n\nContainers & Platforms\n\n• 2+ years of experience working with Kubernetes.\n\n• Experience developing applications that run in containerized environments.\n\nData & Systems\n\n• Experience working with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL.\n\n• Understanding of data flows, persistence, and integration patterns.\n\nNice to Have\n\n• Experience developing desktop and mobile applications.\n\n• Exposure to cloud platforms such as AWS or Azure.\n\n• Working knowledge of networking concepts.\n\n• Experience supporting or contributing to distributed systems.\n\nSoft Skills\n\n• Excellent communication and collaboration skills.\n\n• Strong organizational abilities and time management.\n\n• Analytical mindset with a structured approach to problem-solving.\n\n• Comfortable working in cross-functional, fast-paced environments.\n\n• Ability to contribute as both an individual contributor and a technical guide.\n\nAt Growth Acceleration Partners, we\'re an equal opportunity employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We value everyone\'s unique background, and we provide equal opportunities regardless of race, color, creed, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, national origin, disability, marital status, veteran status or any other personal right protected by law. We foster a culture of belonging and strive to provide a welcoming environment where everyone feels safe to contribute and grow.\nThis offer from \"Growth Acceleration Partners\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 83% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'experience,solutions,software,responsive,design,data,backend,gap,applications,technical,frontend,engineering,engineer,end,build,strong,services,senior,acceleration partners,acceleration,provide,contributing,js,growth acceleration,years experience'),(9,'jsearch','LA9ky2nrksoc-rMiAAAAAA==','Mid-level Software Engineer','GoFasti',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6999c1d0da7696de2f5a7f7c-mid-level-software-engineer?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nWe Make Remote Work Remarkable • TopTalent from LatAm\n\nHello! We are GoFasti, a Talent-as-a-Service. GoFasti bridges the gap between world-class developers and designers from LatAm and first-class companies around the globe.\n\nWe need an English-fluent Mid-level Software Engineer, based in Latin America, available to work remotely.\n\nWe are looking for someone with exceptional communication and relationship-building skills, who embraces changes while maintaining strong attention to detail. An interested and proactive person, who\'s constantly learning and improving their skills.\n\nYou’ll help evolve a legacy web-based SaaS product while contributing to a next-generation platform using modern tools and infrastructure. The ideal candidate is comfortable navigating legacy codebases and building clean, scalable systems from scratch.\n\nAre you the one we are looking for?\n\nResponsibilities:\n• Contribute to both the legacy PHP/LAMP platform and the modern microservice-based platform.\n• Stabilize, refactor, and incrementally enhance older codebases with clear documentation.\n• Develop new backend and frontend functionality using NestJS and NextJS.\n• Participate in AWS migration efforts and support infrastructure modernization.\n• Collaborate with product managers, designers, and engineers across feature prioritization, implementation, and QA.\n\nTech Stack:\n• Legacy: PHP 7, MySQL 5.7, LAMP stack, Vue, React\n• Modern: NestJS (Node.js backend), NextJS (React frontend), PostgreSQL\n• Infrastructure: AWS (SQS/SNS, ECS, Fargate), cloud-native and event-driven architecture\n\nRequirements:\n• 4+ years of experience in software engineering, including PHP/LAMP and/or Node.js stacks.\n• Proficiency with relational databases (MySQL or PostgreSQL).\n• Experience maintaining and modernizing legacy systems in production environments.\n• Familiarity with cloud-native development and microservices.\n• Strong English communication skills and comfort working asynchronously.\n\nIt\'s a Plus:\n• Experience with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, CloudFormation).\n• Familiarity with event-driven and service-oriented systems.\n• Previous work with nonprofit or mission-driven platforms.\n\nCompensation:\n• The Salary range offered for this position varies from (USD) $2,000 - $3,000 per month, depending on seniority and skillset.\n• This position is for an independent contractor, through a payroll platform.\n• The talent will work REMOTELY allocated at our client.\n\nHere are the steps for this process:\n\nApplication review/approval > Screening interview with GoFasti\'s team > We build and send your profile to our client > Profile review/approval by client > Interview with the client > Live coding > Hiring and onboarding.\n\nOnce you apply for the job, our team will review your resume. If it meets the requirements, we will contact you and move forward in the process.\n\nNote for Candidates Approached Directly:\nIf you were contacted directly by a member of our team and are interested in this opportunity, please do not apply through this link. Instead, reach out to the person who contacted you to coordinate a meeting.\n\nThank you!\n\nThis offer from \"GoFasti\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,24000.00,36000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','legacy,gofasti,lamp,client,review,php,infrastructure,platform,review approval,approval,latam,legacy php,codebases,event,event driven,level software,php lamp,driven,profile,class,mid,service,cloud native,remotely,work remotely'),(10,'jsearch','aUi1nX24qjr51gbcAAAAAA==','Senior Full-Stack Engineer (React/Node/AWS) - Software','True Logic Solutions',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6984b8339242569942757ae7-senior-full-stack-engineer-react-node-aws---software?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nAbout Truelogic\n\nAt Truelogic, we are a leading provider of nearshore staff augmentation services headquartered in New York. For over two decades, we’ve been delivering top-tier technology solutions to companies of all sizes, from innovative startups to industry leaders, helping them achieve their digital transformation goals.\n\nOur team of 600+ highly skilled tech professionals, based in Latin America, drives digital disruption by partnering with U.S. companies on their most impactful projects. Whether collaborating with Fortune 500 giants or scaling startups, we deliver results that make a difference.\n\nBy applying for this position, you’re taking the first step in joining a dynamic team that values your expertise and aspirations. We aim to align your skills with opportunities that foster exceptional career growth and success while contributing to transformative projects that shape the future.\n\nOur Client\n\nOur client is a digital-first technology company that supports political initiatives, advocacy groups, consultants, and organizations of all sizes. They provide a powerful, scalable text messaging platform that enables teams to communicate directly with constituents, supporters, and voters in a fast, personalized, and highly effective way. Their solution is designed to help campaigns and movements launch quickly, stay agile, and drive real engagement through one of the most impactful communication channels in modern politics: SMS.\n\nJob Summary\n\nWe are seeking a Senior Full-Stack Developer with expertise in developing modern, scalable web applications. This role is ideal for a true “builder” who enjoys working hands-on across the entire stack—delivering high-quality features from polished React interfaces to efficient Node.js services running on AWS Lambda.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Lead end-to-end feature development, from interactive React UIs to scalable Node.js business logic.\n• Design, develop, and deploy optimized AWS Lambda functions with a focus on performance and cost.\n• Write, optimize, and maintain complex PostgreSQL queries and schema migrations\n• Build and maintain secure, well-documented RESTful APIs.\n• Ensure high code quality through peer reviews, unit tests, and integration tests.\n• Debug and resolve complex issues across the full stack.\n• Collaborate with Product Managers and stakeholders to refine requirements and provide effort estimates.\n• Identify and resolve performance bottlenecks in frontend and backend systems.\n\nQualifications and Job Requirements\n• 5+ years of experience with React.js, including hooks, state management, and responsive UI design.\n• Strong proficiency in Node.js in a Serverless/AWS Lambda environment.\n• Advanced PostgreSQL skills, including schema design and query optimization.\n• Advanced verbal and written English for collaboration with North American teams.\n• Familiarity with Infrastructure as Code and AWS environments (Terraform, CDK).\n• Experience mentoring developers or leading technical discovery.\n• Experience or strong interest in TypeScript.\n• Hands-on experience with: React, Node.js APIs, Serverless / AWS Lambda, PostgreSQL.\n• Exposure to: Infrastructure as Code, TypeScript, Terraform / CDK.\n\nWhat We Offer\n• 100% Remote Work: Enjoy the freedom to work from the location that helps you thrive. All it takes is a laptop and a reliable internet connection.\n• Highly Competitive USD Pay: Earn an excellent, market-leading compensation in USD, that goes beyond typical market offerings.\n• Paid Time Off: We value your well-being. Our paid time off policies ensure you have the chance to unwind and recharge when needed.\n• Work with Autonomy: Enjoy the freedom to manage your time as long as the work gets done. Focus on results, not the clock.\n• Work with Top American Companies: Grow your expertise working on innovative, high-impact projects with Industry-Leading U.S. Companies.\n\nWhy You’ll Like Working Here\n• A Culture That Values You: We prioritize well-being and work-life balance, offering engagement activities and fostering dynamic teams to ensure you thrive both personally and professionally.\n• Diverse, Global Network: Connect with over 600 professionals in 25+ countries, expand your network, and collaborate with a multicultural team from Latin America.\n• Team Up with Skilled Professionals: Join forces with senior talent. All of our team members are seasoned experts, ensuring you\'re working with the best in your field.\n\nApply now!\nThis offer from \"True Logic Solutions\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'lambda,aws lambda,companies,leading,aws,work,js,node,professionals,senior,working,react,team,node js,stack,america,offer,latin america,latin,expertise,highly,experience react,terraform,startups,infrastructure code'),(11,'jsearch','24ejDWWrP5QR2zLEAAAAAA==','Java Software Engineer, AI Imaging (Backend)','Latino Legends','Mandeville','JM',0,'https://talent.latinolegends.com/jobs/7221470-java-software-engineer-ai-imaging-backend','Java Software Engineer, AI Imaging (Backend)\n\nAbout the Company\n\nOur client is a retail AI platform powering real-world, repeatable success for dozens of enterprise retailers. More than 100 million shoppers each month engage with their AI-driven outfitting, product discovery, and personalization experiences across e-commerce, apps, email, and stores. What sets them apart isn’t just what their AI can generate but the 10+ years of retail data, workflows, tools, experts, and QA systems behind it. These are the mission-critical components required to deliver safe, brand-right, production-ready AI at scale. Retailers trust them to elevate customer experience, drive revenue, and bring proven AI use cases to life.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nOur client is growing a new product line leveraging AI Image generation with all the power of the existing outfitting knowledge. This role is a foundational part of a rapidly growing area with the opportunity to establish the foundations of workflows and delivery of AI content at scale.\n\nWhat You Will Do\n• Write production-level code in Java (with AI tools)\n• Prompt engineering and testing with LLMs, including Claude, Gemini, and OpenAI models\n• Context engineering to determine the right data\n• Agentic workflow design\n• Help us build systems to easily monitor and test LLM performance\n• Design and implement solutions for scale and maintainability across multiple clients\n• Contribute as a thought leader to conversations around LLM usage\n\nMust-Have Qualifications\n• 5+ years of coding experience in Java. Proficient in SQL and relational DB technologies\n• 2+ years in systems with a user interface, prefer javascript driven like React\n• 1+ years of Spring Boot\n• Demonstrated production use of AI in API calls or code assistance\n• Understanding of Cloud Computing and distributed architecture with real experience deploying containerized applications.\n• Confident communication (written and oral) skills and a demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with all levels of internal and external organizations.\n• Strong problem-solving, attention to detail, organizational, and time management skills along with demonstrated strategic thinking abilities.\n\nNice-to-Have Qualifications\n• Experience at a high-growth start-up and comfortable with the unknown.\n• Fashion or imaging process expertise\n• Experience with Clojure\n\nOur Values\n\nOur values reflect what is important to us and serve as the foundation in which we do business. Each core value is best illustrated by actions and attitudes that each team member practices. They define what working with us means and what our teams embody through their time here.\n• We care deeply about delivering high-quality work\n• We work to be the best partners possible\n• We get things done\n• We believe the right team matters most\n• We think like customers and act like owners\n• We relish being pioneers\n\nDetails:\n• CST hours\n• Full time vacancy\n• USD $5000-$6000/month\n• Long Term Contractor Role\n\nHiring Process\n\nOur streamlined hiring process is designed to move quickly while giving you a fair opportunity to showcase your skills:\n• Email Screening Form – Short questionnaire to confirm experience and role alignment.\n• 15–20 Min Live Coding Challenge – Quick technical exercise focused on problem-solving and fundamentals.\n• Cultural Fit Interview – Conversation about your experience, communication style, and team alignment.\n• Final Technical Live Coding – Deeper practical exercise simulating real-world scenarios.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'java,ai,imaging,coding,experience,right,skills demonstrated,outfitting,java software,live coding,client,imaging backend,engineer ai,ai imaging,like,retail,retailers,software engineer,demonstrated,production,llm,problem solving,backend,alignment,solving'),(12,'jsearch','cSsg1rOVn1sVe7U8AAAAAA==','Full Stack Software Engineer','Newsela',NULL,NULL,0,'https://himalayas.app/companies/newsela/jobs/full-stack-software-engineer','About the Role:\n\nWe are seeking a creative and technically-minded Full Stack Software Engineer (Junior to Mid-Level) to help us build the future of student data analytics. In this role, you won\'t just be moving data—you\'ll be designing how educators interact with it. You will work across our entire stack, from building Python-based APIs to crafting beautiful, responsive frontends. A strong eye for design is essential here; we need someone who cares about user experience and knows how to make complex data look clean, intuitive, and actionable.\nWhat You\'ll Be Doing:\n• End-to-End Feature Development: Build and ship new features using Python (Flask) on the backend and React on the frontend.\n• Data Visualization: Create engaging, interactive charts and dashboards using Chart.js and other modern visualization libraries.\n• UI/UX Implementation: Translate product ideas into polished user interfaces, ensuring a high-quality look and feel across the platform.\n• Semantic Layer: Work with Cube (formerly Cube.js) to manage our semantic data layer (we’ll train you on this if you haven\'t used it!).\n• Database Integration: Interface with Postgres (Spanner) and BigQuery to ensure our application has fast, reliable access to student data.\n• Growth & Learning: Actively participate in code reviews and collaborate with senior engineers to level up your technical skills and architectural thinking.\nAbout You:\n• 2-4 years of professional experience in full-stack web development.\n• Frontend Proficiency: Strong experience with React and a deep understanding of modern CSS/styling.\n• Design Sensibility: A \"strong eye for design\" and a passion for creating clean, user-friendly interfaces. You should be comfortable making UI decisions that improve the user experience.\n• Backend Fundamentals: Solid experience with Python and web frameworks (like Flask or FastAPI).\n• Data Viz Interest: Experience with Chart.js, D3.js, or similar visualization libraries to tell stories with data.\n• SQL Skills: Comfortable writing and optimizing queries for relational databases (Postgres) or data warehouses (BigQuery).\n• Adaptability: Excited to learn new technologies like Cube and dive into the nuances of K-12 educational data.\nWhy you’ll love working at Newsela:\n• Work From Home: We are a fully remote company. We provide a monthly tech stipend to support your WFH needs!\n• Time Off: Flexible PTO plus 10 company holidays plus winter break (Dec 24th - Jan 1st).\n• Make A Difference: No matter your role or department, the work you do each day helps share the future of education and improves the lives of students and teachers.\nAbout Newsela:\n\nNewsela takes authentic, real world content from trusted sources and makes it instruction ready for K-12 classrooms. Each text is published at five reading levels, so content is accessible to every learner. Today, over 3.3 million teachers and 40 million students have registered with Newsela for content that\'s personalized to student interests, accessible to everyone, aligned to instructional standards, and attached to activities and reporting that hold teachers accountable for instruction and students accountable for their work. With over 15,000 texts on our platform and multiple new texts published every day across 20+ genres, Newsela enables educators to go deep on any subject they choose.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'data,newsela,visualization,teachers,student,content,students,cube,ll,js,user,python,flask,visualization libraries,semantic,student data,strong eye,eye design,educators,instruction,data ll,chart js,chart,published,texts'),(13,'jsearch','7Elwni3-Tq-IDXtzAAAAAA==','IT Support Engineer – Software Maintenance, Remote','Career.zycto',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/it-support-engineer-software-maintenance-remote/','About Company\n\nAre you a proactive IT professional passionate about ensuring seamless software operations? Career.zycto offers a dynamic and supportive environment where your expertise in software maintenance is highly valued. We are a forward-thinking organization dedicated to innovation and leveraging technology to solve complex challenges. Join a collaborative team committed to excellence and continuous improvement, making a tangible impact on our technological infrastructure. At Career.zycto, an IT Support Engineer finds ample opportunities for professional growth and skill development, contributing directly to our mission of operational efficiency and user satisfaction.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is actively seeking a highly skilled and dedicated Remote IT Support Engineer specializing in Software Maintenance to join our growing team. This is an exciting opportunity for a motivated professional to play a pivotal role in ensuring the optimal performance and reliability of our critical software applications, directly contributing to our operational efficiency from anywhere within Buff Bay, Portland Parish, Jamaica. As a Remote IT Support Engineer, you will be the frontline expert, responsible for diagnosing and resolving complex software issues, implementing preventive measures, and contributing to the overall stability and health of our technological ecosystem.\n\nYour day-to-day will involve a dynamic mix of reactive problem-solving and proactive system enhancement. You\'ll be tasked with meticulously analyzing error logs, tracking recurring issues, and collaborating seamlessly with our development and quality assurance teams to identify root causes and implement sustainable solutions. This includes deploying fixes, patches, and updates, ensuring minimal disruption to business operations. We’re looking for someone who thrives in a remote environment, possesses exceptional communication skills to articulate technical information clearly to both technical and non-technical audiences, and is adept at managing multiple priorities independently while maintaining a high level of accuracy and efficiency.\n\nThis role requires a keen eye for detail, a methodical and structured approach to troubleshooting, and an unwavering commitment to delivering exceptional user support. You\'ll work closely with internal stakeholders across various departments, providing clear, concise technical explanations and actionable advice. Furthermore, you will be instrumental in maintaining comprehensive documentation of solutions, common issues, and procedural guides, enhancing our collective knowledge base. We expect you to contribute actively to improving our support processes and tools, constantly seeking ways to optimize our service delivery.\n\nThis position is ideal for an individual passionate about continuous learning and staying abreast of the latest software technologies, industry best practices, and security protocols. You will have opportunities to engage in projects aimed at scaling our IT infrastructure and implementing new software solutions. If you are a natural problem-solver, possess a strong background in software support and maintenance, and desire to make a significant impact in a remote-first culture, we strongly encourage you to apply. Join Career.zycto and become an integral part of a team that values innovation, efficiency, and the professional growth of its members, all while enjoying the flexibility and autonomy of remote work.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Provide advanced remote technical support for software applications, diagnosing and resolving complex issues.\n• Monitor system performance and application health, proactively identifying potential problems.\n• Analyze error logs, trace application issues, and collaborate with development teams for root cause analysis and resolution.\n• Implement and deploy software patches, updates, and configuration changes.\n• Develop and maintain comprehensive technical documentation, including knowledge base articles and troubleshooting guides.\n• Respond to user inquiries and support requests, ensuring timely and effective resolution.\n• Participate in testing new software releases and updates to ensure stability and functionality.\n• Contribute to the improvement of IT support processes and tools.\n• Escalate unresolved issues to appropriate internal teams when necessary.\n• Provide clear, concise communication to stakeholders regarding issue status and resolution.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in diagnosing and troubleshooting software application issues.\n• Strong understanding of operating systems (Windows, Linux) and network fundamentals.\n• Experience with ticketing systems and IT service management (ITSM) best practices.\n• Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills.\n• Exceptional verbal and written communication abilities.\n• Ability to work independently and manage time effectively in a remote setting.\n• Familiarity with database concepts (SQL) and querying for data analysis.\n• Knowledge of scripting languages (e.g., PowerShell, Python) for automation.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n• Certifications such as ITIL, CompTIA A+, Network+, or Security+.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP).\n• Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git).\n• Previous experience in a remote IT support role.\n• Experience with monitoring tools like Nagios, Zabbix, or Splunk.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits.\n• Flexible remote work environment.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Access to a collaborative and supportive team culture.\n• Equipment allowance for home office setup.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to apply by clicking on the application link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your experience in software maintenance and remote IT support. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'support,remote,software,software maintenance,remote support,career zycto,zycto,issues,support engineer,maintenance,diagnosing,resolution,efficiency,professional,career,updates,troubleshooting,health,technical,comprehensive,exceptional,continuous,ensuring,resolving,diagnosing resolving'),(14,'jsearch','eCHq9zsoqmpQizjMAAAAAA==','Engineer II, Software Quality','FUJIFILM Holdings America Corporation',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6995db76da7696de2f563e0b-engineer-ii-software-quality','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: South America, North America, United States, Central America\n\nPosition Overview:\n\nThis position is intended to focus on software functional testing and quality assurance, and the fulfillment of relevant procedure and documentation per Fujifilm Medical Informatics Design Control process for software development.\n\nCompany Overview:\n\nAt FUJIFILM Healthcare Americas Corporation, we’re on a mission to innovate for a healthier world, and we need passionate, driven people like you to help us get there. Our cutting-edge healthcare solutions span diagnostic imaging, enterprise imaging, endoscopic and surgical imaging, as well as in-vitro diagnostics.\n\nBut we don’t stop at healthcare; our Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) team harnesses advanced radiography solutions to keep transportation infrastructure, aerospace, and oil and gas assets safe and running smoothly.\n\nReady to innovate, collaborate, and make a difference? Join us and bring your big ideas to life while working in a dynamic, flexible environment that fuels your creativity and drive.\n\nOur headquarters is in Lexington, Massachusetts, an inspiring healthcare research hub in a historic town.\n\nFujifilm is globally headquartered in Tokyo with over 70,000 employees across four key business segments of healthcare, electronics, business innovation, and imaging. We are guided and united by our Group Purpose of “giving our world more smiles.” Visit: https://www.fujifilm.com/us/en/about/region/careers\n\nJob Description:\n\nDuties and responsibilities\n• Have advanced knowledge about the Synapse Select product line, including deployment methods and deployment architecture for both on-premise and cloud configurations\n• Create, maintain, and execute manual Software test cases for Verification and Validation protocols for the Synapse Select product line\n• Occasional exploratory functional testing and ticketing of any issues found\n• Reproduce and document any product defects and/or reported bugs in the JIRA development ticketing system.\n• Execute individual development ticket and regression testing with clear documentation of test results.\n• Correspond with Software and Template Engineering, give feedback to any questions they may have, and facilitate the provision of more information if needed\n• Work with contractor QA team(s) on the grooming of development tickets and answer any questions they may have\n• Participate in calls with the automated testing team for reviewing implementation of new test cases and give feedback for improvement of the protocol\n• Create, Design Forms as required by the Medical Informatics Design Control Process for Synapse Select products as needed.\n• Occasionally help to address Corrective and Preventive actions (CAPA) assigned to Synapse Select as needed and complete in a timely manner.\n• Help to develop, document, and occasionally conduct internal technical trainings regarding new development for the Synapse Select product line.\n• Assist the Medical Informatics documentation team in the creation and maintenance of service manuals and product documentation for Synapse Select.\n• Assist Operations and Support with technical questions related to the Synapse Select product line. This may include attending customer meetings and additional items as necessary.\n• Additional responsibilities as defined by management.\n• Comply with all applicable U.S. Food and Drug Administration (U.S. FDA) medical device regulatory requirements, applicable ISO 13485 standard requirements and all other applicable laws, regulations, and standards.\n\nQualifications\n\nEducational requirements:\n• Bachelor\'s Degree (B.S./B.A.) or equivalent work experience in a scientific or technical discipline.\n\nExperience:\n• Minimum two (2) years of experience in Software Development, Software QA or other related fields.\n• Knowledge of software medical devices, procedures, and terminology, including the DICOM standard and HL7.\n• Knowledge of AGILE Software development and software design controls.\n• Knowledge of complaint handling and corrective and preventive action processes.\n• Knowledge of quality system regulations.\n• Experience with Microsoft® Word, Excel, Visio, and Access or equivalent software.\n• Experience with JIRA and Confluence\n• Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills\n\nSpecial skills or other job requirements:\n• Detailed oriented.\n• Problem solving\n• Ability to multi-task.\n• Highly organized.\n• Project management skills.\n• Excellent verbal, written, and communication skills.\n\nPhysical requirements\n\nThe position requires the ability to perform the following physical demands and/or have the listed capabilities:\n• Usual office working conditions.\n• Frequently required to sit, talk, or hear.\n• Good manual dexterity.\n• Ability to sit for extended periods.\n• Occasionally lift and/or move up to 10 pounds.\n\nTravel\n• Occasional (up to 10%) travel may be required based on business needs.\n• #LI-Remote\n\nIn the event that COVID-19 vaccine mandates issued by the federal government, or by state or local government become effective and enforceable, the Company will require that the successful candidate hired for positions covered under relevant government vaccine mandate(s) be fully vaccinated against COVID-19, absent being granted an accommodation due to medical or sincerely held religious belief or other legally required exemption.\nApplicants to positions where vendor credentialing or other similar requirements exist to enter facilities will be required to comply with the credentialing requirements of the facilities, including complying with vaccine requirements.\nFor all positions, the Company encourages vaccination against COVID-19 and requires that the successful candidate hired be willing to test for the COVID-19 virus periodically and wear a face covering indoors as required, absent being granted an accommodation due to medical or sincerely held religious belief or other legally required exemption.\n\nEEO Information:\n\nFujifilm is committed to providing equal opportunities in hiring, promotion and advancement, compensation, benefits, and training regardless of nationality, age, gender, sexual orientation or gender identity, race, ethnicity, religion, political creed, ideology, national, or social origin, disability, veteran status, etc.\n\nADA Information:\n\nIf you require reasonable accommodation in completing this application, interviewing, completing any pre-employment testing, or otherwise participating in the employee selection process, please direct your inquiries to our HR Department (hcushr.department@fujifilm.com or (330) 425-1313).\n\nThis offer from \"FUJIFILM Holdings America Corporation\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 80% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'select,synapse,fujifilm,synapse select,medical,healthcare,requirements,select product,covid 19,covid,19,required,product line,imaging,software,line,test,vaccine,medical informatics,accommodation,informatics,government,occasionally,applicable,testing'),(15,'jsearch','bWnmJ46V6MTgFqquAAAAAA==','Senior Software Engineer, Developer Experience','Coinme',NULL,NULL,0,'https://himalayas.app/companies/coinme/jobs/senior-software-engineer-developer-experience','At Coinme, we’re redefining access to financial services in a digital world. By combining the cutting-edge power of blockchain technology with everyday simplicity, we make digital currencies accessible and usable for all.\n\nAs the world\'s largest network of cryptocurrency kiosks with over 40,000 locations nationwide, we\'re breaking down barriers to crypto adoption through our seamless mobile app, secure digital wallet, and DeFi integrations. Beyond our consumer offerings, we\'re also the infrastructure powering the crypto revolution for businesses.\n\nThrough our enterprise Crypto-as-a-Service (CaaS) platform, we enable businesses to launch crypto capabilities in weeks, not months. Our modular, API-first infrastructure provides everything from KYC and payment processing to liquidity and custody solutions—all fully licensed and compliant.\n\nWe’re big enough to lead the charge in decentralized finance but small enough that your ideas will make waves. Every role at Coinme contributes to building a financial future where everyone has the tools to thrive. At Coinme, your growth fuels our mission. Together, we RISE.\n\nRole Overview\n\nAs a Senior Fullstack Engineer on the Developer Experience team, you\'ll architect and build the tools that power Coinme\'s ecosystem—from internal platforms that enable our teams to move faster, to partner portals that extend our financial technology to external stakeholders. You\'ll work with cutting-edge technologies including React, TypeScript, and Node.js to create a comprehensive suite of reusable components, modular feature flows, and scalable applications that make complex financial operations seamless. This role blends technical leadership with hands-on development in a fast-paced environment where your architectural decisions will shape how we build and scale our products across web and native platforms.\n\nWe move fast but thoughtfully. You\'ll have autonomy to contribute to and make technical decisions while collaborating with a team that values clean code, reusable patterns, and user-centric design. We\'re building for scale from day one, so your architectural choices matter.\nKey Responsibilities (What You\'ll Be Working On)\n• Frontend Development: Build high-performance React applications with TypeScript, Redux (RTK), and styled-components while ensuring a seamless user experience\n• Backend Development: Work with Node.js/NestJS to develop and optimize API services\n• Reusable component libraries with advanced theming capabilities using CSS-in-JS, styled-components, and ThemeProvider\n• Modular feature flows that can be orchestrated into complete app experiences\n• Internationalized experiences supporting multiple markets and languages\n• Collaboration: Work closely with Product and Design teams to translate business needs into technical solutions\n• Scalability & Performance: Design and deliver scalable, resilient, and secure web applications\n• CI/CD & Testing: Help create and maintain an efficient CI/CD pipeline, incorporating unit testing and static analysis tools (Jest, Testing Library, Storybook)\n• Monitoring & Analytics: Implement instrumentation and logging for performance tracking and data-driven improvements\n• Security & Compliance: Build secure solutions in compliance with industry best practices and regulatory requirements\nQualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or equivalent experience\n• 6+ years of hands-on experience in web development, including:\n• Strong JavaScript & TypeScript fundamentals—we\'re a TS-first team\n• 5+ years with React experience\n• 5+ years React (functional components, hooks, Redux/RTK) expertise\n• Proficiency in HTML/CSS and component-based UI development\n• Experience with styled-components, ThemeProvider, and design systems\n• CSS-in-JS experience for component styling and theming\n• Familiarity with micro-frontend architectures\n• Backend experience with Node.js/Express and API development\n• Strong understanding of web architecture, functional programming, and performance optimization\n• Self-starter who can take ownership of features from concept to deployment\n• Enjoys wearing multiple hats and tackling diverse technical challenges\n• Experience in fast-paced environments where shipping quickly matters\n• Comfortable working with CI/CD pipelines and deployment processes\nNice to Have\n• React Native Experience\n• Experience with component library architecture and design systems\n• Background in fintech or complex data-driven applications\n• Experience with consumer-facing web applications\n• Knowledge of accessibility best practices (WCAG, ARIA)\n• i18n/localization implementation experience (i18next)\n• Experience creating and publishing NPM packages\n• Understanding of state machine concepts for modeling complex application flows\n• Familiarity with cryptocurrency, blockchain technologies, or highly regulated industries\n\nCheck out our AI Usage Guidelines to understand how we approach AI tools during the hiring process.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'experience,component,crypto,coinme,components,financial,styled components,styled,reusable,modular,js,flows,tools,web,react,ll,seamless,css,api,design systems,data driven,cryptocurrency,components themeprovider,compliance,blockchain'),(16,'jsearch','FdmQny4m_RUpjOpUAAAAAA==','Career Opportunities: Senior AI Solutions Engineer - (Open to remote) (285779)','Arvato',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/699578b0da7696de2f559ac4-career-opportunities-senior-ai-solutions-engineer---open-to-remote-285779','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America, United States\n\nThe Data Science team at Penguin Random House is seeking a Senior AI Solutions Engineer to provide technical leadership and architectural direction for AI-powered marketing and discovery platforms.\n\nAt the senior level, this role goes beyond delivering individual solutions. You will define technical roadmaps, design durable multi-team systems, and ensure AI applications scale reliably across products and workflows. You will partner closely with senior stakeholders to translate business goals into long-term technical strategy, while remaining hands-on enough to guide critical implementations and unblock teams.\n\nThis role sits at the intersection of strategy, architecture, and execution, with responsibility for systems that support multiple teams and products over extended time horizons.\n\nThis role may be filled at the Senior or Staff level depending on experience and interview performance.\n\nWhile hybrid NYC is strongly preferred, we will consider remote (US) candidates with the right skills/experience/interest.\n\nSpecific responsibilities include:\n• Propose, design, and deliver AI systems and architectures aligned with long-term marketing and discovery roadmaps.\n• Define and evolve reusable LLM-based application patterns (e.g., RAG architectures, evaluation strategies, retrieval systems) that can be shared across teams.\n• Ensure AI solutions are robust, observable, and adaptable as business needs and AI capabilities evolve.\n• Lead development of end-to-end software systems spanning APIs, automation pipelines, internal tools, front-end applications, and cloud infrastructure.\n• Establish engineering standards and shared platforms that enable teams to safely and effectively leverage AI capabilities.\n• Ensure AI systems are reliable, observable, and cost-effective in production, and resolve cross-team operational issues as they arise.\n• Define technical roadmaps aligned with business priorities and guide teams on model selection, system design, and technical trade-offs.\n• Partner with Product, Marketing, and senior leaders to assess feasibility, align on strategy, and communicate progress.\n• Increase organizational efficiency by reducing duplicated effort through shared AI platforms and standardized engineering processes.\n• Promote a collaborative, high-performing technical environment through strong architectural guidance, documentation, and best practices.\n• Mentor engineers and data scientists, influencing technical direction beyond immediate projects and contributing to the overall maturity of the Data Science organization\n\nPlease apply if you meet the following qualifications:\n• 8–12+ years of experience in software engineering, machine learning engineering, or full-stack development, with demonstrated progression into technical leadership roles.\n• Proven track record of designing and delivering production systems used by multiple teams or products over long time horizons.\n• Expert proficiency in Python, with strong experience designing APIs, automation frameworks, and backend services.\n• Significant experience building internal platforms or tools using modern front-end frameworks (React, Next.js, or similar).\n• Hands-on experience with LLMs and modern AI tooling, including embeddings, vector databases, RAG pipelines, and evaluation workflows.\n• Strong architectural judgment with the ability to balance speed, reliability, cost, and long-term maintainability.\n• Demonstrated ability to lead without authority, influence roadmap decisions, and operate effectively in ambiguous problem spaces.\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n• Experience with search, discovery, metadata systems, or relevance optimization.\n• Background in consumer-facing AI platforms.\n• Familiarity with experimentation frameworks and measurement of business impact.\n• Prior experience operating explicitly at a Staff or equivalent level, supporting multiple teams or domains.\n• Master’s degree or higher in Computer Science, Engineering, Data Science, or a related field.\n\nPlease be advised that candidates selected to advance to the 1st round of interviews will be required to show photo ID on camera, and final interviews for this role will be in person at a Penguin Random House location.\n\nThe salary range for this position is $160,000 - $210,000. All positions are currently eligible for annual profit award or bonus, subject to company results. \n\nPlease apply by February 10th, 2026 and include your resume and cover letter for consideration. Before applying for any role at Penguin Random House, we recommend you review our applicant resources page and our FAQs page. \n\nPenguin Random House job postings include a good faith compensation range for each open position. The salary range listed is specific to each particular open position and takes into account various factors including the specifics of the individual role, and candidate\'s relevant experience and qualifications.\n\nFull-time employees are eligible for our comprehensive benefits program. Our range of benefits include, but are not limited to, Medical/Prescription drug insurance, Dental, Vision, Health Care/Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account, Health Savings Account, Pre-Tax and Roth 401(k), Short and Long-Term Disability Insurance, Life/AD&D Insurance, Commuter Benefits, Student Loan Repayment Program, Educational Assistance & generous paid time off.\n\nPenguin Random House is the leading adult and children\'s publishing house in North America, the United Kingdom and many other regions around the world. In publishing the best books in every genre and subject for all ages, we are committed to quality, excellence in execution, and innovation throughout the entire publishing process: editorial, design, marketing, publicity, sales, production, and distribution. Our vibrant and diverse international community of nearly 300 publishing brands and imprints include Ballantine Bantam Dell, Berkley, Clarkson Potter, Crown, DK, Doubleday, Dutton, Grosset & Dunlap, Little Golden Books, Knopf, Modern Library, Pantheon, Penguin Books, Penguin Press, Penguin Random House Audio, Penguin Young Readers, Portfolio, Puffin, Putnam, Random House, Random House Children\'s Books, Riverhead, Ten Speed Press, Viking, and Vintage, among others. More information can be found at http://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/.\n\nPenguin Random House values the array of talents and perspectives that a diverse workforce brings. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, national origin, religion, age, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or protected veteran status.\n\nCompany: Penguin Random House LLC | Job ID: 285779\n\nThis offer from \"Arvato\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,160000.00,210000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','penguin,random,random house,house,penguin random,senior,ai,publishing,include,long,books,systems,technical,platforms,roadmaps,multiple teams,experience,teams,end,term,long term,architectural,ai solutions,ensure ai,account'),(17,'jsearch','sZc3oRmQDcTaTQVIAAAAAA==','Software Engineer, Backend Engineer','Rescale',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/69987e4cda7696de2f595bb3-software-engineer-backend-engineer','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America\n\nRescale is pioneering the future of engineering and scientific discovery. As the leader in digital engineering, we’re transforming how products are developed—through intelligent automation, applied AI, data management, and the integration of the world’s largest network of engineering and R&D applications. Joining Rescale means becoming part of a diverse, collaborative, and mission-driven team that’s unlocking faster innovation across industries like aerospace, energy, life sciences, and manufacturing. We’re solving complex challenges that traditional HPC can’t—and we’re seeking passionate, curious minds to help build the next wave of breakthroughs.\n\nWe are seeking a systems-oriented Software Engineer, Backend engineer to join our team!\n\nSome of the things you will work on and impact:\n• own end-to-end delivery of essential, core functionality for Rescale customers as well as rapidly iterating on new product ideas.\n• work with your teammates to build and maintain high quality automation for building and testing our main customer-facing platform.\n• develop and maintain critical areas of the product including identity management, elastic cloud workstations, and workflow automation.\n\nWhat we’re looking for:\n• 2+ years of experience building and operating performant, non-trivial backend systems in production.\n• Expertise or strong interest in the following areas: web performance optimization (including ORM and DB profiling), deploying and scaling web applications using cloud services, application security\n• High enthusiasm for supporting both rapid proof-of-concept prototypes as well as robust, mission critical components for both internal and external stakeholders.\n• Comfortable with ambiguity, strong user-first mindset, and ability to come up with non-regrettable technical solutions.\n• Flexibility and dedication to work in a team and ship exceptional software.\n• BS in Computer Science or equivalent experience.\n\nDiversity, equity, inclusion and belonging are fundamental to our success. We strive to be a workplace where we:\n• Welcome ALL and ALL are welcome.\n• Show up with our whole selves or whichever parts of ourselves we’re comfortable sharing, and be ready to see the same in others.\n• Be ready to learn, unlearn, and learn again.\n• Respect others and their opinions. We practice empathy in the way we interact with each other and celebrate uniqueness as a team.\n• Seek to understand - ask more questions than one makes statements.\n• Provide safety from judgment and preserve a collaborative environment.\n\nRescale is an equal opportunities employer and welcomes applications from all qualified persons regardless of their race, sex, disability, religion/belief, sexual orientation or age. As part of our standard hiring process for new employees, employment with Rescale will be contingent upon successful completion of a comprehensive background check.\nThis offer from \"Rescale\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 83% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'rescale,automation,areas,engineer backend,backend engineer,engineer,backend,welcome,non,team,ready,comfortable,management,engineering,learn,critical,collaborative,applications,mission,seeking,software engineer,offer,network engineering,check offer,including identity'),(18,'jsearch','KLXCe9EVL2QNDkKIAAAAAA==','Senior Software Engineer - MetaMask (Predict)','Consensys',NULL,NULL,0,'https://himalayas.app/companies/consensys-io/jobs/senior-software-engineer-metamask-predict','Consensys is the leading blockchain and web3 software company founded by Joe Lubin, CEO of Consensys and Co-Founder of Ethereum. Since 2014, Consensys has been at the forefront of innovation, pioneering technological developments within the web3 ecosystem.\n\nThrough our product suite, including the MetaMask platform, Infura, Linea, Diligence, and our NFT toolkit Phosphor, we have become the trusted collaborator for users, creators, and developers on their path to build and belong in the world they want to see.\n\nWhether building a dapp, an NFT collection, a portfolio, or a better future, the instinct to build is universal. Consensys inspires and champions the builder instinct in everyone by making web3 universally easy to use and develop on.\n\nOur mission is to unlock the collaborative power of communities by making the decentralized web universally easy to access, use, and build on.\n\nYou’ll get to work on the tools, infrastructure, and apps that scale these platforms to onboard one billion participants and 5 million developers. You’ll be constantly exposed to new concepts, ideas, and frameworks from your peers, and as you work on different projects — challenging you to stay at the top of your game. You’ll join a network of builders that reaches the edge of our ecosystem. Consensys alumni have moved on to become tech entrepreneurs, CEOs, and team leads at tech companies.\nAbout MetaMask\n\nMetaMask aims to create a thriving engineering organization that supports the well-being of our engineers while empowering them to do work they are proud of and enjoy. We strive for an environment that gives our people high trust and autonomy, while also facilitating collaboration, communication and camaraderie among teams and teammates. We aspire to build a diverse engineering team, inclusive to people from all backgrounds and demographics. It is also of great importance to us that working at MetaMask is an experience that catalyzes career growth and learning.\nWhat you’ll do\nAs a senior engineer, you will:\n• Build and enhance MetaMask\'s growth engine to drive user engagement and improve retention\n• Implement user-centric solutions across MetaMask Clients including Extension, Mobile, and Web\n• Contribute to backend APIs and middlewares that power these consumer experiences\n• Help create intuitive, efficient, and secure Web3 interactions that delight users\n• Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other engineers to deliver high-quality features\n• Participate in code reviews and help maintain high code quality standards\nWould be great if you brought this to the role\n• 3+ years working with mobile-based technologies\n• 3+ years building websites and/or applications\n• Experience with React and React Native\n• Strong knowledge of modern Javascript (ES6/TypeScript/etc.)\n• Familiarity with blockchain fundamentals and Web3 integration\n• Working knowledge of cross platform/browser compatibility\n• Experience working with APIs and middleware services\n• Experience working in an agile development team\n• Experience developing applications with clean code practices, testing, and adherence to coding standards\n• Understanding of web-based security considerations\nBonus Points\n• Experience with in-app marketing and engagement strategies, including push notifications, carousel banners, and in-app modals.\n• Experience with DeFi protocols, token swaps, or fiat on/off ramps\n• Knowledge of financial products in the digital space\n• Interest in blockchain technologies and Web3\n• Basic understanding of cryptography principles\n• Experience working in distributed teams\n• Previous experience working in Web3\n• Familiarity with the Web3 wallet ecosystem\n• Experience with performance optimization\nOther skills to demonstrate\n• Good verbal and written communication in English\n• Teamwork, flexibility, and organization\n• Eagerness to learn and grow your technical skills\n• Ability to balance technical quality with business needs and user experience\n\nDon\'t meet all the requirements? Don\'t sweat it. We’re passionate about building a diverse team of humans and as such, if you think you\'ve got what it takes for our chaotic-but-fun, remote-friendly, start-up environment—apply anyway, detailing your relevant transferable skills in your cover letter. While we have a pretty good idea of what we need, we\'re ready for you to challenge our thinking on who needs to be in this role.\n\nIt is a requirement of employment in this position that applicants will be required to submit to background checks including but not limited to employment, education and criminal record checks. Further details will be provided to applicants that successfully meet the criteria for the position as determined by the company in its sole discretion. By submitting an application for employment, you are acknowledging and consenting to this requirement.\n\nThe salary range for US-based candidates only will be determined throughout the interview process depending on experience and skills.\n\nUS pay range (not including bonus, equity or other benefits)\n$104,000—$187,000 USD\n\nIn the rapidly evolving Web3 space, we believe that everyone is a builder. This expansive paradigm requires a range of backgrounds, talents, skills, and experiences to influence and shape the future. At Consensys, this diversity fuels our ability to shift control and redefine the realm of possibility. We are committed to ensuring that our technology empowers people and communities with economic and political agency through decentralized technologies. We welcome the range of perspectives and differences and celebrate them. We\'re excited to see how your unique skills as a builder can contribute to our vision, drive innovation, and help us shape a more inclusive Web3.\n\nConsensys is an equal opportunity employer. All employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, genetic information, religion, disability, medical condition, pregnancy, marital status, family status, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law. Consensys is aware of fraudulent recruitment practices and we encourage all applicants to review our best practices to protect yourself which can be found (https://consensys.io/careers/best-practices-to-avoid-recruitment-fraud/).',NULL,104000.00,187000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','web3,consensys,metamask,experience,range,builder,blockchain,working,experience working,applicants,ecosystem,employment,skills,ll,practices,build,determined,space,universally,requirement,backgrounds,universally easy,easy,nft,instinct'),(19,'jsearch','XdNLih7NB46DHLqPAAAAAA==','Quality Assurance Lab Technician- Meat Plant','Caribbean Producers Jamaica Ltd',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Quality-Assurance-Lab-Technician-Meat-Job-226512.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','The Quality Assurance / Lab Technician is responsible for ensuring that CPJ’s products consistently meet agreed standards through consistent implementation and monitoring of required parameters, and effective food safety and quality management systems. 1. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist the QA Manager in the development, implementation and maintenance of the company’s food safety and quality management systems (FSQMS), inclusive of the Prerequisite Programme and Hazard Analysis Critical Control Points (HACCP) system in the food manufacturing, handling, storage and distribution facilities. Assist in improving and driving corporate food safety culture. Ensure that all food products processed conform to public safety regulations and standards established by local and foreign regulatory bodies e.g. Bureau of Standards, Jamaica, US FDA/ FSMA, United Sates Department of Agriculture (USDA), among others. Inspect and record all pertinent information relevant to the receipt of all raw materials/ingredients. Monitor food production facility temperature and calibrate equipment (e.g., thermometer, pH meter) Ensure that all Meat Plant quality checks are undertaken and documented and, assist in resolving quality issues which may arise. Review all product and product information to ensure accuracy in labeling and packaging. Work closely with the Meat Plant Production team to ensure compliance with product specification and regulatory requirements. Conduct sensory analysis on finished products. Collect samples for external and/or internal microbiological analyses, sample retention and shelf-life assessment. Conduct chemical tests (e.g. salinity, pH, fat analysis, residual chlorine) and microbiological testing, as required. Assist in maintaining the microbiology laboratory facilities and equipment in good condition. Support, maintain and conduct sanitation verification checks such as ATP and environmental monitoring programme to ensure acceptable food safety standards of the plant. Identify and investigate areas of concern and communicate information to all levels of staff.  Identify continuous improvement measures and work with the Quality Assurance and Production teams towards continuous improvement. Ensure proper documentation of all non-conformances to CPJ’s FSQMS and the subsequent corrective actions. Ensure compliance to all established SOPs, food safety requirements, good manufacturing practices, and sanitation requirements in accordance with CPJ’s FSQMS. Conduct GMP inspections, and where possible, assist with internal audits and supplier audits as per the company’s internal audit schedule. Assist in overseeing the use and replenishment of sanitation supplies and personal protective equipment (PPE). Actively participate in product research and development. 1.1 General Responsibilities: To implement any activity, process or strategy that will improve the competitive advantage of the company, in consultation with the Food Safety, Quality and Sustainability Committee. Ensuring the maintenance of the good name and reputation of Caribbean Producers Jamaica Ltd. in general through the demonstration and practice of the highest standards of ethical conduct. To abide by the disciplinary code of the company. Any other duties as may be assigned. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Well organized and methodical approach to work and the work environment. Capable of analytical/critical thinking Must be computer proficient including use of Microsoft platform (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.) Good decision making, planning and problem-solving skills Must display initiative and ability to work independently Should possess good written and verbal communication skills Ability to develop and maintain good relationships with colleagues, staff and customers Excellent time management skills and ability to multi-task Ability to work flexible hours as the needs of the service dictate, including out of normal hours as required Ability to work in a fast-paced environment whilst adhering to basic occupational health and safety guidelines Ability to work within Company Policies Education & Experience: At least a Bachelor of Science Degree in a Technical Discipline (Microbiology, Food Science, Chemistry, etc.) or equivalent qualifications At least 2 years’ experience in a food processing industry in a similar capacity A good knowledge of microorganisms in foods and ability to apply such knowledge towards food safety and quality of products. Food safety (e.g. HACCP) and quality (e.g. ISO) certification are desirable Knowledge and understanding of relevant Health and Safety Regulations A current Food Handler’s Permit',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'food,food safety,quality,safety,assist,good,ensure,safety quality,product,ability,conduct,work,products,plant,standards,cpj,sanitation,assurance,quality assurance,meat,fsqms,meat plant,production,ability work,internal'),(20,'jsearch','CykwqzbFOWilprJvAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-86/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nAt Career.zycto, we believe in nurturing the next generation of scientific talent. Our dynamic R&D division is a hub of innovation, committed to pushing boundaries in agricultural biotechnology and sustainable solutions. We offer a supportive, hands-on environment where an entry-level lab technician can thrive, learn from experienced professionals, and directly contribute to impactful projects aimed at improving lives and the local economy. Join a team passionate about discovery and making a tangible difference, providing the perfect launchpad for your scientific career in Salt Spring, St. James. We value curiosity and a drive to excel.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a recent graduate or an aspiring scientist with a passion for discovery and a keen eye for detail? Career.zycto is seeking a motivated and enthusiastic Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative Research & Development team in Salt Spring, St. James. This is a fantastic opportunity for an individual eager to kick-start their career in a dynamic laboratory setting, working on cutting-edge projects within agricultural biotechnology. You will play a crucial role in supporting our scientists and researchers, contributing to experiments that aim to develop sustainable and impactful solutions for the region. While prior extensive experience is not required, a foundational understanding of laboratory practices and a strong desire to learn are essential. We are looking for someone who is meticulously organized, committed to accuracy, and thrives in a collaborative environment. If you\'re ready to apply your scientific knowledge in a practical, hands-on role and grow with a forward-thinking company, we encourage you to apply and become a vital part of our mission to drive scientific advancement and create positive change.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare and process samples for various laboratory experiments and analyses according to established protocols.\n• Perform routine laboratory tests and experiments under the guidance of senior scientists and researchers.\n• Maintain laboratory equipment, ensuring proper calibration, cleanliness, and functionality; troubleshoot minor issues as needed.\n• Accurately record and document experimental data, observations, and results in lab notebooks and electronic systems.\n• Assist with inventory management of laboratory supplies, reagents, and chemicals, ensuring adequate stock levels and proper storage.\n• Adhere strictly to all safety protocols, quality control standards, and regulatory guidelines to ensure a safe and compliant working environment.\n• Contribute to the general upkeep, organization, and cleanliness of the laboratory space.\n• Participate actively in team meetings, contributing to discussions on research progress, experimental design, and data interpretation.\n• Learn and implement new laboratory techniques, methodologies, and procedures as required for ongoing projects.\n• Support the R&D team in various ad-hoc tasks, administrative duties, and special projects as they arise.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Associate\'s degree or Diploma in Science, Biology, Chemistry, or a closely related scientific field.\n• Basic understanding of laboratory safety procedures and best practices for chemical handling and waste disposal.\n• Proficiency in using standard laboratory equipment such as pipettes, centrifuges, pH meters, and microscopes.\n• Strong attention to detail, precision, and accuracy in all experimental procedures and data collection.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks effectively.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively as part of a diverse research team.\n• Proficient in basic computer applications, including Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint).\n• Strong communication skills, both written and verbal, for documenting results and interacting with colleagues.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in a scientific discipline such as Biochemistry, Microbiology, or Agricultural Science.\n• Prior hands-on experience (academic projects, internships, or volunteer work) in a laboratory setting.\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) and Quality Assurance (QA) principles.\n• Basic knowledge of statistical analysis tools or software for interpreting experimental data.\n• Demonstrated eagerness to learn, adapt to new technologies, and embrace continuous improvement in laboratory techniques.\n• Experience or coursework specifically related to agricultural science, plant biology, or biotechnology labs is a significant advantage.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and opportunities for performance-based incentives.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package, including medical and dental coverage.\n• Robust opportunities for professional development, training, and continuous learning to advance your career.\n• Direct mentorship from experienced scientists and researchers in a supportive environment.\n• A collaborative, inclusive, and stimulating work environment focused on innovation.\n• The chance to contribute to impactful research that directly benefits local communities and the environment.\n• Generous paid time off, including vacation and public holidays.\n• Access to an employee assistance program for personal and professional support.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their comprehensive resume and a compelling cover letter outlining their qualifications, relevant experience, and genuine interest in this entry-level position. Please click on the application link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'agricultural,laboratory,scientific,agricultural biotechnology,spring st,salt,salt spring,spring,agricultural science,biotechnology,projects,environment,james,drive,sustainable,st james,impactful,career,research,local,team,contribute impactful,cleanliness,experimental,scientists researchers'),(21,'jsearch','qHmdKihUX253CphXAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Kellits','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-83/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nDiscover the future with Career.zycto, a forward-thinking research and development firm dedicated to pioneering solutions in biotechnology. We pride ourselves on a vibrant culture of innovation, collaboration, and continuous learning, providing an ideal launchpad for aspiring scientists. For an entry-level lab technician, Career.zycto offers a unique opportunity to gain hands-on experience with cutting-edge technology, work alongside experienced mentors, and contribute to projects that truly make a difference. Join our team in Kellits, where your precision and passion for science will directly impact our groundbreaking discoveries and contribute to meaningful advancements.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a recent science graduate brimming with curiosity and a passion for discovery? Do you dream of applying your academic knowledge in a real-world research and development setting, contributing to projects that truly matter? Career.zycto invites an enthusiastic and meticulously organized Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative R&D team nestled in the vibrant community of Kellits, Clarendon. This is an unparalleled opportunity to kickstart your scientific career, working alongside experienced researchers and contributing directly to groundbreaking projects that aim to solve complex challenges, drive innovation, and ultimately improve lives within our target markets.\n\nAt Career.zycto, we believe in nurturing nascent talent and fostering an environment where innovative ideas flourish from every team member. As an Entry-Level Lab Technician, you will be an integral part of our daily laboratory operations. Your core responsibilities will encompass the precise execution of experiments, meticulous maintenance of state-of-the-art laboratory equipment, and ensuring adherence to the highest standards of safety and quality control protocols. Your daily tasks will involve a diverse range of activities, including preparing reagents and samples, performing analytical tests using various techniques, accurately recording and meticulously interpreting experimental data, and actively assisting in the development and refinement of new methodologies and protocols. We are specifically looking for a proactive individual who is eager to learn new skills, adapt quickly to evolving research demands, and demonstrate a strong commitment to growth within our fast-paced and highly collaborative research environment.\n\nThis role is specifically designed for someone who thrives on precision, possesses exceptional attention to detail, and naturally adopts a structured, methodical approach to scientific inquiry. You will gain invaluable hands-on experience with a diverse array of laboratory techniques and advanced instrumentation, thereby expanding your practical skill set significantly. Beyond the fundamental technical aspects, this position will cultivate your critical thinking capabilities, sharpen your problem-solving abilities, and enhance your professional communication skills—all of which are absolutely essential for a successful and impactful scientific career. Career.zycto is deeply committed to your professional development, offering structured mentorship programs, access to internal training workshops, and ample opportunities for continuous learning and career advancement. Join us and contribute to a dynamic team that is dedicated to pushing the boundaries of scientific knowledge and making a tangible, positive impact within our industry and the communities we serve. If you are ready to transform your academic potential into practical innovation and become a vital part of our future discoveries, we strongly encourage you to apply today!\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare and analyze samples, reagents, and media according to established protocols.\n• Operate, calibrate, and maintain laboratory instruments and equipment, including glassware.\n• Accurately record, organize, and interpret experimental data and observations.\n• Assist senior researchers in conducting experiments and research projects.\n• Adhere strictly to safety guidelines, GLP (Good Laboratory Practice), and quality control procedures.\n• Perform routine laboratory tasks such as inventory management, ordering supplies, and waste disposal.\n• Troubleshoot basic equipment malfunctions and report complex issues to supervisors.\n• Contribute to the development and optimization of laboratory procedures.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory environment.\n• Collaborate effectively with team members on ongoing projects and share findings.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Strong theoretical understanding of scientific principles (Biology, Chemistry, Biochemistry, etc.).\n• Proficiency in basic laboratory techniques and equipment operation.\n• Excellent attention to detail and accuracy in performing tasks.\n• Solid data recording, organizational, and analytical skills.\n• Ability to follow complex instructions and protocols precisely.\n• Basic computer proficiency (MS Office Suite, data entry software).\n• Effective written and verbal communication skills.\n• Strong problem-solving aptitude and critical thinking abilities.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Previous hands-on experience in a research or academic laboratory setting (e.g., through internships, university projects).\n• Familiarity with specific analytical instruments (e.g., spectrophotometers, pH meters, centrifuges, PCR machines).\n• Knowledge of Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) and relevant safety regulations.\n• Demonstrated ability to work both independently and as part of a collaborative team.\n• Proactive attitude and eagerness to learn new technologies and techniques.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive entry-level salary aligned with industry standards.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance coverage.\n• Generous paid time off and observance of public holidays.\n• Extensive opportunities for professional development, training, and certifications.\n• Structured mentorship programs with experienced scientists and researchers.\n• Supportive, inclusive, and collaborative work environment.\n• Exposure to cutting-edge research and innovative technology.\n• Clear pathways for career advancement and growth within the company.\n• Employee wellness programs and initiatives.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to submit their application promptly. Please click on the link below to apply for this exciting opportunity. Ensure your resume and a cover letter detailing your qualifications and interest in an entry-level R&D lab technician role are attached.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'laboratory,career,structured,research,entry,projects,development,projects truly,kellits,career zycto,zycto,entry level,level,scientific,team,structured mentorship,critical thinking,lab technician,thinking,technician,truly,specifically,learn new,skills,lab'),(22,'jsearch','9y0IWW-pm8HT-MY_AAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Technological Solutions Limited','Stony Hill','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-2/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nTechnological Solutions Limited (TSL) is a leading analytical services and consulting firm based in Jamaica, dedicated to delivering precise, reliable, and timely scientific data and solutions to a diverse clientele. For over two decades, TSL has been at the forefront of quality assurance, research support, and environmental monitoring, serving vital sectors including agriculture, food and beverage, manufacturing, and health. Our unwavering commitment to scientific excellence, innovation, and client success has established us as a trusted partner in driving progress and ensuring compliance across the Caribbean. At TSL, we believe in fostering a culture of continuous learning, professional growth, and collaboration, where every team member contributes to our mission of advancing scientific understanding and practical applications. We pride ourselves on maintaining state-of-the-art facilities and upholding the highest standards of safety and quality in all our operations. Join our dynamic team and be part of an organization that values integrity, precision, and tangible impact on industry and society.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a passionate, detail-oriented individual eager to kickstart your career in scientific research and development? Technological Solutions Limited (TSL) is seeking an enthusiastic Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative R&D team in Stony Hill, St. Andrew. This is an unparalleled opportunity for a recent graduate or an individual with foundational lab experience to immerse themselves in a dynamic environment, contributing directly to groundbreaking projects that impact various industries across Jamaica and the wider Caribbean. As an Entry-Level Lab Technician, you will play a crucial supporting role in our R&D efforts, working closely with senior scientists, chemists, and researchers. Your responsibilities will be instrumental in the preparation of samples, execution of routine laboratory tests, meticulous data collection, and the diligent upkeep of our state-of-the-art laboratory equipment. This position is perfect for someone with a strong scientific aptitude, excellent organizational skills, and an unwavering commitment to precision, quality, and safety. You will gain invaluable hands-on experience with diverse analytical techniques, learn to operate sophisticated instruments, and contribute directly to the development of new methodologies, product enhancements, and quality control solutions. We are dedicated to nurturing talent, providing comprehensive training, and offering a clear path for professional development and career advancement within our organization. If you\'re looking for a challenging yet rewarding role where you can grow your skills, apply your scientific knowledge to real-world problems, and make a tangible difference, we strongly encourage you to apply. Join TSL and help us shape the future of scientific innovation.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare samples for various analytical tests according to established protocols and standards.\n• Conduct routine laboratory experiments and tests under the supervision of senior researchers.\n• Operate, maintain, and calibrate laboratory equipment, ensuring proper functionality and accuracy.\n• Accurately record and document experimental data, observations, and results in lab notebooks and databases.\n• Assist senior scientists in the design and execution of research projects and methodology development.\n• Perform quality control checks on raw materials, in-process samples, and finished products.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory environment, strictly adhering to safety guidelines and waste disposal procedures.\n• Manage laboratory inventory, including ordering supplies and reagents to ensure continuous operations.\n• Participate in team meetings, contributing to discussions and presenting findings as required.\n• Troubleshoot minor equipment malfunctions and perform basic preventive maintenance tasks.\n\nRequired Skills\n• High School Diploma or equivalent; Associate\'s Degree in Chemistry, Biology, or a related scientific field preferred.\n• Basic understanding of laboratory safety protocols and aseptic techniques.\n• Strong attention to detail and high level of accuracy in performing tasks and recording data.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills.\n• Proficiency in basic computer applications (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite).\n• Ability to follow instructions meticulously and work effectively both independently and as part of a team.\n• Strong verbal and written communication skills.\n• A genuine passion for science and a proactive approach to learning.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Chemistry, Biochemistry, Microbiology, or a related scientific discipline.\n• Previous experience in a laboratory setting (e.g., academic, internship, or volunteer work).\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) and ISO 17025 standards.\n• Experience with specific analytical instrumentation (e.g., pH meters, spectrophotometers, chromatographs).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package and performance incentives.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Pension plan contributions.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Access to cutting-edge laboratory equipment and technologies.\n• A supportive, collaborative, and innovative work environment.\n• Paid time off and holidays.\n• Employee assistance programs.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nEager to contribute to a leading scientific organization? We invite qualified candidates to submit their applications. Please click on the application link below to apply for this exciting opportunity. Ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience, academic background, and passion for research and development. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to the TSL family!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'tsl,scientific,laboratory,development,solutions limited,limited tsl,technological solutions,solutions,applications,technological,quality,research,analytical,caribbean,unwavering commitment,experience,skills,lab,team,organization,unwavering,leading,limited,execution,data'),(23,'jsearch','_VYbWpQfHzFS_cRkAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Negril','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-72/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nCareer.zycto fosters a dynamic environment where curiosity meets innovation, especially for emerging talent. We empower our team members to contribute meaningfully from day one, offering unparalleled mentorship and growth opportunities. For an ambitious entry-level lab technician, this is more than just a job; it’s a launchpad for a rewarding career in scientific exploration. Join us, and become an integral part of ground-breaking research, shaping future advancements in our field within a supportive and collaborative culture. Discover your potential and thrive at Career.zycto.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you passionate about scientific discovery and eager to kick-start your career in a vibrant research setting? Career.zycto is seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative Research & Development team in Negril, Westmoreland. This is an exceptional opportunity for an enthusiastic individual to gain hands-on experience in a cutting-edge laboratory, contributing directly to projects that push the boundaries of scientific knowledge. As an integral part of our R&D unit, you will be responsible for executing various laboratory procedures, maintaining equipment, and meticulously documenting experimental data. You’ll work alongside experienced scientists and researchers, learning best practices in laboratory management, experimental design, and data analysis. Our ideal candidate possesses a foundational understanding of scientific principles, a strong commitment to accuracy, and an insatiable desire to learn and grow within a fast-paced research environment. You will play a crucial role in preparing samples, conducting routine tests, and ensuring the smooth operation of our lab facilities. If you’re ready to apply your academic knowledge to real-world challenges and contribute to impactful discoveries, we encourage you to apply and grow with us at Career.zycto. This role offers not just a job, but a pathway to developing specialized skills and making tangible contributions to our research objectives.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare samples, reagents, and media according to standard operating procedures (SOPs) for various research experiments.\n• Perform routine laboratory tests and analyses accurately and efficiently under direct supervision.\n• Operate and maintain laboratory equipment, including calibration and troubleshooting minor issues.\n• Collect, record, and organize experimental data clearly and consistently in laboratory notebooks and digital systems.\n• Adhere strictly to all laboratory safety protocols, quality control standards, and regulatory guidelines.\n• Assist senior researchers and scientists with experimental setup, data interpretation, and report generation.\n• Maintain inventory of laboratory supplies, reagents, and chemicals, ensuring proper storage and timely reordering.\n• Clean and sterilize laboratory glassware, equipment, and workspaces to maintain a sterile and organized environment.\n• Participate in team meetings and contribute to discussions regarding experimental design and results.\n• Undertake continuous professional development to stay updated with new techniques and research methodologies.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Basic knowledge of laboratory techniques and safety procedures.\n• Strong attention to detail and meticulous record-keeping abilities.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills.\n• Proficiency in basic computer applications (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite).\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team.\n• Effective written and verbal communication skills.\n• Proactive attitude and a strong willingness to learn new skills and adapt to new challenges.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in Biology, Chemistry, Biochemistry, Medical Technology, or a related scientific field.\n• Prior hands-on experience in a laboratory setting (academic or professional).\n• Familiarity with specific laboratory instruments relevant to research & development.\n• Understanding of Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) and Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP).\n• Basic understanding of statistical analysis for experimental data.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and benefits package.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and training.\n• Mentorship from experienced scientists and researchers.\n• A collaborative and innovative work environment.\n• Access to cutting-edge laboratory equipment and technologies.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting entry-level opportunity, please click on the application link below. Ensure your resume highlights your academic achievements, relevant coursework, and any laboratory experience. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'laboratory,research,experimental,career,scientific,just job,data,zycto,career zycto,development,skills,edge laboratory,just,level,entry,entry level,experimental data,experimental design,environment,lab,team,equipment,apply,researchers,challenges'),(24,'jsearch','p-ZqCL