roject needs. You will work closely with senior researchers and mentors who are dedicated to fostering your professional growth and helping you develop advanced laboratory skills. If you are passionate about scientific discovery, thrive in a collaborative setting, and are eager to contribute to meaningful innovations, we encourage you to apply. Join Career.zycto and be part of a team that is making a difference.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare samples, reagents, and solutions according to established protocols and safety guidelines.\n• Conduct routine laboratory experiments, tests, and analyses under the supervision of senior scientists.\n• Accurately record, compile, and present experimental data, observations, and results using laboratory information systems and software.\n• Perform calibration, maintenance, and basic troubleshooting of laboratory equipment and instrumentation.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory environment, strictly adhering to all health, safety, and environmental regulations.\n• Manage laboratory inventory, including tracking supplies, ordering new materials, and ensuring proper storage.\n• Assist in the development and optimization of new experimental procedures and protocols.\n• Collaborate effectively with team members on ongoing projects and contribute to scientific discussions.\n• Document procedures, results, and findings in lab notebooks and electronic records with meticulous detail.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in Chemistry, Biology, Biochemistry, Materials Science, or a related scientific field.\n• Fundamental understanding of basic laboratory techniques and safety procedures.\n• Exceptional attention to detail and strong organizational skills.\n• Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) for data entry and report generation.\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\n• Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team setting.\n• Strong problem-solving aptitude and a proactive approach to tasks.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Previous laboratory experience gained through academic projects, internships, or volunteer work.\n• Familiarity with laboratory information management systems (LIMS).\n• Basic knowledge of statistical analysis software or techniques.\n• Experience with specific analytical instruments such as spectrophotometers, pH meters, or centrifuges.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning through workshops and mentorship programs.\n• Paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, and public holidays.\n• A vibrant and inclusive work culture focused on collaboration and innovation.\n• Access to state-of-the-art laboratory equipment and research tools.\n• Career advancement pathways within our growing R&D department.\n• Employee wellness programs and initiatives.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nEager to contribute to groundbreaking research? Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and a cover letter detailing your interest in this entry-level Lab Technician position and how your skills align with Career.zycto\'s mission. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'laboratory,career,research,scientific,montego,materials science,bay,montego bay,career zycto,zycto,lab,team,eager contribute,materials,entry,contribute meaningful,development,skills,projects,contribute,lab technician,laboratory information,level,technician,entry level'),(25,'jsearch','Sy-Y2tpmh_XmG5HLAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Longville Park','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-68/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nAt Career.zycto, we are at the forefront of scientific exploration, dedicated to pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible in biotechnology. We thrive on curiosity and innovation, transforming complex challenges into groundbreaking solutions that improve lives. For an aspiring Lab Technician, our collaborative environment offers an unparalleled opportunity to immerse yourself in real-world research from day one. You\'ll gain invaluable hands-on experience, contribute to meaningful projects, and grow your expertise alongside a team of passionate scientists. We believe in nurturing talent, providing a supportive launchpad for your career in R&D, making us the ideal place to start your scientific journey.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a recent graduate or an enthusiastic individual with a foundational understanding of laboratory practices, eager to launch your career in scientific research and development? Career.zycto is actively seeking a dedicated and meticulous Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative R&D team in Longville Park, May Pen. This is an exceptional opportunity for someone passionate about discovery, who thrives in a dynamic, hands-on environment and is committed to contributing to cutting-edge scientific advancements. We are looking for a proactive individual ready to learn, grow, and become an integral part of our mission to explore new frontiers in biotechnology and beyond.\n\nIn this pivotal entry-level role, you will work closely with our experienced researchers and scientists, providing essential support across various research projects. Your daily activities will be diverse, encompassing everything from preparing samples and reagents to operating and maintaining laboratory equipment, conducting preliminary experiments under supervision, and meticulously documenting observations. This position is designed to provide comprehensive exposure to the full lifecycle of R&D, allowing you to develop critical technical skills, understand experimental design, and contribute to data collection and analysis. We value precision, attention to detail, and a steadfast commitment to laboratory safety protocols.\n\nCareer.zycto fosters an environment of continuous learning and professional development. As an Entry-Level Lab Technician, you will not only perform crucial tasks but also be encouraged to ask questions, propose ideas, and actively participate in team discussions. We believe in empowering our team members, offering mentorship, and providing clear pathways for career progression within the scientific community. If you are detail-oriented, possess a strong work ethic, and are excited by the prospect of turning scientific curiosity into tangible breakthroughs, we invite you to apply. Join us in making a real impact and shaping the future of scientific innovation.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare samples, reagents, media, and solutions according to established protocols and researcher instructions.\n• Operate, calibrate, and perform routine maintenance on laboratory equipment such as centrifuges, pH meters, spectrophotometers, and analytical balances.\n• Maintain accurate and detailed records of experiments, observations, and results in lab notebooks and digital systems.\n• Ensure strict adherence to safety guidelines, chemical handling procedures, and waste disposal protocols.\n• Assist senior technicians and scientists with setting up and executing experiments, collecting data, and initial data entry.\n• Manage laboratory inventory, including ordering supplies, receiving shipments, and organizing chemicals and consumables.\n• Perform general laboratory upkeep, including cleaning glassware, sterilizing equipment, and maintaining a tidy and organized workspace.\n• Troubleshoot minor equipment malfunctions and report larger issues to appropriate personnel.\n• Participate in regular team meetings to discuss project progress and contribute to problem-solving.\n\nRequired Skills\n• High School Diploma or equivalent; Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in a scientific field (e.g., Biology, Chemistry, Biotechnology) preferred.\n• Basic understanding of laboratory safety protocols and good laboratory practices (GLP).\n• Proficiency in basic mathematical calculations and data recording.\n• Strong attention to detail and high level of accuracy in performing tasks.\n• Ability to follow written and verbal instructions precisely.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills.\n• Basic computer literacy (Microsoft Office Suite, especially Excel for data entry).\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Prior hands-on experience in a laboratory setting (academic or industrial internships).\n• Familiarity with aseptic techniques.\n• Knowledge of common laboratory equipment operation and basic troubleshooting.\n• Experience with laboratory information management systems (LIMS) is a plus.\n• Demonstrated passion for scientific research and continuous learning.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive entry-level salary.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship from experienced scientists and researchers.\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Participation in groundbreaking scientific research.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application, including a resume and cover letter, by clicking on the application link below. Please highlight your relevant experience and explain why you are a great fit for an entry-level R&D Lab Technician role at Career.zycto.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'scientific,laboratory,entry,level,career,research,entry level,scientific research,biotechnology,team,lab,lab technician,data,technician,zycto,career zycto,equipment,scientists,providing,high,protocols,basic,experiments,environment,development'),(26,'jsearch','iIuSKfEoA2RNM30gAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Wisynco Group Limited','Spanish Town','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nWisynco Group Limited is a leading Jamaican manufacturer, bottler, distributor, and retailer of beverages, food, and industrial products. With a rich history spanning over 50 years, Wisynco has grown to become a household name, synonymous with quality, innovation, and community development. Our diverse portfolio includes iconic local brands and internationally recognized products, all produced and distributed with a commitment to excellence. At Wisynco, we believe in fostering a dynamic and inclusive work environment where every team member is valued, and opportunities for growth are abundant. We are deeply committed to sustainability, driving economic growth, and positively impacting the lives of Jamaicans through our operations and philanthropic initiatives. Joining Wisynco means becoming part of a vibrant team dedicated to shaping the future of manufacturing and distribution in the Caribbean. We pride ourselves on our state-of-the-art facilities and a culture that encourages learning, collaboration, and continuous improvement, ensuring that our products meet the highest standards of quality and delight consumers daily.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a recent science graduate or a highly motivated individual with a foundational understanding of laboratory principles, eager to kickstart your career in a dynamic research and development environment? Wisynco Group Limited is seeking an enthusiastic and detail-oriented Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative R&D team in Spanish Town, St. Catherine. This is a fantastic opportunity for an individual passionate about scientific inquiry and product development to gain hands-on experience with cutting-edge techniques and contribute to the creation of market-leading products. As an Entry-Level Lab Technician, you will play a crucial supporting role in our R&D initiatives, working alongside experienced scientists and engineers. You will be instrumental in executing experiments, conducting routine analyses, and maintaining our laboratory\'s operational efficiency and safety standards. This role is designed for someone who thrives in a collaborative setting, possesses a meticulous approach to data collection, and is keen to learn and grow within a fast-paced manufacturing and product development landscape. We offer comprehensive training and a supportive environment where your contributions will directly impact the quality and innovation of products enjoyed by millions. If you are ready to apply your academic knowledge in a practical setting and contribute to a company that values innovation and excellence, we encourage you to apply! This position offers a pathway for aspiring scientists to develop essential lab skills and grow within a reputable industry leader.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare samples and reagents for various chemical, physical, and microbiological analyses.\n• Perform routine laboratory tests and experiments accurately under supervision, following established protocols.\n• Accurately record and document experimental data, observations, and results in lab notebooks and digital systems.\n• Operate, calibrate, and maintain laboratory equipment and instrumentation to ensure proper functioning.\n• Adhere strictly to all safety protocols, quality control procedures, and good laboratory practices (GLP) and good manufacturing practices (GMP).\n• Assist in the inventory management of laboratory supplies, chemicals, and reagents.\n• Contribute to the general cleanliness, organization, and upkeep of the laboratory environment.\n• Support senior technicians and scientists in research projects, data analysis, and troubleshooting.\n• Assist in the preparation of lab reports and presentations as required.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Foundational knowledge of chemistry, biology, or food science principles.\n• Basic understanding of laboratory safety procedures and practices.\n• Excellent attention to detail and precision in executing tasks and recording data.\n• Strong organizational and time management skills to handle multiple tasks efficiently.\n• Ability to follow written and verbal instructions meticulously.\n• Basic computer proficiency, particularly with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel).\n• Effective written and verbal communication skills for clear reporting and collaboration.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in Chemistry, Biochemistry, Food Science, Applied Science, or a closely related scientific field.\n• Prior experience in a laboratory setting (academic coursework, industrial internships, or volunteer experience is a plus).\n• Familiarity with Quality Control (QC) or Research & Development (R&D) processes in a manufacturing environment.\n• Knowledge of specific laboratory equipment (e.g., pH meters, spectrophotometers, refractometers).\n• Ability to work both independently and collaboratively as an integral part of a team.\n• Proactive attitude towards learning new techniques and adapting to new challenges.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package.\n• Health, dental, and vision insurance coverage.\n• Opportunities for professional development, training, and career advancement within a leading company.\n• A vibrant, dynamic, and supportive work culture that values innovation and teamwork.\n• Employee discounts on a wide range of company products.\n• Contribution to a leading national brand with a direct impact on daily consumer lives and economic growth in Jamaica.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant scientific background, laboratory experience (if any), and your passion for research and development.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'wisynco,products,laboratory,leading,manufacturing,development,food,values innovation,wisynco group,economic,economic growth,quality innovation,group limited,group,lab,values,research,quality,food science,science,innovation,environment,product development,limited,research development'),(27,'jsearch','5olkv8wZSKDv-o73AAAAAA==','Laboratory Technician – Medical Lab (Entry-Level)','Negril Medical Centre','Negril','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/laboratory-technician-medical-lab-entry-level/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nNegril Medical Centre is a cornerstone of health and wellness in the vibrant community of West End, Negril, Jamaica. For years, we have been dedicated to providing comprehensive, compassionate, and high-quality medical services to both residents and visitors. Our facility is equipped with modern diagnostic tools and staffed by a team of committed healthcare professionals who prioritize patient care and well-being above all else. We pride ourselves on creating a supportive and friendly environment where every team member is valued and encouraged to grow. As a vital part of the Negril community, we are constantly striving to enhance our services and expand our reach, ensuring accessible and excellent healthcare for everyone who walks through our doors. Join a team where your work truly makes a difference in people\'s lives.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a recent graduate or an aspiring professional looking to kickstart your career in medical diagnostics? Negril Medical Centre invites passionate and detail-oriented individuals to join our team as an Entry-Level Laboratory Technician. This is a unique opportunity to gain hands-on experience in a dynamic medical laboratory setting, contributing directly to patient care and community health in beautiful Negril. As an integral part of our diagnostic team, you will be responsible for assisting senior laboratory staff with various tasks, from sample collection and processing to preparing slides and maintaining laboratory equipment. We are looking for someone who is eager to learn, possesses excellent organizational skills, and is committed to upholding the highest standards of accuracy and safety. This role is perfect for individuals who are meticulous, have a strong sense of responsibility, and are keen to develop their technical skills under the guidance of experienced professionals. You will learn best practices in laboratory safety, quality control, and patient confidentiality, laying a solid foundation for a successful career in medical laboratory science. If you are ready to make a tangible impact and grow professionally within a supportive healthcare environment, we encourage you to apply.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist with the collection, labeling, and processing of biological samples (blood, urine, etc.) according to established protocols.\n• Prepare samples and reagents for analysis, ensuring accurate measurements and proper documentation.\n• Perform routine laboratory tests under the direct supervision of certified medical technologists.\n• Maintain and clean laboratory equipment, glassware, and work areas to ensure a sterile and safe environment.\n• Document test results accurately and meticulously in laboratory records and information systems.\n• Adhere strictly to all safety regulations, quality control procedures, and infection prevention guidelines.\n• Manage laboratory supplies, including inventory tracking and restocking as needed.\n• Assist with data entry and administrative tasks related to laboratory operations.\n• Participate in ongoing training and professional development activities to enhance technical skills and knowledge.\n• Collaborate effectively with medical technologists, nurses, and other healthcare professionals to ensure efficient patient care.\n\nRequired Skills\n• High School Diploma or equivalent (vocational training in a science-related field preferred).\n• Basic understanding of laboratory safety procedures and aseptic techniques.\n• Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy.\n• Strong organizational and time management abilities.\n• Ability to follow instructions precisely and work effectively in a team environment.\n• Basic computer proficiency (Microsoft Office Suite).\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n• A strong work ethic and a commitment to professional growth.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Associate\'s Degree or Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology, Biology, Chemistry, or a related science field.\n• Prior experience (even voluntary or internship) in a laboratory setting.\n• Knowledge of medical terminology.\n• Familiarity with laboratory information systems (LIS).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package.\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance.\n• Paid time off and holiday benefits.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship from experienced medical laboratory technologists.\n• A supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Contribution to vital community health services.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume and a cover letter detailing your interest and qualifications for this entry-level position are attached. We thank all applicants for their interest, however, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'medical,laboratory,negril,medical laboratory,healthcare,patient,technologists,community,patient care,care,services,centre,laboratory technician,medical centre,career medical,negril medical,team,technical skills,medical technologists,processing,professionals,healthcare professionals,diagnostic,community health,environment'),(28,'jsearch','uFtN0GCB0lFKmX5qAAAAAA==','Medical Lab Technologist','Apex Medical Laboratory',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/medical-lab-technologist/','About Company\n\nApex Medical Laboratory is a leading diagnostic service provider in Jamaica, committed to delivering accurate, reliable, and timely laboratory results to support patient care. For over two decades, we have been at the forefront of medical diagnostics, utilizing state-of-the-art technology and a team of highly skilled professionals to ensure the highest standards of quality. Our mission is to empower healthcare providers and patients with precise diagnostic information, contributing significantly to the health and well-being of the Jamaican community. We pride ourselves on a culture of excellence, continuous learning, and a deep commitment to our community, fostering an environment where our employees can thrive professionally and personally. At Apex, we believe in the power of accurate diagnostics to transform lives, and we continually invest in our people and technology to maintain our position as a trusted leader in medical laboratory services.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a meticulous and dedicated Medical Lab Technologist with a passion for precision and a commitment to patient care? Apex Medical Laboratory, a cornerstone of diagnostic excellence in Jamaica, is seeking a highly motivated Full-Time Medical Lab Technologist to join our dynamic team in Kingston. In this critical role, you will be instrumental in performing a wide range of laboratory tests, from routine analyses to complex diagnostic procedures, ensuring the accuracy and integrity of results that directly impact patient treatment and health outcomes. This position requires a professional who is not only proficient in laboratory techniques across various disciplines (e.g., hematology, chemistry, microbiology, serology, parasitology, immunology) but also possesses an unwavering dedication to quality control, safety protocols, and ethical practice. You will operate and maintain advanced laboratory equipment, interpret findings, and contribute to a collaborative environment focused on continuous improvement and exceptional service. If you are looking for an opportunity to apply your expertise in a supportive, state-of-the-art facility where your contributions are valued and directly enhance community health, we encourage you to apply. Join Apex Medical Laboratory and become a vital link in the chain of patient care, helping us maintain our reputation for diagnostic excellence and trusted results. We offer a challenging yet rewarding environment where professional growth is encouraged, and your skills make a tangible difference every day. Your commitment to detail, adherence to strict protocols, and ability to work effectively within a fast-paced setting will be paramount to your success and our collective mission.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Perform a wide range of clinical laboratory tests in areas such as hematology, chemistry, microbiology, serology, and urinalysis.\n• Operate, calibrate, and maintain sophisticated laboratory equipment and instruments.\n• Ensure accurate and timely recording, interpretation, and reporting of test results.\n• Adhere strictly to quality control procedures, laboratory safety protocols, and regulatory guidelines.\n• Perform routine quality assurance checks and troubleshooting of equipment and assays.\n• Collect and process biological specimens (blood, urine, etc.) with precision and care.\n• Communicate effectively with healthcare professionals regarding test results and laboratory procedures.\n• Participate in the training and mentorship of junior staff or students as required.\n• Maintain an organized and clean work environment.\n• Stay current with advances in medical laboratory technology and best practices.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in clinical laboratory techniques across multiple disciplines.\n• Strong understanding of quality control and quality assurance principles.\n• Experience with laboratory information systems (LIS).\n• Excellent attention to detail and strong analytical skills.\n• Ability to troubleshoot and maintain laboratory equipment.\n• Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills.\n• Demonstrated ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment.\n• Adherence to ethical guidelines and patient confidentiality.\n• Computer literacy (Microsoft Office Suite).\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s Degree in Medical Technology, Medical Laboratory Science, or a related field.\n• Registration with the Council for Professions Supplementary to Medicine (CPSM) in Jamaica.\n• Additional certifications in specialized laboratory areas.\n• Experience with specific brands of automated analyzers common in diagnostic labs.\n• Familiarity with international laboratory accreditation standards (e.g., ISO 15189).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package and performance incentives.\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance.\n• Pension plan contributions.\n• Paid time off for vacation, sick leave, and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for continuous professional development and training.\n• A supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n• Modern, state-of-the-art laboratory facilities.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested and qualified candidates are invited to submit their application, including a detailed resume and cover letter outlining their experience and suitability for the role, by clicking on the application link below. Please ensure your application clearly demonstrates how you meet the required skills and qualifications.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'medical,laboratory,medical laboratory,diagnostic,apex,patient,care,apex medical,lab technologist,technologist,medical lab,patient care,accurate,technology,microbiology serology,hematology chemistry,chemistry microbiology,effectively fast,diagnostic excellence,serology,hematology,quality,community,excellence,jamaica'),(29,'jsearch','uS4Sf-9nkJJReg4fAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Port Antonio','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-52/','About Company\n\nAspiring to launch your career in scientific discovery? Career.zycto offers an unparalleled environment for an entry-level Lab Technician to thrive and contribute meaningfully to groundbreaking research. We partner with innovative leaders across various industries, including food science, pharmaceuticals, and environmental technology, right here in Port Antonio. Joining us means gaining hands-on experience with cutting-edge methodologies and instrumentation, guided by experienced professionals. This is your chance to turn theoretical knowledge into practical application, driving forward critical projects that impact daily lives. Career.zycto is where your scientific journey begins, fostering growth and expertise.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you an enthusiastic and detail-oriented individual with a passion for scientific inquiry? Career.zycto is actively seeking an Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our dynamic Research & Development team in Port Antonio, Portland. This is an exceptional opportunity for a recent graduate or someone embarking on their scientific career path to contribute to innovative projects and gain invaluable hands-on experience in a supportive and collaborative environment. As an integral part of our R&D department, you will play a crucial role in the execution of experiments, data collection, and maintaining the pristine condition of our state-of-the-art laboratory facilities. We are looking for someone eager to learn, meticulous in their work, and committed to upholding the highest standards of safety and quality. This role offers exposure to a wide array of scientific disciplines, including but not limited to, chemical analysis, material science, and process optimization, depending on ongoing project needs. You will work closely with senior scientists and researchers, providing essential support that directly impacts the progression of our research initiatives. If you possess a foundational understanding of laboratory practices, a strong work ethic, and a genuine curiosity for discovery, we encourage you to apply and grow with us, helping to shape the future of our R&D endeavors.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Perform routine laboratory tests, experiments, and analyses under supervision, adhering strictly to established protocols and safety guidelines.\n• Accurately record and document experimental data, observations, and results in laboratory notebooks and digital systems.\n• Prepare reagents, media, and samples for experiments, ensuring precise measurements and proper labeling.\n• Maintain, clean, and sterilize laboratory equipment and glassware to ensure a safe and efficient working environment.\n• Assist in the calibration and maintenance of laboratory instruments, reporting any malfunctions or issues promptly.\n• Manage laboratory inventory, including tracking supplies, chemicals, and ordering new materials as needed.\n• Contribute to the upkeep of a clean and organized laboratory space, ensuring compliance with all health and safety regulations.\n• Collaborate effectively with senior scientists and team members on various research projects.\n• Assist in the preparation of technical reports, summaries, and presentations of experimental findings.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in Chemistry, Biology, Biochemistry, Chemical Engineering, or a related scientific field.\n• Strong foundational understanding of basic laboratory techniques and safety procedures.\n• Proficiency in data collection, organization, and basic analysis.\n• Excellent attention to detail and strong organizational skills.\n• Ability to follow written and verbal instructions precisely.\n• Basic computer literacy, including experience with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel).\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Previous experience (academic or professional) working in a laboratory setting.\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP).\n• Experience with specific analytical instruments (e.g., pH meters, spectrophotometers, chromatographs).\n• A demonstrated interest in research and development processes.\n• Problem-solving aptitude and a proactive approach to learning.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits.\n• Paid time off and holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship from experienced R&D scientists.\n• A collaborative and inclusive work environment.\n• Contribution to meaningful and impactful research projects.\n• Modern, well-equipped laboratory facilities.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo embark on this exciting journey with Career.zycto, please click on the application link below. Ensure your resume and a cover letter highlighting your passion for research and relevant skills are attached.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'laboratory,research,scientific,port antonio,antonio,port,career,career zycto,zycto,experience,projects,including,chemical,experiments,development,environment,safety,work,journey,senior scientists,laboratory facilities,scientists,research projects,data collection,lab technician'),(30,'jsearch','Q36hZCO_3oabVQUDAAAAAA==','Laboratory Assistant – Hospital Lab (Entry-Level)','Medical Associates Diagnostic Services','Portmore','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/laboratory-assistant-hospital-lab-entry-level/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nMedical Associates Diagnostic Services, a division of the esteemed Medical Associates Hospital, is a leading provider of comprehensive diagnostic solutions across Jamaica. For decades, we have been committed to delivering precise, timely, and reliable diagnostic results, playing a crucial role in patient care and public health. Our state-of-the-art facilities, combined with a team of dedicated professionals, ensure that we maintain the highest standards of quality and service. We believe in fostering an environment of learning, growth, and mutual respect, where every team member contributes to our mission of advancing healthcare through excellence in diagnostics. Join us and become part of a legacy of medical innovation and compassionate service.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a highly motivated and detail-oriented individual looking to launch your career in a dynamic hospital laboratory setting? Medical Associates Diagnostic Services in Greater Portmore is seeking an enthusiastic and dedicated Entry-Level Laboratory Assistant to join our growing team. This is a fantastic opportunity for someone eager to learn and contribute to vital diagnostic processes that impact patient lives daily. As a Laboratory Assistant, you will play a crucial supporting role in ensuring the efficient and accurate operation of our clinical laboratory. You will be instrumental in the pre-analytical phase of testing, handling specimens with utmost care and precision, and maintaining a sterile and organized work environment. This entry-level position is designed for individuals who are passionate about healthcare and possess a foundational understanding of laboratory principles. We offer comprehensive on-the-job training and mentorship to equip you with the skills and knowledge needed to excel in this role and potentially advance your career within our organization. If you are meticulous, responsible, a quick learner, and thrive in a collaborative team setting, we encourage you to apply. Your contribution will directly support our medical technologists and pathologists in delivering accurate results that guide critical medical decisions, ultimately enhancing patient outcomes.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Receive, label, and log patient specimens (blood, urine, tissue, etc.) accurately and efficiently upon arrival.\n• Prepare specimens for testing, which may include centrifugation, aliquoting, and distribution to appropriate testing stations.\n• Maintain laboratory equipment and instruments by performing routine cleaning and calibration checks under supervision.\n• Ensure strict adherence to all laboratory safety protocols, including the proper handling and disposal of biohazardous materials.\n• Manage and organize laboratory supplies, inventory, and assist with ordering new stock.\n• Perform basic clerical tasks such as data entry, filing, and answering departmental calls.\n• Assist medical technologists with general laboratory duties as needed.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and sterile work environment according to established guidelines.\n• Adhere to all quality control procedures and participate in quality assurance activities.\n• Communicate effectively with colleagues and other healthcare professionals to ensure smooth workflow.\n\nRequired Skills\n• High school diploma or equivalent (CXC/GCE O\'Levels, including Science subjects, preferred).\n• Strong attention to detail and accuracy in all tasks.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills.\n• Basic computer proficiency (Microsoft Office Suite).\n• Ability to follow instructions meticulously and work independently as well as part of a team.\n• Strong verbal and written communication skills.\n• A keen interest in laboratory science and healthcare.\n• Ability to handle sensitive patient information with confidentiality and professionalism.\n• Physical stamina to stand for extended periods and lift light laboratory equipment/supplies.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Completed a science-related course or subject at the CAPE/A\'Level standard.\n• Previous volunteer or observational experience in a clinical or research laboratory setting.\n• Knowledge of medical terminology.\n• Familiarity with laboratory information systems (LIS).\n• Certification in Basic Life Support (BLS).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package and benefits.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness programs.\n• Opportunities for professional development and career advancement.\n• Supportive and collaborative team environment.\n• On-the-job training and mentorship from experienced professionals.\n• Contribution to a vital service that positively impacts community health.\n• Employee assistance program.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nClick on the application link below to submit your resume and cover letter. Ensure your application highlights your enthusiasm for laboratory work, your commitment to precision, and how you align with our mission of providing exceptional diagnostic services.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'diagnostic,laboratory,medical,patient,healthcare,medical associates,laboratory assistant,hospital,associates,assistant,diagnostic services,testing,specimens,service,services,associates diagnostic,job training,team,technologists,clinical,medical technologists,professionals,delivering,care,sterile'),(31,'jsearch','IVxYcaiA1R5nT7eTAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Runaway Bay','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-7/','About Company\n\nCareer.zycto is more than just a company; it\'s a launchpad for scientific careers. Here, aspiring lab technicians discover an environment where curiosity is celebrated, and foundational research drives real-world impact. We believe in nurturing talent from the ground up, providing comprehensive training and mentorship within our cutting-edge R&D facilities. Join us and contribute to groundbreaking projects, gaining invaluable hands-on experience that will define your professional journey. At Career.zycto, your scientific aspirations find their true home, fostering innovation with every experiment.\n\nJob Description\n\nEmbark on an exciting scientific journey with Career.zycto as an Entry-Level Lab Technician in our dynamic Research & Development department. This is a unique opportunity for an enthusiastic and detail-oriented individual to kickstart their career in a supportive and innovative environment. As a key member of our R&D team, you will contribute directly to groundbreaking scientific discoveries and product development, working alongside experienced researchers and scientists. We are seeking a proactive individual with a foundational understanding of laboratory practices and a keen interest in experimental science. You will be instrumental in executing experiments, meticulous data collection, and ensuring the smooth operation of our state-of-the-art laboratory facilities. This role provides comprehensive training, mentorship, and a clear pathway for professional growth in the scientific field. If you are passionate about contributing to the advancement of knowledge, possess a strong work ethic, and are eager to learn and develop new skills in a fast-paced R&D setting, we encourage you to apply. This position is perfect for recent graduates or individuals with limited lab experience who are ready to dive into the world of scientific research and make a tangible impact.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Perform routine laboratory experiments and tests under supervision, following established protocols and safety guidelines.\n• Prepare chemical reagents, solutions, and media with accuracy and precision.\n• Maintain, calibrate, and troubleshoot laboratory equipment, ensuring optimal functionality and cleanliness.\n• Accurately record and document experimental data, observations, and results in laboratory notebooks and digital systems.\n• Assist senior researchers in the setup and execution of more complex experimental procedures.\n• Manage laboratory inventory, including ordering supplies, receiving shipments, and organizing stock.\n• Ensure strict adherence to all health, safety, and environmental regulations and best practices.\n• Conduct literature reviews and assist in data analysis as required.\n• Contribute to the general upkeep and organization of the laboratory space.\n• Participate in team meetings and contribute to discussions regarding experimental design and results.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Associate\'s degree or Diploma in a scientific discipline (e.g., Chemistry, Biology, Biochemistry, Medical Technology, or related field).\n• Basic understanding of general laboratory techniques and safety procedures.\n• Proficiency in using standard laboratory equipment (e.g., pipettes, pH meters, centrifuges).\n• Strong attention to detail and accuracy in experimental execution and data recording.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills.\n• Ability to follow written and verbal instructions precisely.\n• Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint).\n• Strong communication skills, both written and verbal.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in a relevant scientific field.\n• Previous hands-on experience in an academic or industrial laboratory setting (even through internships or coursework).\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) or similar quality systems.\n• Experience with basic statistical analysis software.\n• A demonstrated interest in research and development.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Opportunities for continuous learning and professional development.\n• Mentorship from experienced scientists and researchers.\n• Access to state-of-the-art laboratory equipment and technologies.\n• Vibrant and collaborative work environment.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Employee assistance program.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting Entry-Level Lab Technician role, please click on the application link below. Ensure your resume and a cover letter detailing your interest in scientific research and relevant skills are attached. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'laboratory,scientific,research,experimental,journey career,development,lab,skills,contribute,comprehensive training,training mentorship,execution,data,career,scientific research,career zycto,zycto,experience,art laboratory,journey,general,researchers,field,art,state art'),(32,'jsearch','pLHzHlSjA63JPHdrAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-46/','About Company\n\nImagine launching your scientific career in a place where curiosity is championed, and every experiment pushes the boundaries of possibility. Career.zycto is a dynamic force in biotechnology research, dedicated to pioneering innovative solutions that impact lives. We believe in fostering a collaborative environment where fresh perspectives thrive, making us the perfect launchpad for aspiring lab technicians. Join our mission to transform discovery into tangible progress, working alongside experienced mentors who are eager to guide your development. Your journey into cutting-edge science starts here, shaping the future with every test and analysis.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a recent graduate or an ambitious individual with a foundational understanding of laboratory practices and a burning passion for scientific discovery? Career.zycto is seeking an enthusiastic and meticulous Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative Research & Development team in Ingleside, Mandeville. This is an unparalleled opportunity to kickstart your career in a vibrant, supportive environment where learning and growth are paramount. You will play a crucial role in supporting our cutting-edge research projects, contributing directly to experiments that aim to develop novel products and solutions.\n\nIn this hands-on position, you will be instrumental in the daily operations of our R&D lab, performing a variety of tasks from preparing samples and running analytical tests to maintaining laboratory equipment and documenting results. We are looking for someone who demonstrates exceptional attention to detail, a strong commitment to accuracy, and an eagerness to master new techniques and methodologies. While this is an entry-level role, your contributions will be valued and directly impact the progression of our research initiatives. You will work closely with senior scientists and experienced technicians, gaining invaluable mentorship and practical experience that will lay a solid foundation for your professional development in the biotechnology sector. This role offers a unique chance to grow your skills, expand your scientific knowledge, and become an integral part of a team dedicated to pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare samples and reagents according to standard operating procedures (SOPs) for various R&D experiments.\n• Perform routine laboratory tests and analyses accurately and efficiently under supervision.\n• Operate and maintain a range of laboratory equipment, including calibration and basic troubleshooting.\n• Record, document, and organize experimental data and results meticulously in lab notebooks and electronic systems.\n• Assist senior researchers and technicians with experimental setups and complex analytical procedures.\n• Ensure strict adherence to safety protocols, quality control standards, and good laboratory practices (GLP).\n• Manage laboratory inventory, including ordering supplies and ensuring adequate stock levels.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe working environment within the R&D laboratory.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in a scientific discipline (e.g., Biology, Chemistry, Biochemistry, Biomedical Science).\n• Basic knowledge of laboratory techniques and safety procedures.\n• Proficiency in basic computer applications (Microsoft Office Suite).\n• Strong attention to detail and accuracy in performing tasks and documenting results.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team.\n• Good written and verbal communication skills.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Prior hands-on experience in a laboratory setting (academic or industrial, including internships).\n• Familiarity with specific analytical instruments (e.g., pH meters, spectrophotometers, centrifuges).\n• Understanding of Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP) or GLP principles.\n• Basic data analysis skills.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship from experienced scientists and technicians.\n• Collaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Paid time off and holidays.\n• Contribution to groundbreaking research and innovation.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to apply directly via the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant academic background, laboratory experience (if any), and any projects that demonstrate your passion for R&D. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to our team.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'laboratory,technicians,research,documenting results,development,skills,lab,scientific,career,documenting,biotechnology,basic,analytical,team,environment,directly,performing,experienced,good,including,invaluable mentorship,relevant academic,position instrumental,innovative solutions,mandeville unparalleled'),(33,'jsearch','qZVLrt2qX_PFdiuBAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-45/','About Company\n\nJoin a team that’s at the forefront of innovation! Career.zycto is a dynamic and forward-thinking organization dedicated to pioneering advancements across various sectors. We believe in fostering an environment where curiosity is celebrated, and scientific inquiry leads to groundbreaking discoveries. For an entry-level lab technician, this means unparalleled exposure to diverse projects, cutting-edge equipment, and mentorship opportunities that will shape your scientific career. We’re committed to developing our talent, ensuring every team member contributes meaningfully to our mission to push the boundaries of what\'s possible.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking a highly motivated and enthusiastic Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative Research & Development team in Anchovy, St. James. This is an exceptional opportunity for individuals eager to kick-start their career in a cutting-edge scientific environment, contributing directly to groundbreaking research and product development. As an integral part of our R&D department, you will work closely with experienced scientists and researchers, gaining invaluable hands-on experience with various laboratory techniques, equipment, and experimental protocols. Your role will be crucial in ensuring the smooth and efficient operation of our lab, supporting critical research initiatives that aim to solve complex challenges and bring new discoveries to life. We are looking for someone with a meticulous eye for detail, a strong commitment to laboratory safety, and an insatiable desire to learn and grow within a dynamic scientific setting. If you\'re passionate about science and ready to embark on a fulfilling career path where your contributions truly matter, we encourage you to apply and become a part of our pioneering team.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist senior scientists and researchers in conducting various experiments and research projects.\n• Prepare samples, reagents, and solutions according to standard operating procedures (SOPs).\n• Operate and maintain laboratory equipment, ensuring proper calibration and functionality.\n• Accurately record and document experimental data, observations, and results.\n• Perform routine laboratory tasks, including glassware washing, sterilization, and inventory management.\n• Adhere strictly to all laboratory safety protocols and good laboratory practices (GLP).\n• Troubleshoot minor equipment issues and report complex problems to supervisors.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe working environment.\n• Participate in team meetings and contribute to discussions on experimental design and results.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Strong foundational knowledge in chemistry, biology, or related scientific field.\n• Excellent attention to detail and manual dexterity.\n• Proficiency in basic laboratory techniques (e.g., pipetting, preparing solutions).\n• Ability to follow written and verbal instructions precisely.\n• Basic computer skills (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite).\n• Strong organizational and time management skills.\n• Commitment to laboratory safety and quality control.\n• Effective communication and teamwork abilities.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in Chemistry, Biology, Biochemistry, or a closely related scientific discipline.\n• Previous experience (academic or professional) in a laboratory setting.\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) and Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP).\n• Experience with data entry and basic statistical analysis.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship programs with experienced scientists.\n• State-of-the-art laboratory facilities.\n• A collaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Contribution to meaningful and impactful research.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo seize this exciting opportunity and join our innovative R&D team, please submit your resume and a compelling cover letter outlining your relevant experience and why you are the ideal candidate for this entry-level role. We encourage you to click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'laboratory,scientific,research,team,entry,career,commitment laboratory,laboratory safety,level,entry level,pioneering,discoveries,experience,equipment,environment,lab,development,chemistry biology,experimental,good,scientists,related scientific,various,lab technician,new discoveries'),(34,'jsearch','0np4AbeSJdLXSWogAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Browns Town','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-70/','About Company\n\nSeeking to launch your scientific career in a dynamic, innovative environment? At Career.zycto, we are a forward-thinking research and development firm committed to pushing the boundaries of scientific discovery. We pride ourselves on fostering a collaborative atmosphere where curiosity is encouraged, and new ideas are valued. For an entry-level Lab Technician, this means unparalleled opportunities to gain hands-on experience, learn from seasoned professionals, and contribute directly to projects that make a tangible impact. Join our team in Brown’s Town and grow with a company dedicated to scientific excellence and personal development, providing the perfect foundation for your professional journey.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is excited to announce an opening for an enthusiastic and dedicated Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our innovative Research & Development team in Brown’s Town, St. Ann. This is an exceptional opportunity for a recent graduate or an individual with foundational laboratory experience looking to embark on a fulfilling career in scientific research. As an integral part of our R&D department, you will play a crucial role in supporting our scientists and researchers in various ongoing projects, contributing to data collection, sample preparation, and routine lab maintenance.\n\nWe are looking for someone with a meticulous eye for detail, a strong commitment to laboratory safety protocols, and a genuine passion for scientific inquiry. You will gain invaluable practical experience with cutting-edge equipment and methodologies, working alongside experienced professionals who are eager to mentor and guide your growth. This role offers a unique chance to develop a robust skill set in a real-world research setting, making a tangible impact on our product development and scientific advancements. If you are eager to learn, proactive, and ready to contribute to ground-breaking research, we encourage you to apply and become a part of our pioneering team.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare samples and reagents according to established protocols and standard operating procedures (SOPs).\n• Perform routine laboratory tests and analyses under supervision, accurately recording observations and results.\n• Operate and maintain laboratory equipment, ensuring proper calibration and functionality.\n• Assist senior scientists and researchers with experimental setup and data collection.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory environment, adhering strictly to health and safety regulations.\n• Inventory and order laboratory supplies and consumables, ensuring adequate stock levels.\n• Document experimental procedures, results, and findings meticulously in lab notebooks and digital systems.\n• Participate in team meetings and contribute to discussions regarding project progress and challenges.\n• Support quality control and assurance processes for laboratory materials and products.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Associate’s degree or Diploma in a scientific discipline (e.g., Chemistry, Biology, Biochemistry, Medical Technology).\n• Basic understanding of laboratory techniques and safety procedures.\n• Proficiency in basic computer applications (MS Office Suite).\n• Excellent attention to detail and strong organizational skills.\n• Ability to follow instructions precisely and work methodically.\n• Strong communication skills, both written and verbal.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Previous experience in a laboratory setting (academic or industrial, including internships).\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP).\n• Experience with specific analytical instruments (e.g., pH meters, spectrophotometers).\n• A proactive attitude towards learning new techniques and technologies.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and training.\n• Mentorship programs for entry-level professionals.\n• Collaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Modern, well-equipped laboratory facilities.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n• Pension scheme contributions.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your academic background, any relevant lab experience, and your passion for research and development.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'laboratory,scientific,research,development,brown town,brown,team brown,experience,lab,town,professionals,team,research development,entry,entry level,career,level,tangible impact,data collection,contribute,lab technician,pride fostering,processes laboratory,proactive ready,pension scheme'),(35,'jsearch','AqjZsGTaid2E3ZR8AAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Ewarton','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-28/','About Company\n\nAre you eager to launch your scientific career in a dynamic, supportive environment? Career.zycto provides unparalleled opportunities for budding scientists to thrive. We are a forward-thinking organization dedicated to pioneering advancements through rigorous research and development. Join a team where curiosity is celebrated, and every experiment contributes to meaningful innovation. At Career.zycto, we believe in nurturing talent, offering mentorship, and providing the resources necessary for an entry-level Lab Technician to grow, learn, and make a tangible impact from day one. Discover your potential with us.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented individual to join our Research & Development team as an Entry-Level Lab Technician. This is a foundational role perfect for someone passionate about science and eager to kickstart their career in a vibrant R&D setting. You will play a vital role in supporting our ongoing scientific investigations, directly contributing to the success of innovative projects. This position offers an unparalleled opportunity to develop essential laboratory skills, work collaboratively with experienced researchers, and immerse yourself in the world of scientific discovery. The ideal candidate will possess an insatiable curiosity, a meticulous eye for detail, and a commitment to high standards. You will assist in experimental setup, meticulous data collection, and preliminary analysis, all while strictly adhering to safety and quality protocols. This role is a fantastic stepping stone, offering significant growth and advancement opportunities within the scientific field, making a real impact on our groundbreaking work.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Perform routine laboratory tests and analyses accurately under supervision.\n• Prepare reagents, solutions, and media following established protocols and specifications.\n• Maintain precise and detailed records of experiments, observations, and results in lab notebooks and electronic systems.\n• Operate, calibrate, and maintain various laboratory equipment to ensure optimal functionality and accuracy.\n• Assist in the setup and breakdown of experimental apparatus, ensuring readiness for research activities.\n• Strictly adhere to laboratory safety regulations, waste disposal procedures, and quality control guidelines.\n• Monitor, order, receive, and inventory laboratory supplies and materials, ensuring adequate stock levels.\n• Collaborate effectively with team members, providing support and contributing to a cohesive work environment.\n• Contribute to maintaining a clean, organized, and efficient laboratory environment.\n• Conduct basic data entry and assist with preliminary analysis of experimental results.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Strong foundational knowledge in a relevant scientific discipline (e.g., Biology, Chemistry, Biotechnology).\n• Excellent attention to detail and accuracy in performing laboratory tasks.\n• Ability to follow complex instructions and scientific protocols precisely.\n• Basic proficiency in using common laboratory equipment (e.g., pipettes, centrifuges, pH meters).\n• Solid organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks.\n• Effective verbal and written communication skills for documentation and team collaboration.\n• A strong commitment to laboratory safety, ethical research practices, and quality assurance.\n• Ability to work both independently and collaboratively as an integral part of a research team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Previous hands-on experience in a laboratory setting, either through academic projects or internships.\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) and standard operating procedures.\n• Proficiency in basic data analysis software, such as Microsoft Excel or similar tools.\n• Knowledge of specific analytical techniques relevant to R&D, such as spectroscopy or chromatography.\n• A keen interest in scientific innovation, problem-solving, and continuous learning.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Abundant opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Structured mentorship program with experienced scientists and researchers.\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Access to cutting-edge laboratory facilities and advanced technology.\n• A collaborative, supportive, and intellectually stimulating work environment.\n• Performance-based bonuses and recognition programs.\n• Employee assistance programs and wellness initiatives.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting entry-level Lab Technician – Research & Development position, please click on the application link below to submit your resume and a compelling cover letter detailing your interest and relevant experience. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'laboratory,scientific,research,preliminary analysis,entry,preliminary,basic data,lab,work,team,development,lab technician,research development,setup,offering,technician,entry level,career,level,collaboratively,environment,skills,relevant,analysis,experimental'),(36,'jsearch','UhQy_BispGPeRnvEAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Chapelton','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-4/','About Company\n\nJoin Career.zycto, a vibrant hub of innovation dedicated to pushing the boundaries of scientific discovery. We foster an environment where curiosity is celebrated, and every team member, even at the entry-level, contributes meaningfully to groundbreaking research. For an aspiring Lab Technician, this means unparalleled learning opportunities, direct involvement in exciting projects, and a chance to grow your expertise alongside seasoned professionals. We believe in empowering our talent to make a real impact from day one, nurturing the next generation of scientific leaders in a collaborative and supportive setting.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a detail-oriented, enthusiastic individual with a passion for scientific exploration? Career.zycto is seeking a highly motivated Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our dynamic Research & Development team in Chapelton, Clarendon. This is an incredible opportunity for someone just starting their career to gain hands-on experience in a cutting-edge laboratory environment. You will play a crucial role in supporting our research initiatives, working alongside experienced scientists and contributing to projects that aim to innovate and create