w to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to click on the application link below to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their qualifications and interest in this entry-level Lab Technician position.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'scientific,research,laboratory,lab,team,advancements,senior technicians,scientific advancements,guidance,work,development,projects,lab technician,preparation,technician,entry,entry level,level,data,career,technicians,collaborative supportive,chance,environment,laboratory environment'),(37,'jsearch','KzVlciTaJ7CX6HXHAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-48/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nKickstart your scientific career with Career.zycto, a dynamic organization dedicated to fostering innovation and scientific discovery right here in Gordon Town. For an aspiring lab technician, we offer a unique blend of hands-on experience and mentorship within a collaborative R&D environment. Join a team passionate about pushing the boundaries of knowledge, providing an unparalleled opportunity to apply your academic learning to real-world challenges from day one. Our commitment to growth ensures that entry-level professionals receive the support and resources needed to develop essential skills and make tangible contributions to groundbreaking projects. Career.zycto values curiosity and dedication, making it the perfect launchpad for your professional journey in research.\n\nJob Description\n\nThis role is for an enthusiastic and meticulous individual eager to embark on a career in scientific research and development. As an Entry-Level Lab Technician at Career.zycto, you will be an integral part of our R&D team, contributing to cutting-edge projects from their initial experimental phases through data analysis. This position offers an unparalleled opportunity to gain hands-on experience in a dynamic laboratory setting, working alongside experienced scientists and researchers. You will be responsible for preparing samples, maintaining laboratory equipment, executing routine experiments, and accurately recording observations. We are looking for someone with a foundational understanding of laboratory techniques and a strong desire to learn and grow within a fast-paced scientific environment.\n\nYour day-to-day activities will involve a variety of tasks crucial to the smooth operation of our research initiatives. This includes ensuring the laboratory adheres to stringent safety protocols, managing inventory of reagents and supplies, and performing quality control checks on experiments. We value precision, attention to detail, and a proactive approach to problem-solving. While this is an entry-level role, your contributions will directly impact our ability to innovate and deliver impactful scientific outcomes. Career.zycto is committed to providing a supportive and collaborative workplace where curiosity is encouraged, and professional development is a priority. If you are passionate about science, possess a diligent work ethic, and are ready to apply your academic knowledge in a practical, impactful way, we encourage you to apply and grow with us. This position is a fantastic stepping stone for a long and successful career in research and development, offering exposure to diverse scientific methodologies and the opportunity to specialize in areas of particular interest as you develop your expertise. We believe in nurturing talent and providing the tools and guidance necessary for our team members to thrive.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Prepare reagents, solutions, and samples according to established protocols and safety guidelines.\n• Perform routine laboratory experiments and tests, accurately recording data and observations.\n• Maintain and calibrate laboratory equipment, ensuring proper functionality and cleanliness.\n• Assist in the collection, organization, and basic analysis of experimental data.\n• Adhere strictly to laboratory safety procedures and quality control standards.\n• Manage and monitor laboratory supplies and inventory, placing orders as needed.\n• Document experimental procedures and results thoroughly and precisely in lab notebooks or digital systems.\n• Collaborate with senior technicians and researchers to optimize experimental techniques.\n• Conduct basic troubleshooting of equipment and experimental issues.\n• Participate in team meetings and contribute to scientific discussions.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Foundational knowledge of basic laboratory techniques (e.g., pipetting, sterile technique, solution preparation).\n• Proficiency in using standard laboratory equipment.\n• Strong attention to detail and accuracy in performing tasks and recording data.\n• Excellent organizational and time management skills.\n• Ability to follow complex instructions and protocols precisely.\n• Basic computer skills, including familiarity with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel).\n• Strong communication skills, both written and verbal.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team.\n• A strong commitment to laboratory safety and ethical research practices.\n• Eagerness to learn and adapt to new techniques and methodologies.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Associate\'s degree or higher in a scientific field (e.g., Biology, Chemistry, Biochemistry, Medical Technology).\n• Previous experience in a laboratory setting (academic or industrial internships preferred).\n• Familiarity with specific analytical instruments (e.g., spectrophotometers, pH meters).\n• Basic understanding of Good Laboratory Practices (GLP).\n• Experience with data entry and basic statistical software.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive entry-level salary.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship program with experienced scientists.\n• Collaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Exposure to cutting-edge research and technology.\n• Paid time off and holidays.\n• Employee assistance program.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and interest in this role. Please ensure your application highlights your passion for scientific research and your ability to thrive in a collaborative laboratory setting. Click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'laboratory,scientific,research,career,entry,basic,experimental,day,entry level,level,data,zycto,career zycto,apply academic,apply,team,experience,skills,development,recording,accurately recording,recording data,program,techniques,providing'),(38,'jsearch','PZn3ghciG0J2FnHKAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','Old Harbour','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-6/','About Company\n\nAt Career.zycto, we\'re building the future of sustainable solutions right here in Old Harbour. We believe in fostering an environment where curiosity thrives and scientific exploration leads to tangible impact. For an aspiring Lab Technician, this means direct involvement in groundbreaking research from day one, working alongside seasoned professionals who are passionate about mentorship. Join a team dedicated to pushing boundaries, where your keen eye for detail and foundational scientific knowledge will be instrumental in driving our R&D initiatives forward and contributing to meaningful discoveries that shape tomorrow.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our dynamic Research & Development team in Old Harbour, St. Catherine. This is an exceptional opportunity for a recent graduate or an aspiring scientist eager to launch their career in a cutting-edge research environment. As a Lab Technician, you will play a crucial role in the daily operations of our laboratory, supporting various scientific projects aimed at innovation and discovery.\n\nIn this hands-on position, you will be responsible for executing a range of laboratory procedures, from preparing samples and reagents to performing routine analytical tests with precision and accuracy. You\'ll work closely with experienced scientists and researchers, gaining invaluable practical experience and contributing directly to the success of our R&D initiatives. We are looking for an individual with a strong foundational understanding of scientific principles, an unwavering commitment to laboratory safety, and an eagerness to learn and grow within a fast-paced setting.\n\nYou will be instrumental in maintaining the integrity and efficiency of our lab. This includes meticulously documenting experimental data, managing lab inventory, ensuring equipment is properly calibrated and maintained, and upholding stringent quality control standards. Your keen observational skills and ability to follow standard operating procedures will be vital in generating reliable and reproducible results. This role offers a unique chance to immerse yourself in real-world scientific challenges, develop specialized skills, and make tangible contributions to projects that have the potential to significantly impact our industry. Join us and become a part of a collaborative team dedicated to scientific excellence and groundbreaking innovation.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Perform routine laboratory tests and analyses accurately following established protocols.\n• Prepare samples, reagents, and solutions according to standard operating procedures (SOPs).\n• Operate, maintain, and calibrate various laboratory equipment and instruments.\n• Record experimental procedures, observations, and results meticulously in lab notebooks and electronic systems.\n• Assist senior researchers in experimental design, setup, and data collection.\n• Ensure strict adherence to all laboratory safety protocols, quality control standards, and regulatory guidelines.\n• Manage laboratory inventory, including tracking usage, ordering supplies, and maintaining organized stock.\n• Contribute to the overall cleanliness, organization, and efficient functioning of the laboratory workspace.\n• Participate actively in team meetings, brainstorming sessions, and scientific discussions.\n• Troubleshoot basic equipment issues and escalate complex problems to appropriate personnel.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Biology, Chemistry, Biochemistry, or a closely related scientific field.\n• Strong foundational knowledge of general laboratory techniques and scientific principles.\n• Proficiency in basic data entry and Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint).\n• Exceptional attention to detail and strong observational skills.\n• Ability to follow complex written and verbal instructions precisely.\n• Excellent communication skills, both written and verbal, for effective teamwork and documentation.\n• Capacity to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within a team environment.\n• A genuine passion for scientific research, curiosity, and a proactive attitude towards learning.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Prior hands-on experience in a laboratory setting (e.g., academic projects, internships, volunteer work).\n• Familiarity with specific analytical instruments such as spectrophotometers, pH meters, centrifuges, or chromatographs.\n• Basic knowledge of Good Laboratory Practices (GLP) or other relevant quality systems.\n• Understanding of basic statistical analysis for experimental data.\n• Eagerness to learn new scientific techniques, adapt to evolving research needs, and embrace challenges.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package.\n• Opportunities for professional development, training, and continuous learning.\n• Direct mentorship from experienced scientists and industry leaders.\n• Exposure to cutting-edge research projects and innovative technologies.\n• A collaborative, supportive, and intellectually stimulating work environment.\n• The chance to contribute to impactful scientific discoveries and advancements.\n• Health and wellness programs.\n• Generous paid time off and holidays.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to kickstart your career in scientific research? We encourage all qualified candidates to apply. Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and a compelling cover letter outlining your interest in this entry-level Lab Technician role and how your skills align with our mission. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'scientific,laboratory,research,lab,observational skills,old harbour,old,harbour,skills,observational,lab technician,technician,team,scientific principles,eagerness learn,projects,experimental,team dedicated,eagerness,data,entry,career,chance,industry,scientific research'),(39,'jsearch','URRRztuFF8wgxlWOAAAAAA==','Biology, Department of Applied Sciences and Professional Studies - Adjunct Faculty','University of Maryland Global Campus',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6998fcafda7696de2f59da04-biology-department-of-applied-sciences-and-professional-studies---adjunct-faculty?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America, United States\n\nAdjunct Faculty\n\nBiology\n\nDepartment of Applied Sciences and Professional Studies\n\nUMGC Stateside\n\nLocation: Stateside Remote\n\nUniversity of Maryland Global Campus (UMGC) seeks adjunct faculty to teach remotely for the Biology program.\n\nREQUIRED EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE:\n• Masters degree in Biology or related field from an accredited institution of higher learning.\n• Professional experience in Biology, Natural Science or related field.\n• Experience teaching adult learners online and in higher education is strongly preferred.\n• This position is specifically to teach remotely.\n\nMaterials needed for submission\n• Resume/Curriculum Vitae\n• Cover letter highly preferred\n• If selected, candidates with international degrees may be required to submit a translation/degree evaluation from a NACES approved vendor.\n\nWho We Are and Who We Serve\n\nUMGC—one of 12 degree-granting institutions in the University System of Maryland (USM)—is a mission-driven institution with seven core values that guide us in all we do. At the top of the list is \"Students First,” and we strive to do just that for our 90,000 students at home and abroad. From its start in 1947, UMGC has demonstrated its commitment to adult learners. We recognize that adult students need flexibility and options. UMGC is proud to be a global, 24-hour, institution of higher learning.\n\nThe typical UMGC student is an adult learner juggling a career, family, and other priorities. Roughly 80% work full time, half are parents, and half are minority students. They are continuing their education to better themselves, their families, and their professional opportunities. UMGC is also a leading higher education provider to the U.S. military, enrolling 55,000 active-duty service members, reservists, National Guard members, veterans, and family members annually. We are proud of our military heritage and are committed to this service.\n\nThe Adjunct Faculty Role at UMGC\n\nUMGC is committed to helping students achieve success not only with us, but also in their professional fields. As a result, we actively seek faculty members who are scholar-practitioners: professionals who are actively and successfully engaged in their field who additionally wish to help the next generation of professionals grow in their knowledge and expertise through education.\n\nYour role as an adjunct faculty member will be to:\n• Actively engage students through frequent interaction that motivates them to succeed, and conveys a genuine energy and enthusiasm for their learning.\n• Guide students in active collaboration and the application of their learning in problem- and project-based learning demonstrations.\n• Provide rich and regular constructive feedback, utilizing rubrics effectively for the assessment of student work, and acknowledging student accomplishments.\n• Demonstrate relevant and current subject-matter expertise, and help students connect concepts across their academic program.\n• Provide feedback to your program chair on possible curricular improvements.\n\nThe Biology Program at UMGC\n\nPlease visit Healthcare & Science | UMGC to learn more about this program, including its description, outcomes, and coursework.\n\nFaculty Training at UMGC\n\nWe are committed to your professional success at UMGC. Each new faculty member is required to successfully complete our online two-week new faculty orientation, FacDev 411, as a condition of hire.\n\nPosition Available and will Remain Open until Filled\n\nSalary Commensurate with Experience\n\nAll submissions should include a cover letter and resume.\n\nThe University of Maryland Global Campus (UMGC) is an equal opportunity employer and complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding nondiscrimination. UMGC is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all persons and does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, age, marital status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, disability, religion, ancestry, political affiliation or veteran status in employment, educational programs and activities, and admissions.\n\nWorkplace Accommodations:\n\nThe University of Maryland Global Campus Global Campus (UMGC) is committed to creating and maintaining a welcoming and inclusive working environment for people of all abilities. UMGC is dedicated to the principle that no qualified individual with a disability shall, based on disability, be excluded from participation in or be denied the benefits of the services, programs, or activities of the University, or be subjected to discrimination. For information about UMGC’s Reasonable Workplace Accommodation Policy or to request an accommodation, applicants/candidates can contact Employee Accommodations via email at employee-accommodations@umgc.edu.\n\nBenefits Package Highlights:\n• Health Coverage: Access to health care, medical with vision, dental, and prescription plans for both individuals and families, effective from the 1st of the month following your hire date. NOTE: Adjuncts are not eligible for the State of Maryland subsidized rates. Adjuncts would be responsible for the total cost if enrolled.\n• Insurance Options: Term Life Insurance and Accidental Death and Dismemberment Insurance.\n• Supplemental Retirement Plans: include 401(k), 403(b), 457(b), and various Roth options. The university does not provide matching funds.\n\nFor additional information please see: SS Adjunct Faculty_2020.pdf (umgc.edu)\n\nHiring Range by Rank and Degree:\n\nInstructor: No Terminal Degree: Step 1 $806 - Step 11 $1,050 per credit hour\n\nAssistant Adjunct Professor: No Terminal Degree Step 1 $877 - Step 11 $1,127 per credit hour\n\nAssistant Adjunct Professor: Terminal Degree Step 1 $1,023 - Step 11 $1,288 per credit hour\n\nAssociate Adjunct Professor: No Terminal Degree Step 1 $947 - Step 11 $1,205 per credit hour\n\nAssociate Adjunct Professor: Terminal Degree Step 1 $1,202 - Step 11 $1,483 per credit hour\n\nAdjunct Professor: No Terminal Degree Step 1 $1,023 - Step 11 $1,288 per credit hour\n\nAdjunct Professor: Terminal Degree Step 1 $1,347 - Step 11 $1,645 per credit hour\nThis offer from \"University of Maryland Global Campus\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 79% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'umgc,step,adjunct,faculty,students,hour,degree,credit hour,credit,degree step,terminal degree,university,step 11,11,terminal,adjunct professor,professor terminal,adjunct faculty,biology,maryland,professor,university maryland,program,global campus,campus'),(40,'jsearch','3a_cL99VTNxPrD9RAAAAAA==','Scientist – Research Lab (Experienced)','Seprod Group','Port Antonio','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/scientist-research-lab-experienced/','About Company\n\nSeprod Group is a leading Jamaican manufacturing and distribution powerhouse, deeply embedded in the nation\'s economic fabric for over 80 years. We are committed to producing high-quality food, beverage, and agricultural products that nourish communities and drive local industry. Our success is built on a foundation of innovation, sustainability, and a relentless pursuit of excellence, constantly investing in research and development to create products that meet evolving consumer needs and global standards. Joining Seprod means becoming part of a legacy dedicated to growth, community impact, and shaping the future of Jamaican industry, fostering an environment where scientific curiosity and practical application thrive.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you an ambitious and experienced research scientist eager to apply your expertise in a dynamic lab environment? Seprod Group, a cornerstone of Jamaican industry, is seeking a highly motivated Scientist to join our dedicated Research Lab team in Bryan’s Bay, Port Antonio. This is a pivotal role where your scientific acumen will directly contribute to the innovation and quality control of our diverse product portfolio, spanning food, beverages, and agricultural inputs. You will be instrumental in designing and executing complex experiments, analyzing critical data, and translating findings into tangible improvements and new product developments that reach countless homes across the region.\n\nAs an Experienced Research Lab Scientist, you will be at the forefront of our R&D initiatives, working on projects that range from enhancing product shelf-life and nutritional value to exploring novel ingredients and sustainable processing methods. Your day-to-day will involve hands-on laboratory work, sophisticated data interpretation, and collaborative problem-solving within a multidisciplinary team. We are looking for a professional who thrives on challenge, possesses a meticulous approach to scientific investigation, and is passionate about driving meaningful impact through applied research. This position offers a unique opportunity to grow your career within a reputable organization that values scientific rigor, continuous learning, and fostering a culture of innovation. You will play a key role in developing new testing methodologies, validating analytical procedures, and ensuring compliance with national and international quality standards. The ability to mentor junior staff, present technical data clearly, and manage multiple projects simultaneously will be essential for success in this demanding yet rewarding role. If you are ready to elevate your career and contribute to a legacy of quality and excellence, we invite you to explore this exciting opportunity. We expect you to maintain impeccable laboratory standards, adhere to all safety protocols, and contribute to a thriving, collaborative scientific community focused on pushing boundaries and delivering results.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, execute, and analyze complex laboratory experiments and research projects related to product development, quality improvement, and process optimization.\n• Develop and validate new analytical methods and procedures for testing raw materials, in-process samples, and finished products.\n• Interpret and present scientific data and research findings clearly and concisely to internal stakeholders, including management and cross-functional teams.\n• Operate and maintain sophisticated laboratory equipment, ensuring calibration and troubleshooting as needed.\n• Prepare comprehensive technical reports, research papers, and documentation in accordance with scientific standards and regulatory guidelines.\n• Ensure strict adherence to all laboratory safety protocols, quality control standards (e.g., ISO, HACCP), and Good Laboratory Practices (GLP).\n• Collaborate with production, quality assurance, and marketing teams to translate research insights into commercially viable products.\n• Stay abreast of scientific advancements, emerging technologies, and industry trends to inform research strategies.\n• Provide guidance and mentorship to junior lab technicians and scientists, fostering a culture of learning and continuous improvement.\n• Manage multiple research projects concurrently, ensuring timely completion and adherence to project objectives and budgets.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Master\'s degree in Food Science, Chemistry, Biochemistry, Microbiology, or a related scientific field.\n• Minimum of 4 years of hands-on experience in a research and development or quality control laboratory setting, preferably within the food, beverage, or agricultural industry.\n• Proven expertise in experimental design, data analysis, and statistical interpretation.\n• Proficiency in operating and maintaining standard laboratory equipment (e.g., HPLC, GC, spectrophotometers, pH meters, rheometers).\n• Strong understanding of GLP, HACCP, ISO standards, and food safety regulations.\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills for technical reporting and presentations.\n• Demonstrated problem-solving abilities and critical thinking.\n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Ph.D. in a relevant scientific discipline.\n• Experience with LIMS (Laboratory Information Management System) software.\n• Knowledge of sensory evaluation techniques and consumer testing methodologies.\n• Familiarity with sustainable practices and green chemistry principles.\n• Project management experience in a scientific research context.\n• Publications in peer-reviewed journals or patents.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Retirement savings plan (pension scheme).\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Employee discount programs on company products.\n• A dynamic and supportive work environment.\n• Contribution to impactful national and regional initiatives.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting opportunity, please submit your detailed resume and a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and why you are the ideal candidate for this role. Encourage applicants to click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'laboratory,research,scientific,standards,quality,food,lab,products,projects,agricultural,safety,learning,seprod,ensuring,experienced,jamaican,quality control,research lab,contribute,data,innovation,new,testing,control,continuous'),(41,'jsearch','wXRc_D1caTaeov3yAAAAAA==','Quality Assurance Analyst','Contax 360 BPO Solutions','Montego Bay','JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Quality-Assurance-Analyst-Job-226893.aspx','Contax360 BPO Solutions Inc , a leading provider of global contact center solutions and a dynamic, focused and upwardly mobile organization; seeks qualified and professional individuals to join our team. Now hiring for our Montego Bay, Jamaica Office: Quality Assurance Analyst Job Summary: The Quality Analyst (QA) is responsible for assessing the quality of the performance of our call center agents who deal with our existing and potential customers. The QA will monitor inbound and outbound call responses to assess agents’ demeanor, accuracy, performance, and conformity to company policies and procedures. This individual will assist in developing, creating and implementing call center quality processes and procedures; as well as making recommendation for enhancements. Specific Duties: Performs call monitoring and provides trend data to site management team. Uses quality monitoring data management system to compile and track performance at team and individual level. Participates in customer and client listening programs to identify customer needs and expectations. Provides actionable data to various internal support groups as needed. Coordinates and facilitates call calibration sessions for call center staff. Provides feedback to call center team leaders and managers. Prepares and analyzes internal and external quality reports for management staff review. Assists the supervisor with the preparation and administering of training sessions. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications : Minimum of 5CXC’s (including English Language and Mathematics) along with relevant experience. Post secondary degree preferred. Required Experience : Minimum 2-3 years knowledge and experience particularly in a Call Center environment as a QA or Supervisor Prior face-to-face sales/telesales would be an asset Required Competencies : Strong mentoring and relationship building skills with the ability to effectively manage group and interpersonal conflict situations. Proficiency in the use of computer software applications including Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Excellent teamwork and interpersonal skills. Strong analytical and problem solving skills. Ability to work under pressure and without constant supervision. Excellent oral and written communication skills Ability to work on own initiative. Ability at planning and coordinating activities. Ability to demonstrate tact, confidentiality and professionalism in the execution of duties. All applicants should be 18 years or older and must have a valid Government issued photo ID, TRN & NIS. Successful candidates must be able to furnish a clean police record and pass an employment background check prior to starting. Only short-listed applicants will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'center,quality,provides,ability,duties,face,supervisor,interpersonal,prior,data,team,skills ability,skills,individual,qa,analyst,solutions,staff,internal,applicants,assurance analyst,years,including,minimum,required'),(42,'jsearch','kmnvRqeFlHufXhsLAAAAAA==','Quality Analyst – Kingston, Jamaica','Fusion CX',NULL,NULL,0,'https://careers.fusioncx.com/job/quality-analyst-kingston-jamaica/','Are you passionate about quality and performance? Do you thrive in an environment that values both individual contributions and team collaboration? Fusion CX is looking for a Quality Analyst to join our dynamic team in Kingston, Jamaica. As a QA, you will be instrumental in ensuring that our Customer Service Associates (CSA) meet the highest quality standards. This is a fantastic opportunity for professionals looking to make an impact in a global company where career growth, innovation, and customer satisfaction come together. If you’re seeking quality analyst jobs in Kingston, Jamaica, where you can contribute to something meaningful and take your career to the next level, Fusion CX is the place for you! Apply now!\nJob Description\n\nAs a quality analyst, you will be responsible for closely monitoring all calls handled by customer service associates to ensure strict adherence to quality and compliance standards. In this role, the quality analyst will collaborate with and support the Team Leader in coaching agents, providing feedback, and driving continuous development for overall success.\n\nKey responsibilities of the quality analyst in Kingston, Jamaica:\n• Monitor Agent Performance: Observe and assess Agent calls on a daily basis, both remotely and through side-by-side sessions, ensuring quality standards are met.\n• Coach & Develop Agents: Provide ongoing coaching and constructive feedback based on monitored calls to foster agent improvement and success.\n• Provide Insights & Recommendations: Collaborate with Team Leaders (TLs), Senior Team Leaders (STLs), Project Managers (PMs), and Operations Managers (OMs) to identify opportunities for account-specific improvements.\n• Track & Evaluate Performance: Consistently track and evaluate calls to ensure performance metrics and quality standards are being achieved.\n• Participate in Training & Calibration: Attend training sessions, team meetings, and calibration activities to maintain alignment with company standards and client expectations.\n• Report & Analyze Trends: Evaluate and report on call scores, identifying trends and areas of improvement on a daily basis.\n• Achieve Goals: Strive to meet and exceed departmental and client-specific goals and KPIs.\n• Handle Audit Requests & Projects: Complete audit requests and assist with quality-related projects as needed.\n• Conduct High-Level Evaluations: Ensure timely completion of high-level call evaluations and audits in accordance with quality standards.\n\nJob Requirements\n\nRequired skills and attributes required to excel in the role of the quality analyst in Kingston, Jamaica:\n• Educational Qualification: A bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience is required.\n• Quality Assurance Experience: Previous experience in Quality Assurance and working in a contact center environment is essential.\n• Strong Communication Skills: Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present findings clearly and effectively.\n• Customer-Centric Attitude: A strong focus on delivering customer satisfaction and maintaining high service quality.\n• Collaborative Mindset: Ability to work effectively within a team environment, sharing knowledge and supporting colleagues.\n• Fast-Paced Adaptability: Capable of thriving in a dynamic, high-pressure environment.\n• Performance-Driven: Strong desire to meet and exceed measurable performance goals and KPIs.\n• Self-motivation: Highly self-driven with a proactive approach to work and continuous improvement.\n• Time Management & Organization: Strong ability to manage time effectively and stay organized in a fast-paced setting.\n• Reporting & Analytical Skills: Proficient in tracking, analyzing, and reporting on performance data.\n• Presentation Skills: Strong ability to present findings and insights in a clear and compelling way to various stakeholders.\n• Technical Proficiency: Must possess experience in Microsoft Office Suite, especially Excel and PowerPoint.\n\nWhy Join Fusion CX?\n\nAt Fusion CX, we are committed to fostering an environment where our employees are empowered, supported, and highly valued. By joining us as a quality analyst in Kingston, Jamaica, you will become a key player in a growing global team that thrives on collaboration and professional development. Fusion CX dedicates major resources to your career advancement, innovation, and building an inclusive culture to nurture your growth.\n\nIf you are looking for QA jobs in Kingston, Jamaica, or quality analyst jobs in Jamaica, look no further; join us at Fusion CX. Enjoy endless opportunities to grow, develop new skills, and contribute to a company that values its people, and be part of a dynamic organization where your contributions will make a lasting impact.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'quality,quality analyst,fusion,fusion cx,cx,kingston,kingston jamaica,analyst,jamaica,analyst kingston,team,career,jobs,looking,performance,quality standards,customer,standards,calls,skills,dynamic,environment,high,join,strong'),(43,'jsearch','9hHI9JScg38BDSYTAAAAAA==','Quality Analyst','Optimum',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/quality-analyst-at-optimum-4371657486','Job Summary\n\nWe are seeking a detail-oriented Quality Analyst to ensure the highest standards of quality in our products, services, or processes. The ideal candidate will be responsible for evaluating, monitoring, and improving workflows, identifying areas for enhancement, and ensuring compliance with company and industry standards.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Analyze processes, products, and services to identify quality issues and areas for improvement.\n• Develop and implement quality control systems, test cases, and performance metrics.\n• Conduct audits, inspections, and reviews to ensure compliance with company and regulatory requirements.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to improve efficiency and quality.\n• Document and report defects, errors, and non-compliance issues with corrective action plans.\n• Perform root cause analysis and suggest preventive measures to minimize future errors.\n• Provide training and guidance to teams on quality assurance best practices.\n• Stay updated with industry trends, tools, and best practices related to quality assurance.\n\nQualifications\n\nRequirements:\n• Proven experience in a Quality Analyst, Quality Assurance, or related role.\n• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n• Experience with quality management systems (QMS) and methodologies such as\n• Six Sigma, Lean, or ISO standards.\n• Proficiency in data analysis, reporting, and quality monitoring tools.\n• Excellent communication and documentation skills.\n• Attention to detail and a commitment to continuous improvement.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'quality,quality analyst,compliance company,errors,tools,products services,services,best practices,analyst,areas,industry,issues,practices,teams,products,systems,analysis,standards,improvement,best,compliance,monitoring,quality assurance,assurance,suggest'),(44,'jsearch','hvU06naIaVx55DB4AAAAAA==','Bilingual Quality Assurance Analyst (English & Spanish)','Centerfield',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Bilingual-Quality-Assurance-Analyst-English-Job-226178.aspx','Purpose: The Quality Assurance Analyst ensures that all calls meet quality and compliance standards while supporting agent development. This role requires fluency in Spanish and English to evaluate interactions across both languages and maintain alignment with client policies and procedures. Key Responsibilities: Monitor and evaluate agent calls daily in both English and Spanish. Meet departmental and client evaluation goals. Communicate effectively with the QA team to maintain consistent processes. Provide coaching and feedback to agents based on monitored calls. Track and document evaluations, scores, and trends. Use company software to locate and review call recordings. Attend training sessions, meetings, and calibrations as needed. Report daily production, scores, and trends. Build strong relationships with account managers, supervisors, and team leads. Complete audits and quality-related projects as assigned. Ensure timely completion of high-level evaluations. Maintain punctuality and reliability. Required Skills & Qualifications: Fluency in Spanish and English (written and spoken). Established experience in Quality Assurance and contact center environment. Strong communication skills and attention to detail. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and meet performance goals. Tech-savvy with intermediate computer skills. Strong time management and organizational skills. Preferred Skills : One (1) year experience in contact center Sales Advanced Excel and intermediate PowerPoint skills. Familiarity with speech analytics software. Reporting and presentation skills.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'spanish,skills,english,calls,quality,meet,fluency spanish,english spanish,spanish english,fluency,maintain,intermediate,scores trends,scores,evaluate,evaluations,daily,assurance analyst,agent,strong,center,contact,contact center,client,goals'),(45,'jsearch','EGE53cLEEivlDMxNAAAAAA==','Quality Assurance Analyst','Centerfield','Montego Bay','JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/quality-assurance-analyst-at-centerfield-4357456859','Hi, We\'re Centerfield!\n\nSupercharged customer acquisition. Centerfield delivers outcome-based digital marketing solutions and personalized omnichannel experiences for the world’s leading brands. Powered by our proprietary Dugout platform, Centerfield acquires customers at scale for leading residential service, insurance, e-commerce, and B2B brands. Centerfield’s digital experiences and digital brands, such as Business.com and BroadbandNow.com, reach more than 150 million in-market shoppers annually. Centerfield is headquartered in Silicon Beach and is proud to be recognized by Built in LA as a Best Place to Work in Los Angeles.\n\nThe fundamental purpose of a Quality Assurance Analyst (QA) is to ensure that quality and compliance guidelines are achieved on all calls taken from each agent at Centerfield Media. The QA will also make sure that agents, supervisors, team leads and other necessary departments are updated with client policies and procedures. One of the key objectives of a QA is to establish a transparent, professional and respectful relationship with account supervisors and team leads in an attempt to assure that agents are provided with the development and coaching that they need.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Monitor/evaluate agent calls daily.\n• Meet departmental and/or provider evaluation goals.\n• Effectively communicate with other members of the Quality team regarding strategies, processes and procedures to ensure consistent productivity.\n• Coach and develop agents on calls monitored.\n• Track and document calls monitored, evaluation scores and trends on a daily basis.\n• Utilize company software to locate calls and listen to call recordings.\n• Attend trainings, meetings or calibrations to ensure that they are aligned (as needed).\n• Report daily production, scores, trends and other activities completed at that time.\n• Proactively establish healthy relationships with account managers, supervisors, team leads and agents.\n• Complete audit requests and quality related projects (as needed).\n• Satisfy high-level call evaluations/audits in a timely fashion.\n• Prove reliable and punctual as it pertains to attendance.\n\nSkills/Attributes Required\n• Previous experience in Quality Assurance and contact center experience mandatory\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills\n• Naturally curious and passionate with an entrepreneurial spirit\n• Customer centric attitude\n• Collaborative mindset\n• Loves to learn and has the ability the be coached and mentored\n• Ability to work in fast pace environment\n• Desire to meet and exceed measurable performance goals\n• Highly self-driven sense of motivation\n• Strong time management and organizational skills\n• Tech savvy (intermediate computer skills)\n\nSkills/Attributes Desired\n• Reporting skills\n• Presentation skills – Ability to speak to groups\n• Excel – higher skills desired\n• PowerPoint – Intermediate skills desired\n• Speech Analytics Software knowledge\n• Bachelor’s degree or established QA experience required\n\nTo learn more, visit us Here.\n\nInterviews will take place after resumes have been screened for minimum requirements. Please note that this position is not restricted solely to the responsibilities listed above and that the job scope and responsibilities are subject to change.\n\nFor more information about our collection, use, and disclosure of your personal information in connection with our evaluating your candidacy, please visit our Privacy Policy at https://www.centerfield.com/privacy-policy/.\n\nCenterfield Media is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected under federal, state or local law.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'centerfield,skills,calls,desired,brands,digital,agents,quality,supervisors team,com,supervisors,leads,team leads,qa,skills desired,calls monitored,daily,team,privacy,privacy policy,attributes,protected,skills attributes,learn,experiences'),(46,'jsearch','jY2ujNzDP7j9LkvrAAAAAA==','Bilingual Quality Assurance Analyst (English & Spanish)','Centerfield','Portmore','JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/bilingual-quality-assurance-analyst-english-spanish-at-centerfield-4356659525','Hi, We\'re Centerfield!\n\nSupercharged customer acquisition. Centerfield delivers outcome-based digital marketing solutions and personalized omnichannel experiences for the world’s leading brands. Powered by our proprietary Dugout platform, Centerfield acquires customers at scale for leading residential service, insurance, e-commerce, and B2B brands. Centerfield’s digital experiences and digital brands, such as Business.com and BroadbandNow.com, reach more than 150 million in-market shoppers annually. Centerfield is headquartered in Silicon Beach and is proud to be recognized by Built in LA as a Best Place to Work in Los Angeles.\n\nPurpose\n\nThe Quality Assurance Analyst ensures that all calls meet quality and compliance standards while supporting agent development. This role requires fluency in Spanish and English to evaluate interactions across both languages and maintain alignment with client policies and procedures.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Monitor and evaluate agent calls daily in both English and Spanish.\n• Meet departmental and client evaluation goals.\n• Communicate effectively with the QA team to maintain consistent processes.\n• Provide coaching and feedback to agents based on monitored calls.\n• Track and document evaluations, scores, and trends.\n• Use company software to locate and review call recordings.\n• Attend training sessions, meetings, and calibrations as needed.\n• Report daily production, scores, and trends.\n• Build strong relationships with account managers, supervisors, and team leads.\n• Complete audits and quality-related projects as assigned.\n• Ensure timely completion of high-level evaluations.\n• Maintain punctuality and reliability.\n\nRequired Skills & Qualifications\n• Fluency in Spanish and English (written and spoken).\n• Established experience in Quality Assurance and contact center environment.\n• Strong communication skills and attention to detail.\n• Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and meet performance goals.\n• Tech-savvy with intermediate computer skills.\n• Strong time management and organizational skills.\n\nPreferred Skills\n• One (1) year experience in contact center Sales\n• Advanced Excel and intermediate PowerPoint skills.\n• Familiarity with speech analytics software.\n• Reporting and presentation skills.\n\nTo learn more, visit us Here.\n\nInterviews will take place after resumes have been screened for minimum requirements. Please note that this position is not restricted solely to the responsibilities listed above and that the job scope and responsibilities are subject to change.\n\nFor more information about our collection, use, and disclosure of your personal information in connection with our evaluating your candidacy, please visit our Privacy Policy at https://www.centerfield.com/privacy-policy/.\n\nCenterfield Media is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected under federal, state or local law.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'centerfield,spanish,skills,english,digital,brands,com,calls,quality,meet,visit,privacy policy,experiences,protected,fluency,fluency spanish,spanish english,privacy,english spanish,maintain,scores trends,policy,place,intermediate,leading'),(47,'jsearch','pchUIuHpb3-RAD1MAAAAAA==','QUALITY ASSURANCE AND COMPLIANCE OFFICER','International Seabed Authority',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.unjobnet.org/jobs/detail/84107581','Org. Setting and Reporting\nThis position is based in the Office of Contract Management and Capacity-Building (OCMC) of the International Seabed Authority (ISA) in Kingston, Jamaica. ISA is an international organization established under the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS) and the 1994 Agreement relating to the Implementation of Part XI of the UNCLOS. The ISA is the organization through which States Parties to UNCLOS shall, in accordance with the regime for the seabed and ocean floor and subsoil thereof beyond the limits of national jurisdiction (the Area) established in Part XI and the 1994 Agreement, organize and control activities in the Area, particularly with a view to administering the resources of the Area. The position has a matrix reporting to the Chief of Compliance Assurance and Regulatory Management Unit (CARMU) as first reporting officer and Director of Office of Contract Management and Capacity-building (OCMC) as second reporting officer. The incumbent will exercise quality assurance, compliance assurance and process-oversight functions, and play a pivotal role in ensuring that operations, processes, and contractual obligations adhere to established standards, regulatory frameworks, and best practices. The incumbent will contribute to strengthening quality and compliance assurance mechanisms, improving risk management, and promoting transparency and accountability.\n\nResponsibilities\nUnder the overall guidance of the Director, Office of Contract Management and Capacity-Building, the direct supervision of the Chief, Compliance Assurance and Regulatory Management Unit and within delegated authority, the Quality Assurance and Compliance Officer will be responsible for the following duties: 1. Quality assurance, compliance assurance and process framework • Develop and coordinate the review of appropriate quality assurance, compliance assurance and process-integrity frameworks in collaboration with the Office of Legal Affairs (OLA) and the Office of Stewardship, Environment and Resources (OSER), in particular the relevant guidelines, deep seabed minerals development-specific management process standards, risk management matrices and standards, standard operating procedures (SOPs) and toolkits, including, but not limited, to: • Ensure the consistent implementation and application of approved quality assurance and compliance assurance frameworks and standards. • Ensure that contractors integrate risk management standards and approaches into their planning and operations. • Ensure that relevant stakeholders and experts are consulted and, as appropriate, in the development and periodic review of quality assurance and compliance assurance frameworks. • Provide relevant information and sound, timely advisory inputs to the Legal and Technical Commission (LTC) and expert working group(s) established to support the development and implementation of the quality assurance and compliance assurance frameworks. • Assess evidence on quality assurance and compliance assurance presented by applicants for exploration or exploitation contracts, and advise superiors in consultation with OLA, as appropriate. • Develop and periodically update the process and SOPs relating to the quality assurance and compliance assurance by the contractors with their contractual obligations, including audit readiness, compliance review and inspection-support process relating to the activities of the contractors. 2. Compliance monitoring and contractual performance oversight • Coordinate the monitoring of exploration / exploitation activities, vessels and facilities in collaboration with the OSER, to ensure compliance with relevant regulations, standards, SOPs, and approved plans of work for exploration or exploitation. • Participate in the preliminary evaluation of contractors\' annual reports, review of five-year periodic reports, applications for approval of plans of work, and applications for extension, and provide compliance-related input to the LTC and the secretariat processes, including contract preparation following approval of the plan of work. • Identify and assess risks of non-compliance or non-performance by contractors and recommend appropriate follow-up actions, in consultation with OLA, including requests for additional information and organization of meetings between the contractors and the LTC. • Coordinate or support audit, review and inspection-related processes, in accordance with applicable rules, regulations, procedures and Council-approved mechanisms. • Prepare guidance documents relating to activities of the contractors to support compliance with their respective contractual obligations. • Prepare compliance-related documents for consideration by the LTC, the Council or other organs of the Authority. 3. Engagement with Contractors and Stakeholders • Maintain regular professional engagement with contractors to develop a comprehensive understanding of quality assurance, compliance and control processes across all stages of deep seabed minerals activities. • Support the preparation and organization of meetings and events involving contractors, sponsoring States and other stakeholders, including the contractors’ annual meetings and the Secretary-General’s dialogues with the contractors and the sponsoring States. • Provide guidance, as required, for contractors and sponsoring States concerning their respective roles and responsibilities. • Liaise regularly with contractors and stakeholders, ensuring professional, transparent and consistent communication. • Prepare and review draft press responses and media enquiries relating to contractors’ activities and performance, in coordination with relevant offices and the Communications Unit. 4. Seabed Mining Register (SMR) – Governance and Compliance Dimension • Drive CARMU’s contribution, in collaboration with OSER and relevant technical units, to the development and management of the Seabed Mining Register (SMR). • Establish and apply robust data governance and compliance standards to ensure accurate and timely recording of activities in Area, and guarantee data integrity and stakeholder accessibility. • Facilitate effective coordination between CARMU, OSER, contractors, and other stakeholders to ensure alignment on SMR requirements, updates, and best practices. • Oversee and coordinate, in collaboration with relevant technical units, the development of dashboards and reporting tools to support monitoring of compliance status. • Support continuous improvements of the SMR, including interoperability with other systems, development of user guidance and post-implementation reviews. • Propose and document workflows to ensure the SMR is regularly and properly maintained and updated. 5. Secretariat Planning, Advisory and Reporting Functions • Prepare work plans and contribute to organizational planning relating to the contractors’ compliance and performance oversight. • Prepare and disseminate good practice guidance to stakeholders, in collaboration with the OSER and OLA. • Draft official correspondence and notes for signature by the Secretary-General or designated representatives. • Ensure timely responses to key stakeholders and maintain records of official communications, events and compliance-related incidents. • Participate in the relevant workshops and conference relating to activities in the Area. • Perform other duties as required by the Secretary-General.\n\nCompetencies\nPROFESSIONALISM: Strong negotiating skills and ability to influence others to reach agreement. Ability to work to tight deadlines and handle multiple concurrent projects/cases. Knowledge of contemporary international relations and of UN system, organization and interrelationships. Strong knowledge of the international law of the sea, particularly the 1982 UN Convention on the Law of the Sea and related international agreements. Familiarity with current legal and political developments in the international law of the sea. Familiarity with current issues relating to critical minerals policy. Demonstrated understanding of due process, procedural fairness, evidence handling, confidentiality and institutional accountability in regulatory and compliance contexts. Shows pride in work and in achievements; demonstrates professional competence and mastery of subject matter; is conscientious and efficient in meeting commitments, observing deadlines and achieving results; is motivated by professional rather than personal concerns; shows persistence when faced with difficult problems or challenges; remains calm in stressful situations. COMMUNICATION: Speaks and writes clearly and effectively; listens to others, correctly interprets messages from others and responds appropriately; asks questions to clarify and exhibits interest in two-way communication; tailors language, tone, style and format to match audience; demonstrates openness in sharing information and keeping people informed. PLANNING AND ORGANIZING: Develops clear goals that are consistent with the ISA mission and goals; identifies priority activities and assignments; adjusts priorities as required; allocates appropriate amount of time and resources for completing work; foresees risks and allows for contingencies when planning; monitors and adjusts plans and actions as necessary; uses time efficiently; works collaboratively with colleagues to achieve organizational goals. ACCOUNTABILITY: Takes ownership of all responsibilities and honours commitments. Delivers outputs for which one has responsibility within prescribed time, cost and quality standards. Operates in compliance with organizational regulations and rules. Supports subordinates, provides oversight, and takes responsibility for delegated assignments. Takes personal responsibility for his/her own shortcomings and those of the work unit, where applicable.\n\nEducation\nAn advanced university degree (Master\'s degree or equivalent) in resource management, engineering, quality assurance and compliance, and/or law, or related area is required. A first-level degree (Bachelor\'s degree or equivalent) in the specified fields of studies, with two (2) additional years of qualifying work experience may be accepted in lieu of the advanced university degree.\n\nJob - Specific Qualification\nCertification in Project management e.g. (PMP-RMP, PRINCE2) is desirable. Certification in CQI, IRCA and/or ISO is desirable.\n\nWork Experience\n• More than seven (7) years\' experience in quality assurance and compliance assurance monitoring and/or in-house regulatory compliance roles in international organizations, national governments, private sector (preferably in a marine science, mining and metals, or environment setting) is required. • At least 5 years\' experience in developing and implementing quality assurance standards, SOPs, and regulatory instruments and writing and reviewing quality assurance policies is required • Experience interacting with senior government officials and representatives of development partners is required • Experience in report writing and preparation of high-level analytical papers is desirable. • Experience in establishing and maintaining performance-monitoring and reporting systems is desirable. • Experience supporting or coordinating regulatory compliance assurance, audit preparedness or inspection-related processes within an international or governmental framework is desirable. • Ability to work cross-functionally, and cross-culturally is desirable.\n\nLanguages\nEnglish and French are the working languages of the United Nations Secretariat. For this job opening, English is required. The table below shows the minimum required level for each skill in these languages, according to the UN Language Framework (please consult https://languages.un.org for details).\nRequired Languages\nLanguage\nReading\nWriting\nListening\nSpeaking\n\nEnglish\nUN Level III\nUN Level III\nUN Level III\nUN Level III\n\nAssessment\nEvaluation of qualified candidates may include an assessment exercise which may be followed by competency-based interview.\n\nSpecial Notice\nThe appointment is available for a fixed period of 2 years, and renewal thereof is subject to the availability of the post, funds and satisfactory performance in the role. ISA reserves the right to not make any appointment to the vacancy, and/or to make an appointment at a lower level from the one advertised. At the ISA/ United Nations, the paramount consideration in the recruitment and employment of staff is the necessity of securing the highest standards of efficiency, competence and integrity, with due regard to geographic diversity. All employment decisions are made on the basis of qualifications and organizational needs. The ISA/United Nations is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive environment of mutual respect. The ISA/United Nations recruits and employs staff regardless of gender identity, sexual orientation, race, religious, cultural and ethnic backgrounds or disabilities. The ISA/United Nations Secretariat is committed to achieving 50/50 gender balance and geographical diversity in its staff. Female candidates are strongly encouraged to apply for this position. Only nationals of ISA Member States are eligible for consideration.\n\nUnited Nations Considerations\nAccording to article 101, paragraph 3, of the Charter of the United Nations, the paramount consideration in the employment of the staff is the necessity of securing the highest standards of efficiency, competence, and integrity. Candidates will not be considered for employment with the United Nations if they have committed violations of international human rights law, violations of international humanitarian law, sexual exploitation, sexual abuse, or sexual harassment, or if there are reasonable grounds to believe that they have been involved in the commission of any of these acts. The term “sexual exploitation” means any actual or attempted abuse of a position of vulnerability, differential power, or trust, for sexual purposes, including, but not limited to, profiting monetarily, socially or politically from the sexual exploitation of another. The term “sexual abuse” means the actual or threatened physical intrusion of a sexual nature, whether by force or under unequal or coercive conditions. The term “sexual harassment” means any unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature that might reasonably be expected or be perceived to cause offence or humiliation, when such conduct interferes with work, is made a condition of employment or creates an intimidating, hostile or offensive work environment, and when the gravity of the conduct warrants the termination of the perpetrator’s working relationship. Candidates who have committed crimes other than minor traffic offences may not be considered for employment. Due regard will be paid to the importance of recruiting the staff on as wide a geographical basis as possible. The United Nations places no restrictions on the eligibility of men and women to participate in any capacity and under conditions of equality in its principal and subsidiary organs. The United Nations Secretariat is a non-smoking environment. Reasonable accommodation may be provided to applicants with disabilities upon request, to support their participation in the recruitment process. By accepting a letter of appointment, staff members are subject to the authority of the Secretary-General, who may assign them to any of the activities or offices of the United Nations in accordance with staff regulation 1.2 (c). Further, staff members in the Professional and higher category up to and including the D-2 level and the Field Service category are normally required to move periodically to discharge functions in different duty stations under conditions established in ST/AI/2023/3 on Mobility, as may be amended or revised. This condition of service applies to all position specific job openings and does not apply to temporary positions. Applicants are urged to carefully follow all instructions available in the online recruitment platform, inspira, and to refer to the Applicant Guide by clicking on “Manuals” in the “Help” tile of the inspira account-holder homepage. The evaluation of applicants will be conducted on the basis of the information submitted in the application according to the evaluation criteria of the job opening and the applicable internal legislations of the United Nations including the Charter of the United Nations, resolutions of the General Assembly, the Staff Regulations and Rules, administrative issuances and guidelines. Applicants must provide complete and accurate information pertaining to their personal profile and qualifications according to the instructions provided in inspira to be considered for the current job opening. No amendment, addition, deletion, revision or modification shall be made to applications that have been submitted. Candidates under serious consideration for selection will be subject to reference checks to verify the information provided in the application. All external candidates recruited in accordance with section ‎2.2 (a) of ST/AI/2025/3 for a fixed term appointment without limitation and all external candidates recruited in accordance with section 2.2. (c) of ST/AI/2025/3 for a fixed term appointment limited to the entity are subject to an initial probationary period of one year under a fixed-term appointment. Job openings advertised on the Careers Portal will be removed at 11:59 p.m. (New York time) on the deadline date.\n\nNo Fee\nTHE UNITED NATIONS DOES NOT CHARGE A FEE AT ANY STAGE OF THE RECRUITMENT PROCESS (APPLICATION, INTERVIEW MEETING, PROCESSING, OR TRAINING). THE UNITED NATIONS DOES NOT CONCERN ITSELF WITH INFORMATION ON APPLICANTS’ BANK ACCOUNTS.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'contractors,united nations,nations,compliance,united,compliance assurance,assurance compliance,sexual,assurance,international,isa,relating,process,appointment,staff,quality,activities,area,exploitation,seabed,term,stakeholders,candidates,including,quality assurance'),(48,'jsearch','pYl_xhiX6z8uRrbDAAAAAA==','Quality Assurance Officer (Remote)','One on One',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697be04456210e27292186a3-quality-assurance-officer-remote','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Jamaica\n\nRole Overview\n\nWe are seeking a meticulous and proactive Quality Assurance Officer to join our team at One on One. In this role, you will be instrumental in ensuring the highest quality standards across our products and services. You will work closely with cross-functional teams to establish robust testing protocols, identify potential risks, and drive continuous improvement initiatives that enhance customer satisfaction and operational efficiency.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Develop and implement comprehensive quality assurance strategies and testing methodologies to ensure product quality and compliance with industry standards.\n• Conduct thorough testing of products and services, including functional, regression, performance, and usability testing, to identify defects and ensure adherence to specifications.\n• Collaborate with product development teams to analyze requirements and design testing plans that align with project objectives.\n• Maintain detailed documentation of testing processes, results, and defect tracking to provide transparency and facilitate continuous improvement.\n• Lead root cause analysis sessions for identified defects and work with relevant teams to drive corrective actions.\n• Establish and monitor key quality metrics to assess performance and drive improvements.\n• Implement automated testing strategies.\n• Coordinating a team of Quality Assurance Officers.\n\nRequirements\n\nRequired and Preferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.\n• 2+ years of experience in quality assurance or a related field, with a proven track record of successfully testing software products.\n• Strong understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) and quality assurance methodologies.\n• Proficiency in creating and executing test plans, test cases, and automated tests.\n• Experience with Agile methodologies and participating in Scrum processes.\n\nThis offer from \"One on One \" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 72% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'testing,quality,methodologies,drive,assurance,quality assurance,teams,products,assurance officer,automated,remote,related field,offer,officer,defects,functional,product,services,strategies,field,products services,test,implement,plans,establish'),(54,'jsearch','LfyevTjb4fR828TNAAAAAA==','Medical Lab Assistant – Entry Level','Career.zycto',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/medical-lab-assistant-entry-level/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nKickstart your healthcare career with Career.zycto, a dynamic organization committed to fostering talent and delivering exceptional support services within the medical sector. We understand the vital role every team member plays in patient care, especially at the foundational level. For an aspiring Medical Lab Assistant, our environment offers a unique blend of mentorship, practical exposure, and opportunities to learn from seasoned professionals. We believe in nurturing raw talent, providing the necessary tools and guidance to transform potential into proficiency. Join a team where your dedication to precision and patient well-being will be recognized and developed, paving your path for significant career growth in medical diagnostics.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a meticulous, enthusiastic individual eager to embark on a vital career in healthcare? Career.zycto is thrilled to announce an opening for an Entry-Level Medical Lab Assistant in our Norbrook, St. Andrew facility. This is an exceptional opportunity for a motivated individual to step into the dynamic world of medical diagnostics, providing crucial support to our team of dedicated laboratory technologists and scientists.\n\nIn this role, you will be at the heart of our operations, learning the foundational elements that contribute to accurate and timely patient diagnoses. Your daily contributions will directly impact patient care, making this not just a job, but a chance to make a tangible difference in people\'s lives. We understand that starting a new career can be daunting, which is why we\'ve designed this entry-level position to offer comprehensive, hands-on training and mentorship. You won\'t just be performing tasks; you\'ll be developing a deep understanding of laboratory procedures, quality control, and the importance of precision in every step.\n\nAs a Medical Lab Assistant, your primary focus will be on the meticulous handling and preparation of various biological specimens for analysis. This includes tasks such as receiving and logging samples, centrifuging, aliquoting, and preparing slides. You will also play a key role in maintaining the sterility and functionality of our laboratory equipment, ensuring all instruments are clean and ready for use. Adherence to strict safety protocols and proper waste disposal will be paramount, safeguarding both yourself and your colleagues.\n\nBeyond the technical aspects, this position cultivates a strong sense of teamwork and collaboration. You will work closely with experienced professionals who are passionate about sharing their knowledge and guiding you through complex procedures. This collaborative environment is designed to foster your growth, allowing you to ask questions, gain practical experience, and build a solid foundation for a long-term career in medical laboratory science.\n\nCareer.zycto is committed to your professional development. This entry-level role is seen as a springboard, offering opportunities to learn new techniques, expand your skill set, and potentially advance within our organization. If you are detail-oriented, possess a strong work ethic, and are passionate about contributing to the health and well-being of the community, we encourage you to apply and become a valued member of our growing team.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Receive, label, and process patient specimens (blood, urine, tissue, etc.) accurately and efficiently.\n• Prepare specimens for testing, including centrifuging, aliquoting, and creating microscopic slides.\n• Perform routine cleaning and maintenance of laboratory equipment and work areas.\n• Monitor and maintain inventory of lab supplies, chemicals, and reagents, reporting needs to senior staff.\n• Assist Medical Technologists with routine tests and procedures under direct supervision.\n• Accurately record and document all patient and specimen information in laboratory systems.\n• Adhere strictly to all laboratory safety protocols, quality control measures, and infection prevention guidelines.\n• Dispose of biohazardous waste according to established procedures.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe working environment.\n• Communicate effectively with team members regarding specimen status and workflow.\n• Participate in ongoing training and professional development activities.\n\nRequired Skills\n• High School Diploma or CAPE equivalent\n• Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy\n• Basic computer proficiency (data entry, word processing)\n• Strong communication and interpersonal skills\n• Ability to follow written and verbal instructions precisely\n• Excellent organizational and time management abilities\n• A strong work ethic and willingness to learn\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team\n• Basic understanding of biology or chemistry principles\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Certificate or Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology or a related scientific field\n• Previous volunteer or internship experience in a healthcare or laboratory setting\n• Familiarity with medical terminology\n• Certification in First Aid and CPR\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive entry-level salary\n• Comprehensive health and dental benefits package\n• Paid time off and holidays\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuing education\n• Mentorship from experienced laboratory professionals\n• Modern and well-equipped laboratory facility\n• Employee assistance program\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment\n• Pathways for career advancement within the organization\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting entry-level opportunity, please click on the application link below. We look forward to reviewing your qualifications.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'medical,laboratory,career,lab assistant,entry,level,entry level,patient,assistant,work,team,medical lab,organization,zycto,career zycto,lab,specimens,understand,centrifuging aliquoting,just,waste,opportunities learn,step,specimen,healthcare career'),(55,'jsearch','csn5bWEjW6oySP99AAAAAA==','Civil Design Engineer','GDM Associates Limited',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Civil-Design-Engineer-Job-227365.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Summary The ideal candidate will possess practical experience in civil engineering design and demonstrate a strong commitment to delivering high-quality technical outputs and effective project support. Key Objectives & Responsibilities Prepare and complete civil engineering design deliverables, including: Drainage systems Roadway design Sewage systems Water supply systems Assist with and complete project management deliverables, including post-contract supervision and site monitoring. Coordinate with multidisciplinary teams to ensure technical accuracy and timely project delivery. Support the preparation of technical reports, drawings, and contract documentation. Required Skills & Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in Civil Engineering from a recognized institution Minimum of three (3) years’ experience in civil engineering design Strong analytical, problem-solving, and technical skills Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines Preferred Skills & Qualifications Demonstrated experience in the design of: Roads Drainage systems Proficiency in AutoCAD Civil 3D Experience in infrastructure project supervision',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'civil,design,engineering design,systems,experience civil,deliverables including,skills qualifications,civil engineering,project,technical,complete,contract,deliverables,engineering,experience,drainage,drainage systems,support,supervision,skills,prepare complete,design demonstrate,project support,design deliverables,preparation technical'),(56,'jsearch','ER_AR2YnXLbiCTDwAAAAAA==','Civil Engineer II - Transportation','RETTEW',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/civil-engineer-ii-transportation-at-rettew-4372736967?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Type\n\nFull-time\n\nDescription\n\nRETTEW is seeking a Civil Engineer II to join our Transportation Team. In this role, you will apply your engineering expertise to deliver high-quality design solutions that keep people and goods moving safely and efficiently. This is an excellent opportunity to grow your career while contributing to projects that have a lasting impact on communities.\n\nAbout RETTEW:\n\nAt RETTEW, we bring our clients\' goals to life through engineering, environmental, and safety expertise. With a strong presence across Pennsylvania, we deliver innovative solutions in transportation, energy, water/wastewater, and land development. Guided by our core values—acting like owners, valuing relationships, and exemplifying excellence—we are dedicated to both client success and employee growth.\n\nWork Environment:\n• Hybrid (3 days/week in-office)\n• Locations: Lancaster or Mechanicaburg, PA\n\nPosition Summary / What You’ll Do:\n\nAs a Civil Engineer II in Transportation, you will support roadway and traffic design projects, collaborate with senior engineers and project managers, and help deliver effective solutions for municipal, state, and private clients.\n\nResponsibilities / Day-to-Day:\n• Develop roadway and traffic design plans using CAD and design software\n• Conduct technical analyses, reports, and calculations to support design efforts\n• Ensure compliance with PennDOT, AASHTO, and local design standards\n• Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to deliver projects on time and within budget\n• Support permitting, bidding, and construction phases with technical input\n• Contribute to client presentations and proposal development\n\nQualifications:\n\nRequired:\n• Bachelor’s degree in Civil Engineering or related field\n• 2–5 years of relevant transportation/roadway design experience\n• EIT certification\n• Proficiency with MicroStation, OpenRoads, or AutoCAD Civil 3D\n• Familiarity with PennDOT standards and procedures\n\nPreferred:\n• PE license in Pennsylvania (or ability to obtain within 1–2 years)\n• Experience with traffic engineering studies and analyses\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills\n\nWhat We Offer:\n• Competitive Salary\n• Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP)\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision benefits\n• 401(k) with company match\n• Paid time off, holidays, and flexible scheduling\n• Professional development opportunities and tuition reimbursement\n• Supportive, collaborative culture focused on growth and innovation\n\nRETTEW is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy, sexual orientation, or gender identity), national origin, age, disability, veteran status, genetic information, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.\n\nIf you are an individual with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to complete any part of the application process, please contact us at jperalta@rettew.com to request assistance.\n\nRequirements\n\nRequirements listed above.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'rettew,transportation,deliver,design,ii,engineer ii,traffic,roadway,civil,civil engineer,ii transportation,disability,pennsylvania,penndot,traffic design,roadway traffic,analyses,solutions,time,support,client,day,employee,requirements,engineering'),(57,'jsearch','wh2VY75kWn_5Jqz9AAAAAA==','Civil Engineer – Construction Site (Experienced)','Surrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd.','Stony Hill','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/civil-engineer-construction-site-experienced/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nSurrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd. is a leading name in Jamaica\'s construction and civil engineering landscape, renowned for delivering high-quality infrastructure projects that shape the nation\'s development. With decades of experience, we specialize in road construction, aggregate production, heavy equipment rental, and comprehensive civil works. Our unwavering commitment to excellence, innovation, and safety has established us as a trusted partner in both public and private sector initiatives across the island. We pride ourselves on fostering a dynamic and supportive work environment where talented professionals can thrive, contribute to impactful projects, and advance their careers. Join our dedicated team and be a part of building Jamaica\'s future, contributing to projects that enhance connectivity, safety, and economic growth for communities nationwide.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking an accomplished and highly motivated Civil Engineer with significant construction site experience to join our dedicated team in Stony Hill, St. Andrew. This pivotal role involves overseeing all civil engineering aspects of various construction projects from inception to completion, ensuring strict adherence to design specifications, budget, and schedule. The successful candidate will play a critical role in on-site problem-solving, meticulous quality control, and the efficient management of resources and personnel. You will be instrumental in translating complex engineering designs into tangible structures, ensuring structural integrity, paramount safety, and operational excellence on every project. This is an exceptional opportunity for an experienced professional to contribute to landmark projects across Jamaica, mentor junior staff, and make a tangible impact on the nation\'s infrastructure development. If you possess a strong technical background, exceptional leadership skills, and a passion for hands-on site management, we strongly encourage you to apply and help us pave the way forward.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Manage and supervise all civil engineering activities directly on construction sites in Stony Hill and surrounding areas.\n• Ensure strict compliance with engineering designs, specifications, local building codes, and paramount safety regulations.\n• Oversee comprehensive quality control for all materials and workmanship, conducting regular site inspections and rigorous tests.\n• Collaborate effectively with project managers, architects, contractors, and other stakeholders to ensure project alignment, smooth progress, and successful delivery.\n• Identify potential site risks and proactively develop robust mitigation strategies to maintain project timelines and stay within allocated budgets.\n• Prepare detailed project reports, comprehensive progress updates, and meticulous documentation for both internal and external communication channels.\n• Provide expert technical guidance and mentorship to junior engineers and site staff, fostering their professional growth.\n• Assist in the strategic procurement and efficient management of materials, equipment, and subcontractors.\n• Conduct thorough feasibility studies, detailed site investigations, and prepare precise tender documents as required.\n• Implement and rigorously enforce all health, safety, and environmental (HSE) policies and procedures on site.\n• Resolve complex engineering problems and site challenges efficiently and effectively, minimizing disruptions.\n• Review and approve shop drawings and submittals, ensuring they consistently meet all project requirements and standards.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proven experience (minimum 4 years) in civil engineering, specifically in a hands-on construction site environment.\n• Proficiency in AutoCAD, Civil 3D, or other relevant engineering design and analysis software.\n• Strong understanding of construction methodologies, materials science, and project processes.\n• Excellent project management, organizational, and time management skills.\n• Demonstrated ability to accurately read, interpret, and implement complex engineering drawings and specifications.\n• In-depth knowledge of Jamaican building codes, construction standards, and regulatory requirements.\n• Exceptional problem-solving and critical decision-making abilities, especially under pressure.\n• Strong communication (written and verbal), interpersonal, and proven leadership skills.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary team.\n• Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, Project) for reporting and planning.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license or eligibility for registration with the Professional Engineers Registration Board of Jamaica.\n• Master\'s degree in Civil Engineering, Construction Management, or a related technical field.\n• Specific experience with particular types of projects such as road infrastructure, bridges, drainage systems, or large-scale commercial/residential developments.\n• Familiarity with advanced project management software (e.g., Primavera P6, Microsoft Project).\n• Certifications in construction safety (e.g., OSHA, NEBOSH) or equivalent local safety training.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package commensurate with your experience and expertise.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance for you and your family.\n• Retirement savings plan with generous company contributions to secure your future.\n• Generous paid time off (PTO) and observance of all national public holidays.\n• Extensive opportunities for professional development, continuing education, and career advancement.\n• Company vehicle or substantial transportation allowance for all required site travel.\n• Performance-based bonuses acknowledging your contributions and achievements.\n• A collaborative, supportive, and dynamic work environment focused on teamwork.\n• Exposure to diverse and impactful infrastructure projects that shape Jamaica\'s landscape.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume and a comprehensive cover letter outlining their qualifications and experience relevant to this critical role. Please ensure your application highlights your construction site management experience and your familiarity with local regulations and project demands. Click on the application link below to apply for the job and take the next step in your career with us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'site,construction,project,civil,management,engineering,safety,projects,construction site,jamaica,comprehensive,experience,professional,civil engineering,complex engineering,critical,join dedicated,leadership skills,efficient management,engineering designs,microsoft,stony,stony hill,critical role,hill'),(58,'jsearch','o1PLQQ_cB3Un0VZMAAAAAA==','Graduate Geotechnical Engineer','targetjobs UK',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/graduate-geotechnical-engineer-at-targetjobs-uk-4372086096?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','See it differently\n\nYou see the world through a unique lens and that’s exactly what we need. We embrace how you see things differently – it’s essential for creating a sustainable future.\n\nArup is a global consultancy with advisory and technical expertise across more than 150 disciplines. We guide, plan and design the future of the built environment. Globally, each year we recruit hundreds of graduates to help us see things differently and solve the most complex challenges facing our clients, climate and communities.\n\nOur Geotechnical Engineers apply their specialist skills to buildings and infrastructure projects across the globe. We offer our clients a broad spectrum of expertise and consulting services in a wide variety of projects including transport, energy, water, resources, waste, land development, education, sports and leisure facilities, government/commercial and industrial buildings.   \n\nAs one of the world\'s leading building and infrastructure design consultancies, we offer clients the innovation and technical know-how to continually deliver their projects on schedule, on budget, and increasingly sustainably, but without compromise. \n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe are looking for enthusiastic graduates to join our Ground Engineering teams across our UK offices. From your first day, you\'ll join an unrivalled community of experts, where everyone is supported in their career path and encouraged to work towards a professional qualification. \n\nYou will help us to deliver effective and professional services for a range of varied and high-profile clients. While you will have a great deal of responsibility from day one, we will give you the chance to take on more as you progress and broaden your skills and experience.  \n\nYou will be working within a multi-disciplinary office supported by other ground engineering professionals of all levels of experience. There will be opportunity to develop a strong base in ground engineering, problem solve and develop designs, or specialise in areas such as numerical modelling, seismic, risk and resilience, or sustainability. You will focus on geotechnical aspects at all stages of the project lifecycle, including desk studies, ground investigation, analysis & design, carbon management, construction supervision & monitoring, and asset management.  \n\nYou will have the opportunity to collaborate in multi-disciplinary project teams, working alongside experts in other Arup disciplines. You will support the team across your region, we may require you to work in our other offices and regions on occasion. Our structure enables us to encourage and support opportunities to share workload, take international assignments, develop new skills and build your network across the firm.\n\nIs this role right for you?\n\nWe Are Looking For Candidates With The Following Criteria\n• A minimum of a Bachelor\'s degree in Civil Engineering, Geotechnical Engineering or similar subject, at 2.1 or above (predicted or attained)\n• A Master\'s degree in Civil Engineering or post-graduate qualification in Geotechnics, Soil Mechanics, Seismic Engineering or related subject is desirable; \n• Enthusiasm for a career in ground engineering, underpinned by a knowledge and understanding of our sector and work;\n• Excellent engineering knowledge of soil mechanics and soil-structure interaction supplemented with a good understanding of sustainable development principles.\n• An ability to communicate effectively, work well within a team and possess an analytical mindset;\n• The aptitude to work on your own initiative and be proactive, seeking to improve existing ways of working;  \n• An understanding how to apply the principles of Eurocodes in geotechnical and structural design;\n• An aptitude for learning new technical and engineering software, including those that utilise 3D design and digital automation.\n• Experience with coding languages, finite element software, or digital design would be beneficial.  \n• We\'re also interested in hearing from people who may have developed a speciality, through postgraduate or PhD studies.\n\nWe\'re Looking For\n\nChangemakers: A passion for sustainable development and creating a better world is key.\n\nInnovative minds: We\'re looking for critical thinkers who embrace new ideas and challenge the status quo.\n\nGrowth seekers: You have a growth mindset, always eager to learn and explore new ways of working.\n\nAdaptable adventurers: You\'re ready to take on any challenge that comes your way.\n\nYou should be able to start this opportunity in September 2026.\n\nPlease note, in the event of high applicant volume, this role may be closed ahead of the advertised closing date. Early application is recommended.\n\nLocation Preferences\n\nWhile the role you applied for is based in the location specified in the job advert, we may have other opportunities that align with your profile. To help us assess this, please let us know which Arup office locations you would be interested in working in on your application form\n\nDuplicate applications\n\nPlease note, candidates are permitted to submit only one application per recruitment cycle. We recommend reviewing all available opportunities and selecting the role and location(s) that best align with your skills and interests before applying.\n\nEligibility\n\nYou must ensure that you are eligible to work permanently in the UK without our sponsorship.\n\nWhat we offer you\n\nBeyond a great salary and stimulating, technically challenging work, Arup offers a range of additional benefits to its people.\n\nAs a membership organisation, everyone shares in our success through a global profit share scheme. Our members also have access to a range of broader wellbeing benefits. You’ll have access to lots of learning and development opportunities. This includes a structured induction and ongoing training through Arup university.\n\nAdditionally, you\'ll have the opportunity to utilise your technical expertise to do meaningful work that strengthens the resilience of communities and places to improve lives through Arup\'s community engagement programme.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'arup,geotechnical,working,ground,ground engineering,engineering,work,location,differently,soil,new,design,looking,clients,range,sustainable,world,opportunity,help,ll,mindset,multi disciplinary,mechanics,note,profile'),(59,'jsearch','SjE6-a9SFMa-FuywAAAAAA==','Civil Engineer – Site Management, On-Site','Surrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd.','Spanish Town','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/civil-engineer-site-management-on-site/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nSurrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd. stands as a cornerstone in Jamaica\'s civil engineering and construction landscape. With decades of experience, we have proudly built a reputation for excellence, innovation, and unwavering commitment to quality. Our portfolio spans a wide array of critical infrastructure projects, including major road networks, bridges, airport runways, and comprehensive land development schemes. We are deeply invested in the growth and modernization of Jamaica, contributing significantly to the nation\'s economic development and improving the quality of life for its citizens. At Surrey Paving, we believe in fostering a culture of teamwork, continuous learning, and professional growth, empowering our employees to achieve their fullest potential while delivering projects that exceed expectations. Join a team where your expertise will not only be valued but will also directly contribute to building a stronger, more connected Jamaica.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a seasoned Civil Engineer with a passion for transforming visions into tangible infrastructure? Do you thrive in dynamic on-site environments, leading teams, and ensuring project excellence from the ground up? Surrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd., a venerable leader in Jamaica\'s construction industry, is seeking a highly motivated and experienced Civil Engineer specializing in Site Management to join our robust and expanding team in Spanish Town, Saint Catherine Parish. This is an unparalleled opportunity to contribute significantly to critical national development projects, shaping the very landscape and future of Jamaica.\n\nIn this pivotal on-site role, you will be the driving force behind the successful execution of diverse civil engineering projects, ranging from large-scale road construction and complex bridge works to advanced drainage systems and essential urban infrastructure development. You will be directly responsible for overseeing all on-site activities, meticulously ensuring strict adherence to project specifications, budget constraints, predetermined schedules, and stringent quality control and safety standards. Your expertise will be absolutely crucial in managing daily operational logistics, coordinating seamlessly with various subcontractors, suppliers, clients, and internal teams, and proactively mitigating potential risks to keep projects on an optimal trajectory. We are specifically looking for a hands-on leader who possesses the ability to inspire and guide a diverse project team, solve complex engineering and logistical challenges in real-time, and maintain meticulous documentation and progress reports throughout the entire project lifecycle.\n\nBeyond direct oversight, you will play an instrumental role in the strategic planning, meticulous organization, and effective direction of the entire construction process. This includes optimizing resource allocation, managing equipment and materials, and ensuring that all work not only complies with both international best practices but also strictly adheres to local building codes and environmental regulations. This position demands a keen eye for detail, exceptional analytical and problem-solving abilities, and the unwavering capacity to make informed, critical decisions efficiently, often under pressure. You will be the primary point of contact for all site-related matters, responsible for communicating progress, challenges, and solutions effectively to senior management and clients. If you are ready to take full ownership of significant infrastructure projects, make a lasting, tangible impact on community development, and grow your professional career within a reputable, innovative, and forward-thinking organization that values excellence and dedication, we strongly encourage you to apply. Join us at Surrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd. and build not just structures, but a lasting legacy for Jamaica.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Manage and supervise all on-site construction activities from project inception to completion.\n• Ensure strict adherence to project plans, specifications, drawings, and quality standards.\n• Develop and maintain project schedules, ensuring milestones are met and potential delays are addressed.\n• Oversee and manage project budgets, tracking expenses and identifying cost-saving opportunities.\n• Implement and enforce rigorous health, safety, and environmental protocols on site.\n• Coordinate and liaise effectively with subcontractors, suppliers, consultants, clients, and local authorities.\n• Conduct regular site inspections to monitor progress, identify potential issues, and ensure compliance.\n• Prepare comprehensive progress reports, daily logs, and other documentation for management and clients.\n• Lead, mentor, and motivate site teams, fostering a collaborative and productive work environment.\n• Resolve technical and logistical problems that arise on-site efficiently and effectively.\n• Manage material procurement, storage, and deployment to optimize site operations.\n• Ensure all work is performed in accordance with local building codes, regulations, and industry best practices.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s Degree in Civil Engineering from an accredited institution.\n• Minimum of 4 years of proven experience in site management for civil engineering projects.\n• Demonstrated ability to manage construction projects effectively, including budget and schedule adherence.\n• Proficiency in project management software (e.g., MS Project, Primavera P6).\n• Strong understanding of construction methods, materials, and legal regulations.\n• Excellent leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills.\n• Ability to read and interpret blueprints, structural drawings, and schematics.\n• Proven problem-solving skills and decision-making capabilities under pressure.\n• Valid driver\'s license and willingness to travel to various project sites as needed.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Registered Professional Engineer (P.E.) or eligibility for registration in Jamaica.\n• Master\'s degree in Civil Engineering or Construction Management.\n• Certifications in Project Management (e.g., PMP) or Construction Safety.\n• Experience with specialized software such as AutoCAD Civil 3D or similar design tools.\n• Previous experience with large-scale road infrastructure or bridge construction projects.\n• Familiarity with FIDIC contract conditions.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Pension plan with company contributions.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous training.\n• Vehicle allowance or company vehicle.\n• Paid vacation and sick leave.\n• A dynamic and supportive work environment focused on innovation and impact.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume and a cover letter outlining their qualifications and experience to the email address provided below. Please include \'Civil Engineer - Site Management, Spanish Town\' in the subject line of your email. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview. We encourage you to click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'site,project,construction,management,projects,civil,jamaica,site management,surrey,surrey paving,paving,civil engineer,development,ensuring,clients,progress,engineering,manage,effectively,potential,engineer,infrastructure,civil engineering,critical,adherence'),(60,'jsearch','DO7SX9d-wng9Y7ekAAAAAA==','Structural Engineer – Construction Design, Full-Time','Y.P. Seaton & Associates Limited','Portmore','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/structural-engineer-construction-design-full-time/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nY.P. Seaton & Associates Limited is a distinguished Jamaican civil and structural engineering consulting firm with a proud legacy spanning several decades. Known for its innovative solutions, commitment to excellence, and significant contributions to Jamaica\'s infrastructure development, the company provides a comprehensive range of engineering services, including structural design, project management, feasibility studies, and construction supervision. Our portfolio encompasses diverse projects from commercial and industrial buildings to vital public infrastructure, always prioritizing safety, sustainability, and structural integrity. At Y.P. Seaton, we foster a collaborative environment where talent thrives, and every team member plays a crucial role in building a resilient future for Jamaica. We are dedicated to pushing the boundaries of engineering excellence and delivering projects that stand the test of time.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Full-Time Structural Engineer to join our dynamic team in Portmore, Saint Catherine Parish. This pivotal role involves leading the structural design aspects of diverse construction projects, ensuring all designs comply with national and international building codes, standards, and best practices. The ideal candidate will possess a strong foundational understanding of structural engineering principles, exceptional analytical skills, and a proven track record in designing safe, efficient, and cost-effective structures. You will be instrumental in conceptualizing, developing, and reviewing structural plans for various building types, from residential and commercial developments to industrial facilities and infrastructure projects. This position demands a meticulous approach to problem-solving, a commitment to quality, and the ability to work collaboratively within multidisciplinary project teams. You will be responsible for translating architectural concepts into robust structural systems, performing detailed calculations, preparing comprehensive technical reports, and providing expert guidance throughout the project lifecycle. Your expertise will directly contribute to the successful realization of landmark projects that shape Jamaica\'s built environment. We offer an exciting opportunity to grow professionally, tackle complex engineering challenges, and make a tangible impact on communities by contributing to structures that are both aesthetically pleasing and structurally sound.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Lead the structural analysis and design of various building and infrastructure projects using relevant software and manual calculation methods.\n• Prepare detailed structural drawings, specifications, and reports in accordance with local and international building codes (e.g., IBC, ACI, AISC, BS, Eurocodes where applicable to Jamaican context).\n• Collaborate effectively with architects, M&E engineers, contractors, and clients to integrate structural designs seamlessly into overall project plans.\n• Conduct site visits to assess existing conditions, monitor construction progress, and ensure adherence to design specifications and quality standards.\n• Perform structural inspections and provide expert recommendations for modifications, repairs, or retrofits as needed.\n• Manage project timelines, budgets, and resources related to structural engineering deliverables.\n• Mentor junior engineers and technical staff, fostering a culture of continuous learning and professional development.\n• Participate in business development activities, including preparing proposals and presentations for potential clients.\n• Stay abreast of industry trends, new technologies, and advancements in structural engineering and construction materials.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Civil Engineering with a specialization in Structural Engineering.\n• Minimum of 5 years of progressive experience in structural design and analysis of various building types.\n• Proficiency in structural analysis and design software (e.g., SAP2000, ETABS, SAFE, AutoCAD Civil 3D, Revit Structure).\n• Strong understanding of concrete, steel, timber, and masonry design principles.\n• Thorough knowledge of relevant building codes and standards applicable in Jamaica.\n• Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills for technical reports, presentations, and client interactions.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team.\n• Registered Professional Engineer (PE) or eligible for registration in Jamaica.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s degree in Structural Engineering.\n• Experience with seismic design and hurricane-resistant structural solutions.\n• Project management experience with a focus on engineering deliverables.\n• Familiarity with BIM (Building Information Modeling) workflows.\n• Experience in value engineering and constructability reviews.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Professional development opportunities and support for continuing education/certifications.\n• Access to cutting-edge engineering software and tools.\n• Collaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Opportunity to work on diverse and impactful projects across Jamaica.\n• Company-sponsored social events and team-building activities.\n• Pension scheme with company contributions.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their comprehensive resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and qualifications. Please highlight your specific experience in structural design projects and your familiarity with Jamaican building codes. Click on the application link below to apply for this exciting opportunity.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'structural,structural engineering,engineering,building,design,projects,jamaica,structural design,various building,building codes,codes,project,time,jamaican,construction,experience,comprehensive,diverse,analysis,international building,seaton,building types,structural engineer,engineering deliverables,preparing'),(61,'jsearch','qz72QZkX6AFSaGZmAAAAAA==','Mason, Construction Site','Surrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd.',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/mason-construction-site/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nSurrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd. is a leading civil engineering and construction company in Jamaica, renowned for its commitment to excellence, innovation, and sustainable development. With decades of experience, we specialize in road construction, infrastructure development, aggregate production, and general civil works that significantly contribute to the nation\'s growth. Our projects span across various parishes, impacting communities positively and setting benchmarks for quality and durability. At Surrey Paving, we believe our people are our greatest asset. We foster a culture of safety, continuous learning, and mutual respect, empowering our team members to achieve their full potential while delivering exceptional results. Join a company where your skills are valued, your growth is supported, and your work truly builds the future of Jamaica.\n\nJob Description\n\nSurrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd. is seeking a skilled and dedicated Mason to join our dynamic construction team on an active project site in Highgate, Saint Mary Parish. As a Mason, you will be instrumental in executing high-quality masonry work for various civil and building construction projects. This role requires a keen eye for detail, precision, and a strong understanding of different masonry techniques and materials. You will be responsible for laying bricks, blocks, and other construction materials to construct or repair walls, foundations, partitions, and other structures according to blueprints and specifications. The ideal candidate will have a proven track record of delivering excellent craftsmanship, adhering to strict safety protocols, and working effectively within a team environment. This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to significant infrastructure development projects and grow your career with a reputable company committed to quality and employee well-being. We are looking for someone who takes pride in their work and is committed to maintaining the highest standards of construction. Your ability to interpret plans, measure accurately, and execute tasks with minimal supervision will be key to your success in this role, ensuring that all masonry work meets the required specifications and contributes to the overall success of the project.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Read and interpret blueprints, drawings, and specifications to determine layout and dimensions.\n• Lay bricks, blocks, and other masonry units to construct or repair walls, foundations, arches, and other structures.\n• Mix mortar, concrete, and other masonry compounds accurately and consistently.\n• Cut and trim masonry units to size using hand and power tools.\n• Ensure structural integrity and aesthetic quality of masonry work.\n• Operate and maintain a variety of hand and power tools safely and efficiently.\n• Collaborate with other construction workers and project supervisors to ensure project completion on schedule.\n• Adhere strictly to all company safety policies, procedures, and relevant construction regulations.\n• Maintain a clean and organized work area.\n• Identify and report any potential hazards or structural issues on site.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proven expertise in various masonry techniques (e.g., bricklaying, blocklaying, pointing).\n• Strong knowledge of construction materials, their properties, and proper application.\n• Ability to accurately read and interpret blueprints and construction drawings.\n• Excellent physical stamina, dexterity, and hand-eye coordination.\n• Proficiency in using masonry tools and equipment (trowels, levels, hammers, saws, mixers).\n• Commitment to workplace safety practices.\n• Effective communication and teamwork skills.\n• Attention to detail and precision in work.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Vocational training or certification in masonry or a related field.\n• Experience with specific types of masonry finishes or decorative work.\n• Ability to mentor junior masons or apprentices.\n• Valid driver\'s license (Class C or equivalent).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive monthly salary.\n• Opportunities for professional development and training.\n• Provision of necessary safety equipment and personal protective gear.\n• Stable employment with a reputable, industry-leading company.\n• Supportive and safety-conscious work environment.\n• Contribution to significant national infrastructure projects.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates who meet the qualifications are invited to submit their applications by clicking on the link below. Please ensure your application includes a detailed resume outlining your relevant experience and qualifications. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to the Surrey Paving & Aggregate Co. Ltd. family!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'masonry,construction,work,safety,masonry work,mason,hand,company,surrey,paving,surrey paving,aggregate,accurately,blueprints,paving aggregate,interpret,repair walls,bricks,precision,committed,walls foundations,blocks,walls,techniques,repair'),(62,'jsearch','YiSmbKWkLxhWgRP8AAAAAA==','Infrastructure Engineer','Airtm',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/698188349242569942711582-infrastructure-engineer?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nAbout us:\n\nAirtm is a financial-infrastructure company building the future of the online-work economy. We are on a mission to empower the world\'s growing number of Digital Entrepreneurs in the Global South, giving them the financial freedom to thrive.\nThe problem is clear: in emerging markets, accessing the dollar economy is difficult. Cross-border payments are slow, expensive, and often lose value to inflation. This limits the potential of millions of talented individuals.\n\nAirtm’s solution is a swift and comprehensive financial platform that facilitates low-value cross-border payments and local cash-outs. As pioneers in stablecoin-payment infrastructure, Airtm has built the most advanced cross-border payment system available on the market.\n\nAs a company married to the world of online work, Airtm will go beyond payments to build the necessary infrastructure the online-work economy needs to thrive. We are fostering an entirely new economy, giving individuals, communities, and countries the tools to take control of their financial destinies.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nWe\'re looking for a Mid-Level Infrastructure Engineer to design, build, and maintain our cloud infrastructure and platform systems. You\'ll work closely with development teams to create scalable, reliable, and secure infrastructure that powers our products.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n- Design, implement, and manage AWS cloud infrastructure including VPCs, EC2, RDS, S3, IAM, Lambda, and other services\n- Develop and maintain Terraform modules to provision and manage infrastructure in a repeatable, version-controlled manner\n- Deploy, manage, and optimize Kubernetes clusters (EKS) including workload orchestration, autoscaling, and resource management\n- Build and improve continuous integration and deployment pipelines to enable fast, safe releases\n- Implement logging, monitoring, and alerting solutions to ensure system health and rapid incident response\n- Apply infrastructure security best practices, manage secrets, and ensure compliance with security policies\n- Write scripts and tools to automate operational tasks and improve developer experience\n- Create and maintain runbooks, architecture diagrams, and technical documentation\n- Partner with development teams to improve platform reliability and streamline deployments\n- Participate in an on-call rotation schedule to respond to production incidents and ensure system reliability\n\nQualifications\n\n- 4+ years of experience in infrastructure, DevOps, or platform engineering\n- Strong proficiency with AWS services and architecture patterns\n- Hands-on experience with Terraform for infrastructure as code\n- Solid understanding of Kubernetes concepts: deployments, services, ingress, RBAC, Helm charts\n- Experience with containerization with Docker and container registries\n- Proficiency in TypeScript and Bash scripting\n- Familiarity with CI/CD tools (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, ArgoCD)\n- Understanding of networking fundamentals (DNS, load balancing, firewalls, VPNs)\n- Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills\n- Good communication skills and ability to work collaboratively\n\nNice to Have\n\n- Experience with Golang\n- Knowledge of GitOps practices and tools (ArgoCD, Flux)\n- Familiarity with observability stacks (Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog, ELK)\n- AWS certifications (Solutions Architect, DevOps Engineer)\n- CKA/CKAD certification\n- Experience with service mesh (Istio, Linkerd)\n- Background in cost optimization and FinOps practices\nThis offer from \"Airtm\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'infrastructure,airtm,financial,economy,platform,online,payments,online work,aws,cross,cross border,border,tools,improve,experience,manage,work,services,build,payment,cloud infrastructure,individuals,create,security,work economy'),(63,'jsearch','1NMZ5vboiSzBDgh4AAAAAA==','Sports Statistician (Data Collection)','Genius Sports','Portmore','JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/sports-statistician-data-collection-at-genius-sports-4362266428','JOIN OUR TEAM AT GENIUS SPORTS!\n\nWHO ARE WE?\n\nGenius Sports is the official data, technology, and commercial partner driving the connection between sports, betting, and media on a global scale. Our mission is to create a more sustainable sports data network powered by rich, official live data. To achieve this, we\'re seeking enthusiastic Statisticians to join our team and collect match data while attending live sporting events.\n\nARE YOU PASSIONATE ABOUT FOOTBALL?\n\nIf you love football and want to be part of the action while getting paid, this is your opportunity! We are looking for individuals in the Portmore, Saint Catherine, Jamaica area to collect official live data from football events across the Jamaica Premier League.\n\nAs a Statistician, you will use our user-friendly smartphone-enabled software to report live events, including every shot, goal, tackle, and save. Don’t worry if you lack previous reporting experience - we provide comprehensive e-learning courses and practical training to ensure you’re fully prepared to cover live games. This is the perfect chance for sports enthusiasts to earn extra income while doing something they love.\n\nWHAT WE OFFER:\n• Guaranteed base pay of €35 per game\n• A performance-based reward system\n• Coverage of travel expenses\n\nIf you’re eager to immerse yourself in the world of sports and want to be part of our global network of statisticians, we want to hear from you!\n\nJOB REQUIREMENTS:\n• Basic level in English\n• Regular availability for a few hours on weekends and weekday evenings\n• Familiarity with using a smartphone\n• Willingness to travel\n• A strong knowledge of football\n• Reliability, commitment, organization, and integrity\n• Exceptional attention to detail\n\nGET TO KNOW US:\n\nFor more information about our mission and values, visit: Genius Sports\n\nARE YOU READY TO JOIN THE GENIUS SPORTS TEAM?\n\nIf you’re excited about this opportunity, we’d love to hear from you! Apply now and become a vital part of our team!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sports,data,live,team,genius sports,genius,football,official,love,join,events,want,live data,smartphone,opportunity,collect,statisticians,official live,statistician,network,mission,travel,join team,jamaica,hear'),(64,'jsearch','IhG_wpRgEqdwxQQFAAAAAA==','Environmental Officer – Sustainability Project, Full-Time','Excellence Oyster Bay','Falmouth','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/environmental-officer-sustainability-project-full-time/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nExcellence Oyster Bay is an adults-only, all-inclusive luxury resort nestled on a secluded peninsula in Falmouth, Trelawny. Part of The Excellence Collection, we are renowned for our exceptional service, breathtaking ocean views, and unwavering commitment to providing unparalleled guest experiences. Beyond luxury, we recognize our profound responsibility to the environment and the vibrant Jamaican community that surrounds us. We are dedicated to implementing sustainable practices across all our operations, from resource management and waste reduction to preserving the natural beauty of our pristine location. Our mission is to integrate world-class hospitality with robust ecological stewardship, ensuring our stunning environment thrives for generations to come. Join our passionate team and contribute to a legacy of luxury that harmonizes seamlessly with nature.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a passionate environmental advocate with a knack for turning sustainability visions into tangible projects? Excellence Oyster Bay is seeking an experienced and dynamic Environmental Officer to lead and champion our sustainability initiatives. This pivotal full-time role will see you at the forefront of developing, implementing, and monitoring comprehensive environmental management systems and sustainability projects across our luxury resort. You will be instrumental in ensuring our operations not only comply with local and international environmental regulations but also set new benchmarks for ecological best practices within the hospitality sector. Your expertise will be critical in identifying opportunities for ecological improvement, fostering a culture of environmental stewardship among our staff and guests, and driving the resort\'s commitment to responsible tourism. From optimizing energy consumption and water usage to managing waste streams, promoting responsible sourcing, and protecting our delicate coastal ecosystems, your contributions will directly impact our environmental footprint. This is more than a job; it\'s an opportunity to make a significant, positive impact on a world-class property in a stunning natural setting, shaping the future of sustainable luxury in Jamaica.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop, implement, and maintain the resort’s Environmental Management System (EMS) in accordance with relevant standards (e.g., ISO 14001, Green Globe).\n• Identify and assess environmental risks and opportunities, proposing and implementing innovative solutions for continuous improvement.\n• Lead and manage a portfolio of sustainability projects, including initiatives focused on energy efficiency, water conservation, waste reduction, recycling programs, and biodiversity protection.\n• Ensure the resort’s full compliance with all local, national, and international environmental laws, regulations, and company policies.\n• Conduct regular environmental audits, inspections, and monitoring activities, preparing detailed reports and actionable plans for corrective and preventive measures.\n• Design and deliver comprehensive environmental training and awareness programs for all resort staff, fostering a pervasive culture of sustainability.\n• Collaborate cross-functionally with various departments (e.g., Engineering, Housekeeping, Food & Beverage, Procurement) to integrate sustainable practices into daily operations and supply chains.\n• Manage relationships and liaise effectively with external stakeholders, including government environmental agencies, local community groups, environmental organizations, and eco-friendly suppliers.\n• Monitor, analyze, and report on key environmental performance indicators (KPIs), presenting findings and recommendations to management.\n• Research, evaluate, and recommend innovative eco-friendly technologies, materials, and operational practices to enhance the resort\'s environmental performance.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proven experience (minimum 3 years) in environmental management or sustainability roles, preferably within the hospitality or tourism sector.\n• Strong knowledge of Jamaican environmental laws, regulations, and permitting processes.\n• Proficiency in developing, implementing, and maintaining Environmental Management Systems (EMS).\n• Demonstrated project management skills with a successful track record in leading sustainability initiatives from conception to completion.\n• Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making abilities, with a data-driven approach.\n• Exceptional written and verbal communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills, capable of influencing and collaborating across all organizational levels.\n• High proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook).\n• Ability to conduct thorough environmental audits and prepare comprehensive, clear, and concise reports.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in Environmental Science, Environmental Engineering, Sustainability Studies, Natural Resource Management, or a closely related field.\n• Certification in Environmental Management Systems (e.g., ISO 14001 Lead Auditor) or related environmental certifications.\n• Experience with green building certifications, sustainable tourism standards (e.g., Green Globe, EarthCheck), or corporate social responsibility reporting.\n• Fluency in Spanish, both written and spoken, would be a significant advantage.\n• Prior experience working within a luxury resort or premium hospitality environment.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Highly competitive salary commensurate with experience and performance-based incentives.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance coverage.\n• Opportunities for continuous professional development, training, and career advancement within The Excellence Collection.\n• Generous employee discounts and special rates at Excellence Collection properties worldwide.\n• Complimentary meals during working shifts at our staff dining facilities.\n• Access to resort facilities, employee wellness programs, and robust employee recognition initiatives.\n• A dynamic, inclusive, and supportive work environment committed to pioneering sustainability in luxury hospitality.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to make a significant difference in a world-class luxury setting? We invite passionate and qualified candidates to join our esteemed team. Please click the link below to submit your application directly through our official careers portal. Ensure your resume and a compelling cover letter highlight your relevant experience in environmental management, project leadership, and your passion for sustainability. We look forward to reviewing your application and exploring how your expertise can contribute to Excellence Oyster Bay\'s environmental stewardship.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'environmental,sustainability,management,resort,luxury,environmental management,excellence,experience,hospitality,implementing,initiatives,sustainable,comprehensive,practices,environment,excellence oyster,green,excellence collection,systems,operations,opportunities,management systems,luxury resort,natural,local'),(65,'jsearch','Jbh-ulvJmNKhgqNtAAAAAA==','Junior / Graduate Data Scientist','Manchester',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.justjobs.co.uk/jobs/junior-graduate-data-scientist-ca9f5bbb?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Junior / Graduate Data Scientist\n\nOur client, a fast-growing and innovative organisation, is looking for a Junior / Graduate Data Scientist to join their expanding data function.\n\nThis is an excellent opportunity for an early-career data professional to gain hands-on experience across the full machine learning lifecycle in a regulated, real-world environment. You’ll work closely with Senior Data Scientists, Data Engineers, and Analysts to develop, test, and support production-ready models using modern cloud technologies.\n\nThe Role\n\nYou will work primarily with Python, SQL, and AWS (including Amazon SageMaker) to:\n\nExtract, transform, and analyse data from AWS data platforms\n\nPerform exploratory data analysis and communicate insights clearly\n\nBuild and evaluate baseline machine learning models (classification & regression)\n\nSupport model experimentation in Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio\n\nContribute to model deployment, monitoring, and safe rollout practices\n\nFollow best practices in Git, code review, testing, and Agile delivery\n\nSupport data governance, documentation, and privacy-by-design principles\n\nThis role offers structured mentorship and exposure to data science beyond modelling — including productionisation, compliance, and engineering collaboration.\n\nEssential Requirements\n\nDegree in a quantitative discipline (Data Science, Computer Science, Maths, Statistics, Physics, Engineering) or equivalent experience\n\nEarly career stage (graduate, placement, bootcamp, or personal projects)\n\nStrong Python skills (pandas, scikit-learn)\n\nSolid SQL skills (joins, aggregations, relational data)\n\nUnderstanding of ML fundamentals (train/test splits, overfitting, evaluation metrics)\n\nClear communication skills\n\nStrong learning mindset and interest in AWS/cloud technologies\n\nComfortable working in a regulated environment\n\nDesirable\n\nExposure to Amazon SageMaker\n\nExperience with Jupyter Notebooks\n\nGit and basic software engineering practices\n\nData visualisation tools (e.g., Power BI)\n\nFinancial services data exposure (risk, fraud, payments)\n\nWhat’s on Offer\n\nStructured development and mentorship\n\nHybrid working model\n\nCompany pension\n\n23–28 days holiday + bank holidays\n\nBirthday leave, charity day, wellbeing day, wedding leave\n\nInterested? Please Click Apply Now!\n\nJunior / Graduate Data Scientist',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'data,graduate data,data scientist,junior graduate,graduate,junior,scientist,sagemaker,amazon sagemaker,amazon,exposure,aws,regulated,early,early career,cloud technologies,science,learning,support,engineering,practices,model,leave,mentorship,day'),(66,'jsearch','vKNRBcdZFPWDbKtwAAAAAA==','Analytics Scientist (Compliance)','Bitso',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6975ff2873a8e8b5e77972b4-analytics-scientist-compliance?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nWorking At Bitso\n\nWe are a diverse team that takes pride in understanding the perspectives of others. We fully embrace working remotely and we are eager to act, improve and accelerate progress inside and outside of our organization.\n\nTo drive revolutionary changes in society and make crypto useful, we delight our customers with world-class products, deep care, and intentional empathy.\n\nYour Purpose\n\nData Analytics & Research (DAR) has the mission to deliver high-quality data metrics and apply rigorous analytics for decision-making and innovation. We transform data into actionable insights across the organization.\n\nIn this role your scope will include:\n• Law Enforcement & Regulatory Support: Handle data extraction and analysis for Law Enforcement Requests (LER), Regulatory Reports, and Audits.\n• Compliance Monitoring: Design, develop, and maintain systems to detect and report suspicious activity.\n• Risk Strategy: Translate complex regulatory requirements into technical data specifications and actionable tools.\n\nReports To\n\nAnalytics Manager\n\nWho You Are\n\nAn Analytics Scientist with 3+ years of experience who can own the analytics work for our Compliance area: designing data models, defining complex KPIs for risk monitoring, building insightful dashboards, and leading advanced analytics that ensure our platform remains secure and compliant with global and local regulations. A trusted partner to Legal, Compliance, and Engineering teams that brings strong judgment and clear communication.\n• Experience: 3+ years in data analytics roles.\n• Compliance Context: Familiarity with common compliance practices; understanding the types of data and analysis used for Anti-Money Laundering (AML) and Financial Regulation.\n• Domain Knowledge: Familiarity with key compliance concepts such as PEP (Politically Exposed Persons), High-Risk classifications, AML patterns (e.g., structuring), and EDD (Enhanced Due Diligence).\n• SQL & Data Quality: Advanced SQL proficiency to extract, validate, and shape data for analysis and reporting ; strong discipline and attention to detail regarding data quality checks.\n• BI & Storytelling: Experience building decision-oriented dashboards in BI tools (e.g., Looker, Tableau, Power BI), with strong narrative and usability.\n• Advanced Analytics for Compliance:\n• Ability to apply analytics to diagnose and generate risk alerts.\n• Capability to identify suspicious patterns.\n• Ability to perform deep-dives into user behavior.\n• Metrics & Modeling: Experience defining and documenting complex KPIs and working with semantic/modeling layers (e.g., LookML/table modeling).\n• Data Tools: Experience working with either Python or R for advanced analytics.\n• Communication & Collaboration: Strong written and verbal communication; effective partner to Compliance and Engineering, able to present clearly to senior stakeholders.\n\nEducation & Language\n• Bachelor\'s degree (Master\'s degree is a plus).\n• Excellent oral and written communication in English.\n\nNice-to-Have\n• Prior experience in Compliance specific roles\n• Experience with Databricks/Snowflake or similar cloud data platforms.\n• Familiarity with Git/version control and analytics engineering practices (tests, code review).\n• Prior experience in experimentation platforms, event instrumentation, or product analytics frameworks.\n\nWhat You Will Do\n• Data Modeling & Metrics: Build and maintain semantic/data models to power consistent reporting and define complex KPIs.\n• Stakeholder Management & Collaboration: Be the main point of contact for the Compliance team, owning the end-to-end analytics loop from request intake to implementation.\n• Dashboards & Decision Support: Develop and iterate on interactive dashboards that highlight performance and establish monitoring views/alerts to detect anomalies in key metrics.\n• Advanced Analytics & Insights: Lead deep-dives to uncover root causes, quantify opportunities, and propose actions while turning ambiguous questions into structured analytical plans.\n\nIn a nutshell, you\'ll be known for\n• Being the go-to analytics partner for your squad—turning ambiguity and regulatory requirements into clear plans and decisions.\n• Raising the bar on metric quality and documentation so stakeholders can maintain trust in the numbers.\n• Shipping analyses that actually define priorities and improve compliance outcomes.\n• Communicating complex findings in a clear, simple, and elegant manner, even under tight deadlines.\n• Operating with a strong ownership mindset, proposing your own ideas to improve business and compliance outcomes.\n\nResearch in Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion suggests that individuals may hesitate to apply for jobs if they do not meet all the listed criteria. At Bitso, we value diversity and your unique strengths could be just what we\'re looking for. If this role excites you but you don\'t match every point in the description, we still want to hear from you.\n\n#LI-Remote\nWho We Are\n\nWith over 9 million users, Bitso is the leading cryptocurrency platform in Latin America. We are developing the cryptocurrency ecosystem in the region and enabling financial inclusion. We believe crypto is the future of finance, and we’re committed to making it useful by providing equal access to safe and intuitive financial products.\n\nWhen we hire people for our team, we specifically test for the following traits in addition to our cultural values:\n• Mission-Driven: We seek individuals who are passionate about crypto and Bitso’s mission and resilient in facing industry challenges\n• High Sense of Urgency: We prioritize candidates who demonstrate a high sense of urgency and responsibility.\n• Exceptional Hard Skills: We seek individuals who possess exceptional skills in their respective fields, with no room for mediocrity.\n• Self-Management: We look for individuals who can independently manage their work, career, and professional development.\n\nCompensation & Benefits\n\nAt Bitso, you are taking the front seat on the edge of crypto innovation, creating the next generation of crypto-powered products.\n\nSo for those willing to commit, adapt and pioneer the most important change of the century we offer:\n• Me Time program, including unlimited paid time off.\n• Remote-first work environment.\n• Employee Stock Option program.\n• Zero trading fees through our Bitso Alpha app.\n• Extended Family Leave Policy: all birthing parents, non-birthing parents and adopting parents are eligible for a 4-months leave.\n• Premium health, dental and life insurances in Mexico, Gibraltar, Colombia, USA, Brazil and Argentina.\n• Monthly stipend for gym memberships, relaxation activities, sports equipment, cooking classes, books, entertainment and more.\n\nWant to leave an undoubtedly legacy with us? Fasten your seatbelt and join this spaceship, where you will find exponential growth and the opportunity to thrive!\n• These are the applicable requisites, although equivalent competencies in any of the above will also be considered.\n• To see our Privacy Policy please click here.\n\nThis offer from \"Bitso\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'analytics,compliance,data,bitso,crypto,advanced,experience,regulatory,individuals,dashboards,quality,advanced analytics,complex,metrics,working,modeling,risk,high,decision,remote,kpis,partner,parents,products,complex kpis'),(67,'jsearch','VEtNYOitgUHTPgP7AAAAAA==','AI Developer – Research Role, Full-Time','Career.zycto',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/ai-developer-research-role-full-time/','About Company\n\nCareer.zycto is at the forefront of innovation, pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible with artificial intelligence. For an AI Developer seeking impact, our collaborative environment fosters ground-breaking research and development. We empower our team to explore novel algorithms, create intelligent systems, and transform complex data into actionable insights. Join us to contribute to projects that redefine industries and elevate human potential, all while being part of a vibrant, forward-thinking collective committed to pioneering AI solutions globally.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking a passionate and innovative AI Developer for a crucial research role to join our dynamic team in Highgate, Saint Mary Parish. In this full-time position, you will be instrumental in designing, developing, and deploying cutting-edge artificial intelligence solutions that address complex challenges across various sectors. This is an unparalleled opportunity for a driven individual with a strong foundation in machine learning, deep learning, and data science to contribute to ground-breaking research and translate theoretical models into practical, high-impact applications. You will work closely with a diverse group of engineers, researchers, and domain experts, fostering an environment of continuous learning and innovation. Your work will involve exploring novel algorithms, experimenting with new methodologies, and contributing to the scientific community through internal reports and potential publications. We are looking for someone who thrives on intellectual curiosity, possesses exceptional problem-solving skills, and is eager to shape the future of AI.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Conduct in-depth research into new AI/ML algorithms, models, and techniques, focusing on their potential application to real-world problems.\n• Design, develop, and implement scalable machine learning models and deep learning architectures using various frameworks and programming languages.\n• Evaluate the performance and efficacy of AI models, identifying areas for improvement and optimization through rigorous testing and validation.\n• Collaborate with data scientists and engineers to integrate AI solutions into existing platforms and develop new data pipelines for model training.\n• Stay abreast of the latest advancements in AI research, contributing innovative ideas and maintaining a competitive edge in the field.\n• Prepare comprehensive documentation, research papers, and presentations to communicate findings and methodologies to both technical and non-technical audiences.\n• Mentor junior developers and contribute to the overall technical growth and knowledge sharing within the AI research team.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in Python and relevant AI/ML libraries (e.g., TensorFlow, PyTorch, scikit-learn).\n• Strong understanding of machine learning principles, algorithms, and statistical modeling.\n• Experience with deep learning architectures (CNNs, RNNs, Transformers) and their application.\n• Solid grasp of data structures, algorithms, and software development best practices.\n• Excellent problem-solving skills and an analytical mindset.\n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced research environment.\n• Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git).\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s or Ph.D. in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or a related quantitative field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP) for deploying and managing AI models.\n• Familiarity with MLOps practices and tools for model lifecycle management.\n• Demonstrated experience with large-scale data processing (e.g., Spark, Hadoop).\n• Track record of relevant publications in top-tier AI conferences or journals.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Access to cutting-edge tools and technologies.\n• Collaborative and inclusive work environment.\n• Company-sponsored team building events and social activities.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume, cover letter outlining their research interests and relevant experience, and a portfolio or links to any published work. Please click on the application link below to apply for this exciting opportunity. We thank all applicants for their interest; however, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'research,learning,algorithms,ai,ai developer,developer,models,machine learning,machine,deep learning,potential,application,data,environment,edge,relevant,deep,zycto,career zycto,learning architectures,research role,novel algorithms,solving skills,breaking research,artificial intelligence'),(68,'jsearch','eBKs7mWNjzgc2vn8AAAAAA==','Machine Learning Assistant – Entry Role','Career.zycto',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/machine-learning-assistant-entry-role/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nLooking to kickstart your journey in artificial intelligence? Career.zycto is a dynamic and innovative firm at the forefront of leveraging data to drive intelligent solutions across various sectors. We believe in nurturing talent and providing a fertile ground for budding professionals to thrive. For a Machine Learning Assistant, this means direct exposure to real-world projects, mentorship from seasoned experts, and the chance to contribute meaningfully from day one. Join a collaborative environment where curiosity is celebrated, continuous learning is encouraged, and your foundational work directly impacts our mission to solve complex challenges through cutting-edge ML technologies. It’s an ideal place to build a robust career.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking an enthusiastic and highly motivated Machine Learning Assistant to join our growing team in the vibrant University District, St. Andrew. This entry-level position is perfect for a recent graduate or an aspiring professional eager to dive into the exciting world of artificial intelligence and machine learning. As a Machine Learning Assistant, you will play a crucial role in supporting our senior ML engineers and data scientists in developing, deploying, and maintaining cutting-edge machine learning models. You\'ll gain hands-on experience with real-world datasets, model training, evaluation, and deployment pipelines.\n\nThis role offers an unparalleled opportunity to learn from experienced professionals, contribute to impactful projects, and build a strong foundation for a successful career in AI. We are looking for someone with a solid grasp of foundational programming concepts, a keen interest in data science, and an eagerness to embrace new challenges. You will be instrumental in assisting with data preparation, feature engineering, model testing, and documentation, ensuring the integrity and performance of our ML solutions. If you are a proactive problem-solver with a passion for innovation and a desire to make a tangible difference, we encourage you to apply and grow with us. We value curiosity, a collaborative spirit, and a commitment to continuous learning.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist in the collection, cleaning, and preprocessing of large datasets to prepare them for machine learning model training.\n• Support senior ML engineers in developing and evaluating various machine learning models and algorithms.\n• Perform exploratory data analysis to identify patterns, anomalies, and insights.\n• Contribute to the documentation of machine learning models, methodologies, and experimental results.\n• Write and maintain scripts for data pipeline automation and model testing using Python.\n• Collaborate with team members to troubleshoot issues and optimize model performance.\n• Research and stay up-to-date with the latest advancements in machine learning techniques and tools.\n• Participate in team meetings, brainstorming sessions, and project planning activities.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in Python programming for data manipulation and scripting.\n• Basic understanding of machine learning concepts (e.g., supervised, unsupervised learning, regression, classification).\n• Familiarity with data manipulation libraries like Pandas and NumPy.\n• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Engineering, Mathematics, or a related quantitative field.\n• Experience with machine learning frameworks such as scikit-learn, TensorFlow, or PyTorch (even through academic projects).\n• Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git).\n• Experience with data visualization tools (e.g., Matplotlib, Seaborn).\n• Prior internship or project experience in a data science or machine learning role.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Mentorship program with experienced ML professionals.\n• Opportunities for continuous learning and professional development (courses, conferences).\n• Modern office environment with state-of-the-art tools and technologies.\n• Vibrant and inclusive company culture.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and interest in the Machine Learning Assistant role. Please click on the application link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'learning,machine,machine learning,data,assistant,learning assistant,model,ml,professionals,role,experience,team,science,collaborative,continuous learning,continuous,career,datasets,data manipulation,entry,experienced,foundational,model testing,senior ml,ml engineers'),(69,'jsearch','r0xbcjJY8dzoP9StAAAAAA==','Medical Physics, Mechanics, Dynamics, Kinematics home tutor','TeacherOn.com',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.teacheron.com/teacher-job/6MiV','I am looking for someone to tutor me for a few hours for Medical Physics. The topics I would like to be tutored for are Physical Quantities, Density, Mass, Dynamics and Kinematics, Human Mechanics, Energy, Work and Power. It is for two persons. I need tutoring ASAP. I have no physics experience\n\nLevel: O level\n\nGender Preference: None\n\nMeeting options:\nStudent can travel 10 km',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'physics,level,kinematics,dynamics kinematics,dynamics,medical physics,mechanics,medical,tutor,tutor hours,tutor looking,tutored,tutored physical,tutoring asap,tutoring,work,work power,quantities,preference meeting,power persons,preference,student travel,travel 10,topics like,travel'),(89,'jsearch','wCzO_MSOY3hZt-snAAAAAA==','Lab Technician – Research & Development (Entry-Level)','Career.zycto','May Pen','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/lab-technician-research-development-entry-level-13/','About Company\n\nCareer.zycto is more than just a job platform; we are pioneers in professional growth and innovation. We believe in fostering an environment where curiosity thrives and scientific exploration leads to tangible breakthroughs. Joining our team means becoming part of a forward-thinking organization dedicated to unlocking potential, both for individuals and for the future of various industries. We empower our employees to contribute meaningfully, providing the tools and mentorship necessary for an entry-level Lab Technician to launch a successful R&D career. Discover your path to impactful science with us.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a highly motivated and detail-oriented individual with a genuine passion for scientific discovery and innovation? Career.zycto is thrilled to announce an opening for an enthusiastic Entry-Level Lab Technician to join our dynamic Research & Development team located in May Pen, Clarendon. This presents an exceptional opportunity for recent graduates or individuals eager to kickstart their professional journey in a vibrant and forward-thinking R&D environment. As an integral part of our team, you will play a crucial role in contributing to exciting and impactful projects that continually push the boundaries of scientific understanding and technological advancement, working collaboratively alongside experienced researchers and senior scientists.\n\nIn this hands-on and immersive role, your primary responsibilities will include executing a variety of laboratory experiments and tests with precision, ensuring the optimal maintenance and calibration of essential laboratory equipment, and meticulously documenting all experimental results and observations. We are specifically looking for a candidate who demonstrates a strong eagerness to learn, a high capacity for adaptability, and a clear desire to grow within a fast-paced and intellectually stimulating scientific setting. You will gain invaluable practical experience across a diverse range of fundamental and advanced laboratory techniques, master various experimental procedures, and develop foundational analytical skills that are absolutely critical for fostering a successful and rewarding career path in scientific research and development. At Career.zycto, we are deeply committed to providing comprehensive training, continuous professional development opportunities, and dedicated mentorship to ensure your complete success and accelerated professional growth within our organization.\n\nYour day-to-day will involve actively supporting critical research activities, diligently ensuring the smooth and efficient operation of the laboratory, and adhering strictly to all established safety protocols, industry regulations, and rigorous quality standards. This position is ideally suited for someone who thrives in a collaborative and interdisciplinary atmosphere, possesses an unwavering commitment to precision and accuracy in every aspect of their work, and is driven by curiosity. If you possess a solid foundational understanding of scientific principles, demonstrate an exemplary work ethic, and harbor an insatiable curiosity for uncovering new knowledge, we strongly encourage you to submit your application. Join Career.zycto and become a vital part of a pioneering team that is actively shaping the future through dedicated research and groundbreaking development efforts right here in the heart of May Pen.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Perform routine laboratory experiments and tests accurately, following established protocols and procedures.\n• Prepare reagents, media, and samples for various research and development activities.\n• Operate and maintain laboratory equipment, ensuring proper calibration and functionality.\n• Record, organize, and analyze experimental data, contributing to clear and concise reports.\n• Assist senior researchers in the design and execution of complex experiments.\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe laboratory working environment, adhering to all safety regulations and quality control standards.\n• Manage laboratory supplies and inventory, ensuring adequate stock levels.\n• Collaborate effectively with team members, sharing insights and contributing to problem-solving.\n• Participate in ongoing training and professional development activities to enhance skills and knowledge.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in Chemistry, Biology, Biotechnology, or a related scientific field.\n• Strong foundational understanding of basic laboratory techniques and safety protocols.\n• Excellent attention to detail and precision in experimental execution and data recording.\n• Proficiency in basic computer applications (e.g., Microsoft Office Suite).\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team.\n• Strong communication skills, both written and verbal.\n• Demonstrated problem-solving abilities and a proactive approach to tasks.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Prior hands-on experience in a laboratory setting (academic projects, internships, or volunteer work).\n• Familiarity with Good Laboratory Practices (GLP).\n• Experience with specific analytical instruments (e.g., pH meters, spectrophotometers).\n• Basic understanding of statistical analysis software.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship programs for career growth.\n• Vibrant and supportive team culture.\n• Contribution to cutting-edge research and innovation.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and enthusiasm for this entry-level role. Please click on the application link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'laboratory,scientific,development,career,research,team,professional,activities,pen,development activities,career zycto,zycto,successful,experiments tests,path,experimental,precision,understanding,research development,laboratory experiments,execution,entry,entry level,level,clear'),(90,'jsearch','pahHf1feB_9GkDX7AAAAAA==','Reading and Mathematics, Reading, Mathematics home tutor','TeacherOn.com','Old Harbour','JM',0,'https://www.teacheron.com/teacher-job/6MBn?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Hello good evening my name is Tina Glave I’m a mother of Three ages 9 and 6 twins girls are 9 and my son is 6 I would love to find out where in old you located, because I’m\nInterested for you to teach my kids.\nYou can call ********* thank you\n\nLevel: Grade 4\n\nGender Preference: None\n\nMeeting options:\nStudent can travel 20 km',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'reading mathematics,reading,mathematics,tutor hello,twins girls,tutor,tina glave,tina,thank level,thank,teach kids,teach,travel 20,twins,student,student travel,son,son love,preference meeting,preference,options student,options,old located,old,mother ages'),(91,'jsearch','4qmneE5fON13bhVTAAAAAA==','Actuarial Consultant - GMP Equalisation and Project Work (Nationwide)','Marsh McLennan',NULL,'JM',0,'https://builtin.com/job/actuarial-consultant-gmp-equalisation-and-project-work-nationwide/7558207','Company:Mercer\n\nDescription:\n\nJoin Our Team as an Actuarial Consultant - GMP Equalisation and Project Work (Nationwide)\n\nAre you a talented and ambitious actuary with a strong background in GMP rectification and equalisation? At Mercer, we are excited to expand our dynamic team by welcoming skilled part-qualified or qualified actuaries to a vital role that not only drives revenue but also fosters professional growth and collaboration.\n\nThis is your chance to be part of an established centre of excellence, specialising in a diverse array of retirement solutions. You will provide invaluable technical expertise and support to our UK Retirement market, particularly in the critical areas of GMP rectification and equalisation, while also engaging in a variety of actuarial project work across different pension-related initiatives.\n\nIf you’re ready to take your career to the next level and make a difference in the world of pensions, we want to hear from you! Join us at Mercer and be part of a team that values your contributions and supports your growth.\n\nWe will count on you to:\n• Collaborate and Lead: Work within a fantastic multi-disciplinary team on complex defined benefit modelling, utilising advanced actuarial skills and techniques to specialise in intricate UK pension solutions\n• Quality Assurance: Take charge of checking and reviewing complex calculations, ensuring accuracy and clarity in communicating results to consultants and wider support teams\n• Drive Improvement: Contribute to our culture of continuous improvement by developing and delivering knowledge-sharing initiatives, training sessions, and coordinating new process rollouts across various locations\n• Build Relationships: Partner with internal teams to deliver a seamless service across different lines of business within Mercer, enhancing collaboration and efficiency\n• Support and Develop: Play a key role in the development of junior colleagues within the team, supporting their performance reviews, training, and personal development plans\n• Client Engagement: Develop your consulting skills by engaging directly with clients on various aspects of actuarial projects, enhancing your professional experience\n• Project Involvement: Participate in a variety of actuarial projects, including but not limited to pension scheme valuations, risk assessments, and benefit design initiatives. Your role will involve applying actuarial techniques to solve complex problems and deliver tailored solutions for our clients\n• Team Leadership: Lead in team meetings to discuss progress, share insights, and address challenges, ensuring that everyone is working towards common objectives in GMP rectification, equalisation, and other actuarial projects\n\nWhat you need to have:\n• Qualified or part-qualified actuary\n• Extensive experience in actuarial technical calculations\n• Strong understanding of UK Defined Benefit pension schemes and experience in benefit calculations\n• Excellent analytical, numerical, and critical thinking skills, with a solid grasp of actuarial approaches for pensions\n• People management skills\n\nWhat makes you stand out:\n• Previous experience in a similar role within an Actuarial team, particularly in Pensions, with a focus on technical aspects and solid exposure to consultants and broader client support teams\n\nWhy join our team:\n• We help you be your best through professional development opportunities, interesting work and supportive leaders\n• We foster a vibrant and inclusive culture where you can work with talented colleagues to create new solutions and have impact for colleagues, clients and communities\n• Our scale enables us to provide a range of career opportunities, as well as benefits and rewards to enhance your well-being\n\nMercer is a business of Marsh (NYSE: MRSH), a global leader in risk, reinsurance and capital, people and investments, and management consulting, advising clients in 130 countries. With annual revenue of over $24 billion and more than 90,000 colleagues, Marsh helps build the confidence to thrive through the power of perspective. For more information about Mercer, visit mercer.com, or follow us on LinkedIn and X.\n\nMarsh is committed to embracing a diverse, inclusive and flexible work environment. We aim to attract and retain the best people and embrace diversity of age background, civil partnership status, disability, ethnic origin, family duties, gender orientation or expression, gender reassignment, marital status, nationality, parental status, personal or social status, political affiliation, race, religion and beliefs, sex/gender, sexual orientation or expression, skin color, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. We are an equal opportunities employer. We are committed to providing reasonable adjustments in accordance with applicable law to any candidate with a disability to allow them to fully participate in the recruitment process. If you have a disability that may require reasonable adjustments, please contact us at reasonableaccommodations@mmc.com.\n\nMarsh is committed to hybrid work, which includes the flexibility of working remotely and the collaboration, connections and professional development benefits of working together in the office. All Marsh colleagues are expected to be in their local office or working onsite with clients at least three days per week. Office-based teams will identify at least one “anchor day” per week on which their full team will be together in person.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'actuarial,team,mercer,work,marsh,gmp,colleagues,equalisation,teams,pension,professional,solutions,status,benefit,clients,collaboration,technical,calculations,committed,projects,actuarial projects,uk,rectification equalisation,rectification,pensions'),(92,'jsearch','CsAjogH_oveHeNCfAAAAAA==','Risk Assessment Officer, Microcredit Regulatory Oversight Department, Financial Institutions Supervisory Division','Bank of Jamaica',NULL,NULL,0,'https://proactuary.com/job/133926/risk-assessment-officer-microcredit-regulatory-oversight-department-financial-institutions-supervisory-division-kingston','Applications are invited from suitably qualified members of staff to resource the role of Risk Assessment Officer, Microcredit Regulatory Oversight Department, Financial Institutions Supervisory Division.\n\nReporting to the Head, Microcredit Regulatory Oversight Department, Financial Institutions Supervisory Division the successful candidate will be responsible for:\n• Receiving, collating and analyzing data submitted by MCIs against predetermined standards in order to: (1) understand risks inherent in the microcredit sector and (2) categorize microcredit institutions based on their individual levels of risk.\n• Building out/recommending components of the risk-based criteria for selection of MCIs for onsite inspection.\n• Assisting with engaging microcredit institutions during the data collection process.\n• Reviewing and verifying data and information to ensure the quality and completeness of data submissions in conformity with project objectives.\n• Participating in on-site inspections where necessary to support the development of risk-management framework.\n• Documenting findings and creating initial risk profile of the microcredit sector.\n• Maintaining effective working relationships with stakeholders and licensees to assist in advancing the risk assessment.\n• Preparing information collection instruments and requests consistent with the assessment workplan.\n• Keeping abreast of current and related legislations as well as developments in other jurisdictions.\n\nQUALIFICATION AND EXPERIENCE\n• Undergraduate degree in Risk Management, Actuarial Science, Banking and Finance, Economics or other related quantitative discipline plus 3 years\' related working experience.\n\nSPECIFIC KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS REQUIRED\n• Knowledge of risk management principles, accounting principles and standards inclusive of the IFRS, particularly as they relate to the recognition and measurement of financial assets and liabilities.\n• Ability to effectively interpret and analyse financial statements.\n• Investigative, analytical and research skills.\n• Organisational and time management skills.\n• Communication skills, including strong writing ability and effective presentation skills.\n• Ability to establish, build and maintain effective working relationships with staff and clients to facilitate the provision of support.\n• The ability to work intensely and under pressure, without compromising the delivery of accurate, timely and relevant data.\n• The ability to work in a team-oriented environment.\n• Ability to liaise effectively with stakeholders (by being emotionally intelligent and diplomatic).\n• Good interpersonal relationship skills\n\nSPECIAL CONDITIONS ASSOCIATED WITH THE JOB\n• Exposed to highly confidential information.\n• Required to work beyond normal working hours, when necessary, in order to meet deadlines.\n• Extended period of concentration on exacting details.\n• Exposure to unpredictable work demands related to developments beyond the control of and external to the Division.\n• Exposed to stressful work-related conditions.\n• Exposed to tardiness of financial institutions in the submission of data.\n\nInterested persons who meet the above requirements should complete the application form with cover letter and full resume no later than\nThursday, 19 February 2026.\n\nNB. Only short-listed candidates will be able to access the panel interview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'microcredit,risk,financial,data,ability,institutions,skills,financial institutions,assessment,division,work,related,institutions supervisory,microcredit regulatory,regulatory,regulatory oversight,risk management,risk assessment,department financial,department,effective,exposed,supervisory division,supervisory,oversight'),(94,'jsearch','m_DqWrnFxRzl6HlRAAAAAA==','Clinical Scientist in CNS  - LATAM','IQVIA',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6994ec18da7696de2f5528bc-clinical-scientist-in-cns---latam','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nIQVIA provides scientific services spanning clinical trials, real world evidence, and consulting in all areas of the product lifecycle. The Patient Centered Solutions (PCS) team leads the industry in generating data to ensure that the patient voice is incorporated into the development and commercialization of medication and other drug/non-drug interventions. We focus on understanding and meeting the needs of our clients – mostly life science/pharmaceutical companies – through the application of broad consulting expertise and technical scientific knowledge to design scientifically rigorous research. This research is broad and includes qualitative (e.g. interviews, focus groups), quantitative (e.g. clinical outcome assessments (COAs)/patient-reported outcomes (PROS), preference research) and passive (e.g. digital health technology tools) approaches to understand patient, caregiver and healthcare professional experiences and expectations of disease and treatment.\n\nTo meet our client expectations and retain the excellent reputation built up over time the IQVIA PCS team is committed to recruiting, training and supporting driven individuals who have both consulting skills and life science skills that can be applied to PCS research activities. Individuals joining us are assured of a rewarding and progressive career in patient-focused research. You’ll have the opportunity to address challenging client issues, across multiple geographies with a hands-on influence in developing and delivering solutions. We operate in a truly multi-cultural, collegial and collaborative work environment that is rich in development and growth.\n\nRole & Responsibilities\n\nThe role-holder will need to be a committed individual, who combines high emotional intelligence and excellent communication skills. They will thrive in a fast-paced environment and be comfortable managing conflicting priorities. The environment is dynamic and ever-changing, moving at the pace of our clients’ needs and the candidate will be expected to understand the sense of urgency that is synonymous with the business.\n\nAs a Consultant, ClinRO Services within the PCS team at IQVIA, you will directly administer assessments to participants in a clinical trial, or evaluate the quality of assessments performed by others and provide feedback regarding interview technique and scoring. Responsibilities include:\n• Review of scales administered by raters in a clinical trial to ensure that assessments are being conducted in a standardized manner to ensure data reliability.\n• Evaluation the quality of assessments, conducting live interactions with raters to discuss assessment methodology, scoring technique, and to provide guidance, as necessary.\n• Evaluate case data and appropriately prepare for discussions with raters (e.g., prepared to discuss relevant issues and scale items, and have necessary documents available).\n• Complete rater interactions and assigned tasks as scheduled.\n• Responsible for timely submission of all documentation associated with assigned tasks.\n• Participate in all orientation, training and calibration activities as required.\n• Functional assessments of rater performance (e.g., mock interview) and assistance in preparing and disseminating communications.\n• Contacting clinical trial participants remotely (e.g., via proprietary app, Engage) to administer assessments, and will appropriately document resultant information (e.g., notes, scores)\n\nWhat do you need to apply?\n• Minimum of a Master’s degree (MA/MS) in Psychology, Counseling, Psychiatric, Nursing or Social Work, or equivalent.\n• Minimum of 3 years’ clinical experience working with schizophrenia and major depressive disorder populations.\n• Minimum of 3 years clinical experience working administering psychiatric assessments including the PANSS, to these populations is also required.\n• Clinical Trials experience preferred.\n• Advanced level of English.\n\nHome based position in Latin America.\n\n#LI-Remote\n\n#LI-NITINMAHAJAN\n\nIQVIA is a leading global provider of clinical research services, commercial insights and healthcare intelligence to the life sciences and healthcare industries. We create intelligent connections to accelerate the development and commercialization of innovative medical treatments to help improve patient outcomes and population health worldwide. Learn more at https://jobs.iqvia.com\n\nIQVIA is committed to integrity in our hiring process and maintains a zero tolerance policy for candidate fraud. All information and credentials submitted in your application must be truthful and complete. Any false statements, misrepresentations, or material omissions during the recruitment process will result in immediate disqualification of your application, or termination of employment if discovered later, in accordance with applicable law. We appreciate your honesty and professionalism.\n\nThis offer from \"IQVIA\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 81% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'clinical,assessments,iqvia,patient,pcs,trial,raters,clinical trial,research,healthcare,services,consulting,pcs team,minimum,ensure,tasks,technique,rater,administer,administer assessments,appropriately,scoring,evaluate,assigned,assigned tasks'),(95,'jsearch','OWAhiBvAnrDlb0CrAAAAAA==','Field Applications Scientist I, North America','Watchmaker Genomics',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697e121792425699426e8711-field-applications-scientist-i-north-america?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America\n\nPosition: Field Applications Scientist I, North America\n\nPosition Type: Full-Time\n\nDepartment: Scientific Support\n\nLocation: Remote. Must be close to a major airport (within 30 miles). Preference for West Coast.\n\nExperience: MS required; 4+ years experience in a Field Applications role\n\nPosition Summary\n\nWatchmaker Genomics (WMG) is inviting applications for the full-time position of Field Applications Scientist I, North America (remote).\n\nThis position reports to the Associate Director, Field and Automation Support and will be mainly responsible for providing field technical support for Watchmaker’s Next-Gen Sequencing (NGS) and precision enzyme product portfolios. This position will support the North American technical team by providing pre- and post-sales technical and scientific support, including presenting technical content to customers, co-travel with sales team members, attending and/or presenting at conferences and assisting with various marketing activities. This position is field based, with approximately up to 75% travel within the US (potential for some international travel).\n\nPrior experience with providing field application support is required. The successful candidate will be self-motivated, proactive, and thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced working environment contributing directly to our company culture and success.\n\nThe position is expected to have a deep technical understanding of our current product portfolio, maintain knowledge of current and new NGS products, workflows-associated applications, competitor products and NGS automation support offerings, and identify and escalate changes in the market dynamics. This position is also accountable for providing customer feedback on WMG products, in addition to identifying unmet customer needs that will enable the development of new and innovative products.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Responsible for providing pre- and post-sales technical and scientific support, both onsite and remote, for customers across WMG’s NGS and precision enzyme product portfolio.\n• North America-based travel (up to 75%) activities including co-travel with sales team members, meetings with key customers, providing training and troubleshooting, and participating in trade shows/conferences. Possible opportunity for international travel.\n• Provides deep product knowledge to solve customer challenges. Triages issues, troubleshoots investigations, and identifies solutions.\n• Creation of training material, and presenting technical content to new or current customers.\n• Inform and implement processes as a part of our North American-field based scientific support organization.\n• Maintain expert-level knowledge of current and new NGS products and workflows, our precision enzyme portfolio and associated applications, competitor products and NGS automation support offerings.\n• Provide customer and market feedback on WMG products; Identify and communicate unmet customer needs that will aid in the development of new and innovative products.\n• Work closely with the commercial team to identify and support collaborations with leading research institutions and industry partners to accelerate the sales cycle, including both pre-sales and post-sales troubleshooting.\n• Support marketing activities including generation of customer-facing technical content (i.e. posters, app/tech notes, white papers, webinars) as well as participating in and presenting at trade shows/conferences.\n• Participate in sales, marketing, and product strategy meetings when appropriate.\n• Follow best practices and documentation requirements for customer-related activities and events in CRM.\n• Additional duties as required within the remit and responsibilities of the role.\n\nRequired Qualifications and Experience\n\nRelevant experience providing field-based applications support for next-generation sequencing (NGS) experiments and/or other advanced genomics applications. Relevant experience includes working in high-throughput sequencing labs developing, optimizing and troubleshooting NGS workflows both manually and on automated platforms and managing large sequencing projects.\n\nQualified candidates will have a proactive approach with a can-do attitude, and be great communicators with a high level of self-motivation. Candidates will also have a strong desire to continually improve, learn and collaborate to help WMG stay at the forefront of exciting new applications spaces. Candidates will be able to demonstrate a high standard experience to our customer base, excel in the art of troubleshooting, and take ownership and pride in their work.\n\nCandidates will have the courage to initiate discussions with customers to challenge the current \"status quo\" and have the confidence to drive change and adoption of new concepts. Full product training will be provided.\n\nThe following skills and experience are requirements for the position:\n• MSc in Genetics, Molecular Biology, Biochemistry or related field\n• 4+ Years experience within NGS field applications\n• Advanced knowledge of and practical experience with experimental design, applications/assay development, NGS library preparation, PCR, qPCR, good lab practices, and troubleshooting. Automation knowledge of NGS assays is a plus.\n• Ability to travel up to 75% of time\n• Strong customer consultative skills which includes application of scientific knowledge and analysis, exceptional customer engagement, and fostering of customer relationships\n• High self-motivation and must have demonstrated ability to work in a collaborative team environment\n• Experience with CRM software (particularly Salesforce.com) highly desirable\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills, multiple languages is a plus\n\nThe base compensation for the Field Applications Scientist role starts at $100,000 - $120,000 + bonus + equity; actual pay will be adjusted based on skills and experience. Employees are eligible for Flexible Time Off, Holidays, employer covers 75% of base medical plan with buy-up options, EAP (employee assistance program), employer paid dental with a buy-up option, employer paid vision, employer paid $25,000 life/AD&D policy, paid parental leave, and a 401(k) retirement plan with a 4% match.\n\nApplication Requirements\n\nTo apply for the position, please submit the following in a PDF format on watchmakergenomics.com:\n• Letter of motivation (upload where it says cover letter)\n• Resume or Curriculum vitae, highlighting relevant qualifications and experience\n\nApplications without a Letter of Motivation will not be considered.\n\nApplications will be accepted on a rolling basis and the position will remain open until filled; however, early submission is encouraged as review will begin immediately.\n\nIf selected to participate in the interview process, the names and contact information of three professional references who are able to assess your suitability for the position in terms of the specified requirements will be requested.\n• ** NO RECRUITMENT AGENCIES PLEASE\n\nWe are only accepting direct applications for this position. We are not working with external recruiters or agencies at this time. Unsolicited resumes or candidate submissions from third-party recruiters will not be considered and will be deemed the property of Watchmaker Genomics.\n• ** WE ARE AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY/AFFIRMATIVE ACTION EMPLOYER\n\nWatchmaker Genomics is committed to being an equal opportunity employer and creating a culturally diverse environment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability status, age, or veteran status or any other characteristics as protected by applicable law.\n\nAll applicants will be asked if currently eligible to work in the United States of America; and if now or in the future will require visa sponsorship to continue working in the United States.\n\nThis position may be subject to pre-employment checks, including driving history check, drug screening and a background check for any convictions directly related to its duties and responsibilities. All pre-employment checks will comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws.\nThis offer from \"Watchmaker Genomics\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,100000.00,120000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','applications,position,field,experience,support,customer,ngs,technical,products,sales,travel,new,providing,north,product,knowledge,field applications,america,employer,north america,wmg,troubleshooting,current,watchmaker,customers'),(96,'jsearch','1a9lWeh84p8ycHEzAAAAAA==','Associate Clinical Scientist - LATAM','IQVIA',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/698fc233da7696de2f51a21d-associate-clinical-scientist---latam','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nIQVIA provides scientific services spanning clinical trials, real world evidence, and consulting in all areas of the product lifecycle. The Patient Centered Solutions (PCS) team leads the industry in generating data to ensure that the patient voice is incorporated into the development and commercialization of medication and other drug/non-drug interventions. We focus on understanding and meeting the needs of our clients – mostly life science/pharmaceutical companies – through the application of broad consulting expertise and technical scientific knowledge to design scientifically rigorous research. This research is broad and includes qualitative (e.g. interviews, focus groups), quantitative (e.g. clinical outcome assessments (COAs)/patient-reported outcomes (PROS), preference research) and passive (e.g. digital health technology tools) approaches to understand patient, caregiver and healthcare professional experiences and expectations of disease and treatment.\n\nWhat do you need to apply?\n• Minimum of a Master’s degree (MA/MS) in Psychology, Counseling, Psychiatric, Nursing or Social Work, or equivalent.\n• Experience with psychiatric populations (e.g., schizophrenia, major depressive disorder) required.\n• Experience administering psychiatric assessments, ratings scales and/or structured clinical interviews required.\n• Advanced level of English.\n\nHome based position in Latin America.\n\n#LI-Remote\n\n#LI-NITINMAHAJAN\n\nIQVIA is a leading global provider of clinical research services, commercial insights and healthcare intelligence to the life sciences and healthcare industries. We create intelligent connections to accelerate the development and commercialization of innovative medical treatments to help improve patient outcomes and population health worldwide. Learn more at https://jobs.iqvia.com\n\nIQVIA is committed to integrity in our hiring process and maintains a zero tolerance policy for candidate fraud. All information and credentials submitted in your application must be truthful and complete. Any false statements, misrepresentations, or material omissions during the recruitment process will result in immediate disqualification of your application, or termination of employment if discovered later, in accordance with applicable law. We appreciate your honesty and professionalism.\n\nThis offer from \"IQVIA\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 81% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'iqvia,clinical,patient,healthcare,psychiatric,research,application,focus,broad,commercialization,services,consulting,development commercialization,interviews,assessments,latin,drug,outcomes,li,latin america,america,com,scientific,offer,required'),(97,'jsearch','1kmLJqDW_rkXugV7AAAAAA==','Analytics Scientist','Bitso',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6975b8ff73a8e8b5e7789067-analytics-scientist','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nWorking At Bitso\n\nWe are a diverse team that takes pride in understanding the perspectives of others. We fully embrace working remotely and we are eager to act, improve and accelerate progress inside and outside of our organization.\n\nTo drive revolutionary changes in society and make crypto useful, we delight our customers with world-class products, deep care, and intentional empathy.\n\nYour Purpose\n\nThe Data Analytics & Research (DAR) Team has the mission to deliver high-quality data metrics and apply rigorous analytics for decision-making and innovation. We transform data into actionable insights across the organization.\n\nReports To\n\nAnalytics Manager\n\nWho You Are\n\nAn Analytics Scientist with 3+ years of experience who can own the analytics work for a particular area of the business: designing data models, defining complex KPIs, building insightful dashboards, and leading advanced analytics that translate into relevant business decisions. A trusted partner to Product and Engineering that brings strong statistical judgment and clear communication.\n\nQualifications & Core Competencies\n• Experience: 3+ years in data analytics roles.\n• Analytical ownership: Demonstrated ability to turn ambiguous questions into structured analyses and actionable recommendations that influence decisions.\n• SQL & data quality: Advanced SQL proficiency to extract, validate, and shape data for analysis and reporting; strong discipline around data quality checks.\n• BI & storytelling: Experience building decision-oriented dashboards in BI tools (e.g., Looker, Tableau, Power BI), with strong narrative and usability.\n• Metrics & modeling: Experience defining and documenting complex KPIs and working with semantic/modeling layers (e.g., LookML/table modeling).\n• Advanced analytics: Ability to apply advanced analytics to diagnose performance drivers, classify segments, quantify sensitivity to changes (e.g., pricing/incentives), understand unit-level economics, forecast key metrics, and analyze user journeys.\n• Statistical fundamentals: Comfortable interpreting common statistical tests, developing simple models (t-tests, chi-square, regression/logit), and doing A/B testing.\n• Data tools:\n• Experience working with either Python or R for advanced analytics.\n• Familiarity applying ETL fundamentals to collaborate with Data Engineers.\n• Communication & collaboration: Strong written and verbal communication; effective partner to Product and Engineering, able to present clearly to senior stakeholders.\n• Education: Bachelor’s degree in a quantitative field (Economics, Statistics, Computer Science, Engineering, Actuarial Science, or similar); a Master’s degree is a plus.\n• Language: Excellent oral and written communication in English.\n\nNice-to-Have\n• Experience with Databricks/Snowflake or similar cloud data platforms.\n• Familiarity with Git/version control and analytics engineering practices (tests, code review).\n• Prior experience in experimentation platforms, event instrumentation, or product analytics frameworks.\n• Experience applying A/B tests and causal inference models (DiD, matching, IV) to real-world problems, even if not used daily.\n\nWhat You Will Do\n• Data Modeling & Metrics\n• Build and maintain semantic/data models to power consistent reporting.\n• Define complex KPIs and maintain documentation.\n• Stakeholder Management & Collaboration\n• Be the main point of contact for a specific team, owning the end-to-end analytics loop from request intake to recommendation and implementation.\n• Continuous alignment on definitions, timelines, and tradeoffs.\n• Communicate complex ideas and bring disruptive innovation.\n• Dashboards & Decision Support\n• Develop and iterate on interactive dashboards that highlight performance, drivers, and tradeoffs.\n• Establish monitoring views/alerts (where applicable) to detect anomalies and changes in key metrics.\n• Advanced Analytics & Insights\n• Lead deep-dives to uncover root causes, quantify opportunities, and propose actions.\n• Turn ambiguous questions into structured analytical plans (assumptions, segmentation, validation steps).\n• Experimentation (A/B testing)\n• Partner with PM/Eng to define hypotheses, success metrics, and guardrails.\n• Set up analysis frameworks for test readouts; escalate anomalies or instrumentation issues.\n\nIn a nutshell, you’ll be known for:\n• Being the go-to analytics partner for your squad—turning ambiguity into clear plans and decisions.\n• Raising the bar on metric quality and documentation so stakeholders can maintain trust in the numbers.\n• Shipping analyses that actually define priorities and improve outcomes.\n• Communicating complex findings in a clear, simple, and elegant manner, with clear tradeoffs and recommendations.\n• Operating with a strong ownership mindset, proposing your own ideas to improve business outcomes.\n\nResearch in Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion suggests that individuals may hesitate to apply for jobs if they do not meet all the listed criteria. At Bitso, we value diversity and your unique strengths could be just what we\'re looking for. If this role excites you but you don\'t match every point in the description, we still want to hear from you.\n\n#LI-Remote\nWho We Are\n\nWith over 9 million users, Bitso is the leading cryptocurrency platform in Latin America. We are developing the cryptocurrency ecosystem in the region and enabling financial inclusion. We believe crypto is the future of finance, and we’re committed to making it useful by providing equal access to safe and intuitive financial products.\n\nWhen we hire people for our team, we specifically test for the following traits in addition to our cultural values:\n• Mission-Driven: We seek individuals who are passionate about crypto and Bitso’s mission and resilient in facing industry challenges\n• High Sense of Urgency: We prioritize candidates who demonstrate a high sense of urgency and responsibility.\n• Exceptional Hard Skills: We seek individuals who possess exceptional skills in their respective fields, with no room for mediocrity.\n• Self-Management: We look for individuals who can independently manage their work, career, and professional development.\n\nCompensation & Benefits\n\nAt Bitso, you are taking the front seat on the edge of crypto innovation, creating the next generation of crypto-powered products.\n\nSo for those willing to commit, adapt and pioneer the most important change of the century we offer:\n• Me Time program, including unlimited paid time off.\n• Remote-first work environment.\n• Employee Stock Option program.\n• Zero trading fees through our Bitso Alpha app.\n• Extended Family Leave Policy: all birthing parents, non-birthing parents and adopting parents are eligible for a 4-months leave.\n• Premium health, dental and life insurances in Mexico, Gibraltar, Colombia, USA, Brazil and Argentina.\n• Monthly stipend for gym memberships, relaxation activities, sports equipment, cooking classes, books, entertainment and more.\n\nWant to leave an undoubtedly legacy with us? Fasten your seatbelt and join this spaceship, where you will find exponential growth and the opportunity to thrive!\n• These are the applicable requisites, although equivalent competencies in any of the above will also be considered.\n• To see our Privacy Policy please click here.\n\nThis offer from \"Bitso\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'analytics,data,bitso,metrics,advanced analytics,crypto,complex,modeling,partner,tests,dashboards,clear,models,engineering,experience,advanced,strong,individuals,mission,complex kpis,decision,decisions,kpis,bi,tradeoffs'),(98,'jsearch','RK5FArYoVeP1z4sWAAAAAA==','MEP Engineer','Catalonia Hotels & Resorts','Montego Bay','JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/MEP-Engineer-Job-226497.aspx','Are you a skilled Mechanical, Electrical, or Industrial Engineer ready to take the lead on a world‑class resort development? Catalonia Montego Bay is seeking a dynamic MEP Engineer to play a pivotal role in the review, validation, and execution of major project phases for it\'s development property in Montego Bay. Core Functions: PROJECT PHASE : Reviewing and validation of executive project documentation; Control of technical and regulatory feasibility. Review of material execution bids; control of measurements and prices. Reviewing and validation of the execution schedule. Control of administrative procedures. EXECUTION PHASE : Supervision and control of execution on site: ensuring that the work carried out corresponds to the approved project requirements, detection of deviations and proposal of technical solutions. Execution schedule control: monitoring schedule compliance and validating updates. Coordination between Project Management, Engineering and Main Contractor: daily coordination meetings , daily (not weekly) report to project management, monitoring of possible modifications to the project and follow-up of these modifications. Cost control and quality of materials. Acceptance of facilities: approval of work acceptance reports and verification of start-up tests. Control and management of facility documentation. Control of official regulatory inspections. REQUIREMENT: Degree in mechanical, electrical or similar industrial engineering. Solid knowledge of the following installations: Medium and Low Voltage. HVAC systems. Sanitary Water. Wastewater AV/IT Systems. BMS control systems. Experience in the execution of large-scale hotel resorts, minimum 5-7 years. Knowledge of local and American standards. (NFPA…) Knowledge of Marriott standards (MEP, FA&LS…) Fluent English. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office suite (MSWORD, EXCEL, POWERPOINT, etc.) Knowledge of AutoCAD and Revit. If you are passionate about delivering high‑quality MEP systems, thrive in fast‑paced environments, and are ready to contribute to a signature Caribbean project, we would love to hear from you.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'control,execution,project,mep,validation,schedule,knowledge,montego bay,documentation control,bay,montego,reviewing validation,reviewing,execution schedule,validation execution,ready,modifications,schedule control,acceptance,phase,mep engineer,coordination,regulatory,management,systems'),(99,'jsearch','hkmIVaLNHKhTahw1AAAAAA==','Mechanical Engineer – Industrial Plant (Professional)','The University of the West Indies, Mona Campus',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/mechanical-engineer-industrial-plant-professional/','About Company\n\nThe University of the West Indies (UWI), Mona Campus, stands as a beacon of academic excellence and innovation in the Caribbean. For over 75 years, UWI has been committed to fostering intellectual growth, conducting impactful research, and contributing significantly to the social and economic development of the region. The Mona Campus, nestled in the vibrant parish of St. Andrew, Jamaica, is a bustling hub comprising a diverse community of students, world-class faculty, and dedicated staff. Our extensive campus infrastructure supports a wide array of facilities, including research laboratories, residential halls, academic buildings, medical facilities, and critical utility plants that are essential for the smooth operation of a leading educational institution. We pride ourselves on creating an environment that not only promotes learning and discovery but also embraces sustainability, efficiency, and safety across all our operations.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a highly skilled and experienced Mechanical Engineer looking to apply your expertise in a dynamic and intellectually stimulating environment? The University of the West Indies, Mona Campus, invites applications for a professional Mechanical Engineer to join our dedicated Facilities Management team. This pivotal role is essential for ensuring the optimal functioning, maintenance, and strategic development of the campus\'s complex industrial plant systems and mechanical infrastructure. You will be instrumental in maintaining the reliability, efficiency, and safety of critical utilities, including our power generation and distribution systems, extensive HVAC networks, water treatment and distribution plants, and a wide array of specialized mechanical equipment vital for our laboratories and academic operations.\n\nAs a Professional Mechanical Engineer, you will be tasked with more than just maintenance; you will be a key contributor to strategic planning, energy management initiatives, and the implementation of modern engineering solutions to enhance campus sustainability and operational resilience. This involves comprehensive oversight from design consultation to commissioning of new projects, as well as the continuous improvement of existing systems. You will play a crucial role in troubleshooting complex mechanical failures, developing preventative maintenance programs, and ensuring strict adherence to local and international engineering standards and safety protocols. The ideal candidate will possess a proactive approach to problem-solving, a deep commitment to operational excellence, and the ability to collaborate effectively with diverse teams across the campus. This is an exceptional opportunity to make a tangible impact on the foundational operations of a premier regional university, contributing directly to an environment that fosters education, research, and community service.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, specify, and manage the installation, maintenance, and repair of mechanical systems, equipment, and industrial plant components across the campus.\n• Develop and implement robust preventative and predictive maintenance programs for HVAC systems, boilers, pumps, chillers, generators, and other critical mechanical infrastructure.\n• Conduct detailed engineering analyses, fault diagnosis, and troubleshooting to resolve complex mechanical issues efficiently and effectively.\n• Oversee and manage engineering projects from conception through to completion, including scope definition, budget management, contractor supervision, and quality assurance.\n• Ensure strict compliance with all relevant engineering standards, safety regulations, and environmental guidelines.\n• Lead initiatives for energy conservation, system optimization, and the adoption of sustainable engineering practices to reduce operational costs and environmental footprint.\n• Prepare comprehensive technical reports, operational manuals, and project documentation.\n• Collaborate with other engineering disciplines, facilities staff, and campus stakeholders to integrate mechanical systems seamlessly with overall campus infrastructure.\n• Provide technical guidance and mentorship to junior engineering staff and technicians.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Mechanical Engineering from an accredited institution\n• Proficiency in mechanical design software (e.g., AutoCAD, SolidWorks)\n• Strong understanding of thermodynamics, fluid mechanics, and material science\n• Expertise in HVAC, plumbing, power generation, and industrial plant operations\n• Proven experience with preventative maintenance systems and troubleshooting industrial equipment\n• Excellent project management and organizational skills\n• Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities\n• Exceptional written and verbal communication skills\n• Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment\n• Knowledge of relevant local and international engineering codes and standards\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s degree in Mechanical Engineering or a related field\n• Professional Engineering (PE) license or eligibility for registration with the Professional Engineers Registration Board of Jamaica (PERB)\n• Certifications in project management (e.g., PMP) or specific industrial plant technologies\n• Experience in an academic, healthcare, or large institutional environment\n• Demonstrated experience with Building Management Systems (BMS) and energy management platforms\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance\n• Generous pension scheme\n• Paid vacation and sick leave\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning\n• Access to university facilities and resources\n• A vibrant and diverse campus community\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested and qualified candidates are invited to apply by clicking on the application link below. Please ensure your application includes a detailed resume and a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and why you are the ideal candidate for this role at The University of the West Indies, Mona Campus.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'campus,mechanical,university,industrial plant,engineering,academic,mona campus,mona,mechanical engineer,systems,west indies,indies,west,university west,plant,professional,management,facilities,maintenance,energy,research,infrastructure,industrial,hvac,environment'),(100,'jsearch','rkaXt1NMr3UYvK86AAAAAA==','Mechanical Engineer – Production Plant, Full-Time','Pan Caribbean Sugar Company (Frome Division)','Savanna la Mar','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/mechanical-engineer-production-plant-full-time/','About Company\n\nPan Caribbean Sugar Company (Frome Division) is a pivotal player in Jamaica\'s agricultural and industrial landscape, renowned for its large-scale sugar cane cultivation and processing operations. Located in the heart of Westmoreland Parish, the Frome Estate has been a cornerstone of the local economy for decades, providing significant employment and contributing substantially to national exports. We are committed to sustainable practices, technological advancement in our production facilities, and fostering a collaborative and supportive work environment. Joining our team means becoming part of a legacy dedicated to excellence in sugar production, while embracing innovation and continuous improvement. We are at the forefront of modernizing our operations, integrating advanced mechanical engineering principles to enhance efficiency, safety, and productivity across our expansive production plant. Our focus extends beyond mere production; we are dedicated to developing our people, empowering them with the tools and knowledge to thrive in a dynamic industrial setting. We value integrity, dedication, and a proactive approach to problem-solving, cultivating a culture where every team member contributes to our collective success.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Full-Time Mechanical Engineer to join our dynamic team at the Frome Production Plant in Savanna-la-Mar. This critical role involves overseeing the mechanical integrity, reliability, and performance of a wide array of industrial machinery and systems essential to our sugar processing operations. The successful candidate will be instrumental in ensuring optimal plant functionality, minimizing downtime, and implementing continuous improvement initiatives. You will be responsible for the design, installation, maintenance, and troubleshooting of mechanical equipment, ranging from heavy machinery to intricate process systems. This position demands a keen eye for detail, strong analytical skills, and a proactive approach to identifying and resolving complex mechanical challenges. You will work closely with cross-functional teams, including production, electrical, and operations departments, to develop and execute maintenance strategies, capital projects, and safety protocols. A significant part of this role will be focused on preventative and predictive maintenance planning, ensuring our assets operate efficiently and safely, contributing directly to the plant\'s productivity and profitability. This is an exciting opportunity for a results-oriented engineer to make a tangible impact within a vital Jamaican industry, driving innovation and operational excellence in a fast-paced production environment. We offer a challenging yet rewarding career path where your expertise will be valued, and your professional growth supported within a company committed to its employees and the community.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, install, and commission new mechanical equipment and systems.\n• Oversee the maintenance, repair, and upgrade of existing plant machinery and infrastructure.\n• Conduct root cause analysis for mechanical failures and implement corrective and preventive actions.\n• Develop and execute comprehensive preventative and predictive maintenance programs.\n• Ensure compliance with all safety, health, and environmental regulations and company policies.\n• Manage capital projects, including scope definition, budgeting, scheduling, and contractor oversight.\n• Optimize plant processes and equipment performance to improve efficiency and reduce operational costs.\n• Provide technical support and guidance to maintenance technicians and production staff.\n• Prepare technical reports, specifications, and documentation for equipment and projects.\n• Stay abreast of industry trends, technologies, and best practices in mechanical engineering.\n• Contribute to the continuous improvement culture of the plant through proactive identification of enhancement opportunities.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Mechanical Engineering\n• Minimum of 4 years of experience in a production plant or heavy industrial setting\n• Proficiency in CAD software (e.g., AutoCAD, SolidWorks)\n• Strong understanding of mechanical systems, hydraulics, pneumatics, and rotating equipment\n• Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills\n• Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, and specifications\n• Familiarity with industrial safety standards and best practices\n• Effective communication and interpersonal skills\n• Project management capabilities\n• Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Postgraduate degree in Mechanical Engineering or related field\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license or eligibility for registration in Jamaica\n• Experience with CMMS (Computerized Maintenance Management Systems)\n• Knowledge of lean manufacturing principles and Six Sigma methodologies\n• Experience in the sugar, food processing, or heavy manufacturing industry\n• Certifications in reliability engineering or asset management\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive annual salary\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance\n• Pension plan contribution\n• Paid vacation and sick leave\n• Professional development opportunities\n• Employee assistance program\n• Safe and supportive work environment\n• Opportunity for career advancement\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume and a cover letter outlining their qualifications and experience relevant to this role. Please ensure your application highlights your experience in production plant environments and your mechanical engineering expertise. Always encourage applicants to click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'mechanical,production,plant,production plant,sugar,mechanical engineering,frome,heavy,maintenance,processing,equipment,engineering,machinery,safety,supportive work,specifications,develop execute,experience production,capital projects,processing operations,integrity,industrial,systems,experience,company'),(101,'jsearch','iMIeKi4PRF4Cs-GlAAAAAA==','Chief Engineer (Engineer Manager) | Shift Engineer | Certified Lifeguard | Houseman | Busser','ROK Hotel Kingston Tapestry Collection by Hilton',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Chief-Engineer-Engineer-Manager-Shift-Job-226793.aspx','CHIEF ENGINEER (ENGINEERING MANAGER) Requirements & Technical Competencies: MUST be an all-rounder HVAC and plant systems certification preferred Fire Life Safety and safety compliance certification Engineering or technical certification in Mechanical Electrical or Building Services Bachelors Degree + Skill Certifications is a Plus Key Responsibilities: Overall accountability for the hotel’s Plant Operations Maintenance Engineering and Compliance POMEC function Ensure uninterrupted operation of all mechanical electrical plumbing HVAC fire life safety and building systems Lead preventive and corrective maintenance programs aligned with luxury brand standards Oversee statutory inspections safety systems and regulatory compliance Manage engineering budgets contractors energy efficiency and capital projects Provide technical leadership to the Engineering team while supporting operational excellence and guest satisfaction SHIFT ENGINEER Requirements & Technical Competencies: Technical certification or formal training in Electrical, Plumbing, Mechanical, or Building Services Strong theoretical and practical knowledge of: Electrical systems (low and medium voltage, controls, troubleshooting) Plumbing systems (domestic water, drainage, pumps) Mechanical systems HVAC systems (preferred but not required) Key Responsibilities: Maintain and support all plant, equipment, and building systems Ensure compliance with life safety, statutory, and brand standards Coordinate inspections, testing, and preventive maintenance Supervise Engineers and ensure SOP and service standards are met Apply structured, project-based execution to maintenance and repairs Support energy conservation, vendor works, and minor projects Resolve guest-related engineering issues efficiently LIFEGUARD (POOL & PUBLIC AREA MAINTENANCE) Requirements & Technical Competencies Up to date Certified Lifeguard and Lifesavers Certification through NEPA & The Royal Life Saving Society Jamaica Proven experience as a Certified Lifeguard and/or Pool Attendant Key Responsibilities Proactively identify, anticipate, and resolve operational issues to prevent service disruptions. Maintain pool and spa chemical balance and temperature levels in accordance with local regulations and guest comfort standards . Ensure pool and public areas are clean, safe, and debris-free through daily skimming, vacuuming, cleaning and inspection. Perform plumbing repairs efficiently, including maintenance of pipework, showers, filters, grates, and related fixtures. Conduct routine and deep cleaning of pool surfaces, tiles, and surrounding areas as required. Maintain and service pool filtration systems, drums, and jets to ensure optimal performance. Accurately log daily temperature and chemical readings in accordance with compliance requirements. Support special projects and assignments as directed by management. Why Work With Us? ? Competitive compensation and growth opportunities ? Be part of a world-class hospitality team ? Ongoing training and development ? Fun, collaborative work environment ?️ Discounts on dining and stays Don’t miss your chance to work at Kingston’s top hotel, where your talent meets endless possibilities! Apply now and be part of something extraordinary!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pool,lifeguard,plumbing,certification,systems,life,building,certified,certified lifeguard,requirements technical,life safety,technical competencies,guest,safety,compliance,maintenance,technical,ensure,hvac,competencies,standards,mechanical,requirements,engineering,maintain'),(102,'jsearch','xPemvcHRDnLncjnLAAAAAA==','Senior Electrical Engineer','Loring Consulting Engineers, Inc.',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/senior-electrical-engineer-at-loring-consulting-engineers-inc-4373703371','Electrical Engineer (Senior-Level)\n\nLoring Consulting Engineers, Inc. Kingston, Jamaica (In-Office)\n\nThe Company\n\nLoring Consulting Engineers, Inc. is an award-winning consulting engineering firm headquartered in New York City that delivers smart, sustainable, and energy-efficient solutions for prestigious healthcare, academic, and cultural institutions, as well as federal, state, and local public agencies. Founded in 1956, the company has grown to more than 200 staff across offices in the U.S., Canada, and Jamaica and have worked on over 12,500 projects worldwide (e.g., World Trade Center, New York University, JFK International Airport, Mount Sinai, etc.). We are looking for new members to join our collaborative environment and make a difference on impactful projects.\n\nThe Team\n\nWe are seeking an Electrical Engineer with a proven interest in building design and sound knowledge of electrical engineering fundamentals for an immediate full-time position in our Kingston, Jamaica office. This incumbent will report in office 5 days/week.\n\nRole and Responsibilities\n\nMain responsibilities include but are not limited to:\n• Design power, lighting, fire alarm, and telecommunications plans including all associated circuitry, details, one-line diagrams, and specifications.\n• Perform system design calculations, load calculations, lighting, and any other calculations required to support electrical design.\n• Develop data analytics tools for engineering projects.\n• Review of vendor drawings to ensure conformity with engineering designs equipment sizing.\n• Coordination with other engineering disciplines to ensure the accuracy of design, and the timely flow of information throughout the project.\n• Develop and recommend improvements in design standards and improve work quality\n• Report writing and specification preparation.\n• Coordinate work with engineers of other disciplines and architects.\n• Attend meetings and communicate with clients to establish their needs and discuss design issues with them.\n• Train/Oversee/Mentor -on-site electrical/mechanical designers.\n\nQualifications and Education Requirements\n• A bachelor\'s degree in Electrical Engineering.\n• Understanding of the construction industry specific to electrical building systems.\n• Minimum of 8 years professional experience.\n• Professional Engineering License required.\n• Excellent communication skills and the ability to communicate thoughts and technical ideas in an accessible way, both verbally and in writing.\n• Strong computer skills.\n• Experience with 2D and 3D design tools (AutoCAD/Revit).\n• Working knowledge of Microsoft Office suite (Word, Excel, Outlook).\n• Strong Analytical and quantitative skills, and a demonstrated capability for analysis, problem solving and strategic thinking.\n• Strong initiative—the willingness and ability to succeed in a collaborative, team-based environment.\n• Ability to manage time appropriately and multi-task with multiple projects in order to meet deadlines;',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'design,electrical,consulting,engineering,office,calculations,electrical engineer,projects,engineers,loring,disciplines,jamaica office,loring consulting,kingston jamaica,lighting,tools,consulting engineers,york,new york,senior,ability,jamaica,new,building,writing'),(103,'jsearch','kfAVWoPm4c9XNI2VAAAAAA==','Junior Engineer – Mechanical Assistant (Entry-Level)','Jamaica Broilers Group','Old Harbour','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/junior-engineer-mechanical-assistant-entry-level/','About Company\n\nThe Jamaica Broilers Group is a leading agribusiness conglomerate in the Caribbean, with operations spanning Jamaica, the United States, and Haiti. Founded in 1958, we have grown from a small poultry operation into a diverse group of companies involved in poultry, feed, beef, pork, and other agricultural products. Our commitment to quality, innovation, and sustainable practices has made us a household name and a significant contributor to the region\'s economy. We pride ourselves on fostering a culture of excellence, continuous improvement, and employee development, providing a dynamic and supportive environment where talent can thrive and make a real impact on food security and agricultural advancement.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a passionate and aspiring mechanical enthusiast eager to launch your career in a dynamic industrial environment? Jamaica Broilers Group, a leading agribusiness in the Caribbean renowned for its commitment to innovation and operational excellence, is actively seeking a highly motivated Junior Engineer – Mechanical Assistant to join our dedicated engineering team in Old Harbour Bay, St. Catherine. This entry-level position represents an unparalleled opportunity for a recent graduate, a certified technician, or an individual with foundational mechanical knowledge to gain invaluable hands-on experience, learn directly from seasoned professionals, and contribute significantly to the efficient and reliable operation of our state-of-the-art facilities. We believe in nurturing talent and providing a robust platform for professional growth within our diverse operations.\n\nAs a Junior Engineer – Mechanical Assistant, you will be an integral and active member of our engineering and maintenance department. Your primary role will involve providing essential support in the preventative maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of a wide array of mechanical systems, critical machinery, and industrial equipment crucial to our production processes. You will work closely under the guidance of senior engineers and experienced technicians, actively assisting in the meticulous implementation of preventative maintenance schedules, conducting routine and detailed inspections, and diligently ensuring that all mechanical assets operate at their peak performance levels while adhering to the highest safety and quality standards. This role is specifically designed for individuals who possess a strong mechanical aptitude, are not afraid to tackle practical challenges, embrace continuous learning, and demonstrate an unwavering commitment to professional development.\n\nYour daily responsibilities will extend beyond mere observation; you will be actively involved in diagnostic procedures, assist with the precise installation and calibration of new equipment, help maintain accurate and comprehensive records of all maintenance activities, and consistently contribute to fostering a safe, organized, and highly productive work environment. We highly value curiosity, a meticulous approach to every task, and a proactive attitude towards identifying and resolving potential issues before they escalate. This is your chance to apply theoretical knowledge acquired during your studies or early career into a real-world, high-impact setting, thereby developing critical practical skills that will form the solid bedrock of a successful and rewarding engineering career. If you are ready to immerse yourself in an environment where cutting-edge technology meets unwavering reliability, and where your diligent contributions directly impact our operational success and broader mission, then we strongly encourage you to apply. Join the Jamaica Broilers Group family and grow with us in our commitment to excellence, playing a vital role in our continued success and industry leadership.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist senior engineers and technicians with routine preventative maintenance tasks on mechanical equipment.\n• Support the troubleshooting and repair of machinery breakdowns under supervision.\n• Conduct daily inspections of mechanical systems and report any anomalies or potential issues.\n• Assist in the installation, testing, and commissioning of new mechanical equipment.\n• Maintain accurate records of all maintenance activities, repairs, and inspections.\n• Adhere strictly to all safety protocols and company policies.\n• Participate in training sessions and workshops to enhance technical knowledge and skills.\n• Help maintain a clean, organized, and safe work area.\n• Support inventory management for spare parts and tools.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Basic understanding of mechanical principles and systems\n• Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities\n• Excellent communication and teamwork skills\n• Eagerness to learn and adapt to new technologies\n• Ability to read and interpret technical manuals and diagrams (basic level)\n• Proficiency in basic computer applications (e.g., Microsoft Office)\n• Strong attention to detail and a methodical approach to tasks\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Diploma or Certificate in Mechanical Engineering, Industrial Maintenance, or related field.\n• Familiarity with basic hand and power tools.\n• Basic knowledge of CAD software (e.g., AutoCAD) is a plus.\n• Previous practical experience (e.g., internships, vocational training) in an industrial or manufacturing setting.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance.\n• Pension plan contributions.\n• Structured training and professional development programs.\n• Opportunities for career advancement within a large, diversified group.\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n• On-site cafeteria and employee discounts.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to apply by clicking on the application link below. Please ensure your resume is up-to-date and highlights your relevant skills and qualifications. We thank all applicants for their interest; however, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'mechanical,basic,group,broilers group,broilers,engineer mechanical,assistant,practical,mechanical assistant,junior engineer,jamaica broilers,maintenance,commitment,career,assist,actively,preventative maintenance,level,inspections,providing,environment,skills,jamaica,unwavering,agribusiness'),(104,'jsearch','x8GcpwpY_mve7FipAAAAAA==','Maintenance Engineer – Factory Equipment, Full-Time','Trade Winds Citrus Limited','Linstead','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/maintenance-engineer-factory-equipment-full-time/','About Company\n\nTrade Winds Citrus Limited, producers of the beloved Tru-Juice brand, stands as a cornerstone of Jamaica\'s food and beverage industry. For over three decades, we have been dedicated to processing and packaging high-quality citrus products and a diverse range of fruit-based beverages, ensuring freshness and authentic Jamaican flavour reach homes locally and abroad. We are committed to agricultural excellence, sustainable practices, and fostering a vibrant community through job creation and empowerment. Join our dynamic team and contribute to a company that prides itself on innovation, quality, and a passion for natural goodness.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly skilled and proactive Full-Time Maintenance Engineer specializing in Factory Equipment to join our dedicated team in Linstead, Saint Catherine Parish. In this pivotal role, you will be instrumental in ensuring the optimal performance, reliability, and safety of our state-of-the-art production machinery and plant infrastructure. As a Maintenance Engineer, you will be at the forefront of our operational efficiency, blending technical expertise with strategic planning to minimize downtime and maximize productivity. This isn\'t just a repair role; it\'s an opportunity to drive continuous improvement, implement predictive maintenance strategies, and contribute significantly to our production goals.\n\nYou will be responsible for diagnosing complex mechanical and electrical issues, implementing effective corrective actions, and developing robust preventive maintenance schedules for a wide array of industrial equipment, including but not limited to, processing lines, packaging machines, conveyors, pumps, and utility systems. A deep understanding of automation controls, hydraulics, pneumatics, and electrical systems specific to food and beverage manufacturing environments is crucial. Beyond the technical aspects, you will play a key role in training junior staff, upholding stringent safety standards, and collaborating cross-functionally with production, quality assurance, and engineering teams to identify and resolve recurring issues. If you are a hands-on engineer with a passion for problem-solving, a commitment to operational excellence, and thrive in a fast-paced manufacturing setting, we encourage you to apply and help us keep the heart of our operations beating strong.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Execute comprehensive preventive maintenance programs for all factory equipment to ensure maximum operational efficiency and extend asset lifespan.\n\n• Diagnose and troubleshoot complex mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, and hydraulic systems issues on production lines, packaging machinery, and utility equipment.\n\n• Perform timely and effective repairs, overhauls, and installations of machinery, adhering to all safety protocols and industry best practices.\n\n• Utilize Computerized Maintenance Management Systems (CMMS) to document work orders, track maintenance history, and manage spare parts inventory.\n\n• Collaborate with production and quality assurance teams to identify root causes of equipment failures and implement corrective and preventive actions.\n\n• Participate in the commissioning of new equipment and process improvements, providing technical input and support.\n\n• Ensure strict adherence to all company safety policies, food safety regulations (HACCP, GMPs), and environmental guidelines.\n\nRequired Skills\n\n• Proficiency in diagnosing and repairing industrial electrical control systems (PLC, VFD, sensors).\n\n• Strong mechanical aptitude for maintaining and troubleshooting pumps, motors, gearboxes, and conveyor systems.\n\n• Expertise in hydraulic and pneumatic systems operation, maintenance, and repair.\n\n• Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, and equipment manuals.\n\n• Proven problem-solving skills and a methodical approach to fault finding.\n\n• Excellent communication and teamwork abilities.\n\n• Commitment to workplace safety and quality standards.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Industrial Engineering, or a related field.\n\n• Experience working within the Food & Beverage or FMCG manufacturing sector.\n\n• Familiarity with CMMS software and lean manufacturing principles.\n\n• Certification in specific industrial equipment or control systems.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n\n• Competitive salary package.\n\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits.\n\n• Pension plan contributions.\n\n• Paid vacation and sick leave.\n\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous training.\n\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment.\n\n• Employee discounts on company products.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to click on the link below to apply for this exciting opportunity.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'production,equipment,maintenance,food,safety,manufacturing,systems,machinery,beverage,packaging,factory equipment,maintenance engineer,factory,food beverage,quality,industrial,company,mechanical,apply,preventive,passion,quality assurance,lines packaging,operational efficiency,complex mechanical'),(105,'jsearch','vPeCwCdjXOgEytsBAAAAAA==','Plant Reliability Engineer','National Rums of Jamaica Ltd',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Plant-Reliability-Engineer-Job-225883.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','CAREER OPPORTUNITY NATIONAL RUMS OF JAMAICA LIMITED Plant Reliability Engineer – Clarendon Distillers Limited This exciting role is essential to maintaining the heart of our operations, ensuring the equipment and facilities run at peak performance. KEY AREAS OF RESPONSIBILITY: • Lead Maintenance Strategy: Develop and implement maintenance strategies using total productive maintenance (TPM) to enhance equipment performance, availability, reliability, and lifespan. • Lead Maintenance Operations: Oversee execution of all planned, preventive, and scheduled maintenance activities, ensuring real-time updates in CMMS to track and track and meet KPIs, minimizing downtime. • Collaborate & Innovate: Work closely with Operations and Project teams on equipment upgrades, replacements, and installations to support production goals. • Ensure Safety & Compliance: Enforce rigorous safety protocols and ensure compliance of all activities with industry regulations and company policies. • Mentor & Develop Team: Inspire and mentor the maintenance team, fostering a culture of continuous improvement and professional growth. • Budget management: Manage the maintenance budget and inventory to ensure cost-effective and timely availability of spares. Qualifications & Experience: • B.Sc., Degree in Engineering (Mechanical, Electrical or related field). • 5+ years’ experience in industrial maintenance management in a manufacturing setting, ideally in a distillery or similar environment. • Proficiency in using CMMS software for maintenance planning, tracking, analysis and reporting. • Strong technical expertise in production machinery, utilities, and maintenance best practice. Key Competencies: • Leadership & Team Building: Motivate and guide a diverse team with confidence, fostering a collaborative and respectful work environment. • Technical & Analytical Skills: Exhibit resourcefulness and critical thinking to troubleshoot complex equipment issues and implement lasting solutions. • Safety Focused: Demonstrate resilience by prioritizing OSHA-aligned safety protocols and environmental standards for team well-being and operational safety. • Communication & Collaboration: Collaborate effectively across teams and with external vendors, embodying a spirit of respect and teamwork. • Cost Management: Ensure innovative and resourceful solutions for managing maintenance budgets and inventory, supporting cost-effective operations.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'maintenance,safety,cost,team,operations,availability,cost effective,lead maintenance,reliability engineer,plant reliability,ensure,reliability,equipment,mentor,track,using,activities,budget,collaborate,inventory,limited,effective,cmms,management,production'),(106,'jsearch','ehuM3WHVyKjk0M_TAAAAAA==','Senior HVAC Engineer in Jamaica','Energy Jobline ZR',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.energyjobline.com/job/senior-hvac-engineer-jamaica-28325021?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Energy Jobline is the largest and fastest growing global Energy Job Board and Energy Hub. We have an audience reach of over 7 million energy professionals, 400,000+ monthly advertised global energy and engineering jobs, and work with the leading energy companies worldwide.\n\nWe focus on the Oil & Gas, Renewables, Engineering, Power, and Nuclear markets as well as emerging technologies in EV, Battery, and Fusion. We are committed to ensuring that we offer the most exciting career opportunities from around the world for our jobseekers.\n\nJob DescriptionJob Description\n\nSenior HVAC Engineer\n\nType: Full Time / Part Time\n\nLocation: New York City\n\nAbout the Job\n\nNY Building Systems Consultant Inc. (NYBSC) is a Professional Engineering and Energy Consulting Company. It was formed by industry professionals that each has a more than 10 years’ experience. NYBSC Energy and Engineering team is comprised of individuals with complete industry certifications including NYS & CTS Registered Professional Engineers (PE), Existing Building Commissioning Professional (EBCP), Certified Energy Auditor (CEA) and Certified Energy Manager (CEM).\n\nWe are currently seeking Senior HVAC Engineer for our design and build team in our New York City office. Equal Employment Opportunity is a vital component of our company culture and our success. We offer a competitive salary, vacation, and personal days.\n\nExperience: You should have demonstrated experience in at least five of the following areas:\n\n· Load calculations and some Energy modeling experience\n\n· Design mechanical systems including: heating, cooling, heat rejection, air and water distribution, ventilation, air conditioning, building automation and controls.\n\n· Familiarity with codes, specifically NYCECC, CMR, IMC, ASHRAE standards 55, 62.1, 90.1\n\n· Familiar with LL97, LL87, energy auditing and commissioning.\n\n· Prepare contract drawings detailing the designed systems using AutoCAD.\n\n· Select equipment for use in building systems.\n\n· Manage a small project, work area or technical skill set, monitor quality of work, and is involved in client liaison.\n\nRequirements:\n\nØ Bachelor’s Degree in Mechanical Engineering with a sound knowledge of mechanical engineering fundamentals.\n\nØ 4+ years of experience in commercial and residential HVAC design.\n\nØ PE License .\n\nØ LEED AP .\n\nØ Experience in Revit .\n\nØ Proven interest in the field of building design and energy savings.\n\nQualities:\n\nv Good communication skills essential for team-based working\n\nv Excellent planning and organization skills required for our fast-paced environment\n\nv Must be highly motivated, proactive and willing to take on new challenges\n\nBenefits:\n• Competitive Salary + Benefits\n\nFor apply this job, send your resume to info@nybscinc.com.\n\nIf you are interested in applying for this job please press the Apply Button and follow the application process. Energy Jobline wishes you the very best of luck in your next career move.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'energy,hvac engineer,senior hvac,building,job,hvac,design,experience,engineering,senior,nybsc,air,global,jobline,energy engineering,energy jobline,certified energy,global energy,systems,york city,city,new york,york,offer,professionals'),(107,'jsearch','XYFaD5YcwY_WsL0fAAAAAA==','Geologist – Mining Operations','Jamalco (Clarendon Alumina Production)',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.supersecrets.com.ng/jobs/geologist-mining-operations/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nJamalco, a joint venture between the Government of Jamaica (through Clarendon Alumina Production) and Noble Group, is a leading bauxite mining and alumina refining company operating in Jamaica. With a rich history spanning decades, Jamalco is committed to sustainable resource management, operational excellence, and contributing significantly to the Jamaican economy and community. We pride ourselves on a culture of safety, innovation, and environmental stewardship, ensuring responsible extraction and processing of Jamaica\'s valuable bauxite reserves.\n\nJob Description\n\nJamalco is seeking a dedicated and experienced Geologist to join our dynamic team in Clarendon, Jamaica. This pivotal role involves contributing to all phases of our bauxite mining operations, from exploration and resource definition to mine planning and environmental monitoring. The successful candidate will be instrumental in ensuring the efficient and sustainable extraction of bauxite resources, applying advanced geological principles and techniques to optimize our operations. You will be responsible for conducting fieldwork, analyzing geological data, supervising drilling programs, and preparing detailed reports that inform critical business decisions. This position offers a unique opportunity to work with a leading player in the global alumina industry, utilizing cutting-edge technology and collaborating with a diverse team of engineers, environmental specialists, and operational staff. We are looking for an individual with a strong foundation in economic geology, a passion for fieldwork, and a commitment to maintaining the highest standards of safety and environmental responsibility. Your expertise will directly impact our production targets and long-term resource sustainability. Join us in shaping the future of mining in Jamaica, where your contributions are valued, and your professional growth is encouraged.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Conduct geological mapping, sampling, and data collection in designated exploration and mining areas.\n• Supervise drilling programs, including core logging, sample preparation, and quality control (QA/QC) procedures.\n• Interpret geological data (e.g., geochemical, geophysical, drill hole data) using specialized software to generate accurate geological models and resource estimates.\n• Assist in the preparation of short-term and long-term mine plans, ensuring alignment with geological models and operational objectives.\n• Monitor active mining faces, providing geological guidance to mining operations and ensuring adherence to geological controls.\n• Prepare comprehensive geological reports, technical presentations, and progress updates for various stakeholders.\n• Collaborate with mine engineers, surveyors, and environmental teams to optimize resource utilization and minimize environmental impact.\n• Ensure strict adherence to company safety protocols, environmental regulations, and industry best practices.\n• Participate in ongoing professional development and training initiatives to stay abreast of geological advancements and industry trends.\n• Conduct geological risk assessments and contribute to mitigation strategies.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Geology or Earth Sciences from an accredited institution.\n• Minimum of 3 years of progressive experience as a Geologist, preferably within the mining sector (bauxite experience is highly advantageous).\n• Proficiency in geological modeling software (e.g., Leapfrog Geo, Micromine, Surpac, ArcGIS).\n• Strong understanding of geological principles, mineralogy, petrology, and structural geology.\n• Proven experience in field mapping, core logging, and supervision of drilling programs.\n• Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and data interpretation skills.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team.\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present complex geological information clearly.\n• Valid Jamaican driver\'s license and ability to conduct fieldwork in various terrains and weather conditions.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s degree in Economic Geology, Mining Geology, or a related field.\n• Professional registration with a relevant geological or engineering body.\n• Experience with bauxite deposit geology and resource estimation methodologies.\n• Familiarity with Jamaican geological frameworks and regulatory requirements.\n• Proficiency in advanced statistical analysis for geological data.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Retirement savings plan with company contributions.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Safe and supportive work environment.\n• Company-sponsored training and certifications.\n• Access to state-of-the-art geological tools and technology.\n• Relocation assistance may be available for eligible candidates.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume and a cover letter outlining their qualifications and experience relevant to this role. Please ensure your application highlights your experience in mining geology and your proficiency with relevant software. To apply, please click the link below.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'geological,mining,geology,environmental,resource,experience,data,bauxite,jamaica,company,professional,operations,ensuring,safety,term,team,jamaican,mining operations,skills,industry,relevant,geologist,geological data,operational,fieldwork'),(108,'jsearch','cCKo75t0etyyUE5NAAAAAA==','Biology, Chemistry, Physics home tutor','TeacherOn.com','Mandeville','JM',0,'https://www.teacheron.com/teacher-job/6MAJ','Bio Chem Tutor for CXC 2026\n\nLevel: Grade 11\n\nGender Preference: None\n\nMeeting options:\nAt home - Student can meet at their place.\nStudent can travel 10 km',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'tutor,student,home,tutor bio,travel,travel 10,student travel,student meet,preference meeting,preference,place student,place,physics home,tutor cxc,physics,options home,meeting options,options,meet place,meet,level grade,meeting,level,km,home tutor'),(112,'jsearch','-FE6LntlBlvVPXLuAAAAAA==','Methods Engineer','Alstom',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.recruit.net/job/methods-engineer-jobs/87E7A1B94B26484A','Req ID:505665\n\nAt Alstom, we understand transport networks and what moves people. From high-speed trains, metros, monorails, and trams, to turnkey systems, services, infrastructure, signalling and digital mobility, we offer our diverse customers the broadest portfolio in the industry. Every day, more than 80 000 colleagues lead the way to greener and smarter mobility worldwide, connecting cities as we reduce carbon and replace cars.\n\nCould you be the full-time Methods Engineer in Kingston, ON we’re looking for?\n\nYour future role\n\nTake on a new challenge and apply your industrialization and manufacturing expertise in a cutting-edge field. You’ll work alongside dynamic, collaborative, and innovative teammates.\n\nYou\'ll play a key role in ensuring that our manufacturing processes are optimized, our products are market-ready, and our industrial requirements align with project Quality, Cost, and Delivery (QCD) objectives. Day-to-day, you’ll work closely with teams across the business (Engineering, Manufacturing, Supply Chain, Tetsing, Procurement, EHS and Quality), lead industrialization activities, and ensure smooth collaboration with internal and external stakeholders.\n\nManage the methods and manufacturing processes to optimize production QCD performance (organization of the work, tooling and processes). Ensure data, tools and components are always available for production and repairs all along the life cycle.\n\nWe\'ll look to you for:\n• Deploy Signaling industrialization processes for products and DFM rules\n• Develop industrial means for product & project manufacturing and test with EHS mind-set\n• Develop, set up, and improve the manufacturing processes: workstations, tooling, industrialization rules, special process, routings, assembly/work instructions while meeting EHS standards\n• Set up and maintain the bookshop of times / methods library\n• Create Work Instructions (WI) including shop floor designs, tools, technicques, MBOM and special process\n• Design and optimize the machines setting-up in workshops as well as the organization of every workstation\n• Measure and calculate method time vs production time ensuring OEE targets are met\n• Provide and sustain Industrial maturity report per product line (definition files MR, test First Passed Yield per phase, failure rate at first installation, production cost, industrial scheme, lead time)\n• Review electrical diagrams, rack schematics, cable lists, and integration drawings to validate accuracy\n• Define routing principles, wiring segmentation, cable tray & harness approaches\n• Validate interface points between racks, power subsystem, and telecom equipment\n• Guarantee the application of the Manufacturing (DFM) and test Rules (DFT) and repairs requirements\n• Manage industrial risk through Process Failure Mode and Effect Analysis (PFMEA) and associated improvement action plan\n• Work closely with industrial planners on production order development based on production time, capacity, resources, MBOM\n• Train the production workers and EPU managers during design and industrialization phases\n• In case of non-conformity or incident, investigate root causes, finds and implement corrective solutions\n• Support for continuous improvement of manufacturing lines\n• Participate in the design of machines and specific tooling equipment\n• Qualify industrial means related to manufacturing, repairs and rework\n• Ensure the technology watch to evolve process and manufacturing means\n• Develop and insure the follow-up of the performance indicators of production tools and set up the associated action plans (predictive, preventive or curative actions)\n• Complies with EHS Alstom, Ethics and Compliance policies and external standards\n• Issue relevant documents in the Quality System\n• Ensure schedules, inputs and QCD targets are achieved\n\nExecution / Serial manufacturing:\n• Guarantees internal control and good application of process rules in line with customers’ requirements\n• Insure the maintenance of the production equipment\n• Manage maintenance and control of active tools on site and at subcontractors\n• In case of non-conformity or incident, investigate root causes, finds and implement corrective solutions\n• Contribute to industrial REX on manufacturing processes\n\nAll about you\n\nWe value passion and attitude over experience. That’s why we don’t expect you to have every single skill. Instead, we’ve listed some that we think will help you succeed and grow in this role:\n• Engineering degree in electrical, electromechanical or mechanical is mandatory\n• Minimum 5 years of experience in manufacturing or industrial engineering preferably for electrical products\n• 3-5 years of experience in industrial methods, work instructions development, special process, wiring/assembly engineering, cabinet integration, electrical manufacturing engineering, signalling/telecom/automation experience is a strong asset\n• Experience with Time analysis (MTM, MEK, UAS), MBOM/EBOM concepts, electrical diagram interpretation, wiring, routing, cable preparation, terminal blocks and manufacturing processes in electrical assembly\n• Experience in process engineering, design, lean manufacturing, and industrial operations\n• Excellent technical problem solving\n• Proficiency in ERP tools (e.g. SAP) for Bill of Materials, routings, and configuration follow-up\n• Strong knowledge of CAD and Product Lifecycle Management tools (e.g. CATIA, DELMIA, ENOVIA)\n• Understanding of Quality, EHS standards, ergonomics, and operations management\n• Knowledge of project management, production management and process FMEA methodologies\n• Fluent in English\n• Desirable: Familiarity with railway industry practices and signaling products\n\nThings you’ll enjoy Join us on a life-long transformative journey – the rail industry is here to stay, so you can grow and develop new skills and experiences throughout your career. You’ll also:\n• Enjoy stability, challenges, and a long-term career free from boring daily routines.\n• Work with new security standards for rail signalling.\n• Collaborate with transverse teams and helpful colleagues.\n• Contribute to innovative projects shaping the future of mobility.\n• Utilise our flexible and inclusive working environment.\n• Steer your career in whatever direction you choose across functions and countries.\n• Benefit from our investment in your development, through award-winning learning programs.\n• Progress towards senior leadership or technical expert roles.\n• Benefit from a fair and dynamic reward package that recognises your performance and potential, plus comprehensive and competitive social coverage (life, medical, pension).\n\nYou don’t need to be a train enthusiast to thrive with us. We guarantee that when you step onto one of our trains with your friends or family, you’ll be proud. If you’re up for the challenge, we’d love to hear from you!\n\nImportant to note\n\nAs a global business, we’re an equal-opportunity employer that celebrates diversity across the 63 countries we operate in. We’re committed to creating an inclusive workplace for everyone.\n\nJob Type:​Experienced​',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'manufacturing,ll,production,industrialization,manufacturing processes,ehs,industrial,process,processes,rules,set,electrical,tools,methods,work,time,special,assembly,work instructions,test,cable,special process,mbom,wiring,mobility'),(114,'jsearch','vof5ztCINH_0P1xYAAAAAA==','Senior Manager - Energy Engineering – Industrial','Edison Energy',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697b99c256210e2729206911-senior-manager---energy-engineering---industrial','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America, United States\n\nTrio is a global energy and sustainability advisory company that helps large commercial, industrial, and institutional organizations navigate the energy landscape. Trio provides integrated strategy and implementation offerings across energy supply management, data management, energy optimization and electrification, clean energy, and sustainability to help the world’s largest organizations deliver on their strategic objectives and priorities.\n\nThe Trio family of companies are wholly owned subsidiaries of Edison International (NYSE: EIX).\n\nPosition Overview:\n\nWe are seeking an experienced professional with a full understanding of relevant engineering concepts and experience with energy consulting projects, including energy audits, retro-commissioning (RCx) studies, conceptual development of capital energy efficiency, carbon reduction, renewable energy projects, and ability to resolve a variety of technical client issues. This is a client facing role that will include working with our Sales team to support Business Development efforts. This team member will lead a high performing team on exciting energy efficiency consulting projects. This job requires a fully qualified engineer who has shown previous success as a Project Manager or Senior Energy Engineer.\n\nJob Responsibilities:\n• Lead completion of energy audits, retro-commissioning, investigations, and carbon reduction (decarbonization) audits of various facilities - primarily in industrial facilities, occasionally including healthcare, laboratory, higher education, commercial, and municipal facilities.\n• Lead business development from the service line by analyzing market trends, partnering with sales staff for client outreach strategies, developing proposals, scopes of work, etc. and participating in discussions with clients as the subject matter expert.\n• Identify energy conservation projects that include both capital and operational measures\n• Analyze data from temporary data loggers, permanent submeters, and customer provided BMS trend data to identify and quantify opportunities\n• Troubleshoot faulty systems and provide recommendations for corrective actions\n• Perform calculations of energy savings and help develop calculation templates\n• Prepare project implementation cost estimates\n• Review engineering designs, shop drawings, operation & maintenance manuals, and other construction documentation\n• Prepare technical reports and presentations and assist in presenting to clients and senior leaders\n• Ensure that savings projects for identified projects are plausible and financial risk is identified\n• Experience with ongoing measurement and verification of projected energy savings is a plus\n• Attend jobsite meetings and field surveys as required\n• Manage execution of projects and associated staff assignments to ensure timely client deliverables and quality\n• Work with national clients to help achieve sustainability goals\n• Develop and train Project Engineers and Associate Project Engineers\nEssential Functions:\n• Drive repeat business through excellent work; identify cross-sell and portfolio expansion opportunities\n• Collaborate directly with sales and marketing teams\n• In-depth knowledge of HVAC systems (steam, air and water distribution systems, etc.)\n• Field experience with HVAC systems - boiler, chillers, air-handlers, etc.\n• Knowledge of process systems (Compressed air, process heating, process cooling, purified water, GMP / clean rooms, etc.)\n• Experience in estimating HVAC and other energy project costs\n• Experience in financial analysis of various energy projects\n• Experience in measurement and verification of projected energy savings\n• Familiarity with the Greenhouse Gas Protocol, Electrification projects, commercial and industrial heat pumps.\n• A willingness to learn and work in a team environment with extensive contact with clients\n• Ability to work autonomously and independently\n• Strong computer skills (Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams, Power Point)\n• Ability to travel up to 30%\n• Determine methods and procedures on new assignments and coordinate activities of other personnel\n• Contribute to and coordinate team development activities (training, tool development, etc.)\n• Actively pursue technical development in areas relevant to project/team needs\n• Share knowledge via team trainings upon request\n• Assist with tool development without guidance\n• Present audit and strategy results to clients virtually and/or in-person as needed\n• Manage energy engineers and senior energy engineers on projects\nRequirements:\n• 10-15 years of experience in the energy and/or retro-commissioning field\n• Previous experience conducting on site analysis and leading ECM investigations.\n• Proven track record of new business development and client retention\n• BS in engineering or higher\n• Client facing communication skills\n• Valid driver’s license is required\n• CEM certification\nPreferred:\n• LEED AP, and other technical certifications a plus\n• EIT/PE License\n• Networks with key contacts outside own area of expertise\n• Business development skills and contributions with new and existing clients\nBenefits for Full-Time Employees:\n• Generous Paid Time Off (includes but not limited to Paid Parental Leave, Bereavement, Jury Duty, Sick, Vacation, etc.)\n• National Holiday Pay & Floating Holidays\n• 401(k) Employer Matching\n• Health Benefits: Medical, Dental, Vision\n• Paid Parental Leave (Short term disability and 6 weeks of paid parental leave unless superseded by any state-specific benefits.) \n• Employer 100% Paid Life Insurance Benefits\n• Employer 100% Paid Short Term and Long-Term Disability\n• Supplemental (Flexible Spending Accounts, Commuter Benefits, Cancer/Critical Care, Hospitalization, Accident)\n• Parent Company ESPP\n• Education tuition or certification reimbursement program (from an accredited institution for college level and/or advance degree)\n• Short Term Incentive (STI) Bonus Based on Performance Goals\n\n#LI-Remote\n\nTrio is committed to building a diverse and inclusive workplace. We are a proud Equal Opportunity Employer and will not discriminate based on race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national original, age, disability, protected veteran status or any other protected status.  \n\nThis employer participates in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm that you are authorized to work in the U.S. If E-Verify cannot confirm that you are authorized to work, this employer is required to give you written instructions and an opportunity to contact Department of Homeland Security (DHS) or Social Security Administration (SSA) so you can begin to resolve the issue before the employer can take any action against you, including terminating your employment. Employers can only use E-Verify once you have accepted a job offer and completed the Form I-9.\n\nNOTE: Trio is not the same company as Southern California Edison, the utility, and Trio is not regulated by the California Public Utilities Commission.\nThis offer from \"Edison Energy\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'energy,client,clients,trio,employer,projects,business,business development,development,term,savings,team,paid,experience,verify,air,commercial,edison,audits,retro commissioning,retro,energy savings,disability,sales,parental leave'),(115,'jsearch','OmzKfS_6e6u2n6HEAAAAAA==','Chemical Engineer – Manufacturing Plant, Professional','National Water Commission (NWC)','Port Antonio','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/chemical-engineer-manufacturing-plant-professional/','About Company\n\nThe National Water Commission (NWC) is Jamaica\'s leading provider of water and wastewater services, dedicated to delivering safe, reliable, and high-quality water to homes, businesses, and industries across the island. For decades, NWC has been a cornerstone of public health and economic development, operating a vast network of water treatment plants, pumping stations, and distribution systems. Our commitment extends beyond mere utility provision; we are deeply invested in environmental stewardship, sustainable resource management, and employing innovative technologies to enhance service delivery and meet the evolving needs of the Jamaican population. At NWC, we believe in fostering a culture of excellence, continuous learning, and community engagement, ensuring that our operations not only provide essential services but also contribute positively to the well-being and prosperity of Jamaica. Join a team where your expertise directly impacts the lives of millions and helps shape the future of a vital national resource.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Chemical Engineer to join our professional team at our water treatment manufacturing plant in Port Antonio, Portland Parish. This critical role involves the application of chemical engineering principles to optimize and manage the complex processes involved in producing potable water, which we consider a highly refined manufacturing process. As a Chemical Engineer, you will be instrumental in ensuring the efficiency, quality, and compliance of our water treatment operations, from raw water intake to final distribution. You will be responsible for process design, optimization, troubleshooting, and quality control, working with a diverse range of chemical and physical treatment methods. This position requires a proactive problem-solver with a strong understanding of environmental regulations, process safety, and advanced water treatment technologies. You will play a pivotal role in maintaining the highest standards of water quality, ensuring that our operations meet or exceed national and international benchmarks. This is an excellent opportunity for a professional chemical engineer to make a significant impact on public health and environmental sustainability in Jamaica, contributing to an essential service within a dynamic and challenging operational environment. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams, including operations, maintenance, and environmental compliance, to drive continuous improvement and innovation.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, optimize, and monitor chemical and physical water treatment processes to ensure efficiency, cost-effectiveness, and compliance with regulatory standards.\n• Conduct comprehensive analysis of water quality data, identify trends, and implement corrective actions to maintain optimal water parameters.\n• Develop and implement Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) for chemical dosing, plant operations, and safety protocols.\n• Troubleshoot operational issues related to chemical processes, equipment performance, and water quality deviations.\n• Manage chemical procurement, storage, and handling, ensuring adherence to safety regulations and environmental guidelines.\n• Lead or participate in process improvement projects, including the evaluation and implementation of new technologies and methodologies.\n• Prepare detailed technical reports, presentations, and documentation for internal and external stakeholders.\n• Ensure strict compliance with local and international environmental, health, and safety (EHS) regulations.\n• Provide technical guidance and training to plant operators and other staff members on chemical processes and safety procedures.\n• Collaborate with R&D, environmental, and maintenance teams to drive innovation and continuous improvement initiatives.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Chemical Engineering or a closely related field from an accredited institution.\n• Minimum of 4 years of progressive experience in chemical process engineering, preferably within water treatment, wastewater treatment, or a related continuous process manufacturing industry.\n• Strong understanding of water chemistry, treatment technologies (e.g., coagulation, flocculation, sedimentation, filtration, disinfection), and chemical dosing systems.\n• Proficiency in process simulation and optimization software.\n• Demonstrated experience with regulatory compliance and environmental permitting.\n• Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills for technical reporting and interdepartmental collaboration.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s degree in Chemical Engineering or Environmental Engineering.\n• Professional Engineering (PE) license or eligibility for registration with the Professional Engineers Registration Board of Jamaica (PERBJ).\n• Experience with SCADA systems and process control automation.\n• Familiarity with ISO 9001 and ISO 14001 standards.\n• Project management experience in an industrial setting.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Pension plan with company contributions.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous training.\n• Generous paid time off and holidays.\n• A supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Meaningful work that contributes directly to public health and national development.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates who meet the requirements are encouraged to apply by clicking on the application link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience and qualifications for this specialized role.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'chemical,water,treatment,environmental,water treatment,process,chemical engineer,nwc,water quality,public health,meet,national,professional,compliance,safety,technologies,quality,public,chemical engineering,operations,continuous,health,processes,plant,engineering'),(117,'jsearch','w6lXcJ1nRJzULpB8AAAAAA==','Chemical Engineer – Manufacturing Plant (Experienced)','Wisynco Group Limited',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/chemical-engineer-manufacturing-plant-experienced/','About Company\n\nWisynco Group Limited is a leading Jamaican manufacturer and distributor of an extensive portfolio of food, beverages, and industrial products. For over 55 years, Wisynco has been committed to enhancing the lives of Jamaicans by consistently delivering high-quality products and fostering sustainable practices. With a diverse range of beloved brands and a robust manufacturing infrastructure, we are at the forefront of innovation in the Caribbean\'s consumer goods sector. Our state-of-the-art facilities and dedicated team drive our mission to maintain excellence in all aspects of our operations, from sourcing to production and distribution. We pride ourselves on a dynamic, collaborative culture that values continuous improvement, safety, and environmental stewardship, making Wisynco not just a workplace, but a community where careers thrive.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you an experienced Chemical Engineer with a passion for optimizing industrial processes and driving innovation in a dynamic manufacturing environment? Wisynco Group Limited is seeking a highly skilled and results-oriented Chemical Engineer to join our thriving manufacturing plant team in Hope Pastures, St. Andrew. In this pivotal role, you will be instrumental in the design, development, optimization, and troubleshooting of our production processes for a wide array of consumer goods, beverages, and industrial products.\n\nAs a key contributor, you will leverage your expertise to enhance operational efficiency, ensure product quality, and uphold stringent safety and environmental standards. You will be responsible for identifying opportunities for process improvement, implementing cost-saving measures, and scaling production while maintaining consistency and compliance. This position requires a proactive problem-solver with a strong analytical mind, capable of working collaboratively with cross-functional teams including production, quality assurance, research & development, and maintenance.\n\nYour day-to-day will involve hands-on engagement with our state-of-the-art equipment and systems, from raw material conversion to final product packaging. You will conduct experiments, analyze data, and provide technical guidance to production staff, playing a crucial role in preventing and resolving operational challenges. Beyond current operations, you will contribute to strategic planning for new product development and facility expansions, ensuring that our manufacturing capabilities remain at the cutting edge. This is an unparalleled opportunity to make a tangible impact on processes that deliver essential and beloved products to communities across Jamaica and beyond. If you are ready to apply your advanced engineering skills in a challenging yet rewarding setting, and contribute to a legacy of excellence, we encourage you to apply.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, optimize, and troubleshoot manufacturing processes to improve efficiency, quality, and cost-effectiveness.\n• Monitor and analyze process performance data, identifying trends, deviations, and areas for improvement.\n• Implement and manage process control systems to ensure consistent product quality and operational stability.\n• Lead and participate in root cause analysis for production issues, developing and implementing corrective and preventative actions.\n• Collaborate with R&D teams on new product development and scale-up from pilot to full production.\n• Ensure all processes comply with industry standards, regulatory requirements, and internal safety protocols.\n• Prepare technical reports, process documentation, and operational procedures.\n• Mentor junior engineers and technical staff, fostering a culture of continuous learning and improvement.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Chemical Engineering or a related field\n• Minimum of 4 years of proven experience in a manufacturing plant environment\n• Strong understanding of process design, optimization, and control principles\n• Proficiency in process simulation software and data analysis tools\n• Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and critical thinking skills\n• Solid knowledge of safety regulations and quality assurance standards (e.g., ISO, HACCP)\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s degree in Chemical Engineering or related discipline\n• Experience in the food & beverage or consumer goods manufacturing industry\n• Project management certification (e.g., PMP)\n• Lean Six Sigma Green or Black Belt certification\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance\n• Generous paid time off and holidays\n• Retirement savings plan with company match\n• Professional development and training opportunities\n• Employee wellness programs and on-site facilities\n• Opportunities for career advancement within a leading company\n• Product discounts\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application by clicking the link below. Please include a detailed resume and a cover letter outlining your experience and qualifications relevant to this role.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'product,chemical,manufacturing,production,wisynco,process,consumer,consumer goods,goods,processes,products,quality,chemical engineer,manufacturing plant,safety,beverages industrial,wisynco group,group limited,new product,product quality,industrial products,product development,safety environmental,data,development'),(120,'jsearch','8EKZK59YNtdGhkS-AAAAAA==','JUNIOR ENGINEER - PROCESS CONTROL SYSTEMS','Automatic & Computers Systems Ltd.',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/JUNIOR-ENGINEER-PROCESS-CONTROL-SYSTEMS-Job-226082.aspx','A leading manufacturing company is seeking suitably qualified candidates for the position of: JUNIOR ENGINEER - PROCESS CONTROL SYSTEMS Key Responsibilities: Monitor Local Control Network (LCN) and Universal Control Network (UCN) health on a daily basis and resolve identified issues. Maintain process control system health by effective predictive, preventative and corrective maintenance practices. Provide on-call support for the process control infrastructure and applications. Complete System compliance audits and close-out of associated actions. Assist with PCN/LCN/UCN infrastructure upgrades and maintenance. Troubleshoot and resolve electrical and operational problems with installed systems. Demonstrate a strong commitment to the company’s policies and values for environment, health and safety. Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Systems, Electrical Engineering or Electronics Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite Strong analytical, problem solving, and troubleshooting skills. Effective oral and written communications skills. Assets: Experience with Honeywell Experion or Total Plant Solution (TPS) System Maintenance and electrical engineering experience Applications along with resumes should be submitted no later than February 28, 2026 to the Services Manager.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'process control,control,process,health,control network,ucn,lcn,junior engineer,engineer process,systems,applications,network,junior,maintenance,company,infrastructure,effective,resolve,control systems,electrical,skills,electrical engineering,total,safety requirements,complete compliance'),(122,'jsearch','q-V9JYsxS3O0UVX_AAAAAA==','Electrical Technician','Discovery Bauxite Atlantic Alumina',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Electrical-Technician-Job-226592.aspx','Electrical Technician The successful candidate will be responsible for troubleshooting and repairing critical safety devices, power generation and railway control systems in addition to the general Plant instrumentation, power and control systems to maintain the highest levels of equipment availability. Main Responsibilities include: Maintain, repair, install and troubleshoot plant electrical systems and instrumentation - electrical motors, generators, hydraulics and pneumatic electrical control systems, switch gears, transformers, switchboard metres, regulators. Test electrical and electronic equipment and components for continuity, current voltage and resistance. Conduct preventive maintenance programmes and keeps maintenance records. Install examine replace or repair electrical wiring, receptacle and other electrical components. Collaborate with other craftsmen and operating personnel in carrying out maintenance activities. Participate in Reliability Centred Maintenance activities inclusive of gathering CM data, assessing equipment condition and risks of failure and recommending mitigation actions to maximize equipment accuracy, uptime and efficiencies. Read and interpret drawings and electrical code specifications to determine layout of industrial equipment installation. Identify and correct boiler defects. Calibrate Instrumentation. Prepare calibration records. Identify and order parts and electrical components subject to the requisite approvals Required Competencies: Working knowledge of Programmable Logic Controllers and Industrial Instrumentation. Demonstrated ability to solve complex maintenance problems and sound understanding of electrical and mechanical maintenance processes. Demonstrated ability to analyze electrical systems and their interaction with associated mechanical systems/hydraulic systems and associated equipment. Ability to prioritize across multiple projects. Excellent troubleshooting and condition monitoring techniques. Proficiency with PC-based software applications including Microsoft Office. Qualifications and Experience: Bachelors Degree or Diploma in Electrical /Instrumentation Engineering. Three (3) to five (5) years experience in industrial controls and instrumentation.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'electrical,instrumentation,systems,maintenance,equipment,components,industrial,control systems,associated,electrical components,electrical technician,electrical systems,demonstrated ability,install,demonstrated,plant,maintenance activities,ability,control,condition,activities,identify,records,troubleshooting,power'),(123,'jsearch','BNrjUqKLhdekUkpPAAAAAA==','Electrical Engineer – Power Systems, Full-Time','Jamaica Public Service Company Limited (JPSCo)','Old Harbour','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/electrical-engineer-power-systems-full-time/','About Company\n\nJamaica Public Service Company Limited (JPSCo) is the sole integrated electric utility company in Jamaica, responsible for generating, transmitting, and distributing electricity to over 600,000 customers island-wide. As an essential service provider, JPSCo is committed to powering Jamaica\'s progress through reliable, safe, and efficient energy solutions. We are at the forefront of modernizing our grid, investing in renewable energy, and enhancing our infrastructure to meet the growing demands of the nation while fostering sustainable development. Our team comprises dedicated professionals who are passionate about innovation, operational excellence, and making a tangible impact on the lives of Jamaicans. Join us in shaping the future of energy in the Caribbean.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Electrical Engineer with a specialization in Power Systems to join our dynamic team in Old Harbour. This critical role involves contributing to the design, analysis, operation, and maintenance of our extensive power generation, transmission, and distribution systems. The successful candidate will play a pivotal role in ensuring the reliability, efficiency, and safety of Jamaica\'s electrical grid. You will be instrumental in identifying system improvements, implementing new technologies, and resolving complex technical challenges related to power quality, grid stability, and infrastructure upgrades. This position offers a unique opportunity to work on large-scale projects that directly impact national development and to advance your career within a leading utility company committed to innovation and sustainability. We value proactive problem-solvers who can work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment and demonstrate a strong commitment to engineering best practices and safety standards.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Design, analyze, and optimize power system components including generators, transformers, switchgear, protection relays, and control systems.\n\n• Conduct power system studies, including load flow, short circuit, stability, and harmonic analysis, using specialized software (e.g., ETAP, PSS/E, PSCAD).\n\n• Develop and implement protection schemes for transmission and distribution networks to ensure grid reliability and safety.\n\n• Oversee the installation, testing, and commissioning of new electrical infrastructure and equipment.\n\n• Diagnose and troubleshoot complex electrical system faults, proposing and implementing effective solutions.\n\n• Prepare technical specifications, reports, and documentation for projects, adhering to international and local engineering standards.\n\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including operations, maintenance, and project management, to deliver successful projects.\n\n• Stay abreast of emerging technologies and industry best practices in power systems engineering.\n\nRequired Skills\n\n• Bachelor\'s Degree in Electrical Engineering with a focus on Power Systems.\n\n• Minimum of 3 years of progressive experience in power systems engineering, preferably within a utility or heavy industrial environment.\n\n• Proficiency in power system analysis software (e.g., ETAP, PSS/E, DigSilent PowerFactory).\n\n• Strong understanding of electrical codes, standards (e.g., IEEE, IEC, ANSI), and safety regulations.\n\n• Demonstrated experience with protection and control systems for high voltage networks.\n\n• Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills.\n\n• Effective communication skills, both written and verbal, for technical reporting and collaboration.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• Master\'s Degree in Electrical Engineering or a related field.\n\n• Professional Engineer (PE) license or eligibility for registration with the Professional Engineers Registration Board (PERB) of Jamaica.\n\n• Experience with renewable energy integration into traditional grids.\n\n• Project management experience in an engineering context.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and life insurance plans.\n\n• Defined contribution pension scheme.\n\n• Opportunities for continuous professional development and training.\n\n• Company vehicle or vehicle allowance.\n\n• Employee wellness programs and a supportive work environment.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application, including a detailed resume and cover letter, through our official careers portal. Please ensure your application highlights your relevant experience in power systems engineering and your alignment with the required skills. We encourage you to apply promptly as applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Click on the application link below to proceed with your submission.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'power,power systems,grid,systems,jamaica,company,engineering,electrical,protection,systems engineering,application,energy,utility,safety,analysis,skills,including,etap pss,registration,pss,transmission distribution,transmission,stability,company jamaica,impact'),(125,'jsearch','6ZCl-nXlSzA2EKqlAAAAAA==','RF Engineer (Onsite) / Core Network Engineer (Onsite) / Microwave Engineer (Onsite)','Confidential',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/RF-Engineer-Onsite-Core-Network-Job-226037.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','1. Radio Frequency Engineer (Onsite) Job Responsibilities for Radio Frequecy Engineer include, but are not limited to the following: 1. Improve and optimize network experience, including OSS and drive test KPI 2. Responsible for the wireless network optimization project delivery, rollout site verification and output report: - GSM, UMTS, LTE Radio Network planning (site design, audit, simulation, link budget, cell planning, parameter design, site survey, model tuning, etc) - GSM, UMTS, LTE Radio Network optimization (Drive test, site RF tuning and performance & parameter optimization, site delivery, trouble shooting, etc)- Optimizes new and existing network elements, links budget analysis, system dimensioning for coverage and capacity, initial system design and dimensioning, site identification and evaluation and zones analysis. - Customer technical communication and internal organization, project management and be able to independently communicate with customers about network performance and handle VIP issues Qualification and Requirements for Radio Frequency Engineer 1. Have understanding of GSM, UMTS, and LTE radio network knowledge, be able to comprehensively improve network performance, including network rate, accessibility, and retainability 2. English to be used as the working language, 3. willingness for overtime work and cross-country business trips 4. At least 3 years of project delivery experience in the mobile network domain (e.g. FTTX, GSM, UMTS or CDMA Project) 2. Core Network Engineer - (Onsite) Job Responsibilitiesfor Core Network Engineer include, but are not limited to, the following: 1. Act as the core network delivery Technical Engineer (TE), Team Lead (TL), or Technical Director (TD) responsible for the foll owi ng tasks during Core Network CS&IMS/PS/5G/HSS/PCRF/DRA projects: 2. Network design, installation, and deployment. Interconnection commissioning, system cutover, upgrades, and capacity expansion s. Ensure seamless communication support for major events, guaranteeing data and voice service availability. 3. Facilitate effective communication with customers throughout the project delivery lifecycle to ensure successful delivery and ma intain high levels of customer satisfaction. 4. Be open and available for business travel across Central America and the Caribbean to provide technical support to projects i n n ear by countries Professional Service Skills Requirement for Core Network Engineer: 1. Strong ability to communicate technical solutions, project plans, and progress updates with junior level customer representatives, securing customer support and trust. 2. Ability to accurately understand, analyze, and manage customer requirements while translating them into actionable and feasible technical solutions. 3. Proactively identify and mitigate technical risks, such as: Delivery strategies, Technical solutions and designs, Cybersecurity compliance and related challenges. 4. Address and resolve technical challenges during project execution by: Developing effective solution plans.Conducting design reviews, quality controls, and on site construction supervisions. Tracking partner performance and progress to ensure adherence to process specifications. 5. Possess at least 2 years of experience in the telecommunications or IT industry, with expertise in relevant technologies such as: • Telecom: Core network, IP, network management, etc. • IT: Operating Systems (OS), databases, cloud platforms, virtualization, and middleware. Professional Knowledge Requirements for Cor Network Engineer 1. Proficient understanding of CS, IMS, NGN, HSS, PCRF, PS, NFV, and IT related products from any vendor. Preferably, hands on experience with developing, testing, and maintaining core network products, such as NFVI, MANO, CS/PS, and 5GC. 2. Familiar with call signaling protocols, network evolution strategies, and datacom network design and commissioning within the communications industry. 3. Knowledgeable in IT system architecture, Internet system development, and operational best practices. 4. Basic expertise in public, private, or hybrid cloud environments, including: - Cloud network design principles, - Integration, implementation, and operational strategies. 3. Microwave Engineer (onsite) Position responsibilities for microwave engineer include, but are not limited to, the following: 1. System Design: Designing microwave communication systems based on project requirements and specifications. 2. Network Planning: Conducting network planning activities, such as link budget calculations, path analysis, and frequency plan nin g for microwave communication networks. 3. Installation and Commissioning: Overseeing the installation and commissioning of microwave equipment and antennas, ensuring p rop er alignment and configuration. 4. System Troubleshooting: Identifying and resolving technical issues with microwave networks, performing troubleshooting activi tie s, and implementing necessary corrective actions. 5. Performance Optimization: Monitoring and optimizing the performance of microwave networks, analyzing performance metrics, and making recommendations for improvements 6. Documentation and Reporting: Maintaining accurate documentation of network configurations, performing regular reporting on ne two rk performance and status, and providing technical reports as required Knowledge and Skillset requirements for Microwave engineer 1. Bachelor’s Degree or above in communication engineering, electrical engineering, photoelectric engineering, computer field or re lated fields. 2. Technical knowledge both in microwave theory and microwave equipment. 3. Understand well microwave project delivery flow, and with project management knowledge. 4. Capability of microwave maintenance and troubleshooting. 5. IP knowledge. 6. Excellent team spirit with good communications and interpersonal skill, having the service consciousness. 7. Good English listening, speaking, reading and writing skill.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'network,microwave,engineer,technical,delivery,core network,project,site,performance,design,core,radio,onsite,engineer onsite,network engineer,knowledge,communication,optimization,umts,gsm,gsm umts,microwave engineer,project delivery,commissioning,customer'),(126,'jsearch','h7BveOBmgxf0m8DVAAAAAA==','Electrical Support Engineer - North West','Easthampstead',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.justjobs.co.uk/jobs/electrical-support-engineer-north-west-2c80de1e?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Electrician\'s Mate\n\nLocation: UK-wide (Field Based)\n\nEmployment Type: Full-time | Permanent\n\nSalary: £35,000 - £45,000\n\nOverview\n\nWe\'re looking for an experienced Electrician\'s Mate to support commercial and renewable electrical installations across the UK. The role involves hands-on site work, assisting qualified electricians with all aspects of installation, testing, and commissioning. Ideal for someone keen to develop their trade skills within a professional and safety-driven environment.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nSupport electricians with commercial and renewable installations.\nAssist with containment, cable routing, pulling, fixing, and termination.\nHelp with testing and commissioning under supervision.\nMaintain high safety and quality standards on-site.\nReport progress or issues to the site lead or project manager.\nEssential Requirements\n\nExperience as an Electrician\'s Mate, Electrical Improver, or Electrical Labourer.\nValid ECS or CSCS card.\nCity & Guilds or EAL Level 2 and Level 3 Electrical Installations (Building & Structures).\nFull UK driving licence and own transport.\nDesirable Qualifications\n\nNVQ Level 3 or equivalent.\nAM2 Assessment.\n2391/2394/2395 Inspection & Testing.\nPV or EV Installation Course (C&G, EAL, or BPEC).\nECS Gold Card.\nOffer\n\nSalary £35,000-£45,000 depending on experience.\nCareer progression and on-site development.\nInvolvement in large-scale commercial and renewable projects',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'000,electrician mate,commercial,commercial renewable,electrician,mate,uk,site,renewable,level,installations,eal,electricians,000 45,45,35,35 000,salary 35,card,electrical installations,45 000,ecs,testing,electrical,testing commissioning'),(127,'jsearch','B3QwVMx1QpuPKGKMAAAAAA==','Business Solutions Engineer','Digicel',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.recruit.net/job/business-solutions-engineer-jobs/9245A78DE9576B8A','Primary Objective of Job:\nThe Business Solutions Engineer is responsible for the design, implementation, and maintenance of Digicel\'s Business Solutions portfolio. This role ensures service delivery excellence by providing superior technical support to clients and maintaining high availability of solutions in line with agreed SLAs.\n\nMain Duties & Responsibilities:\nSolution Design & Planning\n• Develop technical designs, budgets, and implementation plans for Business Solutions products (cloud services, M2M, connectivity, data management, etc.)\n• Complete service questionnaires, scope of work documents, and proposals to support solution delivery\n\nImplementation & Deployment\n• Oversee end-to-end service installation at client sites\n• Interface with vendors for hardware/software supply, delivery, and installation\n• Ensure accurate and up-to-date network and solution documentation\n\nTechnical Support & Maintenance\n• Provide timely technical support to clients and internal sales teams\n• Perform corrective and preventative maintenance to ensure infrastructure availability\n• Respond to emergencies, outages, and potential failures within the Business Solutions infrastructure\n\nInnovation & Improvement\n• Research, evaluate, and simulate new hardware, software, and services aligned with Business Solutions strategy\n• Continuously review infrastructure resiliency plans and recommend improvements\n• Prepare incident and outage reports for internal teams and clients\n\nCollaboration & Compliance\n• Ensure SLA targets are met through timely response to Sales team requests\n• Work closely with internal departments and external providers\n• Perform any other related duties as assigned\n\nAcademic qualifications and experience required:\nEducation\n• Diploma or degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related field\n\nCertifications\nRecognized professional certification in IT, IP, or Telecommunications (e.g., CCNA, Azure Fundamentals, MTA)\nExperience\n• Minimum of 3 years in implementation and maintenance of IT or Telecommunications infrastructure\n• Hands-on experience with Business Solutions in a telecom environment preferred\n\nFunctional Skills:\n• Strong knowledge of:\n\nCloud platforms (Azure, Microsoft 365)\nWindows Server environments (2008+)\nNetworking (Cisco, Fortinet, TCP/IP, LAN/WAN, VLANs, firewalls, SIP)\nVirtualization technologies (VMware, Hyper-V)\nVoIP systems (Avaya)\n• Understanding of telecom Business Solutions (cloud, M2M, connectivity)\n• Excellent problem-solving, documentation, and client communication skills',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'business solutions,business,solutions,implementation,infrastructure,technical support,internal,clients,delivery,cloud,solution,support,hardware,support clients,hardware software,m2m connectivity,implementation maintenance,sales,solutions engineer,m2m,end,duties,connectivity,client,azure'),(140,'jsearch','kSUwBkNoAbBwzBrBAAAAAA==','Technical Lead, Developer Experience','The Browser Company',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6999cf97da7696de2f5a8bd1-technical-lead-developer-experience?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America\n\nHi, we\'re The Browser Company ? and we\'re building a better way to use the internet.\n\nBrowsers are unique in that they are one of the only pieces of software that you share with your parents as well as your kids. Which makes sense, they\'re our doorway to the most important things — through them we socialize with loved ones, work on our passion projects, and explore our curiosities. But on their own, they don’t actually do a whole lot, they’re kind of just there. They don’t help us organize our messy lives or make it easier to compose our ideas. We believe that the browser could do so much more — it can empower and support the amazing things we do on the internet. That’s why we’re building one: a browser that can help us grow, create, and stay curious.\n\nTo accomplish this lofty task, we’re building a diverse team of people from different backgrounds and experiences. This isn’t optional, it’s crucial to our mission, as we need a wide range of perspectives to challenge our assumptions and shape our browser through a bold, creative lens. With that in mind, we especially encourage women, people of color, and others from historically marginalized groups to apply.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nBuilding software is changing. With modern AI coding tools and automated reviewers, the bottlenecks in shipping products are shifting from “how fast can you type” to “how have you designed the system that writes, reviews, and ships the code.” At The Browser Company, we believe this shift is so profound that how we build is as important, and ultimately as defensible, as what we build.\n\nWe’re investing deeply in “building how we build”: an AI‑native development stack that turns our way of working into compounding leverage for every engineer and team. Our vision is a world where most code is generated and reviewed by AI, where model training and prompt optimization are automated, and where product builders operate at a higher layer—seeing trends, deciding what to build, and clicking the “right” buttons rather than hand‑crafting every line.\n\nAs our Technical Lead for Developer Experience at Browser Company, you won’t just maintain tools or CI pipelines–you’ll lead the creation of a second product: an internal, AI‑powered software generation and review platform that changes how Dia gets built.\n\nOverall you will...\n• Design and lead the “build how we build” platform: an internal SaaS‑like experience where engineers and non‑engineers can describe what they want, and our system realizes the rest.\n• Partner with AI and infra teams to wire together the pieces we already have—AI coding tools, virtualized environments, CI, AI code reviewers, evals, and prompt and model optimization—into a cohesive, opinionated product that our teams love to use.\n• Define success metrics for this platform and iterate quickly based on real usage and feedback from our engineers.\n• Turn our DevEx stack into true leverage, so that every engineer and PM can move with 10x more impact.\n\nQualifications\n• 5+ years of experience with developer tools and build environments, open-source developer tooling, or low-level systems experience.\n• Experience owning a zero‑to‑one product or platform, ideally in a role with founder‑like autonomy (founder/CTO, tech lead, staff/principal on a platform or DevEx team).\n• You\'re passionate about building tools and systems that make other engineers more productive and strive to make them elegant and maintainable.\n• You thrive in a high‑trust, high‑ambiguity environment: you seek feedback, but you don’t need hand‑holding.\n• We’re primarily focused on hiring in North American time zones and require that folks have 4+ hours of overlap time with team members in Eastern Time Zone.\n\nCompensation and Benefits\n• Our total compensation package for full-time employees includes base salary, equity, and benefits. The annual salary range for this role is $290,000 - $340,000 USD. The actual salary offered will vary based on experience level and interview performance.\n• Benefits: We offer a wide range of perks and benefits designed to support you, your family, and help you engage with your local community. To learn more, visit go.atlassian.com/perksandbenefits.\n• Location: We’re a remote-friendly company and can hire in any country where Atlassian has a legal entity. If you live in New York (or want to visit), you’re welcome to work from our beautiful office in Williamsburg.\n\nThe Browser Company is an ambitious team of close to 100 people (and growing!) who are passionate about building great products. We are a remote-first, distributed team, with the option to work from office in Brooklyn, New York. We strongly support diversity and encourage people from all backgrounds to apply.\n\n? To read more about what we value as a company, check out Notes on Roadtrips on our blog.\nThis offer from \"The Browser Company\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,290000.00,340000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','browser,browser company,ai,company,build,lead,tools,building,platform,people,don,engineers,benefits,range,team,experience,time,passionate building,visit,backgrounds,model,leverage engineer,coding tools,pieces,reviewers'),(141,'jsearch','wXenIFGMItMQ4ZLUAAAAAA==','Systems Developer','TheHiveCareers',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/systems-developer-at-thehivecareers-4366869079?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Systems Developer\n\nRole Purpose:\n\nThe Systems Developer is responsible for developing, enhancing, and maintaining enterprise systems to meet business requirements. This role ensures that systems are reliable, efficient, and scalable while providing ongoing support and improvements.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Develop, enhance, and maintain enterprise applications and systems\n• Collaborate with business analysts and stakeholders to understand system requirements and translate them into technical solutions\n• Perform system testing, debugging, and performance tuning to ensure system reliability and efficiency\n• Provide maintenance and support for existing systems, including troubleshooting and resolving issues\n• Document system designs, changes, and operational procedures\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless integration with other systems and platforms\n• Stay updated with emerging technologies and recommend enhancements to improve system performance\n\nRequired Experience & Skills:\n• 5+ years of experience in systems development or software engineering\n• Strong knowledge of programming languages and development frameworks relevant to enterprise systems\n• Experience in system enhancements, maintenance, and support\n• Ability to analyze complex requirements and provide effective technical solutions\n• Strong problem-solving, debugging, and troubleshooting skills\n• Excellent communication and collaboration abilities\n\nPreferred (Nice to Have):\n• Experience with enterprise-level applications in banking, finance, or corporate environments\n• Familiarity with database design, APIs, and integration techniques\n• Exposure to Agile or DevOps development methodologies',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'systems,systems developer,enterprise,enterprise systems,maintenance support,support,debugging,enhancements,troubleshooting,developer,experience,technical solutions,integration,requirements,maintenance,issues document,enhance maintain,seamless integration,resolving,integration techniques,platforms stay,systems meet,technologies recommend,design apis,meet business'),(142,'jsearch','lht1knd8cetSR9axAAAAAA==','Systems Developer','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/Y63VW339?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Systems Developer\n\nRole Purpose:\n\nThe Systems Developer is responsible for developing, enhancing, and maintaining enterprise systems to meet business requirements. This role ensures that systems are reliable, efficient, and scalable while providing ongoing support and improvements.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Develop, enhance, and maintain enterprise applications and systems\n• Collaborate with business analysts and stakeholders to understand system requirements and translate them into technical solutions\n• Perform system testing, debugging, and performance tuning to ensure system reliability and efficiency\n• Provide maintenance and support for existing systems, including troubleshooting and resolving issues\n• Document system designs, changes, and operational procedures\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless integration with other systems and platforms\n• Stay updated with emerging technologies and recommend enhancements to improve system performance\n\nRequired Experience & Skills:\n• 5+ years of experience in systems development or software engineering\n• Strong knowledge of programming languages and development frameworks relevant to enterprise systems\n• Experience in system enhancements, maintenance, and support\n• Ability to analyze complex requirements and provide effective technical solutions\n• Strong problem-solving, debugging, and troubleshooting skills\n• Excellent communication and collaboration abilities\n\nPreferred (Nice to Have):\n• Experience with enterprise-level applications in banking, finance, or corporate environments\n• Familiarity with database design, APIs, and integration techniques\n• Exposure to Agile or DevOps development methodologies',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'systems,systems developer,enterprise,enhancements,maintenance support,troubleshooting,enterprise systems,debugging,maintenance,requirements,support,technical solutions,developer,experience,integration,provide,development,business,ensure,relevant enterprise,designs,issues document,debugging troubleshooting,tuning ensure,engineering strong'),(144,'jsearch','s55z7ZpwVXHykLHEAAAAAA==','Senior Frontend Engineer, Growth','CookUnity',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6999c1a2da7696de2f5a75dd-senior-frontend-engineer-growth?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nAbout CookUnity:\n\nFood has lost its soul to modern convenience. And with it, it has lost the power to nourish, inspire, and connect us. So in 2018, CookUnity was founded as the first-of-its-kind platform that connects the world with the source of truly great food: chefs. Today, CookUnity delivers 50 million meals a year from the industry’s best chefs to homes all over the country. Fresh. Ready-to-eat. And crafted with the passion that nourishes body and soul.\n\nUnwilling to stop there, CookUnity is expanding beyond delivery to become an ever-innovating marketplace focused on our singular mission: empower Chefs to nourish the world.\n\nIf that mission has you hungry in more ways than one, you’ve found the right job posting.\n\nAbout The Team:\n\nThe Growth Engineering team focuses on delivering an excellent customer experience from when a customer lands on CookUnity’s homepage through the sign-up process and finishing with checking out. The team tackles high-impact projects that delight our customers and deliver meaningful business value.\n\nThe Role:\n\nAs a Senior Engineer (front-end or full-stack) in Growth engineering, you will be instrumental in building and delivering a world-class experience to our customers. You will also define and uphold the highest engineering standards to build reliable performant applications.\n\nResponsibilities:\n• Serve as the subject matter expert in front end technologies including React and NextJs.\n• Mentor and educate developers on clean code methodologies through knowledge sharing and PR reviews\n• Work cross-functionally (Product and Design) to develop and deploy applications and features on time with high quality.\n• Implement best practices to enable the team to ship quality code faster.\n\nMinimum Requirements:\n• Prior experience building and shipping complex customer facing applications at scale.\n• You have at least +5yrs of experience as a Software Engineer, and you can engage with projects in ReactJS, NodeJS, GraphQL, MySQL, and TypeScript.\n• Passion for shipping world-class products for our users!\n• Have excellent communication skills for articulating complex technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders.\n• Willing to experiment with, test, and learn new technologies.\n• Handle ambiguity and quickly evolving priorities.\n• Be self-motivated and eager to learn new things!\n• Natural leadership qualities with the ability to inspire and guide cross-functional teams.\n• Advanced level of English.\n\nPreferred Requirements:\n• Are able to thrive on small, collaborative engineering teams.\n• Have experience in a fast-paced environment.\n• You\'re proficient in web development including performance (web vitals) monitoring.\n• Experience working with Docker/Kubernetes/CI environments.\n• Experience in the food technology sector is a plus.\n\nBenefits:\n\n? Get paid in USD.\n\n? Work remotely: design the life that you want.\n\n⛱ Enjoy 15 business days of vacation each year from the start date.\n\n? Healthcare Benefit: Monthly stipend to use in your preferred healthcare provider.\n\n? 16 fully paid Argentinean holidays.\n\n? Compassionate Leave: 3-5 days each time the need arises.\n\n? Paid family leave.\n\n?‍? Personalized English coach.\n\n??‍♀️Customize the benefits that suit your needs! Access a range of perks tailored to you, including learning opportunities, wellness memberships, delivery apps, and more through our comprehensive benefit platform.\n\n?️ 5- year Sabbatical: After 5 years with CookUnity, you get a 4-week paid sabbatical.\n\nLearn More About CookUnity:\n\nWe believe great leadership starts with alignment on vision, values, and ways of working. To give you deeper insight into who we are and what we’re looking for, we invite you to explore: CookUnity\'s Leadership Principles – The values and behaviors that guide how we operate, collaborate, and scale.\n\nWe hope this provides valuable insight into our culture and product vision. If this excites you, we’d love to connect!\n\nIf you’re interested in this role, please submit your application, and if we think you might be a fit, we\'ll get in touch with you. Thank you for your time!\n\nCookUnity is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are dedicated to creating a community of inclusion and an environment free from discrimination or harassment. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship status, protected veteran status, genetic information, or physical or mental disability.\n\nA quick note for all candidates\nWe’ve recently seen an increase in recruitment scams across the industry, and we want to make sure you (and your data) stay safe while applying to CookUnity. We also want you to know that we take this seriously — sometimes, as part of our process, we may ask for a brief “proof of humanity” to confirm that we’re connecting with a real person, not an impersonator. Here are a few tips to help you protect yourself and know what to expect from us:\n• Apply only through our official channels. All open roles are listed on our official careers page: careers.cookunity.com\n• Our recruiters are real people — and easy to verify. You can always find them on LinkedIn with verified profiles. If you’re unsure, feel free to reach out to us on our official LinkedIn Company Page.\n• We only communicate through official CookUnity channels. That means emails ending in @cookunity.com and interviews held through official company platforms (Google Meet or Zoom) — never WhatsApp, Telegram, or SMS.\n• We’ll never ask for payment or personal financial details. If anyone does, please don’t share any information and let us know right away.\n\nIf something ever feels off or you’re unsure about a message, we’d much rather you double-check with us. You can always contact us directly through any of our social media channels. We appreciate your interest in joining CookUnity — and we care about keeping your experience (and safety) as genuine as possible.\n\nThis offer from \"CookUnity\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cookunity,official,experience,food,want,customer,leadership,chefs,know,year,engineering,world,channels,learn,paid,engineer,com,free,leave,cookunity com,class,learn new,careers,insight,inspire'),(145,'jsearch','hxalKdn7CqgGgxedAAAAAA==','Developer','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/RYV6476X?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Developer\n\nRole Purpose\n\nDesign, develop, and deliver high-quality, scalable application code that supports and enhances client-facing platforms. The role focuses on building reliable solutions, contributing to technical excellence, and supporting the full software delivery lifecycle.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, test, and maintain high-quality application code in line with best practices and coding standards\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to translate business and technical requirements into effective solutions\n• Participate actively in peer code reviews to ensure code quality, performance, and maintainability\n• Support testing activities, including unit, integration, and system testing\n• Assist with deployment activities and provide post-deployment support as required\n• Identify, troubleshoot, and resolve application issues and defects\n• Contribute to continuous improvement of development processes, tools, and frameworks\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• 4+ years of professional software development experience\n• Strong experience with modern programming languages and frameworks\n• Solid understanding of software design principles, version control, and CI/CD practices\n• Experience working in Agile / Scrum delivery environments\n• Ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented, fast-paced environment\n• Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP)\n• Familiarity with microservices architecture and RESTful APIs\n• Exposure to DevOps practices, infrastructure as code, or containerization (Docker, Kubernetes)\n• Experience with automated testing frameworks and test-driven development (TDD)\n• Knowledge of security best practices and secure coding standards\n• Experience mentoring junior developers or contributing to technical knowledge sharing\n• Background in performance tuning, scalability, or high-availability systems',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'experience,code,application code,contributing technical,contributing,practices,frameworks,delivery,quality,high quality,high,testing,application,test,activities,technical,software,support,design develop,coding standards,design,tools frameworks,support testing,driven development,development tdd'),(148,'jsearch','wOVDhqpPWKHk5bGmAAAAAA==','Professional Web Developer – IT Solutions','Career.zycto','Treasure Beach','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/professional-web-developer-it-solutions/','About Company\n\nImagine a place where your code impacts real lives, driving innovation in Jamaica\'s rapidly evolving digital landscape. Career.zycto empowers businesses across St. Elizabeth and beyond with bespoke digital solutions, from elegant e-commerce platforms to robust enterprise systems. We cultivate a collaborative, forward-thinking environment perfect for web developers passionate about crafting high-quality, scalable web applications. Join us and contribute to a team dedicated to excellence, learning, and making a tangible difference with every line of code.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking a highly skilled and motivated Professional Web Developer to join our dynamic IT team in Treasure Beach, St. Elizabeth. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced developer who thrives on building innovative web solutions and possesses a strong understanding of full-stack development. You will be instrumental in designing, developing, and maintaining cutting-edge web applications that meet the evolving needs of our diverse clientele. From initial concept to deployment and ongoing support, you will contribute across the entire software development lifecycle, ensuring our products are robust, user-friendly, and performant. We are looking for an individual who is not only proficient in modern web technologies but also a creative problem-solver with an eye for detail and a commitment to best practices. If you are passionate about pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible on the web and want to make a significant impact within a growing IT company, we encourage you to apply. This role offers the chance to work on challenging projects, collaborate with a supportive team, and grow your expertise in a vibrant and engaging work environment.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and implement responsive and scalable web applications using modern front-end and back-end technologies.\n• Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code following industry best practices and company standards.\n• Collaborate closely with project managers, designers, and other developers to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Perform thorough testing and debugging to ensure optimal performance, security, and functionality of web applications.\n• Participate in code reviews, providing constructive feedback and ensuring code quality across the team.\n• Maintain and optimize existing web applications, databases, and APIs to improve performance and user experience.\n• Stay abreast of emerging web technologies and industry trends, suggesting and implementing improvements to our development processes and toolset.\n• Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues, providing timely and effective solutions to ensure continuous operation.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript (ES6+)\n• Strong experience with at least one modern JavaScript framework (React, Angular, or Vue.js)\n• Solid understanding of server-side languages (e.g., Node.js, Python, PHP, or Java) and associated frameworks.\n• Experience with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL) and NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB).\n• Familiarity with RESTful APIs and asynchronous request handling.\n• Proficient with version control systems, particularly Git.\n• Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud).\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines and deployment strategies.\n• Knowledge of UI/UX principles and best practices.\n• Experience with containerization technologies like Docker.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Dynamic and supportive work environment with a focus on innovation.\n• Team-building activities and social events.\n• Modern office space located in beautiful Treasure Beach.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their experience and qualifications by clicking on the application link below. Please highlight your most relevant web development projects and your contribution to them. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'web,team,applications,web applications,experience,code,modern,technologies,solutions,development,databases,proficient,treasure beach,st,work environment,treasure,evolving,elizabeth,professional web,st elizabeth,providing,beach,professional,best,practices'),(152,'jsearch','IQzK0Aj2RG1rANjUAAAAAA==','Senior Software Developer','Symptai Consulting Limited','May Pen','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/senior-software-developer/','About Company\n\nSymptai Consulting Limited is a leading technology and cybersecurity consulting firm in the Caribbean, dedicated to delivering innovative solutions and services that empower businesses to thrive in the digital age. With a strong commitment to excellence and a passion for cutting-edge technology, we help our clients optimize their operations, enhance security, and achieve their strategic objectives. We foster a collaborative and dynamic work environment where creativity, continuous learning, and professional growth are highly valued. Our diverse team of experts works on challenging projects that make a real impact, from custom software development to advanced cybersecurity implementations, serving a wide array of industries across the region. Join us and become part of a company that is shaping the future of technology in the Caribbean.\n\nJob Description\n\nSymptai Consulting Limited is seeking an experienced and highly skilled Senior Software Developer to join our dynamic team in Mineral Heights, May Pen. As a Senior Software Developer, you will play a critical role in the design, development, and deployment of robust, scalable, and secure software solutions for our diverse client base. This is a hands-on technical leadership position where you will be responsible for driving key aspects of the software development lifecycle, from architectural decisions to code reviews and mentorship of junior developers. You will work closely with project managers, business analysts, and other technical leads to translate complex business requirements into high-quality software products. We are looking for a professional who is passionate about technology, committed to best practices, and eager to contribute to a culture of innovation and excellence. The ideal candidate will possess a deep understanding of modern software development methodologies, strong problem-solving abilities, and a proven track record of delivering successful projects in an agile environment. If you thrive in a fast-paced, challenging environment and are ready to make a significant impact, we encourage you to apply.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Lead the design, development, testing, and deployment of complex software applications.\n• Architect scalable and secure solutions, ensuring adherence to best practices and industry standards.\n• Write clean, efficient, well-documented, and maintainable code.\n• Conduct code reviews, providing constructive feedback and ensuring code quality across the team.\n• Mentor and guide junior developers, fostering their growth and skill development.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including product management, QA, and operations, to define and deliver features.\n• Troubleshoot and resolve complex technical issues and bugs.\n• Participate in agile ceremonies, including sprint planning, daily stand-ups, and retrospectives.\n• Research and evaluate new technologies to identify opportunities for improvement and innovation.\n• Contribute to the continuous improvement of development processes and tools.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• Minimum of 5 years of professional experience in software development.\n• Expertise in at least one modern programming language (e.g., Python, Java, C#, JavaScript/Node.js).\n• Strong understanding of front-end frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js) and back-end frameworks (e.g., Django, Spring Boot, ASP.NET Core).\n• Proficiency with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server) and NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB, Redis).\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud).\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Solid understanding of software design patterns and architectural principles.\n• Experience with version control systems, particularly Git.\n• Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and communication skills.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master’s degree in a relevant technical field.\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Knowledge of cybersecurity principles and secure coding practices.\n• Familiarity with microservices architecture.\n• Certifications in relevant technologies or cloud platforms.\n• Previous experience in a consulting environment.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance plan.\n• Paid time off and holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Access to latest technologies and tools.\n• Collaborative and inclusive work environment.\n• Company-sponsored team building events.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience, skills, and qualifications that align with this Senior Software Developer role at Symptai Consulting Limited. We appreciate all applications, but only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'software,consulting,senior software,development,consulting limited,symptai,symptai consulting,senior,experience,cybersecurity,software developer,code,environment,software development,developer,secure,end frameworks,scalable secure,technology,technologies,technical,practices,limited,team,professional'),(153,'jsearch','odomrgyeNGatVDOwAAAAAA==','Software Developer – Professional IT Services','Career.zycto',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/software-developer-professional-it-services/','About Company\n\nPropelling technological advancement in the Caribbean, Career.zycto stands as a dynamic IT firm dedicated to crafting innovative software solutions. We specialize in bespoke applications and enterprise-level systems that empower businesses across various sectors. Our collaborative culture thrives on curiosity and continuous learning, offering unparalleled opportunities for software developers to push boundaries and make a tangible impact. Join a team where your coding prowess directly translates into meaningful projects, fostering both personal and professional growth in a vibrant, supportive environment.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is actively searching for a highly motivated and skilled Software Developer to join our innovative team nestled in the beautiful locale of Tower Isle, Ocho Rios. As a pivotal professional within our organization, you will play a central role in the entire software development lifecycle, from initial conceptualization and architectural design to robust development, rigorous testing, and seamless deployment of scalable software solutions. We cater to a diverse clientele, meaning your work will span various industries and address unique technological challenges. We are specifically looking for an individual with an unwavering passion for writing clean, efficient, and well-documented code, a keen interest in leveraging cutting-edge technologies, and an unshakeable commitment to continuous learning and improvement. In this hands-on role, you\'ll be instrumental in transforming complex business requirements into elegant and intuitive technical solutions, operating within an agile development framework to ensure timely delivery of high-quality applications. Your expertise will directly contribute to mission-critical projects that drive operational efficiency, significantly enhance user experiences, and provide substantial, measurable value to our clients, thereby solidifying Career.zycto\'s reputation as a leading innovator in IT across the vibrant Caribbean region. We pride ourselves on fostering an inclusive and dynamic environment where creativity, critical thinking, and collaborative problem-solving are not just encouraged but celebrated. This position offers ample opportunities for accelerated professional growth, skill refinement, and the chance to contribute to impactful projects that leave a lasting mark. If you thrive in a fast-paced, collaborative setting and are eager to tackle challenging technical endeavors with a forward-thinking and supportive team, this represents a prime opportunity to significantly advance your career and truly make a difference.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, test, and deploy high-quality software solutions using modern programming languages and frameworks.\n• Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other developers to understand project requirements and translate them into technical specifications.\n• Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code following best practices and coding standards.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality, share knowledge, and foster a collaborative development environment.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software to improve functionality and performance.\n• Contribute to all phases of the software development lifecycle, from conceptualization to deployment and ongoing support.\n• Stay updated with emerging technologies and industry trends to continuously enhance our development practices and technological stack.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in at least one modern programming language (e.g., Python, Java, C#, JavaScript/TypeScript).\n• Strong understanding of object-oriented programming (OOP) principles and design patterns.\n• Experience with relational and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB).\n• Familiarity with web development frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue, .NET, Spring Boot, Django, Node.js).\n• Solid grasp of API design and development (RESTful services).\n• Experience with version control systems, particularly Git.\n• Ability to write clean, well-documented, and testable code.\n• Strong problem-solving and analytical skills.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud).\n• Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Experience working in an Agile/Scrum development environment.\n• Excellent communication and teamwork skills.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Professional development and training opportunities.\n• Mentorship programs and a clear career growth path.\n• Flexible working hours and work-life balance initiatives.\n• Modern office environment with state-of-the-art equipment.\n• Company-sponsored team building events and social activities.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nEager to make your mark with an innovative Caribbean IT firm? Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and a cover letter detailing your relevant experience and why you are the ideal candidate for this role. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'software,development,career,code,zycto,career zycto,technological,programming,environment,experience,professional,development environment,solutions,collaborative,design,software solutions,clean,team,significantly,firm,vibrant,mark,conceptualization,modern programming,quality'),(156,'jsearch','np8BLaGD12wP4aQUAAAAAA==','Software Developer – IT Company (Professional)','Career.zycto',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/software-developer-it-company-professional/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nInnovation drives us at Career.zycto, a forward-thinking IT company reshaping digital landscapes from our vibrant Kingston hub. For software developers eager to tackle complex challenges and build impactful solutions, we offer an environment ripe with opportunity. We believe in empowering our team to push boundaries, fostering a culture of continuous learning, collaboration, and cutting-edge technology. Join us if you\'re passionate about crafting robust software, influencing product direction, and growing alongside a dynamic group of tech enthusiasts committed to excellence.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is actively seeking a highly skilled and passionate Professional Software Developer to join our growing team in Half Way Tree, Kingston. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced developer to contribute significantly to the design, development, and deployment of innovative software solutions that address real-world business challenges. As a Professional Software Developer, you will play a critical role in our agile development process, working closely with cross-functional teams including product managers, UI/UX designers, and quality assurance engineers.\n\nYou will be responsible for writing clean, scalable, and efficient code across various platforms and technologies. We\'re looking for someone who thrives on problem-solving, has an excellent understanding of software development best practices, and is committed to continuous improvement. Your day-to-day will involve translating business requirements into technical specifications, designing robust architectures, implementing new features, and maintaining existing systems. You\'ll engage in code reviews, contribute to architectural discussions, and mentor junior developers, fostering a collaborative and high-performing team environment.\n\nOur projects span a diverse range of technologies, offering ample opportunities to expand your skill set and work on cutting-edge applications. You\'ll be instrumental in shaping the future of our products, ensuring they are not only functional but also secure, performant, and user-friendly. This role demands a proactive individual who is self-motivated, pays meticulous attention to detail, and possesses strong communication skills to articulate complex technical concepts clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders. If you are a professional software developer looking to make a tangible impact and grow your career within a supportive and dynamic IT company, we encourage you to apply and help us build the next generation of digital solutions.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain robust and scalable software solutions.\n• Collaborate with product managers and stakeholders to understand business requirements and translate them into technical specifications.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and efficient code adhering to coding standards and best practices.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality, share knowledge, and provide constructive feedback.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software to improve functionality and performance.\n• Contribute to architectural discussions and decisions, offering insights on design patterns and technology choices.\n• Mentor junior developers, sharing expertise and fostering a culture of continuous learning.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies and industry trends, evaluating their potential application.\n• Ensure the security, reliability, and performance of applications.\n• Develop and maintain technical documentation for developed solutions.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Minimum 3 years of professional experience in software development.\n• Proficiency in at least one modern programming language (e.g., Python, Java, C#, JavaScript/TypeScript).\n• Strong understanding of object-oriented programming (OOP) principles and design patterns.\n• Experience with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server) and ORM frameworks.\n• Familiarity with front-end technologies (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js) if working on full-stack applications.\n• Experience with version control systems, particularly Git.\n• Knowledge of RESTful API design and development.\n• Solid understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) and Agile methodologies.\n• Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and critical thinking skills.\n• Strong communication and collaboration abilities.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud).\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Experience with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Knowledge of message queues (e.g., RabbitMQ, Kafka) or microservices architecture.\n• Proven ability to lead small projects or technical initiatives.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Professional development and training opportunities.\n• Flexible work arrangements (where applicable).\n• Modern and collaborative office environment.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n• Opportunities for career growth and advancement within the company.\n• Team-building events and social activities.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are a talented and motivated Software Developer looking for a challenging yet rewarding opportunity, we invite you to apply. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience and technical skills. Click on the link below to submit your application directly.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'software,software developer,technical,professional software,developer,professional,development,company,career,technologies,code,experience,fostering,solutions,technical specifications,strong communication,specifications,offering,developer looking,understanding software,contribute architectural,design,looking,robust,developers'),(157,'jsearch','RXlJfi-i0P3XPu1JAAAAAA==','Software Manager','Manchester',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.justjobs.co.uk/jobs/software-manager-6e35859c','Software Engineering Manager – Lead a Talented Tech Team | Hybrid – Manchester\n\nAre you ready to take the reins of a high-performing engineering team at a fast-growing, forward-thinking company?\n\nWe\'re looking for a hands-off, people-focused Software Engineering Leader to inspire and guide a team of brilliant, multi-skilled engineers. You\'ll be at the heart of driving innovation, building robust, scalable digital consumer products that impact thousands—if not millions—of users.\n\nThis isn’t your typical management role. We\'re seeking a true technical leader someone with the experience, empathy, and strategic vision to grow a top-tier engineering function. You’ll work alongside highly skilled senior engineers and help shape a tech culture built on trust, autonomy, and continuous improvement. We don’t expect you to code, but you’ll be managing engineers who build with cutting-edge tech to solve complex challenges. Think scalable systems, slick user experiences, modern DevOps practices, and cloud infrastructure that can handle millions of requests.\n\nSkills Required-\n\nLeadership & Influence – You know how to bring out the best in engineers. You’ve led high-performing teams, built trust quickly, and created environments where engineers thrive.\n\nTechnical Background – You’ve walked the path of a software or data engineer. You can speak the language of modern architecture, OOP, TDD, CI/CD, and cloud-native development (AWS ideally).\n\nEngineering Best Practices – You drive clean code, robust testing, and elegant automation. Agile, DevOps, and product-driven development are second nature to you.\n\nThe company -\n\nValues are simple but powerful:\n\nZero politics – Just kind, smart people working together.\nDown-to-earth – No egos here. We work hard and support one another.\nHigh standards – We’re proud of what we build and how we build it.\nFlexibility & Fairness – Work where and how you do your best. We trust you.\nHybrid Working – Manchester Based- 2 days per week',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'engineers,trust,engineering,manager,millions,built trust,hybrid,manchester,performing,leader,high performing,tech,ll,built,ve,best,build,people,high,software,skilled,devops,robust,team,fast growing'),(160,'jsearch','4ena9QvUHKxwI6mPAAAAAA==','Backend Developer','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/8X3YRWXV?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Back End Developer\n\nDesign, develop, and maintain scalable, secure, and high‑performance backend systems that support enterprise‑grade banking and financial platforms.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and maintain RESTful APIs and backend services\n• Build scalable and resilient server‑side applications to support high‑volume transactions\n• Ensure system performance, reliability, scalability, and security in line with banking standards\n• Integrate databases, third‑party services, and internal systems\n• Collaborate closely with Frontend Developers, DevOps engineers, QA teams, and product stakeholders\n• Write clean, maintainable, and well‑documented code\n• Participate in code reviews, architectural discussions, and system design decisions\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize existing backend applications\n• Adhere to secure coding practices and compliance requirements relevant to financial systems\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• 5+ years of professional backend development experience\n• Strong proficiency in one or more backend technologies such as Java, .NET, Node.js, or equivalent\n• Solid experience with relational and/or NoSQL databases\n• Hands‑on experience with API development and integration (REST, JSON, authentication mechanisms)\n• Strong understanding of backend architecture, design patterns, and microservices\n• Experience with version control systems (e.g., Git)\n• Good understanding of performance optimization and security best practices\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Experience working in banking, financial services, or other regulated industries\n• Exposure to cloud platforms and containerization tools\n• Familiarity with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices\n• Knowledge of messaging systems and asynchronous processing',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'backend,financial,banking,banking financial,experience,systems,services,develop maintain,design,performance,practices,support,design develop,secure,net node,practices compliance,mechanisms strong,code participate,developers devops,closely frontend,relevant financial,development integration,microservices experience,apis backend,mechanisms'),(168,'jsearch','dIdajla5Xi50Fy9qAAAAAA==','Web Developer – Professional Role','Career.zycto','Kingston','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/web-developer-professional-role/','About Company\n\nShaping the digital landscape of tomorrow, Career.zycto is a dynamic IT firm dedicated to innovation and excellence in web solutions. We empower our team to build cutting-edge applications and platforms that drive real-world impact for our diverse client base. For a web developer seeking a collaborative environment, a culture of continuous learning, and direct involvement in high-impact projects, Career.zycto offers unparalleled growth opportunities. Join us in Kingston and contribute to a vibrant tech community, pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible in web development.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a passionate Web Developer eager to transform innovative ideas into robust, user-friendly applications? Career.zycto, a rapidly growing IT company headquartered in Kingston, Jamaica, is seeking a talented and dedicated Web Developer to join our dynamic team. We specialize in crafting bespoke web solutions, from intricate e-commerce platforms to sophisticated enterprise applications, for a diverse portfolio of clients across various sectors. This professional role offers an exciting opportunity to work on challenging projects, utilizing modern technologies and best practices in a collaborative and supportive environment where your contributions directly influence project success and client satisfaction.\n\nAs a key member of our development team, you will be instrumental in the full software development lifecycle. This involves hands-on engagement from the initial conceptualization and detailed design phases, through development, comprehensive testing, and seamless deployment of web applications. You will collaborate closely with product managers to refine requirements, work alongside UX/UI designers to translate wireframes into pixel-perfect interfaces, and partner with other developers to integrate complex functionalities. We value clean, maintainable, and scalable code, adhering to industry best practices and fostering a culture of continuous learning and knowledge sharing. Your daily tasks will span both front-end development, ensuring an intuitive and responsive user experience, and back-end development, architecting powerful server-side logic and managing database interactions. Our projects frequently demand integration with third-party APIs, optimizing application performance, and implementing stringent security measures to protect user data and maintain application integrity.\n\nCareer.zycto fosters a vibrant and inclusive culture of innovation where your ideas are not just heard but actively encouraged and implemented. We believe in empowering our developers with the tools and resources they need to excel, including access to cutting-edge technologies, opportunities for professional development courses, and dedicated mentorship programs. You will be encouraged to explore new technologies, contribute to architectural discussions, and take ownership of significant project modules. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment, possess a keen eye for detail, a problem-solving mindset, and are committed to delivering exceptional web solutions that make a tangible difference, then we invite you to explore this exciting opportunity. Advance your career with a team that is not just building websites, but shaping the digital future for businesses in Jamaica and beyond, solidifying our reputation for technical excellence and groundbreaking innovation.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop, test, and deploy responsive and high-performance web applications using modern web technologies.\n• Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other developers to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and scalable code following best practices.\n• Participate in code reviews to maintain code quality and share knowledge.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software to ensure optimal functionality.\n• Integrate third-party APIs and web services to enhance application capabilities.\n• Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability.\n• Contribute to architectural discussions and technology stack decisions.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging web technologies and industry trends.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in JavaScript, HTML5, and CSS3.\n• Strong experience with at least one modern front-end framework (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js).\n• Solid understanding of back-end development with a language like Node.js, Python, PHP, or Java.\n• Experience with relational databases (e.g., MySQL, PostgreSQL) and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB).\n• Familiarity with version control systems, especially Git.\n• Understanding of RESTful APIs and asynchronous programming.\n• Ability to write clean, maintainable, and testable code.\n• Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud).\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and agile development methodologies.\n• Experience with UI/UX principles and responsive design.\n• Excellent communication and teamwork skills.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Mentorship programs and career growth pathways.\n• Modern office environment with state-of-the-art equipment.\n• Regular team-building activities and social events.\n• Access to a well-stocked kitchen with snacks and beverages.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume and a cover letter outlining their experience and suitability for this role. Please ensure your application highlights your proficiency in relevant web technologies and your passion for innovative development. Click on the application link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'web,development,career,technologies,applications,application,career zycto,zycto,experience,team,code,end development,professional,end,modern,web solutions,responsive,environment,web developer,encouraged,integrate,explore,access,scalable code,party'),(169,'jsearch','JYrjczSqIoz4lIbGAAAAAA==','Web Developer (Professional Role)','Career.zycto',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/web-developer-professional-role-2/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nJoin a forward-thinking team where innovation meets impact. Career.zycto is rapidly transforming the digital landscape, building robust, scalable web solutions that empower businesses across various sectors. For a talented web developer, this means a dynamic environment filled with complex challenges, cutting-edge technologies, and ample opportunities for professional growth. We champion a collaborative culture, encouraging continuous learning and the freedom to experiment with new ideas. If you\'re passionate about crafting exceptional user experiences and writing clean, efficient code, Career.zycto offers the perfect platform to elevate your career and make a tangible difference.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking an experienced and highly motivated Web Developer to join our growing IT team in Cherry Gardens. In this professional role, you will be instrumental in designing, developing, and maintaining innovative web applications and platforms that drive our business forward. You will work within an agile development environment, collaborating closely with product managers, UX/UI designers, and other developers to translate complex requirements into intuitive and high-performing web solutions. This position requires a strong understanding of full-stack development principles, a keen eye for detail, and a commitment to producing clean, efficient, and well-documented code. We are looking for a creative problem-solver who is eager to contribute to all phases of the software development lifecycle, from concept and design to deployment and ongoing support. Your work will directly impact our user experience and overall technical infrastructure, making this a pivotal role within our organization.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop, test, and deploy robust, scalable, and secure web applications using modern front-end and back-end technologies.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including designers, product managers, and other developers, to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code, adhering to best practices and coding standards.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality and knowledge sharing across the team.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing systems to improve functionality and performance.\n• Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability.\n• Stay abreast of emerging technologies and industry trends to continuously improve our development processes and product offerings.\n• Contribute to the documentation of technical specifications and project requirements.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in JavaScript, HTML5, and CSS3.\n• Strong experience with at least one modern front-end framework (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js).\n• Solid understanding of back-end development with languages such as Node.js, Python, PHP, or Java.\n• Experience with relational and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MongoDB, MySQL).\n• Familiarity with RESTful APIs and asynchronous request handling.\n• Proficiency with version control systems (e.g., Git).\n• Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud).\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Understanding of UI/UX principles and responsive design.\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines and automated testing frameworks.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Access to the latest tools and technologies.\n• Collaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Modern office facilities in Cherry Gardens.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n• Company-sponsored team-building events and social gatherings.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to submit their application, including a resume and cover letter detailing their relevant experience and qualifications, by clicking on the application link below. Please highlight your portfolio or examples of past web development projects.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'web,development,experience,career,technologies,team,professional,efficient,zycto,web developer,career zycto,code,cherry gardens,clean efficient,gardens,cherry,end,work,efficient code,improve,robust scalable,professional role,developer,clean,understanding'),(170,'jsearch','EWriCp9mrvtXqR3SAAAAAA==','Professional Web Developer','Career.zycto','Riversdale','ZA',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/professional-web-developer/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nSeeking a dynamic environment where your code directly shapes user experience? Career.zycto is an emerging IT powerhouse based in Riversdale, St. Catherine, dedicated to crafting cutting-edge web solutions that empower businesses. We pride ourselves on fostering a culture of innovation, continuous learning, and collaborative problem-solving. Here, web developers find a vibrant space to transform creative ideas into robust, scalable applications. Join our team and leverage modern technologies, contribute to impactful projects, and advance your professional journey in a supportive, forward-thinking setting that values your technical expertise and passion for development.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is on the lookout for a highly skilled and passionate Professional Web Developer to join our growing team in Riversdale, St. Catherine. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced developer who thrives on building innovative, high-performance web applications that deliver exceptional user experiences. As a key member of our development team, you will be instrumental in all phases of the software development lifecycle, from conceptualization and design to development, testing, and deployment.\n\nYou will work on a diverse range of projects, primarily focusing on developing responsive, intuitive, and visually appealing web interfaces (front-end) as well as robust and scalable server-side logic (back-end). Our ideal candidate possesses a strong understanding of modern web technologies, best practices, and a keen eye for detail. You’ll be contributing to critical business applications, internal tools, and client-facing platforms, playing a direct role in our company\'s success and expansion.\n\nAt Career.zycto, we believe in fostering an environment where creativity is encouraged, and continuous learning is paramount. You will have the opportunity to work with cutting-edge technologies, collaborate with talented professionals, and contribute to projects that make a tangible impact. We are looking for someone who is not just a coder, but a problem-solver who takes ownership, embraces challenges, and is eager to push the boundaries of what\'s possible in web development. If you\'re ready to advance your career in a supportive, dynamic, and forward-thinking IT company, we encourage you to apply and become a part of our exciting journey.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop, test, and deploy highly responsive and scalable web applications using modern front-end and back-end frameworks.\n• Collaborate with product managers, UI/UX designers, and other developers to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code following best practices and coding standards.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software to ensure optimal performance and security.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality and knowledge sharing within the team.\n• Implement and maintain robust APIs to integrate with various third-party services.\n• Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability.\n• Stay updated with emerging technologies and industry trends to continuously improve our development processes and product offerings.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript (ES6+)\n• Strong experience with at least one modern front-end framework (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js)\n• Solid understanding of back-end development using languages such as Node.js, Python, PHP, or Java.\n• Experience with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL) and NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB).\n• Familiarity with version control systems, particularly Git.\n• Experience with RESTful APIs and asynchronous request handling.\n• Understanding of responsive design principles and cross-browser compatibility.\n• Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• Ability to work effectively in a collaborative team environment.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud).\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and automated testing frameworks.\n• Experience with GraphQL.\n• Contributions to open-source projects or a strong portfolio of personal projects.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits.\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Access to the latest tools and technologies.\n• Dynamic and collaborative work environment.\n• Regular team-building activities and social events.\n• On-site parking.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and qualifications by clicking on the application link below. Please ensure your application highlights your proficiency in modern web development technologies and your passion for creating impactful digital solutions.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'web,end,development,technologies,modern,team,experience,projects,career,st catherine,catherine,riversdale,professional web,riversdale st,responsive,career zycto,zycto,applications,st,modern web,modern end,continuous learning,code,professional,environment'),(179,'jsearch','JcvcNIbc8oV0RVQjAAAAAA==','Business Applications Developer','Pavago',NULL,'JM',0,'https://startup.jobs/business-applications-developer-pavago-7727378?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Business Applications Developer\nPosition Type: Full-Time, Remote\nWorking Hours: EST-aligned business hours\n\nAbout the Role:\nWe are seeking a highly skilled Business Applications Developer to design, build, and maintain automated solutions and business intelligence systems that drive operational efficiency. This role focuses on developing integrations, workflows, dashboards, and internal applications using the Microsoft 365 and Power Platform ecosystem. You will work closely with technical and business stakeholders to translate operational needs into scalable, secure, and high-impact solutions.\n\nResponsibilities\n\nBusiness Applications & Automation\n• Design and develop Power BI dashboards, reports, and data models that deliver actionable insights across business functions.\n• Build complex Power Automate workflows, Power Apps, and Copilot Studio agents to automate core operational processes.\n• Implement Dataverse-based solutions and analytics systems to transform raw data into business value.\n• Automate end-to-end workflows across operations, HR, and internal business systems.\n\nIntegrations & Platform Development\n• Develop Azure-based integrations using Functions, APIs, webhooks, and custom connectors.\n• Build and maintain Microsoft Teams applications, including notification bots, adaptive cards, and workflow integrations.\n• Integrate internal systems with third-party tools and services using REST APIs.\n\nCollaboration & Documentation\n• Work closely with stakeholders to gather requirements and translate them into technical solutions.\n• Document workflows, data models, and application logic for maintainability and scalability.\n• Provide ongoing improvements and optimizations based on system usage and feedback.\n\nSecurity & Reliability\n• Ensure applications follow security best practices and data governance standards.\n• Implement error handling, monitoring, and performance optimization across solutions.\n\nWhat Makes You a Perfect Fit\n• Strong problem-solving mindset with the ability to design scalable business solutions.\n• Comfortable working across automation, analytics, and application development.\n• Able to communicate technical concepts clearly to non-technical stakeholders.\n• Self-driven and capable of managing multiple priorities in a remote environment.\n\nRequired Experience & Skills (Minimum)\n• 2–4 years of development experience with Microsoft technologies.\n• Strong proficiency in Power BI, including DAX, data modeling, and visualization best practices.\n• Advanced experience with Power Automate, including complex flows and custom connectors.\n• Hands-on experience with Azure services and Azure Functions.\n• Solid skills in JavaScript and TypeScript.\n• Strong understanding of REST APIs, webhooks, and system integrations.\n\nIdeal Experience & Skills\n• Experience with advanced Power BI features such as row-level security, incremental refresh, and embedded analytics.\n• Familiarity with Power Apps (canvas and model-driven).\n• Experience developing Microsoft Teams apps (bots, messaging extensions, adaptive cards).\n• Knowledge of Copilot Studio and AI-powered agents.\n• Exposure to Azure DevOps or CI/CD practices.\n• Working knowledge of SQL and data warehousing concepts.\n\nWhat Does a Typical Day Look Like?\nA Business Applications Developer’s day centers on building automation, improving data visibility, and enhancing internal systems. You will:\n• Review requirements and prioritize development tasks.\n• Build or enhance Power BI dashboards and automated workflows.\n• Develop integrations and troubleshoot system issues.\n• Collaborate with stakeholders to refine solutions.\n• Test, document, and deploy updates to production systems.\n• Continuously optimize performance, security, and usability.\n\nIn essence: you enable smarter decision-making and operational efficiency through automation, analytics, and scalable business applications.\n\nKey Metrics for Success (KPIs)\n• Successful delivery of automation and analytics projects.\n• Reduction in manual processes and operational bottlenecks.\n• Reliability and performance of business applications.\n• Stakeholder satisfaction and adoption of developed solutions.\n• Quality of documentation and maintainability of systems.\n\nInterview Process\n• Initial Phone Screen\n• Technical Interview with Recruiter\n• Technical Assessment / Case Discussion\n• Final Interview\n• Offer & Background Verification',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'power,business applications,business,analytics,data,integrations,bi,applications developer,automate,power bi,workflows,applications,automation,microsoft,operational,automation analytics,dashboards,solutions,apps,interview,stakeholders,internal,systems,build,experience'),(181,'jsearch','gOZjgC57K7UksbM4AAAAAA==','Internal Software Support Engineer','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/RYV7V97R?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Internal Software Support Engineer\n\nLocation: Remote (Carribean)\n\nEmployment Type: Full-time Contract\n\nReports to: Chief Technology Officer\n\nRole Overview\n\nWe are seeking a technically strong, service-oriented Internal Software Support Engineer who will act as the first line of support for internal software systems and websites. This role combines IT and software support, hands-on website development, and solution design, including recommending and implementing software and CRM platforms to improve business processes and internal efficiency.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nInternal Software & Technical Support\n• Provide Level 1–2 technical support for internal software tools, platforms, and web applications\n• Troubleshoot system, website, and application issues; identify root causes and implement fixes\n• Monitor system performance and escalate complex issues when required\n• Install, configure, and maintain internal software, tools, and user access\n• Log, track, and resolve incidents using ticketing systems while meeting defined SLAs\n• Document issues, solutions, and support processes to build internal knowledge bases\n\nWebsite & Application Support\n• Support, maintain, and update company websites and internal web platforms\n• Fix bugs, improve performance, and ensure website functionality and uptime\n• Implement content and feature updates using CMS platforms\n• Collaborate with product, design, and engineering teams on enhancements and new features\n• Ensure websites are secure, responsive, and optimized for performance\n\nSolution Design & Business Process Optimization\n• Analyze existing business processes and daily workflows to identify inefficiencies and technology gaps\n• Creating solutions and recommending software/CRM platforms to optimize business processes and day to day functions\n• Design and recommend technical solutions to improve productivity, automation, and system reliability\n• Research, evaluate, and recommend software tools, SaaS products, and CRM platforms to support business needs\n• Support or lead the implementation, configuration, and optimization of selected tools and platforms\n• Act as a technical advisor to internal teams by translating business requirements into effective system solutions\n• Ensure recommended solutions are scalable, cost-effective, and aligned with company goals\n• Document system configurations, integrations, and best practices for long-term maintainability\n\nCollaboration & Process Improvement\n• Work closely with internal teams to understand system needs and resolve issues efficiently\n• Assist with system testing, deployments, upgrades, and integrations\n• Recommend improvements to tools, workflows, and system architecture\n• Support a culture of continuous improvement and operational excellence\n\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\n• 2–4+ years of experience in technical support, software support, or IT support roles\n• Hands-on experience with website development and maintenance\n• Working knowledge of HTML, CSS, JavaScript (basic to intermediate)\n• Experience with CMS platforms (WordPress, Webflow, or similar)\n• Familiarity with basic backend concepts (APIs, databases, hosting environments)\n• Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills\n• Ability to communicate technical concepts clearly to non-technical users\n\nPreferred / Nice-to-Have\n• Experience with React, PHP, or Node.js\n• Understanding of cloud hosting, DNS, and server environments\n• Exposure to ticketing systems (Jira, Zendesk, Freshdesk, etc.)\n• Experience evaluating or implementing CRM platforms (HubSpot, Salesforce, Zoho, or similar)\n• Knowledge of workflow automation and system integrations\n• Basic knowledge of cybersecurity best practices\n• Experience working in a fast-paced startup or scale-up environment\n\nWhat We Offer\n• Opportunity to work in a growing, impact-driven company\n• Remote working environment\n• Exposure to both support engineering and development work\n• Collaborative and supportive team culture\n• Career growth and learning opportunities',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'support,internal,internal software,website,software support,software,crm platforms,crm,platforms,software tools,technical support,support engineer,business processes,technical,business,issues,basic,websites,tools,integrations,processes,engineer,recommend,experience,solutions'),(182,'jsearch','35wPfAPYmmJi2z-GAAAAAA==','Senior Web Developer – Innovate with tTech Limited','tTech Limited','Kingston','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/senior-web-developer-innovate-with-ttech-limited/','About Company\n\ntTech Limited is a leading Jamaican Information Technology (IT) services company, dedicated to empowering businesses with innovative and reliable technology solutions. Established with a vision to transform the IT landscape in Jamaica and the wider Caribbean, we specialize in managed IT services, cloud solutions, cybersecurity, and custom software development. Our team comprises highly skilled and passionate professionals committed to delivering exceptional value and driving digital transformation for our diverse client base. At tTech, we foster a culture of continuous learning, collaboration, and excellence, encouraging our employees to grow their careers while making a tangible impact on the success of our clients.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a highly skilled and experienced Web Developer passionate about crafting elegant, efficient, and scalable web solutions? tTech Limited is seeking a Senior Web Developer to join our dynamic and growing team in Kingston. In this professional role, you will be instrumental in designing, developing, and maintaining cutting-edge web applications for our clients across various industries. You will work closely with product managers, designers, and other developers to translate complex business requirements into high-performing, user-friendly digital experiences. We are looking for an individual who thrives in a collaborative environment, possesses a strong problem-solving mindset, and stays abreast of the latest web technologies and best practices. This role offers an exciting opportunity to lead projects, mentor junior developers, and contribute significantly to our product roadmap and technical strategy. If you are ready to take on challenging projects, drive innovation, and make a significant impact within a forward-thinking IT company, we encourage you to apply and become a vital part of the tTech family.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Lead the design, development, testing, and deployment of robust and scalable web applications using modern front-end and back-end technologies.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams, including product owners, UI/UX designers, and other developers, to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and maintainable code following industry best practices and company standards.\n• Conduct code reviews, provide constructive feedback, and ensure code quality and adherence to architectural guidelines.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize application performance, ensuring responsiveness and reliability.\n• Mentor junior developers, share knowledge, and contribute to the growth and development of the team.\n• Stay informed about emerging technologies, industry trends, and continuously seek to improve development processes and tools.\n• Contribute to the technical design and architectural discussions for new and existing projects.\n• Ensure security best practices are integrated into all stages of the development lifecycle.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in JavaScript, HTML5, and CSS3\n• Strong experience with at least one modern front-end framework (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js)\n• Extensive experience with back-end development using Node.js, Python, PHP, or Java\n• Proficiency with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL) and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB)\n• Solid understanding of RESTful APIs and microservices architecture\n• Experience with version control systems, particularly Git\n• Familiarity with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud)\n• Strong problem-solving abilities and analytical skills\n• Excellent communication and teamwork skills\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes)\n• Experience with mobile application development (e.g., React Native, Flutter)\n• Knowledge of cybersecurity principles and secure coding practices\n• Relevant professional certifications (e.g., AWS Certified Developer, Microsoft Certified: Azure Developer Associate)\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package\n• Comprehensive health and life insurance\n• Paid time off and public holidays\n• Opportunities for professional development and training\n• Modern and collaborative office environment\n• Team-building activities and social events\n• Exposure to cutting-edge technologies and diverse projects\n• Pension Plan\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to make your mark as a Senior Web Developer at tTech Limited? We invite passionate and experienced individuals to apply by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience, technical skills, and any projects that demonstrate your capabilities. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ttech,web,web developer,ttech limited,development,developer,senior web,projects,experience,limited,practices,technologies,developers,end,senior,certified,development team,scalable web,modern end,company,passionate,code,team,skills,cybersecurity'),(183,'jsearch','BJm80fGnaJkPKWR7AAAAAA==','Software Developer (Professional)','Career.zycto','Portmore','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/software-developer-professional-2/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nAt Career.zycto, we are pioneering innovative technology solutions that empower businesses across various sectors. For a software developer, this means an environment rich in complex challenges and unparalleled opportunities to shape the future of digital landscapes. We thrive on collaboration, continuous learning, and consistently pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible. Join a culture where your code directly impacts user experiences and business success, making Career.zycto an ideal launchpad for your professional growth and significant impact in the dynamic tech world.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a seasoned Software Developer looking to leverage your expertise in a vibrant and forward-thinking IT company? Career.zycto is seeking a professional Software Developer to join our dynamic team in Bridgeport, Portmore. We are on the hunt for a passionate and skilled individual who excels at transforming complex business requirements into high-quality, scalable, and robust software solutions. This is an exceptional opportunity to contribute significantly to diverse projects, working with cutting-edge technologies and collaborating with a talented group of engineers, designers, and product managers. If you\'re driven by innovation, problem-solving, and a desire to build impactful applications that delight users and drive business success, we encourage you to apply.\n\nIn this role, you will be instrumental in the entire software development lifecycle, from conceptualization and design to deployment and ongoing maintenance. You will be expected to write clean, maintainable, and efficient code, participate actively in code reviews, and contribute to architectural discussions. Our team values individuals who take initiative, are eager to learn new technologies, and can adapt quickly to evolving project needs. You\'ll be working in an agile environment, where your contributions are recognized, and your professional growth is actively supported through continuous learning opportunities and challenging assignments. Join us to make a tangible difference and propel your career to new heights within the evolving tech landscape of Jamaica.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain robust and scalable software solutions.\n• Collaborate with product owners, designers, and other engineers to define and implement new features.\n• Write clean, efficient, and well-documented code following industry best practices.\n• Participate actively in code reviews, providing constructive feedback and ensuring code quality.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing systems to improve performance and reliability.\n• Contribute to the continuous improvement of software development processes, tools, and methodologies.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies, tools, and industry trends to inform future development.\n• Mentor junior developers, sharing technical knowledge and fostering a collaborative learning environment.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in at least one modern programming language (e.g., Python, Java, C#, JavaScript/TypeScript).\n• Strong understanding of software development principles, object-oriented design, data structures, and algorithms.\n• Experience with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server) and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB, DynamoDB).\n• Familiarity with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud) and their services.\n• Expertise in using version control systems, particularly Git.\n• Solid understanding of Agile development methodologies (Scrum, Kanban).\n• Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and critical thinking skills.\n• Ability to work both independently and collaboratively as part of a high-performing team.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\n• Experience with front-end frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js) or mobile development (iOS/Android).\n• Knowledge of containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines and automated testing frameworks.\n• Familiarity with API design and development (RESTful APIs, GraphQL).\n• Certifications in relevant technologies or cloud platforms (e.g., AWS Certified Developer).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Generous paid time off, including vacation and sick leave.\n• Professional development opportunities, including training allowances and conference attendance.\n• A collaborative, inclusive, and innovative work environment.\n• Modern office space located conveniently in Bridgeport, Portmore.\n• Opportunities for significant career advancement and growth within a dynamic company.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nEager to join our team? We encourage all qualified candidates to apply by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume and cover letter highlight your relevant experience and passion for software development.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'software,software developer,development,career,code,software development,professional,technologies,actively,developer,bridgeport portmore,evolving,business success,actively code,portmore,bridgeport,opportunities,participate actively,engineers,join,zycto,career zycto,dynamic,software solutions,company career'),(184,'jsearch','WcA7mvnU190KkeYxAAAAAA==','Senior Web Developer','Career.zycto','Negril','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/senior-web-developer/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nCareer.zycto is at the forefront of digital innovation, empowering businesses through cutting-edge web solutions. We are a dynamic IT company dedicated to crafting exceptional online experiences and driving technological advancement for our diverse client base. For a web developer, this translates into an environment rich with diverse projects, modern tech stacks, and a commitment to continuous learning and professional growth. Here, your code isn\'t just lines; it\'s the architecture for tomorrow\'s digital landscape. Join our collaborative team and shape the future, making a tangible impact on projects that matter.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly skilled and experienced Senior Web Developer to join our growing team in Negril, Westmoreland. As a pivotal member of our IT department, you will be instrumental in designing, developing, and maintaining robust, scalable, and user-friendly web applications for a variety of clients. This professional role demands not only deep technical expertise but also a creative problem-solving mindset and a passion for crafting elegant digital solutions.\n\nAt Career.zycto, you\'ll have the opportunity to work on exciting projects that span across different industries, from enhancing e-commerce platforms to building intricate data visualization tools. We believe in fostering an environment where innovation thrives, and your contributions directly impact our clients\' success. You\'ll lead development efforts, mentor junior developers, and collaborate closely with product managers, UI/UX designers, and other stakeholders to translate complex requirements into intuitive web experiences. This is more than just coding; it\'s about shaping the digital future and pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible on the web. We are looking for someone who is not only proficient in current web technologies but also eager to explore new frameworks and methodologies, ensuring our solutions remain cutting-edge and future-proof. If you are ready to take on a challenging yet rewarding role where your expertise will be valued and your ideas can flourish, we encourage you to apply.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Lead the full lifecycle development of web applications, including design, development, testing, deployment, and maintenance.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and efficient code adhering to best practices and coding standards.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Conduct code reviews, provide constructive feedback, and mentor junior developers.\n• Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing systems.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging web technologies and industry trends to recommend and implement solutions.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in front-end technologies: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES6+)\n• Extensive experience with at least one modern JavaScript framework (React, Angular, or Vue.js)\n• Strong back-end development skills with languages like Python (Django/Flask), Node.js (Express), or PHP (Laravel/Symfony)\n• Expertise in database management (SQL and NoSQL databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB)\n• Experience with RESTful API design and integration.\n• Solid understanding of version control systems (Git)\n• Familiarity with responsive design principles and cross-browser compatibility.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP).\n• Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Experience in Agile/Scrum development methodologies.\n• Strong portfolio of successful web development projects.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package\n• Health and wellness programs\n• Professional development opportunities and training allowances\n• Paid time off and holidays\n• Collaborative and innovative work environment\n• Team-building events and social gatherings\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and why they are a perfect fit for this role. Please click on the application link below to apply directly. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'web,digital,development,web developer,senior web,projects,expertise,future,technologies,experience,senior,apply,solutions,web technologies,junior developers,mentor,clients,mentor junior,just,desig