plex challenges and continuously enhancing your skill set, we encourage you to apply and grow with us.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop, test, and deploy robust and scalable web applications using modern web technologies.\n• Collaborate with product owners, designers, and other developers to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code following best practices and coding standards.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality and knowledge sharing.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software to improve functionality and performance.\n• Implement responsive designs to ensure cross-browser and cross-device compatibility.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging web technologies and industry trends.\n• Contribute to the entire application lifecycle, focusing on coding and debugging.\n• Optimize applications for maximum speed and scalability.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in HTML5, CSS3, and JavaScript (ES6+)\n• Experience with at least one modern front-end framework (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js)\n• Solid understanding of server-side languages (e.g., Python, Node.js, PHP, Ruby, Java)\n• Familiarity with database technologies (e.g., SQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB)\n• Experience with RESTful APIs and asynchronous request handling\n• Version control system proficiency (e.g., Git)\n• Strong problem-solving abilities and analytical skills\n• Excellent communication and teamwork skills\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud)\n• Knowledge of UI/UX principles and design best practices\n• Familiarity with Agile/Scrum development methodologies\n• Experience with testing frameworks (e.g., Jest, Mocha, Cypress)\n• Understanding of containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes)\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance\n• Paid time off and public holidays\n• Opportunities for professional development and training\n• Modern office environment with state-of-the-art tools\n• Team-building activities and social events\n• Employee wellness programs\n• Contribution to pension scheme\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume and a cover letter outlining their experience and suitability for this role. Please ensure you highlight relevant projects and technologies you have worked with. Click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'web,technologies,code,cross,applications,experience,zycto,career zycto,career,web developer,user,performance,modern,professional,ensure,web technologies,end,developer,coding,efficient code,apply,skills,digital,environment,eager'),(197,'jsearch','eORpx6DexZPvBmvQAAAAAA==','Software Engineer – Corporate IT (Experienced)','Digicel Jamaica','Harbour View','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/software-engineer-corporate-it-experienced/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nDigicel is a leading telecommunications provider operating across 32 markets in the Caribbean, Central America, and Oceania. We are committed to delivering the best network, best value, and best customer service. Innovation is at the heart of what we do, and our Corporate IT team plays a critical role in powering our operations, driving efficiency, and enabling our strategic initiatives across the group. Join us and be part of a dynamic team shaping the future of connectivity, where your expertise will contribute directly to keeping millions connected and businesses thriving. We foster a culture of collaboration, continuous learning, and significant professional growth, making Digicel an ideal place for experienced engineers looking to make a substantial impact.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated and experienced Software Engineer to join our Corporate IT team in Harbour View, Kingston. This is a fantastic opportunity for a professional with a strong background in software development, system architecture, and operational support within an enterprise environment. As a Software Engineer, you will be instrumental in designing, developing, testing, and deploying robust software solutions that support Digicel’s internal business functions and critical infrastructure. You will work closely with various departments, understanding their needs and translating them into scalable and efficient software applications. Your expertise will be crucial in maintaining the stability, security, and performance of our corporate systems, ensuring uninterrupted operations for our vast network. This role demands a proactive problem-solver with excellent analytical skills and a passion for leveraging technology to drive business success. If you thrive in a fast-paced, challenging yet rewarding environment and are ready to make a significant impact on a leading regional telecommunications company, we encourage you to apply. You will be a key player in our digital transformation journey, contributing to projects that directly enhance operational efficiency and technological resilience across our extensive operations.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and implement high-quality, scalable software solutions for various corporate IT needs, focusing on reliability and performance.\n• Collaborate with business analysts, project managers, and stakeholders to gather requirements, define project scope, and deliver solutions that align with business objectives.\n• Write clean, efficient, and well-documented code following established best practices, coding standards, and architectural guidelines.\n• Conduct thorough testing, debugging, and performance tuning of applications to ensure optimal functionality and user experience.\n• Participate actively in code reviews, providing constructive feedback and ensuring adherence to design principles and quality standards.\n• Provide ongoing maintenance, support, and enhancements for existing corporate IT systems, addressing incidents and implementing improvements.\n• Contribute to the full software development lifecycle (SDLC), from conceptualization and design to deployment, monitoring, and post-implementation support.\n• Identify and implement automation opportunities to streamline processes, improve operational efficiency, and reduce manual effort.\n• Stay abreast of emerging technologies, industry trends, and best practices to recommend innovative solutions and continuous improvements.\n• Ensure all software solutions comply with Digicel\'s security policies, data privacy regulations, and other relevant compliance standards.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in at least one modern programming language (e.g., Java, Python, C#, JavaScript/TypeScript)\n• Strong understanding of relational databases (e.g., SQL Server, Oracle, PostgreSQL) and experience with NoSQL databases is a plus.\n• Experience with front-end frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js) and back-end frameworks (e.g., Spring Boot, .NET Core, Django, Flask)\n• Familiarity with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud) and containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes)\n• Solid grasp of software development methodologies (Agile, Scrum) and experience working in cross-functional teams.\n• Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and critical thinking skills with attention to detail.\n• Strong communication, interpersonal, and collaboration abilities to work effectively with diverse teams.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced, dynamic, and evolving environment.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related technical field.\n• Experience with enterprise resource planning (ERP) or customer relationship management (CRM) systems integration and development.\n• Knowledge of telecommunications industry standards, network protocols, cybersecurity principles, and data privacy regulations (e.g., GDPR, CCPA).\n• Relevant certifications in programming languages, cloud platforms, or specific enterprise technologies.\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines, DevOps practices, and automated testing frameworks.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance for you and your family.\n• Generous paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, and public holidays.\n• Extensive opportunities for professional development, training, and continuous learning.\n• Employee assistance programs and various wellness initiatives to support overall well-being.\n• Exclusive discounted Digicel products and services.\n• A dynamic, inclusive, and collaborative work environment where your contributions are valued.\n• The chance to make a significant impact on a leading regional telecommunications company and shape its future.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their applications by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience, technical skills, and educational background, especially detailing your accomplishments in software development within an enterprise IT setting. Only shortlisted candidates who meet the specified criteria will be contacted for an interview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'software,corporate,experience,digicel,development,standards,enterprise,environment,software development,solutions,best,team,skills,business,telecommunications,performance,continuous,software engineer,significant,applications,dynamic,leading,critical,various,efficiency'),(201,'jsearch','NNci-zPVaYgSWkL-AAAAAA==','Web Developer – Innovative IT Solutions','Career.zycto','Montego Bay','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/web-developer-innovative-it-solutions/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nImagine building innovative digital experiences that impact thousands. At Career.zycto, we empower web developers to transform ideas into robust, user-centric applications. We are a dynamic IT firm in Montego Bay, dedicated to leveraging cutting-edge technology to solve complex problems for our diverse client base. Our collaborative environment fosters continuous learning and encourages creative problem-solving, making it the perfect place for a passionate web developer eager to push boundaries and grow their skill set within a supportive team. Join us and help shape the future of digital presence.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is on the lookout for a talented and enthusiastic Web Developer to join our growing team in Flankers, Montego Bay. This professional role offers an exceptional opportunity to design, develop, and maintain cutting-edge web applications that drive significant value for our clients across various industries. As a Web Developer at Career.zycto, you will be instrumental in bringing digital visions to life, working on both front-end and back-end aspects of our projects.\n\nYou will collaborate closely with a diverse team of project managers, designers, and fellow developers to deliver high-quality, scalable, and secure web solutions. Your day-to-day will involve everything from conceptualizing new features and refining existing functionalities to writing clean, efficient, and well-documented code. We value innovation and encourage our team members to explore new technologies and methodologies to continuously improve our development processes and product offerings.\n\nThis role demands a blend of technical expertise, problem-solving prowess, and a keen eye for detail. You should be passionate about creating seamless user experiences and robust, reliable systems. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment, possess a strong work ethic, and are eager to contribute to impactful projects, Career.zycto offers a platform for you to excel. We are committed to fostering a culture of growth, learning, and mutual support, ensuring that every team member has the resources and opportunities to reach their full potential. Join us and become a pivotal part of a company that’s shaping the digital landscape in Jamaica and beyond. We believe in empowering our developers to take ownership of their work and contribute strategically to every project phase, from inception to deployment and maintenance. This is more than just a coding role; it\'s a chance to innovate, lead, and make a tangible difference.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop and maintain robust, scalable, and high-performance web applications using modern web technologies.\n• Collaborate with product managers and UI/UX designers to translate requirements and wireframes into functional web features.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and efficient code following best practices and coding standards.\n• Implement responsive design principles to ensure applications perform optimally across various devices and browsers.\n• Integrate third-party APIs and services to enhance application functionality.\n• Conduct thorough testing, debugging, and troubleshooting to ensure application reliability and performance.\n• Participate in code reviews, providing constructive feedback to peers and continuously improving code quality.\n• Stay updated with emerging web technologies, frameworks, and industry trends, and suggest their adoption where beneficial.\n• Contribute to the entire software development lifecycle, from planning and design to deployment and maintenance.\n• Assist in the deployment and continuous integration processes.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in front-end technologies: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES6+)\n• Strong experience with at least one modern JavaScript framework (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js)\n• Solid understanding of back-end development using languages such as Node.js, Python, PHP, or Java\n• Experience with relational databases (e.g., MySQL, PostgreSQL) and NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB)\n• Familiarity with RESTful APIs and API integration\n• Proficiency with version control systems, especially Git\n• Strong problem-solving abilities and analytical skills\n• Excellent communication and teamwork skills\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud)\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes)\n• Understanding of Agile/Scrum development methodologies\n• Experience with testing frameworks (e.g., Jest, Mocha, Cypress)\n• Knowledge of security best practices in web development\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses\n• Health and wellness programs\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning\n• Flexible work arrangements (where applicable)\n• Vibrant and collaborative company culture\n• Modern office environment with state-of-the-art tools\n• Team-building activities and social events\n\nHow to Apply\n\nEager to make your mark as a Web Developer? Please submit your resume and a cover letter detailing your relevant experience and why you are the ideal candidate for this role. We encourage you to highlight any personal projects or portfolios. Click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'web,web developer,zycto,career zycto,team,digital,developer,career,technologies,montego,montego bay,bay,end,development,eager,code,experience,developers,robust,offers,project,deployment maintenance,develop maintain,contribute,learning'),(206,'jsearch','b5oC9KwfPuGAqTK8AAAAAA==','SYSTEMS ADMINISTRATOR (MIS/IT 5)','The Casino Gaming Commission',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/SYSTEMS-ADMINISTRATOR-MIS-IT-5-Job-226723.aspx','SYSTEMS ADMINISTRATOR (MIS/IT 5) Job Summary The Systems Administrator is responsible for the installation, configuration, maintenance, and secure operation of the Commission’s server infrastructure, operating systems, and enterprise platforms. The post holder ensures the availability, integrity, and security of ICT systems, manages user access and system performance, supports disaster recovery and business continuity arrangements, and provides technical support to ensure uninterrupted operations in fulfilment of the Commission’s mandate. Key Responsibilities Systems Administration and Infrastructure Management Install, configure, upgrade, and maintain physical and virtual servers, operating systems, enterprise software, and peripherals Monitor server performance, availability, and capacity to ensure reliability, efficiency, and optimal system operation Manage system updates, patches, and version upgrades in accordance with established change management and security protocols Install, configure, and maintain server environments to support development, testing, training, and production systems Replace, upgrade, and decommission obsolete or defective hardware and software components as required Security, Data Protection and Business Continuity Manage user accounts, access rights, groups, and permissions in accordance with approved security policies and segregation-of-duties requirements Enforce system security best practices to prevent cyber threats, unauthorised access, and data breaches Implement, monitor, and maintain backup, recovery, and disaster recovery solutions to ensure data integrity and system resilience Collaborate with the Security Manager and relevant stakeholders on ICT security matters and incident response Support cybersecurity initiatives, data governance requirements, and audit readiness within a regulated environment Implement and monitor controls to ensure compliance with applicable legislation, gaming regulations, and data protection requirements Systems Support, Integration, and Deployment Diagnose and resolve hardware, software, operating system, and network issues, documenting problems and solutions Deploy and support enterprise applications across test, training, and production environments Support system integrations with external government platforms to facilitate validation, reporting, and regulatory compliance Automate system and application deployments where feasible to improve efficiency and reduce risk Provide technical documentation and specifications to support system planning, upgrades, and enhancements Reporting, Documentation, and Continuous Improvement Maintain accurate system documentation, configuration records, and operational procedures Prepare technical reports and proposals for review by the Director and Infrastructure Manager Research emerging technologies, tools, and industry trends and recommend improvements to enhance system performance and security Participate in ICT and cross-functional projects aimed at improving service delivery and operational efficiency Support digital forensic investigations and ICT-related incident response activities in collaboration with the Enforcement Division Training and User Support Provide technical support to users as required and escalate issues where necessary Facilitate training and sensitisation sessions to improve users’ understanding of systems and security practices Minimum Required Qualifications and Experience First Degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field At least three (3) years’ experience in systems administration or a related ICT role Certification in systems administration or networking (e.g. Microsoft, Linux, or equivalent) would be an asset Strong knowledge of server and networking technologies, operating systems, databases, and infrastructure security Working knowledge of the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) Experience in high-security or regulated environments such as government, financial institutions, or gaming operations would be an asset Experience with scripting and automation tools would be an asset Knowledge of applicable legislation, regulations, and ICT governance standards Remuneration: Salary Scale $ $4,266,270.00 – $5,737,658.00 per annum plus gratuity Application along with detailed Curriculum Vitae should be submitted no later than March 1, 2026.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'systems,security,ict,support,operating,server,training,data,infrastructure,technical,recovery,operating systems,experience,maintain,ensure,software,systems administrator,user,access,related,efficiency,asset,systems administration,environments,performance'),(207,'jsearch','WGrgsMeRVSjRYfiiAAAAAA==','Data Engineer (Senior)','TheHiveCareers',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/data-engineer-senior-at-thehivecareers-4365943415','Job Title : Data Engineer (Senior)\n\nRole Purpose\n\nThe Senior Data Engineer is responsible for designing, building, and maintaining scalable and reliable data pipelines and platforms that enable analytics, reporting, and data-driven decision-making across the organization.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, build, and maintain robust ETL/ELT pipelines for structured and unstructured data\n• Optimize data storage, processing, and access to ensure performance, scalability, and reliability\n• Develop and maintain data models that support analytics, reporting, and downstream consumption\n• Collaborate closely with analytics, reporting, and business teams to understand data requirements\n• Ensure data quality, integrity, security, and compliance with governance and regulatory standards\n• Monitor, troubleshoot, and continuously improve data pipelines and platform performance\n• Contribute to data architecture standards, best practices, and technical documentation\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• Minimum 7+ years of experience in data engineering or related roles\n• Strong proficiency in SQL and Python; experience with distributed processing frameworks such as Spark\n• Hands-on experience with cloud data platforms and modern data architectures\n• Solid understanding of data modeling, data warehousing, and performance optimization techniques\n• Experience working in banking or other highly regulated environments\n• Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work independently in complex technical environments\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with real-time or streaming data technologies (e.g., Kafka, Kinesis)\n• Familiarity with data governance, lineage, and metadata management tools\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines, infrastructure as code, or DevOps practices for data platforms\n• Exposure to data visualization or BI tools and analytics workflows\n• Experience mentoring junior engineers or leading technical initiatives',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'data,experience,pipelines,analytics,platforms,reporting,senior,performance,technical,engineer,data engineer,analytics reporting,practices,standards,processing,strong,skills,tools,maintain,governance,environments,ensure,engineer senior,data platforms,data pipelines'),(208,'jsearch','F4RGp4bHNbVIq6G7AAAAAA==','Data Engineer (Senior)','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/63XW4X9R','Job Title : Data Engineer (Senior)\n\nRole Purpose\n\nThe Senior Data Engineer is responsible for designing, building, and maintaining scalable and reliable data pipelines and platforms that enable analytics, reporting, and data-driven decision-making across the organization.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, build, and maintain robust ETL/ELT pipelines for structured and unstructured data\n• Optimize data storage, processing, and access to ensure performance, scalability, and reliability\n• Develop and maintain data models that support analytics, reporting, and downstream consumption\n• Collaborate closely with analytics, reporting, and business teams to understand data requirements\n• Ensure data quality, integrity, security, and compliance with governance and regulatory standards\n• Monitor, troubleshoot, and continuously improve data pipelines and platform performance\n• Contribute to data architecture standards, best practices, and technical documentation\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• Minimum 7+ years of experience in data engineering or related roles\n• Strong proficiency in SQL and Python; experience with distributed processing frameworks such as Spark\n• Hands-on experience with cloud data platforms and modern data architectures\n• Solid understanding of data modeling, data warehousing, and performance optimization techniques\n• Experience working in banking or other highly regulated environments\n• Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work independently in complex technical environments\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with real-time or streaming data technologies (e.g., Kafka, Kinesis)\n• Familiarity with data governance, lineage, and metadata management tools\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines, infrastructure as code, or DevOps practices for data platforms\n• Exposure to data visualization or BI tools and analytics workflows\n• Experience mentoring junior engineers or leading technical initiatives',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'data,experience,pipelines,analytics,platforms,reporting,senior,performance,technical,engineer,data engineer,analytics reporting,practices,standards,processing,strong,skills,tools,maintain,governance,environments,ensure,engineer senior,data platforms,data pipelines'),(209,'jsearch','pDCtuqA_oiKxoxFRAAAAAA==','Information Security Analyst','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/V63WXY46?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Information Security Analyst\n\nRole Purpose\n\nMonitor, detect, and respond to information security threats and incidents to protect enterprise systems, data, and infrastructure. Support the implementation and testing of security controls and contribute to the organizations overall security posture.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Monitor security events, alerts, and logs using SIEM and other security tools\n• Analyze security incidents to identify root causes, scope, and impact\n• Support incident response activities, including containment, remediation, and reporting\n• Perform regular control testing to ensure effectiveness of security policies and procedures\n• Collaborate with IT, risk, and business teams to implement security controls and best practices\n• Maintain accurate documentation of incidents, findings, and security controls\n• Contribute to continuous improvement of security monitoring, detection, and response processes\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• 5+ years of experience in information security, cybersecurity, or related roles\n• Hands-on experience with SIEM tools (e.g., Splunk, QRadar, ArcSight) and security monitoring solutions\n• Knowledge of security frameworks, standards, and best practices (ISO 27001, NIST, CIS)\n• Strong analytical, problem-solving, and investigative skills\n• Experience supporting incident response and vulnerability management activities\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with endpoint detection and response (EDR) tools\n• Familiarity with cloud security monitoring (AWS, Azure, GCP)\n• Relevant security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CISM, CEH, GCIA)\n• Knowledge of network security, firewall, and intrusion detection/prevention systems\n• Exposure to threat intelligence, malware analysis, or penetration testing',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'security,response,experience,security controls,testing,detection,security monitoring,information security,information,incidents,monitoring,controls contribute,contribute,incident response,incident,best practices,detection response,best,activities,practices,tools,controls,systems,support,monitor'),(210,'jsearch','a52Uo0BaG7YMocMbAAAAAA==','Cyber Security Analyst','TheHiveCareers',NULL,NULL,0,'https://cybersecurityjobslist.com/companies/thehivecareers/jobs/a2d71954492142759d4595ad9b93ceda-cyber-security-analyst?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Position Overview:\n\nAs a Cybersecurity Analyst, you will play a critical role in protecting the company\'s digital assets. You will be responsible for monitoring, detecting, and responding to security incidents, analyzing vulnerabilities, implementing security measures, and ensuring compliance with security policies and standards. Your expertise will be vital in maintaining a proactive security posture and minimizing risk.\n\nQualifications:\n• Bachelors degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or related field (or equivalent experience).\n• Proven experience as a Cybersecurity Analyst, Security Operations Center (SOC) Analyst, or similar role.\n• Strong understanding of security frameworks, such as NIST, ISO 27001, and CIS Controls.\n• Experience with SIEM tools (e.g., Splunk, ArcSight, ELK Stack).\n• Knowledge of firewalls, VPNs, IDS/IPS, endpoint security, and other security technologies.\n• Familiarity with vulnerability assessment tools (e.g., Nessus, OpenVAS).\n• Understanding of networking protocols and technologies (e.g., TCP/IP, DNS, HTTP/S, SSL/TLS).\n• Strong problem-solving and analytical skills, with the ability to manage and prioritize multiple tasks.\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'security,analyst,cybersecurity analyst,technologies,understanding,experience,cybersecurity,tools,strong,role,skills,tools nessus,verbal communication,analyzing,analyzing vulnerabilities,understanding networking,arcsight elk,analytical skills,analyst similar,understanding security,tls strong,assets,assets responsible,verbal,bachelors'),(211,'jsearch','2PNoXQoh_7spWptGAAAAAA==','Information Security Analyst','TheHiveCareers',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/information-security-analyst-at-thehivecareers-4365950140?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Information Security Analyst\n\nRole Purpose\n\nMonitor, detect, and respond to information security threats and incidents to protect enterprise systems, data, and infrastructure. Support the implementation and testing of security controls and contribute to the organizations overall security posture.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Monitor security events, alerts, and logs using SIEM and other security tools\n• Analyze security incidents to identify root causes, scope, and impact\n• Support incident response activities, including containment, remediation, and reporting\n• Perform regular control testing to ensure effectiveness of security policies and procedures\n• Collaborate with IT, risk, and business teams to implement security controls and best practices\n• Maintain accurate documentation of incidents, findings, and security controls\n• Contribute to continuous improvement of security monitoring, detection, and response processes\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• 5+ years of experience in information security, cybersecurity, or related roles\n• Hands-on experience with SIEM tools (e.g., Splunk, QRadar, ArcSight) and security monitoring solutions\n• Knowledge of security frameworks, standards, and best practices (ISO 27001, NIST, CIS)\n• Strong analytical, problem-solving, and investigative skills\n• Experience supporting incident response and vulnerability management activities\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with endpoint detection and response (EDR) tools\n• Familiarity with cloud security monitoring (AWS, Azure, GCP)\n• Relevant security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CISM, CEH, GCIA)\n• Knowledge of network security, firewall, and intrusion detection/prevention systems\n• Exposure to threat intelligence, malware analysis, or penetration testing',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'security,response,experience,security controls,testing,detection,security monitoring,information security,information,incidents,monitoring,controls contribute,contribute,incident response,incident,best practices,detection response,best,activities,practices,tools,controls,systems,support,monitor'),(215,'jsearch','UPsRnsozU6kp7iadAAAAAA==','Identity & Access Management (IAM) Analyst','TheHiveCareers',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/identity-access-management-iam-analyst-at-thehivecareers-4365952091?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Identity & Access Management (IAM) Analyst\n\nRole Purpose\n\nManage and support the identity lifecycle and access control processes to ensure secure, compliant, and efficient access to systems and applications. The role plays a key part in protecting enterprise and customer data by enforcing strong identity and access management controls.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Provision, modify, and deprovision user access across systems and applications in line with approved requests and policies\n• Enforce IAM policies, standards, and segregation of duties controls\n• Manage identity lifecycle processes including onboarding, role changes, and offboarding\n• Support internal and external audits, security reviews, and compliance assessments\n• Monitor access controls and investigate access-related issues or violations\n• Collaborate with technology, security, and business teams to implement access requirements\n• Maintain IAM documentation, procedures, and access evidence\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• 5+ years of experience in Identity and Access Management or information security roles\n• Strong hands-on experience with Active Directory and enterprise IAM tools\n• Experience working in banking or other highly regulated security environments\n• Solid understanding of authentication, authorization, and access control principles\n• Experience supporting audits, risk assessments, and security reviews\n• Strong attention to detail and ability to manage sensitive access data\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with privileged access management (PAM) solutions\n• Familiarity with cloud IAM (Azure AD, AWS IAM, GCP)\n• Knowledge of regulatory and compliance requirements in financial services\n• Experience with automation, scripting, or workflow tools for access provisioning\n• Relevant security certifications (e.g., CISSP, CISM, IAM-related certifications)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'access,iam,identity,access management,identity access,experience,management,security,manage,access control,requirements,management iam,assessments,iam analyst,audits,applications,lifecycle,identity lifecycle,access systems,systems applications,security reviews,reviews,compliance,controls,role'),(216,'jsearch','oODHAiXDeURfXda1AAAAAA==','IT Technician','Confidential',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/IT-Technician-Job-227158.aspx','This role offers an opportunity to provide on-site technical support to our internal customers, as well as ensuring that our systems and networks are operating effectively. The IT Technician will be required to travel between locations as needed to provide support and troubleshoot infrastructure and applications issues. KEY DUTIES & RESPONS I BILITIES include but are not limited to: Install, configure, and maintain hardware and software systems. Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues, both remotely and on-site. Train end-users in the use of hardware and software systems. Manage and track IT assets, including hardware and software inventory. Create and maintain documentation, including user manuals and support procedures. Collaborate with other IT teams to ensure that systems and networks are integrated effectively. Keep up to date with new technologies and IT support best practices and make recommendations for improvements. Support operations and incidents on applications and technological platforms, including support, maintenance, and updates. ACADEMIC & EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS : Undergraduate / bachelor’s degree From 3-5 years of experience in IT support. Basic understanding of IT systems and troubleshooting HW and SW issues. Basic experience with Windows, and virtual machine operating systems. Familiarity with networking concepts, including TCP/IP, DNS, and DHCP. Basic knowledge in configuring communication appliances such as firewalls, switches, routers, Access Points, to act as remote hands and/or L1 support. Experience with remote support tools such as TeamViewer or Remote Desktop Kindly add subject line: “IT Technician” ONLY SHORTLISTED CANDIDATES WILL BE CONTACTED',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'support,systems,hardware,hardware software,remote,including,software,issues,software systems,systems networks,site,networks,effectively,provide,experience,basic,troubleshoot,applications,operating,technical,maintain,technician,add subject,bilities include,academic experience'),(217,'jsearch','4c8qGsMeGBdVBLLaAAAAAA==','FIELD SERVICE TECHNICIAN','Confidential',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/FIELD-SERVICE-TECHNICIAN-Job-227198.aspx','FIELD SERVICE TECHNICIAN Duties and Responsibilities Performing repairs to electrical, electronic and mechanical equipment. Providing service and customer support during field visits and dispatches Operating company vehicles in a safe manner Providing timely and detailed service reports for each job using company\'s procedures Building positive relationships with customers through excellent service. Requirements Associate Degree in Industrial Engineering/Electrical Engineering and Computing At least one year experience and exposure to electrical installation Valid General Driver’s License Must have passes in Mathematics and English A Willing to travel for work Must be willing to work flexible hours Strong computer skills Good customer service skills',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'service,field,providing,willing,service technician,field service,electrical,customer,engineering,skills,company,requirements associate,performing repairs,operating company,safe manner,excellent service,equipment providing,willing work,willing travel,english willing,procedures building,travel work,engineering electrical,timely detailed,engineering computing'),(218,'jsearch','eONdsTYnkZ-5GwFaAAAAAA==','Maintenance Technician','T. Geddes Grant (Dist.) Limited',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Maintenance-Technician-Job-227301.aspx','SUMMARY The Maintenance Technician is responsible for performing routine and extensive preventative maintenance and repair procedures on the company’s mechanical equipment and utility systems. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Conduct minor and major repair of all mechanical equipment. Conduct routine preventive maintenance procedures on mechanical equipment in keeping with schedules; inspects belts, checks fluid levels, replaces filters, greases bearings, seals, etc.; repairs or replaces broken parts in addition to clean and inspect compressor, generator and water system. Conduct routine inspection of boilers and maintain quality standards through the treatment of water. Conduct building repairs as assigned including replacing windows; repairs doors, door locks, etc. Execute and record daily and weekly maintenance activities in keeping with checklists. Conduct electrical installation for wiring and equipment; new electrical services, replaces and repairs wiring as needed. Conduct repairs on electrical equipment and control circuits; replaces faulty electrical switches; repairs refrigeration equipment including electrical locks and control panels to maintain building security as needed. Actively respond and execute emergency maintenance requests as required. Maintains records of scheduled maintenance procedures. Obtain estimates for supplies, repair parts; orders parts as needed. Assist in the startup, operation and conduct the servicing of machines. EDUCATION & EXPERIENCE: Level 3 vocational certification in mechanics and/or electronics Minimum of three CSES inclusive of Mathematics & English Minimum two (2) years of experience in a similar capacity COMPETENCIES: Excellent teamwork and interpersonal skills Strong analytical and problem solving skills Meticulous attention to details Must be resourceful, innovative, forward thinking Should have strong analytical, decision-making and delegating skills and be experienced in quality analysis testing auditing and problem-solving.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'conduct,replaces,maintenance,repairs,electrical,equipment,routine,mechanical equipment,procedures,conduct routine,maintenance procedures,execute,strong analytical,keeping,water,water conduct,locks,parts,needed,maintenance technician,analytical,building,repair,mechanical,wiring'),(219,'jsearch','MkzojUyZg1nTkt7jAAAAAA==','SERVICE CENTER TECHNICIAN - KINGSTON','Automotive Art',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/SERVICE-CENTER-TECHNICIAN-KINGSTON-Job-227023.aspx','SERVICE CENTER TECHNICIAN - KINGSTON The successful candidate should possess technical skills, problem solving abilities, effective communication skills, a positive attitude and enjoy working in a team environment. Work experience in the automotive industry would be an asset with skills for installing tyres, wheels/batteries, repairing and servicing tyres. Must be automotive Certified and have a diploma from JGAS or NCTVET or equivalent. Must have a valid Driver’s License. Only suitable applications will be acknowledged.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'service center,kingston,tyres,center technician,technician kingston,center,automotive,skills,service,industry asset,equivalent valid,enjoy working,enjoy,effective communication,skills problem,skills positive,suitable applications,work experience,diploma jgas,automotive industry,kingston successful,suitable,certified diploma,servicing tyres,skills installing'),(220,'jsearch','Rr2tqZQeiv8U5PekAAAAAA==','Apprentice/Junior Technician','ILDS International',NULL,NULL,0,'https://recruiterflow.com/ildsinternational/jobs/383','Job Title: Apprentice/Junior Technician\n\nOur client is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Apprentice/Junior Technician to join their technical operations team. This role is ideal for individuals who have a strong interest in mechanical systems and are eager to build a career in the marine or mechanical service industry.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Maintain a clean, organized, and safe workshop environment.\n• Assist technicians with servicing, maintenance, and repairs of equipment and machinery.\n• Perform basic mechanical tasks such as cleaning, lubricating, and handling components and tools.\n• Conduct simple preventative maintenance checks to ensure equipment is operational.\n• Examine equipment to identify visible faults or irregularities and report findings.\n• Handle workshop tools and equipment safely and responsibly.\n• Support inventory control of tools, spare parts, and workshop supplies.\n• Input service or repair information into the computer system in a timely manner.\n• Provide general support to technical and sales teams as required.\n• Carry out other related duties assigned by supervisors.\n\nRequired Attributes\n• Strong interest in mechanical or technical work.\n• Willingness to learn and follow instructions.\n• Good problem-solving mindset.\n• Organized with attention to detail.\n• Reliable, punctual, and hardworking.\n• Positive attitude and ability to work well in a team.\n• Basic computer literacy is an asset.\n\nWorking Hours\n\nNormal working hours are Monday to Friday, 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM. Overtime during weekdays and occasional weekends may be required.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'apprentice,apprentice junior,junior technician,workshop,junior,mechanical,equipment,00,working hours,strong mechanical,tools,technical,organized,hours,required,strong,working,computer,basic,technician,service,maintenance,team,support,attention reliable'),(221,'jsearch','awEm2ouwrVShb4pHAAAAAA==','Level 2 and Level 3 + Senior IT Support Engineers (Remote)','support adventure',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jaabz.com/jobs/154363-remote-it-support-technician-level-23?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Established in 2016, Support Adventure is an expat outsourcing company that provides people the opportunity to live and work in exciting cities worldwide while offering tech support online in a location independent manner.Support Adventure offers worldwide remote work opportunities with the freedom to work from anywhere, as long as you have a stable power supply...',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'support,worldwide,remote,support adventure,adventure,work,level,senior support,senior,offers worldwide,offers,offering tech,offering,location,outsourcing company,outsourcing,worldwide remote,worldwide offering,live work,live,manner support,opportunity live,support online,manner,stable power'),(222,'jsearch','_3N8o-iiRTNj3lEWAAAAAA==','Casino Technician','Sizzling Slots',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Casino-Technician-Job-227170.aspx','Responsibilities: Complete all Technical activities in assigned areas, ensure provision of excellent customer service. Ensure that Technical work space areas are kept clean and all machines are Service, Repair/Replace parts when necessary. Check and test machines each morning and after a shift ends to ensure that every slot machine and table games equipment is in optimum operational condition at all times. Clear machines whenever a Hand pay, Special pay or Un-certain transaction is needed. Respond to service calls in a timely manner, ensuring that customer service standards are met. Perform meter readings first of each month to submit to the BGLC (Betting Gaming and Lotteries Commission). Continually update personal knowledge of new products or equipment introduced to the slot and table games gaming industry. Remove / Carry in machines from or to gaming floor when needed. Control television stations in order to satisfy customers’ needs on required sports they wishes to watch. Unlock and clear machines to reduce machine blocking during shift. Keep radio on with music to be played on the floor to entertain customers. Turn on/off the MxWallPro so that customers are able to watch when needed. Find required tv station or sport when requested by a customer. Protect all assets of the Company at all times. Continually update personal knowledge of new products or equipment introduced to the slot and table games gaming industry. EDUCATION AND /OR EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS: High school diploma, College Degree or equivalent related field Electronic gaming technical certification background is an advantage. A minimum of one year technical experience in slot or table games operations is preferred. Basic understanding of electronics and an understanding of trouble shooting such electronics. Ability to work overtime, weekends, evenings, and holidays as needed Must have good verbal communication skills. Customer-service skills Organizational skills Please to send your application letter and resume by latest August 30, 2023. We thank all applicants for their application, however, only shortlisted applicants will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'gaming,machines,table,games,table games,slot,customer,slot table,needed,service,technical,customer service,customers,equipment introduced,clear machines,floor,continually,update personal,update,new products,products equipment,gaming industry,games gaming,personal knowledge,watch'),(224,'jsearch','WMXhKwvradbl3D4PAAAAAA==','Repair Technician PMD','Quipt Home Medical','Black Hill','AU',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/repair-technician-pmd-at-quipt-home-medical-4369279524','Apply\n\nDescription\n\nIf you have compassion and the passion for helping others, then we want you to join our growing team! Quipt Home Medical is a rapidly growing leader in the provision of clinical respiratory equipment and service in the durable medical equipment industry.\n\nLet’s start with what’s important to you. The Benefits.....\n• Medical Insurance- multiple plans to choose from\n• Dental & Vision Insurance\n• Short Term Disability & Long Term Disability Options\n• Life Insurance\n• Generous PTO plan\n• Paid Holidays\n• 401K\n• 401K match\n• Competitive Pay\n\nPosition\n\nPower Mobility Repair Technician\n\nGeneral Description\n\nThe Power Mobility Repair Technician will be responsible for troubleshooting, diagnosing, and repairing Power Mobility Devices.\n\nSchedule\n\nMonday-Friday\n• evening or weekends may be required for emergency repairs\n\nDuties/Responsibilities\n• Visiting client’s homes, clinics and SNF to troubleshoot, diagnose and repair Power Wheel Chairs and Custom Manual WCs as well as other seating systems.\n• Communicating with clients regarding concerns and resolutions\n• Training/educating clients and caregivers in the proper use, care and safety of equipment\n• Following up with clients to ensure client satisfaction\n• Working with manufacturers’ tech support to troubleshoot and identify required parts for repairs\n• Working with customer service team to coordinate daily routes and coordinate order processing\n• Obtaining quotes from manufactures for the repairs.\n• Communicate repairs needed and quotes on assessments and trouble shooting forms\n• Completing necessary documents in a timely and accurate manner\n• Assists in cleaning and disinfecting of equipment\n\nTo Succeed\n• Ability to communicate effectively through electronic devices (ie. iPhone)\n• Possess a valid State Driver’s License with an acceptable driving record\n• Ability to learn in-house operational systems\n• Experience using hand and power tools\n• Mechanical and situational problem solving abilities\n• Ability to utilize basic electronic devices\n• Organizational skills\n• High School diploma/GED required\n• durable medical equipment (DME): Preferred but not Required\n• Pass a background check\n\nRequirements\n\nPhysical Requirements:\n• Must be able to lift up to 50 pounds at times.\n• Must be able to withstand prolonged periods of sitting, standing, and traveling in vehicle',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'medical,power,repair technician,mobility,power mobility,insurance,devices,clients,equipment,repairs,repair,mobility repair,medical equipment,durable medical,electronic devices,durable,quotes,401k,coordinate,required,description,term disability,term,disability,communicate'),(225,'jsearch','_qV2b52hCs2efcQrAAAAAA==','Cleaning Technician','Clean Moves',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.jamaicanjobsonline.com/jobs/clean-technician/','Clean Moves is expanding and seeking reliable, detail-driven Cleaning Technicians to join our growing team. This role is ideal for trained professionals who are committed to delivering exceptional cleanliness and presentation standards within hospitality and private service environments. Key ResponsibilitiesPerform thorough cleaning of Airbnb, villa, and residential propertiesPrepare and present properties to exceptional guest-ready standardsFollow certified hospitality and private service cleaning protocolsMaintain high attention to detail in all assigned tasksEnsure all areas meet company quality and presentation standards RequirementsCertification in hospitality or private service cleaning techniquesStrong attention to detail and commitment to excellenceDependable, professional, and punctualAbility to work flexible schedules, including weekends and holidays if requiredPride in delivering consistently high standards of work',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cleaning,hospitality private,private service,private,hospitality,presentation standards,exceptional,service cleaning,presentation,delivering,standards,service,attention,high,technician clean,technicians join,clean moves,professional,standards requirementscertification,requirementscertification hospitality,certified hospitality,requirementscertification,standards hospitality,punctualability work,tasksensure areas'),(227,'jsearch','jwW6pzqkUpUSzLUsAAAAAA==','R.O. - Maintenance Technician','Capital Vacations','Montego Bay','JM',0,'https://www.recruit.net/job/o-maintenance-technician-jobs/EAE11FCBE341D63D?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Opportunity for career advancement in a fast-paced, growth-oriented organization!\n\nBelow are just some of the benefits you\'ll receive:\n• Competitive Salary\n• Paid Time Off and Paid Holidays\n• Career Growth\n• Medical/Dental with employer contribution\n• Voluntary Life Insurance, Disability, and Aflac Insurance\n• Company-paid life insurance and long-term disability\n• 401 (k) retirement plan\n• Travel Perks to Resort Locations\n• Company Perks Program\n\nWhat are you motivated by?:\n\nThe Maintenance Technician implements the upkeep and maintenance of the Sales Center and Welcome Center.\n\nWhat you\'re great at:\n• Implements preventative maintenance programs such as A/C filters, fire extinguishers, and appliances\n• Maintains daily upkeep, included but not limited to painting, plumbing, electrical work, moving furniture, hanging drywall and landscaping clean-up\n• Completes maintenance calls, general upkeep of Sales Center and Welcome Center\n• Notifies manager of any issues\n• Assists guests when needed\n• Completes all other duties as requested\n\nResponsibilities listed may not include all tasks or apply to all resort locations, an official job description will be provided and signed on the first day of employment.\n\nCapital Vacations is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We celebrate diversity and support an inclusive workplace!\n\nHere’s what you can expect: At Capital Vacations we are united by a common purpose of “Travel. Gather. Smile. Repeat.” We pride ourselves on bringing our passion, innovation, and boldness to travel, enriching the lives of those we serve. We encourage you to join our team and help us in fulfilling our purpose. If this opportunity excites you, and if you have the following qualifications, we invite you to apply for our team:\n\nHere’s what you have already achieved:\n• High School Diploma\n• Have a valid driver\'s license and proof of insurance\n• Have and maintain a good driving record clear of significant violations\n• Knowledge of the Timeshare industry\n• Experience in general resort maintenance such as landscaping, construction, and upkeep\n• Able to read construction work orders and use basic tools',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'upkeep,insurance,center,maintenance,resort,paid,opportunity,travel,capital,capital vacations,completes,perks,implements,vacations,center welcome,construction,welcome center,welcome,employer,sales center,resort locations,purpose,landscaping,life insurance,growth'),(228,'jsearch','48IuBtxuW3-e8WgnAAAAAA==','Automotive/ Diesel HVAC Technician in Jamaica','Energy Jobline ZR',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.energyjobline.com/job/automotive-diesel-hvac-technician-jamaica-28182003?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Energy Jobline is the largest and fastest growing global Energy Job Board and Energy Hub. We have an audience reach of over 7 million energy professionals, 400,000+ monthly advertised global energy and engineering jobs, and work with the leading energy companies worldwide.\n\nWe focus on the Oil & Gas, Renewables, Engineering, Power, and Nuclear markets as well as emerging technologies in EV, Battery, and Fusion. We are committed to ensuring that we offer the most exciting career opportunities from around the world for our jobseekers.\n\nJob DescriptionJob DescriptionBenefits:\n• Bonus based on performance\n• Competitive salary\n• Flexible schedule\n• Opportunity for advancement\n\nJob Opportunity: Automotive HVAC Technician\nLocation:Jamaica, NY\nCompany: TM Bus\nPay Rate: $27 $35 per hour (based on experience)\n\nTM Bus is seeking a skilled and reliable Automotive HVAC Technician to join our growing maintenance team. If you have a strong background in diagnosing and repairing heating, ventilation, and air conditioning systems in buses and other commercial vehicles, we want to hear from you!\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Diagnose and repair HVAC systems on school buses and other fleet vehicles\n• Perform routine inspections, maintenance, and troubleshooting of climate control systems\n• Ensure compliance with safety and environmental standards\n• Work closely with fleet maintenance supervisors and mechanics\n• Maintain accurate records of all repairs and services performed\n\nQualifications:\n• Proven experience as an automotive HVAC technician (school bus experience )\n• Certification in HVAC systems or equivalent field training\n• Strong diagnostic and mechanical skills\n• Ability to work independently and in a team environment\n• Valid drivers license (CDL but not required)\n• Strong attention to detail and commitment to safety\n\nWhat We Offer:\n• Competitive hourly pay ($27$35 based on experience)\n• Opportunity for overtime\n• Supportive team environment\n• Opportunities for growth within the company\n• Steady, year-round work\n\nIf you are interested in applying for this job please press the Apply Button and follow the application process. Energy Jobline wishes you the very best of luck in your next career move.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'energy,hvac,hvac technician,automotive,automotive hvac,bus,based,job,strong,opportunity,systems,27,global,hvac systems,global energy,jobline,tm,offer,tm bus,energy jobline,27 35,buses,based experience,35,work'),(229,'jsearch','JNqzrIKS0UvYLNHFAAAAAA==','Heavy Duty Technician','Toyota Jamaica Ltd.',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/heavy-duty-technician-at-toyota-jamaica-ltd-4371979951?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Essential Duties and Responsibilities (include the following, but are not limited to):\n• Performs complex main engine, engine ignition, fuel system, and engine emission control system diagnosis and repair, to include repair of diesel, gas, and alternative fuel system configurations.\n• Performs complex diagnosis and repair of automatic, standard, and electronic transmission mechanical and control systems, to include standard transmission clutch operating systems, transaxle and transfer case systems, and all phases of final drive operation.\n• Performs complex diagnosis and repair of various types of suspension, steering, power assist, and alignment systems; diagnoses and repairs various types of brake systems, to include hydraulic systems, disc and drum brake applications, air brake systems, and anti-lock brake systems operation.\n• Performs complex general electrical and electronic system diagnosis and repair, to include starting and charging systems, electrical wiring systems, gauges and warning systems, and accessory systems; diagnoses and repairs ventilation systems, heat and air conditioning systems, refrigerant recovery, and mechanical systems.\n• Performs all phases of maintenance required for fleet vehicles operation.\n• Assists in maintaining records of work performed.\n• Assists and instructs automotive technicians with problematic assignments.\n• Ensures proper care in the use and maintenance of equipment and supplies; promotes continuous improvement of workplace safety and environmental practices.\n• Performs miscellaneous job-related duties as assigned by Field & Fleet Service Manager or his designate.\n• Participates in Toyota’s Technical Training Programme and is required to make reasonable progress.\n• Must be available for work when required, clients in the commercial space are not limited to requiring support during the conventional work week as such week-end work will be the standard for the Commercial Technician.\n\nQualifications\n\nProven vehicle maintenance & preparation experience; successful completion of the Toyota Team 21 curriculum at the Toyota Technician level.\n\nSuperlative interpersonal skills;\n\nValid Jamaican Category A driver\'s license without restrictions for at least two years AND a clean driving record;\n\nAbility to manage multiple, competing priorities;\n\nDemonstrated problem-solving and organizational skills within a fast-paced, dynamic and multi-faceted organization;\n\nBasic computer skills and experience with relationship management software, Word, Excel preferred;\n\nCompletion of vocational training in automotive service technology with experience in vehicle electronics\n\nGood reading, mathematical skills and the ability to interpret and study technical manuals and keep abreast of new technology as well as learn new service and repair procedures;\n\nSecondary level school leaving certificate or equivalency.\n\nNCTVET Certification in Automotive Training at Level 2 (minimum with experience).\n\nPhysical Demands\n\nThe physical demands here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n\nWhile performing the duties of this job, the employee is occasionally required to stand; walk; sit; use hands to finger, handle, feel objects, tools or controls; reach with hands and arms; climb stairs; balance; stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl; talk or hear; taste or smell. The employee must occasionally lift and/or move up to 25 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by the job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Regular intra-island travel required.\n\nWork Environment\n\nWork environment characteristics described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. While performing most of the duties of this job, the employee may not be exposed to adverse weather conditions. The noise level in the work environment is usually of loud to moderate volumes.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'systems,performs,essential,employee,vision,include,brake,perform essential,performs complex,diagnosis repair,functions,essential functions,diagnosis,job,complex,repair,level,work,engine,toyota,reasonable,standard,brake systems,required,perform'),(231,'jsearch','l8eNPRFoSFnFg76PAAAAAA==','IT Executive / IT Specialist / Systems Administrator – Kingston, Jamaica','Fusion CX',NULL,NULL,0,'https://careers.fusioncx.com/job/it-executive-it-specialist-systems-administrator-kingston-jamaica/','Are you searching for call center IT jobs in Kingston, Jamaica, where you can support business-critical systems, infrastructure, and end-user operations? Fusion CX is hiring an IT Executive / IT Specialist / Systems Administrator to manage local IT infrastructure, support end users, and ensure smooth technology operations. If you’re exploring hiring in Jamaica for IT support roles or looking for systems administrator opportunities with growth potential, this role offers a strong platform to advance your technical career.\nJob Description:\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs an IT Executive / IT Specialist / Systems Administrator, you will support the day-to-day IT operations of the site, oversee infrastructure components, and provide technical assistance to end users. This includes managing desktops, laptops, CCTV, access control systems, UPS, telecom support, and compliance-related requirements. The role requires hands-on troubleshooting, coordination with service vendors, and maintaining accuracy across asset, system, and IT operational workflows.\nKey Responsibilities\n\nTechnical & Infrastructure Support\n• Recommend and implement technologies that improve efficiency or reduce operational costs.\n• Update existing software to ensure compatibility with new systems.\n• Maintain desktops and laptops, including software installation and hardware replacement.\n• Collaborate with IT team members to develop and implement solutions for system issues.\n• Identify and troubleshoot system performance problems, adjusting hardware or software configurations.\n• Evaluate new technologies and equipment based on business needs.\n• Monitor computer network performance, availability, and connection stability.\n• Ensure security controls are enforced, including encryption, firewalls, and system safeguards.\n\nOperational Responsibilities\n• Provide local IT support to end users for troubleshooting and issue resolution.\n• Support onsite technology components such as desktops, laptops, CCTV, access control systems, UPS, and power dependencies.\n• Maintain local asset and software inventory records.\n• Coordinate with local vendors to resolve technical issues and fulfil IT service needs.\n• Track and resolve daily IT incidents through the ticketing system.\n• Support IT compliance requirements and audits in collaboration with the central security team.\n\nNote: Responsibilities may evolve based on business needs.\nJob Requirements:\n• Education: Professional certification in information technology preferred.\n• Basic networking knowledge (IP addressing, DNS, DHCP, network troubleshooting).\n• Minimum 3–5 years of IT support experience, preferably in a BPO or IT operations environment.\n• Ability to support a 24x7 operational environment during incidents or crises.\n• Understanding of data center technology, telecom, dialer systems, enterprise shared services, and endpoint management.\n• Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making abilities.\n• Ability to coordinate with internal teams, auditors, external vendors, and operational stakeholders.\n• Strong verbal and written communication skills.\n• Ability to manage reports, documentation, and system logs accurately.\n• Ability to maintain effective working relationships across departments.\n\nWorking Environment:\n\nUsual office working conditions. The noise level in the work environment is typical of most office environments with telephones, personal interruptions, and background noises. May be exposed to dust and debris. May be required to lift heavy computer equipment.\nWhy Join Fusion CX?\n\nJoin Fusion CX in Kingston, Jamaica, as an IT Executive / IT Specialist / Systems Administrator and grow with a global company.\n• Work in a hands-on technical role supporting mission-critical infrastructure and operations.\n• Build technical expertise across networks, endpoints, security, telecom, and compliance workflows.\n• Collaborate with IT, operations, and security teams in a dynamic, fast-paced environment.\n• Develop clear growth opportunities in systems administration, IT operations, and infrastructure management.\n\nIf you are looking for call center IT jobs in Kingston, Jamaica or seeking rewarding technology jobs or hiring in Jamaica for systems administration roles, apply now and grow your technical career with Fusion CX.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'systems,support,jamaica,technical,operations,infrastructure,local,fusion cx,executive,kingston,kingston jamaica,ability,specialist,specialist systems,cx,fusion,executive specialist,end,environment,technology,systems administrator,operational,security,role,needs'),(232,'jsearch','oA1Z0xDYrgtgOOYIAAAAAA==','Applications Administrator','Supreme Ventures Group',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Applications-Administrator-Job-227161.aspx','Supreme Ventures Services Limited, a subdidairy of Supreme Ventures Limited, is seeking to hire an Applications Administrator for the Aplications Department. The incumbent is responsible for providing administrative support to the unit by ensuring that Retailer documentation/information is maintained and adequately filed, while performing the following duties: Duties and Responsibilities: Monitor the applicant’s holistic experience from application to terminal installation/relocation/retrieval to ensure expert service delivery in a timely manner as set out by the Company. Maintain an accurate database by utilizing the lottery Enterprise System software, whilst being responsible for updating Retailer information to the CRM Lottery, Sports Betting and Horse Racing database as stipulated by the company. Initiate and maintain contact with applicants regarding their application submission as it relates to their requirements, deadlines and application process. Provide consistently high quality service by responding to customer queries relating to application submission, rejection and installation process Respond to telephone, emails, and in person enquiries from applicants in a timely manner Work effectively with the Business Development Officers and Manager in ensuring all the required documentations are received in accordance the application/compliance checklist. To be conversant with Lottery, Sports Betting and Horse Racing conditions and sound practices and to have a good knowledge of their relevant SOPs. Ensure proposed Retailer submission file is completed and reviewed by Manager to ensure full compliance and adherence to company policies and procedures. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE: Minimum Associate degree or equivalent Proven 3 years’ experience of administration Good experience of customer care services Knowledgeable of the CRM/Lottery enterprise System SKILLS: Excellent oral and written communications skills Strong organization and planning skills Excellent interpersonal and social skills Excellent IT skills, in particular, Excel, Word and Database Management We thank all applicants, however only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'lottery,application,skills,submission,applicants,retailer,skills excellent,excellent,database,experience,company,process,sports,sports betting,racing,limited,manner,lottery sports,lottery enterprise,horse racing,horse,good,supreme ventures,supreme,betting horse'),(236,'jsearch','RfAG3YoR4CeAUlheAAAAAA==','Senior Azure DevOps Engineer','Growth Acceleration Partners',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/699594d8da7696de2f55b243-senior-azure-devops-engineer?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nWHAT WE DO\n\nFounded in 2007, Growth Acceleration Partners (GAP) is a consulting and technology services company. We consult, design, build and modernize revenue-generating software and data engineering solutions for clients. With modernization services and AI tools, we help businesses achieve a competitive advantage through technology. GAP’s remote, integrated engineering teams use end-to-end solutions to innovate and align with your business goals. We have 600+ English-speaking engineers based in Latin America and approximately 20 U.S.-based engineers. With some of the highest customer satisfaction scores in the industry, GAP’s focus is customer and employee success.\n\nGAP is a woman-owned company headquartered in Austin Texas. We are a values-based company focused on growing our people by investing in education, onsite English classes and training in the latest technologies, including AI, data analytics and machine learning. Our goal is to provide solutions for our customers that help them achieve critical business outcomes, while enabling our GAPSters and our communities to attain long-term success.\n\nSummary\n\nWe are looking for a Senior Azure DevOps Engineer to design, implement, and optimize secure, scalable, and highly available cloud-native environments within Microsoft Azure.\n\nIn this role, you will lead infrastructure automation, CI/CD strategy, platform reliability, and DevSecOps practices across enterprise-grade systems. You will act as a technical reference for Azure architecture and DevOps standards, ensuring infrastructure is resilient, cost-efficient, and aligned with modern engineering practices.\n\nThis position requires deep hands-on expertise in Azure services, Infrastructure as Code, Kubernetes, automation, and production-grade CI/CD pipelines.\n\nEducation\n\n• Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Systems, or related field (or equivalent experience).\n\nProfessional Experience\n\n• 5+ years of experience in DevOps, Cloud Engineering, or Infrastructure roles.\n\n• 3+ years of hands-on experience working specifically with Microsoft Azure.\n\n• Proven experience managing production-grade Azure environments.\n\n• Experience working in Agile delivery environments.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nAzure Cloud Architecture & Infrastructure\n\n• Design and implement scalable Azure-based cloud infrastructure.\n\n• Manage Azure environments including networking, security, compute, and storage.\n\n• Architect high-availability and fault-tolerant systems.\n\n• Optimize Azure resource utilization and cost management.\n\nInfrastructure as Code (IaC)\n\n• Implement and maintain Infrastructure as Code using:\n\n• Terraform (preferred)\n\n• Azure ARM / Bicep\n\n• Automate multi-environment deployments (dev, staging, production).\n\n• Ensure repeatability and compliance through codified infrastructure.\n\nCI/CD & Automation\n\n• Design and maintain CI/CD pipelines using:\n\n• Azure DevOps\n\n• GitHub Actions\n\n• Implement blue/green, canary, and rolling deployment strategies.\n\n• Automate build, test, security scanning, and deployment processes.\n\n• Integrate automated testing and security validation into pipelines.\n\nContainerization & Kubernetes\n\n• Deploy and manage containerized applications using:\n\n• Docker\n\n• Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)\n\n• Implement container orchestration best practices.\n\n• Manage cluster scaling, upgrades, and monitoring.\n\nSecurity & DevSecOps\n\n• Implement security best practices in Azure (RBAC, Managed Identities, Key Vault).\n\n• Secure APIs and services using OAuth and token-based authentication.\n\n• Enforce security policies and compliance controls.\n\n• Integrate vulnerability scanning and secrets management.\n\nMonitoring & Observability\n\n• Implement monitoring and logging using:\n\n• Azure Monitor\n\n• Application Insights\n\n• Log Analytics\n\n• Configure alerts, dashboards, and performance metrics.\n\n• Support incident response and root-cause analysis.\n\nCollaboration & Technical Leadership\n\n• Partner with development teams to improve release reliability.\n\n• Provide guidance on cloud architecture decisions.\n\n• Mentor engineers on DevOps best practices.\n\n• Contribute to platform engineering and automation strategy.\n\nRequired Technical Skills\n\nAzure Core Services\n\n• Azure App Services\n\n• Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)\n\n• Azure Functions\n\n• Azure Virtual Machines\n\n• Azure Storage (Blob, Files)\n\n• Azure SQL\n\n• Azure Key Vault\n\n• Azure Virtual Network (VNet), NSGs, Load Balancers\n\n• Azure Entra ID (Identity & Access Management)\n\nInfrastructure & Automation\n\n• Terraform (advanced level)\n\n• ARM Templates or Bicep\n\n• PowerShell and/or Bash scripting\n\nCI/CD & DevOps\n\n• Azure DevOps Pipelines\n\n• GitHub Actions\n\n• Git workflows and branching strategies\n\nContainers & Orchestration\n\n• Docker\n\n• Kubernetes (AKS preferred)\n\nMonitoring & Logging\n\n• Azure Monitor\n\n• Application Insights\n\n• Log Analytics\n\n• Experience with centralized logging solutions\n\nReliability & Deployment Patterns\n\n• High availability design\n\n• Load balancing\n\n• Auto-scaling\n\n• Blue/green deployments\n\n• Canary releases\n\n• Disaster recovery strategies\n\nNice to Have\n\n• Azure DevOps Engineer Expert certification.\n\n• Experience implementing Zero Trust security models.\n\n• Experience with policy management (Azure Policy).\n\n• Exposure to FinOps practices.\n\n• Experience supporting regulated environments.\n\n• Familiarity with GitOps workflows.\n\nSoft Skills\n\n• Advanced English proficiency (written and verbal).\n\n• Strong analytical and troubleshooting skills.\n\n• Ownership mindset with proactive problem-solving.\n\n• Ability to communicate complex infrastructure concepts clearly.\n\n• Comfortable working in distributed teams.\n\n• Continuous learning attitude toward evolving Azure services.\n\nAt Growth Acceleration Partners, we\'re an equal opportunity employer committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We value everyone\'s unique background, and we provide equal opportunities regardless of race, color, creed, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, national origin, disability, marital status, veteran status or any other personal right protected by law. We foster a culture of belonging and strive to provide a welcoming environment where everyone feels safe to contribute and grow.\nThis offer from \"Growth Acceleration Partners\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 83% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'azure,infrastructure,experience,devops,azure devops,implement,security,services,provide,gap,kubernetes,based,automation,practices,engineering,strategies,aks,company,best,best practices,acceleration,acceleration partners,technical,production,architecture'),(237,'jsearch','TFCi1c0-dA4o1i56AAAAAA==','DevOps Engineer','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/8X3Y63WR?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title : DevOps Engineer\n\nRole Purpose\n\nThe DevOps Engineer is responsible for enabling continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD), driving automation, and ensuring the reliability, scalability, and security of platforms and applications.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, build, and maintain CI/CD pipelines to support efficient and reliable software delivery\n• Automate infrastructure provisioning, configuration, and application deployments using infrastructure-as-code practices\n• Monitor system performance, availability, and reliability; proactively identify and resolve issues\n• Collaborate with development, security, and operations teams to improve deployment processes and platform stability\n• Implement and maintain logging, monitoring, and alerting solutions\n• Support incident response, root cause analysis, and continuous improvement initiatives\n• Ensure systems comply with security, compliance, and governance requirements\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• Minimum 5+ years of experience in DevOps, Site Reliability Engineering, or related roles\n• Strong experience with CI/CD tools and practices\n• Hands-on experience with containerization and orchestration technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes)\n• Experience working with cloud platforms and services\n• Solid understanding of automation, scripting, and infrastructure-as-code tools\n• Strong awareness of security, compliance, and risk management principles\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with monitoring and observability tools (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, ELK)\n• Familiarity with DevSecOps practices and automated security testing\n• Experience supporting high-availability or mission-critical systems\n• Exposure to regulated or enterprise environments\n• Experience mentoring junior engineers or leading platform initiatives',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'experience,security,devops,devops engineer,continuous,reliability,initiatives,security compliance,engineer,infrastructure,ci,practices,cd,ci cd,tools,automation,platforms,delivery,platform,compliance,monitoring,code,systems,maintain,support'),(238,'jsearch','6fiASFhmktRK2vj6AAAAAA==','Cloud Engineer (REMOTE)','thehivecareers.co',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.careers-page.com/thehivecareers/job/93R96R66?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Job Title: Cloud Engineer\n\nRole Purpose\n\nDesign, implement, and manage secure, scalable, and cost-effective cloud infrastructure aligned with enterprise banking standards, security requirements, and governance frameworks.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, build, and maintain cloud infrastructure environments across public and hybrid cloud platforms\n• Implement and enforce cloud security, governance, and compliance controls in line with enterprise and regulatory standards\n• Monitor, optimize, and continuously improve cloud performance, availability, and cost efficiency\n• Collaborate with application, security, and DevOps teams to support cloud-based solutions and migrations\n• Automate infrastructure provisioning and configuration using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) practices\n• Troubleshoot cloud infrastructure issues and perform root cause analysis to ensure system stability\n• Maintain documentation for cloud architectures, configurations, and operational procedures\n\nRequired Experience & Skills\n• Minimum 5 years experience in infrastructure, cloud engineering, or platform engineering roles\n• Hands-on experience with AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform (GCP)\n• Strong understanding of cloud networking, compute, storage, and identity management concepts\n• Experience implementing security controls within cloud environments, preferably in financial services\n• Strong problem-solving skills and ability to operate in enterprise, regulated environments\n• Experience supporting high-availability and mission-critical systems\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience within banking or financial services environments\n• Exposure to DevOps and CI/CD pipelines\n• Experience with Infrastructure as Code tools such as Terraform, CloudFormation, or ARM templates\n• Familiarity with cost management, monitoring, and optimization tools\n• Cloud certifications (e.g., AWS, Azure, or GCP certifications)',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'cloud,experience,infrastructure,environments,security,cloud infrastructure,cost,gcp,financial services,aws azure,banking,aws,cloud engineer,certifications,experience infrastructure,financial,enterprise,standards,controls,governance,azure,design,maintain,management,implement'),(239,'jsearch','6JvmhbsWePC7TzjGAAAAAA==','Revenue Operations (AI & Automation)','Linear',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6984c5fd9242569942759b08-revenue-operations-ai-automation','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America\n\nAt Linear, we are on a mission to bring magic back to software. To empower product teams to do their best work, we are building an issue tracking and project management tool that combines UI elegance with world-class performance. Founded in 2019, Linear has become the tool of choice for 20,000+ companies to plan and build their products.\n\nLinear was set up as a fully remote company from the start. Today, our small but mighty team is distributed across North America and Europe. What unites us is relentless focus, fast execution, and our passion for software craftsmanship. We are all makers at heart and care deeply about the quality of our work.\n\nLinear is in a unique position—we are profitable, which gives us the flexibility to invest thoughtfully as we grow. We want to build a company that scales well—not just in our product, but in how we run our GTM programs. In this role, you’ll design, own, and evolve the systems that power our sales, success, and marketing teams. You’ll take ideas from concept to execution, streamlining our tech stack, introducing automation and AI where it meaningfully improves outcomes, and building scalable workflows that help our customer-facing teams focus on high-impact work.\n\nPlease note: We are an equal opportunity employer and remote-only company. At this time, we can only support hiring within the US for this role.\n\nWhat you\'ll do\n• Own and evolve our GTM systems to support sales, success, and marketing as we scale\n• Increase the productivity of our Customer-facing teams through automation, AI, and process improvement\n• Help the business make data-informed decisions through analysis and discussion\n• Work cross-functionally with functional leaders to align on priorities, communicate plans, and ensure GTM systems support company goals\n\nWhat we\'re looking for\n• 5+ years of experience at a fast-growing SaaS company, ideally in a Revenue Operations, Systems, or similar role\n• Expert experience with GTM systems:\n• HubSpot, Salesforce or or equivalent CRMs\n• Clay, Cargo, or similar enrichment and workflow tools\n• Outreach or comparable sales engagement platforms\n• Pocus or other product and revenue analytics tools\n• Experience with automation and AI\n• Comfortable oscillating between detailed system work and higher-level thinking about process, scale, and outcomes\n• Ability to operate in ambiguity, adjust priorities as the business evolves, and make pragmatic decisions with good judgment and common sense\n• A strong partner to Sales, Customer Success, Marketing and leadership to translate business needs into scalable systems and processes\n\nWhat we offer\n• Interesting and challenging work\n• Work-life balance\n• Competitive salary and equity\n• Employee-friendly equity terms (early exercise, extended exercise)\n• Stipend to set up your home office\n• Paid lunch and coffee during workdays\n• Work remotely, no commuting to the office\n• Paid co-working space/desk at an office\n• Health, dental, and vision insurance (US)\n• Regular team events and offsites\n• 5 weeks of paid vacation\n• 4 months of paid parental leave\n\nLearn how we think and work:\n• A story about our mission: Read Me\n• How we work: Designing remote work at Linear\n• Our CEO and co-founder, Karri at 20VC: How to Grow Capital Efficiently in a World of BS Growth\n• Make an Org Chart You Want to Ship — Advice from Linear on How Heirloom Tomatoes Should Inspire Team Design\n• Building our teams: Why and how we do work trials at Linear\n• A video series: Conversations on Quality\n• Read about our recent Series C Fundraise and Giving our team liquidity\n\nThis offer from \"Linear\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 86% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'linear,work,gtm,automation ai,success marketing,gtm systems,sales,paid,automation,office,systems,revenue,make,company,office paid,sales success,revenue operations,read,work linear,remote company,facing teams,teams,role ll,customer facing,marketing'),(240,'jsearch','xxorvv04cmkrzhObAAAAAA==','Career Opportunities: Machine Learning Scientist, Pricing (Open to Remote) (286643)','Arvato',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/699040b5da7696de2f5202df-career-opportunities-machine-learning-scientist-pricing-open-to-remote-286643','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America, United States\n\nThe Data Science team at Penguin Random House is seeking a Machine Learning Scientists to build and improve machine learning products that power how we understand demand, set strategy, and connect readers with books, with a focus on pricing.\n\nIn this role, you’ll use rich datasets to build sophisticated models that help price books for the market. Our pricing products model market response to optimize revenue while mitigating risks to sales and brands.\n\nAs the world’s leading publishing house, Penguin Random House is AI-forward and continues to invest in modern machine learning to shape the future of book discovery, sales, and customer engagement. Our Data Science team applies ML across personalization, forecasting, pricing, and experimentation, and we actively explore emerging AI capabilities to meaningfully improve customer experiences.\n\nThis role spans the ML lifecycle; from problem framing and prototyping to production and iteration, with a strong emphasis on building robust, maintainable software and using modern AI tools thoughtfully to accelerate development.\n\nSpecific responsibilities include:\n• Owns the ML lifecycle: Frames problems, prototypes solutions, validates performance, and iterates based on measurement and feedback.\n• Applies sound statistical and ML practices for feature development, training, evaluation, validation, and maintenance.\n• Defines success metrics and uses offline evaluation plus online experimentation (including A/B tests) to validate performance, monitor quality over time, and drive ongoing iteration.\n• Partners with engineering and platform counterparts to productionize models, including repeatable training, deployment workflows, monitoring, and refresh strategies.\n• Diagnoses model performance issues and data quality problems; communicates findings and recommended actions clearly to stakeholders.\n• Writes maintainable, production-minded code and contributes to team standards (code review, documentation, reproducibility, and testing where appropriate).\n• Stays current on applied ML and uses modern AI tools to accelerate exploration, questioning, and implementation without sacrificing quality.\n\nPlease apply if you meet the following qualifications:\n• Master’s with 2+ years of applied work experience OR PhD in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Engineering, Operations Research, Statistics or a related quantitative field\n• Strong proficiency in Python and common ML frameworks and libraries (for example PyTorch or TensorFlow).\n• Strong SQL skills and experience working with large datasets for feature development, analysis, and validation.\n• Experience taking models from development to production (batch scoring, APIs, or downstream integration).\n• Solid understanding of experimentation and measurement.\n• Proficiency with the latest AI tools to develop well-designed and robust software.\n• Strong communication skills and ability to translate between business goals and technical solutions.\n• Familiarity with cloud and modern data/ML tooling (AWS, Databricks, Docker, Kubernetes, Spark, or similar).\n• Exposure to MLOps concepts and tooling (model registries, pipelines, monitoring, reproducibility).\n\nPreferred qualifications:\n\nWe welcome candidates with depth in either (or both) of these applied ML areas:\n• Experience with time series forecasting, causal/market-response modeling, optimization, or risk-aware modeling.\n• Familiarity with automated model retraining, monitoring, and long-running model maintenance.\n• Familiarity with experimentation, measurement, and online evaluation.\n\nPlease be advised that candidates selected to advance to the 1st round of interviews will be required to show photo ID on camera, and final interviews for this role will be in person at a Penguin Random House location.\n\nThe salary range for this position is $130,000 - $175,000. All positions are currently eligible for an annual profit award or bonus, subject to company results.  \n\nApplications for this role will be accepted through March 1, 2026 or until the role is filled. We encourage you to apply early, as we review applications on a rolling basis. Please include your resume and cover letter for consideration. Before applying for any role at Penguin Random House, we recommend you review our applicant resources page and our FAQs page.\n\nPenguin Random House job postings include a good faith compensation range for each open position. The salary range listed is specific to each particular open position and takes into account various factors including the specifics of the individual role, and candidate\'s relevant experience and qualifications.\n\nFull-time employees are eligible for our comprehensive benefits program. Our range of benefits include, but are not limited to, Medical/Prescription drug insurance, Dental, Vision, Health Care/Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account, Health Savings Account, Pre-Tax and Roth 401(k), Short and Long-Term Disability Insurance, Life/AD&D Insurance, Commuter Benefits, Student Loan Repayment Program, Educational Assistance & generous paid time off.\n\nPenguin Random House is the leading adult and children\'s publishing house in North America, the United Kingdom and many other regions around the world. In publishing the best books in every genre and subject for all ages, we are committed to quality, excellence in execution, and innovation throughout the entire publishing process: editorial, design, marketing, publicity, sales, production, and distribution. Our vibrant and diverse international community of nearly 300 publishing brands and imprints include Ballantine Bantam Dell, Berkley, Clarkson Potter, Crown, DK, Doubleday, Dutton, Grosset & Dunlap, Little Golden Books, Knopf, Modern Library, Pantheon, Penguin Books, Penguin Press, Penguin Random House Audio, Penguin Young Readers, Portfolio, Puffin, Putnam, Random House, Random House Children\'s Books, Riverhead, Ten Speed Press, Viking, and Vintage, among others. More information can be found at http://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/.\n\nPenguin Random House values the array of talents and perspectives that a diverse workforce brings. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, national origin, religion, age, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, or protected veteran status.\n\nCompany: Penguin Random House LLC | Job ID: 286643\n\nThis offer from \"Arvato\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,130000.00,175000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','penguin,house,random house,random,penguin random,books,ml,publishing,pricing,model,include,experimentation,machine learning,machine,modern,monitoring,measurement,role,learning,account,range,production,applied,open,development'),(242,'jsearch','vSDiifZb-cJlUKuPAAAAAA==','Senior AI Agent Architect','Visual Concepts',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/69987028da7696de2f5937d7-senior-ai-agent-architect','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America\n\nAt Visual Concepts, we believe great games are made by diverse and empowered teams with a shared passion for play. As one of the world’s top game development studios, we have shipped over 100 multi-sku titles to critical acclaim and commercial success. Our teams are independent and ambitious. Our studios in Novato, Irvine, Budapest, Shanghai, Austin, Boise, Seoul and Parksville, Canada are committed to artistry and ground breaking technology, offering top candidates the opportunity to learn and grow with some of the hardest working and most creative minds in the industry.\n\nWhat We Need:\n\nWe create NBA 2K and our teams push the boundaries of realism, scale, and player experience—and now we’re investing deeply in artificial intelligence to redefine how games are built.\n\nMost studios use AI to polish the edges; we’re using it to rewrite the core. We aren\'t looking for someone to optimize a pipeline—we’re looking for an architect to design a future where intelligent agents act as force multipliers for human creativity. If you’re a C++/Python hybrid who believes the next great leap in gaming won’t come from better pixels, but from smarter workflows then we need to chat.\n\nWe are looking for an exceptional AI Engineer to help design and develop intelligent agents that will fundamentally change the way our games are made. This role is not about simply improving existing pipelines or automating isolated tasks. It’s about exploring new, AI-driven approaches to game development that can unlock brand new workflows, capabilities, and creative possibilities.\n\nYou’ll work at the intersection of AI research, systems engineering, and game development, helping shape a long-term vision for how intelligent agents can augment and transform the work of developers across disciplines.\n\nWhat You Will Do:\n• Design and implement AI-driven agents that assist, collaborate with, or autonomously perform complex development tasks across large-scale game projects\n• Create agents that can understand game engine context, assist in asset generation, debug complex systems, or simulate player behavior at scale\n• Identify bottlenecks in traditional game dev (design, QA, coding, or art) and bridge the gap with AI-driven solutions that turn weeks of manual work into hours of supervised generation\n• Collaborate with gameplay engineers and technical artists to integrate these agents into our proprietary engine and toolsets\n• Explore novel applications of modern AI techniques (e.g., LLMs, reinforcement learning, multi-agent systems) to create new ways of building, iterating on, and shipping games\n• Work closely with engineers, designers, artists, and technical leadership to identify high-impact opportunities for AI-powered transformation\n• Prototype, evaluate, and iterate on experimental systems, balancing long-term vision with practical integration into real production environments\n• Help define internal platforms, tools, and architectures that enable AI agents to operate safely, effectively, and at scale within our development ecosystem\n• Stay ahead of emerging research and industry advances, translating pioneering ideas into production-ready solutions\n\nWho Will Be A Great Fit:\n• 5+ years in Software Engineering, with at least 2+ years focused specifically on AI/Machine Learning\n• BS/MS in Computer Science, AI, Robotics, or a related field (or equivalent \"in-the-trenches\" experience)\n• Strong background in AI, machine learning, or applied research, with experience building real-world systems (not just models)\n• Hands-on experience with modern AI frameworks and techniques, such as large language models, agent frameworks, reinforcement learning, or hybrid symbolic/ML systems\n• Excellent software engineering skills, with experience working in large, complex codebases\n• Expert-level proficiency in **Python** (for AI/Tools) and **C++** (for Engine integration)\n• Demonstrated success deploying agentic workflows or complex ML models into production environments\n• Ability to think beyond incremental optimization and envision entirely new workflows enabled by intelligent systems\n• Strong communication skills and the ability to collaborate across teams\n• Passion for games, interactive systems, or creative technology is a major plus\n\nThis is a role that can be remote and may be based anywhere in the United States. Below are the expected salary and wage ranges for applicants based in locations where the pay transparency law is in effect: California: $152,500 - $200,00 per year. New York State (inclusive of New York City): $137,300 - $180,000 per year. Washington: $152,500 - $200,00 per year. New Jersey: $137,300 - $180,000 per year. British Columbia: $135,000 - $173,500 (CAD) per year. Base pay offered is based on market location, and may vary further depending on individualized factors for job candidates, such as job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and other objective business considerations. Subject to those same considerations, the total compensation package for this position may also include other elements, including a bonus and/or equity awards, in addition to a full range of medical, financial, and/or other benefits. Details of participation in these benefit plans will be provided if an employee receives an offer of employment. If hired, employee will be in an \'at-will position\' and the company reserves the right to modify base salary (as well as any other discretionary payment or compensation or benefit program) at any time, including for reasons related to individual performance, company or individual department/team performance, and market factors.\n\nTo learn more about Visual Concepts and our studio locations, check out our website at www.vcentertainment.com\n\nThis offer from \"Visual Concepts\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,135000.00,180000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','game,games,agents,ai,new,systems,year,intelligent agents,visual concepts,game development,500,visual,intelligent,studios,agent,development,great,creative,complex,engine,concepts,create,york,locations,new workflows'),(245,'jsearch','z2-7qRVJsinwMEDlAAAAAA==','DIGITAL IMPLEMENTATION OFFICER','University of the Commonwealth Caribbean',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/DIGITAL-IMPLEMENTATION-OFFICER-Job-227166.aspx','The University of the Commonwealth Caribbean (UCC) invites applications from qualified, dynamic professionals for the position of: DIGITAL IMPLEMENTATION OFFICER JOB SUMMARY: This position is responsible for supporting the implementation, deployment, and optimization of digital systems and artificial intelligence enabled solutions across the university. The role focuses on translating approved digital and AI initiatives into operational systems that support academic, administrative, and research activities. The incumbent will work closely with the IS&T team, functional units, and external vendors to ensure systems are implemented securely, efficiently, and in alignment with institutional policies and governance frameworks. RESPONSIBILITIES: (including but not limited to) 1. Digital Systems Implementation: Support the implementation, configuration, and rollout of institutional digital platforms including administrative systems, learning technologies, document management systems, workflow automation tools, and cloud-based services. Coordinate implementation planning by reviewing functional requirements, timelines, dependencies, and vendor documentation. Configure system components such as user roles, permissions, workflows, templates, and forms in accordance with approved specifications. Coordinate with internal IS&T team and external vendors during deployment, testing, go-live, and stabilization phases. Support user acceptance testing by preparing test cases, validating outcomes, and documenting issues. Assist with data migration, validation, and post-implementation verification activities. Provide continuous implementation support and assist with complex issues where required. 2. Artificial Intelligence Systems Support: Support the implementation and operation of approved AI-enabled solutions such as chatbots, intelligent document processing tools, analytics platforms, and automation systems. Configuring AI tool parameters, prompts, workflows, access controls, and usage limits under supervision. Participate in testing AI outputs to ensure accuracy, reliability, and alignment with approved institutional use cases. Support data preparation and validation activities related to AI systems while ensuring compliance with data protection and privacy requirements (Supporting the Data Protection Officer). Assist in monitoring AI systems usage, performance and report issues, limitations, or risks. Support the application of responsible AI principles, including transparency, data privacy, bias awareness, and acceptable use. 3. Training, Documentation, and User Support: Assist in preparing user guides, standard operating procedures, AI usage guidelines, and training materials. Support system demonstrations, onboarding sessions, and awareness initiatives for staff and stakeholders. Respond to user queries related to implemented digital and AI systems and provide first-line support. Maintain accurate implementation documentation, configuration records, and handover notes for operational teams. 4. General Tasks: Troubleshoot and resolve operational issues related to implemented digital and AI systems. Maintain documentation of system configurations, workflows, and implementation decisions for future reference and audits. Any other duties consistent with the nature, level, and grade of the post as may be required. REQUIREMENTS AND SKILLS At least 2 years’ experience in system implementation, application support, or digital transformation initiatives. Working knowledge of enterprise digital systems and cloud-based platforms. Expert understanding of artificial intelligence concepts such as automation, chatbots, analytics, and AI-assisted tools. Familiarity with data protection, access control, and information security principles. Ability to follow implementation plans, technical documentation, and standard operating procedures. Basic troubleshooting and documentation skills. CORE VALUES Commitment: Actively contributes to achieving organizational goals Diversity: Respects others and values their diverse perspectives and contributions Integrity: Acts in a manner consistent with UCC’s core values and organizational principles Accountability: Takes responsibility for own action and delegated work CORE COMPETENCIES Communication: Communicates clearly and effectively with colleagues, users, and stakeholders Collaboration: Works effectively with others and contributes to a positive team environment Planning: Organizes tasks and supports projects in a structured and timely manner Analysis and decision-making: Assists in analyzing information and identifying practical solutions Initiative-taking: Demonstrates willingness to learn and support improvement initiatives Flexibility: Responds positively to changing priorities and operational needs KEY Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in information technology, Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Science, or a related field (or equivalent work experience). Certifications in cloud platforms or digital systems implementation. Certificate in AI Systems or automation-related certifications. IT service management or project support certifications We thank all applicants, however, only those who are shortlisted will be contacted!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'implementation,digital,support,systems,user,approved,digital systems,ai,documentation,ai systems,assist,initiatives,implemented,institutional,digital ai,data protection,officer,operational,issues,certifications,protection,related,automation,platforms,data'),(246,'jsearch','3rGMKjFPy1Kwy5bfAAAAAA==','LATAM Controller','Connectly',NULL,NULL,0,'https://himalayas.app/companies/connectly/jobs/latam-controller','Are You Ready to Revolutionize Communication and Commerce with Connectly.ai?\nAt Connectly.ai, we’re transforming how businesses connect with their customers. Our mission is to enable seamless, intelligent conversations through AI-powered messaging. This is a bold, expansive vision that requires a team as dynamic, driven, and inventive as the technology we’re creating.\nTo bring this vision to life, we’re looking for candidates who are passionate about redefining customer engagement and have a deep belief in the power of AI and WhatsApp to create genuine, impactful interactions. We seek individuals who are eager to tackle tough challenges, value continuous growth, and thrive in a collaborative, high-energy environment. We want teammates who are driven to make a lasting difference, undaunted by complex problems, and motivated to shape the future of conversational commerce.\nWhat It Takes to Thrive at Connectly.ai\nOur culture is ambitious and fast-paced, designed for those who want to work with top-tier professionals and are committed to excellence. If you’re ready to grow beyond what you thought possible, are excited about joining a mission-driven team, and are open to continuous learning, Connectly.ai might be the place for you.\nConnectly.ai’s Vision:\nAt Connectly, we’re building the future of conversational commerce in Latin America, starting with WhatsApp. Our 360° AI engagement platform empowers retailers to sell, support, and scale directly inside the app their customers already use every day.\nWe’re a VC-backed Series B startup with a world-class team from Meta, Google, Uber, McKinsey, BCG and other leading companies. We operate as a hybrid organization, with offices in Bogotá and San Francisco, and distributed teams across Latin America, including Brazil, where many of our AI initiatives are based.\nIf you’re ready to help shape this future with us, we can’t wait to meet you!\nJob Summary\n• We are looking for a hands-on Controller based in Latin America to own the full accounting and financial operations function. This is a high-impact role reporting directly to the CFO. You will be responsible for the accuracy of our books across three geographies (US, Greece, Brazil),manage relationships with outsourced accounting firms, oversee month-end close and consolidations, and supervise a junior FinOps team member.\n• This is not a back-office role. You will be the single point of accountability for everything backward-looking in finance: if the numbers are right, it is because of you. If they are wrong, it is on you.\nResponsibilities\n• Month-End Close & Consolidations\n• Own the end-to-end month-end close process across all entities (US, Greece, Brazil)\n• Prepare and review consolidated financial statements under US GAAP\n• Ensure intercompany eliminations, currency translation, and reconciliations are accurate\n• Deliver close within established timelines with full documentation\n• Outsourced Firm Management\n• Serve as the primary point of contact for three outsourced accounting teams (US, GR,BR)\n• Set quality standards, review deliverables, and hold firms accountable for accuracy\n• Assess outsourced firm performance within first 90 days and recommend changes if needed\n• Manage the transition if firms need to be replaced\n• Financial Operations Oversight\n• Supervise the junior FinOps associate (payments, billing, expense review)\n• Establish and enforce internal controls and approval workflows\n• Ensure compliance with local regulations across all jurisdictions\n• Accuracy & Process Improvement\n• Act as the quality gate for all financial data before it reaches the Head of Finance\n• Identify and fix recurring accuracy issues in the books\n• Document and standardize accounting processes across geographies\n• Support external audit preparation and liaison\nRequirements\n• Must-Have\n• 5+ years of progressive accounting experience, including consolidations\n• Strong US GAAP knowledge (working experience, not just theoretical)\n• Experience managing or working closely with outsourced accounting teams\n• Fluent English (written and verbal). You will interface with US-based firms and leadership\n• Hands-on mentality. This is a doer role, not a delegator role\n• Experience with multi-entity, multi-currency environments\n• Proficiency with ERP systems and Excel/Google Sheets at an advanced level\n• Nice-to-Have\n• CPA or equivalent local certification\n• Experience in a startup or high-growth environment\n• Familiarity with Brazilian and/or Greek accounting standards\n• Experience with NetSuite, QuickBooks, or Xero\n• Portuguese or Spanish fluency (in addition to English)\nJoin Us\nAt Connectly, we believe in curiosity, excellence, and a relentless drive to innovate. If you’re passionate about building transformative AI systems and want to shape the technical direction of a fast-growing global company, we’d love to meet you.Connectly is an equal opportunity employer. We’re committed to building a diverse, inclusive, and supportive global workplace.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'connectly,accounting,outsourced,connectly ai,firms,close,end,ai,outsourced accounting,brazil,consolidations,end close,month end,financial,accuracy,month,commerce,want,currency,supervise,gaap,firm,google,whatsapp,close consolidations'),(247,'jsearch','i0p7BoWx7A3JQO_zAAAAAA==','Senior AI Engineer (Remote - LATAM)','Seagull Scientific',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697d939c92425699426e29a1-senior-ai-engineer-remote---latam','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nWHO WE ARE\n\nSeagull Software, LLC, is a global leader in real-time, item-level visibility and label management solutions, dedicated to powering the world’s most complex supply chains with innovative tools for traceability, authentication, and automated inventory management. Our BarTender™️ platform enables businesses across all industries to design, manage, print, and automate the production of labels, barcodes, and RFID tags, ensuring seamless tracking and compliance for over 100 billion unique identifiers each year. Leveraging the Mojix™️ high-security, scalable SaaS traceability platform, Seagull delivers end-to-end intelligence, harmonizing data to drive operational efficiency, enhance customer experiences, and reduce risk. Learn more at www.seagullsoftware.com.\n\nWe’re a growing, profitable, mid-size business with a 40-year history of leading in our field. Headquartered in Redmond, Washington, with offices across the United States, Europe, and Asia, Seagull empowers businesses worldwide to keep their products moving, traceable, and safe. You’ll work with global, talented, and diverse teams, passionate about what they do and its impact on everyone, everywhere. Join us and help shape the way the world works.\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis is a full-time Direct Contractor position, and the role is remote—candidates may be located in any LATAM country.\n\nJOB SUMMARY\n\nThe Senior AI Engineer is responsible for leading the design, development, and implementation of artificial intelligence initiatives focused on Backoffice functions. This role drives automation, process optimization, and intelligent decision support across internal business areas by leveraging AI technologies and integrations with existing enterprise systems.\n\nThe position works closely with IT, Finance, HR, Operations, and other corporate teams to identify opportunities where AI can improve efficiency, scalability, and operational performance.\n\nWHAT YOU WILL DO\n\nBackoffice AI Enablement\n• Design and implement AI-driven solutions to optimize Backoffice processes.\n• Identify, prioritize, and execute AI and automation use cases with business impact.\nAI Development & Automation\n• Develop, deploy, and maintain AI models, intelligent workflows, and automation solutions.\n• Integrate AI solutions with enterprise systems (ERP, CRM, ITSM, data platforms).\nSystems Integration & Data\n• Work with structured and unstructured data sources to enable AI-driven insights.\nGovernance, Security & Compliance\n• Ensure AI solutions comply with security, privacy, and governance standards.\nCollaboration & Enablement\n• Partner with stakeholders to translate business needs into technical solutions.\n• Support adoption through documentation and best practices.\nWHAT WE REQUIRE\n• 5+ years of experience in AI/ML, data-driven automation, intelligent systems, or software engineering (e.g., AI Engineer, ML Engineer, Data Scientist with production experience) with at least 3+ years of experience focused on AI development and automation.\n• Experience using GitHub for source control, collaboration, versioning, and review of AI and automation code, following established development and security practices.\n• Hands-on experience with AI technologies including LLMs, prompt engineering, natural language processing, document intelligence, and automation tools.\n• Experience integrating AI solutions with enterprise systems.\n• Solid understanding of Middlewares, REST APIs, webhooks, and event-driven integrations.\n• Experience designing and implementing data pipelines and preparing data for AI use.\n• Familiarity with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure or GCP) and managed AI/ML services.\n• Experience with version control, CI/CD, and basic MLOps practices.\n• Ability to translate business/backoffice problems into technical AI solutions and measurable outcomes.\n• Proficiency in written and spoken English.\n• Strong ability to understand business processes and collaborate with non-technical stakeholders to identify and refine AI opportunities.\n• Clear, structured communicator who can explain complex technical concepts in simple terms for decision makers.\n• Proactive, ownership-driven mindset: comfortable taking a problem from idea to proof of concept to production.\n• Strong collaboration skills; able to work closely with IT, security, data, and engineering teams.\n• Curiosity and continuous learning attitude towards new AI technologies, tools, and best practices.\n• Ability to work as a direct contractor.\nEDUCATION\n• Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field of study, or equivalent experience.\n• AI related certifications are a plus.\nTERMS OF EMPLOYMENT\n\nUpon hire, you must be able to provide documentation that proves authorization to work in your country of residence.\n\nOUR CULTURE\n\nWe offer a dynamic, culturally diverse, and fun environment where people with energy, creativity, and passion work together to deliver amazing product experiences for our customers. Join a team where your background is valued and respected, and your unique insights and ideas contribute to building a culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion.\n\nEQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY\n\nSeagull Software, LLC, is proud to provide equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws. This policy applies to all terms and conditions of recruiting and employment.\n\n#LI-Remote\n\n#LI-Hybrid\n\n#LI-LATAM\n\n#LI-Peru\nThis offer from \"Seagull Scientific\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ai,seagull,automation,li,backoffice,solutions,security,data,ai solutions,enterprise systems,experience ai,ai technologies,experience,business,employment,engineer,terms,ai engineer,collaboration,latam,driven,practices,development,work,intelligent'),(248,'jsearch','BEzb_m0Ad0wnw_rjAAAAAA==','Data Scientist |  AI & ML Ops','Addi',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/698ca10d92425699427ce09d-data-scientist-ai-ml-ops','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nAbout Addi\n\nWe are a leading financial platform, building the future of payments, shopping, and banking—a world where consumers and merchants can transact effortlessly and grow together. Today, we serve over 2 million customers and partner with more than 20,000 merchants, making Addi Colombia’s fastest-growing marketplace.\n\nWith a state-of-the-art, technology-first approach, we provide banking solutions (deposits, payments, unsecured credit) and commerce services (e-commerce, marketing), bridging the financial gap for millions and redefining how people experience financial freedom. As the country’s leading Buy Now, Pay Later provider, we have secured regulatory approval to operate as a bank, unlocking even greater opportunities for our customers. In the past year, we have also achieved profitability, reinforcing the strength of our business model and our ability to scale sustainably.\n\nOur mission has earned the trust of world-class investors, including Andreessen Horowitz, Architect Capital, GIC, Goldman Sachs, Greycroft, Monashees, Notable Capital, Quona Capital, Union Square Ventures, Victory Park Capital, and more, who back our vision for the future. With their support, we are not just growing—we are transforming Latin America’s financial ecosystem and shaping the next generation to shop, pay, and bank in Colombia.\n\nBut what truly sets us apart is how we build. We are a conscious company, driven by deep experience in scaling technology, services and products, and we live by our values every day.\n\nAbout the Role\n\nThis is where you come in. Below, you’ll find what this role is all about—the impact you’ll drive, the challenges you’ll tackle, and what it takes to thrive at Addi. If you’re ready to be part of something big, keep reading.\n\nWhat’s the mission you’ll drive\n\nDesign, build, and operate the Decision Intelligence Engines that power Addi’s personalized customer journeys, while transforming Addi’s Shop into an automated, AI-driven ecosystem by deploying State-of-the-Art (SOTA) architectures, including Sequential Deep Learning and LLMs to optimize customer LTV, activation, and retention in real-time.\n\nWhat you will do\n• Segmentation & Behavioral Analysis: Design and maintain segmentation models based on behavior, performance, lifecycle stage, and growth potential.\n• Outcome Prediction: Design, train, and deploy models to predict customer behaviors and risks, ensuring outputs are interpretable and segment-aware.\n• Applied AI Production: Design and deploy LLM-based solutions for customer growth, treating them as production systems with strong guardrails.\n• Develop and Implement ML Models: Design, implement, and scale machine learning and ML models to analyze customer behavior, optimize marketing strategies, and improve overall engagement with Addi’s platform. This includes leveraging techniques like supervised and unsupervised learning, propensity scoring, and recommendation systems.\n• Manage Data Pipelines and Model Deployment: Collaborate with data engineering teams to design and optimize data pipelines that support the seamless deployment of the models into production. Ensure that models are integrated efficiently and can be scaled, maintained, and monitored for performance in a live environment.\n• Monitor and Evaluate Model Performance: Continuously monitor the performance of deployed models, evaluate their impact on business metrics, and iterate to improve their accuracy, scalability, and overall performance.\n• Collaboration and Knowledge Sharing: Work closely with product managers, marketing teams, and stakeholders to translate data insights into actionable strategies, and actively participate in cross-functional meetings to align ML models with business goals.\n• Innovate and Improve Processes: Continuously innovate by proposing ML models, algorithms, or tools that enhance customer experience, optimize product recommendations, and improve overall marketplace performance.\n• Conduct A/B Testing: Design and execute A/B tests to assess the impact of different offers, product recommendations, and marketing strategies on customer engagement and conversion rates. Analyze the results to understand customer sensitivity to various factors and refine approaches accordingly.\n\nWhat we’re looking for\n• Proven Technical Tenure in Applied AI/ML\n• 3+ years of experience building and deploying AI/ML solutions end-to-end, specifically in high-impact or internal automation roles.\n• Evidence of shipping models with guidance in a collaborative environment, moving beyond local notebooks into production systems.\n• Bachelor’s degree in Physics, Mathematics, Statistics, Economics, or Computer Science, providing the first-principles thinking needed for complex AI debugging.\n• Possesses Experience with LLM-Based Solutions\n• Demonstrated success in building or contributing to systems that utilize modern LLM approaches (e.g., LangChain, LangGraph) to solve real-world tasks.\n• Experience designing knowledge bases or retrieval structures to improve the reliability of AI outputs.\n• Possesses Strong Classic Data Science Foundations\n• Demonstrates a deep understanding of statistics, experimentation (A/B testing, sampling), and classical ML methods to ensure AI isn\'t used where a simpler model suffices.\n• Proven ability to frame business problems into data science solutions, moving from raw data to production-ready iteration.\n• Has Solid Expertise in Deep Learning & Transformers\n• Skilled in neural architectures and optimization, with a working knowledge of attention mechanisms and transformer-based models.\n• Proficiency in modern frameworks like PyTorch, TensorFlow, or Scikit-learn to build and evaluate models from the ground up.\n• Experienced in Modern AI & Agentic Systems\n• Hands-on experience building with LLMs using advanced techniques: prompting, structured outputs, tool use, and guardrails.\n• Familiarity with orchestration patterns (routing, memory, handoffs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) to build reliable, non-hallucinatory agents.\n• Demonstrates Ability to Build Production-Adjacent Code\n• Mastery of Python for creating reproducible pipelines and evaluation tooling.\n• Comfortable working in shared codebases using Git/GitHub, with the ability to build internal automation utilities and connectors/APIs.\n• Track Record of Driving Efficiency & Impact\n• Focused on \"Results over Research\"—prioritizes automation rate, time saved, and throughput improvements over purely academic model performance.\n• Takes accountability for the success of projects, ensuring solutions meet both technical stability and business expectations.\n• Communicates Technical Tradeoffs with Clarity\n• Exceptional ability to explain the limitations and risks of AI to non-technical stakeholders, ensuring expectations are managed and scope is realistic.\n• Proactively collaborates with Engineering to navigate production constraints, such as latency, cost, and reliability.\n\nWhy join us?\n• Work on a problem that truly matters – We are redefining how people shop, pay, and bank in Colombia, breaking down financial barriers and empowering millions. Your work will directly impact customers\' lives by creating more accessible, seamless, and fair financial services.\n• Be part of something big from the ground up – This is your chance to help shape a company, influencing everything from our technology and strategy to our culture and values. You won’t just be an employee—you’ll be an owner\n• Unparalleled growth opportunity – The market we’re tackling is massive, and we’re growing faster than almost any fintech lender at our stage. If you’re looking for a high-impact role in a company that’s scaling fast, this is it.\n• Join a world-class team – Work alongside top-tier talent from around the world, in an environment where excellence, ownership, and collaboration are at the core of everything we do. We care deeply about what we build and how we build it—and we want you to be a part of it.\n• Competitive compensation & meaningful ownership – We believe in rewarding our talent. You’ll receive a generous salary, equity in the company, and benefits that go beyond the basics to support your growth.\n\nHow the hiring process looks like\n\nWe believe in a fast, transparent, and engaging hiring experience that allows both you and us to determine if there\'s a great fit. Here’s what our process looks like:\n• Step 1: People Interview (30 min)\nA conversation with a recruiter or hiring manager to get to know you, your experience, and what you\'re looking for. We’ll also share more about Addi, our culture, and the role.\n• Step 2: Initial Interview (45-60 min)\nA more in-depth conversation with the hiring manager, where we explore your skills, experience, and problem-solving approach. We want to understand how you think and work.\n• Step 3: Take Home Challenge (5-6 days)\nComplete a simple take-home challenge within a 1-week window. With this technical challenge, we want to see your technical expertise solving a real-world problem. We expect that you invest 5 hours or less in developing a working solution.\n• Step 4: Take Home Challenge Review (60 min)\nMeet with a Data Scientists and the Data Science Lead to talk about your take-home exercise submission and any questions you might have.\n• Step 5: Co-Founder Interview\nIf there’s a strong match, you’ll have a final conversation with our Founder to align on expectations, cultural fit and ensure mutual excitement. From there, we’ll move quickly to an offer and discuss next steps.\n\nWe value efficiency and respect for your time, so we aim to complete the process as quickly as possible. Our goal is to make this experience insightful and exciting for you, just as much as it is for us. Regardless of the outcome, we are committed to always providing feedback, ensuring that you walk away with valuable insights from your experience with us.\n\nThis offer from \"Addi\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'addi,models,step,ml,financial,ll,experience,production,build,customer,improve,data,ml models,impact,model,performance,challenge,home,design,ai,expectations,home challenge,shop,colombia,bank'),(249,'jsearch','01eQd0KgAc9MHMDeAAAAAA==','Director, Physical AI','Runway',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/69777a9073a8e8b5e77bbed1-director-physical-ai?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America\n\nWe are building AI to simulate the world through merging art and science.\n\nWe believe that world models are at the frontier of progress in artificial intelligence. Language models alone won’t solve the world’s hardest problems – robotics, disease, scientific discovery. Real progress requires models that experience the world and learn from their mistakes, the same way that humans do. And this kind of trial and error can be massively accelerated when done in simulation, rather than in the real world.\n\nWorld models offer the most clear path to general-purpose simulation, changing how stories are told, how scientific progress is made and how the next frontiers of humanity are reached.\n\nOur team consists of creative, open minded, caring and ambitious people who are determined to change the world. We aspire to continuously build impossible things and our ability to do so relies on building an incredible team. If you are driven to do the same, we\'d love to hear from you.\n\nAbout the role\n• Open to hiring remote across North America— we also have offices in NYC, San Francisco and Seattle.\n\nYou\'ll build Runway\'s Physical AI business from early pilots to production. Your job is to turn research capability into customer outcomes - proving that our world models deliver results that transfer to the real world.\n\nThis is an early-stage role with significant upside. You\'ll work directly with customers, shape the product, and define a new market.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Own the Physical AI business from pilot to production\n• Run forward-deployed programs with robotics and autonomy customers\n• Translate customer needs into product and research priorities\n• Build partnerships that establish Runway as credible in the space\n• Align engineering, design, and research partners around priorities\n• Grow the team as revenue justifies\n\nWhat We\'re Looking For\n• Deep understanding of robotics, autonomy, or simulation\n• Can speak credibly with technical customers\n• Comfortable building from pilot stage\n• Willing to run customer engagements directly\n\nRunway strives to recruit and retain exceptional talent from diverse backgrounds while ensuring pay equity for our team. Our salary ranges are based on competitive market rates for our size, stage and industry, and salary is just one part of the overall compensation package we provide.\n\nThere are many factors that go into salary determinations, including relevant experience, skill level and qualifications assessed during the interview process, and maintaining internal equity with peers on the team. The range shared below is a general expectation for the function as posted, but we are also open to considering candidates who may be more or less experienced than outlined in the job description. In this case, we will communicate any updates in the expected salary range.\n\nLastly, the provided range is the expected salary for candidates in the U.S. Outside of those regions, there may be a change in the range, which again, will be communicated to candidates.\n\nSalary range: $280,000-$350,000\nWorking at Runway\n\nGreat things come from great teams. We’d love to hear from you.\n\nWe’re committed to creating a space where our employees can bring their full selves to work and have equal opportunity to succeed. So regardless of race, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, religion, origin, ability, age, veteran status, if joining this mission speaks to you, we encourage you to apply.\n\nMore about Runway\n• Universal World Simulator\n• GWM-1\n• Gen-4.5\n• General World Models\n• Robotics SDK\n• Conversational Real-time Agents\n• Runway Studios\n\nWe\'re excited to be recognized as a best place to work Crain\'s | InHerSight | BuiltIn NYC | INC\n\nThis offer from \"Runway\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,280000.00,350000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','runway,world models,world,robotics,salary,models,physical ai,simulation,range,general,progress,physical,stage,open,love hear,hear,robotics autonomy,pilot,ai business,team,real,expected,change,love,expected salary'),(250,'jsearch','jxLHimUDPp37WtxKAAAAAA==','AI Strategy Consultant','Hightouch',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697e123e92425699426e8fea-ai-strategy-consultant?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: North America\n\nAbout Hightouch\n\nHightouch is the modern AI platform for marketing and growth teams. Our AI agents reimagine marketing workflows, allowing marketers to create content, plan campaigns, and execute strategies with transformational velocity and performance.\n\nHightouch is a rare company built on the intersection of two fundamental technological shifts: advances in LLMs and agentic AI, and the creation and rapid adoption of cloud data warehouses like Snowflake and Databricks. Building on these tailwinds, we’ve become a leader in AI marketing and partner with industry leaders like Domino’s, Chime, Spotify, Ramp, Whoop, Grammarly, and over 1000 others.\n\nOur team focuses on making a meaningful impact for our customers. We approach challenges with first-principles thinking, move quickly and efficiently, and treat each other with compassion and kindness. We look for team members who are strong communicators, have a growth mindset, and are motivated and persistent in achieving our goals.\n\nAbout The Role\n\nAt its core, the AI Strategy Consultant role centers around driving marketing strategy and transformation in enterprise organizations.\n\nToday, most marketing communications are planned weeks in advance on a calendar based on dates and internal priorities. Each email, push, campaign takes 3-5 people and dozens of steps to create. Our customers come to us looking to transform the way they do marketing: using AI agents to rapidly learn about consumer preferences and deliver highly effective marketing and product experiences to each customer 1:1. Strategy Consultants are responsible for turning that vision into reality.\n\nAs a Strategy Consultant, you’ll work with as a part of a driven and creative team of ML + product engineers, product designers, and other Strategy Consultants to deploy new use cases with the largest customer-facing brands in the world. Your mission is to uncover the most impactful use cases for our customers, understand the insights that are derived from the decision engine, and recommend to our customers new campaigns or adjustments they can to achieve greater outcomes.\n\nYou’ll immerse yourself in our customer’s marketing organization. You’ll partner with customer teams and explore the data, and plunge into the product landscape to help us scale. In this role, the problems you’ll seek will require a curious and analytical approach, a sharp intuition for product, and a strong degree to use insight to ultimately empower our customers to improve decisions.\n\nNo two days are the same, but you can expect to:\n• Own all phases of AI Decisioning use case delivery working alongside Hightouch engineers, customer executives, marketers, and IT stakeholders\n• Run design sessions with customers to decide on and document use case requirements and improvements\n• Champion delivery & project management excellence through development of process playbooks and best practices\n• Proactively identify, escalate and mitigate potential project risks\n• Build relationships with key stakeholders at Hightouch customers\n• Participate in determining the AI Decisioning product strategy\n\nWhat We\'re Looking For\n• Ability to travel 10 - 25% required\n• Experience working with Martech tools/CEMs/CDPs/etc.\n• Strong discovery and interpersonal skills\n• Intellectual curiosity, high ambition, and humility\n• Clear communicator: you are able to express yourself clearly and persuasively, both in writing and speech\n• Experience managing and executing technical projects with a customer-first attitude and a strong sense of empathy\n\nBonus If You Have\n• Experience with programming, scripting or statistical packages (e.g. Python, R, Matlab, SQL)\n\nWe are looking for talented, intellectually curious, and motivated individuals who are interested in tackling the problems above. We focus on impact and potential for growth more than years of experience. The salary range for this position is $170,000-$200,000 (80/20 split variable) USD per year.\nThis offer from \"Hightouch\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 84% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hightouch,strategy,marketing,customers,strategy consultant,consultant,product,customer,ai,use,curious,ai strategy,strategy consultants,decisioning,consultants,use case,marketers,ai decisioning,campaigns,motivated,ai agents,delivery,ll,case,growth'),(251,'jsearch','fO2PZGHW7D5QgTAGAAAAAA==','Video Session Moderator – AI Data Collection (Remote - Americas)','Your Personal AI',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/698db9ed0f33c87a10ea077d-video-session-moderator---ai-data-collection-remote---americas?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: South America, North America, Central America\n\nGuide participants through live video collection sessions for AI training datasets\n\nWe\'re expanding our AI data collection operations across the Americas and need skilled moderators to conduct live video sessions with participants. You\'ll guide people through technical setup, coordinate video calls, and ensure smooth data collection for advanced AI training projects.\n\nWhat You\'ll Do Daily\n\nLive Session Moderation\n• Conduct 4-6 video sessions per day with individual participants (45 minutes each)\n• Guide participants through technical setup including remote desktop access and browser configuration\n• Moderate structured interview sessions where participants answer simple questions on camera\n• Handle real-time troubleshooting for video, audio, and software issues\n\nTechnical Support & Coordination\n• Help participants install and configure Amazon DCV remote desktop software\n• Coordinate Microsoft Teams video calls and screen sharing\n• Walk participants through browser setup and camera/filter configurations\n• Resolve technical issues quickly to maintain session flow\n\nParticipant Management\n• Schedule video sessions with participants across North and South American timezones\n• Send pre-session instructions and collect required information (headshots, IP addresses)\n• Provide friendly, professional guidance to ensure participants feel comfortable\n• Manage session logistics and ensure all data collection requirements are met\n\nQuality Control & Documentation\n• Verify technical requirements are met before sessions begin\n• Ensure video quality and audio clarity meet project standards\n• Document any technical issues or participant feedback\n• Maintain detailed session logs for quality tracking\n\nWork Structure & Compensation\n\nSchedule: Flexible American timezone hours with 4-6 sessions per day\n\nSession Duration: 45 minutes per participation\n\nWork Type: Remote freelance position with potential for long-term engagement\n\nGrowth Opportunities:\n• Potential to lead training for other moderators\n• Opportunity to expand into other data collection projects\n• Flexible scheduling with consistent daily work\n\nYour moderation directly enables the collection of high-quality video datasets that train AI systems for advanced computer vision applications. You\'ll be instrumental in ensuring smooth data collection processes that support breakthrough AI research and development.\n\nReady to help build the datasets powering tomorrow\'s AI technology?\n\nWe\'re looking for patient, technically-minded moderators who can create excellent participant experiences while maintaining high data quality standards.\nThis offer from \"Your Personal AI\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 80% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'participants,collection,session,video,sessions,data collection,sessions participants,moderators,video sessions,setup,participant,guide,quality,data,ai,datasets,technical,ensure,issues,live,minutes,guide participants,moderation,desktop,requirements met'),(252,'jsearch','yfNKWoxGpv6fFrhoAAAAAA==','Remote AI Startup Recruiter','HireLATAM',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697eacbc92425699426f3c82-remote-ai-startup-recruiter?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nHireLatam is a premier recruitment agency that places top Latin American talent in independent contractor roles in US companies. With a proven track record and a commitment to excellence, we\'re your trusted partner in the pursuit of career success. Our extensive network, personalized approach, and supportive guidance ensure that you\'re in the best hands to find your next job opportunity.\n\nJob Title: Remote AI Startup Recruiter (100% Work From Home)\n\nLocation: Remote from Latin America\n\nPosition Type: Full-time\n\nSalary: $2,000 - $4,000 USD/month base (depending on seniority) + uncapped commissions, with top performers earning up to an additional $4,000 USD/month\n\nSchedule: Monday to Friday, flexible but some overlap with Pacific Time is required as well as some hours on evenings or weekends when needed.\n\nJob Overview\n\nThis is a fast-growing AI start-up that is fundamentally rethinking how top talent discovers their next dream job. They partner with leading, venture-capital-backed start-ups (many of which are in the AI space) to help them hire world-class teams.\n\nThey believe the hiring experience should always be talent-first, emphasizing:\n• Easy access to top companies\n• Guidance and coaching throughout the process\n• Real outcomes: focused on offers and hires, not just endless conversations\n\nWhile we are building powerful automation for recruiting, we know the human touch is irreplaceable. That\'s where you come in.\n\nWe are hiring a Recruiter focused on US-based roles, primarily within tech and Go-to-Market (GTM) functions. You will work directly with the founders as part of their early-stage team and help shape how they build and scale their AI-powered recruiting engine.\n\nYou’ll be working remotely from Latin America with flexible hours, but with regular overlap with US Pacific Time, including some evenings and occasional weekend touchpoints to reach candidates.\n\nWhat You’ll Get\n• Direct exposure to fast-growing, VC-backed US start-ups\n• A front-row seat in building an AI start-up and modern recruiting engine\n• High ownership, autonomy, and the ability to shape processes from the ground up\n• Competitive, above-market compensation for the right talent\n\nResponsibilities\n• Communicate with top talent via email, phone, and video calls\n• Understand candidate goals, skills, and constraints and match them with the right roles in our network\n• Manage high-volume candidate pipelines, especially for the junior role\n• Use Clera’s proprietary recruiting software and automation tools to source, engage, and track candidates\n• Run screening calls to assess fit for US-based clients (mainly start-ups, often in tech/AI)\n• Coordinate interviews and case study steps with candidates and clients\n\nQualifications, Skills and Key Competencies\n\nMust-have:\n• Strong English (C1–C2 level): confident leading calls with US candidates\n• 2+ years recruiting for US-based roles (agency, RPO, or in-house)\n• Experience working with ATS/CRM or recruiting systems and comfort learning new tools quickly\n• Ability to work with overlap to US Pacific Time, including some evenings and occasional weekend availability\n• Proven track record in either recruiting or sales-like roles (e.g., managing lead lists, pipelines, doing discovery calls, closing candidates or deals)\n• Reliable home office setup with your own computer and strong internet connection\n\nNice-to-have:\n• Tech recruiting experience (software engineers, data, product, GTM roles for tech companies)\n• Experience supporting US start-ups or VC-backed companies\n• Previous experience in early-stage start-ups or scrappy, fast-changing environments\n\nPersonality & Culture Fit\n\nYou’ll thrive in this role if you are:\n• Proactive and resourceful – you don’t wait to be told what to do, you move things forward\n• A fast learner – especially with new tools, AI, and evolving processes\n• Detail-oriented but fast, comfortable with context-switching and high-volume work\n• A clear, direct communicator who is comfortable pushing for clarity with candidates and clients\n• Excited about building, not just operating a fixed process\n\nOther Details:\n• PTO: ~15–20 days/year (aligned with local norms; can be discussed)\n• Payment: Monthly in USD via international transfer (e.g., Wise or similar)\n\nIf you’re excited about combining human recruiting excellence with cutting-edge AI tools, and you want to work closely with founders and top-tier start-ups, we’d like to meet you.\n\nThis offer from \"HireLATAM\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'recruiting,ups,start ups,start,talent,roles,tech,calls,candidates,pacific time,overlap pacific,pacific,overlap,evenings,fast,companies,ai,recruiter,backed,clients,latin,usd,evenings occasional,remote ai,weekend'),(253,'jsearch','eeU6h_tfx4VlCxskAAAAAA==','Senior Applied Scientist (AI/ML - Pricing)','NIR-YU',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697893fc73a8e8b5e77cb160-senior-applied-scientist-ai-ml---pricing?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nThe Role:\n\nThe Senior Applied Scientist (AI/ML - Pricing) plays a crucial role in the development and deployment of innovative machine learning solutions for retail pricing that includes understanding various customer and operational business constraints and translating complex real-world problems into well-defined mathematical objectives. The ability to research, develop, and implement machine learning models for pricing and price optimization strategy is crucial for the success of this role.\n\nYou should have a robust background in machine learning, optimization, forecasting, and causal inference, particularly within pricing applications or closely related fields. You will be involved in every stage of the ML development pipeline - from data acquisition and ingestion to analysis, prototyping and deployment. You should be able to thrive and succeed in an entrepreneurial setting, working collaboratively in a fast-paced environment with multiple stakeholders.\n\nRoles and Responsibilities:\n• Research and develop machine learning and statistical models and apply optimization to solve complex pricing challenges.\n• Analyze large and complex datasets to derive insights that inform key algorithmic strategies for pricing.\n• Employ state-of-the-art Machine Learning methodologies and frameworks to develop robust and scalable models.\n• Develop and maintain clean, efficient, and scalable code that meets industry standards.\n• Communicate ideas and results effectively, verbally and in writing, to technical and non-technical audiences.\n• Collaborate with key stakeholders in the development of data-driven solutions and deployable products.\n• Contribute to the company\'s intellectual property and technical leadership through patents and publications at top-tier conferences and journals.\n• Influence technical direction and take ownership of key components of systems and solutions, ensuring that they meet the needs of the business.\n• Mentor junior team members to help establish team domain expertise.\n\nMinimum Requirements:\n• PhD or Masters degree in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Statistics, Operation Research or related field\n• 5+ years of industry experience in applied Machine Learning, 3+ years experience in building, deploying, and managing machine learning and deep learning models in production environments at scale\n• Deep understanding of ML best practices (A/B testing, training/serving pipelines, feature engineering etc), algorithms/techniques (gradient boosting, deep neural networks, optimization, regularization), and experiment design\n• Proficiency with scientific libraries in Python (numpy, pandas, polars) and Machine Learning tools and frameworks (Scikit-Learn, Tensorflow, Keras, PyTorch)\n• Strong data engineering skills and experience working with large scale datasets\n• Experience with big data tools (Apache Beam, Apache Kafka, Spark)\n• Experience with cloud technologies AWS, GCP or Azure\n• Fluency in Python, SQL\n\nPreferred Requirements:\n• PhD preferred (CS, ML, AI, Statistics, Operation Research or related field)\n• Background in applying ML techniques to solve real-world business problems in the retail sector, especially pricing.\n• Familiarity with MLOps tools and pipelines.\n• Impact-focused and passionate about delivering high-quality models.\n• Demonstrated leadership experience, with the ability to lead and inspire a team.\n\nThis offer from \"NIR-YU\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 77% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'pricing,machine,machine learning,learning,ml,models,develop,optimization,applied,research,deep,applied scientist,apache,statistics operation,senior applied,ml pricing,operation research,research develop,research related,requirements phd,experience,key,learning models,scientist ai,operation'),(254,'jsearch','eSXEJzWZydP3kTsPAAAAAA==','Senior Software Engineer II (AI Website) LATAM - Remote','Luxury Presence',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/6979ad1a73a8e8b5e77e17ed-senior-software-engineer-ii-ai-website-latam---remote?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nLuxury Presence is the leading growth platform for high-performing real estate agents, teams, and brokerages. The company provides agent-branded websites, advanced marketing tools, and Presence® CRM, the AI relationship engine that transforms an agent’s sphere into a proactive source of new business. More than 17,000 real estate businesses rely on Luxury Presence to elevate their brand, attract clients, and grow their business, including 30% of the Wall Street Journal RealTrends top agents and teams.\n\nAs a Senior Software Engineer II, you will be a key contributor on a cross-functional team, building the foundation of our AI-first platform. You’ll take ownership of major features and services, drive meaningful improvements to our architecture, and collaborate closely with product, design, and AI teams to deliver high-impact outcomes for our customers.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n• Contribute to key architectural decisions and support a large scale re-imagining of our Site Generation and Site Builder Experience\n• Design and build cloud-native APIs, services, and front-end experiences used across our platform to support building Websites\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver AI-powered workflows to Site Building experiences\n• Write clean, testable, scalable code across the stack\nWhat We’re Looking For\n• Passion for building in an AI-augmented environment\n• Familiarity with modern AI tools; experience developing AI-driven solutions is a plus (Claude Code is a must)\n• 5+ years of professional experience in full-stack engineering (leaning backend), ideally having supported a product from MVP to scale in rapid iterations\n• Strong skills in JavaScript/TypeScript, Node.js, and React\n• Experience with scalable microservice architecture (AWS preferred)\n• Solid command of GraphQL, event-driven systems (Kafka/SQS), and distributed databases\n• Track record of delivering high-quality features in rapid prototyping environments and integrating with feedback quickly\n• While you will have Product and Design partners, we value strong communicators and collaborators; able to work with limited product and design guidance, and operate independently in chasing well defined outcomes\n• Customer-first mindset with the ability to empathize with internal and external stakeholder needs\nTech Stack\n• Frontend: React, Tailwind, Apollo, SingleSPA\n• Backend: Node.js, TypeScript (microservices), Python ETLs\n• AI: LangChain, LangFuse, OpenRouter, Mastra, Claude Code\n• Data: PostgreSQL, DynamoDB, Elasticsearch\n• Infrastructure: AWS, Kubernetes, Lambda\n• Messaging: Kafka, SQSJoin us in shaping the future of real estate\n\nThe real estate industry is in the midst of a seismic shift, and the future belongs to those who break new ground. As one of the fastest-growing companies in the proptech and marketing sectors, Luxury Presence challenges the status quo of what technology can do for real estate agents, leaders, and brokerages.\n\nWe’re a team of agile and tenacious innovators working collaboratively to drive the industry forward. Together, we build game-changing products that empower modern real estate entrepreneurs to dominate their markets. From award-winning web design to agile SEO solutions to cutting-edge AI tools, we deliver tech that anticipates market shifts and keeps our clients ahead of their competition.\n\nFounded in 2016 by Stanford Business School alum Malte Kramer, Luxury Presence has grown to a global team ranked on the Inc. 5000 fastest-growing companies list three years in a row. We’re backed by world-class investors, including Bessemer Venture Partners, Toba Capital, and Switch Ventures, and have raised $52.6 million to date.\n\nMore than 17,000 real estate businesses rely on our platform, including 30% of the Wall Street Journal RealTrends top agents and teams. Additionally, many of the industry’s most powerful brokerages — including Compass, Coldwell Banker, and Sotheby’s International Realty — rely on Luxury Presence as a trusted business partner.\n\nEvery year since 2020, Luxury Presence has ranked on BuiltIn’s Best Place to Work lists. HousingWire named our founder and CEO a 2024 Tech Trendsetter, we’ve received several Tech100 Awards, and our lead nurturing tool just scored an Inman Innovation Award for Best AI-Powered Platform.\n\nLuxury Presence is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, or national origin.\nThis offer from \"Luxury Presence\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 81% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'presence,luxury,luxury presence,real estate,estate,ai,real,brokerages,agents teams,site,product design,platform,agents,rely,stack,tech,design,industry,claude code,realtrends,estate agents,ii,journal,journal realtrends,estate businesses'),(255,'jsearch','uITHRWNglUtaRctTAAAAAA==','Spanish (Latin America) Language Data Contributor (Multimodal) – Freelance AI Trainer Project','Invisible Expert Marketplace',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/698b412792425699427ae0b6-spanish-latin-america-language-data-contributor-multimodal---freelance-ai-trainer-project?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nAre you a Spanish (Latin America) language expert eager to shape the future of AI? Large‑scale language models are evolving from clever chatbots into powerful engines of linguistic discovery. With high‑quality training data, tomorrow’s AI can democratize world‑class education, keep pace with cutting‑edge research, and streamline communication for Spanish speakers everywhere. That training data begins with you—we need your expertise to help power the next generation of AI.\n\nWe’re looking for Spanish (Latin America) language specialists who live and breathe phonetics, morphology, syntax, semantics, pragmatics, and sociolinguistics of the Spanish language. You’ll challenge advanced language models on topics like verb conjugation, noun-adjective agreement, subjunctive usage, sentence structure, regional dialects, word order, idiomatic expressions, and cultural nuances—documenting every failure mode so we can harden model reasoning.\n\nOn a typical day, you will converse with the model on language scenarios, verify factual accuracy and logical soundness, capture reproducible error traces, and suggest improvements to our prompt engineering and evaluation metrics.\n\nA degree in Spanish language, linguistics, or a closely related field is ideal; peer‑reviewed publications, teaching experience, or hands‑on linguistic analysis projects signal fit. Clear, metacognitive communication—“showing your work”—is essential.\n\nReady to turn your Spanish language expertise into the knowledge base for tomorrow’s AI? Apply today and start teaching the model that will teach the world.\n\nWe offer a pay range of $6-to- $65 per hour, with the exact rate determined after evaluating your experience, expertise, and geographic location. Final offer amounts may vary from the pay range listed above. As a contractor you’ll supply a secure computer and high‑speed internet; company‑sponsored benefits such as health insurance and PTO do not apply.\n\nData Collection & Participation Notice:\n\nThis engagement involves participation in AI data collection and evaluation. Services include providing audio, video, image, and written inputs—including recordings of your voice and likeness—to support the development and refinement of AI systems.\n\nEligibility for this project requires that you are 18 years or older and agree to the applicable participant and consent agreements.\n\nWhen providing services, submit content featuring only yourself. Avoid the inclusion of third-party or sensitive personal information to maintain project security standards.\n\nJob title: Spanish Language Specialist (Latin America) – AI Trainer\nEmployment type: Contract\nWorkplace type: Remote\nSeniority level: Entry Level\nThis offer from \"Invisible Expert Marketplace\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 79% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'language,spanish,spanish language,america language,spanish latin,latin america,latin,ai,expertise,model,project,training data,ai trainer,linguistic,pay range,teaching,trainer,america,data,tomorrow,providing,tomorrow ai,collection,data collection,language models'),(256,'jsearch','TGq9OBi_TDbqb_MBAAAAAA==','LILT | Latin American Spanish AI Content Experts','Lilt',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697cceb356210e272922be63-lilt-latin-american-spanish-ai-content-experts?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\n\nAre you passionate about AI and skilled at analyzing both text and multimedia content?\n\nWe’re looking for detail-oriented linguists with native speaker fluency in Latin American Spanish to support in AI-training related projects, including tasks such as prompt evaluation, video content understanding, text review & correction, and more.\n\nThis is a remote, freelance opportunity.\n\nWho we\'re looking for\n\n? Native speaker fluency only\n\n? Strong command of English\n? Experience as a reviewer, annotator, or evaluator preferred\n? High attention to detail and ability to thoroughly and accurately categorize content\n? Comfortable working with both textual and audio/video materials\n? Ability to follow detailed guidelines consistently and provide clear feedback\n\nWhat we offer\n\n✅ Free access to our leading-edge NMT technology, with full training and support\n\n✅ Rapid payments via Tipalti — no invoicing needed\n✅ Opportunity to contribute to cutting-edge developments in AI and content understanding\n\nIf you’re interested, please submit an updated version of your resume in English.\n\nAI is changing how the world communicates — and LILT is leading that transformation.\n\nLILT\'s mission is to make the world\'s information available to everyone, no matter the language they speak. Join our global community who thrive on innovation and excellence. Our collective knowledge, uniqueness, and skills deliver multilingual AI and human-verified services to Enterprises, Governments, and AI Developers around the world.\n\nEarn money. Have fun. Advance human knowledge. Work on diverse projects from anywhere, any time you want. Get paid quickly and fairly, and build your professional network in a supportive community—all through a streamlined application process tailored to your expertise.\n\nInformation collected and processed as part of your application process, including any job applications you choose to submit, is subject to LILT\'s Privacy Policy at https://lilt.com/legal/privacy.\n\nAt LILT, we are committed to a fair, inclusive, and transparent hiring process. As part of our recruitment efforts, we may use artificial intelligence (AI) and automated tools to assist in the evaluation of applications, including résumé screening, assessment scoring, and interview analysis. These tools are designed to support human decision-making and help us identify qualified candidates efficiently and objectively. All final hiring decisions are made by people. If you have any concerns, require accommodations, or would like to opt-out of the use of AI in our hiring process, please let us know at recruiting@lilt.com.\n\nLILT is an equal opportunity employer. We extend equal opportunity to all individuals without regard to an individual’s race, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, genetic characteristics, veteran or marital status, pregnancy, or any other classification protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. We are committed to the principles of fair employment and the elimination of all discriminatory practices.\nThis offer from \"Lilt\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 83% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'lilt,content,ai,human,lilt com,american spanish,text,native speaker,application process,content understanding,speaker,speaker fluency,process,native,latin american,ai content,hiring,opportunity,latin,spanish,fluency,privacy,fair,hiring process,american'),(257,'jsearch','cGZajjLFhndKjt46AAAAAA==','RSM - Americas','Vectra AI',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/69908741da7696de2f523ec2-rsm---americas?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: South America, North America, United States, Central America\n\nVectra® is the leader in AI-driven threat detection and response for hybrid and multi-cloud enterprises.\n\nThe Vectra AI Platform delivers integrated signal across public cloud, SaaS, identity, and data center networks in a single platform. Powered by patented Attack Signal Intelligence, it empowers security teams to rapidly prioritize, investigate and respond to the most advanced cyber-attacks. With 35 patents in AI-driven threat detection and the most vendor references in MITRE D3FEND, organizations worldwide rely on the Vectra AI to move at the speed and scale of hybrid attackers. For more information, visit www.vectra.ai.\n\nAbout Vectra.ai\n\nVectra.ai delivers a new class of advanced threat defense that provides real-time detection and analysis of active network intrusions. We continuously analyze internal and internet-facing network traffic to automatically detect and correlate attacker behaviors, prioritize risk, and help customers respond faster as attacks evolve.\n\nThe Opportunity\n\nWe’re continuing to build a high‑performing enterprise sales organization and are hiring an experienced Regional Sales Manager (RSM) to drive strategic growth across enterprise accounts. This role is ideal for a relationship‑driven seller with a proven cybersecurity track record and strong executive‑level engagement skills. You’ll collaborate closely with Sales Engineering and Channel teams to land new customers and expand within existing enterprise accounts.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n• Own and drive growth across a defined set of enterprise accounts.\n• Develop and execute territory and account plans including whitespace analysis, multi‑threading, and executive alignment.\n• Lead business‑outcome‑focused conversations with senior non-technical executives (C‑suite, SVP/VP), leveraging Sales Engineering for technical depth.\n• Manage complex sales cycles ($200K–$1M+), including multi‑stakeholder alignment, evaluations/POCs, and negotiation to close.\n• Partner with channel organizations (resellers/SIs) to extend reach, build pipeline, and accelerate deals.\n• Maintain accurate forecasting and CRM hygiene in Salesforce.\n• Collaborate cross‑functionally with Marketing, Sales Engineering, Customer Success, and Product teams.\n• Represent Vectra with professionalism, urgency, and integrity in a fast‑paced environment.\n\nWhat You’ll Bring\n• 10+ years of enterprise field sales experience, primarily in cybersecurity, with consistent quota attainment.\n• Demonstrated success managing large enterprise customers with strong, activatable executive relationships.\n• Proven track record closing complex, multi‑threaded deals at $200K–$1M+ ACV.\n• Business‑value‑driven selling approach; comfortable leading executive conversations and relying on SEs for technical validation.\n• Strong channel motion experience: co‑selling with VARs/SIs and coordinating partner activities.\n• Evidence of stability and progression in previous roles, with true quota‑carrying ownership.\n• Experience from leading cybersecurity vendors is highly valued.\n\nNice to Have\n• A point of view on building repeatable sales velocity within enterprise accounts.\n• Experience selling into large, complex enterprises across multiple verticals.\n\nOur competitive total rewards package includes cash compensation within the range provided below. Actual pay for this position may vary based on the hired candidate’s location, experience and relevant incumbent pay position. \nVectra Total Rewards\n$182,200—$264,100 USD\n\nVectra provides a comprehensive total rewards package that supports the financial, physical, mental and overall health of our employees and their families. Compensation includes competitive base pay, incentive plan eligibility, and participation in the employee equity plan (stock options). Specific benefits offered varies by location, but commonly include health care insurance, income protection / life insurance, access to retirement savings plans, behavioral & emotional wellness services, generous time away from work, and a comprehensive employee recognition program.\n\nVectra is committed to creating a diverse environment and is proud to be an equal opportunity employer.\n\nWe are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status.\n\nThis offer from \"Vectra AI\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 80% flex score.',NULL,182000.00,264000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','vectra,vectra ai,sales,enterprise,enterprise accounts,accounts,executive,selling,threat,cybersecurity,detection,rewards,channel,total rewards,sales engineering,multi,total,ai,pay,threat detection,1m,attacks,sis,rsm,ai vectra'),(258,'jsearch','ZmbjGgWYqq50uMATAAAAAA==','Clinical Management Administrative Assistant','Omega Medical Services Ltd.',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Clinical-Management-Administrative-Assistant-Job-227448.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','OMEGA MEDICAL SERVICES LTD Position: Clinical Management Administrative Assistant (Ward Clerk) Location: Omega Medical Hospital, Negril, Westmoreland, Jamaica. The Clinical Management Administrative Assistant will communicate effectively and network with doctors, nurses and patients to manage the operations and flow of traffic on the ward. The employee will provide administrative/secretarial support to the Chief Medical Officer, Clinical Director, Medical Administrator, Matron/Nursing Manager, Doctors and Nurses for the Omega Medical Hospital. Key Responsibilities includes but not limited to: Scheduling appointments with patients, doctors and other health care providers Scheduling meetings as per directions from the CMO, and the Head of Medical Departments. Communicate effectively and network with doctors, nurses and patients to manage the flow of traffic on the ward. Assist with the preparation for patients who will be going into surgery by checking supplies and sending reminders to operating team and following up to ensure readiness. Prepare the Medical Release Form for signing. Prepare the discharge summaries for all patients seen in the hospital (Accident and Emergencies, Out Patient and Ward) Make contact with health staff as directed by the CMO or Head of Nursing or designate Assist in maintaining patient database on the information system (HIMS) Guided by instructions, provide assistance in preparing reports on patient care, update medical records with test results and other information on the patient. Ensure all doctors and nurses complete the medical records. Organize, transcribe and prepare the medical reports, lab reports and patient information for easy access by the doctors and nurses Provide directions for visiting protocols to visitors on the ward Prepare relevant forms needed for maintaining the policies and protocols on the wards Monitor calls made to the ward and dispatch as necessary Ensure compliance to health & safety policies and procedures, by all people on the ward Qualifications and Requirements: Associate Degree in Business Administration/ Office Administration/Medical Administration Assisting Training for Certified Patient Account Manager (CPAM) or related Certification in Health Care Administration Strong Computer Skills and working knowledge of Microsoft Office Ability to work in a fast-paced environment, with a commitment to delivering high-quality care. If you are a qualified, dedicated looking for an exciting opportunity to advance your career in healthcare, we would love to hear from you! Shortlisted applicants will be contacted. The location is Negril, Westmoreland.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'medical,ward,patient,doctors,administrative,administration,nurses,patients,doctors nurses,omega,management,management administrative,administrative assistant,omega medical,clinical management,reports,health,clinical,prepare,care,assistant,provide,information,ensure,hospital'),(259,'jsearch','tI6hW5_KPbc42UlqAAAAAA==','Medical Assistant II - Ortho Spine','Mass General Brigham',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.recruit.net/job/medical-assistant-ortho-spine-jobs/499CE404B2762905?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Site: The Brigham and Women\'s Hospital, Inc.\n\nMass General Brigham relies on a wide range of professionals, including doctors, nurses, business people, tech experts, researchers, and systems analysts to advance our mission. As a not-for-profit, we support patient care, research, teaching, and community service, striving to provide exceptional care. We believe that high-performing teams drive groundbreaking medical discoveries and invite all applicants to join us and experience what it means to be part of Mass General Brigham.\n\nJob Summary\nSummary\nThe role supports healthcare teams by assisting with both clinical and non-clinical patient services under the direction of healthcare providers. Key responsibilities include taking vital signs, documenting patient information, scheduling appointments, and managing patient flow. This role involves direct interaction with patients to ensure their comfort and address concerns, as well as collaboration with physicians, nurse practitioners, and nursing staff to facilitate efficient care.\nDoes this position require Patient Care? Yes\nEssential Functions\n-Assists junior Medical Assistants with day-to-day questions and responsibilities and helps facilitate their learning by participating in onboarding training.\n-Show patients to examination rooms, prepare necessary equipment for healthcare providers, and interview patients to obtain medical information, measure their vital signs, weight, and height, and record information in the patient\'s medical record.\n-Explain treatment procedures, medications, diets, and physician instructions to patients, ordering and organizing educational materials to reinforce patient education.\n-Perform general office duties, such as answering phones, taking dictation, and completing insurance forms, while acting as a liaison with other departments and advocating for patients with a positive customer service approach.\n-Collect blood, tissue, or other laboratory specimens, log them, and prepare them for testing; perform phlebotomy if competence is demonstrated.\n-Maintains inventory of immunizations and check expiration dates.\n-Provides immunizations (as applicable) which requires certification or 3 years of experience administering a vaccine and supervision of a provider.\n-Responsible for improving appropriate departmental quality initiatives, such as two patient identifiers and hand hygiene.\n\nQualifications\nEducationHigh School Diploma or Equivalent required or Associate\'s Degree Medical Assisting preferredCan this role accept experience in lieu of a degree?NoLicenses and CredentialsBasic Life Support [BLS Certification] - Data Conversion - Various Issuers preferred Certified Medical Assistant [National Certification] - Data Conversion - Various Issuers preferredExperienceDirect MA experience or medical field work 1-2 years requiredKnowledge, Skills and Abilities- Strong interpersonal and communication skills are essential for success in this position. - Ability to prioritize tasks in complex and busy environments. - Accuracy and attention to detail. - Comply with all local, state, and federal privacy and confidentiality rules and regulations. - Ability to take vital signs and manual blood pressure, as well as collect blood samples and other specimens. - Comprehensive knowledge of medical terminology, procedures, and protocols. - Proficiency in electronic health record (EHR) systems and medical office software. - Using logic and reasoning to identify the strengths and weaknesses of alternative solutions, conclusions, or approaches to problems. - Managing one\'s own time and the time of others.\n\nAdditional Job Details (if applicable)\nPhysical Requirements\n• Standing Frequently (34-66%)\n• Walking Frequently (34-66%)\n• Sitting Occasionally (3-33%)\n• Lifting Frequently (34-66%) 35lbs+ (w/assisted device)\n• Carrying Frequently (34-66%) 20lbs - 35lbs\n• Pushing Occasionally (3-33%)\n• Pulling Occasionally (3-33%)\n• Climbing Rarely (Less than 2%)\n• Balancing Frequently (34-66%)\n• Stooping Occasionally (3-33%)\n• Kneeling Occasionally (3-33%)\n• Crouching Occasionally (3-33%)\n• Crawling Rarely (Less than 2%)\n• Reaching Frequently (34-66%)\n• Gross Manipulation (Handling) Frequently (34-66%)\n• Fine Manipulation (Fingering) Frequently (34-66%)\n• Feeling Constantly (67-100%)\n• Foot Use Rarely (Less than 2%)\n• Vision - Far Constantly (67-100%)\n• Vision - Near Constantly (67-100%)\n• Talking Constantly (67-100%)\n• Hearing Constantly (67-100%)\n\nRemote Type\nOnsite\n\nWork Location\n1133 Centre Street\n\nScheduled Weekly Hours\n40\n\nEmployee Type\nRegular\n\nWork Shift\nDay (United States of America)\n\nPay Range\n$17.71 - $24.94/Hourly\n\nGrade\n3\n\nAt Mass General Brigham, we believe in recognizing and rewarding the unique value each team member brings to our organization. Our approach to determining base pay is comprehensive, and any offer extended will take into account your skills, relevant experience if applicable, education, certifications and other essential factors. The base pay information provided offers an estimate based on the minimum job qualifications; however, it does not encompass all elements contributing to your total compensation package. In addition to competitive base pay, we offer comprehensive benefits, career advancement opportunities, differentials, premiums and bonuses as applicable and recognition programs designed to celebrate your contributions and support your professional growth. We invite you to apply, and our Talent Acquisition team will provide an overview of your potential compensation and benefits package.\n\nEEO Statement:\n2200 The Brigham and Women\'s Hospital, Inc. is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religious creed, national origin, sex, age, gender identity, disability, sexual orientation, military service, genetic information, and/or other status protected under law. We will ensure that all individuals with a disability are provided a reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. To ensure reasonable accommodation for individuals protected by Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Vietnam Veteran’s Readjustment Act of 1974, and Title I of the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, applicants who require accommodation in the job application process may contact Human Resources at (857)-282-7642.\n\nMass General Brigham Competency Framework\n\nAt Mass General Brigham, our competency framework defines what effective leadership “looks like” by specifying which behaviors are most critical for successful performance at each job level. The framework is comprised of ten competencies (half People-Focused, half Performance-Focused) and are defined by observable and measurable skills and behaviors that contribute to workplace effectiveness and career success. These competencies are used to evaluate performance, make hiring decisions, identify development needs, mobilize employees across our system, and establish a strong talent pipeline.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'34,66,34 66,frequently,frequently 34,medical,job,brigham,33,occasionally,occasionally 33,general,patient,general brigham,67 100,67,100,mass,mass general,experience,constantly,constantly 67,applicable,essential,pay'),(265,'jsearch','SgO_UOvK7Nd7H7ZtAAAAAA==','Public Health Officer – Awareness Campaign, Contract','Food For The Poor Jamaica','Spanish Town','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/public-health-officer-awareness-campaign-contract/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nFood For The Poor (FFTP) is an interdenominational Christian relief and development organization that has been serving the poor in Jamaica and across the Caribbean and Latin America for decades. Our mission is to transform the lives of the materially poor by providing food, housing, healthcare, education, and various sustainable development programs. In Jamaica, FFTP plays a critical role in addressing poverty, disaster relief, and improving community health outcomes. We are committed to fostering self-sufficiency and empowering communities through sustainable initiatives. Joining our team means becoming part of a passionate group dedicated to making a tangible difference in the lives of vulnerable populations.\n\nJob Description\n\nFood For The Poor Jamaica is seeking a dedicated and proactive Public Health Officer to lead and execute critical awareness campaigns on a contract basis in Spanish Town, Saint Catherine Parish. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced public health professional to directly impact community well-being by designing, implementing, and evaluating health education programs and campaigns. The Public Health Officer will be instrumental in promoting positive health behaviours, disseminating vital health information, and mobilizing community participation in public health initiatives targeting various health challenges prevalent in the region. This role requires strong communication skills, a deep understanding of public health principles, and a commitment to serving underserved communities. The successful candidate will work closely with community leaders, local health authorities, and FFTP\'s program teams to ensure the effective reach and impact of our health awareness efforts. Your work will directly contribute to empowering individuals with knowledge and resources to lead healthier lives, fostering a healthier and more resilient Spanish Town.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, plan, and implement comprehensive public health awareness campaigns tailored to the specific needs of communities in Spanish Town and surrounding areas.\n• Develop engaging and culturally appropriate health education materials, including flyers, posters, presentations, and digital content.\n• Conduct community outreach, workshops, and educational sessions on various public health topics (e.g., sanitation, nutrition, chronic disease prevention, maternal and child health, hygiene).\n• Collaborate with local health agencies, community groups, schools, and volunteers to expand the reach and effectiveness of campaigns.\n• Monitor and evaluate the effectiveness of awareness campaigns, collecting data, and preparing detailed reports on progress, challenges, and outcomes.\n• Identify community health needs and gaps in knowledge through needs assessments and community engagement.\n• Manage project timelines, resources, and budgets for assigned campaigns, ensuring efficient and impactful execution.\n• Act as a key liaison between Food For The Poor Jamaica and local community stakeholders on public health matters.\n• Provide regular updates and reports to the Program Manager on campaign activities and community impact.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including public speaking and presentation abilities.\n• Proven experience in designing and implementing public health awareness campaigns or health education programs.\n• Strong project management and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines.\n• Demonstrated ability to work effectively with diverse community groups, showing cultural sensitivity and empathy.\n• Proficiency in data collection, analysis, and report writing.\n• Competency in using standard office software (Microsoft Office Suite: Word, Excel, PowerPoint).\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team.\n• Valid driver\'s license and access to reliable transportation for community travel.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s degree in Public Health, Community Health, Health Promotion, or a related field.\n• Previous experience working with non-profit organizations or NGOs in a community development or public health context.\n• Familiarity with the specific health challenges and cultural nuances of communities in Saint Catherine Parish, Jamaica.\n• Experience in grant writing or fundraising for public health initiatives.\n• Knowledge of local health policies and structures in Jamaica.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Opportunity to make a significant, tangible impact on community health in Jamaica.\n• Engage in meaningful work that directly addresses social determinants of health.\n• Collaborative and supportive work environment within a reputable international NGO.\n• Professional development opportunities and exposure to diverse public health challenges.\n• Reimbursement for approved work-related travel expenses within the campaign area.\n• Access to a network of dedicated professionals and community leaders.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to visit the Food For The Poor Jamaica careers page to submit their application. Please ensure your resume and cover letter clearly outline your experience in public health, community engagement, and campaign management, specifically addressing how your skills align with the requirements for this Public Health Officer role. We encourage you to highlight any previous work within Jamaican communities. Click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'health,community,public,public health,jamaica,work,campaigns,awareness,poor,communities,skills,food,education,officer,local,impact,food poor,experience,community health,development,poor jamaica,challenges,campaign,awareness campaigns,health officer'),(269,'jsearch','T3yVPdLI54RLGFhtAAAAAA==','Environmental Officer – Consultancy Firm (Experienced)','Environmental Solutions Ltd.','Spanish Town','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/environmental-officer-consultancy-firm-experienced/','About Company\n\nEnvironmental Solutions Ltd. (ESL) is a premier environmental consulting firm in Jamaica, dedicated to promoting sustainable development through expert environmental management. For over two decades, ESL has been at the forefront of providing comprehensive environmental services across various sectors, including infrastructure, energy, tourism, and agriculture. Our commitment to scientific rigor, regulatory compliance, and innovative solutions has earned us a reputation as a trusted partner for both public and private sector clients. We believe in fostering a culture of excellence, continuous learning, and environmental stewardship, making a tangible difference in Jamaica\'s ecological landscape and beyond. Joining ESL means becoming part of a team that is passionate about safeguarding natural resources, driving environmental innovation, and contributing to a greener, more sustainable future for Jamaica.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you an experienced environmental professional passionate about sustainable development and ready to make a significant impact? Environmental Solutions Ltd. (ESL), a leader in environmental consulting in Jamaica, is seeking a highly skilled and motivated Environmental Officer to join our dynamic team in Spanish Town, St. Catherine. This is a unique opportunity for an experienced individual to contribute to a diverse portfolio of projects, ensuring environmental compliance, promoting best practices, and driving sustainable outcomes across various industries. We are looking for an individual who can not only manage complex environmental projects but also serve as a mentor and a critical resource within our growing team.\n\nAs an Environmental Officer at ESL, you will play a pivotal role in the planning, execution, and oversight of environmental projects from inception to completion. Your responsibilities will span from conducting comprehensive Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs) and Environmental Audits (EAs) to developing and implementing robust Environmental Management Systems (EMS). You will be instrumental in ensuring that our clients’ projects adhere strictly to local and international environmental regulations, providing expert guidance on mitigation strategies, monitoring protocols, and adaptive management plans. This role demands a proactive individual with a strong understanding of environmental legislation, excellent analytical skills, and the proven ability to manage multiple projects concurrently while maintaining high standards of quality and accuracy.\n\nYour day-to-day tasks will include conducting thorough field investigations, collecting and analyzing environmental data using advanced tools and methodologies, preparing detailed technical reports, and presenting findings lucidly to clients, regulatory bodies, and internal stakeholders. Collaboration is key; you will work closely with multidisciplinary teams, engage proactively with clients, interact with government agencies, and consult with local communities and other stakeholders to achieve project objectives and foster environmental excellence. If you thrive in a challenging yet rewarding environment, are committed to safeguarding Jamaica’s natural heritage, and are adept at facilitating responsible development through sound environmental practices, we encourage you to apply and help us shape a sustainable future.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Lead and manage environmental projects, including Environmental Impact Assessments (EIAs), Environmental Audits (EAs), and Environmental Management Plans (EMPs).\n• Conduct field investigations, site assessments, and environmental monitoring programs.\n• Collect, analyze, and interpret environmental data, utilizing appropriate scientific methods and software.\n• Prepare comprehensive technical reports, proposals, and presentations for clients and regulatory agencies.\n• Ensure projects comply with Jamaican environmental laws, regulations (e.g., NRCA Act, NEPA permits), and international standards.\n• Provide expert environmental advice and recommendations to clients on sustainable practices, risk management, and mitigation strategies.\n• Liaise effectively with government agencies, stakeholders, and community groups.\n• Contribute to the development and implementation of Environmental Management Systems (EMS).\n• Stay abreast of emerging environmental trends, technologies, and regulatory changes.\n• Mentor junior staff and contribute to team knowledge sharing and capacity building.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor’s degree in Environmental Science, Environmental Engineering, Natural Resource Management, or a related field.\n• Minimum of 3 years of progressive experience in environmental consulting or a related field.\n• Demonstrated experience in conducting EIAs, EAs, and EMPs.\n• Strong understanding of Jamaican environmental legislation and regulatory frameworks.\n• Proficiency in data collection, analysis, and report writing.\n• Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team.\n• Valid driver’s license and willingness to travel for field work.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master’s degree in a relevant environmental discipline.\n• Professional certification (e.g., Certified Environmental Professional).\n• Experience with GIS software (e.g., ArcGIS) for mapping and spatial analysis.\n• Project management certification (e.g., PMP).\n• Familiarity with international environmental standards (e.g., IFC Performance Standards, World Bank EHS Guidelines).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• Health and dental insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and training.\n• Dynamic and collaborative work environment.\n• Contribution to impactful environmental projects in Jamaica.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their comprehensive resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and qualifications. Please click on the link below to apply for the job.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'environmental,projects,regulatory,esl,management,jamaica,clients,sustainable,environmental projects,field,team,development,environmental management,experience,standards,comprehensive,assessments,environmental consulting,eias,expert,consulting,eas,professional,work,natural'),(270,'jsearch','SuN4lPRK4o3LPMsaAAAAAA==','Registered Nurse, Total Rewards Department, Human Resources Division','Bank of Jamaica',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Registered-Nurse-Total-Rewards-Department-Job-226980.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Applications are invited from suitably qualified professionals to resource the position of Registered Nurse , Human Resources Division. The successful candidate will be responsible for: Assisting the Bank\'s Nurse with operations of the Clinic by: maintaining relevant equipment and instruments in a sterile and socially clean state. sourcing and ordering pharmaceutical items for the Clinic stock and the Sports Club and ensuring that these items are available at all times. maintaining records of all cases treated at the Clinic and preparing reports containing analysis of health statistics. preparing dressings and ensuring that they are kept sterilized. managing the inventory of the Clinic, ensuring supplies are within re-order levels at all times. Assisting with medical problems occurring on the Bank\'s premises by: providing general nursing care/first aid to staff, pensioners and visitors. administering the necessary nursing care until the patient either recuperates or is transferred to a medical center. arranging for transportation to hospital or home for sick/injured personnel. drafting reports to Bank’s Nurse, on the sickness/injury of the person. following–up biometric screening of staff members by conducting weekly blood sugar and blood cholesterol checks. performing blood pressure checks where necessary. Assisting with the nursing care of any official visitor to the Bank who becomes ill or injured either on or off the Bank’s premises. Checking Food Handler’s permits for Staff Dining personnel, porters and Recreational Facility personnel. Providing off-site inspection of the Bank’s caterers and reporting on findings. Providing health assessments of applicants for the use of the Bank’s gymnasium. Drafting monthly reports on the operations of the Clinic and inventory management. Drafting monthly expenditure report and preparing annual budget for the Clinic. Performing any other duties that may be assigned from time to time. QUALIFICATION AND EXPERIENCE A registered nurse from an institution recognized by the General Nursing Council of Jamaica. A registered midwife. The incumbent should possess post-nursing qualifications such as BSc. or Certificate in Public Health and/or Industrial Health and Safety. The job holder should also have a minimum of five (5) years experience as a general nurse. SPECIFIC KNOWLEDGE AND SKILLS REQUIRED Sound knowledge of industrial health care. Practical knowledge in techniques and practices required for treatment of fractures, communicable diseases, drug addiction, respiratory ailments and other common illnesses. A sound understanding of the Bank’s structure, system and procedures. A broad knowledge of the Bank’s staff demographical composition. A good working knowledge of the core workplace laws particularly those relating to Occupational Safety and Health. Excellent interpersonal communication skills. SPECIFIC CONDITIONS ASSOCIATED WITH THE JOB The work is carried out in a modern office environment. A fair amount of walking is required as the incumbent will be required to make regular visit to areas around the Bank. Interested persons who meet the above requirements should complete the application form with cover letter and full resume no later than Wednesday, 25 February 2026 .',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'bank,clinic,preparing,reports,drafting,health,nurse,assisting,personnel,general,blood,knowledge,nursing,drafting monthly,operations clinic,industrial,industrial health,human,human resources,bank nurse,bank premises,injured,sound,premises,monthly'),(271,'jsearch','tGmdTujMLCGma5LyAAAAAA==','nurse – hospital ward (experienced)','Career.zycto','Buff Bay','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/nurse-hospital-ward-experienced/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nAs a dedicated healthcare professional, you understand the critical role exceptional patient care plays. Career.zycto connects passionate nurses with leading medical institutions across Jamaica, ensuring you find a role where your skills are valued, and your impact is tangible. We partner with facilities prioritizing professional growth and a supportive environment, ideal for an experienced hospital ward nurse. Join a network that believes in empowering healthcare heroes, offering opportunities to shape the future of community wellness. Discover how your expertise can truly thrive with our personalized placement services, fostering a fulfilling and dynamic career.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you an experienced and compassionate Registered Nurse seeking to make a profound impact within a dynamic hospital setting? Career.zycto is proud to partner with a leading healthcare facility in Buff Bay, Portland, to recruit a dedicated and skilled Ward Nurse. This pivotal role offers a unique opportunity to apply your expertise in a supportive environment where patient well-being is paramount and professional growth is encouraged.\n\nAs an Experienced Ward Nurse, you will be at the forefront of delivering exceptional, holistic patient care. You will manage a diverse caseload, utilizing your clinical judgment and critical thinking to assess, plan, implement, and evaluate nursing interventions. This role requires a nurse who thrives in a collaborative team setting, capable of mentoring junior staff while maintaining the highest standards of care. Our partner hospital is committed to providing a safe and healing environment for its community, and your contribution will be vital in upholding this mission.\n\nThe successful candidate will demonstrate proficiency in acute care management, wound care, medication administration, and electronic health record documentation. You will serve as a primary advocate for patients, communicating effectively with families, physicians, and multidisciplinary teams to ensure comprehensive care plans are executed seamlessly. This position demands resilience, empathy, and a steadfast commitment to continuous learning and professional development. We are looking for a leader in patient care, someone who can anticipate needs, respond proactively to emergencies, and contribute positively to a vibrant healthcare culture.\n\nJoin a team that values your experience and provides avenues for skill enhancement and career advancement. This is more than just a job; it’s an opportunity to solidify your legacy in healthcare, positively impacting lives daily in the beautiful parish of Portland. If you are ready to bring your seasoned nursing skills to a community that genuinely needs and appreciates them, we encourage you to apply. We are eager to welcome a nurse who is not only clinically exceptional but also deeply committed to patient advocacy and team collaboration.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Provide comprehensive and compassionate nursing care to assigned patients on the hospital ward.\n• Conduct thorough patient assessments, develop individualized care plans, and evaluate patient responses to interventions.\n• Administer medications safely and accurately, monitor for adverse reactions, and educate patients/families on drug regimens.\n• Perform wound care, IV insertion, catheterization, and other clinical procedures with precision and adherence to protocols.\n• Maintain accurate and timely electronic health records, ensuring all patient data is meticulously documented.\n• Collaborate effectively with physicians, therapists, and other healthcare professionals to optimize patient outcomes.\n• Respond promptly and effectively to medical emergencies, demonstrating strong critical thinking and decisive action.\n• Educate patients and their families on health conditions, treatment plans, and discharge instructions.\n• Supervise and mentor junior nursing staff, fostering a culture of continuous learning and excellence.\n• Adhere strictly to all hospital policies, procedures, and national healthcare regulations.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Registered Nurse (RN) license in Jamaica (or eligibility for licensure).\n• Minimum of 2 years of post-registration experience in a hospital ward setting (medical-surgical, acute care, or similar).\n• Demonstrated proficiency in clinical assessment, critical care interventions, and emergency response.\n• Strong knowledge of medication administration, wound care management, and infection control protocols.\n• Excellent communication, interpersonal, and team collaboration skills.\n• Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced and demanding environment.\n• Proficiency in electronic health record (EHR) systems.\n• CPR and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN).\n• Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS) certification.\n• Experience with mentorship or preceptorship of new nursing staff.\n• Specialized training or certification in a relevant area (e.g., palliative care, geriatric nursing).\n• Fluency in an additional language relevant to the local community.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and benefits package.\n• Opportunities for continuous professional development and training.\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Paid time off and holiday benefits.\n• Health and wellness programs.\n• Employee assistance program.\n• Career advancement opportunities within the network.\n• Contribution to a vital community healthcare mission.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to advance your nursing career in Buff Bay, Portland? We invite qualified candidates to submit their application by clicking the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience and qualifications. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to a team dedicated to excellence in patient care.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'care,patient,healthcare,nursing,nurse,career,ward,portland,hospital,partner,team,community,professional,health,patients,patient care,critical,hospital ward,wound care,ward nurse,wound,environment,buff,zycto,buff bay'),(272,'jsearch','CedxWEE0GuwhovtoAAAAAA==','Experienced Registered Nurse – Hospital Ward','Spanish Town Hospital','Spanish Town','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/experienced-registered-nurse-hospital-ward/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nSpanish Town Hospital stands as a cornerstone of healthcare in St. Catherine Parish, Jamaica, serving a diverse and vibrant community with unwavering dedication. As a leading public health institution in the region, we are committed to providing comprehensive, compassionate, and high-quality medical services to thousands of patients annually. Our facility features a wide range of specialized departments, including emergency services, surgical units, pediatric care, internal medicine, and robust inpatient wards. We pride ourselves on a patient-centered approach, fostering an environment where healing and recovery are paramount. Our team of skilled professionals, from physicians and nurses to administrative and support staff, works collaboratively to ensure that every individual receives the best possible care. At Spanish Town Hospital, we believe in continuous improvement, embracing modern medical practices and investing in the professional development of our staff, thereby contributing significantly to the health and well-being of the Jamaican populace. Joining us means becoming part of a legacy of care and making a tangible difference in the lives of many within the community we serve.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you an experienced, compassionate, and highly skilled Registered Nurse eager to make a profound impact in a dynamic hospital environment? Spanish Town Hospital invites dedicated professionals to join our esteemed nursing team in our busy hospital wards. This pivotal role is perfect for a nurse who thrives in a fast-paced setting, possesses exceptional clinical acumen, and is committed to delivering outstanding patient care. As an Experienced Registered Nurse on our hospital ward, you will be at the forefront of patient recovery and well-being. Your responsibilities will encompass a broad spectrum of nursing duties, from conducting comprehensive patient assessments and administering medications with precision, to developing and implementing individualized care plans. You will serve as a vital link between patients, their families, and the multidisciplinary healthcare team, ensuring clear communication and coordinated care. This role demands a strong ability to manage complex cases, respond effectively to emergencies, and provide empathetic support to patients and their loved ones during challenging times. We are looking for a proactive individual who embraces continuous learning, demonstrates strong leadership potential, and contributes positively to a collaborative team culture. Your expertise will be instrumental in maintaining the highest standards of clinical excellence and patient safety within our wards. If you are passionate about healthcare, possess a proven track record in acute care, and are ready to advance your career in a supportive and impactful setting, we encourage you to apply. This is an unparalleled opportunity to grow professionally while contributing significantly to the health of our community.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Conduct comprehensive patient assessments, including physical, psychological, and social aspects.\n• Administer medications and treatments as prescribed by physicians, accurately and safely.\n• Develop, implement, and evaluate individualized patient care plans.\n• Monitor and record vital signs, symptoms, and medical information, reporting changes to physicians.\n• Provide wound care, perform minor medical procedures, and assist with examinations.\n• Educate patients and their families on health conditions, medications, and self-care techniques.\n• Collaborate effectively with interdisciplinary healthcare teams (doctors, therapists, etc.).\n• Maintain accurate and confidential patient records in accordance with hospital policies and regulations.\n• Respond promptly and effectively to medical emergencies, providing life support where necessary.\n• Ensure a safe, clean, and therapeutic environment for all patients.\n• Adhere strictly to infection control protocols and safety standards.\n• Act as a patient advocate, ensuring patient rights and preferences are respected.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Registered Nurse (RN) license in Jamaica (or eligibility for licensure)\n• Minimum of 2 years of experience in an acute care hospital ward setting\n• Proficiency in clinical assessment, diagnosis, and treatment planning\n• Strong knowledge of pharmacology and medication administration\n• Excellent critical thinking and problem-solving abilities\n• Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills\n• Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, high-pressure environment\n• Proficiency in electronic health record (EHR) systems\n• Demonstrated empathy, compassion, and patient-centered care approach\n• Basic Life Support (BLS) certification\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN)\n• Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS) certification\n• Pediatric Advanced Life Support (PALS) certification\n• Experience in specialized wards (e.g., ICU, ER, Medical-Surgical)\n• Leadership or charge nurse experience\n• Fluency in additional languages (e.g., Spanish)\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance\n• Pension plan with employer contributions\n• Paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, and holidays\n• Opportunities for continuing education and professional development\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment\n• Employee wellness programs\n• Access to modern medical facilities and technology\n• Subsidized meals\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo seize this exciting opportunity and join our dedicated team at Spanish Town Hospital, please click on the application link below. Ensure your resume and cover letter highlight your relevant experience and qualifications for this Experienced Registered Nurse position. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to our family of healthcare professionals.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'care,spanish,patient,hospital,town hospital,town,spanish town,wards,medical,nurse,health,support,patients,experienced registered,life support,team,registered nurse,healthcare,comprehensive,life,environment,registered,contributing significantly,pediatric,modern medical'),(273,'jsearch','exK2GWIQA8E3RtCMAAAAAA==','Nurse Assistant – Hospital Ward (Training Provided)','May Pen General Hospital','May Pen','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/nurse-assistant-hospital-ward-training-provided/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nMay Pen General Hospital stands as a cornerstone of healthcare in Clarendon Parish, Jamaica. As a public institution operating under the Southern Regional Health Authority (SRHA), we are deeply committed to providing comprehensive, compassionate, and high-quality medical services to our vibrant community. Our state-of-the-art facility encompasses various specialized wards, a fully equipped emergency department, and a range of outpatient clinics, all designed to cater to a diverse patient population from Denbigh, May Pen, and surrounding areas. We pride ourselves on cultivating a robust culture of continuous learning, professional development, and collaborative teamwork, fostering an environment where both patients and staff feel profoundly supported and genuinely valued. Joining May Pen General Hospital means becoming an integral part of a dedicated team that is passionate about improving health outcomes and making a tangible, positive difference in the lives of individuals and families across the region.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you passionate about patient care and eager to embark on a truly rewarding career in the vital healthcare sector? May Pen General Hospital is actively seeking enthusiastic, empathetic, and dedicated individuals to join our compassionate team as Nurse Assistants in our bustling hospital wards. This is an exceptional and unique opportunity for those who are new to healthcare or looking to transition into a supportive patient care role, as comprehensive on-the-job training will be meticulously provided to equip you with all the necessary foundational skills, practical knowledge, and confidence to excel in this crucial position.\n\nAs a Nurse Assistant, you will play an absolutely crucial role in the daily operations of our wards, directly contributing to the comfort, safety, and overall well-being of our patients. You will work closely and collaboratively under the direct supervision of experienced registered nurses and other seasoned healthcare professionals, diligently assisting with a wide range of essential tasks that ensure our patients receive the highest standard of care. Your contributions will be invaluable in maintaining a meticulously clean, thoroughly organized, and therapeutic environment, thereby allowing our skilled nursing staff to focus more intently on complex medical interventions and critical care. This position offers an unparalleled chance to gain invaluable hands-on experience in a dynamic and fast-paced hospital setting, learn directly from expert professionals, and grow significantly within a vital public health institution. We are specifically looking for individuals who are inherently empathetic, exceptionally reliable, possess an unwavering strong work ethic, and are genuinely eager to learn and continuously develop their skills within a supportive and collaborative team environment. If you are ready to begin a meaningful and impactful career where you can genuinely touch and improve lives every single day, we wholeheartedly encourage you to apply and become a vital and cherished part of our healthcare family.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist patients with essential daily living activities, including bathing, dressing, grooming, and safe mobility.\n• Support nurses by accurately taking, recording, and monitoring vital signs (temperature, pulse, respiration, blood pressure).\n• Provide assistance with patient feeding, ensuring all dietary needs and restrictions are precisely met.\n• Maintain a consistently clean, organized, and hygienic patient environment, including tidying rooms and changing bed linens.\n• Assist with safe patient transportation within the hospital using appropriate equipment like wheelchairs or stretchers.\n• Observe, monitor, and promptly report any significant changes in patient condition, behavior, or complaints to the nursing staff.\n• Respond promptly and compassionately to patient call lights and requests.\n• Document all care activities accurately and thoroughly in patient records as per established hospital protocols.\n• Ensure medical supplies are adequately stocked and readily accessible in patient rooms and throughout ward areas.\n• Adhere strictly to all infection control policies, patient safety procedures, and hospital regulations.\n\nRequired Skills\n• High school diploma or equivalent (CXC/CSEC passes preferred, especially in English and a science subject).\n• Excellent verbal and written communication and strong interpersonal skills.\n• Demonstrated ability to follow instructions accurately and work effectively as part of a multidisciplinary team.\n• A genuinely compassionate, patient-centered, and empathetic approach to care.\n• Good physical stamina and the ability to perform tasks requiring prolonged standing, walking, lifting, and bending.\n• Strong willingness to learn new skills and adapt to a dynamic, fast-paced clinical environment.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Previous experience in a customer service role or any environment requiring direct interaction and support for the public.\n• Basic computer literacy for electronic health record documentation and general administrative tasks.\n• Certification in First Aid and Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation (CPR) – training can be provided post-hire if not currently possessed.\n• Understanding of basic medical terminology.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Comprehensive on-the-job training and a structured mentorship program designed for professional growth.\n• Significant opportunities for professional development and clear pathways for career advancement within the public health sector.\n• Access to a highly supportive, collaborative, and team-oriented work environment.\n• The profound satisfaction of contributing to a vital community service and positively impacting lives.\n• Paid time off and sick leave benefits in accordance with government regulations (after successful probationary period).\n• Access to health and pension benefits as per standard government employment guidelines.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested and qualified candidates are warmly invited to click on the application link below to submit their detailed applications. Please ensure your resume is thoroughly up-to-date and clearly highlights any relevant experience, qualifications, or personal attributes that align with this role. We eagerly look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to the dedicated May Pen General Hospital team.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'patient,pen,hospital,general,general hospital,pen general,genuinely,thoroughly,learn,provided,tasks,environment,team,health,vital,care,wards,individuals,training,healthcare,patients,public,empathetic,skills,rooms'),(274,'jsearch','rqfS_NsfSJ64s0PxAAAAAA==','Experienced Ward Nurse','St. Ann\'s Bay Regional Hospital',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/experienced-ward-nurse/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nSt. Ann\'s Bay Regional Hospital is a cornerstone of healthcare in Jamaica\'s north-central region, serving as a comprehensive medical facility dedicated to providing high-quality, compassionate care to the residents of St. Ann and surrounding parishes. As a leading public institution, we are committed to excellence in patient treatment, health promotion, and community well-being. Our multi-specialty hospital environment fosters a culture of continuous learning, professional growth, and teamwork, ensuring that our staff are empowered to deliver the best possible outcomes. We pride ourselves on our experienced medical professionals, state-of-the-art facilities, and a deep commitment to the health of the communities we serve. Joining St. Ann\'s Bay Regional Hospital means becoming part of a vital organization that makes a tangible difference in people\'s lives every single day, contributing to a healthier Jamaica.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly motivated, compassionate, and experienced Ward Nurse to join our dedicated team at a community health center affiliated with St. Ann\'s Bay Regional Hospital, specifically located in the vibrant district of Priory, St. Ann. This crucial full-time role offers an exceptional opportunity for a seasoned nursing professional to apply their extensive expertise in a dynamic inpatient setting, focusing on the holistic care of diverse patient populations, ranging from medical to post-surgical cases. As an experienced Ward Nurse, you will be instrumental in delivering and coordinating exemplary patient-centered care, guiding individuals and their families from the moment of admission through to a successful discharge, ensuring that the highest standards of clinical practice, ethical conduct, and patient safety are not just met, but consistently exceeded. You will leverage your advanced assessment skills to meticulously monitor patient conditions, identify subtle changes in health status, proficiently administer a wide range of medications and complex treatments, and respond promptly and effectively to any evolving medical needs or emergencies.\n\nBeyond the direct provision of clinical patient care, this role involves significant and continuous collaboration with a diverse multidisciplinary team. This includes working closely with physicians, specialty nurses, allied health professionals such as therapists, and essential support staff, all united in the common goal of developing, implementing, and continually refining individualized care plans tailored to each patient\'s unique requirements. You will serve as a vital patient advocate, empowering individuals and their families by providing comprehensive education and empathetic support regarding their health conditions, prescribed treatment plans, medication management, and practical self-care techniques for recovery and wellness. We are specifically looking for an individual who embodies deep empathy, sharp critical thinking abilities, strong leadership potential, and a proactive, solution-oriented approach to problem-solving within a busy healthcare environment. Your proven ability to work effectively and calmly under pressure, skillfully manage multiple competing priorities, and meticulously maintain accurate electronic health records will be absolutely paramount to your success and the safety of our patients. This position is ideal for a dedicated nurse who is passionate about making a tangible contribution to community health, enhancing patient outcomes through evidence-based practice, and advancing their professional career within a supportive, respectful, and professional hospital network. Join us in our unwavering mission to provide exemplary healthcare services to the cherished people of St. Ann.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Conduct comprehensive patient assessments, including physical and psychosocial evaluations, and develop individualized nursing care plans.\n• Administer medications, treatments, and procedures accurately and safely, adhering strictly to established protocols and physician orders.\n• Monitor and record vital signs, observe patient conditions, and promptly document and report any significant changes to the medical team.\n• Collaborate effectively with physicians, therapists, and other healthcare professionals to ensure coordinated and comprehensive patient care.\n• Educate patients and their families on health conditions, treatment plans, medication management, and self-care techniques.\n• Maintain precise and thorough electronic health records (EHRs), ensuring all patient data is accurate and up-to-date.\n• Provide supervision and mentorship to junior nursing staff and nursing students, fostering a learning-rich environment.\n• Respond rapidly and effectively to medical emergencies, participating in resuscitation efforts and critical interventions.\n• Ensure a safe, clean, and therapeutic ward environment, adhering to infection control policies and safety regulations.\n• Participate in ward meetings, care conferences, and continuous quality improvement initiatives.\n• Demonstrate cultural sensitivity and provide compassionate care to patients from diverse backgrounds.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Active Registered Nurse (RN) license in Jamaica.\n• Minimum of 3 years of post-registration nursing experience in an acute care hospital ward setting.\n• Demonstrated strong clinical assessment and critical thinking skills.\n• Proficiency in medication administration and IV therapy.\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n• Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, high-pressure environment.\n• Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively in a team.\n• Proficiency in using electronic health record (EHR) systems.\n• Current Basic Life Support (BLS) certification.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) or equivalent from an accredited institution.\n• Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS) certification.\n• Experience in specialized ward areas such as medical-surgical, geriatric, or orthopedics.\n• Demonstrated leadership potential or experience in charge nurse duties.\n• Fluency in additional languages common in the community (e.g., Jamaican Patois).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package.\n• Opportunities for continuous professional development, training, and specialist certifications.\n• Supportive, respectful, and collaborative work environment.\n• Direct contribution to a vital community healthcare service.\n• Generous paid time off and sick leave.\n• Access to employee wellness programs and counseling services.\n• Career advancement opportunities within the regional health authority and beyond.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates who meet the specified requirements are invited to apply by clicking on the link below. Please ensure your application includes a detailed resume and a compelling cover letter outlining your relevant experience, key achievements, and why you are the ideal candidate to excel in this pivotal role. Only shortlisted applicants who demonstrate a strong match with our criteria will be contacted for an interview. We eagerly look forward to receiving your application and potentially welcoming you to our dedicated team at St. Ann\'s Bay Regional Hospital, Priory.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ann,st ann,health,patient,care,st,regional,regional hospital,bay regional,ann bay,ward,bay,medical,hospital,comprehensive,nurse,nursing,environment,experienced ward,healthcare,effectively,team,community,professional,vital'),(275,'jsearch','feOrZaNjzr2QwBQOAAAAAA==','Experienced Hospital Ward Nurse','Andrews Memorial Hospital',NULL,'JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/experienced-hospital-ward-nurse/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nAndrews Memorial Hospital, established in 1944, is a leading healthcare institution located in the heart of Kingston, St. Andrew. As a private, not-for-profit hospital dedicated to providing holistic, patient-centered care, we are deeply rooted in the Seventh-day Adventist philosophy of health and wellness. Our mission is to extend the healing ministry of Jesus Christ through compassionate service, medical excellence, and health education. We offer a comprehensive range of medical services, including emergency care, surgery, maternity services, diagnostic imaging, and various specialty clinics. We pride ourselves on our state-of-the-art facilities, highly skilled medical professionals, and a warm, supportive environment that prioritizes both patient recovery and staff well-being. Joining Andrews Memorial Hospital means becoming part of a legacy of care, innovation, and community impact in Jamaica.\n\nJob Description\n\nAndrews Memorial Hospital is seeking a highly skilled and compassionate Experienced Hospital Ward Nurse to join our dedicated nursing team in Hope Pastures, St. Andrew. This pivotal role involves providing exceptional direct patient care within a dynamic hospital ward setting, catering to patients with a diverse range of medical conditions. As an experienced nurse, you will be instrumental in assessing, planning, implementing, and evaluating patient care plans, ensuring adherence to the highest standards of clinical practice and patient safety protocols. You will leverage your extensive clinical knowledge and critical thinking abilities to manage complex patient cases, respond effectively to emergent situations, and provide comprehensive patient education to promote recovery and prevent readmission.\n\nThis position calls for a proactive individual who excels in a collaborative environment, working closely with physicians, other nurses, and allied health professionals to deliver coordinated and effective care. You will be a mentor to junior staff, contributing to a culture of continuous learning and professional development within the ward. Beyond direct care, you will be responsible for accurate documentation, medication administration, wound care, and managing patient flow efficiently. We are looking for a nurse who embodies empathy, resilience, and a steadfast commitment to improving patient outcomes and upholding the hospital\'s values of integrity, respect, and service excellence. If you are passionate about making a tangible difference in the lives of patients and are eager to contribute your expertise to a respected institution, we encourage you to apply.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Provide direct and comprehensive nursing care to patients on the hospital ward, adhering to established policies and procedures.\n• Conduct thorough patient assessments, develop individualized care plans, and evaluate their effectiveness regularly.\n• Administer medications and treatments as prescribed by physicians, ensuring accuracy and documenting all interventions.\n• Monitor and record vital signs, observe patient conditions, and report changes or adverse reactions promptly to the medical team.\n• Collaborate effectively with physicians, therapists, and other healthcare professionals to ensure coordinated and holistic patient care.\n• Educate patients and their families on health conditions, treatment plans, medication management, and self-care techniques.\n• Assist with patient admissions, transfers, and discharges, ensuring a smooth transition of care.\n• Maintain accurate and detailed electronic health records, including nursing notes, medication records, and care plans.\n• Participate in ward rounds, interdisciplinary team meetings, and contribute to care planning discussions.\n• Respond promptly and efficiently to medical emergencies, performing CPR and other life-saving measures as required.\n• Ensure a safe, clean, and therapeutic environment for patients and staff.\n• Mentor and provide guidance to junior nurses and nursing students.\n• Adhere strictly to infection control protocols and patient safety standards.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Active Registered Nurse (RN) license in Jamaica\n• Minimum of 3 years of experience working in a hospital ward setting\n• Proficiency in administering medications and performing various nursing procedures (e.g., IV insertion, wound care)\n• Strong critical thinking and problem-solving abilities\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills\n• Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, high-pressure environment\n• Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary team\n• Compassionate and patient-centered approach to care\n• Basic Life Support (BLS) certification\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN)\n• Advanced Cardiovascular Life Support (ACLS) certification\n• Specialty certification in Medical-Surgical Nursing or a related field\n• Experience with electronic health record (EHR) systems\n• Previous experience in a mentorship or charge nurse role\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package\n• Comprehensive health and dental insurance\n• Pension plan contributions\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuing education\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment\n• Employee wellness programs\n• Paid time off and holidays\n• Access to state-of-the-art medical facilities and technology\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their detailed resume and a cover letter outlining their qualifications and experience. Please click on the link below to apply for this job. We thank all applicants for their interest; however, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'care,patient,hospital,ward,medical,health,memorial hospital,andrews,andrews memorial,memorial,nursing,hospital ward,patients,nurse,comprehensive,plans,direct,education,environment,st andrew,andrew,range medical,efficiently,team,physicians'),(276,'jsearch','50H0SzWb3jciw2GqAAAAAA==','Registered Nurse - Special Care Baby Unit (SCBU) - Work in the Bermuda','Manchester',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.justjobs.co.uk/jobs/registered-nurse-special-care-baby-unit-scbu-work-in-the-bermuda-acb79a1c?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Registered Nurse – Special Care Baby Unit (SCBU)\nLocation: Bermuda\nHours: 35 per week across days, nights, weekends, and public holidays\nStarting Salary: $88,670.83 per annum (approx. £66,295.09)\n\nTake your career as a Registered Nurse to an entirely new level by joining the Special Care Baby Unit in Bermuda. This is a standout opportunity for experienced Neonatal Nurses looking for an overseas nursing role that offers professional challenge, excellent resources, and an outstanding lifestyle. Nursing jobs in Bermuda are highly sought after due to the quality of healthcare, strong community feel, and the chance to work in a modern environment with exceptional clinical standards.\n\nRelocation & Accommodation\n\nFree accommodation for the first 3 months, including utility bills\nAfter the initial period, you can choose to remain in staff accommodation at a subsidised rate (utilities included) or explore private rentals, which are significantly more expensive\nRelocation package of $5,000: $3,000 paid in your first salary, then $2,000 paid at the end of 12 months\nDue to the high cost of living, this opportunity is only suitable for those relocating alone or with a partner\nAbout the Role\n\nThis SCBU Nurse position is ideal for someone confident working within a Level 3 Neonatal setting. You will be part of a team that prioritises safe, evidence-based practice and supports both personal and professional growth.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nProvide specialised care to neonates within a Level 3 Special Care Baby Unit\nCarry out assessments, develop care plans, deliver interventions, and evaluate clinical outcomes\nWork collaboratively with the multidisciplinary team and update senior nursing staff on patient status\nTake on leadership responsibilities when required and use hospital and community resources effectively\nParticipate in quality improvement projects and approved research within the neonatal service\nAct as a preceptor to new or junior SCBU Nursing staff\nEnsure safe and responsible use of neonatal equipment and clinical supplies\nAttend staff meetings, committees, and in-service training as part of ongoing development\nMaintain accountability for continuous professional development\nUndertake additional nursing and delegated medical duties when needed\nRequirements\n\nRegistered Nurse with a Bachelor’s Degree or Diploma from an accredited nursing institution\nEligibility for registration with the Bermuda Nursing & Midwifery Council\nMinimum of two years’ post-registration experience as a Level 3 Neonatal Nurse\nCurrent certifications: CPR, NICU, IV, and Neonatal Resuscitation Programme (NRP)\nStrong physical assessment skills and proven clinical competence\nUp-to-date neonatal nursing knowledge, particularly within Level 3 neonatal care\nWhy Bermuda?\n\nBermuda provides a unique balance of high-standard clinical practice and an excellent lifestyle. With beautiful beaches, outdoor activities, and a close-knit community, it offers a refreshing change of pace from the UK. Nurses relocating here benefit from strong teamwork, supportive leadership, and high-quality working environments designed to help you thrive professionally while enjoying life outside of work.\n\nAbout Sanctuary Personnel:\nSanctuary Personnel is an award-winning recruitment agency with an excellent Trustpilot rating based on over 1,000 reviews. We connect qualified professionals with roles that suit their experience and offer competitive pay rates with exceptional ongoing support',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'neonatal,bermuda,level,care baby,unit,000,scbu,baby unit,baby,special care,special,nursing,level neonatal,accommodation,care,nurse,clinical,sanctuary personnel,000 paid,relocating,lifestyle,relocation,unit scbu,months,ongoing'),(277,'jsearch','zsex87iV84m8zLo4AAAAAA==','Actuarial Support Trainee – Flexible Schedules','Guardian Life Limited',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/actuarial-support-trainee-flexible-schedules/?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','About Company\n\nGuardian Life Limited, a proud member of the Guardian Group, stands as a beacon of financial stability and innovative insurance solutions across Jamaica and the wider Caribbean. With a legacy spanning decades, we are committed to enriching the lives of our customers through a comprehensive suite of life, health, and pension products, alongside unparalleled customer service. Our success is built on a foundation of integrity, expertise, and a forward-thinking approach, driven by a diverse team of dedicated professionals. We believe in nurturing talent and providing an environment where individuals can thrive, grow, and contribute meaningfully to our collective vision of securing futures.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a highly analytical individual with a keen eye for detail, eager to kickstart your career in the dynamic world of actuarial science? Guardian Life Limited invites ambitious and driven candidates to join our team as an Actuarial Support Trainee. This unique opportunity offers a flexible work schedule designed to accommodate your learning and personal commitments, making it an ideal entry point for those balancing further studies or seeking a progressive environment. As an Actuarial Support Trainee, you will play a crucial role in providing essential assistance to our experienced actuaries, contributing to the rigorous analysis, valuation, and risk assessment that underpins our diverse product offerings. You\'ll gain hands-on experience with real-world data, actuarial software, and regulatory requirements, developing a foundational understanding of the principles of insurance and pensions. This role is not just a job; it\'s a comprehensive training ground where you will be mentored by industry experts, fostering your analytical capabilities and problem-solving skills. If you possess a strong quantitative background, a desire to learn, and the ambition to become a future leader in the actuarial field, we encourage you to apply and embark on a rewarding career journey with Guardian Life Limited.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist actuaries with data collection, validation, and analysis for various actuarial projects.\n• Prepare and maintain actuarial models and spreadsheets, ensuring accuracy and consistency.\n• Generate reports and summaries of actuarial findings for internal and external stakeholders.\n• Support the valuation of insurance and annuity products, and pension plans.\n• Perform experience studies on mortality, morbidity, lapses, and expenses.\n• Contribute to the development and testing of new insurance products and features.\n• Research and analyze industry trends, regulatory changes, and economic factors impacting actuarial work.\n• Collaborate effectively with other departments, including Underwriting, Claims, and Finance.\n• Participate in training sessions and workshops to enhance actuarial knowledge and skills.\n• Adhere to all company policies, procedures, and regulatory requirements.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Strong analytical and quantitative reasoning skills.\n• Proficiency in Microsoft Excel (advanced functions, pivot tables, VLOOKUP).\n• Excellent attention to detail and accuracy.\n• Effective written and verbal communication skills.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a team.\n• Strong problem-solving abilities.\n• Time management and organizational skills, especially with flexible schedules.\n• Minimum of a Bachelor\'s degree in Actuarial Science, Mathematics, Statistics, Economics, or a related quantitative field.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Completion of at least one actuarial examination (e.g., SOA/CAS, IFoA).\n• Familiarity with actuarial software (e.g., Prophet, MoSes, R, Python) is a plus.\n• Previous internship or work experience in an actuarial, finance, or data analysis role.\n• A strong academic record.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and life insurance.\n• Company-sponsored pension plan.\n• Flexible work schedule options to promote work-life balance.\n• Opportunities for professional development and actuarial exam support.\n• Mentorship from experienced actuarial professionals.\n• A supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n• Generous paid time off.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to launch your actuarial career with a leading financial institution? We invite qualified candidates to submit their applications by clicking on the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your quantitative skills and any relevant academic or professional experience. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'actuarial,skills,work,life,support,insurance,strong,quantitative,guardian,flexible,experience,support trainee,life limited,trainee,team,products,pension,limited,regulatory,role,guardian life,environment,analysis,data,comprehensive'),(282,'jsearch','hSxI5R2id0hgTNUmAAAAAA==','Paralegal Officer (PLG/LS 5)','Ministry of Water, Environment and Climate Change\"',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Paralegal-Officer-PLG-LS-5-Job-227452.aspx','KEY RESPONSIBILITY AREAS Technical/Professional Responsibilities Assist in the preparation of legal documents, under the guidance of the Paralegal and Legal Officers; Draft all legal documents – sale agreements, lease agreement, instruments of transfer etc. relating to the sale or lease of property; Liaise with external clients to track the progress of sale agreements to ensure timely completion; Liaise with external clients to track the progress of lease agreements and ensure timely completion; Ensure retention schedules for legal documents/files relating to land sub-divisions and housing developments are strictly adhered to and files are stored securely and easily retrievable; Liaise with Agencies and other Departments as required when conducting searches and ensure documents received are checked for accuracy; Serve as liaison with other GOJ entities; Conduct research into legislation and other sources of law as directed; Meet with walk-in clients and assist in providing updates on their matters before escalating; Assist in organising meetings to review and discuss legal documents; Assists in collating documents in preparation for legal hearings and consultations; Provides information to stakeholders and other parties subject to maintaining confidentiality and/or upon the instructions of the Legal Officers where necessary; Processes general inquiries and requests as directed; Maintains the files and records in a confidential, secure and reliable manner in accordance with established records management principles to ensure expeditious retrieval of files. Management/Administrative Responsibilities Develops Individual Work Plans based on alignment to the overall plan for the section; Participates in meetings, seminars, workshops and conferences as required; Prepares reports and programme documents as required. Other Responsibilities Performs all other related duties and functions as may be required from time to time.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'documents,legal,files,legal documents,agreements,assist,lease,sale,ensure,required,clients,sale agreements,officers,relating,timely completion,timely,external clients,preparation,paralegal,ensure timely,track progress,liaise external,clients track,directed,records'),(284,'jsearch','fV5v6kltKXJIpRQVAAAAAA==','Pharmacist','Grace Bay Pharmacy',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Pharmacist-Job-226758.aspx?utm_campaign=google_jobs_apply&utm_source=google_jobs_apply&utm_medium=organic','Position Available: Pharmacist Duties and Responsibilities: Dispensing prescription medication, checking dosage and advising on the proper use of prescription and over-the-counter medicines and medical appliances. Patient counseling on health matters including managing chronic illnesses and administering tests for these conditions. Providing counseling and education to patients on medication, potential side effects, drug interactions, and storage requirements. Liaising with doctors, nurses and other healthcare providers about prescriptions, medications and clinical conditions. Maintaining accurate patient records. Filing claims with the National Health Insurance Board as required. Engaging with regulators and industry groups and staying current with the latest advancements in pharmaceuticals, clinical guidelines, and best practices. Supervising pharmacy technicians, interns, and support staff as required. Managing prescription inventory. Preparing and providing reports to management as required. Participate is quarterly inventory counting at all stores and distribution facilities, as required by the company. Participating in community health awareness and promotional events. Maintaining an empathetic and patient-centered approach while at all times performing duties and responsibilities with skill, care, professionalism, and courteousness. Required Skills and Competencies In-depth knowledge of pharmacology, drug interactions, and proper medication administration. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills for patient counseling and teamwork with healthcare professionals. Ability to train and manage people. Strong attention to detail and high standards of accuracy and efficiency. Ability to interpret and analyze prescriptions and medical charts. Problem-solving skills and ability to make informed clinical decisions. Proficiency with pharmacy information systems and technology. Commitment to confidentiality and ethical practices. The role may require standing for extended periods and working evenings, weekends, and public holidays Proficiency in English is required; ability to speak and read Spanish and or French Creole is a strong asset Minimum Education and Licensing Requirements Bachelor of Pharmacy degree from an accredited school. Currently registered and practicing as a licensed pharmacist. Be qualified for licensure by the Turks & Caicos Islands Health Professionals Authority. Be qualified to obtain a valid Turks & Caicos Islands Work Permit or otherwise be legally permitted to work within the TCI.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'required,patient,health,ability,clinical,counseling,pharmacy,prescription,skills,pharmacist,medication,drug,work,caicos,conditions,caicos islands,drug interactions,islands,interactions,inventory,healthcare,duties,duties responsibilities,education,patient counseling'),(285,'jsearch','S3dJI-Jq_TDzJP6mAAAAAA==','General Dentist with Orthodontic Experience!','New York Family Dentistry',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.recruit.net/job/general-dentist-orthodontic-experience-jobs/FDA7A0017530819E','We are seeking a qualified General Dentist with orthodontic experience to join our team and help provide exceptional patient care. We are looking for a well experienced orthodontist who possesses comprehensive knowledge of orthodontic treatment including diagnosis, treatment planning and appliance placement and adjustment and has the ability to work effectively with a dental team for our 5+ practices in Brooklyn and Queens. We are seeking a motivated individual who is well detail-oriented and able to work collaboratively with other dental professionals to ensure comprehensive patient care.\n\nSalary: ranging from up to $400,000 annually\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Perform general dental procedures including cleanings, fillings, crowns, and preventive care, while utilizing orthodontic skills to assess and create treatment plans for patients requiring braces or other orthodontic appliances.\n• Evaluate, diagnose, and treat orthodontic cases, including designing and adjusting braces and aligners, and monitor patient progress throughout the course of treatment.\n• Skilled in managing patient comfort, including sedation and anesthesia techniques when necessary\n• Educate patients on oral hygiene, post-surgical care, and orthodontic maintenance, providing clear instructions for successful treatment outcomes.\n• Maintain accurate patient records, document treatments and progress, and collaborate with specialists as needed for complex cases.\n• Participating in continuing education to stay current with the latest orthodontic techniques and technology\n• Coordinating with the treatment coordinator to ensure efficient scheduling and follow-up care\n• Maintaining communication with referring dentists and other healthcare providers\n• Proficiency in using orthodontic appliances, including braces, clear aligners, and retainers\n\nQualifications:\n• Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS) or Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) degree from an accredited dental school.\n• DDS or DMD and Completion of an Accredited Orthodontic Residency Program\n• Expertise in orthodontic treatment planning and execution\n• Proficiency in using orthodontic appliances, including braces, clear aligners, and retainers\n• Experience with Various Orthodontic Technologies and Appliances\n\nGeneral Skills:\n• Orthodontic Treatment Planning\n• Braces and Aligners\n• Clear Aligners (e.g., Invisalign)\n• Retainers and Post-Treatment Care\n• Space Maintainers\n• Orthodontic Appliances\n• Proficiency in Digital Imaging (CBCT, 3D Imaging)\n• Malocclusion Diagnosis\n• Attention to Detail and Precision in Treatment\n• Ability to Manage Patient Expectations and Treatment Outcomes',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'orthodontic,treatment,appliances,braces,aligners,clear,orthodontic appliances,patient,including,care,orthodontic treatment,clear aligners,retainers,general,dental,planning,treatment planning,including braces,general dentist,imaging,braces clear,outcomes,aligners retainers,dentist orthodontic,appliances including'),(286,'jsearch','aRdegRLXOUPQo3e2AAAAAA==','Dentist – Dental Clinic (Professional)','Brown\'s Town Dental Centre','Browns Town','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/dentist-dental-clinic-professional/','About Company\n\nBrown\'s Town Dental Centre is a leading dental practice proudly serving the community of St. Ann, Jamaica, for over a decade. We are committed to providing exceptional, patient-centered oral healthcare in a warm, welcoming, and state-of-the-art environment. Our clinic is equipped with modern dental technology, enabling us to offer a comprehensive range of services from routine check-ups and cleanings to advanced restorative and cosmetic procedures. We believe in fostering a collaborative and supportive atmosphere for our dental professionals, ensuring they have the resources and autonomy to deliver the highest standard of care. At Brown\'s Town Dental Centre, we prioritize patient education, preventive care, and building lasting relationships based on trust and respect. Join our dedicated team and contribute to enhancing the oral health and smiles of our vibrant community.\n\nJob Description\n\nWe are seeking a highly skilled, compassionate, and dedicated Dentist to join our esteemed team at Brown\'s Town Dental Centre. This is an excellent opportunity for a professional who is passionate about delivering top-tier dental care and making a tangible difference in patients\' lives. As a Dentist with our clinic, you will be responsible for providing a full spectrum of general dentistry services, including diagnosis, treatment planning, and execution of various dental procedures. You will work alongside a supportive team of dental hygienists, assistants, and administrative staff, all committed to creating a positive patient experience. We are looking for an individual who embodies professionalism, possesses excellent communication skills, and is committed to continuous learning and professional development. The ideal candidate will be adept at building rapport with patients of all ages, explaining treatment options clearly, and ensuring their comfort and understanding throughout their visit. Your role will be crucial in maintaining our clinic\'s reputation for excellence and expanding our reach within the Brown\'s Town community. We value ethical practice, meticulous attention to detail, and a proactive approach to patient care. This role offers the chance to work in a community-focused practice, utilizing modern equipment and techniques to deliver outstanding results.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Perform comprehensive oral examinations, diagnose dental conditions, and develop appropriate treatment plans.\n• Execute a wide range of general dental procedures, including fillings, extractions, root canal treatments, crowns, bridges, and dentures.\n• Provide preventive dental care, including professional cleanings, fluoride treatments, and patient education on oral hygiene.\n• Administer local anesthesia effectively and safely.\n• Maintain accurate and detailed patient records, including medical history, treatment plans, and progress notes.\n• Adhere strictly to all sterilization protocols and infection control guidelines.\n• Collaborate with dental hygienists and assistants to ensure seamless patient care and efficient clinic operations.\n• Educate patients on proper oral health maintenance, nutrition, and treatment options.\n• Handle dental emergencies promptly and effectively.\n• Participate in continuing education and professional development activities to stay abreast of the latest dental techniques and technologies.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS) or Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD) degree from an accredited institution.\n• Valid dental license to practice in Jamaica.\n• Minimum of 3 years of clinical experience as a practicing Dentist.\n• Proficiency in all aspects of general dentistry.\n• Excellent diagnostic and treatment planning skills.\n• Strong interpersonal and communication skills.\n• Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented environment.\n• Compassionate and patient-focused approach to care.\n• Meticulous attention to detail and strong organizational skills.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Experience with digital radiography and intraoral scanning technologies.\n• Proficiency in basic orthodontic procedures or cosmetic dentistry techniques.\n• Active participation in professional dental associations.\n• Bilingual (English and Spanish) skills are a plus.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package.\n• Performance-based bonuses.\n• Paid vacation and sick leave.\n• Health and dental insurance.\n• Opportunities for continuing education and professional development.\n• Supportive and collaborative work environment.\n• Access to modern dental equipment and technology.\n• Contribution to a pension scheme.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting opportunity, please click on the application link below. Ensure your resume and a cover letter detailing your experience and why you are the ideal candidate for this role are attached. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to our dedicated team at Brown\'s Town Dental Centre.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'dental,town,brown town,brown,patient,town dental,centre,dental centre,care,professional,treatment,clinic,dentist,skills,team,practice,oral,modern,dentistry,general,techniques,community,procedures,including,education'),(287,'jsearch','V95cbiDBcJTUiM8wAAAAAA==','Dental Clinic Assistant – Flexible Hours','Dental Solutions Montego Bay',NULL,NULL,0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/dental-clinic-assistant-flexible-hours/','About Company\n\nDental Solutions Montego Bay is a leading dental practice committed to providing exceptional oral healthcare to the communities of St. James and beyond. With a state-of-the-art facility, our highly skilled team of dentists and specialists offers a comprehensive range of services, from routine check-ups and cleanings to advanced restorative and cosmetic procedures. We pride ourselves on creating a comfortable, welcoming, and patient-centric environment where every individual feels heard, respected, and receives personalized care designed to achieve optimal oral health and radiant smiles. Our mission is to combine cutting-edge technology with compassionate service, ensuring a positive and pain-free experience for all our patients. We believe in continuous learning and professional development, fostering a culture of excellence and innovation within our practice. We are dedicated to making a positive impact on the health and well-being of the communities we serve.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a compassionate, detail-oriented individual with a passion for healthcare and a desire to make a tangible difference in people\'s lives? Dental Solutions Montego Bay is seeking a dedicated and enthusiastic Dental Clinic Assistant to join our growing team, specifically serving our patient base in Anchovy, St. James. This part-time position offers flexible hours, ideal for someone looking to balance professional commitments with other responsibilities while contributing to a thriving dental practice.\n\nAs a Dental Clinic Assistant, you will be the backbone of our clinic\'s operations, playing a crucial role in ensuring the smooth and efficient delivery of dental care. Your primary responsibilities will span across patient support, clinical assistance, and administrative tasks. You will be the first friendly face many of our patients see, setting the tone for a positive dental experience. This role involves preparing treatment rooms, sterilizing instruments, assisting dentists during procedures, and providing essential patient education on oral hygiene. Beyond clinical support, you will manage patient appointments, update medical records, handle billing inquiries, and maintain a pristine and organized clinic environment. We are looking for someone who can anticipate needs, work proactively, and maintain a high standard of professionalism and confidentiality. This is an incredible opportunity to grow your skills in a supportive environment, learn from experienced dental professionals, and contribute directly to the oral health and well-being of the Anchovy community. We value teamwork, empathy, and a strong work ethic, and we are excited to welcome a new member who shares our commitment to excellence in patient care. Your contribution will directly impact our patients\' comfort and satisfaction, making every visit a pleasant one.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Prepare treatment rooms for dental procedures, ensuring all necessary instruments and materials are readily available.\n\n• Sterilize and disinfect instruments and equipment in accordance with strict infection control protocols.\n\n• Assist dentists during a variety of dental treatments, including passing instruments, operating suction, and preparing dental materials.\n\n• Provide post-operative instructions and oral hygiene education to patients.\n\n• Manage patient scheduling, appointments, and confirm upcoming visits.\n\n• Maintain accurate patient records and update medical histories confidentially.\n\n• Handle patient inquiries, explain treatment plans, and assist with billing processes.\n\n• Ensure the clinic environment is clean, organized, and welcoming at all times.\n\n• Order and manage dental supplies, ensuring adequate stock levels.\n\n• Perform basic laboratory procedures, such as pouring models and fabricating temporary crowns.\n\nRequired Skills\n\n• High School Diploma or equivalent.\n\n• Completion of a recognized Dental Assistant program or relevant vocational training.\n\n• Strong interpersonal and communication skills.\n\n• Proficiency in basic computer applications and dental practice management software (e.g., Dentrix, Open Dental).\n\n• Excellent organizational and multitasking abilities.\n\n• Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced environment.\n\n• Knowledge of infection control and sterilization procedures.\n\n• Compassionate and patient-focused approach.\n\n• Ability to maintain strict confidentiality of patient information.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• Previous experience working in a dental clinic or healthcare setting.\n\n• CPR and First Aid certification.\n\n• Familiarity with dental insurance procedures and billing.\n\n• Bilingual (English and Spanish) skills are a plus.\n\n• A strong understanding of dental terminology and procedures.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n\n• Flexible working hours to support work-life balance.\n\n• Opportunity to work with a dedicated and supportive team.\n\n• Continuous professional development and training opportunities.\n\n• Contribution to a highly respected dental practice.\n\n• Exposure to a diverse range of dental procedures and patient cases.\n\n• A positive and patient-centric work environment.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are ready to embark on a rewarding career and contribute to a team dedicated to excellence in dental care, we encourage you to apply! Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and cover letter. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to the Dental Solutions Montego Bay family.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dental,patient,clinic,procedures,environment,solutions montego,hours,montego bay,montego,bay,flexible,clinic assistant,dental solutions,practice,assistant,instruments,dental clinic,work,solutions,billing,dedicated,ensuring,dental practice,positive,oral'),(288,'jsearch','XSP9gdv_bGBg__OqAAAAAA==','Dental Assistant – Clinic Support (Entry-Level)','Smile Solutions Dental Clinic','Portmore','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/dental-assistant-clinic-support-entry-level/','About Company\n\nSmile Solutions Dental Clinic is a leading dental practice dedicated to providing exceptional oral healthcare to the Portmore community. Nestled in the heart of Portmore, Jamaica, our modern clinic is equipped with state-of-the-art technology and staffed by a team of compassionate and highly skilled dental professionals. We are committed to creating a warm, welcoming, and comfortable environment for all our patients, ensuring a positive experience from their very first visit. Our mission is to promote lasting oral health and beautiful smiles through preventative care, restorative treatments, and patient education, all while fostering a supportive and professional atmosphere for our team members. At Smile Solutions, we believe in community engagement and strive to be a trusted partner in the health and well-being of the families we serve.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you looking to kickstart a rewarding career in the dental field? Smile Solutions Dental Clinic in Portmore is seeking a highly motivated and compassionate Entry-Level Dental Assistant to join our dedicated team. This is a fantastic opportunity for individuals eager to learn the foundational aspects of dental care and grow within a supportive environment. As a Clinic Support Dental Assistant, you will be an indispensable part of our daily operations, ensuring our clinic runs smoothly and our patients receive exceptional care.\n\nWe believe that a great patient experience begins with a well-organized and friendly clinic, and that\'s where you come in. Your primary role will be to provide comprehensive support to our dentists, hygienists, and administrative staff, contributing to a seamless and positive patient journey from the moment they step through our doors until their departure. This entry-level position is designed for someone with a strong work ethic, a keen eye for detail, and an enthusiastic willingness to learn the intricacies of dental assisting. No prior dental experience is required; we are committed to providing thorough on-the-job training and mentorship to help you succeed and develop valuable skills.\n\nYour day will be dynamic and varied. You will play a crucial role in preparing treatment rooms, ensuring all necessary instruments and materials are ready for various procedures. Maintaining strict sterilization protocols will be a key part of your responsibilities, upholding our commitment to patient safety and hygiene. You will learn to assist dentists chairside during a wide range of treatments, anticipate their needs, and provide comfort and reassurance to our patients. Beyond clinical support, you will also contribute to the overall efficiency of the clinic by helping with scheduling, managing patient records, and ensuring our waiting areas are welcoming and tidy.\n\nAt Smile Solutions Dental Clinic, we pride ourselves on fostering a collaborative and friendly work environment. We value teamwork, professionalism, and a shared passion for promoting oral health. If you are a proactive individual who enjoys interacting with people, possesses excellent communication skills, and is eager to embark on a fulfilling career path where you can make a real difference in people\'s lives, we encourage you to apply. This role offers not just a job, but a gateway to a professional career in dentistry, with ample opportunities for continuous learning and career advancement within our growing practice. Join us and become a vital part of a team dedicated to creating beautiful, healthy smiles in the Portmore community.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Greet and prepare patients for dental treatments, ensuring their comfort and answering any initial questions.\n\n• Prepare treatment rooms by setting up instruments, equipment, and materials required for various dental procedures.\n\n• Maintain strict sterilization and disinfection protocols for all instruments and equipment, adhering to health and safety standards.\n\n• Assist dentists and hygienists chairside during a wide range of procedures, anticipating their needs and handing instruments.\n\n• Provide post-operative instructions and oral hygiene education to patients, ensuring they understand care requirements.\n\n• Manage patient records, ensuring accuracy and confidentiality of all medical and personal information.\n\n• Assist with scheduling appointments, confirming patient visits, and managing the clinic\'s appointment book.\n\n• Perform general office duties such as answering phones, filing, and maintaining a clean and organized reception area.\n\n• Monitor and maintain inventory of dental supplies, placing orders as needed to ensure smooth clinic operations.\n\n• Contribute to a positive and collaborative team environment, assisting colleagues as required.\n\nRequired Skills\n\n• Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n\n• Strong interpersonal skills with a compassionate and empathetic approach to patient care.\n\n• High attention to detail and ability to follow instructions precisely.\n\n• Proactive and eager to learn new skills and procedures.\n\n• Basic computer proficiency for record-keeping and scheduling.\n\n• Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced and dynamic environment.\n\n• Reliable, punctual, and a strong team player.\n\n• Manual dexterity and good hand-eye coordination.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• High School Diploma or GED equivalent.\n\n• CPR certification (or willingness to obtain upon hiring).\n\n• Previous experience in a customer service role.\n\n• A genuine interest in the dental healthcare field.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n\n• Comprehensive on-the-job training and mentorship.\n\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n\n• Supportive and friendly team environment.\n\n• Uniform provided.\n\n• Opportunity to make a tangible difference in patient\'s lives.\n\n• Pathway to a fulfilling career in the dental industry.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting entry-level opportunity, please click on the application link below. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to the Smile Solutions Dental Clinic family.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dental,clinic,smile,smile solutions,patient,ensuring,solutions,entry level,level,entry,portmore,solutions dental,team,environment,career,learn,dental clinic,instruments,skills,patients,care,eager,required,role,support'),(289,'jsearch','tfeV-dmwNktlMQ1BAAAAAA==','Dental Assistant – Dentist Support, Full-Time','Career.zycto','Linstead','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/dental-assistant-dentist-support-full-time/','About Company\n\nAre you a dedicated Dental Assistant seeking a vibrant place to grow your career and make a tangible difference? Career.zycto is a rapidly expanding dental practice in Linstead, committed to delivering exceptional patient care with a warm, community-focused approach. We believe our strength lies in our supportive team, fostering an environment where every member, especially our vital dental assistants, feels valued and empowered. Joining us means becoming part of a forward-thinking clinic that prioritizes professional development, utilizes modern techniques, and truly impacts the oral health of the Linstead community. We\'re building a legacy of smiles, and we invite you to be a part of it.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking a highly motivated and compassionate Full-Time Dental Assistant to join our dynamic dental team in Linstead, Saint Catherine Parish. As a Dental Assistant, you will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth operation of our dental practice and providing an exceptional patient experience. You will work closely with our dentists, assisting with a variety of procedures, maintaining sterilization standards, and educating patients on oral hygiene. This position is perfect for an individual who is passionate about dental health, possesses excellent interpersonal skills, and thrives in a fast-paced, patient-centered environment. We are dedicated to fostering a supportive and collaborative workplace where professionalism and a commitment to quality care are paramount. If you are eager to contribute your skills to a practice that values its team members and is deeply rooted in community well-being, we encourage you to apply. Your expertise will be vital in supporting our mission to deliver top-tier dental services and create healthy, confident smiles for all our patients.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n• Prepare and sterilize treatment rooms and dental instruments according to strict infection control guidelines.\n\n• Assist the dentist efficiently during a variety of treatment procedures, including restorative, surgical, and prophylactic treatments.\n\n• Take and process accurate dental radiographs (X-rays) as instructed by the dentist.\n\n• Provide comprehensive pre- and post-operative instructions and oral hygiene education to patients.\n\n• Manage patient records, appointments, and billing information with accuracy and strict confidentiality.\n\n• Maintain and monitor dental supplies inventory, ensuring adequate stock levels and timely reordering.\n\n• Perform basic laboratory duties such as pouring impressions and trimming models.\n\n• Ensure patient comfort, alleviate anxiety, and maintain a positive experience throughout their dental visit.\n\n• Adhere to all local health and safety regulations pertinent to dental practice.\n\nRequired Skills\n\n• Minimum of 1 year of proven experience as a Dental Assistant.\n\n• Proficiency with dental instruments, equipment, and sterilization protocols.\n\n• Solid understanding of health and safety regulations (e.g., local equivalents of OSHA/HIPAA).\n\n• Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills, with a patient-first approach.\n\n• Strong organizational abilities and efficient time management.\n\n• Familiarity and experience with common dental software.\n\n• Ability to take accurate dental impressions and assist with minor lab tasks.\n\n• Current CPR certification.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n• Certification from an accredited Dental Assistant program.\n\n• Experience with digital radiography and intra-oral cameras.\n\n• Bilingual proficiency (English and local Jamaican dialects) is a significant advantage.\n\n• Prior experience working in a community-focused dental practice.\n\n• Commitment to continuous professional development.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n\n• Competitive salary commensurate with your experience and qualifications.\n\n• Comprehensive health and dental benefits package.\n\n• Generous paid time off and holidays.\n\n• Opportunities for continuing education and professional development to enhance your skills.\n\n• A supportive, collaborative, and friendly team environment.\n\n• Access to a modern and well-equipped dental facility.\n\n• Employee wellness programs and initiatives.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to bring your skills to a thriving dental practice? We invite you to apply by clicking on the link below. Please ensure your resume and a cover letter highlighting your relevant experience are attached. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to our team!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'dental,dental assistant,assistant,practice,experience,patient,linstead,health,dental practice,time,skills,team,career,local,dentist,community,invite,accurate dental,career zycto,impressions,safety regulations,dental instruments,zycto,regulations,professional development'),(290,'jsearch','lyW2JGpsUnfpfqZfAAAAAA==','Seeking Bilingual Dentists for Our Community - Spanish Latam','Lilt',NULL,NULL,0,'https://jobgether.com/offer/697bdfa356210e2729216396-seeking-bilingual-dentists-for-our-community---spanish-latam','This a Full Remote job, the offer is available from: Latin America\nWhat we are looking for:\nLilt is actively seeking experienced bilingual dentists (or advanced students of Dentistry) to review translated content to ensure clinical accuracy, correct terminology usage, and clarity of information shared.\nWe are looking for professionals who can seamlessly bridge the gap between complex dental science and effective communication. Your clinical expertise is your primary asset!\nWe are particularly interested in expertise across the following domains:\n• Restorative Dentistry (Resto)\n\n• Endodontics (Endo)\n\n• Implantology and Dental Implants\n\n• Orthodontics and Aligners\n\n• Advanced Dental Technology\n\nIf you have clinical experience in other dental specialties (e.g., periodontics, pediatric dentistry, oral surgery), please ensure it is clearly stated on your application.\nPlease note:\n• This is a remote, freelance contractor position.\n\n• We use Tipalti exclusively for contractor payments. An active Tipalti account or the ability to set one up will be a prerequisite for working with Lilt.\n\nRequirements:\n• Clinical Background: A Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS), Doctor of Dental Medicine (DMD), or equivalent degree OR current enrollment as an advanced student (3rd year or higher) in an accredited dentistry program.\n\n• Bilingual Proficiency: Demonstrated native or near-native fluency in English and your mother tongue (both clinical and professional context). Please state your mother tongue clearly.\n\n• Review/Editing Experience: Proven ability to meticulously review and correct specialized medical or technical content. Experience in writing, editing, or translation of dental-related materials is a significant advantage.\n\n• Domain Expertise: Ability to accurately and confidently handle terminology in your declared fields of expertise (e.g., prosthodontics, advanced digital workflows).\n\nAI is changing how the world communicates — and LILT is leading that transformation.\nLILT\'s mission is to make the world\'s information available to everyone, no matter the language they speak. Join our global community who thrive on innovation and excellence. Our collective knowledge, uniqueness, and skills deliver multilingual AI and human-verified services to Enterprises, Governments, and AI Developers around the world.\nEarn money. Have fun. Advance human knowledge. Work on diverse projects from anywhere, any time you want. Get paid quickly and fairly, and build your professional network in a supportive community—all through a streamlined application process tailored to your expertise.\n\nInformation collected and processed as part of your application process, including any job applications you choose to submit, is subject to LILT\'s Privacy Policy at https://lilt.com/legal/privacy.\n\nAt LILT, we are committed to a fair, inclusive, and transparent hiring process. As part of our recruitment efforts, we may use artificial intelligence (AI) and automated tools to assist in the evaluation of applications, including résumé screening, assessment scoring, and interview analysis. These tools are designed to support human decision-making and help us identify qualified candidates efficiently and objectively. All final hiring decisions are made by people. If you have any concerns, require accommodations, or would like to opt-out of the use of AI in our hiring process, please let us know at recruiting@lilt.com.\n\nLILT is an equal opportunity employer. We extend equal opportunity to all individuals without regard to an individual’s race, religion, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, medical condition, genetic characteristics, veteran or marital status, pregnancy, or any other classification protected by applicable local, state or federal laws. We are committed to the principles of fair employment and the elimination of all discriminatory practices.\nThis offer from \"Lilt\" has been enriched by Jobgether.com and got a 83% flex score.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'lilt,ai,expertise,process,dental,com,review,world,use,human,clinical,advanced,dentistry,hiring,editing,tipalti,correct,hiring process,privacy,equal opportunity,contractor,application process,content,fair,lilt com'),(291,'jsearch','4uky8kF89joKj2BsAAAAAA==','Senior Full Stack Software Engineer – .NET (C#) / React - (516)','Ubiminds',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dailyremote.com/remote-job/senior-full-stack-software-engineer-net-c-react-516-4968296','Senior Full Stack Software Engineer – .NET (C#) / React\n\nRemote · Full-time\n\nAbout Ubiminds\n\nUbiminds is a GPTW-certified, people-first company that partners with American software product companies to scale their development teams. We connect Brazil’s top 5% talent with innovative U.S. companies through a unique combination of staff augmentation and employer-of-record services.\n\nWe are supporting a U.S.-based company looking for a Senior Full Stack Software Engineer to join a Platform product team (Lyons team), working on core systems and evolving platform capabilities.\n\nChallenge\n\nWe’re looking for a Senior Full Stack Engineer who thrives in highly dynamic environments, where priorities evolve and ambiguity is part of the day-to-day.\n\nThis role is ideal for someone who is technically strong but also highly adaptable, proactive, and ownership-driven — someone who can move across different domains, quickly understand complex systems, and contribute wherever needed.\n\nYou will work on critical platform areas such as messaging, scheduling, and automation, while helping drive the transition toward modern architectures and AI-enhanced development practices.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n• Develop and maintain features across front-end (React) and back-end (.NET / C#) systems.\n• Work on systems involving messaging (SMS, WhatsApp, email via providers like Twilio).\n• Build and evolve solutions for scheduling, calendar integrations, and event-driven workflows.\n• Contribute to a multi-repository environment with technologies such as C#, Python, and React.\n• Support the evolution toward microservices architecture, Kubernetes, and continuous deployment pipelines.\n• Collaborate in architectural and cross-team technical discussions.\n• Experiment with and adopt AI-driven development approaches across the SDLC.\n• Write clean, maintainable, and testable code.\n• Actively share knowledge and collaborate across teams.\n\nRequired Skills & Qualifications\n• Strong experience with .NET (C#) in production environments.\n• Solid experience building modern front-end applications with React.\n• Experience with relational databases such as MS SQL.\n• Experience working in complex, existing systems (not only greenfield).\n• Familiarity with:\n• Microservices architecture\n• CI/CD pipelines\n• Containerized environments (e.g., Kubernetes)\n• Ability to work across multiple technologies and codebases.\n• Experience working in distributed teams.\n• Strong communication skills in English (C1 level – written and verbal).\n\nSoft Skills (Critical)\n• Strong ownership mindset.\n• Proactive, self-driven attitude (“figure it out” mindset).\n• Ability to ask the right questions and clarify requirements.\n• Comfortable dealing with ambiguity and changing priorities.\n• Collaborative mindset, sharing knowledge and learnings.\n• Ability to ramp up quickly in new domains and technologies.\n\nNice to Have\n• Experience with Python backend services.\n• Experience with AI-assisted development workflows.\n• Exposure to AWS environments.\n• Experience with messaging platforms such as Twilio.\n• Experience with event-driven systems or scheduling platforms.\n\nTeam & Environment\n• Platform product team (Lyons), working across multiple domains.\n• Tech stack includes C#, React, Python, and distributed systems.\n• Ongoing evolution toward microservices and modern infrastructure.\n• Strong culture of collaboration, experimentation (including AI usage), and continuous improvement.\n\nWhy Join\n• Work on core platform systems with real business impact.\n• Be part of a team evolving toward modern architectures and AI-driven development.\n• Collaborate in a highly dynamic and learning-oriented environment.\n• Full support from Ubiminds with HR, career guidance, and administrative services.\n• Remote-first culture with international exposure.\n\nAbout Ubiminds\n\nOur Culture\n\n- People First. We are all about people!\n\n- Challenge yourself. There’s always room for improvement and continuous improvement is in our essence.\n\n- Make it happen. Be ready to take challenges as they come. It’s all about attitude and commitment.\n\n- We’re in this together. We work as a team, thrive as a team, and evolve as a team.\n\n- Averaging on awesome. We work hard to deliver high-quality services and look forward to exceeding expectations.\n\n- Keep it real. We promise you honesty, transparency, and openness, regardless of the situation.\n\nPerks and Benefits\n\n- You are placed in a product-based company, with the same treatment as their full-time employees.\n\n- Have our full back-office support, from career guidance to HR and concierge services.\n\n- Enjoy our remote-first policy – we are a distributed team, after all.\n\n- Get your own MacBook (none of that \"bring your own device\" stuff here).\n\n- Have access to growth opportunities with other amazing technology professionals, through tech talks, chapter meetings, and even remote happy hours for tons of fun!\n\n- Improve your English through free lessons with a native English speaker - get to the next level on your communication skills!\n\n- Candidate Referral bonus (promote Ubi to your tech friends, and get paid for it!)\n\n- Miss working in the office? Our cool Florianópolis headquarters is available, whenever you want, with weekly quick massages & tasty snacks, soft drinks, and games',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'systems,team,environments,ubiminds,platform,experience,senior stack,driven,services,ai,stack,net,messaging,software engineer,microservices,domains,evolve,stack software,scheduling,highly,work,modern,improvement,software,strong'),(292,'jsearch','y4VhRbeNUqgnSsTGAAAAAA==','Software Engineer, Full-Stack (Remote) – Remote','Supermove',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/software-engineer-at-supermove','What you can expect working with us:\n\nYou will rewrite a massive industry with 10000s of businesses\n\nYou will be introducing technology to the moving industry, an industry previously untouched by software. By working with our customer base, you will provide them more time, revenue, and speed – radically uplifting the entire moving experience for everyone in the world. We accompany our customers every step of the way from the moment they partner with us to the end of their journey. We bring passion to what we do every day because what we do matters to real people.\n\nYou will likely determine the fate of our company\n\nWe are a customer-driven team that tackles problems with empathy and logical reasoning. We aim to truly solve problems for our customers and accomplish this through a thorough process of problem discovery, user research, user testing, and iteration. We’re looking for experienced, thoughtful product engineers who enjoy solving real-world problems and seeing their software used by thousands of people everyday.\n\nYou will work with a smart and action-oriented team\n\nAt Supermove, we are trying to do what’s nearly impossible – to create an enduring and iconic company. We are relentless and ambitious with all of our goals. We move extremely quickly, and prefer to iterate rather than deliberate. We always operate with full trust and transparency, knowing that our top priority is to achieve our vision to the best of our ability.\n\nQuick Facts\n• We closed our series A round raising $18M led by a16z in 2022 – read more about it here.\n• We are a 40 person team of Pinterest, Asana, Facebook, and Google alums.\n• We are early and the opportunity is massive. 10,000s of companies have not heard from us yet.\n• We close new customers every week and have >2x our revenue in the past year.\n\nRole & Responsibilities\n• Build new user-facing features end-to-end from the database schema up to the UI components with great attention to detail\n• Create generic systems that are able to solve any workflow in a scalable way. Generalized systems include billing, document creation and storage, task workflow, and customer communication systems\n• Optimize our GraphQL backend for fast performance so that our movers are able to complete their jobs quickly\n• Add real-time support to our notifications framework and customer communication features\n• Work on our early-staged design system to build UI components consistently and quickly. Help define how we build components here at Supermove\n• Open source general frameworks that we use to build entire applications consistently and quickly\n• Shipping code, conduct code reviews\n• Architecture docs and Design handoffs\n• Product brainstorm/scoping (if desired)\n• Design review/brainstorm (if desired)\n\nCompetencies\n• Backend\n• Understanding of relational databases\n• GraphQL\n• Python/Flask\n• AWS Lambdas\n• Basics of testing: e2e, integration, unit\n• Frontend\n• React\n• React Native\n• GraphQL\n• Frontend Testing\n\nSkills & Experience\n• You have relevant experience You have 2-5 years of experience at a relevant tech, product-driven company. Ideally with 1-2 years of experience in an early-stage startup (Seed, Series A).\n• You truly believe in our mission You believe moving is a significant moment in a person’s life and believe we can make the moving experience great.\n• You are curious and empathetic You always aim to understand the full picture from the customer’s point of view. You’re willing to challenge your understanding of this every day to improve it.\n• You embrace change You understand that change is the only constant in a startup. You are excited to propose and lead change when you have a better way.\n\nOur Tech Stack\n• React and React Native client apps built with an Apollo GraphQL data layer, Styled Components for styling our UI, and hooks for handling modals, responsiveness, navigation, and more.\n• Together with our design team, we have built a shared design system used in all client applications.\n• Flask backend with a performant GraphQL layer built with Graphene.\n• Redis for async task handling and working with external systems.\n• Infrastructure is all on AWS with usage of Lambdas, ECS, and Dynamo.\n• We have a CI/CD pipeline that enables us to test every pull request and deploy multiple times per day.\n• Our processes include using Notion, Slack, Zoom, and GitHub for all communication.\n\nWhy this role\n• Large amount of ownership within the first 3 months of joining. You’ll be able to jump into projects within your first 30 days, and own several features by the end of your 90 days.\n• Modern tech stack: Python/JS with React, React Native, GraphQL, Flask, Postgres, AWS (Lambdas, ECS, Dynamo).\n• Fast iteration cycles. We build and launch our features behind flags. This enables us to deploy multiple times a day without disruption to other engineers on the team.\n• Strong engineering backgrounds: Work with bright engineers from Asana, Facebook, Pinterest.\n\nAdditional Perks & Benefits:\n\nMarket comp, medical, vision, dental.\n\nProvide direct input to overall company strategy.\n\nTimeline:\n\nWe move at super speed with a simple four step process.\n\nPhone screen, CTO & Hiring Manager Interview, Technical Interview, and then a three hour virtual final round interview with the founders and future team members.\n\nPay Range:\n\nSoftware Engineer I: $90,000 USD – $140,000 USD\n\nSoftware Engineer II: $120,000 USD – $170,000 USD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'graphql,customer,usd,moving,000 usd,000,customers,believe,lambdas,built,early,day,quickly,problems,react react,way,change,build,react native,software engineer,flask,react,components,software,design'),(293,'jsearch','DGbxxmEOG8mRsO-XAAAAAA==','Senior Engineer, IT - Software Engineering & Development HQ IT-Application Services','Builders FirstSource',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dailyremote.com/remote-job/senior-engineer-it-software-engineering-development-hq-it-application-services-4976445','We are Builders FirstSource, America’s largest supplier of building materials, value-added components and building services to the professional market. You’ll feel proud of the work you do here every day to transform the future of home building and help make the dream of home ownership more achievable. At BFS, we believe building a successful career is not solely defined by a degree. Your experience, skills, and passion are just as important, if not more so. As such, we are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace that welcomes candidates from all backgrounds and experience levels.\n\nPURPOSE\n\nRole Summary\n\nThe Senior Software Engineer – AI is responsible for designing, building, and scaling AI‑enabled solutions that improve engineering productivity, business processes, and customer outcomes. This role focuses on applied AI—integrating large language models (LLMs), machine learning services, and automation into enterprise systems—while maintaining strong software engineering fundamentals.\n\nThis engineer works closely with the Business stakeholders, Architecture, Security, Infrastructure, Application Support to deliver secure, scalable, and maintainable AI solutions aligned with enterprise standards.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nAI & Intelligent Systems Development\n• Design and develop AI‑enabled applications using LLMs, ML services, and intelligent automation\n• Integrate AI capabilities into existing enterprise platforms, workflows, and APIs\n• Build prompt strategies, orchestration layers, and retrieval‑augmented generation (RAG) pipelines\n• Evaluate and improve model outputs for accuracy, reliability, and performance\n• Implement AI guardrails including logging, auditing, and response validation\n\nSoftware Engineering Excellence\n• Design and develop well‑architected, testable, and scalable software solutions\n• Apply engineering best practices across design, development, code reviews, and CI/CD\n• Ensure solutions meet security, compliance, and performance standards\n• Write clean, maintainable code using modern programming languages and frameworks\n• Troubleshoot production issues across AI and non‑AI components\n\nCollaboration & Leadership\n• Partner with product owners, architects, and stakeholders to translate business needs into technical solutions\n• Provide technical mentorship and guidance to other engineers\n• Participate in design reviews and contribute to engineering standards and best practices\n• Lead by example in responsible, ethical AI usage\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\nEducation & Experience\n• Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Engineering, or equivalent practical experience\n• 5+ years of software engineering experience\n• 2+ years of hands‑on experience with AI/ML or LLM‑based solutions\n\nTechnical Skills\n• Experience with modern programming languages (e.g., Python, Java, C#, or similar)\n• Experience integrating AI/ML services, including LLM APIs (Azure OpenAI, OpenAI, etc.)\n• Hands‑on experience with:\n• Cloud platforms (Copilot, Microsoft Foundry and Azure strongly preferred)\n• REST / event‑driven APIs\n• CI/CD pipelines and version control\n• Solid understanding of:\n• Software architecture and design patterns\n• Data structures, algorithms, and system performance\n• Secure coding practices\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Experience building enterprise AI tools (developer productivity, workflow automation, decision support)\n• Experience with RAG architecture, vector databases, and embeddings\n• Knowledge of AI governance, data privacy, and responsible AI principles\n• Experience with observability tools, monitoring, and performance tuning for AI workloads\n• Behavioral Competencies\n• Strong problem‑solving and analytical skills\n• Ability to balance innovation with operational stability\n• Comfortable operating in ambiguity and rapidly evolving technology areas\n• Clear, concise communicator with technical and non‑technical audiences\n• Demonstrated ownership, accountability, and engineering judgment\n\nBusiness and Financial Acumen\n• Demonstrates depth of understanding for the P&L and financial analysis\n• Teaches business and financial acumen to others.\n• Understands KPIs and how BFS makes money.\n• Knows the different business segments and how they relate to one another.\n• Understands customer sales and engagement.\n• Demonstrates functional and/or technical expertise.\n• Understands complex issues and demonstrates problem solving skills.\n• Understands how to maximize business results regardless of industry cycle.\n\nResults Driven\n• Holds self and others accountable.\n• Communicates and sets clear goals with plans to deliver.\n• Manages competing priorities effectively.\n• Demonstrates appropriate urgency.\n• Drives to exceed expectations in alignment with our BFS SPICE values.\n• Embraces and follows best practices.\n• Demonstrates self-starter, can-do attitude.\n\nStrategic Thinking and Decision Making\n• Leverages resources and teams around them to solve problems and create mutually beneficial outcomes.\n• Demonstrates willingness and courage to make tough decisions in a timely manner.\n• Balances short-and-long term priorities\n• Demonstrates proactive versus reactive thinking.\n• Asks questions to identify root cause and analyze situations more accurately.\n\nServant Leadership\n• Demonstrates humility by putting others first.\n• Builds trust-based relationships.\n• Leads by example with kindness and respect.\n• Collaborates well across all areas of the business.\n• Advocates for others\n• Actively listens to understand the meaning and intent of what the other person is communicating.\n• Demonstrates authenticity and encourages others to do the same.\n\nEmotional Intelligence\n• Demonstrates situational awareness – knows when and how to adjust leadership style in different situations.\n• Demonstrates self-awareness – understands strengths and weaknesses.\n• Demonstrates empathy – puts themselves in other’s shoes.\n• Assumes positive intent.\n\nDevelops and Leads Others\n• Drives alignment through clear communication of vision, goals and expectations.\n• Invests time on a regular basis in performance feedback and developmental conversations.\n• Fosters a respectful and inclusive environment.\n• Empowers, motivates, and inspires others.\n• Coaches and mentors others for their development.\n• Guides and persuades others to deliver positive outcomes.\n\nGrowth Mindset\n• Demonstrates a growth mindset; takes appropriate risks, fails fast and forward, learns from mistakes.\n• Perseveres and champions growth, even in the face of resistance, ambiguity, or possible failure.\n• Thinks like an owner with an entrepreneurial spirit.\n• Demonstrates and encourages intellectual curiosity.\n• Continuous learner; seeks opportunities and knowledge for personal and professional growth.\n• Sees possibilities over problems – actively seeks solutions.\n\nInnovation\n• Encourages out-of-the box thinking to create new ways of doing things.\n• Continuously seeks to improve and simplify pain points in the business.\n• Anticipates, embraces, and leads change.\n• Develops and executes breakthrough strategies.\n\nIntegrity\n• Does the right thing even under challenging circumstances?\n• Communicates with honesty.\n• Consistently treats others fairly and equitably.\n• Demonstrates reliability and does what they say they will do.\n• Conducts tough conversations and delivers difficult messages with kindness and respect.\n\nWORK ENVIRONMENT / PHYSICAL ACTIVITY\n\nThe physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n• Work is in an office setting and generally sedentary with physical effort associated with using a computer but may involve walking or standing for brief periods of time.\n• May be required to occasionally lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects up to 25 pounds.\n• Ability to travel up to 40% during the multi-year business transformation, will likely shift down to 20% after initial business transformation is complete.\n\nThis position was posted on May 7, 2026 and we anticipate it will be open for a minimum of five days, though it may be open for a longer period. We encourage your prompt application.\n\nSuccessful, innovative, and fulfilling careers are built here, and your professional development is a high priority. We invest in your future through the latest training, tools, and technologies. Highly collaborative, we work together to solve problems and find better ways to continually grow our business and careers every day. You’ll be empowered to try new things, gain new experiences, and build a career with unlimited horizons. The scale and depth of resources that being the #1 building materials distributor in the nation provides a variety of opportunities for you to explore – all in a friendly, people-first environment. Join us to be more, do more, and build more, together at BFS.\n\nIn addition to the base wage listed, this position is also eligible to earn an annual bonus subject to changes in plan design and documents and in accordance with applicable law. Eligibility and the amount of the bonus varies based on overall company success, thresholds met and other terms and conditions of the Company’s active bonus policy for the respective year.\n\nAt Builders FirstSource, we offer competitive, affordable benefits designed to make life better for you and the people you love. Our goal is simple — provide great plans that help you and your family to live happier, healthier and more secure lives. This role is eligible for medical, dental, vision, and disability insurance plans, 401(k) retirement savings plan, PTO (including paid sick time), and 8 paid holidays per year (for salaried and hourly team members). Details about Builders FirstSource’s benefits offerings are available here www.bldrbenefits.com.\n\nBuilders FirstSource is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, protected veteran status or status as an individual with a disability.\n\nIn compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Builders FirstSource, please call (214) 765-3990 or email: ADA.Accommodation@bldr.com. Please do not send resumes to this email address - it is intended only to be used to request an accommodation in submitting an application for a job opening.\n\nIf there\'s legally required pay transparency information missing from our job posting, it\'s not intentional and we\'d like to know. To let us know, please email the job title and location to JobPostings@bldr.com. Please do not send resumes to this email address - it is intended only be used to provide a notice of non-compliance.\n\nPlease note that due to the volume of applications received, we are unable to respond to individual inquiries about the status of your application.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'demonstrates,ai,business,builders,firstsource,builders firstsource,understands,engineering,bfs,experience,building,email,enterprise,services,seeks,encourages,accommodation,ml,solutions,software engineering,application,software,compliance,physical,financial'),(294,'jsearch','ll8KfP1sQ943OpxcAAAAAA==','Graduate Software Engineer, Open Source and Linux, Canonical Ubuntu','Canonical',NULL,NULL,0,'https://canonical.com/careers/7814327','Canonical is a leading provider of open source software and operating systems to the global enterprise and technology markets. Our platform, Ubuntu, is very widely used in breakthrough enterprise initiatives such as public cloud, data science, AI, engineering innovation, and IoT. Our customers include the world\'s leading public cloud and silicon providers, and industry leaders in many sectors. The company is a pioneer of global distributed collaboration, with 1200+ colleagues in 75+ countries and very few office-based roles. Teams meet two to four times yearly in person, in interesting locations around the world, to align on strategy and execution.\n\nThe company is founder led, profitable and growing.\n\nWe are hiring 2025 and 2026 Graduate Software Engineers into engineering teams around the world. As a global platform company we offer a wide range of software engineering challenges, in both open source products and commercial business systems. We have teams that work in a variety of languages, typically Python, Golang, Rust, C/C++, JavaScript and of course... Bash. We work from the very lowest levels of the Linux system - BIOS and boot loaders, firmware, kernel and drivers, all the way up to desktop applications and containers. We work on tiny devices like the Raspberry Pi and new RISC-V boards, all the way up to supercomputers, clouds and Kubernetes clusters. We work on compilers and toolchains, and we work on security, cryptography, performance and documentation. Some of our teams focus on packaging thousands of pieces of software, others focus on deep contributions to a single body of code.\n\nIf you are excited about the potential that open source has for humanity and the enterprise, you have outstanding results in your academic career, and you are excited to contribute to the open source stack, this is the best way to apply to Canonical. We will work with you to identify teams and projects that would be interesting and a good fit for your skills and motivations. The process is highly competitive, it will require effort and excellence to succeed if you apply here.\n\nMost of our engineering teams work from home. We try to align a single team in a single time zone - EMEA (Europe, Middle East and Africa), APAC (Asia Pacific and Indian Ocean), and AMER (North, South and Central Americas). Even though you work from home, we try to ensure you always have colleagues alongside to coach and mentor you, and for the companionship of shared problem solving and pair programming. Larger projects have multiple teams and might span the globe. We work with the open source community and specialize in building teams that work well in the \'fishbowl\' of open source engineering. This is full time work, five days a week, often solving hard problems with significant responsibility. We don\'t generally work weekends and nights and we do enjoy good holidays but we also expect productive and intense engagement Monday to Friday.\n\nWe bring all our engineering teams together in person twice a year for a deep \'sprint\' with other teams to stimulate discussion and enable a wide range of career development paths. This is a fantastic way to demonstrate and develop your skill in software, learn about a wide range of technologies, make a meaningful impact to open source, and see some very interesting new cities that you might never otherwise get to visit.\n\nIf you find the open source stack amazing, and you have been a consistent high-performing student in your school and university, then this will be a challenging and exciting start to your career.\n\nLocation: This is a Globally remote role.\n\nThe role entails\n• Shaping the roadmap for your product at global sprints every six months\n• Focusing on design and user experience, even for developer tooling and command line apps\n• Writing high quality, resilient and performant code, potentially serving millions of demanding daily users\n• Working towards mastery of key programming languages and Linux system knowledge\n• Engaging with users and the open source community through code reviews and issue trackers\n• Responding to customer issues as a priority, develop an understanding of enterprise requirements\n• Developing skills and awareness of security in software design and implementation\n\nWhat we are looking for in you\n• Exceptional academic track record from both high school and university\n• Undergraduate degree in Computer Science, Business Informatics, Mathematics or another STEM discipline with programming courses\n• Confidence to get started and deliver high quality code in one of Python, Rust, C/C++, Golang, JavaScript or Java\n• Experience with Ubuntu or another Linux distribution\n• Track record of going above-and-beyond expectations to achieve outstanding results\n• Result-oriented and organized, with the drive to meet commitments\n• Personal projects in technology and software engineering beyond the curriculum\n• Professional written and spoken English\n• Excellent interpersonal skills, curiosity, flexibility, and accountability\n• Personal responsibility and accountability\n• Thoughtfulness, self-awareness and the ability to reflect and develop\n• Ability to travel internationally twice a year for company events up to two weeks long\n\nNice-to-have skills\n• Upstream open source contributions\n• Packaging and Linux distribution contributions - Debian, Fedora, Arch, Nix or another\n• Leadership and organization skills\n• Presentation and writing skills\n• Business and commercial interests\n\nWhat we offer colleagues\n\nWe consider geographical location, experience, and performance in shaping compensation worldwide. We revisit compensation annually (and more often for graduates and associates) to ensure we recognize outstanding performance. In addition to base pay, we offer a performance-driven annual bonus or commission. We provide all team members with additional benefits which reflect our values and ideals. We balance our programs to meet local needs and ensure fairness globally.\n• Distributed work environment with twice-yearly team sprints in person\n• Personal learning and development budget of USD 2,000 per year\n• Annual compensation review\n• Recognition rewards\n• Annual holiday leave\n• Maternity and paternity leave\n• Team Member Assistance Program & Wellness Platform\n• Opportunity to travel to new locations to meet colleagues\n• Priority Pass and travel upgrades for long-haul company events\n\nAbout Canonical\n\nCanonical is a pioneering tech firm at the forefront of the global move to open source. As the company that publishes Ubuntu, one of the most important open source projects and the platform for AI, IoT and the cloud, we are changing the world of software. We recruit on a global basis and set a very high standard for people joining the company. We expect excellence - in order to succeed, we need to be the best at what we do. Most colleagues at Canonical have worked from home since its inception in 2004.​ Working here is a step into the future, and will challenge you to think differently, work smarter, learn new skills, and raise your game.\n\nCanonical is an equal opportunity employer\n\nWe are proud to foster a workplace free from discrimination. Diversity of experience, perspectives, and background create a better work environment and better products. Whatever your identity, we will give your application fair consideration.\n\n#LI-remote\n\nRequisition ID: 1339',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'open source,source,open,canonical,teams,work,global,linux,ubuntu,colleagues,software,company,engineering,enterprise,meet,wide,interesting,single,engineering teams,outstanding,teams work,wide range,twice,way,range'),(295,'jsearch','Nx2IRtaA_aZfgMiDAAAAAA==','Remote Software Developer (Entry-Level & Experienced)','The Elite Job',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/14067/remote-software-developer-entry-level-experienced','Job Summary\n\nThe Elite Job is seeking passionate and driven Remote Software Developers to join our innovative tech team. Whether you are an entry-level developer or an experienced professional, this role offers you the opportunity to work on cutting-edge projects that impact millions of users worldwide. As a Remote Software Developer, you will collaborate with a talented and diverse team, designing, coding, testing, and deploying software solutions that drive business success. This is a fully remote position, allowing you to work from anywhere while delivering high-quality software solutions.\nKey Responsibilities\n• *\n\nDesign, develop, and maintain web applications and software solutions to meet business needs.\n• *\n\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to gather and define technical requirements.\n• *\n\nWrite clean, efficient, and maintainable code.\n• *\n\nConduct thorough testing and debugging to ensure the quality and performance of the software.\n• *\n\nParticipate in code reviews and provide constructive feedback to colleagues.\n• *\n\nKeep up to date with industry trends, new technologies, and best practices.\n• *\n\nTroubleshoot, optimize, and enhance existing software solutions.\n• *\n\nContribute to the overall development process, including planning, design, testing, and deployment.\n• *\n\nWork with agile development methodologies to ensure timely delivery of projects.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• *\n\nStrong knowledge of at least one programming language (e.g., Python, Java, C++, JavaScript, or similar).\n• *\n\nUnderstanding of web development technologies (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, etc.).\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with databases (SQL, NoSQL) and version control systems (Git).\n• *\n\nStrong problem-solving and debugging skills.\n• *\n\nAbility to write clean, reusable, and maintainable code.\n• *\n\nExcellent communication skills, with the ability to work effectively in a remote team environment.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with Agile methodologies and development tools (e.g., Jira, Trello, etc.).\n• *\n\nWillingness to learn and grow in the field of software development.\n• *\n\nA portfolio or previous work examples (preferred for entry-level candidates).\n• Experience\n• *\n\nEntry-Level Candidates:\n• *\n\n0-2 years of experience in software development or related field.\n• *\n\nRecent graduates with strong coding knowledge are encouraged to apply.\n• *\n• Experienced Candidates:\n• *\n\n2+ years of professional experience in software development.\n• *\n\nProven experience with software development, debugging, and problem-solving.\n• *\n\nExperience with remote work environments and collaborating with distributed teams is a plus.\n• *\nWorking Hours\n• *\n\nFlexible working hours with the possibility to create your own schedule.\n• *\n\nFull-time and part-time positions available.\n• *\n\nMust be able to attend regular virtual team meetings (schedules vary by team).\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nStrong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively in a remote environment.\n• *\n\nAttention to detail and an ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines effectively.\n• *\n\nKnowledge of modern software development tools and practices.\n• *\n\nAbility to adapt to new technologies quickly and effectively.\n• *\n\nStrong analytical and critical thinking skills.\n• *\n\nExcellent problem-solving abilities and the ability to troubleshoot software issues efficiently.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary with performance-based bonuses.\n• *\n\nHealth insurance (for full-time employees).\n• *\n\nFlexible working hours and the ability to work remotely from anywhere.\n• *\n\nProfessional development opportunities, including access to online learning platforms.\n• *\n\nPaid time off and holidays.\n• *\n\nCollaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Why Join The Elite Job?\n\nAt The Elite Job, we pride ourselves on creating a culture of innovation, collaboration, and growth. Joining our team means being part of an organization that values continuous learning, creative thinking, and career development. We offer a unique opportunity to work on impactful projects while maintaining a healthy work-life balance. Whether you are an entry-level or experienced developer, you will have the opportunity to grow in a supportive, fully remote environment.\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply, please send your updated resume, a cover letter detailing your experience, and any relevant work samples (if applicable) to us. Be sure to include a brief explanation of why you are interested in working with The Elite Job and how your skills make you a great fit for the role. We look forward to hearing from you!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','software,entry,entry level,development,work,ability,level,elite job,elite,remote,experienced,skills,software solutions,remote software,software development,job,experience software,skills ability,level experienced,level candidates,working hours,experience,team,strong,developer'),(296,'jsearch','hiYNUbgyYwpVo1dLAAAAAA==','Full Stack Developer (.NET Core & Angular)','Latino Legends',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dailyremote.com/remote-full-stack-developer-jobs-in-saint-lucia','Build and maintain backend services using .NET Core and optimize SQL data performance for a multi-tenant SaaS platform. Collaborate with a distributed team to develop API integrations and support Angular-based frontend features.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'net core,angular,net,core,develop api,data performance,core optimize,tenant saas,tenant,team develop,sql data,platform collaborate,collaborate distributed,based frontend,platform,core angular,angular build,multi,optimize sql,saas platform,performance multi,angular based,support angular,integrations support,stack developer'),(297,'jsearch','F8DDZw4FWOnzoi9yAAAAAA==','Curriculum Developer II / Instructional Developer II','All Native Group',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dailyremote.com/remote-job/curriculum-developer-ii-instructional-developer-ii-4983221','Summary\n\nBear Mountain Services, a division of All Native Group and Ho Chunk, Incorporated, is seeking an exceptional Curriculum Developer II / Instructional Developer II to independently develop and revise Navy training materials in support of CTC courseware modernization and sustainment efforts.\n\nEssential Functions\n• Assist with development and revision of lesson plans, trainee guides, assessments, and presentation materials.\n• Format products using approved templates, style guides, and authoring tools.\n• Incorporate Government review comments and directed edits.\n• Support OMS repositories, file naming conventions, and version control logs.\n• Conduct proofreading, hyperlink checks, and quality control reviews.\n\nCompetencies\n• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills\n• Demonstrated experience creating assessments\n• Excellent writing, proofreading and design skills to develop training course materials\n• Must possess excellent written and spoken use of the English language\n• Strong interpersonal and organizational skills; and attention to detail\n• Must be proficient in the use of Microsoft Office Suite (MS Word, PowerPoint and Excel)\n• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills\n• Superior organizational skills with a high level of attention to detail\n• Ability to follow technical direction\n• Ability to interact effectively in a multicultural setting\n• Excellent customer service skills\n• Ability to work effectively on a team with colleagues in various employment categories such as active duty military, civil service government employees and other contract employees\n\nSupervisory Responsibility\n\nNone for this position\n\nWork Environment\n\nThis job operates in executive settings with frequent engagement at the highest levels of Navy leadership. This role uses executive office equipment and classified communication systems.\n\nPhysical Demands\n\nThe physical demands are typical of executive positions, with extensive travel and high-stress decision-making requirements. While performing the duties of this job, the employee is regularly required to talk or hear.\n\nPosition Type/Expected Hours of Work\n\nThis is a full-time executive position with flexible hours based on mission requirements.\n\nTravel\n\nTravel is primarily local during the business day, although some out of the area travel and overnight may be expected\n\nExperience\n\nThree to five years Navy curriculum development experience.\n\nEducation\n\nBachelor’s degree in Education, Training, Instructional Design, or related field; equivalent experience may be considered.\n\nAdditional Eligibility Qualifications\n\nNone for this role\n\nDrug Free Workplace\n\nAll Native Group is a Drug Free Workplace. It is our policy that all new hires must successfully complete a pre-employment drug screen as a condition of employment. In addition, all employees are subject to random drug screens throughout the term of their employment with All Native Group.\n\nSecurity Clearance\n\nMust be a U.S. citizen.\n\nAAP/EEO Statement \n\nAll Native Group is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. However, preference may be extended to persons of Indian descent in accordance with applicable laws.\n\nAbout Ho-Chunk, Inc. & All Native Group\n\nHo-Chunk, Inc. is an award-winning economic development corporation of the Winnebago Tribe of Nebraska. Our mission is to provide long-term economic development for the Winnebago Tribe and job opportunities for Tribal members.\n\nAll Native Group is a network of small businesses that support the critical missions of various U.S. Government customers. Our capabilities include telecommunications, health, logistics, specialized training, professional services, and IT solutions. Since earning our first federal contract in 2004, we have continued to grow and diversify our services while maintaining a strong commitment to excellence. As a tribally owned organization, All Native Group operates multiple subsidiary businesses, providing clients with the advantages of working with a small business while leveraging the resources and expertise of a larger, established company. Our work is guided by our core NATIVE values:\n• Native American Owned & Proud – Serving the Winnebago Tribe of Nebraska.\n• Accountable – To always do what’s right.\n• Team-Focused – For inclusive progress.\n• Innovative – In creating solutions.\n• Visionary – In our purpose and direction.\n• Excellence – Through learning and performance.\n\nOther Duties\n\nPlease note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'group,native group,native,executive,developer ii,drug,employment,duties,ii,training,travel,tribe,instructional,winnebago,navy,chunk,winnebago tribe,ho,ho chunk,government,materials,curriculum,job,employees,skills'),(298,'jsearch','jKx8kMWMvpa-OXsKAAAAAA==','Mobile Full Stack, Software Engineer - Equity Opportunity - PINION - The Civic Engagement Platform','PINION',NULL,NULL,0,'https://wellfound.com/jobs/1867561-mobile-full-stack-software-engineer-equity-opportunity-pinion-the-civic-engagement-platform','SOCIAL IMPACT OPPORTUNITY WITH GLOBAL REACH!\n\nThis is a significant opportunity for an experienced technology development professional interested in joining an early-stage startup aiming to transform civic engagement, democracy and politics around the world.\n\nWe\'ve been working on something with potential for significant social impact. Our MVP is almost ready to pilot. We\'re looking to hire a savvy mobile technical professional to join our development team.\n\nPINION - Tinder for Politics meets WIkipedia for Public Opinion About Pinion (https://www.pinionvote.com/): Civic engagement is way too hard. Pinion is a new platform and community where you can easily find and vote on legislation/topics you care about at local, state national and global levels. Easily Share your \"Pinion\" to social media if you like or remain private, view results, and track your representatives to see how well they are representing your interests - plus compare candidates running to replace them in the next election so you can see \"who is voting with me\".\n\nOur tag line, \"Tinder for politics meets Wikipedia for public opinion\" describes our vision. When we share our idea most people say \"I can\'t believe this doesn\'t already exist\". We agree and take this opportunity seriously - intending to create a successful new platform and public benefit corporation dedicated to improving civic engagement, democracy and the nature of our politics.\n\nAbout the position - Pinion is creating a user oriented, interactive environment that utilizes our innovative user engagement mechanism. Our goal is to make the mobile version of this environment available in the 1st half of 2025. We are seeking an experienced mobile engineer to take our existing app and focus on its compatibilty and usability on mobile devices.\n\nAn ideal candidate for this position will be comfortable working in a remote startup environment. A self-motivated team player who works well with other team members and can adapt to fast-changing environments will thrive. You should reliably have available bandwidth to be able to communicate with teammates and work on development tasks.\n\nResponsibilities and Duties\n• Transition our existing environment to a \"mobile forward\" environment\n• Preserve existing functionality on Web App and transfer it to Mobile environment.\n• Be familiar with React, Node, and mobile native technologies.\n• Work with the analytics and front-end team as necessary to enable new functionality.\n• Consistently take on and complete work assignments in reasonable time frames.\n• Participate in governance and review (Workflow staging, QA/QC, documentation, etc)\n\nQualifications\n• Significant experience working with relational / SQL databases.\n• Must have a good experience level with a mix of our core environment: Linux, React, SQL Server, Entity Framework. Node.js.\n• Experience with Client-side and Server-side Development\n• Good team player and willingness to engage with teammates, get to know them and create a collaborative working environment.\n• Available bandwidth - We understand life that happens, jobs change, families require time and we expect to accommodate this but you should expect to consistently contribute at least 10 hours per week, with more welcome.\n\nCompensation - Please Note: We are a true early stage start up (pre-funding/pre-revenue) and all working for future equity only (no salaries yet) using the Slicing Pie methodology (www.slicingpie.com) to fairly allocate equity in the company. This role is intended to grow into a full-time salary+bonus+equity position in the future as we gain funding and revenues. Also, Angel List requires that this post be classified as a \"Cofounder\" in order to post on the site. While you will be part of our founding team, this is NOT a legal employment offer for a \"cofounder role\" - all of our team members are on contractor work agreements. Finally - this is a flexible fully remote position. An ideal candidate should be self-sufficient, with the bandwidth to reliably contribute, interested in our technology and mission, and comfortable with our early stage, “boot strapping” startup status.\n\nIf all that sounds like a match please apply here on WellFound. We try to look at all applications promptly and reach out to set up an introductory meeting to share what we\'re doing and help you understand if we\'re a good fit for your talents.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'mobile,pinion,civic,civic engagement,equity,politics,engagement,environment,bandwidth,social,public,early stage,early,stage,team,good,significant,working,startup,share,position,reliably,funding,easily,public opinion'),(299,'jsearch','RIcrUY8KqHEAet8XAAAAAA==','Growth Engineer','Metanomaly',NULL,'JP',0,'https://japan-dev.com/jobs/metanomaly/metanomaly-growth-engineer-saozy2','What you’ll do\n• Rapidly design and implement lightweight technical solutions to test growth and product hypotheses in user-facing flows\n• Hack together and ship frontend-driven experiments and features that improve activation, conversion, or engagement\n• Implement A/B tests and instrumentation pragmatically, optimizing for learning speed while maintaining experiment validity\n• Iterate aggressively based on results, user feedback, and constraints, prioritizing impact over elegance when appropriate\n\nRequirements\n• Strong frontend engineering skills, with clear ownership of user-facing features and product UI quality\n• Strong at implementing backend logic and API integrations, as needed.\n• Able to turn vague growth ideas into concrete, shippable technical solutions\n• Solid intuition for user behavior, funnels, and friction in real products\n• Data-literate: can write basic SQL to sanity-check outcomes and guide iteration\n• Bias toward speed and impact over perfect architecture\n\nExperience\n• 3–5+ years of experience building and iterating on products used by real users\n• Proven experience shipping frontend features used by real users, with iteration based on feedback or data‘\n• Hands-on experience running A/B tests (or similar product experiments) and iterating in a data‑driven way\n• Professional experience with B2C / consumer‑facing products\n• Experience with product iteration, growth-related work, or independent app development is a strong plus\n\nEducation\n• Bachelor’s degree or above. Practical skills, judgment, and shipped work matter more than formal credentials.\n\nNice to have\n• Interest in anime, otaku culture, creator communities, or related consumer products.\n• Interest in AI generation\n\nNote:\n\nIf you\'ve read this, please tell us the names of your top 5 favorite niche anime at the end of your message.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'products,iteration,facing,user,frontend,product,growth,real users,anime,consumer,tests,iterating,used real,experience,features,experiments,user facing,real,speed,implement,technical solutions,users,used,data,related'),(300,'jsearch','6pst5aNdj36REmvCAAAAAA==','Senior Full-stack Developer','Lemon.io',NULL,NULL,0,'https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/lemon-io-senior-full-stack-developer-8','Are you a talented Senior Developer looking for a remote job that lets you show your skills and get decent compensation? Look no further than Lemon.io — the marketplace that connects you with hand-picked startups in the US and Europe.\n\nWhat we offer:\n• The rate depends on your seniority level, skills and experience. We\'ve already paid out over $11M to our engineers.\n• No more hunting for clients or negotiating rates — let us handle the business side of things so you can focus on what you do best.\n• We\'ll manually find the best project for you according to your skills and preferences.\n• Choose a schedule that works best for you. It’s possible to communicate async or minimally overlap within team working hours.\n• We respect your seniority so you can expect no micromanagement or screen trackers.\n• Communicate directly with the clients. Most of them have technical backgrounds. Sounds good, yeah?\n• We will support you from the time you submit the application throughout all cooperation stages.\n• Most of our projects involve working in a fast-paced startup environment. We hope you like it as much as we do.\n• Through our community, we will connect you with the best developers from more than 71 countries.\n\nWe have several open positions for Full-Stack React.js Developers - please see the details below. We also have some backend positions; the full list is included below as well.\n\nRequirements for the Senior React & Python Position:\n• 4+ years of software development experience\n\nCommercial experience:\n• React.js 3+ years and Python 3+ years OR React.js 2+ years and Python 5+ years OR React.js 5+ years and Python 2+ years\n• Experience with AWS, GCP, or Azure is required\n\nRequirements for the Senior Python Position:\n• 5+ years of software development experience\n• 5+ years of commercial experience with Python\n• 3+ years of commercial experience with Flask\n\nRequirements for the Senior Golang & React Position:\n• 4+ years of software development experience\n• React.js 3+ years and Golang 3+ years OR React.js 2+ years and Golang 5+ years OR React.js 5+ years and Golang 2+ years\n\nRequirements for the Senior Golang Position:\n• 5+ years of software development experience\n• 5+ years of commercial experience with Golang\n\nRequirements for the Senior Node & React Position:\n• 5+ years of software development experience\n\nCommercial experience:\n• React.js: 3+ years, Node.js: 5+ years, and Next.js: 2+ years OR React.js: 5+ years, Node.js: 3+ years, and Next.js: 2+ years\n• Expertise in TypeScript, Supabase and AWS is a must.\n\nOther requirements:\n• Strong technical skills: as a Senior Developer, you are expected to be able to create projects from scratch and have a deep understanding of application architecture.\n• Clear and effective communication in English — advanced ability to discuss business tasks, justify decisions, and communicate issues. Good self-presentation is also essential for upcoming client calls.\n• Strong self-organizational skills — ability to work full-time remotely with no supervision.\n• Reliability — we want to trust you and expect that you won’t let us and the client down.\n• Adaptability and Flexibility — the ability to onboard the project promptly after accepting it and start delivering results quickly.\n\nSounds good for you? Apply now and join the Lemon.io community!\n\nNOT YOUR TECH STACK?\n\nWe have multiple projects available for Senior Developers. If you have 4+ years of commercial software development experience and are proficient in any of the following areas: React & Ruby, PHP & Angular, PHP & Vue, Vue & Node.js, React & .NET, Android & iOS, Angular & .NET, Angular & Node.js, Vue & .NET, Python & Vue, MLOps, React & Java, Data Science, Blockchain (Web3/Solidity/Solana), Symfony & React, Symfony & Vue, Symfony & Angular, Symfony & JavaScript & Next.js & TypeScript, Data Analysis, React & PHP, Data Engineering, AI Engineering, Data Annotation, DevOps, Svelte & Python, Svelte & Node, Svelte & TypeScript, Rust, Shopify & JavaScript, Vue & Nuxt, Python & Node, Angular & TypeScript, Ruby & Ruby on Rails, React Native & Ruby, React Native & Python, PHP & Laravel, .NET & C#, Java & Spring, Unreal Engine & C++, Python & LLM, Unity, Machine Learning Engineering — we’d be happy to connect and match you with a suitable project.\n\nIf your experience matches our requirements, be ready for the next steps:\n• VideoAsk — watch a short video about our startup, up to 10 minutes\n• Complete your profile on our website\n• Screening call\n• Technical interview\n• Feedback\n• Magic Box (we are looking for the best project for you).\n\nWe do not provide visa assistance, and our cooperation model does not include the benefits typically offered with direct hire.\n\nP.S. We work with developers from 71+ countries in different regions: Europe, LATAM, the U.S (if you are an owner of W-9 ben form), Canada, Asia (Japan, Singapore, South Korea, Philippines, Indonesia), Oceania (Australia, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea), and the the UK. However, we have some exceptions.\n\nAt the moment, we don’t have a legal basis to accept applicants from the following countries:\n• European: Hungary, Iceland, Liechtenstein, Kosovo, Belarus, Russia, and Serbia.\n• Latin America: Cuba and Nicaragua\n• Most Asian countries and Africa.\n\nWe expand and shorten the list of exemptions regularly.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'years,js years,react,python,js,react js,senior,golang,commercial,development experience,experience,years software,commercial experience,years react,position years,requirements senior,requirements,countries,years commercial,python years,php,symfony,vue,software development,node'),(301,'jsearch','8fJAMLBRkVpttScgAAAAAA==','Remote .NET Developer (Part-time)','HR Service Jobs',NULL,'CA',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/8402/remote-.net-developer-part-time','Job Summary\n\nHR Service Jobs is seeking a talented and motivated Remote .NET Developer to join our innovative SaaS startup team. As a key member of our development team, you will be responsible for building and maintaining high-quality software solutions that enhance our HR service offerings. This part-time position allows for flexible work hours while contributing to a dynamic, collaborative environment focused on delivering exceptional value to our clients.\nKey Responsibilities\n• * Develop, test, and deploy robust .NET applications to support various HR service functionalities.\n• * Collaborate with cross-functional teams to gather requirements and translate them into technical specifications.\n• * Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize existing applications for improved performance and scalability.\n• * Write clean, maintainable code following best practices and industry standards.\n• * Participate in code reviews and provide constructive feedback to peers.\n• * Stay updated on the latest .NET technologies and industry trends to continually enhance our development processes.\n• * Assist in the documentation of software specifications, user guides, and technical processes.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• * Proficient in .NET Framework and .NET Core with a strong understanding of C# programming language.\n• * Experience with front-end technologies such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript frameworks (e.g., React, Angular).\n• * Familiarity with database systems (e.g., SQL Server, MySQL) and ORM technologies (e.g., Entity Framework).\n• * Understanding of RESTful APIs and web services integration.\n• * Knowledge of version control systems (e.g., Git) and Agile development methodologies.\n• * Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to work independently in a remote setting.\n• Experience\n• * Minimum of 2 years of professional experience in .NET development.\n• * Proven track record of successfully delivering software projects on time and within budget.\n• * Experience in the HR or SaaS industry is a plus but not required.\n• Working Hours\n• * This is a part-time remote position, requiring approximately 20-25 hours per week.\n• * Flexible scheduling is available, allowing you to balance work with other commitments.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• * Strong analytical and debugging skills with attention to detail.\n• * Excellent verbal and written communication skills.\n• * Ability to work collaboratively in a team-oriented environment.\n• * Self-motivated and proactive in identifying areas for improvement.\n• Benefits\n• * Competitive hourly rate with opportunities for performance-based bonuses.\n• * Flexible work schedule to accommodate personal commitments.\n• * Professional development opportunities to enhance your skills and career growth.\n• * A supportive and inclusive work environment that values diversity and innovation.\n• Why Join\n\nAt HR Service Jobs, we believe in fostering a culture of creativity and collaboration. As a part of our team, you will have the chance to work on cutting-edge projects that make a real impact on the HR industry. Join us in our mission to revolutionize HR services and be part of a supportive community that values your contributions.\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and skills. Please send your application to us with the subject line Remote .NET Developer Application. We look forward to reviewing your application and potentially welcoming you to our team!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','hr,net,hr service,net developer,remote net,service,enhance,skills,work,remote,service jobs,specifications,industry,development,team,flexible work,commitments,hours,application,flexible,experience,framework,jobs,motivated,saas'),(302,'jsearch','EotqKNEvYXRhl-62AAAAAA==','Software Engineer, DevOps (Azure)','Upstart 13',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dailyremote.com/remote-job/software-engineer-dev-ops-azure-4957589','Calling All Upstarters!\n\nAZURE DEVOPS WANTED!\n\nWe are Upstart 13. We are humble, hungry, and competent people who are radically changing the expectations and experience of outsourcing for all participants by challenging barriers that create inequality and by bringing down borders in technology for people everywhere. We’re all about delivering value and doing big things. We have become a game changer for teams around the world who look to Upstart’s services as a differentiator.\n\nJob Description:\n\nWe are seeking a DevOps/Cloud Engineer located in Latam to own the full lifecycle of our Azure production environment and provide expert support to our development teams. You will be responsible for designing, building, and operating a secure, scalable infrastructure using Bicep for IaC and managing complex services like AKS, APIM, and Event Hubs. This role focuses on ensuring operational excellence, high availability, and seamless CI/CD integration to enable fast and safe application delivery.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Infrastructure as Code: Design and maintain production-grade Azure infrastructure using Bicep, ensuring all resources from networking to application services are managed as code.\n• Application Delivery & Networking: Implement and manage Azure API Management (APIM), Azure App Gateway, and Azure Front Door to ensure secure, scalable, and high-performance application delivery.\n• Container Orchestration: Deploy and operate containerized workloads on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS), including cluster optimization, Helm chart management, and advanced networking configurations.\n• Event-Driven Architecture: Support and manage Azure Event Hubs with Kafka protocol support for real-time data streaming and event-driven microservices.\n• Develop end-to-end YAML pipelines in Azure DevOps for automated provisioning and application deployment, integrating gates and automated testing.\n• Production Operations: Own the reliability of the Azure environment by monitoring health via Azure Monitor and Application Insights, leading incident response, and performing Root Cause Analysis (RCA).\n• Security & Identity: Enforce Azure Security services, including Entra ID (Azure AD) RBAC, Managed Identities, Azure Key Vault for secrets, and Azure Policy for governance and compliance.\n• Developer Enablement: Collaborate with developers to integrate code into pipelines, manage Git branching strategies, and provide mentorship on cloud-native best practices.\n• Managing all required environments: Primary Environment (Production) and Secondary Environments (Non-Prod).\n\nQualifications\n\nTechnical skills:\n• 5+ years of professional experience in DevOps and Cloud Engineering within the Microsoft Azure ecosystem.\n• Expertise in Azure Core Services: Deep knowledge of VNets, NSGs, Load Balancers, and Storage (Blob/Files).\n• Hands-on with Bicep: Proven ability to build modular, reusable Infrastructure as Code patterns.\n• Advanced Azure Services: Practical experience managing Azure APIM, Azure App Gateway, and Azure Event Hubs (Kafka).\n• Kubernetes Proficiency: Experience running AKS in production, including node pool optimization and pod autoscaling.\n• Security Mindset: Strong experience with Azure Security Center, vulnerability scanning (SAST/DAST), and container registry security (ACR).\n• Automation: Proficiency in PowerShell, Azure CLI, and Python for creating operational tools and self-service platforms.\n\nSoft skills:\n• Excellent problem-solving skills, ownership, and ability to work independently.\n• Excellent communication and collaboration skills with a desire to learn and teach.\n• Excellent understanding of development processes and agile methodologies.\n• Analytic, flexible, adaptative, highly motivated, and able to learn quickly.\n\nBonus skills:\n• Azure certifications such as AZ-400 (DevOps Engineer Expert) or AZ-305 (Solutions Architect).\n• Experience with GitOps (Flux/ArgoCD) and Kubernetes service meshes (Istio).\n• Knowledge of FinOps for cloud cost management and resource optimization.\n\nWhy Upstart13?\n• We put people first at Upstart 13! We believe the world is filled with amazing people and we are willing to go to great lengths to seek out others who share our values to join our cause of bringing down borders in technology for people everywhere.\n• We develop leaders at Upstart 13, we focus on what matters to do meaningful work, we own our shit, we stay curious, and we understand responsibility leads to giving. We do big things together!\n\nPerks:\n• Job type: long-term, full-time job.\n• Fully remote.\n• USD competitive salary.\n• 20+ Paid time off days.\n\nAre you ready to join our cause? Be sure to ask, “why 13?”',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'azure,devops,13,upstart,event,production,services,application,security,management,event hubs,managing,bicep,upstart 13,application delivery,hubs,aks,apim,infrastructure,people,cloud,cause,optimization,kubernetes,manage'),(303,'jsearch','agORJ6wbeud6_eUlAAAAAA==','Angular Software Developer – Bogotá, Colombia / Medellin','CaseWare',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/colombia-medellin-software-angular-developer-at-caseware','Caseware is one of Canada’s original Fintech companies, having led the global audit and accounting software industry for over 30 years, with more than 500,000 users across 130 countries and available in 16 different languages. While you might not have heard of us (yet) over 36,000 accounting and audit professionals list Caseware as a skill on their LinkedIn profiles!\n\nWe seek a skilled Angular Developer to join our team and work on the front end of our cloud-based platform. As an Angular Developer, you will be responsible for developing and implementing user interfaces and enhancing the user experience of our platform. You will work with senior developers to build an intuitive and efficient leading-edge cloud auditing software solution where we add new features in an agile environment to support clear product direction.\n\nContact:\n\nMaira Russo – Senior Talent Acquisition Partner\n\nWhat you will be doing\n• Work in an agile team with other developers, UX developers, testers, and product owners to build innovative, high-quality, user-friendly features\n• Develop user interfaces for our cloud-based platform using Angular and Typescript\n• Participate in the design discussions around the majority of features your team undertakes\n• You will own features from design through to implementation\n• Troubleshoot and debug technical issues as they arise\n• Participate in code reviewing other developers’ work to ensure code quality, share knowledge and provide mentorship\n• Research and explore new technologies, code libraries, and products we may wish to integrate.\n\nWhat you will bring to the team\n• 3+ years web and enterprise development experience\n• Experience with Angular\n• Strong knowledge of HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript\n• B. Sc. in Computer Science or equivalent education/work experience\n• Strong English language communication and collaboration skills\n\nNice to have\n• Experience working in an Agile environment\n• Experience working with other front-end frameworks\n• Full-stack development experience\n• Understanding of Accounting or Auditing concepts\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Contrato a termino Indefinido with all the legal benefits\n• Prepaid Medicine\n• Life insurance and funeral assistance\n• Internet allowance\n• Home office stipend\n• Competitive compensation — above the market average\n• 100% remote work environment and an excellent work-life balance\n• Opportunity to work for a growing global SaaS leader company\n• A culture that promotes independence, innovation, trust, and accountability\n• Open space to be creative, innovative, and strategize for the future\n• Mentorship by a highly experienced professional\n• Budget for training, we want you to grow\n• 5 Personal Time Off days per year\n• Sick Leave Top up to total 100% of salary paid by the employer from Day 3 to 90.\n• Recognition Award, additional paid time off in recognition of the corresponding year of service\n• Upgrade vacation starting at 5 years of service\n\nWhat’s in it for you:\n\n▪️Innovation is at our core. We work with cutting-edge technology in accounting and financial reporting, constantly pushing the boundaries to create impactful software solutions.\n\n▪️We are committed to a collaborative culture, where your ideas are valued, and knowledge sharing is encouraged within a supportive, inclusive team.\n\n▪️Work-life balance is important to us. We offer flexible work options, remote opportunities, and generous time-off policies to ensure a healthy work-life balance.\n\n▪️We offer competitive compensation, including a competitive salary and comprehensive benefits such as health insurance and retirement plans.\n\n▪️We are driven by impactful work. Your contributions directly affect how our clients manage financial processes and drive their success.\n\n▪️Recognition and rewards matter to us. We celebrate hard work through recognition programs, performance bonuses, and opportunities for career growth.\n\n▪️We embrace global opportunities. Work on international projects and collaborate with a diverse, global team.\n\nAbout Caseware:\n\nCaseware’s cutting-edge software products are meticulously designed for accounting firms, corporations, and governments. Our teams are continually collaborating, innovating, and building upon our existing suite of products. With a customer-focused mindset, we are building technology that is shaping what the future of audits, financial reporting, and financial data analytics will look like.\n\nWith a recent strategic investment from Hg Capital in 2020, Caseware is now in its next major growth phase as we double down on the people and products that have made Caseware so successful to date.\n\nOne of Caseware’s core values is Many Voices, One Team and with that in mind, we’re dedicated to building teams as diverse as our customers in an equitable and inclusive way. We welcome and encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Should you require accommodations or have any questions at any point during the application or interview process, please e-mail our People Operations team at talent@caseware.com.\n\nBackground Check:\n\nAny candidates successful in obtaining an offer for a position will need to successfully complete a background check through https://certn.co which typically includes an Identity Verification and Criminal Record Check. Executives and Senior Managers will undergo a Soft Credit Check as well. Candidates residing in the Netherlands and Germany are excluded from undergoing background checks via https://certn.co\n\nSecurity and Fraud:\n\nCaseware takes the security of candidates seriously. All legitimate communication from us will come from email addresses ending in @https://www.caseware.com and our open positions are always listed on reputable job boards and on our website . We will NEVER ask for payment or financial information from you. If you receive an unsolicited job offer, proceed with extreme caution.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'caseware,accounting,work,financial,angular,check,recognition,global,developers,team,products,life balance,https,life,features,user,offer,work life,background,experience,candidates,edge,agile,reporting,based platform'),(304,'jsearch','Rn-sYwEJmgLyMa-BAAAAAA==','Software Engineer Trainee - Freshers','The Elite Job',NULL,'CA',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/3198/software-engineer-trainee-freshers','Are you a recent graduate with a passion for software development? Are you ready to embark on an exciting career journey with one of the leading names in the industry? The Elite Job is seeking enthusiastic and dedicated individuals to join our team as Software Engineer Trainees.\n\nResponsibilities:\n• * Collaborate with senior engineers to develop high-quality software solutions\n• * Participate in the complete software development lifecycle, from concept and design to testing and deployment\n• * Write clean, efficient, and maintainable code\n• * Debug and troubleshoot software issues\n• * Stay updated with the latest industry trends and technologies\n• Required Skills:To thrive in this role, you should possess the following skills:\n• * Strong programming fundamentals in languages such as Java, Python, or C++\n• * Solid understanding of software development principles\n• * Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment\n• * Eagerness to learn and adapt to new technologies\n• * Excellent problem-solving and analytical skills\n• Qualifications:\n• * Bachelor degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field\n• * Relevant internships or project experience is a plus\n• How to Apply: If you are ready to kickstart your career in software engineering with a forward-thinking company, please submit your resume, cover letter, and any relevant portfolio or project work to us.\n\nPerks and Benefits:\n• * Competitive salary\n• * Comprehensive health and wellness programs\n• * Opportunities for professional development and career advancement\n• * Collaborative and inclusive work environment\n• Join The Elite Job, where innovation meets opportunity!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','software,ready,career,development,elite,elite job,software development,project,software engineer,industry,skills,relevant,work,field relevant,following skills,plus apply,engineer trainee,freshers,freshers recent,fundamentals languages,graduate,internships project,engineer trainees,experience plus,graduate passion'),(305,'jsearch','HPSPzwCQ2Uu6TRf0AAAAAA==','SW Dev Eng 6, Prin','Lattice Semiconductor',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dailyremote.com/remote-job/sw-dev-eng-6-prin-4894915','Lattice Overview\nThere is energy here…energy you can feel crackling at any of our international locations. It’s an energy generated by enthusiasm for our work, for our teams, for our results, and for our customers. Lattice is a worldwide community of engineers, designers, and manufacturing operations specialists in partnership with world-class sales, marketing, and support teams, who are developing programmable logic solutions that are changing the industry. Our focus is on R&D, product innovation, and customer service, and to that focus, we bring total commitment and a keenly sharp competitive personality. Energy feeds on energy. If you flourish in a fast paced, results-oriented environment, if you want to achieve individual success within a “team first” organization, and if you believe you can contribute and succeed in a demanding yet collegial atmosphere, then Lattice may well be just what you’re looking for.\nResponsibilities & Skills\n\nThis role is to progress the deployment of a ‘model first’ development model to Hardware Design. In this role you will be architecting and developing complex C++ and SystemC models of hardware solutions. As an expert in the space, acting as a leader and mentor to other engineers less versed with this style of development. This will also involve developing Firmware and other Software, including QEMU emulation to generate both model solutions and Firmware development platforms.\n\nLattice is seeking candidates for the position of Software Development Engineer. This is a full time remote position.\n\nAccountabilities:\n• Contribute as a member of the Architecture modelling team, developing and validating models under senior guidance\n• Develop, debug, and troubleshoot models in SystemC and Firmware\n• Develop, debug python code to process models\n• Apply firmware development experience to support model-driven design flows\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to improve development methodologies and processes\n\nQualifications:\n• BS/MS Electrical Engineering or Computer Science\n• 5–10 years of experience in firmware or embedded software development\n• Proficient with C/C++ in embedded or hardware-adjacent environments\n• Knowledge of FPGA logic design or hardware description concepts preferred\n• Solid foundation in object-oriented programming, data structures, and algorithms\n• Experience with SystemC, QEMU, or hardware modeling is a plus but not required — we will train the right candidate\n• Must possess independent problem-solving skills and a willingness to learn new methodologies\n• Knowledge of Python is preferred\n• Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work across multiple teams',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'energy,hardware,firmware,lattice,models,model,developing,systemc,development,develop debug,embedded,qemu,firmware development,teams,logic,preferred,methodologies,debug,software development,design,solutions,focus,results,oriented,software'),(306,'jsearch','Cp2XxhlMfSMkxRL1AAAAAA==','Senior Android Developer for Sport Team','GR8 Tech',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dailyremote.com/remote-job/senior-android-developer-for-sport-team-4929494','GR8 Tech builds B2B iGaming platforms for operators who play to lead.\n\nWe deliver full-cycle, high-impact tech designed to scale — from seamless integrations and expert consulting to long-term operational support. Our platform powers millions of active players and drives real business growth. Call it what it is: the iGaming Platform for Champions.\n\nWith 1000+ GR8 people across locations and time zones, we don’t just ship technology — we help operators build success stories across brands, markets, and geos.\n\nOur ambition drives us. Our people make it real.\n\nIf you’re a challenger in spirit and a champion in action — join us.\n\nWhy this role exists:\n\nThis role exists to build and scale a high-quality Android experience for our core products. You’ll help us deliver fast, stable, and secure mobile solutions by owning architecture decisions, improving system resilience, and driving engineering excellence across the Android domain.\n\nWhat you’ll drive:\n\nStrategy & outcomes\n• Own Android architecture decisions and long-term technical direction.\n• Improve app performance, stability, and scalability.\n• Drive adoption of modern Android practices (Compose, Coroutines, clean architecture).\n• Identify and reduce technical debt in critical areas.\n• Define and track key engineering quality metrics.\n\nDiscovery & decisions\n• Translate product requirements into scalable technical solutions.\n• Evaluate trade-offs between speed, quality, and complexity.\n• Validate architecture approaches through prototypes and experiments.\n• Contribute to system design across mobile and backend boundaries.\n\nDelivery & execution\n• Build and ship high-quality features end-to-end.\n• Optimize networking, storage, and app performance.\n• Ensure reliable background processing and lifecycle handling.\n• Maintain clean, testable, and maintainable code.\n• Improve CI/CD and release processes.\n\nStakeholder & cross-team collaboration\n• Partner closely with Product, Design, and Backend teams.\n• Align on API contracts and system behavior.\n• Communicate technical decisions clearly to non-technical stakeholders.\n• Contribute to engineering culture and standards.\n\nLeadership & mentorship\n• Mentor junior and middle engineers.\n• Lead code reviews and knowledge sharing.\n• Raise the bar for engineering quality and ownership.\n• Help scale team practices as the product grows.\n\nWhat makes you a GR8 fit\n\nMust-have\n• Strong experience with Android development (Kotlin).\n• Deep understanding of Android SDK, app lifecycle, and system behavior.\n• Hands-on experience with Jetpack Compose.\n• Experience with modern Android stack (Coroutines, Flow).\n• Solid understanding of architecture patterns (MVVM / MVI / Clean Architecture).\n• Experience with networking (Retrofit, OkHttp) and API design.\n• Strong knowledge of multithreading, concurrency, and performance optimization.\n\nNice-to-have\n• Experience with large-scale or high-load mobile apps.\n• Knowledge of security best practices (auth, encryption, data protection).\n• Experience with CI/CD and DevOps practices.\n• Familiarity with backend or cloud architecture.\n• Experience with WebSocket or real-time data handling.\n• Experience mentoring engineers or leading initiatives.\n\nWhy you’ll love working here:\n\nBenefits Cafeteria — annual budget you allocate to:\n\nSports • Medical • Mental health • Home office • Languages.\n\nWork-life & support\n• Paid maternity/paternity leave + monthly childcare allowance.\n• 20+ vacation days, unlimited sick leave, emergency time off.\n• Remote-first + tech support + coworking compensation.\n• Team events (online/offline/offsite).\n• Learning culture with internal courses + growth programs.\n\nOur culture & core values:\n\nGR8 Tech culture is how we win — through trust, ownership, and a growth mindset. We move fast, stay curious, and keep it real, with open feedback, room to experiment, and a team that’s got your back.\n\nFUELLED BY TRUST: we’re open, honest, and have each other’s backs.\n\nOWN YOUR GAME: we take initiative and own what we do.\n\nACCELER8: we move fast, focus smart, and keep it simple.\n\nCHALLENGE ACCEPTED: we grow through challenges and stay curious.\n\nBULLETPROOF: we’re resilient, ready, and always have a plan.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'android,gr8,architecture,decisions,scale,experience,mobile,quality,tech,culture,practices,real,app,help,operators,clean architecture,compose,app performance,engineering quality,exists,role exists,architecture decisions,coroutines,modern android,gr8 tech'),(307,'jsearch','rVTprK44HElKt0ssAAAAAA==','Software Engineer - Internship (Remote)','The Elite Job',NULL,'ID',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/5260/software-engineer-internship-remote','The Elite Job is a leading provider of innovative software solutions, dedicated to pushing the boundaries of technology and fostering a culture of continuous learning and growth. As a forward-thinking company, we prioritize creativity, collaboration, and excellence in everything we do.\n\nJob Title: Software Engineer - Internship (Remote)\n\nJob Summary: Join The Elite Job as a Software Engineering Intern and immerse yourself in a dynamic learning environment where you will contribute to cutting-edge projects and gain hands-on experience in software development. This remote internship offers a unique opportunity to work closely with our experienced team members and make meaningful contributions to real-world projects.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• * Collaborate with team members to design, develop, and maintain software solutions\n• * Assist in troubleshooting, debugging, and resolving technical issues\n• * Contribute to the planning and execution of software development tasks\n• * Stay updated on emerging technologies and industry trends\n• * Communicate effectively with team members to ensure project alignment and success\n• Required Skills and Qualifications:\n• * Pursuing a degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field\n• * Strong understanding of software development fundamentals and best practices\n• * Proficiency in one or more programming languages such as Python, Java, C++, etc.\n• * Familiarity with version control systems (e.g., Git)\n• * Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail\n• * Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a remote team environment\n• Experience:\n• * Previous internship or project experience in software development is a plus but not required\n• Working Hours:\n• * Flexible working hours to accommodate academic schedules and time zone differences\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n• * Strong analytical and critical thinking skills\n• * Effective communication and interpersonal skills\n• * Eagerness to learn and adapt to new technologies\n• * Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment\n• Benefits:\n• * Hands-on experience working on real-world projects\n• * Mentorship and guidance from experienced professionals\n• * Flexible remote work environment\n• * Opportunities for professional development and networking\n• * Competitive compensation package\n• Why Join The Elite Job:\n• * Be part of a vibrant and innovative team driving technological advancements\n• * Gain valuable industry experience and expand your skill set\n• * Contribute to impactful projects that make a difference\n• * Join a company culture that values creativity, collaboration, and personal growth\n• How to Apply: Interested candidates should submit their resume and cover letter via The Elite Job Careers Page. Be sure to highlight relevant coursework, projects, and experiences that demonstrate your qualifications for the role. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','internship,software,elite job,elite,job,projects,software development,remote,world projects,internship remote,engineer internship,team members,skills,members,team,development,creativity,creativity collaboration,real world,experience software,experience,contribute,project,dynamic,gain'),(308,'jsearch','q5b-vi_nMm2zM3KZAAAAAA==','Back-End Developer – Join and Grow with Us!','OnTheGoSystems',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/back-end-developer-join-grow-at-onthegosystems','Join our fully remote team and work on a mass-market SaaS product that reaches millions globally. Whether you’re a RoR and React expert or a talented developer eager to learn, we’re interested in you!\n\nWe Value:\n• Smart problem-solvers: Your experience counts, but your ability to learn and tackle challenges matters most.\n• Resourcefulness: You find ways to get things done.\n• Drive: You aim high and don’t settle.\n• Creativity: You bring new ideas to the table.\n• Team spirit: Collaborating and sharing knowledge is second nature to you.\n• Love for learning: You’re always expanding your horizons.\n\nMust-have Experience:\n• Software development (3+ years)\n• Intensive database work\n• Writing automated tests\n• Developing widely-used systems\n• Proficiency in version control\n\nWhat We Offer:\n• Remote Flexibility: Work from anywhere in European, Middle Eastern, or African time zones.\n• Agile Environment: Small teams, short sprints, and supportive daily interactions.\n• Continuous Learning: Get up to speed on RoR, React, and more on the job.\n• Full-Stack Engagement: Contribute to all aspects from backend to front-end.\n• Leadership Opportunities: Rotate as a scrum master within months.\n\nTimezone Alignment\n\nClose collaboration is key. We prefer developers within European, Middle Eastern, or African time zones but are flexible for outstanding candidates willing to adapt to these hours.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'african time,eastern,eastern african,ror react,middle eastern,middle,ror,african,european middle,time zones,zones,european,learn,work,end,matters resourcefulness,flexible outstanding,zones agile,expert talented,expert,experience software,experience counts,expanding horizons,smart problem,job stack'),(309,'jsearch','FlepZRIN9NNKv261AAAAAA==','Senior Backend Engineer — Microservices; Remote','InnovationTeam','Riyadh','SA',0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5084802214/e/','Position: Senior Backend Engineer — Microservices (Remote)\nInnovation Team in Saudi Arabia is looking for a skilled Senior Backend Developer focused on Microservices architecture. The role requires at least 5 years of experience in software development, proficiency in Java, Python, or Node.js, and strong knowledge of RESTful APIs. Responsibilities include participating in all software development phases, collaborating with frontend developers, and conducting code reviews. This position offers benefits like private health insurance, remote work options, and opportunities for professional development.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'senior backend,senior,engineer microservices,microservices remote,microservices,backend engineer,software development,engineer,development,phases,looking skilled,insurance remote,remote innovation,phases collaborating,innovation team,include participating,private,participating software,focused microservices,developer focused,saudi arabia,saudi,collaborating frontend,development proficiency,development phases'),(310,'jsearch','xehkYXPG0VvubWEVAAAAAA==','Remote Backend Developer Jobs in Kingston','Cosmoquick','Kingston','JM',0,'https://cosmoquick.com/remote-jobs-in/kingston/remote-backend-developer','Find remote Backend Developer positions with Kingston employers. 3-8 years in backend development with expertise in building scalable systems',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'remote backend,kingston,backend developer,backend,employers,developer positions,employers years,jobs kingston,kingston remote,kingston employers,scalable systems,expertise building,positions kingston,positions,developer jobs,building scalable,development expertise,backend development,developer,jobs,remote,building,systems,expertise,scalable'),(311,'jsearch','Q6uWcrFTTetwqqYKAAAAAA==','Backend Java Developer – Fully Remote','MNC JOBS INFO',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/16962/backend-java-developer-%E2%80%93-fully-remote','Job Summary\n\nMNC Jobs Info is seeking a highly skilled and detail-oriented Backend Java Developer to join our growing remote engineering team. In this role, you will play a vital part in building robust, scalable, and high-performance backend services that power our digital platforms and enterprise solutions. This is an excellent opportunity for someone with a strong background in Java and backend technologies to thrive in a collaborative, forward-thinking remote environment.\nKey Responsibilities\n• *\n\nDesign, develop, and maintain scalable backend services using Java and Spring Boot frameworks.\n• *\n\nCollaborate with front-end developers, DevOps engineers, and product managers to deliver high-quality software solutions.\n• *\n\nImplement RESTful APIs, microservices, and data processing pipelines.\n• *\n\nWrite clean, efficient, and well-documented code that follows software engineering best practices.\n• *\n\nTroubleshoot and debug issues across multiple systems and environments.\n• *\n\nParticipate in code reviews, technical discussions, and sprint planning meetings.\n• *\n\nOptimize application performance and ensure system reliability and security.\n• *\n\nStay up to date with the latest industry trends and technologies related to backend development.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• *\n\nStrong programming skills in Java (Java 8 or above).\n• *\n\nHands-on experience with Spring Framework (Spring Boot, Spring MVC, Spring Data).\n• *\n\nSolid understanding of RESTful API design and integration.\n• *\n\nExperience with relational databases like MySQL, PostgreSQL, or Oracle.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with version control systems such as Git.\n• *\n\nKnowledge of containerization tools like Docker is a plus.\n• *\n\nUnderstanding of software development life cycle (SDLC) and Agile methodologies.\n• *\n\nExcellent problem-solving, analytical, and communication skills.\n• Experience\n• *\n\n3+ years of professional experience as a Java Backend Developer or similar role.\n• *\n\nProven track record of working on production-grade backend systems.\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFull-time position\n• *\n\nFlexible working hours with core collaboration time between 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM IST\n• *\n\nFully remote (Work from anywhere)\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nStrong foundation in object-oriented programming and data structures.\n• *\n\nAbility to write reusable, testable, and efficient code.\n• *\n\nComfortable working in a distributed team setup.\n• *\n\nSelf-motivated with the ability to manage tasks independently.\n• *\n\nStrong organizational and time management abilities.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary based on experience and skills.\n• *\n\n100% Remote work flexibility.\n• *\n\nWork-life balance with flexible schedules.\n• *\n\nPaid time off and national holidays.\n• *\n\nLearning and development programs.\n• *\n\nCollaborative and inclusive team culture.\n• *\n\nOpportunity to work on cutting-edge technologies and international projects.\n• Why Join MNC Jobs Info?\n\nAt MNC Jobs Info, we value innovation, teamwork, and integrity. You will work with some of the most talented professionals in the industry in an environment that encourages growth, creativity, and ownership. Join a forward-thinking company where your skills and contributions will make a real impact. Whether you are looking for technical challenges or a flexible remote setup, we provide the tools and culture to help you succeed.\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are passionate about backend development and ready to take on exciting challenges from the comfort of your home, we want to hear from you!\n? Apply now by sending your updated resume to us with the subject line: Application for Backend Java Developer – Remote.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','java,spring,info,mnc,backend java,mnc jobs,jobs info,backend,jobs,java developer,skills,remote,00,working,data,oriented,java backend,industry,experience,time,flexible,work,setup,boot,forward thinking'),(312,'jsearch','MXOU_JSwdSvHWYIxAAAAAA==','Experienced Backend Developer (Laravel/Vue)','NERIS Analytics Limited',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/laravel-developer-experienced-vue-at-neris-analytics','TL;DR:\n• Position: Experienced Laravel dev (5+ years) who can also navigate a Vue 3 frontend when needed.\n• Project: Stable, long-term, fully remote.\n• Hours: Ideally full-time, but part-time can work too.\n• Compensation: $60k-$90k/year or around $50/hour (negotiable, heavily dependent on skills & experience).\n• Why Join: You’ll help modernize and expand a platform (16Personalities) that has already impacted hundreds of millions of people.\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\nImprove Testing & Modernize Legacy Code\n• Increase test coverage (currently using PHPUnit; open to alternatives).\n• Refactor older Laravel code to align with modern best practices and the L11 structure.\n• Integrate robust testing into our deployment pipelines.\n\nBuild New Features\n• Develop new functionality rapidly while maintaining clean, maintainable code.\n• Optimize database queries and cache strategies.\n• Collaborate closely with the team to ensure smooth feature rollouts.\n\nDive into the Full Stack (When Needed)\n• Primary focus: Laravel backend.\n• Occasionally jump into the Vue 3 frontend to debug or confirm data flow.\n• You should be comfortable switching contexts to ensure end-to-end coherence.\n\nEmbrace AI Tools\n• Explore how AI can speed up your own development or test writing.\n• Assist with separate mini-projects involving AI model querying, message batching, output processing etc.\n\nWho You Are\n\nSeasoned Laravel Dev\n• 5+ years of practical Laravel experience.\n• Well-versed in the latest Laravel versions, writing elegant, clear, performant code.\n\nSome Vue 3 Knowledge\n• At least a couple of years using Vue 2/3.\n• Able to navigate frontend components as needed (no design work, just enough to fix issues or align data).\n\nIndependent & Reliable\n• Fully remote means you’re responsible for your schedule.\n• Deliver on time without needing constant follow-ups.\n• Communicate clearly, keep the team in the loop, and “own your st.”\n\nAgile & Curious\n• Thrive in a fast-paced, evolving environment.\n• Take pride in your work; constantly seek ways to improve the code and test coverage.\n\nFun to Work With\n• You’re intellectually honest, and you can argue your viewpoint while staying open to others.\n• You have a sense of humor and a life outside of code.\n\nWhat We Offer\n\nRemote Setup\n• Work from anywhere, on your own schedule.\n• Join a small, friendly, and driven team that values creativity and independence.\n\nFair Compensation\n• $60k–$90k/year salary range (negotiable based on your skill set, plus any rarer expertise you bring).\n• Part-time is around $50/hour.\n• If you’re exceptional, we’re open to discussing more.\n\nMeaningful Work\n• We’ve helped hundreds of millions of people understand themselves better over the past 10+ years.\n• What you do won’t be lost in yet another short-lived startup idea – your work will have a real, lasting impact.\n\nCreative Autonomy\n• Operate in a quality-first, agile environment with freedom to innovate.\n• Room to propose and implement process improvements.\n\nPotential for Growth\n• We value learning and will happily consider new tools and methods you propose.\n• As we expand, so do opportunities for leadership or tackling more complex full-stack tasks.\n\nInterested? Please fill out so we can learn more about you.\n\nWhat to Expect Next:\n• We’ll review your application and reach out if it’s a good fit.\n• An initial chat to understand your experience and see if we mesh well.\n• Possibly a short technical interview or a quick code test.\n• A final talk about terms and next steps.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'laravel,code,test,vue,needed,work,frontend,code test,hundreds millions,60k,50 hour,negotiable,60k 90k,test coverage,modernize,vue frontend,dev,90k,hundreds,dev years,compensation 60k,90k year,laravel dev,millions people,time'),(313,'jsearch','827znUAXYXAvnrZYAAAAAA==','Backend Developer (Work from Home) - Top MNCs Hiring','Houston Skilled Consultancy',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/12804/backend-developer-work-from-home-top-mncs-hiring','Job Summary\n\nHouston Skilled Consultancy is hiring talented and motivated Backend Developers to work remotely for top multinational companies (MNCs). As a Backend Developer, you will be responsible for creating, optimizing, and maintaining server-side logic, database structures, and ensuring seamless integration with front-end technologies. This position is ideal for professionals passionate about backend development and looking to make a significant impact in a dynamic and collaborative environment.\nKey Responsibilities\n• * Develop, test, and maintain server-side applications and APIs for scalable, high-performing systems.\n• * Collaborate with front-end developers and designers to integrate user-facing elements with server-side logic.\n• * Design and implement secure, reliable, and efficient database solutions.\n• * Optimize applications for maximum speed, scalability, and efficiency.\n• * Debug and troubleshoot existing backend systems to resolve performance or security issues.\n• * Write clear, well-documented, and reusable code following best practices.\n• * Stay updated with the latest backend development trends, technologies, and tools.\n• * Ensure adherence to coding standards and participate in code reviews.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• * Proficiency in backend programming languages such as Python, Java, Ruby, PHP, Node.js, or Go.\n• * Hands-on experience with frameworks like Django, Express.js, Spring Boot, or similar.\n• * Solid understanding of RESTful API design and microservices architecture.\n• * Strong knowledge of relational databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL) and NoSQL databases (MongoDB, Cassandra).\n• * Familiarity with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud) and containerization tools (Docker, Kubernetes).\n• * Experience with version control systems (Git).\n• * Excellent problem-solving, debugging, and communication skills.\n• * A solid understanding of security best practices and data protection measures.\n• Experience\n• * 2+ years of experience in backend development or related roles.\n• * Prior experience working remotely or with distributed teams is a plus.\n• Working Hours\n• * Flexible working hours.\n• * Core hours may be required based on the client or project needs.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• * Ability to work independently and as part of a collaborative team.\n• * Strong analytical thinking and attention to detail.\n• * Eagerness to learn and adapt to new technologies and frameworks.\n• * Proactive attitude and commitment to delivering high-quality work.\n• Benefits\n• * Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• * Opportunity to work with top MNCs on diverse and innovative projects.\n• * Remote work flexibility for work-life balance.\n• * Professional growth and learning opportunities through training programs.\n• * Health and wellness benefits (depending on the clients package).\n• Why Join Houston Skilled Consultancy?\n\nAt Houston Skilled Consultancy, we connect skilled professionals with top-tier opportunities across the globe. As a Backend Developer, you will have the chance to work with cutting-edge technologies, collaborate with talented peers, and contribute to impactful projects. Join us to elevate your career while enjoying the benefits of a flexible and supportive work environment.\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to apply by sending their updated resume and a brief cover letter to us. Kindly include Backend Developer Application in the subject line.\n\nApplications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Apply today to secure your spot in a leading global company!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','mncs,backend,work,houston,consultancy,skilled consultancy,houston skilled,skilled,technologies,server,backend developer,backend development,hiring,experience,remotely,logic,server logic,applications,apply,secure,security,solid understanding,hours,developer,updated'),(315,'jsearch','wY09wC4lBMwAYHk6AAAAAA==','Java Backend Developer - AI-Powered APIs; Remote','YO IT Consulting',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5082634997/e/','Position: Java Backend Developer - AI-Powered APIs (Remote)\nYO IT Consulting is seeking an experienced Java Developer for a part-time remote role. The primary responsibilities include designing and optimizing backend APIs while collaborating with AI research teams. Candidates should have over 3 years of experience, strong expertise in RESTful and Graph\n\nQL APIs, and excellent communication skills. The position offers the chance to work in a dynamic environment, testing cutting-edge AI tools and contributing to developer workflows.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ai,apis remote,developer ai,ai powered,powered apis,powered,java backend,apis,java,developer,collaborating ai,consulting,consulting seeking,restful graph,optimizing backend,primary responsibilities,contributing developer,yo consulting,designing optimizing,position java,yo,graph ql,research teams,offers chance,developer workflows'),(316,'jsearch','UHHDjpCjff9lvyt3AAAAAA==','Full-Time Mid-Level Backend Web Developer','Arsenal Studio',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/backend-web-developer-at-arsenal-studio','Time zones: EST (UTC -5), CST (UTC -6), MST (UTC -7), PST (UTC -8), AST (UTC -4), NST (UTC -3:30)\n\nArsenal Studios is growing and we are seeking a Backend Web Developer for a full time opportunity. The immediate objective is to assist in development of websites, web apps and integrations for our rapidly growing custom web design and development business in collaboration with our with our in-house design, development and strategy teams. We are seeking a candidate to help create new solutions and improve / maintain existing solutions in support of long-term marketing campaigns.\n\nImportant: We are currently only able to hire US, Canadian, and Mexican residents. This is not a design position, though interest in interdisciplinary work will be supported and nurtured.\n\nIn this position, the selected candidate will be working with our in-house design, development and strategy teams to construct, customize and configure websites built in WordPress, HubSpot, and other Content Management systems as well as develop web applications using a multitude of different technologies as described below.\n\nAbout Working for Arsenal Studios\n\nArsenal Studios is an ethical digital marketing company working remotely since our inception. Since 2008, we have experienced growth and success due to our reputation for delivering the highest quality solutions by creating honest and collaborative relationships with our clients. We regularly work with the same client on a multitude of projects due to our depth of knowledge and problem-solving skills.\n\nCulture\n\nYou must be an honest, sincere, likable person and be adept at interacting with colleagues and clients through phone, email, video chat. Here are some values that we all share:\n• Passion for learning: You must possess the mindset of an autodidact and have a zeal for knowledge sharing.\n• Accountability: Our clients expect us to deliver on time and on budget as such we take our work seriously.\n• Teamwork: Our team is only as strong as its weakest link. We prop each other up whenever possible.\n• Agility: You will be working on a variety of projects for clients in varying industries and tech stacks.\n• Positivity: We laugh way more than we grumble. Negative Nellies step back.\n• Respect: We respect each other and our time by avoiding excessive meetings, and poorly defined requirements and by communicating proactively.\n• Acceptance: We accept each other as we are, and work together towards our common goals, leaving personal differences behind.\n\nRemote Workplace\n\nWe have been a fully remote workplace since our inception in 2008 and can hire candidates throughout North America. We work during regular East Coast business hours with some flexibility in start and end times if needed.\n\nRole & Requirements\n\nWe are seeking a Full-Time Remote Web Developer with a strong background in PHP and JavaScript. The ideal candidate will have a minimum of 2 years of professional web development experience and a passion for building maintainable and efficient web applications. Experience with Angular and/or NestJS is a bonus as is proficiency with CSS.If you are a proactive problem-solver with a keen eye for detail and the ability to work in a self-directed environment, we would love to hear from you.\n\nWe work as a team on multiple concurrent projects. Everyone meets together three times a week for stand-up style meetings with further breakout sessions as needed for specific projects. Once onboarding is complete you will be given coding assignments. Team members will be available for assistance and code review, but you will be expected to drive progress and communicate any needs efficiently.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Develop applications, APIs and other backend infrastructure using PHP and Javascript\n• Maintain existing web applications using PHP and JavaScript\n• Work on migrating older projects to modern infrastructure generally from PHP to JavaScript\n• Participate in designing new build tooling, automated test tooling, and workflows for building projects\n• Create custom marketing website functinality for our clients (typically by extending CMSs such as WordPress, Hubspot, Wagtail, etc.)\n• Write and maintain clean, maintainable, and efficient code\n• Write understandable and well organized documentation\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality and best practices both as reviewer and reviewee\n• Communicate effectively with team members on progress and priorities, including communication through Slack, video conferencing, and via project management tools\n\nQualifications:\n• Minimum of 2 years of professional experience in web development with a focus on PHP and backend JavaScript. More experience is also welcome, compensation will be commensurate with experience.\n• Very strong communication skills. The ability to provide clear updates on progress, challenges, and successes is crucial. Knowledge sharing is highly valued. Self-direction is a necessity as we are a small team. We all take responsibility for our own productivity.\n• Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail. You will have support from a very experienced team, but you are expected to solve problems with support.\n• Writing skills sufficient for writing clear comments in code, updates on progress, as well as internal documentation.\n• Familiarity with Git, Bash (or similar CLI), VS Code (or similar IDE).\n• Basic understanding of RESTful and other API design patterns.\n\nNice to Have\n\nExperience with the following technologies:\n• Angular and/or NestJS\n• Doctrine\n• WordPress theme development\n• Wagtail / Python / Django\n• Nodejs\n• API Design and development\n• Object-relational mapping (ORM) frameworks\n• Modern build tools i.e. WebPack or SnowPack\n• Building both web sites and web applications\n\nFamiliarity with:\n• HTML, CSS and frontend JS\n• SQL\n\nWhy We’re Awesome\n\nWe are a small, enthusiastic, and friendly team. We have amazing client and employee retention. We have some really unique and fun projects that may be unlike anything you have ever done before due to our roots in the education and nonprofit sectors.\n\nThis is a new, growth position. You will not be replacing anyone. We don’t hire often as our team is happy and stable, so this is a rare opportunity.\n\nAlso, in the intangible department, we are a friendly team that works closely together. We want the best for our employees. You will be treated with respect and your labor will not be abused. We truly care about the happiness and well-being of our team, and in turn, we all happily grow together.\n\nA Safe and Supportive Workplace\n\nCreating a diverse workplace has always been a priority at Arsenal Studios. As an agency delivering creative products for and marketing to a broad range of users, it is our responsibility to reflect our user base in our talent pool. Beyond that, we celebrate and encourage a workplace that is supportive of unique perspectives and backgrounds. We do not discriminate in any capacity including race, ethnicity, socioeconomic background, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, veteran status, religious belief, thought and opinion, professional aspirations, and more.\n\nCompensation & Benefits\n\nOne of the perks of being a small company is that we can tailor our benefits to your needs. We will offer a competitive salary for your region, we have high quality health insurance if you elect to participate, and you will get an annual tech fund to buy whatever you need, educate yourself, etc. Why don’t you just tell us what you want in your cover letter and we will work it out collaboratively? Maybe you want more vacation time in exchange for a little less pay or your partner already has health insurance for your family and you want more money instead. Just let us know! We want you to feel empowered and supported so that you stick around for a long time.\n• Competitive salary\n• 40 hrs / week with some flexibility in schedule\n• Fully remote\n• Supportive and inclusive culture\n• Parental leave\n• 25 days annual leave to start (2 weeks standard + 3 flex days + 12 bank holidays + additional paid vacation each year + negotiable additional time off)\n• Stipend for technology purchases / office supplies\n• Stipend for professional development & conferences\n• Quality health insurance with employer contribution (or additional compensation in lieu of health insurance)\n\nApplication Process\n\nApply\n\nIf this opportunity sounds like it is for you, please reply to the address below with cover letter and attached résumé and portfolio / or links to résumé / portfolio plus any questions you may have.\n\nReview & Code Screening\n\nWe will respond with initial follow-up questions and a take-home code challenge that should require 30 miniutes or less to complete. This will be your only code test / challenge in the interview process, and if we decide to advance you , we will even compensate you for the time spent on the challenge regardless of advancement beyond the second round. We require this challenge simply as a filter to avoid the various bots and scams that are all too common in the current job-search climate.\n\nInitial Meeting\n\nA brief meeting with leadership focused on culture and projects to make sure we are all happy with moving forward.\n\nDirect Report Interview\n\nMeet your direct reports: Dev leadership will provide you with a day-in-the-life, project previews and best-fit analysis based upon upcoming initiatives. We will ask you for code samples, project tours, and details related to your skillset.\n\nMeet Your Peers\n\nAll-hands virtual roundtable where you get to meet our entire team and ask / answer questions until everyone is happy.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'utc,web,workplace,studios,challenge,arsenal studios,php javascript,marketing,arsenal,code,time,design development,team,projects,progress,health insurance,insurance,php,small,questions,additional,want,development,work,clients'),(317,'jsearch','O-Y9Np0CZtggCif1AAAAAA==','Remote Backend Developer – Entry Level','Career.zycto',NULL,'GB',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/remote-backend-developer-entry-level/','About Company\n\nReady to launch your tech career with impact? Career.zycto is a dynamic, forward-thinking company dedicated to crafting innovative digital solutions. We thrive on fostering new talent, providing a supportive remote environment where fresh ideas are celebrated and growth is paramount. For an entry-level backend developer, we offer a unique platform for accelerated learning, mentorship, and the chance to contribute to real-world projects from day one. Join us and help shape the future of technology.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is seeking a passionate and driven Entry-Level Remote Backend Developer to join our growing team. This is an exceptional opportunity for an aspiring developer eager to kickstart their career in a supportive and innovative environment. While we\'re based in Oxted, Surrey, this role is fully remote, offering you the flexibility to work from anywhere in the UK. You will work closely with experienced developers, learning best practices in backend architecture, API design, database management, and server-side logic. We are committed to nurturing your skills through hands-on projects, code reviews, and dedicated mentorship, ensuring you develop a strong foundation in modern backend technologies.\n\nAs part of our team, you\'ll contribute to the development and maintenance of scalable and robust applications that power our cutting-edge services. You\'ll gain practical experience with various programming languages, frameworks, and tools, collaborating with front-end developers, product managers, and QA engineers to deliver high-quality software solutions. We believe in continuous learning and experimentation, encouraging you to bring your curiosity and problem-solving skills to the table. If you\'re looking for a place where you can make a tangible difference, grow rapidly, and be part of a vibrant remote culture, Career.zycto is the place for you. We value diversity, inclusivity, and a collaborative spirit, making sure every team member feels empowered and heard. Come grow with us!\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist in the development and maintenance of server-side logic, databases, and APIs under the guidance of senior developers.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and efficient code adhering to company standards and best practices.\n• Participate in code reviews, providing and receiving constructive feedback to improve code quality and learn new techniques.\n• Help debug and resolve technical issues, contributing to the overall stability and performance of our backend systems.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams (front-end, QA, product) to understand requirements and deliver integrated solutions.\n• Actively engage in learning new technologies, frameworks, and development methodologies.\n• Contribute to documentation of backend processes, APIs, and system architecture.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Foundational understanding of a backend programming language (e.g., Python, Node.js, Java, Ruby, Go, C#)\n• Basic knowledge of relational databases (e.g., SQL, PostgreSQL, MySQL) and database design principles.\n• Familiarity with version control systems, especially Git.\n• Understanding of fundamental web concepts (HTTP, RESTful APIs).\n• Strong problem-solving abilities and an eagerness to learn.\n• Excellent communication and collaboration skills for a remote work environment.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field (or equivalent practical experience/bootcamp completion).\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud) via personal projects or coursework.\n• Exposure to specific backend frameworks (e.g., Django, Flask, Express.js, Spring Boot, Ruby on Rails).\n• Experience with Docker or containerization technologies.\n• Completed personal coding projects demonstrating backend development skills.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Flexible remote work schedule.\n• Dedicated mentorship program with experienced developers.\n• Generous professional development budget for courses, certifications, and conferences.\n• Home office stipend to ensure a comfortable and productive setup.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits package.\n• Regular virtual team-building events and social gatherings.\n• Opportunity for rapid career progression within a growing company.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nEager to start your journey as a Backend Developer with Career.zycto? Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and a cover letter detailing why you\'re a great fit for this remote entry-level role. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'career,entry,entry level,career zycto,zycto,backend,level,mentorship,remote,company,dedicated,skills,place,providing,qa,experienced developers,development maintenance,dedicated mentorship,maintenance,developers,backend developer,projects,development,learning,frameworks'),(318,'jsearch','oFSODZcxPGbA1W5KAAAAAA==','Backend Platform Engineer - APIs & TTS; Remote','Clutch Canada',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/info_technology/5084806147/e/','Position: Backend Platform Engineer - APIs & TTS (Remote)\nClutch Canada is looking for a backend developer to join their Platform team. This role involves designing, developing, and maintaining robust APIs including payment, subscription, and consumption tracking. Ideal candidates will have proven experience with TS/Node and GCP, while knowledge of AWS or Azure is advantageous. The position offers a dynamic work environment with competitive compensation and flexibility. Join a team dedicated to transforming lives through innovative text-to-speech technology.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'platform,backend platform,tts remote,tts,apis tts,engineer apis,platform engineer,apis,engineer,candidates proven,remote clutch,clutch,clutch canada,compensation flexibility,competitive compensation,maintaining robust,lives innovative,payment subscription,including payment,consumption,robust apis,consumption tracking,payment,dynamic work,offers dynamic'),(319,'jsearch','3hwt4smZtZWFuilcAAAAAA==','Django Engineer: small team, real autonomy, Remote Job','Senturo',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dynamitejobs.com/company/senturo1/remote-job/django-engineer-small-team-real-autonomy','Remote · Full-time · Hiring now\n\nWe\'re Senturo! We primarily help US K-12 school districts and other organizations with large device fleets keep their devices secure and provide tools to recover them if they go missing. A TinySeed-backed B2B SaaS serving education customers in 26 states and 8 countries, headquartered in London with a fully remote team. We\'re looking for a backend engineer to join us and help us ship fast.\n\nWhy this role is worth your attention\n• A small team where your work is visible and matters\n• Joint reporting to our CTO (architecture) and COO (product), working alongside our senior backend engineer as a peer\n• A stable, growing, mission-driven business (education)\n• Modern tooling, async culture, and real autonomy\n\nWhat you\'ll do\n\nShip features across our Django backend: automations, reporting, third-party integrations, and work that connects them to the frontend. Contribute to architectural discussions from day one.\n\nWhat we need from you\n• 3–7 years of professional experience shipping production Django/Python — we care about real production experience, not job titles\n• Strong PostgreSQL — schema, queries, migrations\n• REST API design and third-party integration experience\n• Experience with Celery or similar async task queues\n• Real experience with Claude Code or similar AI coding tools — used as a daily tool on production code, with judgment about where they help and where they don\'t\n• Comfortable owning features end-to-end without needing close supervision\n• Excellent written communication — we\'re fully async across time zones (our team currently spans GMT+1 to GMT+8/9)\n\nBonus: MDM/EdTech/B2B SaaS background.\n\nCompensation and benefits\n\nWe\'ll share the specific salary range on the first call, before you invest serious time.\n• Fully remote position\n• 20 days paid holiday per year, plus your country\'s public holidays\n• Flexible hours within reasonable team overlap\n• Equipment provided — high-spec laptop\n• Annual learning budget for courses, books, or conferences\n• Paid sick leave\n\nHow to apply\n\nSend a short note + CV/LinkedIn. In your note, tell us:\n• Why this role specifically — generic applications get discarded\n• Your salary expectation in USD\n\nWe respond within 3 business days. We\'re moving quickly and looking to make an offer within 3–4 weeks.\n\nNotice periods welcome — we\'d rather wait for the right person than rush the wrong one.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'real,async,production,experience,team,remote,backend,help,time,real autonomy,backend engineer,gmt,small,education,b2b saas,b2b,reporting,days,note,ship,small team,salary,fully,django,engineer'),(320,'jsearch','7v2M3-niBBLGUoc1AAAAAA==','Software Engineer (Backend) – Remote Spain','The Elite Job',NULL,'ES',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/19132/software-engineer-backend-%E2%80%93-remote-spain','Job Summary\n\nThe Elite Job is looking for a highly skilled and motivated Software Engineer (Backend) to join our growing remote development team in Spain. This role offers the opportunity to work on innovative projects that power global digital solutions. The successful candidate will be responsible for designing, developing, testing, and maintaining scalable backend systems that drive seamless user experiences and business operations. This is an exciting position for professionals passionate about building efficient server-side applications using cutting-edge technologies.\nKey Responsibilities\n• *\n\nDesign, develop, and maintain robust backend architectures and APIs that support web and mobile applications.\n• *\n\nWrite clean, efficient, and maintainable code while adhering to best practices and coding standards.\n• *\n\nCollaborate closely with frontend developers, DevOps engineers, and product managers to deliver end-to-end solutions.\n• *\n\nOptimize applications for maximum performance, scalability, and security.\n• *\n\nIntegrate data storage solutions such as SQL and NoSQL databases.\n• *\n\nParticipate in code reviews, unit testing, and debugging processes.\n• *\n\nStay updated with emerging technologies, frameworks, and software development trends.\n• *\n\nEnsure technical documentation is up-to-date and accessible across the team.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• *\n\nBachelors degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n• *\n\nProven experience (2–5 years) as a Backend Developer or Software Engineer.\n• *\n\nStrong proficiency in one or more backend languages such as Python, Java, Node.js, or Go.\n• *\n\nExperience with RESTful APIs, microservices architecture, and containerization (Docker/Kubernetes).\n• *\n\nSolid understanding of database systems (MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB).\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.\n• *\n\nGood understanding of version control tools (Git/GitHub).\n• *\n\nExcellent problem-solving and analytical thinking abilities.\n• *\n\nStrong communication and teamwork skills in a remote setting.\n• Experience\n• *\n\nMinimum of 2–5 years of relevant backend software engineering experience.\n• *\n\nPrevious experience in a remote or international team environment is preferred.\n• *\n\nHands-on experience with CI/CD pipelines and Agile/Scrum methodologies is an advantage.\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFlexible remote working schedule based on Central European Time (CET).\n• *\n\nFull-time position (40 hours per week).\n• *\n\nOccasional virtual meetings and collaboration sessions with global teams.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nIn-depth understanding of data structures, algorithms, and system design principles.\n• *\n\nAbility to translate complex business requirements into scalable technical solutions.\n• *\n\nStrong commitment to writing testable and maintainable code.\n• *\n\nCapacity to work independently and manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment.\n• *\n\nProactive mindset with a passion for innovation and continuous learning.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary package based on experience and skillset.\n• *\n\n100% remote work flexibility from anywhere in Spain.\n• *\n\nAnnual performance bonuses and growth opportunities.\n• *\n\nPaid vacation, public holidays, and wellness days.\n• *\n\nTraining and career development support.\n• *\n\nCollaborative, inclusive, and international team culture.\n• Why Join The Elite Job\n\nAt The Elite Job, we value creativity, diversity, and technical excellence. Joining our team means becoming part of a global network of talented professionals committed to innovation and digital transformation. We provide a supportive environment that empowers you to grow, learn, and make a real impact on the future of technology.\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to apply by submitting their updated CV and a short cover letter explaining their interest and relevant experience.\nPlease send your application through The Elite Job career portal or via email us with the subject line Application – Software Engineer (Backend) – Spain.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','spain,elite job,elite,software engineer,engineer backend,software,experience,backend,global,job,engineer,solutions,international team,remote,relevant,maintainable code,team,international,technical,understanding,applications,digital,maintainable,testing,updated'),(322,'jsearch','mLSCi6BeuuLFTswoAAAAAA==','Backend Engineer; PHP​/Node.js - Lead & Optimize','SellAnyCar.com',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5082646900/e/','Position: Backend Engineer (PHP/Node.js) - Lead & Optimize\nin Dubai is looking for a Full-time Developer with expertise in PHP and Node.js. This role requires working in a cross-functional team, mentoring junior members, and contributing to application optimization. Candidates should have at least 3 years of experience, a BSc in computer science, and strong English communication skills. The position offers health insurance and opportunities for professional growth, without remote work options.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'php node,php,engineer php,backend engineer,js lead,lead optimize,lead,engineer,optimize,js,node js,node,backend,position,work options,junior,team mentoring,offers health,js role,position offers,insurance opportunities,looking time,mentoring junior,growth remote,options 18808'),(323,'jsearch','nY4TSVoBSz1qdVzUAAAAAA==','Backend Engineer – Programming Role, Remote','Career.zycto',NULL,'BW',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/backend-engineer-programming-role-remote/','About Company\n\nAre you a Backend Engineer looking to make a tangible impact? Career.zycto is a dynamic and forward-thinking technology firm dedicated to building robust, scalable solutions that power the future. We believe in empowering our engineers with challenging projects, cutting-edge tools, and a collaborative environment where innovation thrives. For a Backend Engineer, this means the opportunity to shape foundational systems, explore new architectural patterns, and contribute directly to products that reach a wide audience. Join us and leverage your expertise to solve complex problems and drive technological advancement from the heart of our remote team.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is actively seeking a talented and motivated Remote Backend Engineer to join our growing team. This is an exceptional opportunity for a skilled programmer to contribute to the development of our core services and platforms, working entirely from your preferred location within Francistown, North-East District, or beyond. We are building the next generation of scalable and resilient software, and we need individuals who are passionate about clean code, robust architecture, and solving complex technical challenges.\n\nAs a Backend Engineer at Career.zycto, you will be instrumental in designing, developing, and maintaining the server-side logic, databases, and APIs that power our innovative applications. You will work closely with front-end developers, product managers, and other stakeholders to understand requirements and translate them into efficient, high-performing backend solutions. We embrace modern development methodologies and encourage continuous learning, ensuring you always have the resources to grow your skill set and advance your career.\n\nYour day-to-day will involve hands-on coding, architectural discussions, performance tuning, and ensuring the reliability and security of our systems. We value engineers who take ownership, are proactive in identifying and resolving issues, and contribute to a culture of technical excellence. If you thrive in a fast-paced, collaborative remote environment and are eager to tackle challenging projects that make a real difference, we encourage you to apply.\n\nWe are committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive work environment where every team member feels valued and has the opportunity to contribute their unique perspectives. This remote role offers significant flexibility while maintaining strong team cohesion through regular virtual stand-ups, collaborative tools, and dedicated communication channels. Come build the future with Career.zycto!\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and maintain robust, scalable, and secure backend services and APIs using chosen programming languages and frameworks.\n• Collaborate with front-end developers, product managers, and other teams to define and implement new features.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and testable code, adhering to best practices and coding standards.\n• Optimize applications for maximum speed, scalability, and stability.\n• Manage and maintain database schemas and data integrity (SQL/NoSQL).\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality, share knowledge, and mentor junior engineers.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and resolve production issues in a timely manner.\n• Implement security and data protection measures.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies and industry trends to continuously improve our tech stack.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in at least one modern backend programming language (e.g., Python, Java, Go, Node.js, C#).\n• Strong understanding of RESTful API design and development principles.\n• Experience with relational and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, Redis).\n• Solid understanding of data structures, algorithms, and software design principles.\n• Familiarity with version control systems, especially Git.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP) and containerization technologies (e.g., Docker) is a plus.\n• Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• Ability to work effectively in a remote, self-managed environment.\n• Strong communication and collaboration skills.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field.\n• Experience with microservices architecture.\n• Familiarity with message queues (e.g., Kafka, RabbitMQ).\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Knowledge of distributed systems and high-availability concepts.\n• Experience with testing frameworks and test-driven development (TDD).\n• Contributions to open-source projects.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Fully remote work flexibility, allowing you to work from anywhere.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits (if applicable for remote team members).\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Budget for professional development, online courses, and certifications.\n• Access to the latest tools and technologies.\n• Collaborative and supportive team culture.\n• Opportunities for career growth and advancement within a fast-paced company.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their comprehensive resume and a compelling cover letter outlining their experience and suitability for this role. Please send your application to the email address provided below. We look forward to reviewing your qualifications.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'backend engineer,career,zycto,career zycto,engineer,remote,backend,contribute,collaborative,experience,programming,challenging,challenging projects,team,development,systems,data,comprehensive,encourage,advancement,developers product,scalable,robust,opportunity,engineers'),(324,'jsearch','SkVps3vzalVyPawOAAAAAA==','Elixir Developer Needed for Backend Systems','Contra',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/elixir-developer-backend-systems-at-contra','We are seeking an experienced Elixir developer to join our team, focusing on developing and maintaining the backend systems of our application. This role involves working closely with our development team to ensure robust and efficient functionality that supports our app’s performance and scalability.\n\nDeliverables:\n• Collaborate with the team to design and develop backend systems using Elixir.\n• Optimize application performance and scalability.\n• Integrate third-party APIs and services as needed.\n• Troubleshoot and resolve backend issues promptly.\n• Document code and development processes for future reference.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'elixir,backend systems,elixir developer,performance scalability,needed,scalability,systems,backend,performance,maintaining backend,closely development,code development,collaborate team,deliverables collaborate,needed backend,scalability integrate,develop backend,processes future,developer needed,deliverables,needed troubleshoot,promptly document,scalability deliverables,efficient functionality,services needed'),(325,'jsearch','b0L0SYJIiCPvlDQTAAAAAA==','Backend Developer Intern – Node.js and Express','DevBridge',NULL,'US',0,'https://theelitejob.com/us/job/1154/Backend-Developer-Intern-%E2%80%93-Node.js-and-Express','Job Summary\n\nDevBridge is seeking a highly motivated and talented Backend Developer Intern with strong knowledge of Node.js and Express to join our dynamic software development team. This internship provides hands-on experience in building scalable web applications, RESTful APIs, and collaborating with cross-functional teams. The ideal candidate is eager to learn, passionate about backend development, and ready to contribute to real-world projects that impact our clients.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop and maintain backend services and APIs using Node.js and Express.\n• Collaborate with frontend developers, UI/UX designers, and product managers to deliver seamless user experiences.\n• Participate in code reviews and contribute to improving code quality, efficiency, and performance.\n• Assist in troubleshooting and debugging applications to ensure high availability and responsiveness.\n• Work with databases (SQL or NoSQL) to design and optimize data models.\n• Stay updated with emerging technologies and best practices in backend development.\n• Document code, processes, and workflows to support team knowledge sharing.\n\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n• Strong understanding of Node.js and Express framework.\n• Basic knowledge of RESTful APIs, JSON, and web services.\n• Familiarity with database systems such as MongoDB, MySQL, or PostgreSQL.\n• Understanding of asynchronous programming and event-driven architecture.\n• Experience with version control systems like Git.\n• Good problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• Effective communication skills and ability to work collaboratively in a team environment.\n\nExperience\n• No prior professional experience required; this internship is ideal for students, fresh graduates, or early-career developers.\n• Exposure to personal or academic projects using Node.js and Express is a plus.\n\nWorking Hours\n• Flexible full-time or part-time internship opportunities.\n• Expected 20–40 hours per week, depending on availability and project requirements.\n• Remote-friendly options available with occasional team meetings or virtual sync-ups.\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSA)\n• Strong analytical and logical thinking.\n• Ability to learn quickly and adapt to new technologies.\n• Self-motivated and proactive in tackling technical challenges.\n• Good documentation and reporting skills.\n• Ability to work independently as well as part of a collaborative team.\n\nBenefits\n• Hands-on experience working on real-world backend projects.\n• Mentorship from experienced software engineers and developers.\n• Exposure to agile development methodologies and modern tech stack.\n• Opportunity to build a strong professional portfolio.\n• Flexible work environment with remote internship options.\n• Certificate of internship completion and potential for full-time offer based on performance.\n\nWhy Join DevBridge\n\nAt DevBridge, we nurture talent and provide a platform for interns to transform their ideas into innovative solutions. You will gain practical experience in backend development, collaborate with skilled professionals, and contribute to projects that make a difference. This is an excellent opportunity to kickstart your career in software development while building a strong foundation in Node.js and Express.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to submit:\n• Updated Resume/CV\n• Portfolio or GitHub links showcasing projects with Node.js/Express (if available)\n• Cover Letter explaining your interest in backend development and DevBridge\n\nSubmit your application via email to us with the subject line: “Backend Developer Intern – Node.js & Express Application”',NULL,10.00,20.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','js express,express,internship,node js,devbridge,node,js,developer intern,intern,backend,development,backend development,projects,skills,experience,developers exposure,intern node,strong,world,real world,availability,using node,portfolio,knowledge,contribute'),(326,'jsearch','wqMo28CtGsbjhZDAAAAAAA==','Remote Backend SaaS Engineer Ubuntu Landscape','Canonical',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5084247073/e/','Position: Remote Backend SaaS Engineer for Ubuntu Landscape\nA leading open-source software firm is seeking a Software Developer (Backend SaaS) to join its team. The role involves contributing to the development of a management solution for Ubuntu, focusing on high-quality code and autonomous problem-solving. Candidates should have a strong background in Python, web applications, and public-facing APIs. The position allows for remote work with periodic travel. Ideal for passionate engineers looking to work with the best in the field.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ubuntu,backend saas,saas,saas engineer,ubuntu landscape,engineer ubuntu,landscape,remote backend,engineer,python web,background python,development management,engineers looking,software firm,autonomous problem,autonomous,facing apis,source software,solving candidates,field 18808,firm seeking,software developer,saas join,periodic travel,looking work'),(327,'jsearch','SXrPzUS_aeplVlPdAAAAAA==','Remote Node.js API Developer — Microservices','Houston Skilled Consultancy',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/17006/remote-node.js-api-developer-%E2%80%94-microservices','Job Summary\n\nHouston Skilled Consultancy is looking for a talented and experienced Remote Node.js API Developer with a strong focus on Microservices architecture to join our fast-growing global team. The ideal candidate will have hands-on experience in designing and developing RESTful APIs, working with distributed systems, and deploying scalable backend services using Node.js. This is a fully remote role ideal for proactive professionals eager to build high-performance APIs in a cloud-first environment.\nKey Responsibilities\n• *\n\nDesign, build, and maintain robust, scalable, and secure RESTful APIs using Node.js.\n• *\n\nDevelop and maintain backend microservices that integrate with various third-party systems and internal services.\n• *\n\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams including frontend developers, DevOps engineers, and product managers to deliver high-quality solutions.\n• *\n\nWrite clean, efficient, and testable code with proper documentation.\n• *\n\nMonitor and optimize application performance, scalability, and reliability.\n• *\n\nTroubleshoot and resolve API and server-side issues quickly and efficiently.\n• *\n\nParticipate in code reviews, contribute to technical documentation, and share best practices within the team.\n• *\n\nContinuously research and apply new technologies, tools, and design patterns.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• *\n\nProficiency in Node.js and JavaScript (ES6+), with experience in building RESTful APIs and server-side applications.\n• *\n\nStrong understanding and practical experience with Microservices architecture and API Gateway patterns.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with Express.js, NestJS, or similar Node.js frameworks.\n• *\n\nKnowledge of Docker, Kubernetes, or similar container orchestration tools is highly desirable.\n• *\n\nHands-on experience with NoSQL and SQL databases (e.g., MongoDB, PostgreSQL, MySQL).\n• *\n\nExperience with authentication and authorization protocols such as OAuth2, JWT, etc.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with CI/CD pipelines, version control systems (e.g., Git), and Agile/Scrum methodologies.\n• *\n\nStrong debugging, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills.\n• Experience\n• *\n\nMinimum of 3+ years of professional experience in backend development with Node.js.\n• *\n\nProven track record of delivering production-grade microservices-based applications.\n• *\n\nExperience in a remote/distributed team environment is a plus.\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFlexible working hours with core collaboration time aligned to GMT/IST.\n• *\n\nMust be available for occasional team meetings and sprint planning sessions.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\n• *\n\nStrong sense of ownership, responsibility, and accountability.\n• *\n\nAbility to work independently with minimal supervision.\n• *\n\nCollaborative team player with a growth mindset.\n• *\n\nQuick learner with a passion for clean code and scalable solutions.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\n100% remote work – work from anywhere.\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• *\n\nFlexible work schedule.\n• *\n\nLearning & development opportunities (access to training resources and certifications).\n• *\n\nSupportive team culture that values innovation and continuous improvement.\n• *\n\nOpportunity to work with cutting-edge technologies and global clients.\n• Why Join Houston Skilled Consultancy\n\nAt Houston Skilled Consultancy, we are more than just a company — we are a mission-driven team of problem-solvers and innovators dedicated to transforming the tech landscape. You will be part of a supportive and diverse community that encourages creativity, embraces challenges, and rewards initiative. If you are ready to work on exciting projects that make an impact — we want to hear from you.\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to take your backend development career to the next level?\n\nPlease submit your updated resume, GitHub profile (if available), and a brief cover letter highlighting your relevant experience to us\nSubject: Application for Remote Node.js API Developer – Microservices\n\nApplications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','microservices,api,js,experience,node js,node,team,api developer,js api,houston,remote node,skilled consultancy,houston skilled,consultancy,remote,restful apis,work,backend,restful,skilled,apis,developer microservices,supportive,clean,global'),(328,'jsearch','46wmeM-rGTXOWq1CAAAAAA==','Web Developer','Quadrant Innovation Technology LLP',NULL,'JM',0,'https://jm.linkedin.com/jobs/view/web-developer-at-quadrant-innovation-technology-llp-4410527164','Quadrant Technology is looking for an Experienced Web Developer to join our growing team!\n\nYou will work hand-in-hand with our team of designers, programmers and project managers to build a variety of interactive web-based projects\n\nYou must be passionate and open to working in a fast-paced environment – collaborating with an ever zealous team – creating and innovating awesomeness.\n\nIf you are interested in becoming an integral part of a cutting-edge digital agency that humanize brands, this is the ideal role for you.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Solid experience in vanilla javascript, API development.\n• Must be able to write organized code and be comfortable working on a complicated code-base with high levels of abstraction\n• Experience in Laravel or similar PHP frameworks.\n• Experience in Angular.js [4x or higher], react.js is a plus.\n• Experience in writing unit tests on Jasmine, Mocha is a plus.\n• Knowledge of Web standards and browser compatibility\n• Coordinate/collaborate with staff and teams to develop and deploy projects\n• Assist and support in the upkeep and maintenance of websites\n• Troubleshoot and resolve technical problems\n\nSkills & Requirements\n• Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science or equivalent with 2 or more years experience in developing websites or web-apps.\n• Strong interpersonal skills and verbal communication skills\n• Experience creating Web sites\n\nIdeal Candidate\n\nA close-knit culture defines us at Quadrant Technology. And we are super proud of it! Our core value rests on our PEOPLE – Employees and Customers. Out culture calls for respect, integrity, passion, commitment, and an open-minded approach and mindset. Strong Character makes for Awesome Team to work with and that’s what we look for in prospective Employees, as well as, Clients.\n• Eager to thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced environment\n• Attention to detail with an analytical mindset\n• Passionate about learning and thirst for knowledge\n• Ability to work as a team player but also achieve individual goals\n\nApply',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'web,experience,team,creating,working,quadrant technology,plus,quadrant,team work,hand,employees,fast,websites,open,paced environment,ideal,fast paced,paced,skills,mindset,work,culture,environment,knowledge,passionate'),(329,'jsearch','mle9uDTtLjEAX7fkAAAAAA==','Freelance Developer','Twine','Kingston','JM',0,'https://www.twine.net/projects/b9fyt0-video-web-graphic-marketing-ai-freelancer-developer-in-kingston-jamaica-job','Developer is needed in Kingston, Jamaica.\n\nWe are looking for a freelancer to support our company, Rillway, located in Kingston, Jamaica, with projects in video & animation, app & web development, graphic & design, marketing, and AI/ML. Work is expected to be hybrid, but we are open to applicants who are willing to travel and work with us in person when required.\n\nBudget range:\nReceive offers\n\nIn what capacity are you hiring?\nMy company\n\nWhat experience level is needed?:\nSenior\n\nClient contact preference:\nOn Twine (contact details private)\nPosted 21 days ago',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'contact,needed,kingston jamaica,kingston,company,jamaica,marketing,app,posted 21,posted,support company,animation app,receive offers,animation,receive,ai ml,ai,level needed,ml,rillway located,rillway,preference twine,preference,video animation,video'),(334,'jsearch','c9nxxLErlNSMNBhNAAAAAA==','Python Developer(Mid Junior)','Torc',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/python-developermid-at-torc','Time zones: EST (UTC -5), MST (UTC -7), ART (UTC -3), UTC -4, UTC -4:30, UTC -3, UTC -2\n\nOur dynamic team is expanding, and we’re in search of a Python Developer who is passionate about technology and eager to make a significant impact. If you’re looking for an opportunity to work on exciting projects in a collaborative, remote environment, we’d love to hear from you.\n\nAbout the Role:\n\nAs a Python Developer, you’ll be instrumental in designing, developing, and implementing software solutions to meet our business needs. You’ll collaborate with a talented team to build scalable, high-quality applications and contribute to all phases of the development lifecycle.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Develop and maintain web applications using Python and Python frameworks.\n• Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Work on bug fixing and improving application performance.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure robustness, usability, and reliability.\n• Stay up-to-date with new technology trends, applications, and protocols in Python development.\n\nQualifications\n• Proven experience as a Python Developer.\n• Familiarity with Python web stacks and various Python frameworks.\n• Solid understanding of object-oriented programming.\n• Experience with front-end technologies (e.g., HTML, CSS, JavaScript) is a plus.\n• Knowledge of relational databases and version control tools.\n• Strong problem-solving skills and a detail-oriented mindset.\n• Excellent communication skills and the ability to work well in a team.\n• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field is preferred.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'utc,python,python developer,utc utc,python frameworks,developer,ll,applications,oriented,frameworks,web,work,needs ll,bug fixing,build scalable,contribute phases,new features,control tools,databases version,date new,passionate technology,define design,design ship,developer familiarity,developer ll'),(335,'jsearch','agy32CuYHD8aY-xVAAAAAA==','Senior React.js & Python / Node Developer','Lemon.io',NULL,NULL,0,'https://remote.com/jobs/lemon-io-c1eumcoq/senior-react-js-python-node-developer-j1kw83fo','Are you a talented Senior Developer looking for a remote job that lets you show your skills and get decent compensation? Look no further than Lemon.io — the marketplace that connects you with hand-picked startups in the US and Europe.\n\nWhat we offer:\n• The rate depends on your seniority level, skills and experience. We\'ve already paid out over $11M to our engineers.\n• No more hunting for clients or negotiating rates — let us handle the business side of things so you can focus on what you do best.\n• We\'ll manually find the best project for you according to your skills and preferences.\n• Choose a schedule that works best for you. It’s possible to communicate async or minimally overlap within team working hours.\n• We respect your seniority so you can expect no micromanagement or screen trackers.\n• Communicate directly with the clients. Most of them have technical backgrounds. Sounds good, yeah?\n• We will support you from the time you submit the application throughout all cooperation stages.\n• Most of our projects involve working in a fast-paced startup environment. We hope you like it as much as we do.\n• Through our community, we will connect you with the best developers from more than 71 countries.\n\nWe have several open positions for Full-Stack React.js Developers - please see the details below. We also have some backend positions; the full list is included below as well.\nRequirements for the Senior React & Python Position:\n• 4+ years of software development experience.\n\nCommercial experience:\n• React.js 3+ years & Python 3+ years\n\nOR React.js 2+ years & Python 5+ years OR React.js 5+ years & Python 2+ years\n• Experience with AWS, GCP, or Azure is required.\n\nRequirements for the Senior Node & React Position:\n• 5+ years of software development experience\n\nCommercial experience:\n• React.js: 3+ years, Node.js: 5+ years, and Next.js: 2+ years OR React.js: 5+ years, Node.js: 3+ years, and Next.js: 2+ years\n• Expertise in TypeScript, Supabase and AI-assisted coding is a must.\n\nOther requirements:\n• Strong technical skills: as a Senior Developer, you are expected to be able to create projects from scratch and have a deep understanding of application architecture.\n• Clear and effective communication in English — advanced ability to discuss business tasks, justify decisions, and communicate issues. Good self-presentation is also essential for upcoming client calls.\n• Strong self-organizational skills — ability to work full-time remotely with no supervision.\n• Reliability — we want to trust you and expect that you won’t let us and the client down.\n• Adaptability and Flexibility — the ability to onboard the project promptly after accepting it and start delivering results quickly.\n\nSounds good for you? Apply now and join the Lemon.io community!\n\nNOT YOUR TECH STACK?\n\nWe have multiple projects available for Senior Developers. If you have 4+ years of commercial software development experience and are proficient in any of the following areas and roles: AI Agent Architect, AI Automation Architect, React & Golang, Golang, PHP & Angular, PHP & Vue, Vue & Node.js, React & .NET, Android & iOS, Angular & .NET, Angular & Node.js, Vue & .NET, Python & Vue, MLOps, React & Java, Data Science, Blockchain (Web3/Solidity/Solana), Symfony & React, Symfony & Vue, Symfony & Angular, Symfony & JavaScript & Next.js & TypeScript, Data Analysis, React & PHP, Data Engineering, AI Engineering, Data Annotation, Python & Flask, DevOps, Svelte & Python, Svelte & Node, Svelte & TypeScript, Rust, Shopify & JavaScript, Vue & Nuxt, Python & Node, Angular & TypeScript, Ruby & Ruby on Rails, React Native & Ruby, React Native & Python, PHP & Laravel, .NET & C#, Java & Spring, Unreal Engine & C++, Python & LLM, Unity, Machine Learning Engineering — we’d be happy to connect and match you with a suitable project.\n\nIf your experience matches our requirements, be ready for the next steps:\n• VideoAsk — watch a short video about our startup, up to 10 minutes\n• Complete your profile on our website\n• Intro call\n• Technical interview\n• Feedback\n• Magic Box (we are looking for the best project for you).\n\nWe do not provide visa assistance, and our cooperation model does not include the benefits typically offered with direct hire.\n\nP.S. We work with developers from 71+ countries in different regions: Europe, LATAM, the U.S (if you are an owner of W-9 ben form), Canada, Asia (Japan, Singapore, South Korea, Philippines, Indonesia), Oceania (Australia, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea), and the the UK. However, we have some exceptions.\n\nAt the moment, we don’t have a legal basis to accept applicants from the following countries:\n• European: Hungary, Iceland, Liechtenstein, Kosovo, Belarus, Russia, and Serbia.\n• Latin America: Cuba and Nicaragua\n• Most Asian countries and Africa.\n\nWe expand and shorten the list of exemptions regularly.',NULL,5000.00,15000.00,NULL,'MONTH','details','react,python,js years,react js,years,vue,js,senior,angular,ai,symfony,countries,net,php,experience,node,ruby,python years,svelte,development experience,years python,years react,typescript,project,requirements'),(336,'jsearch','r0paY7o0JKPkfSpdAAAAAA==','Python Developer – Work from Home','Career.zycto',NULL,'CA',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/python-developer-work-from-home/','About Company\n\nImagine building innovative solutions from anywhere, contributing to a forward-thinking culture that values your expertise. Career.zycto empowers Python Developers to transform complex challenges into elegant, high-performing software. We are a dynamic tech firm leveraging cutting-edge Python frameworks to deliver scalable, impactful applications across diverse industries. We champion a collaborative yet autonomous environment, offering unparalleled opportunities for professional growth and skill enhancement. Join us and shape the future of technology, working alongside passionate experts dedicated to pushing boundaries and fostering a supportive remote community. Your contributions directly fuel our mission to innovate and excel.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a talented Python Developer seeking to unleash your full potential in a remote-first environment? Career.zycto is on the lookout for a highly skilled and motivated individual to join our innovative engineering team. This is an exciting opportunity to design, develop, and deploy robust, scalable, and high-performance applications that will drive our core business initiatives. As a Python Developer with Career.zycto, you will be instrumental in building the next generation of our platforms, contributing to all phases of the development lifecycle, from conceptualization and design to testing and deployment. We embrace agile methodologies, continuous integration, and a culture of technical excellence. You\'ll be working on challenging projects that demand creativity, strong problem-solving skills, and a keen eye for detail. This role offers the flexibility of remote work while ensuring strong team collaboration through modern communication tools. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment where every team member feels valued and empowered to contribute their best work. If you\'re passionate about clean code, robust architecture, and impactful software that makes a real difference, we want to hear from you. This is more than just a job; it’s a chance to grow your skills, innovate, and shape the future of technology with a supportive and forward-thinking team.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain robust Python-based applications and services, ensuring high performance and responsiveness.\n• Write clean, scalable, well-documented, and efficient code following industry best practices and internal coding standards.\n• Collaborate closely with cross-functional teams, including product managers, designers, and QA engineers, to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Actively participate in code reviews, providing constructive feedback to peers and integrating feedback to improve code quality and maintainability.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software to enhance functionality, improve performance, and ensure system reliability.\n• Implement and maintain RESTful APIs, and integrate with various internal and third-party services.\n• Contribute to architectural discussions and strategic technical planning to ensure scalable and sustainable solutions.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies, frameworks, and industry trends to continuously improve our tech stack and development processes.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Minimum of 3 years of professional experience as a Python Developer in a production environment.\n• Proficiency in Python programming language and extensive experience with frameworks like Django, Flask, or FastAPI.\n• Strong understanding of relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL) and experience with Object-Relational Mappers (ORMs).\n• Proven experience with RESTful API design and development, ensuring secure and efficient communication.\n• Familiarity with version control systems, particularly Git, and collaborative development workflows.\n• Solid understanding of object-oriented programming (OOP) principles, data structures, and algorithms.\n• Demonstrated ability to write clean, maintainable, and well-tested code.\n• Excellent problem-solving skills, analytical thinking, and a keen attention to detail.\n• Strong communication and collaboration skills, with the ability to thrive in a remote team setting.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform.\n• Familiarity with containerization technologies like Docker and orchestration tools like Kubernetes.\n• Knowledge of front-end technologies (e.g., HTML, CSS, JavaScript, React, Angular, Vue.js) is a plus.\n• Experience with message queues (e.g., Kafka, RabbitMQ) and microservices architecture.\n• Understanding of CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices for automated deployments.\n• Contributions to open-source projects or active participation in developer communities.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package with performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance coverage.\n• Generous paid time off policy and flexible working hours to promote work-life balance.\n• Dedicated budget for professional development, including online courses, certifications, and conference attendance.\n• Remote-first work culture with support for home office setup (e.g., stipend for equipment).\n• Collaborative and supportive team environment with regular virtual team-building activities.\n• Opportunity to work on challenging and impactful projects that push technological boundaries.\n• A vibrant culture that values innovation, continuous learning, and individual growth.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to make an impact with Career.zycto? We encourage all qualified candidates to apply. Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and a cover letter detailing your experience, your passion for Python development, and why you are the ideal candidate for this remote Python Developer role. We look forward to reviewing your application and exploring how your skills can contribute to our team!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'python developer,python,zycto,career zycto,scalable,career,team,development,design,experience,impactful,thinking,developer,software,performance,culture,work,skills,environment,code,forward,ensuring,improve,remote,technical'),(337,'jsearch','mtajl1Xf8dyH37oeAAAAAA==','Python Developer – Work from Home','Career.zycto',NULL,'SG',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/python-developer-work-from-home-2/','About Company\n\nJoin Career.zycto, a forward-thinking technology consultancy renowned for crafting innovative software solutions that push industry boundaries. We empower our clients with cutting-edge platforms, and our success is built on a foundation of brilliant minds and collaborative spirit. For a Python Developer, this means engaging with diverse, challenging projects, leveraging the latest libraries, and having a direct impact on our product\'s evolution. We foster an environment where continuous learning and technical mastery are not just encouraged, but celebrated, making us the ideal launchpad for your next career chapter.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a seasoned Python Developer with a passion for building robust, scalable applications and the discipline to thrive in a fully remote environment? Career.zycto is seeking an exceptional individual to join our distributed team as a Python Developer, working from the comfort of your home in Singapore. This is an incredible opportunity to contribute to a dynamic portfolio of projects, ranging from backend services and API development to data processing pipelines, automation tools, and even machine learning integrations. You\'ll collaborate with a talented global team, pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible in a supportive and innovative culture.\n\nIn this role, you will be instrumental in the full software development lifecycle, from conceptualisation and design to deployment and maintenance. We are looking for someone who can not only write clean, efficient, and well-documented Python code but also critically think about system architecture, performance optimisation, and secure coding practices. Your expertise will directly influence the functionality and reliability of our core platforms, impacting how our clients leverage technology to achieve their strategic goals across various industries. You will have the opportunity to architect new features, refactor existing codebases for improved performance and maintainability, and contribute to our continuous integration and continuous deployment (CI/CD) pipelines.\n\nWhile the role is remote, effective communication and strong collaboration skills are paramount. You will be expected to actively participate in virtual stand-ups, code reviews, and planning sessions, ensuring seamless integration with other team members and stakeholders. Proactivity in identifying and solving technical challenges, as well as a commitment to best practices in software development, are highly valued. We believe in empowering our developers with autonomy and ownership, providing the freedom to innovate while maintaining a commitment to delivering high-quality solutions on time. If you’re ready to tackle complex challenges, embrace new technologies, and contribute to a company that values both technical excellence and work-life balance, then Career.zycto offers the perfect environment for your continued growth and success.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop, test, and deploy robust and scalable Python applications and services.\n• Design and implement APIs for internal and external consumption.\n• Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other developers to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code following best practices and coding standards.\n• Participate actively in code reviews, providing constructive feedback and ensuring code quality.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software systems and applications.\n• Contribute to the continuous improvement of our development processes, tools, and infrastructure.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Strong proficiency in Python (3+ years professional experience).\n• Solid understanding of web frameworks (e.g., Django, Flask, FastAPI).\n• Experience with relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL) and ORM libraries.\n• Proficiency with version control systems, especially Git.\n• Familiarity with RESTful APIs and microservices architecture.\n• Experience with unit testing and integration testing methodologies.\n• Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and critical thinking skills.\n• Proven ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fully remote team environment.\n• Strong communication skills, both written and verbal.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP).\n• Knowledge of containerization technologies (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Familiarity with message queues (e.g., RabbitMQ, Kafka).\n• Experience with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Understanding of front-end technologies (e.g., JavaScript, React) is a plus.\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary package.\n• Fully remote work model, offering unparalleled flexibility and work-life balance.\n• Opportunity for continuous learning, professional development, and career advancement.\n• Access to modern tools, cutting-edge technologies, and a vibrant developer community.\n• Collaborative and supportive team environment that values innovation.\n• Generous annual leave and public holidays.\n• Opportunities to work on diverse and impactful projects.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this exciting Python Developer - Work from Home opportunity, please send your comprehensive resume, a detailed cover letter highlighting your relevant experience, and a link to your GitHub profile or personal portfolio to the email address provided below. We highly encourage you to click on the link below to submit your application. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'python developer,continuous,career,python,work,opportunity,technical,zycto,career zycto,platforms,developer,software,practices,technologies,experience,code,development,environment,pipelines,integration,contribute,home,fully,fully remote,contribute continuous');
INSERT INTO `jobs` VALUES (338,'jsearch','gs0FG-op_aUkvJsmAAAAAA==','Python Mid Senior Engineer Django REST FastAPI at awesome SaaS','Lead Sherpa, Inc.',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/python-mid-engineer-django-rest-fastapi-at-awesome-saas','Position: Python Mid Senior Engineer Django REST FastAPI at awesome SaaS\n\nCompensation: $90,000 – $160,000\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nAccolades: Best in Biz Silver Award – Fastest Growing Company in USA (under 99 employees)\n\nWeb: www.LeadSherpa.com\n\nWho is Lead Sherpa?\n\nCompany Core Values: Respect, Integrity, Drive, Innovation\n\nOur MISSION is to empower real estate professionals and help guide them to success. Our VISION is to create the most powerful lead and data management technology suite in the real estate industry, and we are well on our way.\n\nLead Sherpa’s office is located in Denver, Colorado, however, we are also a fully remote team strategically positioned across the Western Hemisphere and operating with a high level of autonomy and trust. Our focus is on creating a dynamic, positive, and supportive work environment where our team members can grow and thrive.\n\nSchedules are flexible as long as deadlines are hit. Our team takes full ownership of every project—not only do they work well independently without supervision, but they also work well within the team ecosystem. Our company culture cultivates a feeling of camaraderie and a sense of belonging and direction. Every team member knows exactly what our targets are, where we are going, and how we will get there.\n\nTeam members enjoy company-sponsored health care, a flexible time-off policy, and are eligible for a 401(k) retirement plan with generous company matching contributions. We take ownership of our roles and we are treated with respect, creating an ideal work environment for everyone to thrive. The team is always supported with the necessary resources and training to accomplish their goals and grow professionally.\n\nWe are always searching for more A-Players to join our team. If Lead Sherpa sounds like the place for you to put your drive and skills to good use, please let us know.\n\nPosition Details: Back-end Developer\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nLead Sherpa is looking for mid-and senior-level engineers to join our engineering team with specific experience in Django, REST Framework, and other python-based web frameworks implementing industry best practices. Experience with analogous technologies (e.g. MVC . NET, Spring, Rails) will be considered as long as command of python and web principles are strong. New services are being built as microservices and using newer frameworks like FastAPI and dataclasses, as well as potentially Golang for higher performance applications. Data normalization across synchronous and asynchronous systems is essential, with JSON Schema, OpenAPI, and related technologies being leveraged to that end. Experience with containers is essential, and experience with container orchestration is preferred.\n• Maintain current project standards and offer suggestions for future improvement.\n• Build out new features using our existing stack as well as emerging technologies.\n• Strong focus on building out well-documented, tested, resilient code to improve agility/stability of our products\n• Be a good communicator and express your concerns or need for elaboration on requirements\n\nRequirements:\n• 3+ years of experience working with Django and Django REST Framework\n• 3+ years of experience working with RESTful APIs\n• 3+ years of working with Celery, Prefect, or other task management tools\n• 1+ years of experience implementing asynchronous systems using WebSockets and other message queuing and/or pub/sub-technologies\n• 1+ years of experience building 12-factor applications, container images, and orchestrating a stack in both development and deployment environments\n• PostgreSQL, Elasticsearch, Redis, and RabbitMQ experience preferred\n• Strong preference for and experience with object-oriented programming\n• Believer in DRY principles\n• Experience with auto-generated documentation\n• Experience with building an oauth2 service for outside applications\n• Comfortable working with many 3rd party services\n• A strong desire for continuous improvement and taking great pride in what you build\n• Attention to detail and desire to build out clean and beautiful code that future developers will enjoy\n\nBenefits:\n\nUS Team Members\n• Company-sponsored health insurance, vision, and dental\n• 401(k) with company match\n\nInternational Team Members\n• Company contribution to health insurance expenses, as needed\n\nAll Team Members\n• Fully remote and flexible schedule\n• Flexible and generous PTO policy\n• $2,000 home office/hardware gift – equipment is yours to keep!\n• Individualized paid coaching/growth training',NULL,90000.00,160000.00,NULL,'YEAR','details','company,experience,team,lead,years experience,django rest,lead sherpa,sherpa,team members,years,members,rest,flexible,technologies,mid,building,health,fastapi,mid senior,django,work,strong,working,python,using'),(340,'jsearch','BPEGXWaHD-zwvSC8AAAAAA==','Humble Hacker Wanted: Remote Developer & AI Enthusiast for Scraping and Automation','Biodenix Inc',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/humble-hacker-developer-enthusiast-at-biodenix','About Us:\n\nWe’re a small, scrappy team that loves smart solutions and fast results.\n\nNo egos, no drama—just clever ideas and a drive to build cool stuff.\n\nOur focus? AI and VR.\n\nWe research and create apps about topics like AI girlfriends, deepfake tools, FaceSwap, and AI video generators.\n\nWe use smart SEO and content generation as one of our top marketing channels.\n\nWho We’re Looking For:\n\nA tech-savvy problem solver who’s more hacker than hardcore developer.\n\nYou’re humble, resourceful. Dare i say lazy? (you don’t like manual work and you look for wise solutions).\n\nYou embrace AI, utilize prebuilt tools, and aren’t afraid to dive into web scraping and automation.\n\nExpected Salary: $1,500 – $2,500/month, based on your skills and experience, with plenty of room to grow as we build amazing things together!\n\nMust-Haves:\n• Scraping Skills: Experience with web scraping tools and techniques.\n• Coding Chops: Proficient in at least one programming language (Python, JavaScript, etc.).\n• AI Enthusiasm: Comfortable using AI tools to boost productivity.\n• Humble Attitude: Low ego, high openness to feedback, and eager to learn.\n• Problem-Solving Mindset: You see challenges as opportunities.\n• Clear Communicator: You keep the team in the loop with timely updates.\n\nBonus Points For:\n• SEO Know-How: Familiarity with SEO, keyword research, and tools like Ahrefs.\n• Programmatic SEO Experience: If you’ve automated SEO tasks before, we want to hear about it\n\nWhat You WON’T Be:\n• An Elitist or Diva: No room for big egos or rigid mindsets.\n• Drama Magnet: We value a hassle-free, collaborative environment.\n\nWhat You’ll Do:\n• Tackle web scraping projects to gather essential data.\n• Develop automations to streamline workflows.\n• Collaborate on implementing programmatic SEO strategies.\n• Leverage AI tools to enhance efficiency.\n• Communicate regularly with the team, sharing insights and updates.\n\nWhy Join Us:\n• Results-Driven Focus: We measure success by results, not hours logged. Be effective, work wisely, and take ownership of your time.\n• Ego-Free Environment: We’re committed to results, clarity, and facts—no ego, no fluff, just meaningful work.\n• Flexible Remote Work: Work during the hours when you’re most productive—your time, your schedule.\n• Accelerate Your Growth: Achieve exceptional progress and accomplish more at a faster pace than you ever imagined.\n\nHow to Apply:\n\nYou’ll need to fill a simple Google form (5-10mins max) that will check your attention to detail and give us a glimpse on how your hacker mind works.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'seo,scraping,ai,results,humble,web scraping,ego,hacker,tools,free,drama,scraping automation,egos,smart,room,research,programmatic,500,programmatic seo,ai tools,work,web,skills experience,updates,like'),(341,'jsearch','Ty6LSbGI5uNz-ZwyAAAAAA==','Software Development Apprentice - Java OR Python Training with Live Projects','Apprenticeships',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/us/job/319/Software-Development-Apprentice---Java-OR-Python-Training-with-Live-Projects','Position: Software Development Apprentice\n\nLocation: Remote\n\nDepartment: Software Development / Engineering\n\nProgram Duration: 12 Months (Paid Apprenticeship)\n\nAbout the Role\n\nThis apprenticeship is designed for aspiring software developers eager to build real-world skills in coding, debugging, and deploying applications. As a Software Development Apprentice, you’ll receive structured training in Java and Python, and work alongside experienced developers on live projects that solve actual business problems.\n\nYou’ll gain exposure to software development life cycles, modern development tools, and collaborative coding environments — the perfect foundation to launch your career in tech.\n\nEligibility Criteria\n• Bachlor Degree\n• Entry-level graduates from any stream with a passion for coding\n• Minimum 16 years of age\n• Valid Aadhar card required\n\nKey Learning Areas\n• Writing and debugging basic programs in Java and Python\n• Understanding object-oriented programming (OOP) concepts\n• Exposure to databases, version control (Git), and APIs\n• Participating in code reviews, stand-ups, and agile workflows\n• Building and testing real-world applications as part of a development team\n• Documenting code and following best practices in clean coding\n\nProgram Structure\n• 12-month paid apprenticeship with hands-on learning and mentorship\n• 9 hours per day (including a 1-hour break), 5 working days per week\n• Online assessments at 3-month and 11-month checkpoints\n• Certificate co-branded with company and government authorities upon completion\n\nWhat You’ll Gain\n• Practical coding experience in Java, Python, and real project environments\n• Familiarity with development tools like Git, IDEs, and issue trackers\n• Exposure to teamwork in agile/scrum development settings\n• A recognized certificate and solid foundation for a career in software development',NULL,10.00,20.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','development,software development,software,java python,java,apprenticeship,development apprentice,apprentice,exposure,month,coding,real,program,development tools,certificate,debugging,live,gain,world,live projects,real world,paid apprenticeship,ll gain,foundation,agile'),(343,'jsearch','kpDXd_5qQBlLdoLEAAAAAA==','Remote Python Game Developer; Panda3D AI Simulations','YO IT Consulting',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5060268104/e/','Position: Remote Python Game Developer (Panda3D) for AI Simulations\nYO IT Consulting is looking for an expert Python Game Developer (Panda3D) to join their team. In this remote position, you will contribute to cutting-edge AI training projects using Panda3D, a robust open-source game engine. The role involves designing 3D simulations for AI training, optimizing environments, and ensuring cross-platform compatibility. Candidates must demonstrate proficiency in Python, C++, and Git Hub, alongside excellent communication skills and attention to detail.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'game,panda3d,game developer,python game,developer panda3d,simulations,ai,ai simulations,remote python,ai training,panda3d ai,python,training,developer,remote,position,team remote,involves designing,training optimizing,environments ensuring,python git,robust open,hub alongside,game engine,ensuring cross'),(344,'jsearch','Ipoz_LYnLYjIj4iEAAAAAA==','Python Game Developer; Panda3D - Remote','YO IT Consulting',NULL,'AE',0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5060269154/e/','Position: Python Game Developer (Panda3D) - Remote\n\nJob Title:\n\nPython Game Developer (Panda3D)\n\nJob Type: Contract\n\nLocation: Remote\nJob Summary\n\nJoin our customer\'s team as an expert Python Game Developer (Panda3D), where you’ll contribute to cutting-edge AI training projects using one of the most robust and flexible open-source game engines. This specialized role focuses on harnessing Panda3D’s capabilities to deliver immersive, high-performance simulations compatible with both legacy and contemporary hardware.\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and optimize 3D game simulations and environments using Panda3D for AI training applications.\n• Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to transform requirements into technical solutions.\n• Implement, maintain, and debug Python and C++ codebases integrated with Panda3D.\n• Contribute to version control workflows using Git Hub to ensure smooth project collaboration.\n• Ensure cross-platform compatibility and performance across diverse hardware configurations.\n• Document architectural decisions, code, and processes clearly to support collaborative development.\n• Actively participate in code reviews, brainstorming sessions, and team meetings, emphasizing exceptional verbal and written communication.\nRequired Skills And Qualifications\n• Proven, hands-on experience developing with Panda3D—experience with similar engines does not substitute.\n• Advanced proficiency in Python and C++ programming languages.\n• Strong command of Git Hub for code management, branching, and pull requests.\n• Deep understanding of 3D graphics pipelines, simulation logic, and cross-platform development.\n• Exceptional written and verbal communication skills—clear documentation and collaboration are critical.\n• Ability to work independently in a remote environment, meeting deadlines with minimal supervision.\n• Demonstrated attention to detail and a problem-solving mindset.\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Prior game development experience for AI, simulation, or training purposes.\n• Familiarity with optimizing 3D assets for performance across a range of hardware.\n• Background in collaborative, distributed Agile environments.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'panda3d,game,python game,developer panda3d,game developer,hardware,3d,python,training,panda3d remote,simulation,engines,performance,ai,git hub,simulations,verbal,cross platform,hub,ai training,developer,using,job,exceptional,platform'),(347,'jsearch','EYGu4fbDz1NKdituAAAAAA==','Remote Full Stack Developer Jobs for Malaysians','The Elite Job',NULL,'MY',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/12690/remote-full-stack-developer-jobs-for-malaysians','Job Summary:\n\nThe Elite Job is looking for a highly skilled and motivated Remote Full Stack Developer based in Malaysia to join our growing tech team. As a Full Stack Developer, you will be responsible for both the front-end and back-end development of innovative web applications. The ideal candidate will have a passion for technology, a solid understanding of modern development practices, and the ability to work collaboratively in a remote environment. This is an exciting opportunity for developers looking to make a significant impact while working with a dynamic and innovative team.\nKey Responsibilities:\n• * Develop and maintain web applications, including both front-end and back-end components.\n• * Write clean, maintainable, and efficient code across multiple technology stacks.\n• * Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other developers to deliver high-quality features and solutions.\n• * Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize applications for maximum performance and scalability.\n• * Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies and trends in full-stack development.\n• * Ensure cross-platform compatibility and responsiveness of applications.\n• * Participate in code reviews, knowledge sharing, and collaborative team efforts to improve development practices.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications:\n• * Proficiency in front-end technologies like HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and frameworks such as React or Angular.\n• * Strong experience with back-end technologies like Node.js, Express, or similar technologies.\n• * Expertise in database management, particularly SQL and NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB, PostgreSQL, MySQL).\n• * Familiarity with version control tools such as Git.\n• * Solid understanding of RESTful API development and integration.\n• * Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• * Experience with agile development methodologies.\n• * Excellent communication skills and the ability to work independently in a remote setup.\n• Experience:\n• * Minimum of 2-4 years of experience as a Full Stack Developer or similar role.\n• * Proven experience building and maintaining complex web applications.\n• * Experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, Google Cloud) is a plus.\n• Working Hours:\n• * This is a remote position with flexible working hours.\n• * Collaboration with a global team will require availability during some overlapping hours with team members in other time zones (flexible arrangements can be discussed).\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n• * Strong knowledge of front-end and back-end technologies.\n• * Ability to work in a collaborative, cross-functional team environment.\n• * Ability to troubleshoot, test, and debug applications.\n• * Knowledge of Agile software development methodologies.\n• * Self-motivated and disciplined, able to manage your time efficiently and meet deadlines in a remote setting.\n• Benefits:\n• * Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• * Flexible working hours and the opportunity to work remotely.\n• * Health insurance coverage and other employee welfare benefits.\n• * Opportunities for career growth and professional development.\n• * Collaborative work environment with a focus on innovation and teamwork.\n• * Paid time off and holidays.\n• Why Join:\n• * Be a part of a dynamic and rapidly growing company that values innovation and creativity.\n• * Work in a remote-first environment, providing you the flexibility to balance personal and professional life.\n• * Take on challenging and impactful projects that will push your skills to the next level.\n• * Enjoy a supportive and inclusive work culture that fosters learning and growth.\n• How to Apply:\n\nIf you are excited about the opportunity to work as a Remote Full Stack Developer with The Elite Job, please send your updated resume, portfolio (if applicable), and a brief cover letter outlining your experience and why you would be a great fit for the role. Applications can be submitted via our job portal or sent directly to us.\n\nWe look forward to reviewing your application and potentially having you join our team!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','end,applications,work,development,technologies,remote,remote stack,experience,stack developer,team,hours,working,end technologies,working hours,skills,job,stack,work remote,development methodologies,elite,elite job,ability,flexible,ability work,end end'),(348,'jsearch','G1O5IOUM0f6fSDxcAAAAAA==','Senior Full Stack Engineer (Anywhere in South America, fully remote), Remote Job','PadSplit',NULL,NULL,0,'https://dynamitejobs.com/company/padsplit/remote-job/senior-full-stack-engineer-anywhere-in-south-america-fully-remote','The Role We Need:\n\nPadSplit is hiring Full Stack Engineers to join an international engineering team to ensure seamless integration between frontend and backend components, enhancing the overall efficiency of product development while working in a Pod. This role requires a versatile tech background for quick iteration and problem solving, while working closely in a Pod of Software and QA Engineers led by a Product Manager. We need someone who can foster a cohesive and agile development environment to drive the pod’s productivity and innovation.\n\nThe Person We Are Looking For:\n\nWe need a versatile developer who is proficient in both frontend and backend technologies, such as JavaScript, React, React Native, Django, AWS, and Postgres databases. The ideal candidate has a strong problem-solving mindset, capable of quickly adapting to new challenges and technologies. The right candidate must excel in collaborative environments, effectively communicating with a cross-functional team to deliver high-quality, scalable solutions.\nHere’s What You’ll Do Day-To-Day:\n• Develop and maintain both frontend and backend components of the application using technologies like React, React Native, and Django.\n• Build and optimize mobile applications using React Native, ensuring smooth performance across iOS and Android.\n• Collaborate with designers, product managers, and other developers to translate requirements into technical specifications and deliverable features.\n• Conduct code reviews to ensure best practices and maintainable code standards are upheld across the team.\n• Optimize application performance and address any technical issues or bugs that arise across web and mobile platforms.\n• Implement and maintain automated testing for both frontend (React, React Native) and backend (Django) components to ensure code reliability and quality.\n• Participate in daily stand-ups and sprint planning meetings to align on priorities and progress.\n• Manage and maintain databases, ensuring efficient data storage and retrieval.\n• Stay updated with the latest industry trends and technologies, integrating them into the development process when appropriate.\n\nHere’s What You’ll Need To Be Successful:\n• Proficiency in frontend technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and frontend frameworks like React.\n• Experience in mobile application development using React Native, including knowledge of mobile performance optimization and platform-specific development for iOS and Android.\n• Strong backend development skills with expertise in at least one backend technology such as Python (Django) or Node.js.\n• Experience with database management systems like MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or similar.\n• Knowledge of RESTful API design and implementation.\n• Familiarity with version control systems like Git and collaborative development workflows.\n• Ability to optimize application performance and troubleshoot issues across both web and mobile platforms.\n• Strong problem-solving skills and a proactive approach to debugging and resolving technical challenges.\n• Effective communication and teamwork skills, with the ability to collaborate closely with designers, product managers, and other team members in an agile environment.\n\nThe Interview Process:\n• Your application will be reviewed for possible next steps by the Hiring Manager.\n• If you meet eligibility requirements, the next step would be a video screen with a member of the PeopleOps team for about thirty (30) minutes.\n• If warranted, the next step would be a video interview with our VP of Engineering for one (1) hour.\n• If warranted, the next step would be a video panel interview with key stakeholders at PadSplit for two (2) hours.\n• The panel interview will require a candidate to work on a technical assessment where you will showcase your software skills to the panel for discussion.\n• If warranted, then we move to contract!\n\n$50,000 - $75,000 a year\n\nCompensation is based on the role\'s scope, market benchmarks, the person\'s expertise and experience, and the impact of their contributions to our business goals.\n\n#LI-Remote\n\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'react,development,application,native,react native,mobile,frontend,backend,interview,technical,like,technologies,team,performance,product,skills,hiring,ensure,frontend backend,problem solving,react react,panel,video,problem,warranted'),(349,'jsearch','knolH_GfpBjxryukAAAAAA==','Senior Full Stack Developer, UNICEF Office of Innovation, 12 Months, Remote','UNICEF',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/developer-office-innovation-months-at-unicef','? Exciting job opportunity ?\n\nUNICEF’s Office of Innovation is looking for two Senior Full-Stack Developers to take the engineering lead on an ambitious project—The Learning Cabinet! This online platform connects education decision-makers worldwide with curated EdTech solutions tailored to their unique contexts. ??\n\nWhat You’ll Do:\n\nAs a Senior Full-Stack Developer, you’ll spearhead a headless Drupal and Next.js platform deployed on Cloudflare, empowering education decision-makers to access EdTech tools that will make a tangible difference in children’s learning outcomes. You’ll collaborate with an agile, interdisciplinary team to come up with innovative solutions and implement exciting value propositions—all geared towards impactful change. For more information see our Terms of Reference.\n\nWhat’s in it for You?\n• Be part of a global team at the forefront of tech innovation for social good. ?\n• Use your expertise to shape an MVP into a scalable solution that can reach help reaching millions of children and solve a global learning crisis.\n• Work remotely with a passionate team and join us for a 3-day design sprint in beautiful Helsinki, Finland! ???\n• Are you ready to use your skills to reimagine education for every child?\n\nApply today, and let’s make education a transformative journey for all! ?????',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'education,senior,senior stack,unicef office,unicef,makers,office innovation,education decision,decision makers,decision,children,innovation,ll,office,exciting,edtech,learning,global,use,make,platform,team,solutions,stack developer,stack'),(350,'jsearch','4YZcMdOKbHJgu5CyAAAAAA==','Full Stack Developer, Work from Home','Career.zycto',NULL,'SG',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/full-stack-developer-work-from-home-2/','About Company\n\nAre you ready to revolutionize digital solutions from anywhere? Career.zycto is an innovative, agile technology firm dedicated to pushing the boundaries of what\'s possible in software development. We thrive on creating robust, scalable, and user-centric applications that make a tangible impact. For a Full Stack Developer, we offer a dynamic remote environment where your contributions are valued, your skills are continuously honed, and your ideas can truly shape the future of our products. Join a team passionate about cutting-edge tech and collaborative problem-solving, empowered by a culture that prioritizes flexibility and excellence.\n\nJob Description\n\nCareer.zycto is actively seeking an exceptionally skilled and highly motivated Full Stack Developer to join our dynamic and expanding remote team. This is a critical role where you will wield significant influence, instrumental in the complete lifecycle of our innovative web applications – from initial concept and design through development, testing, and ultimately, deployment. We are searching for a technical virtuoso who excels in a fast-paced, highly collaborative environment, demonstrating mastery of both cutting-edge front-end and robust back-end technologies. Your passion for delivering high-quality, scalable, and user-centric software solutions will be central to your success here.\n\nAs a Full Stack Developer at Career.zycto, you will act as the crucial link between visionary design and powerful, efficient functionality. You will navigate and contribute across our entire technology stack, bringing complex and impactful projects to fruition. Your daily tasks will involve active participation in architectural discussions, contributing valuable insights into system design, and meticulously writing clean, optimized, and maintainable code. Ensuring the seamless integration of our various services and third-party APIs will also be a key area of focus.\n\nThis role offers an incredible opportunity to make a tangible and significant impact on our product roadmap, allowing you to leverage and experiment with cutting-edge development tools and methodologies. You\'ll have ample room to grow your expertise within a supportive, forward-thinking, and truly remote-first culture that values autonomy and innovation. If you are driven by the challenge of building compelling new features, solving intricate technical problems with elegant solutions, and contributing to a company that places a premium on innovation, continuous learning, and employee empowerment, we strongly encourage you to submit your application. We are deeply committed to fostering an inclusive environment where diverse perspectives and backgrounds are celebrated and directly contribute to our collective success.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and maintain robust, scalable, and secure full-stack web applications.\n• Write clean, efficient, and well-documented code across both front-end (UI/UX) and back-end (APIs, databases) components.\n• Collaborate closely with product managers, designers, and other engineers to define, scope, and deliver new features.\n• Participate in architectural discussions, code reviews, and provide constructive feedback to peers.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize application performance and reliability.\n• Integrate third-party APIs and services as required.\n• Stay updated with emerging technologies and industry best practices to continuously improve our tech stack and development processes.\n• Ensure the technical feasibility of UI/UX designs and translate them into functional applications.\n• Deploy and monitor applications in a cloud environment.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in modern JavaScript frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js).\n• Strong command of Node.js and related frameworks (e.g., Express.js) for back-end development.\n• Expertise in relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL) and/or NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB).\n• Solid understanding of RESTful API design and implementation.\n• Experience with version control systems, especially Git.\n• Familiarity with cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, GCP).\n• Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to work independently.\n• Excellent communication and teamwork abilities for a remote setting.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.\n• Experience with containerization technologies (Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.\n• Experience with testing frameworks (e.g., Jest, React Testing Library, Mocha, Chai).\n• Familiarity with serverless architectures.\n• Contribution to open-source projects or a strong portfolio of personal projects.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health and wellness benefits.\n• Generous paid time off and public holidays.\n• Flexible remote work environment.\n• Budget for home office setup and professional development.\n• Opportunities for continuous learning and career growth.\n• Supportive and collaborative team culture.\n• Annual company retreats (optional, location-dependent).\n\nHow to Apply\n\nEager to make an impact with Career.zycto? Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and cover letter. We look forward to reviewing your qualifications and learning how your skills can contribute to our innovative team.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'zycto,career zycto,career,applications,end,stack,design,cutting,edge,cutting edge,contribute,environment,development,stack developer,architectural,architectural discussions,discussions,robust,databases,frameworks,make,innovative,robust scalable,scalable user,make tangible'),(352,'jsearch','5PZfj6q5wM2ZOyaTAAAAAA==','Senior Full-Stack AI EdTech Engineer | Remote','Paradox EN',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5084247958/e/','A leading EdTech company is seeking a Senior Full Stack Developer to create innovative online learning experiences. Located in Dubai or Lisbon, you will develop features for a scalable learning management system, implement AI functionalities, and work in a collaborative environment. This mid-senior level role requires expertise in Type Script, React.js, and Tailwind CSS, while offering a competitive salary, professional development, and remote work options.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'senior,edtech,senior stack,ai,learning experiences,salary professional,lisbon develop,lisbon,js tailwind,requires expertise,leading edtech,located dubai,located,innovative online,functionalities work,functionalities,learning management,tailwind css,tailwind,options 18808,features scalable,expertise type,senior level,experiences located,offering competitive'),(355,'jsearch','B6vV77d2tSZKCEJhAAAAAA==','Freelance Full Stack Engineer Jobs – Work Online','BuildSphere Technologies',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/us/job/1244/Freelance-Full-Stack-Engineer-Jobs-%E2%80%93-Work-Online','Job Summary\n\nBuildSphere Technologies is seeking a talented and highly motivated Freelance Full Stack Engineer to join our dynamic team on a remote, work-from-home basis. The ideal candidate will possess strong expertise in both front-end and back-end development, with a passion for creating scalable, high-performance web applications. This role provides the flexibility to work online while contributing to innovative projects across diverse industries.\n\nAs a Freelance Full Stack Engineer, you will collaborate with cross-functional teams, including product managers, designers, and other developers, to deliver robust solutions that meet client needs. Your creativity, problem-solving skills, and ability to manage multiple projects will be crucial for success in this position.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop and maintain responsive web applications using modern front-end and back-end technologies.\n• Write clean, efficient, and well-documented code following best practices.\n• Collaborate with designers, product managers, and other developers to deliver innovative solutions.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and optimize applications for maximum performance and scalability.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure high-quality software development.\n• Stay updated on emerging technologies and frameworks to continuously enhance the development process.\n• Ensure security, data protection, and compliance standards are met in all projects.\n• Communicate project progress, risks, and technical solutions clearly to stakeholders.\n\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n• Strong proficiency in JavaScript, HTML, CSS, and modern front-end frameworks (React, Angular, or Vue.js).\n• Experience with back-end technologies such as Node.js, Python, Ruby, or Java.\n• Proficient in database management (SQL, NoSQL, MongoDB, PostgreSQL).\n• Understanding of RESTful APIs, GraphQL, and web services integration.\n• Experience with version control systems, preferably Git/GitHub.\n• Knowledge of cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud is a plus.\n• Strong problem-solving skills and ability to work independently in a remote environment.\n• Excellent communication and collaboration skills.\n\nExperience\n• Minimum 2 years of experience in full-stack development or similar roles.\n• Proven track record of delivering web applications or software projects successfully.\n• Freelance or remote work experience is highly desirable.\n\nWorking Hours\n• Flexible working hours with the ability to meet project deadlines.\n• Remote work environment allowing you to manage your schedule efficiently.\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• Ability to learn new technologies quickly and adapt to evolving project requirements.\n• Strong analytical and logical reasoning skills.\n• Attention to detail and a commitment to writing high-quality code.\n• Self-motivated with strong organizational and time-management abilities.\n• Collaborative mindset and willingness to contribute to a team-oriented culture.\n\nBenefits\n• Work remotely from anywhere in the world.\n• Flexible schedule tailored to your productivity.\n• Opportunity to work on diverse projects with cutting-edge technologies.\n• Competitive freelance compensation based on experience and project complexity.\n• Professional growth and development opportunities in a fast-growing tech company.\n\nWhy Join BuildSphere Technologies\n\nAt BuildSphere Technologies, we empower our freelance engineers to thrive in a supportive and innovative environment. You will work with a team of talented professionals on exciting projects that make a real impact. Join us to enhance your skills, contribute to innovative solutions, and enjoy the freedom of remote freelance work.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their resume and portfolio showcasing past projects to us with the subject line: “Application – Freelance Full Stack Engineer”. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for a virtual interview.',NULL,10.00,20.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','freelance,technologies,freelance stack,projects,work,stack engineer,end,skills,buildsphere technologies,buildsphere,innovative,engineer,experience,project,remote work,strong,applications,solutions,work online,web,ability,development,developers deliver,modern end,innovative solutions'),(356,'jsearch','To1RgtOXgMwf4qG2AAAAAA==','Full Stack Developer (MERN) - Real-time Student Analytics Dashboard','GradeBuzz',NULL,'US',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/20189/full-stack-developer-mern-real-time-student-analytics-dashboard','Job Summary\n\nGradeBuzz is seeking a highly skilled and innovative Full Stack Developer specializing in the MERN stack (MongoDB, Express.js, React, Node.js) to design and develop a cutting-edge real-time student analytics dashboard. This role involves building scalable, high-performance applications that transform educational data into actionable insights for students, educators, and institutions. The ideal candidate is passionate about EdTech, data visualization, and delivering seamless user experiences.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nDesign, develop, and maintain full-stack web applications using the MERN stack.\n\nBuild real-time data pipelines and dashboards for student performance tracking and analytics.\n\nDevelop responsive and intuitive UI components using React.js.\n\nCreate robust backend services and RESTful APIs using Node.js and Express.js.\n\nIntegrate third-party APIs and data sources for enriched analytics capabilities.\n\nOptimize applications for speed, scalability, and security.\n\nCollaborate with product managers, designers, and data teams to define and implement new features.\n\nEnsure code quality through testing, code reviews, and best development practices.\n\nTroubleshoot and debug issues across the full application stack.\n\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n\nStrong proficiency in MongoDB, Express.js, React.js, and Node.js (MERN stack).\n\nSolid understanding of JavaScript (ES6+), HTML5, and CSS3.\n\nExperience with real-time technologies such as WebSockets or Socket.io.\n\nFamiliarity with data visualization libraries (e.g., Chart.js, D3.js, Recharts).\n\nKnowledge of RESTful API development and integration.\n\nExperience with version control systems like Git.\n\nUnderstanding of cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, or GCP) is a plus.\n\nStrong problem-solving and analytical thinking skills.\n\nExperience\n\n2–5 years of hands-on experience in full stack development.\n\nProven experience in building scalable web applications.\n\nPrior experience in EdTech, analytics platforms, or dashboard development is highly preferred.\n\nWorking Hours\n\nFull-time position.\n\nFlexible working hours with overlap for team collaboration.\n\nRemote/Hybrid work options available depending on project needs.\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n\nAbility to handle real-time data processing and performance optimization.\n\nStrong understanding of UI/UX principles.\n\nExcellent communication and teamwork skills.\n\nAbility to work in an agile development environment.\n\nSelf-motivated with the ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines.\n\nBenefits\n\nCompetitive salary package with performance-based incentives.\n\nFlexible work environment (Remote/Hybrid).\n\nHealth and wellness benefits.\n\nOpportunities for learning, certifications, and career growth.\n\nAccess to the latest tools and technologies.\n\nCollaborative and innovative work culture.\n\nWhy Join GradeBuzz\n\nBe part of a mission-driven company transforming education through technology.\n\nWork on impactful projects that improve student outcomes.\n\nCollaborate with a passionate and forward-thinking team.\n\nOpportunity to innovate and build scalable solutions in a fast-growing EdTech environment.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates can apply by submitting their updated resume, portfolio, and GitHub profile showcasing relevant projects. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for a technical assessment followed by interview rounds.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','stack,real time,analytics,data,mern,student,js,real,dashboard,mern stack,express js,edtech,express,time,data visualization,student analytics,time student,visualization,mongodb express,stack developer,analytics dashboard,time data,experience,mongodb,node'),(358,'jsearch','FsgaVWESpIizzZIzAAAAAA==','FullStack Software Developer (React/Node.js) – Limassol / Nicosia / Athens / Thessaloniki / Remote','XM',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/nicosia-limassol-athens-software-developer-react-at-xmcmp','FullStack Software Developer (React/Nodejs)\n\nThe Role:\n\nWe are looking for a FullStack Software Developer with strong analytical and problem-solving skills to join our Software Development team. The developer will be responsible for designing, building, and maintaining advanced web applications, ensuring code is maintainable, scalable, and high-performing.\n\nThe role involves active participation in system architecture and Agile collaboration to support project delivery. This position is ideal for someone with a solid background in JavaScript development who enjoys working across the full application stack to build robust server-side components and advanced user interfaces.\n\nThe main responsibilities of the position include:\n• Develops and maintains scalable software applications, ensuring smooth operation across both front-end and back-end stacks\n• Builds advanced user-facing applications using React and robust server-side components using Nodejs\n• Produces detailed technical specifications and implements software in line with business and system requirements\n• Contributes to system design and architecture, ensuring alignment with best practices and long-term maintainability\n• Conducts code reviews to ensure quality, consistency, and adherence to software development standards\n• Continuously monitors application performance and reliability, proactively optimizing systems and resolving issues\n• Works in close collaboration with other developers and stakeholders to gather technical requirements and define project specifications\n• Takes ownership of assigned tasks, ensuring timely delivery and effective communication throughout the software development lifecycle\n\nMain requirements:\n• BSc/MSc in Computer Science, or any other relevant degree\n• Minimum 5 years of work experience in JavaScript development\n• Proven experience in building and maintaining applications using React and Nodejs\n• Solid understanding of the React life cycle, HTML, CSS/SCSS, JavaScript\n• Solid understanding of information design and UI/UX principle\n• Knowledge of REST or equivalent APIs, microservices architecture, and web services implementation\n• Basic knowledge of databases (SQL)\n• Knowledge of GIT\n• Methodical problem solver with strong critical thinking skills\n• Self-motivated, organized, and proactive with the ability to work independently with minimal supervision\n• Excellent team collaboration, interpersonal, and communication skills\n• Fluency in English\n\nThe following will be considered an advantage:\n• Ability to transform raw data into presentable and intuitive tables or graphs\n• Knowledge of Typescript\n• Knowledge of AWS Services, Kubernetes, and Docker\n\nBenefit from:\n• Attractive remuneration package\n• Intellectually stimulating work environment\n• Continuous personal development and international training opportunities\n• Attractive relocation package and support for a smooth relocation for you and your family\n\nThe Hiring Experience: What Awaits You\n• Let’s Connect – Intro Chat with Talent Acquisition\n• Bring It to Life – Role-Specific Take-Home Task\n• Final Connection – Final Interview\n\nAll applications will be treated with strict confidentiality!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'software,applications,software developer,fullstack software,fullstack,ensuring,react,development,advanced,software development,knowledge,solid,nodejs,final,building maintaining,main,server components,life,specifications,developer react,attractive,react nodejs,advanced user,applications ensuring,robust server'),(359,'jsearch','M8xx_ily4f4DzoE-AAAAAA==','Full Stack Developer, Work from Home','Career.zycto',NULL,'CA',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/full-stack-developer-work-from-home-4/','About Company\n\nSeeking an environment where your code genuinely impacts global projects? Career.zycto is a dynamic force in talent acquisition, specializing in connecting top-tier technical professionals with groundbreaking opportunities. We operate at the intersection of innovation and human potential, fostering a culture of continuous learning and growth. For a Full Stack Developer, this means engaging with diverse challenges and cutting-edge technologies that shape tomorrow. We pride ourselves on creating a supportive yet ambitious remote work setting, ensuring you have the tools and autonomy to excel. Join us and build solutions that matter, from wherever you are.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a passionate Full Stack Developer with a knack for building robust, scalable applications? Career.zycto is seeking a talented individual to join our growing team. This remote opportunity allows you to leverage your expertise in both front-end and back-end development to create seamless user experiences and powerful server-side solutions. You\'ll be instrumental in developing and maintaining our core platforms, contributing to all phases of the development lifecycle from concept to deployment. We\'re looking for someone who thrives in an agile environment, is a proactive problem-solver, and is eager to collaborate with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality software. If you\'re ready to make a significant impact from the comfort of your home office, we encourage you to apply. This role offers the chance to work on challenging projects, utilize modern tech stacks, and contribute to a company that values innovation and employee growth. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive remote culture where every team member feels empowered and connected.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, and maintain responsive web applications using modern front-end frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js).\n• Build and manage robust APIs and microservices with back-end technologies (e.g., Node.js, Python, Java, Ruby on Rails).\n• Collaborate with product managers, designers, and other developers to define, design, and ship new features.\n• Write clean, well-documented, and testable code.\n• Implement and maintain secure coding practices and data protection measures.\n• Participate in code reviews to ensure code quality and knowledge sharing.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software.\n• Stay up-to-date with emerging technologies and industry trends.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Proficiency in at least one modern JavaScript front-end framework (React, Angular, or Vue.js).\n• Strong experience with a back-end language/framework (e.g., Node.js, Python/Django/Flask, Java/Spring Boot, Ruby on Rails).\n• Expertise in database design and management (SQL and NoSQL databases like PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB).\n• Solid understanding of RESTful APIs and microservices architecture.\n• Experience with version control systems (Git).\n• Familiarity with cloud platforms (AWS, Azure, GCP).\n• Excellent problem-solving and debugging skills.\n• Strong communication and collaboration abilities in a remote setting.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• Experience with containerization technologies (Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Knowledge of CI/CD pipelines.\n• Experience with unit and integration testing frameworks.\n• Familiarity with Agile/Scrum methodologies.\n• Contributions to open-source projects.\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Flexible work schedule and generous paid time off.\n• Dedicated budget for professional development and training.\n• Home office setup allowance.\n• Access to cutting-edge tools and technologies.\n• Collaborative and supportive remote work environment.\n• Opportunities for career growth and advancement.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nReady to shape the future with us? Please click the application link below to submit your resume and a cover letter detailing your relevant experience and why you are a great fit for a remote Full Stack Developer role at Career.zycto. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'end,technologies,career,zycto,career zycto,stack developer,remote,supportive,home,supportive remote,experience,code,work,apis microservices,rails,home office,ruby rails,js python,fostering,framework,growth,modern,js,projects,office'),(360,'jsearch','sGMMnvIC_UTM7NurAAAAAA==','Software Engineer (React + Node.js) â€“ Remote','HR Service Jobs',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/19073/software-engineer-react-node.js-%E2%80%93-remote','SleekSky is a fast-growing engineering studio that partners with venture-backed product teams to ship modern, cloud-native software. We’re hiring a Software Engineer to join one of our health-tech clients and help build a scalable, user-centric platform that’s making a real-world impact—without revealing any confidential project details.\n\nWhat you’ll do\n• Build and ship production-ready React features that feel fast, accessible and polished.\n• Design and maintain Node.js / Express APIs that are clean, secure and well-documented.\n• Leverage AWS services (EC2, Lambda, Elastic Cache / Redis, load balancers, etc.) to deliver reliable, high-performance solutions.\n• Automate CI/CD pipelines with GitHub Actions and uphold strong Git workflows.\n• Collaborate in an agile, fully remote team that values code reviews, knowledge-sharing and continuous improvement.\n• Champion engineering best practices—testing, monitoring, and infrastructure-as-code—while keeping an eye on new tech that can raise the bar.\n\nWhat you’ll bring\n• 2+ years of hands-on experience in full-stack development.\n• Proven expertise with React (hooks, component architecture, state management) and modern JavaScript/TypeScript.\n• Solid experience building RESTful services in Node.js with Express (or similar).\n• Familiarity with AWS fundamentals (EC2, Lambda, load balancing, caching layers).\n• Comfortable with Git, GitHub and automated CI/CD pipelines (e.g., GitHub Actions).\n• Self-motivated, proactive and enthusiastic about learning new technologies and sharing knowledge with the team.\n• Clear, concise communication skills—vital for an all-remote environment.\n\nNice-to-haves\n• Experience with infrastructure-as-code (Terraform, CloudFormation, CDK).\n• Exposure to containerisation (Docker, ECS, EKS) or serverless architecture patterns.\n• Prior work in health-tech or other regulated domains.\n\nWhy SleekSky?\n\nAt SleekSky, you’ll join a culture that puts people first—pair programming, regular knowledge-sharing sessions and a genuine passion for building things the right way. Expect autonomy, trust and a runway to grow your craft alongside enthusiastic peers.\n\nReady to level up with SleekSky? Submit your résumé on your preferred hiring portal and we’ll be in touch right away.\nSkills:- React.js, NodeJS (Node.js), TypeScript, Javascript and AWS Lambda',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'sleeksky,lambda,ll,github,sharing,js,node js,node,ec2 lambda,ec2,pipelines github,github actions,infrastructure code,actions,enthusiastic,load,health tech,ship,right,infrastructure,knowledge sharing,js express,typescript,cd pipelines,software engineer'),(361,'jsearch','e5rXmzCulMln6NqHAAAAAA==','Full-Stack Engineer — AI-Driven, Remote; React​/Vue + Java','Binance',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5045044875/e/','Position: Full-Stack Engineer — AI-Driven, Remote (React/Vue + Java)\nA leading blockchain ecosystem in Singapore is seeking a Full Stack Developer to design and maintain web applications and backend services. You will work with React/Vue for front-end and Java/Spring Cloud for backend development, taking ownership of features and collaborating with a talented team. Qualified candidates will have 3–5 years of experience, strong proficiency in both frontend and backend technologies, and a passion for AI and the crypto industry.\n\nThis role offers opportunities for innovation and career growth, along with competitive salary and benefits.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'react vue,java,driven remote,engineer ai,vue java,remote react,ai,vue,ai driven,stack engineer,backend,driven,react,engineer,stack,applications backend,team qualified,singapore seeking,taking ownership,benefits 18808,ecosystem singapore,ecosystem,blockchain ecosystem,candidates years,leading blockchain'),(362,'jsearch','43tTStLo6BU18z_LAAAAAA==','Web Developer – Website & Payment Integration','Contra',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/web-developer-website-payment-integration-at-contra','Contra is seeking a skilled Web Developer to join our team for a special project aimed at enhancing our platform. The successful candidate will be responsible for developing and integrating a new website with a payment system. This role is ideal for an individual who is proficient in web development and has experience with payment integration.\n\nResponsibilities\n• Develop a user-friendly website that aligns with Contra’s brand and objectives.\n• Integrate a secure and efficient payment system into the website.\n• Collaborate with the team to ensure seamless functionality and user experience.\n• Provide regular updates and reports on progress.\n• Troubleshoot and resolve any issues that arise during the development process.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'website,payment,web developer,website payment,payment integration,contra,web,user,integration,seamless functionality,friendly website,experience provide,experience payment,regular updates,resolve issues,enhancing platform,efficient payment,developing integrating,developer website,skilled web,successful candidate,develop user,seeking skilled,team special,role ideal'),(363,'jsearch','pgS0ZhmNnH7P0iPvAAAAAA==','Fullstack Software Engineer - Commerce​/Partner Success; Remote','Hopper',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5046910336/e/','Position: Fullstack Software Engineer - Commerce/Partner Success (100% Remote )\n\nAbout the Role\n\nAs a Full‑Stack Software Engineer within Hopper Technology Solutions (HTS), you will architect the travel commerce engines powering our rapid expansion into APAC markets. This role is critical to building and localizing world‑class travel portals for major financial institutions and consumer brands (such as Comm Bank and ), directly impacting how millions of users in the region experience travel.\nWhat Would Your Day‑to‑Day Look Like\n• Design and operate full‑stack solutions and APIs optimized for high‑scale B2B commerce partnerships across APAC.\n• Collaborate closely with product and engineering teams to localize portal features, ensuring seamless integration with regional payment and distribution standards.\n• Leverage LLMs and AI tooling to generate production‑grade code that accelerates the delivery of partner‑specific requirements.\n• Develop and maintain gRPC and REST‑based microservices that power real‑time travel inventory and fintech ancillaries.\n• Work autonomously to resolve complex technical challenges while maintaining strong asynchronous alignment with global stakeholders.\n• Iterate quickly on engineering improvements that enhance the scalability and performance of our B2B travel ecosystems.\nAn Ideal Candidate Has\n• Extensive experience with React and Type Script used to build highly localized, performant web interfaces for complex e‑commerce environments.\n• Proficiency in Scala and distributed systems or a strong desire to apply functional programming to large‑scale backend architectures.\n• Commercial mindset that prioritizes regional product‑market fit and the unique user behaviors found in APAC digital ecosystems.\n• Adeptness with AI‑driven workflows, including the use of LLMs for development and the implementation of agentic AI systems to enhance partner support.\n• Hands‑on knowledge of GCP and cloud‑native practices, specifically in managing the latency and data residency requirements of international partnerships.\n• Strong technical agility and the ability to fearlessly navigate unknown codebases to deliver high‑impact features under tight commercial deadlines.\nPerks And Benefits Of Working With Us\n• Well‑funded and proven startup with large ambitions, competitive salary, and the upsides of a pre‑IPO equity package.\n• Hopper covers 100% of the premiums for a group Health and Dental insurance plan.\n• Hopper offers life insurance and critical illness coverage to all employees.\n• All employees and their dependents have access to an on‑demand network of international doctors – anywhere and anytime.\n• Very generous parental leave, much above industry standards.\n• Unlimited PTO.\n• Access to co‑working space on demand through Flex Desk AND Work‑from‑home stipend.\n• Hopper makes the full employer contributions to CPF for first and second year Permanent Residents.\n• Carrot cash travel stipend.\n• Entrepreneurial culture where pushing limits and taking risks is everyday business.\n• Open communication with management and company leadership.\n• Small, dynamic teams = massive impact.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'travel,commerce,hopper,partner,apac,software engineer,partnerships,partner success,100,scale,employees,ecosystems,llms,b2b,regional,engineer commerce,commerce partner,stipend,demand,ai,enhance,commercial,large,fullstack,fullstack software'),(365,'jsearch','xNlsg3a37VKr4y4eAAAAAA==','Senior React.js & Golang / Java Developer','Lemon.io',NULL,NULL,0,'https://remote.com/jobs/lemon-io-c1eumcoq/senior-react-js-golang-java-developer-j1hm1a9l','Are you a talented Senior Developer looking for a remote job that lets you show your skills and get decent compensation? Look no further than Lemon.io — the marketplace that connects you with hand-picked startups in the US and Europe.\n\nWhat we offer:\n• The rate depends on your seniority level, skills and experience. We\'ve already paid out over $11M to our engineers.\n• No more hunting for clients or negotiating rates — let us handle the business side of things so you can focus on what you do best.\n• We\'ll manually find the best project for you according to your skills and preferences.\n• Choose a schedule that works best for you. It’s possible to communicate async or minimally overlap