g of cross-browser compatibility issues and modern responsive design techniques.\n• *\n\nExcellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• *\n\nAbility to work independently and collaboratively in a remote environment.\n• Experience\n• *\n\n2–5 years of professional experience in front-end web development.\n• *\n\nPrior remote working experience is an added advantage.\n• *\n\nPortfolio or links to past work demonstrating UI/UX implementation are preferred.\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFlexible working hours with core collaboration time between 9:00 AM – 5:00 PM (GMT or as per project requirements).\n• *\n\nFull-time remote position with occasional virtual team meetings.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nDeep understanding of front-end architecture and web performance optimization.\n• *\n\nStrong grasp of design aesthetics and attention to pixel-perfect details.\n• *\n\nKnowledge of accessibility standards (WCAG) and SEO best practices.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with Agile/Scrum development methodologies.\n• *\n\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary based on experience and skills.\n• *\n\n100% remote work flexibility and work-life balance.\n• *\n\nPaid time off, health and wellness benefits.\n• *\n\nOpportunities for professional development, training, and certifications.\n• *\n\nInclusive, supportive, and collaborative team culture.\n• Why Join HR Service Jobs\n\nAt HR Service Jobs, we believe in empowering professionals to grow and innovate from anywhere. You will be part of a forward-thinking organization that values creativity, collaboration, and continuous improvement. We prioritize flexibility, modern tools, and a supportive environment that encourages both personal and professional growth.\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are encouraged to apply by sending their resume, portfolio, and a brief cover letter outlining relevant experience to us with the subject line Front End Developer – Remote. Join us today and help build the future of digital experiences with HR Service Jobs!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','end,end developer,hr service,service,hr,service jobs,jobs,experience,remote,web,developer remote,skills,development,angular vue,react angular,00,digital experiences,modern,accessibility,developer,responsive,professional,work,experience end,experiences'),(409,'jsearch','t-wdhN3hiJrEE3ABAAAAAA==','Frontend Developer Intern - Next.js Responsive Web Design','GradeBuzz',NULL,'US',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/20209/frontend-developer-intern-next.js-responsive-web-design','Job Summary\n\nGradeBuzz is seeking a passionate and detail-oriented Frontend Developer Intern to join our dynamic product development team. This role is ideal for individuals who are eager to build modern, high-performance web applications using Next.js and responsive design principles. As an intern, you will work closely with designers, backend developers, and product managers to create seamless and engaging user experiences across devices.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nDevelop and maintain responsive web interfaces using Next.js and modern JavaScript frameworks.\n\nTranslate UI/UX designs into high-quality, pixel-perfect code.\n\nOptimize applications for maximum speed, scalability, and performance.\n\nEnsure cross-browser compatibility and mobile responsiveness.\n\nCollaborate with backend developers to integrate APIs and services.\n\nParticipate in code reviews and follow best coding practices.\n\nTroubleshoot and debug issues to improve application functionality.\n\nStay updated with the latest frontend development trends and technologies.\n\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n\nBasic to intermediate knowledge of JavaScript, HTML5, and CSS3.\n\nFamiliarity with React.js and Next.js framework.\n\nUnderstanding of responsive design and mobile-first development.\n\nKnowledge of version control systems such as Git.\n\nStrong problem-solving and analytical skills.\n\nGood communication and teamwork abilities.\n\nExperience\n\nFreshers or students currently pursuing a degree in Computer Science, IT, or a related field are encouraged to apply.\n\nPrior internship experience or personal projects in frontend development is an added advantage.\n\nWorking Hours\n\nFlexible working hours with a focus on deliverables.\n\nRemote or hybrid work model depending on project requirements.\n\nExpected commitment: 20–40 hours per week.\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n\nUnderstanding of modern UI frameworks and component-based architecture.\n\nAbility to write clean, maintainable, and reusable code.\n\nBasic knowledge of SEO principles and web performance optimization.\n\nFamiliarity with tools like Figma or Adobe XD for design collaboration.\n\nWillingness to learn and adapt in a fast-paced startup environment.\n\nBenefits\n\nHands-on experience working on real-world projects.\n\nMentorship from experienced developers and industry professionals.\n\nOpportunity to build a strong portfolio.\n\nFlexible work environment.\n\nCertificate of internship upon successful completion.\n\nPotential for full-time employment based on performance.\n\nWhy Join GradeBuzz\n\nAt GradeBuzz, we foster innovation, creativity, and continuous learning. As a Frontend Developer Intern, you will gain exposure to cutting-edge technologies and work on impactful projects that reach real users. Our collaborative culture ensures that your ideas are heard and valued, making it the perfect place to kickstart your tech career.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates can apply by submitting their updated resume along with a portfolio or GitHub profile showcasing relevant projects. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for a technical assessment and interview process.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','intern,developer intern,frontend,gradebuzz,frontend developer,js responsive,js,internship,using js,responsive,projects,knowledge,modern,performance,web,design,frontend developme