t development.\n• *\n\nExperience with version control systems (preferably Git).\n• *\n\nKnowledge of front-end build tools such as Webpack, npm, or Gulp.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with modern JavaScript frameworks/libraries such as React, Vue.js, or Angular is a plus.\n• *\n\nUnderstanding of RESTful APIs and JSON.\n• *\n\nAbility to write clean, efficient, and well-documented code.\n• *\n\nExcellent problem-solving and debugging skills.\n• *\n\nStrong communication skills in both English and Portuguese.\n• Experience\n• *\n\n2+ years of experience in front-end web development or a related field.\n• *\n\nProven portfolio or project samples showcasing front-end development capabilities.\n• *\n\nExperience working in an Agile or remote team environment is preferred.\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFlexible remote schedule aligned with Brazil Standard Time (BRT).\n• *\n\nCore collaboration hours between 10:00 AM – 6:00 PM BRT.\n• *\n\nOccasional meetings with global teams may require flexibility.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nStrong understanding of UI/UX principles and accessibility standards.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with cross-browser and cross-platform compatibility challenges.\n• *\n\nKnowledge of SEO best practices related to front-end development.\n• *\n\nAbility to manage time effectively and meet project deadlines.\n• *\n\nTeam-oriented mindset with a proactive approach to problem-solving.\n• *\n\nAdaptability and eagerness to learn new technologies quickly.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\n100% remote work flexibility from anywhere in Brazil.\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary package based on experience.\n• *\n\nHealth insurance and wellness benefits.\n• *\n\nAnnual performance bonuses and professional growth opportunities.\n• *\n\nAccess to learning and development resources and paid online training.\n• *\n\nInclusive, innovative, and supportive work culture.\n• Why Join The Elite Job\n\nAt The Elite Job, we believe in empowering talent and fostering innovation. You will work with a global team of professionals who are passionate about technology, creativity, and delivering world-class digital experiences. Joining us means being part of a company that values collaboration, diversity, and continuous learning. We encourage initiative, reward excellence, and provide the flexibility you need to thrive personally and professionally.\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are excited about crafting intuitive digital experiences and want to grow your career with a leading global company, we would love to hear from you!\n\nPlease submit your updated resume, a portfolio or GitHub link, and a brief cover letter explaining why you are the perfect fit for this role to us',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','end,brazil,css javascript,experience,development,web,elite,elite job,global,brt,end developer,clean efficient,using html,html css,html,css,remote,web interfaces,digital experiences,00,updated,javascript,code,best practices,cross'),(412,'jsearch','zi_V0hY29bpCS9QcAAAAAA==','Remote Web Developer - Work From Home Canada','HR Service Jobs',NULL,'CA',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/19998/remote-web-developer-work-from-home-canada','Job Summary\n\nHR Service Jobs is seeking a talented and self-motivated Remote Web Developer to join our dynamic technology team. In this role, you will be responsible for designing, developing, and maintaining scalable web applications while collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver high-quality solutions. This is a fully remote position based in Canada, offering flexibility and the opportunity to work in a fast-paced, innovative environment.\nKey Responsibilities\n• *\n\nDevelop, test, and deploy responsive web applications using modern frameworks and technologies.\n• *\n\nCollaborate with UX/UI designers, product managers, and other developers to implement functional and visually appealing web features.\n• *\n\nMaintain and enhance existing codebases, ensuring performance optimization and scalability.\n• *\n\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve software defects and technical issues.\n• *\n\nWrite clean, maintainable, and well-documented code following coding standards and best practices.\n• *\n\nStay up-to-date with emerging web technologies and industry trends to recommend improvements.\n• *\n\nEnsure website security, accessibility, and performance compliance.\n• *\n\nParticipate in code reviews and provide constructive feedback to peers.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• *\n\nProficiency in front-end technologies: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript, and frameworks such as React, Angular, or Vue.js.\n• *\n\nStrong experience with back-end development using Node.js, PHP, Python, Ruby, or similar technologies.\n• *\n\nExperience with database management systems (SQL, NoSQL).\n• *\n\nKnowledge of RESTful APIs, GraphQL, and web services integration.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with version control systems such as Git.\n• *\n\nUnderstanding of responsive and mobile-first web design principles.\n• *\n\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• *\n\nExcellent communication skills in English, both written and verbal.\n• Experience\n• *\n\nMinimum of 3 years of professional experience in web development or a related field.\n• *\n\nExperience working in remote teams or distributed environments is highly preferred.\n• *\n\nProven track record of successfully delivering complex web projects.\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFull-time, flexible hours (Remote work from anywhere in Canada).\n• *\n\nSome overlap with standard business hours may be required for team collaboration and meetings.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nStrong analytical and technical troubleshooting abilities.\n• *\n\nAbility to work independently while managing multiple projects simultaneously.\n• *\n\nDetail-oriented with a focus on quality and performance.\n• *\n\nAdaptable to new technologies and able to learn quickly.\n• *\n\nSelf-disciplined with excellent time management skills.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• *\n\nFully remote work environment with flexible schedule.\n• *\n\nHealth, dental, and vision coverage.\n• *\n\nProfessional development and training opportunities.\n• *\n\nCollaborative and inclusive company culture.\n• *\n\nAccess to cutting-edge tools and technologies.\n• Why Join Us\n\nAt HR Service Jobs, we value innovation, collaboration, and professional growth. As a Remote Web Developer, you will have the opportunity to work on exciting projects that make a real impact while enjoying the freedom and flexibility of working from home. Join a forward-thinking company that invests in your career development and fosters a supportive work environment.\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their resume and portfolio via email to us with the subject line: Remote Web Developer – Canada Application. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','web,remote web,canada,web developer,remote,work,technologies,hr service,service jobs,service,hr,skills,experience,performance,jobs,management,developer,home,opportunity work,fully,fully remote,professional,development,work environment,projects'),(415,'jsearch','o3p9i4Xd_LFoY0HCAAAAAA==','Urgent Hiring: Next.js Frontend Developer â€“ Remote India','GradeBuzz',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/20221/urgent-hiring-next.js-frontend-developer-ae%E2%80%9C-remote-india','Job Summary\n\nGradeBuzz is seeking a highly skilled and passionate Next.js Frontend Developer to join our growing remote team in India. This role is ideal for a developer who thrives in a fast-paced, product-driven environment and is eager to build scalable, high-performance web applications. You will play a key role in designing and implementing user-facing features, optimizing performance, and collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver seamless digital experiences.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\nDevelop and maintain responsive, high-quality web applications using Next.js and modern frontend technologies\n\nTranslate UI/UX designs into pixel-perfect, interactive user interfaces\n\nOptimize applications for maximum speed, scalability, and performance\n\nCollaborate with backend developers, designers, and product managers to deliver end-to-end solutions\n\nImplement SEO best practices and ensure strong Core Web Vitals performance\n\nWrite clean, maintainable, and reusable code following industry standards\n\nDebug, troubleshoot, and resolve frontend issues efficiently\n\nStay updated with the latest frontend trends and technologies\n\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n\nStrong proficiency in Next.js, React.js, and JavaScript (ES6+)\n\nSolid understanding of HTML5, CSS3, and modern styling frameworks (e.g., Tailwind CSS)\n\nExperience with REST APIs and integration of backend services\n\nFamiliarity with version control systems such as Git\n\nUnderstanding of responsive design and cross-browser compatibility\n\nKnowledge of performance optimization techniques\n\nStrong problem-solving skills and attention to detail\n\nExperience\n\nMinimum 2â€“5 years of professional experience in frontend development\n\nProven experience working with Next.js in production environments\n\nExperience in remote or distributed teams is a plus\n\nWorking Hours\n\nFull-time, remote position (India-based candidates only)\n\nFlexible working hours with overlap required for team collaboration\n\nOccasional availability for meetings across different time zones\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n\nStrong understanding of frontend architecture and component-based design\n\nAbility to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment\n\nExcellent communication and collaboration skills\n\nSelf-motivated with the ability to work independently\n\nAdaptability to evolving project requirements and technologies\n\nBenefits\n\nCompetitive salary package\n\nFully remote work environment\n\nFlexible work schedule\n\nOpportunity to work on cutting-edge technologies\n\nCareer growth and learning opportunities\n\nCollaborative and innovative team culture\n\nWhy Join GradeBuzz\n\nAt GradeBuzz, we are committed to building impactful digital solutions in the EdTech space. You will have the opportunity to work on meaningful projects that make a difference, collaborate with talented professionals, and grow your technical expertise in a supportive and forward-thinking environment.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates can apply by submitting their updated resume along with a portfolio or GitHub profile showcasing relevant projects. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for further technical evaluation and interviews.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','frontend,india,gradebuzz,js,js frontend,performance,experience,remote,work,technologies,candidates,frontend developer,strong,environment,opportunity work,skills,deliver,digital,applications,web,understanding,fast paced,paced,modern,updated'),(416,'jsearch','CQHTFMh4Qhd5_vr_AAAAAA==','Data Analyst - Part Time work from home','The Elite Job',NULL,'US',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/9348/data-analyst-part-time-work-from-home','The Elite Job is seeking a meticulous and detail-oriented Data Analyst to join our dynamic team on a part-time basis. This remote position is ideal for individuals who thrive in data-driven environments and possess strong analytical skills. As a Data Analyst, you will be responsible for interpreting complex datasets to provide actionable insights that drive business decisions. Your role will involve collecting, processing, and analyzing data to identify trends, patterns, and anomalies, which will support our strategic initiatives and operational improvements. The successful candidate will have a solid understanding of statistical analysis, data visualization tools, and database management. You will collaborate closely with various departments to ensure data integrity and reliability, ultimately contributing to the overall success of the organization. This is an excellent opportunity for someone looking to advance their career in data analysis while enjoying the flexibility of a part-time, work-from-home schedule.\nKey Responsibilities\n• * Collect, clean, and validate data from various sources to ensure accuracy and reliability.\n• * Analyze large datasets to identify trends, patterns, and insights that inform business strategies.\n• * Create and maintain dashboards and reports using data visualization tools to present findings effectively.\n• * Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand data needs and provide data-driven solutions.\n• * Develop and implement data management processes and best practices.\n• * Assist in the preparation of presentations for stakeholders, summarizing key findings and recommendations.\n• * Monitor key performance indicators (KPIs) and report on performance metrics to support strategic initiatives.\n• * Stay updated on industry trends and emerging data analysis techniques.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• * Bachelor degree in Data Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or a related field.\n• * Proficiency in data analysis tools and programming languages such as SQL, Python, R, or similar.\n• * Experience with data visualization tools such as Tableau, Power BI, or similar platforms.\n• * Strong analytical skills with the ability to interpret complex data sets and draw actionable conclusions.\n• * Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail.\n• * Effective communication skills, both verbal and written, with the ability to present data clearly to non-technical audiences.\n• Experience\n• * Minimum of 2 years of experience in a data analysis or related role.\n• * Proven experience in working with large datasets and using analytical techniques to derive insights.\n• * Previous experience in a remote work environment is a plus.\n• Working Hours\n• * This is a part-time position requiring approximately 20 hours per week, with flexible working hours.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• * Strong understanding of statistical methods and data analysis techniques.\n• * Familiarity with data warehousing concepts and database management systems.\n• * Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines in a fast-paced environment.\n• * Strong organizational skills with a focus on quality and accuracy.\n• Benefits\n• * Competitive hourly rate.\n• * Flexible work schedule, allowing for work-life balance.\n• * Opportunity to work remotely from the comfort of your home.\n• * Professional development opportunities and access to online training resources.\n• * Friendly and collaborative team environment.\n• Why Join The Elite Job?\n\nAt The Elite Job, we believe in fostering a culture of growth, innovation, and collaboration. We value our employees and strive to create an inclusive workplace where everyone contributions are recognized and appreciated. Joining our team means being part of a forward-thinking company that prioritizes data-driven decision-making and continuous improvement. You will have the chance to work with industry professionals, gain valuable experience, and make a real impact on our business outcomes.\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are a motivated data analyst looking to take the next step in your career while enjoying the flexibility of remote work, we want to hear from you! Please submit your resume and a cover letter outlining your relevant experience and skills to [insert email address or application portal link]. We look forward to reviewing your application!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','data,skills,work,analysis,home,data analysis,experience,time work,enjoying,database management,enjoying flexibility,database,analysis techniques,techniques,reliability,elite job,visualization tools,elite,time,data visualization,datasets,work home,using,support strategic,schedule'),(417,'jsearch','YynQE1uekzuXBuRzAAAAAA==','Trainee - Junior Data Analyst','The Elite Job',NULL,'MX',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/4596/trainee-junior-data-analyst','The Elite Job is a dynamic and innovative company dedicated to providing exceptional data analysis solutions across various industries. We thrive on creativity, collaboration, and cutting-edge technology to drive meaningful insights and actionable outcomes for our clients.\n\nJob Title: Trainee - Junior Data Analyst\n\nJob Summary: The Elite Job is seeking a highly motivated Trainee - Junior Data Analyst to join our growing team. This entry-level position offers an exciting opportunity for individuals passionate about data analysis to kickstart their career in a supportive and dynamic environment. The successful candidate will work closely with senior analysts to collect, analyze, and interpret data to drive informed decision-making and strategic initiatives.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• Assist in data collection, cleansing, and validation processes.\n• * Perform exploratory data analysis to identify trends, patterns, and anomalies.\n• * Develop and maintain data models, algorithms, and statistical analyses.\n• * Prepare reports, dashboards, and visualizations to communicate insights effectively.\n• * Collaborate with cross-functional teams to support data-driven initiatives and projects.\n• * Stay updated on industry trends, best practices, and emerging technologies in data analysis.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications:\n• Bachelors degree in Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Economics, or a related field.\n• * Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with attention to detail.\n• * Proficiency in programming languages such as Python, R, or SQL.\n• * Familiarity with data visualization tools such as Tableau, Power BI, or matplotlib.\n• * Excellent communication and interpersonal skills.\n• * Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced environment.\n• * Eagerness to learn and adapt to new technologies and methodologies.\n• Experience: Previous experience or internships in data analysis or a related field is preferred but not required. Fresh graduates are encouraged to apply.\n\nWorking Hours: This is a full-time position, with standard working hours from Monday to Friday. Flexibility may be required to accommodate project deadlines and business needs.\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n• * Understanding of statistical concepts and methods.\n• * Knowledge of data manipulation and transformation techniques.\n• * Ability to interpret and present complex data sets in a clear and concise manner.\n• * Strong organizational and time management skills.\n• * Adaptability and willingness to take on new challenges.\n• Benefits:\n• * Competitive salary package.\n• * Health, dental, and vision insurance coverage.\n• * Opportunities for professional development and career advancement.\n• * Collaborative and inclusive work culture.\n• * Employee wellness programs and perks.\n• Why Join The Elite Job: At The Elite Job, we are committed to nurturing talent and empowering individuals to reach their full potential. As a Trainee - Junior Data Analyst, you will have the opportunity to work on diverse projects, learn from experienced professionals, and make a meaningful impact through data-driven insights. Join us in shaping the future of data analysis and unlocking new possibilities for our clients and partners.\n\nHow to Apply: Interested candidates are invited to submit their resume and cover letter to us. Please include any relevant coursework, projects, or portfolio samples demonstrating your skills and experience in data analysis. We look forward to reviewing your application and welcoming you to our team!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','data,trainee junior,junior data,trainee,data analysis,junior,analysis,job,elite job,elite,skills,clients,new,data analyst,projects,work,meaningful,learn,join,required,analyst,drive,individuals,statistical,career'),(418,'jsearch','iLTTiYcvvP0eyRZhAAAAAA==','AI Data Analyst; Remote','PulseMediaNL',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/info_technology/5084802360/e/','Position: AI Data Analyst (Remote)\n\nPulse\n\nMedia\n\nNL is seeking a detail‑oriented and analytical AI Data Analyst to join our remote team. This role is essential for transforming data into actionable insights, supporting AI‑driven initiatives, and helping optimize business decisions through advanced analytics and data modeling.\nResponsibilities\n• Data Analysis & Insights\n• Collect, clean, and analyze large datasets to identify trends and patterns\n• Translate complex data into clear, actionable insights for stakeholders\n• Develop reports and dashboards to track key performance indicators\n• Support data‑driven decision‑making across departments\nAI & Model Support\n• Assist in the development, evaluation, and optimization of AI and machine learning models\n• Prepare and preprocess data for training and validation purposes\n• Monitor model performance and suggest improvements\n• Collaborate with data scientists and engineers on AI initiatives\nData Management & Quality\n• Maintain data integrity and ensure accuracy across data sources\n• Develop and enforce data quality standards and validation processes\n• Manage structured and unstructured data from multiple systems\n• Document data processes and workflows\nVisualization & Reporting\n• Create visualizations to effectively communicate findings\n• Use BI tools to present insights in an accessible and engaging way\n• Prepare regular reports and presentations for internal teams\n• Support ad hoc analysis requests\nProcess Improvement & Collaboration\n• Identify opportunities to improve data collection and analysis processes\n• Work cross‑functionally with marketing, operations, and product teams\n• Support automation of data workflows and reporting systems\n• Stay updated on industry trends in data analytics and AI\nRequirements\n• About the Ideal Candidate:\n• 2–4 years of experience in data analysis, business intelligence, or a related role\n• Strong analytical and problem‑solving skills\n• Proficiency in data analysis tools such as SQL, Python, or R\n• Experience with data visualization tools (e.g., Power BI, Tableau)\n• Familiarity with machine learning concepts and AI workflows\n• Strong attention to detail and data accuracy\n• Ability to communicate technical findings to non‑technical stakeholders\n• Comfortable working in a remote environment and managing multiple priorities\n• Bachelor’s degree in Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, or related field preferred\nWhat We Offer\n• Meaningful contribution through data-driven insights and AI innovation\n• Remote‑first flexibility to support work‑life balance\n• Opportunities for learning and advancement in data and AI fields\n• Collaborative and forward‑thinking team environment\n• Competitive compensation aligned with experience\n• Long‑term stability within a growing and technology‑focused organization\nDiversity & Inclusion\n\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse, equitable, and inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued, respected, and empowered to contribute. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'data,ai,workflows,ai data,analysis,learning,analyst remote,remote,insights,machine learning,teams support,machine,support,prepare,validation,model,data analysis,processes,reporting,driven,data analyst,technical,communicate,systems,quality'),(419,'jsearch','xDBy5OhRyU8ytv4aAAAAAA==','Analyst - Data and Analytics','The Elite Job',NULL,'NG',0,'https://www.theelitejob.com/job/8016/analyst-data-and-analytics','Job Summary\nThe Elite Job is seeking a highly skilled Analyst - Data and Analytics to join our dynamic Information Technology team. This role is critical in driving data-driven decision-making and strategy by analyzing complex data sets, developing actionable insights, and supporting various business functions with accurate and timely information. The ideal candidate will possess a strong analytical mindset, advanced technical skills, and the ability to communicate findings effectively to stakeholders at all levels.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• * Data Analysis and Interpretation: Collect, clean, and analyze large data sets to identify trends, patterns, and anomalies. Transform data into actionable insights to support business objectives.\n• * Reporting and Visualization: Develop and maintain comprehensive reports, dashboards, and visualizations that effectively communicate data findings and support decision-making processes.\n• * Data Management: Ensure data integrity and accuracy by implementing and following best practices for data collection, storage, and management.\n• * Stakeholder Collaboration: Work closely with various departments to understand their data needs, provide insights, and recommend solutions to enhance business operations and strategy.\n• * Tool and Technology Utilization: Utilize advanced data analysis tools and technologies (e.g., SQL, Python, R, Tableau) to extract, manipulate, and analyze data.\n• * Continuous Improvement: Stay updated with the latest industry trends, tools, and techniques in data analytics and recommend improvements to enhance analytical capabilities.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• * Technical Proficiency: Advanced knowledge of data analysis tools such as SQL, Python, R, or similar programming languages, and experience with data visualization tools like Tableau, Power BI, or similar platforms.\n• * Analytical Skills: Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to interpret complex data and provide actionable insights.\n• * Communication: Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to present data findings clearly and effectively to both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n• * Attention to Detail: Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy in data handling and analysis.\n• * Project Management: Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously, prioritize tasks, and meet deadlines.\n• Experience\n• * Minimum of 3 years of experience in a data analysis or analytics role, preferably in a technology-driven environment.\n• * Proven experience with large data sets and advanced analytics techniques.\n• * Experience in collaborating with cross-functional teams to deliver data-driven solutions.\n• Working Hours\n• * Full-time position; standard working hours are Monday through Friday, 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM. Flexibility in working hours may be required based on project needs and deadlines.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• * Knowledge: Strong understanding of data analytics concepts, methodologies, and best practices.\n• * Skills: Proficiency in data analysis, statistical techniques, and data visualization.\n• * Abilities: Ability to think critically, solve complex problems, and work independently as well as part of a team.\n• Benefits\n• * Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• * Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance plans.\n• * Retirement savings plan with company match.\n• * Paid time off and holiday leave.\n• * Professional development opportunities and support for continuing education.\n• * Flexible work arrangements and remote work options.\n• Why Join The Elite Job?\nAt The Elite Job, we are committed to fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, and growth. As a leading company in the industry, we offer a stimulating environment where your skills and contributions are valued and recognized. Joining our team means being part of a forward-thinking organization that is dedicated to making a difference through data-driven solutions and technology advancements.\n\nHow to Apply\nInterested candidates should submit their resume and a cover letter detailing their relevant experience and qualifications to us with the subject line Analyst - Data and Analytics Application. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','data,analytics,analyst data,data analytics,advanced,skills,analysis,technology,technical,data analysis,data sets,sets,large data,techniques data,ability,experience,techniques,job,data findings,recommend,driven solutions,enhance,elite job,effectively,elite'),(420,'jsearch','EBdnmrNrmSGUhMNgAAAAAA==','Staff Data Analyst, Product','Airalo',NULL,NULL,0,'https://weworkremotely.com/remote-jobs/airalo-staff-data-analyst-product','About Airalo\nAlo! Airalo is the world’s first eSIM store that helps people connect in over 200+ countries and regions across the globe. We are building the next digital service that revolutionizes the telecom industry. We are a travel-tech company and an equal-opportunity environment that values and executes diversity, inclusion, and equity. Our team is spread across 50+ countries and six continents. What glues us together is our commitment to changing the way you connect.\nCheck out more information about Airalo in our Public Handbook: https://airalo-public.notion.site/airalo-public-handbook\n\nAbout you\nWe hope that you care deeply about the quality of your work, the intrinsic worth of tasks, and the success of your team. You are self-disciplined and do not require micromanagement in terms of your skillset and work ethic. You do your best to flourish as an individual every day while working hard to foster a collaborative team environment. You believe in the importance of being — and staying — authentic, honest, positive, and kind. You are a good interlocutor with clear and concise communication. You are able to manage multiple projects, have an analytical mind, pay keen attention to detail, and love to get your hands dirty. You are cognizant, tolerant, and welcoming of vulnerabilities and cultural differences.\n\nAbout the Role\nPosition: Full-time / Employee\nLocation: Remote-first\nBenefits: Health Insurance, work-from-anywhere stipend, annual wellness & learning credits, annual all-expenses-paid company retreat in a gorgeous destination & other benefits\n\nWe\'re looking for a Staff Data Analyst, Product to own product analytics at Airalo. You\'ll be the go-to person for understanding how our 20M+ users across 190+ countries interact with our product-what drives activation, engagement, retention, and ultimately revenue. This is a high-impact IC role with significant scope: you\'ll partner directly with product teams and leadership to shape product strategy through data.\n\nYou\'ll report to the Director of Data and partner closely with analytics engineering, product managers, and cross-functional stakeholders. Success looks like product decisions backed by rigorous analysis, experimentation that compounds learning, and metrics the business trusts and uses. Beyond delivering insights that influence the roadmap, you\'ll help shape how product analytics operates at Airalo-our model is evolving, and you\'ll have real input into how we scale coverage and structure the team.\n\nWhat you’ll do:\n• Partner with Product teams to define success metrics, design experiments, and evaluate feature impact\n• Partner with fractional squad analysts where they exist; serve as the primary analytics partner for squads without dedicated coverage and help evolve our organisational model for product analytics\n• Be hands-on with analysis, dashboards, and metric development while building the foundations for a scalable product analytics practice\n• Define, own, and govern product metrics and KPIs in alignment with our company-wide unified KPI framework-ensuring consistency, clarity, and trust in how we measure product performance in alignment with business goals\n• Build and maintain core product health dashboards in partnership with analytics engineering as we’re transitioning to self-service via Lightdash and maturing our analytics platform\n• Conduct deep-dive analyses on user behavior, funnel performance, and cohort trends to surface opportunities and diagnose issues\n• Design and analyze A/B tests and experiments, establishing best practices for experimentation rigor\n• Translate complex analytical findings into clear recommendations for technical and non-technical stakeholders, including executive leadership\n• Partner with data and product teams, to define data requirements and ensure product event tracking meets analytical needs\n\nMust-haves:\n• 7+ years in product analytics, data science, or quantitative analytics roles, with demonstrated impact at staff/principal level\n• Deep experience with product analytics in a B2C or marketplace environment-you understand funnels, retention curves, and user lifecycle intimately\n• Track record of defining and owning metrics frameworks-you\'ve established KPIs, driven cross-functional alignment, and maintained metric integrity as products and teams scaled\n• Strong SQL skills and proficiency in Python or R for statistical analysis and modeling\n• Proven track record designing and analyzing experiments, with solid understanding of statistical methods and common pitfalls\n• Experience with product analytics tools (Amplitude, Mixpanel, or similar) and modern BI platforms\n• Ability to translate ambiguous business questions into structured analytical approaches\n• Excellent communication skills-you can tell a compelling story with data and influence product decisions at the leadership level\n• Strong business intuition and user empathy; you think beyond the data to understand the \"why\"\n• Comfortable operating with autonomy in a fast-moving environment where not everything is well-defined-you bring structure without waiting for permission\n• You\'ve been the person who brought rigor to a team that didn\'t have it-introduced frameworks, challenged assumptions, and shifted how product teams think about data\n\nGood to Have:\n• Experience in marketplace, telecom, travel or subscription/usage-based businesses\n• Experience building experimentation programs or platforms from scratch-culture, tooling, and processes\n• Previous work at a scale-up during hypergrowth, where you\'ve seen what breaks and what scales\n• You\'ve been the person who brought rigor to a team that didn\'t have it-introduced frameworks, challenged assumptions, and shifted how product teams think about data\n\nBy applying, you acknowledge and agree that, in case of successful application, Airalo may request to run background checks as a condition for entering into an agreement with you. Rest assured that these checks will only occur upon your prior consent and at the end of the selection process, and will be strictly limited to what is allowed under the laws that are applicable to you. All data that you share or that we collect in connection with such checks will be processed in accordance with our Privacy Policy, available here: https://www.airalo.com/more-info/privacy-policy?srsltid=AfmBOooBT0rXAj1FaNelZ3VfN0wvhwzvAoxdtHnOKSVETpiSjiXVuycy\n\nWe sincerely thank all applicants in advance for submitting their interest in this opportunity. Airalo is an equal-opportunity employer and values diversity, equity & inclusion. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations upon request for individuals with disabilities throughout our job interview process.\n\nWe may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support parts of the hiring process, such as reviewing applications, analyzing resumes, or assessing responses. These tools assist our recruitment team but do not replace human judgment. Final hiring decisions are ultimately made by humans. If you would like more information about how your data is processed, please contact us.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'product,airalo,product analytics,analytics,product teams,ll,partner,ve,data,person,think data,airalo public,experiments,experimentation,metrics,rigor,countries,define,staff,checks,alignment,success,teams,leadership,public'),(421,'jsearch','qf1jZgl3fL5OmWUbAAAAAA==','Remote AI Data Analyst: Insights & Model','PulseMediaNL',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/info_technology/5084799827/e/','Position: Remote AI Data Analyst: Insights & Model Support\nPulse\n\nMedia\n\nNL is looking for a detail-oriented AI Data Analyst to work remotely from Al Khobar, Saudi Arabia. The position involves transforming data into actionable insights, supporting AI-driven initiatives, and optimizing business decisions. Candidates should have 2–4 years of experience and be proficient in SQL, Python, and data visualization tools like Power BI. The role offers flexibility, a collaborative team environment, and competitive compensation, promoting a culture of diversity and inclusion.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ai,ai data,insights model,analyst insights,remote ai,data,model,data analyst,insights,proficient sql,optimizing business,position involves,bi role,compensation promoting,offers flexibility,khobar saudi,decisions candidates,culture diversity,flexibility collaborative,like power,experience proficient,promoting culture,model position,promoting,khobar'),(422,'jsearch','7YG7kO_jrPdtAMhvAAAAAA==','Data Analyst – No Experience Required','Peroptyx',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/data-analyst-at-peroptyx','Time zones: EST (UTC -5), CST (UTC -6), MST (UTC -7), PST (UTC -8), AST (UTC -4), NST (UTC -3:30)\n\nFor thousands of years, maps have provided humans with the knowledge they need to make decisions. As a Maps Evaluator, you will have the opportunity to provide ground truth for your town, city or country.\n\nAt Peroptyx, we are looking for Data Analysts who will review mapping data for digital mapping applications. Your research capabilities will validate and ensure that the navigation of certain routes are accurate and safe.\n\nAs part of this role you will verify that business names and opening hours are correct. You will check that the distance from a starting point to an end destination is listed accurately resulting in better user experiences.\n\nWith this job you can plan your days around this highly flexible working schedule, work weekends or late evenings, all from the comfort of your own office. The flexibility of our roles minimizes the impact on your daily routine.\n\nSo, whether you are a student looking to earn as you learn, a retiree looking for a new challenge a part-time/full time professional or a work from home parent, Peroptyx has the right role for you!\n\nIdeal Candidate\n\n· Fluent in English.\n\n· Excellent research skills.\n\n· Excellent local knowledge of your home country.\n\n· Good understanding and general knowledge of the geography and culture of Canada.\n\n· Analytical mindset.\n\nJob Requirements\n\n· Must be living in Canada for a minimum of 5 consecutive years.\n\n· Must pass an online open-book exam that can verify your full understanding of the material and concepts.\n\n· Must be willing to work a minimum of 10 hours and up to 20 hours per week depending on task availability.\n\n· Good working knowledge of search engines, map applications and familiarity with social media platforms.\n\n· Strong ability to learn, understand and apply multiple sets of different instructions.\n\n· All work must be of an independent nature.\n\nBenefits\n\n· Work up to 20 hours per week.\n\n· Earn a competitive rate of pay.\n\n· Develop your research skills.\n\n· Avoid the long commute.\n\n· Work from the comfort of your home office.\n\n· Enjoy the flexibility of setting your own working hours!\n\nApply Today!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'utc,research,hours,home,work,peroptyx,maps,research skills,mapping,earn,knowledge,verify,canada,good,country,looking,office,20,20 hours,minimum,comfort,hours week,week,applications,learn'),(423,'jsearch','LR8-V-odh-lRXCecAAAAAA==','Remote AI Data Analyst: Insights, Dashboards & AI','PulseMediaNL',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/info_technology/5084810887/e/','Position: Remote AI Data Analyst: Insights, Dashboards & AI Support\nPulse\n\nMedia\n\nNL is seeking a detail-oriented AI Data Analyst to join their remote team. The role involves transforming data into actionable insights, supporting AI initiatives, and enhancing business decisions through analytics. Responsibilities include data cleaning, model optimization, and reporting. The ideal candidate has 2–4 years of relevant experience, proficiency in SQL and Python, and a relevant Bachelor\'s degree. This position offers remote flexibility and opportunities for growth within a forward-thinking organization.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ai,ai data,dashboards ai,insights dashboards,analyst insights,remote ai,remote,data,data analyst,insights,degree position,growth forward,enhancing,python relevant,opportunities growth,organization 18808,cleaning model,enhancing business,initiatives enhancing,offers remote,decisions analytics,flexibility opportunities,optimization reporting,relevant bachelor,model optimization'),(424,'jsearch','lXGNBk00BRY7BbmfAAAAAA==','Remote Data Analyst Jobs - Work from Home & Flexible Schedule','The Elite Job',NULL,'US',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/13943/remote-data-analyst-jobs-work-from-home-flexible-schedule','Job Summary\n\nThe Elite Job is seeking a detail-oriented and analytical Remote Data Analyst to join our dynamic team. In this role, you will be responsible for collecting, processing, and analyzing large datasets to help drive business decisions. You will work closely with cross-functional teams to provide actionable insights, optimize processes, and support strategic initiatives. This is a fantastic opportunity for individuals who are passionate about data, problem-solving, and working in a flexible remote environment.\nKey Responsibilities\n• *\n\nCollect, clean, and analyze large datasets to identify trends and insights.\n• *\n\nDevelop and maintain dashboards, reports, and data visualizations to support business decision-making.\n• *\n\nCollaborate with various departments to understand data needs and provide meaningful analysis.\n• *\n\nUse statistical tools and machine learning models to interpret data patterns and forecast business trends.\n• *\n\nMonitor and ensure data integrity, accuracy, and consistency across all databases.\n• *\n\nPresent data findings and recommendations to stakeholders in a clear and actionable manner.\n• *\n\nIdentify opportunities for process automation and efficiency improvements.\n• *\n\nStay updated with industry trends, data analytics tools, and best practices.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• *\n\nBachelors degree in Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, Mathematics, Economics, or a related field.\n• *\n\nStrong proficiency in SQL, Python, R, Excel, or other data analysis tools.\n• *\n\nExperience working with BI tools such as Tableau, Power BI, or Google Data Studio.\n• *\n\nUnderstanding of statistical analysis, predictive modeling, and machine learning concepts.\n• *\n\nAbility to manage large datasets and ensure data integrity.\n• *\n\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills with keen attention to detail.\n• *\n\nExcellent verbal and written communication skills.\n• *\n\nAbility to work independently in a remote and flexible work environment.\n• Experience\n• *\n\nEntry-Level to Mid-Level: 1+ years of experience in data analysis, business intelligence, or a related field.\n• *\n\nExperience working with structured and unstructured datasets is a plus.\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms like AWS, Google Cloud, or Azure is an advantage.\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFlexible work schedule based on project requirements.\n• *\n\nPart-time and full-time positions available.\n• *\n\nWork remotely from any location with reliable internet access.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nStrong mathematical and statistical knowledge.\n• *\n\nAbility to interpret complex data and provide actionable insights.\n• *\n\nCritical thinking and problem-solving mindset.\n• *\n\nAbility to handle multiple projects and meet deadlines.\n• *\n\nStrong organizational and time-management skills.\n• Benefits\n• *\n\nFlexible work schedule – work from anywhere.\n• *\n\nCompetitive salary based on experience.\n• *\n\nCareer growth opportunities in a data-driven environment.\n• *\n\nProfessional development support (certifications, training, and courses).\n• *\n\nWork-life balance with remote work benefits.\n• Why Join The Elite Job?\n• *\n\nBe part of a company that values data-driven decision-making.\n• *\n\nWork on exciting projects with a team of talented professionals.\n• *\n\nGain exposure to different industries and real-world data challenges.\n• *\n\nEnjoy a remote-first company culture that promotes work flexibility.\n• How to Apply\n\nIf you are passionate about data analysis and eager to work in a flexible remote environment, we encourage you to apply!\n\nTo apply:\n• *\n\nSubmit your resume and a cover letter explaining why you are a great fit for this role.\n• *\n\nInclude links to your portfolio, GitHub, or previous projects (if applicable).\n• *\n\nApply through our website or send your application to us.\n• Join The Elite Job today and take your data analytics career to the next level!',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','data,work,flexible,remote,flexible work,schedule,datasets,analysis,remote data,provide,statistical,job,machine learning,google,work schedule,machine,elite,large datasets,elite job,skills,environment,apply,large,level,experience'),(425,'jsearch','hrDSIXFRMLj_nXy6AAAAAA==','Data Analyst Intern –Policy + Ethics','FairwAI','Miami','US',0,'https://wellfound.com/jobs/3257803-data-analyst-intern-policy-ethics','FairwAI is an AI-powered bias detection and compliance platform transforming how industries identify and address algorithmic discrimination. We\'re building the regulatory infrastructure of the future—starting with hospitality, and hiring. We currently have opening opening for faspring 2026. The summer is 20-40 hours a week and fall/spring is 10-20 hours. We can work with CPT/OPT.\n\nOur collaborators include leaders from MIT, Harvard, Stanford, and global institutions working on AI ethics, digital rights, and inclusive capitalism.\n\nTeam:\n\nTeam\n\nMr. Dixon –Chief Compliance Strategist\n\nRole: Visionary founder of FairwAI, Mr. Dixon leads overall strategy, mission alignment, institutional partnerships, and compliance innovation. He ensures the platform remains focused on real-world fairness, risk mitigation, and public accountability—rather than abstract DEI.\n\nBio:\n\nMr. Dixon is a serial founder, public interest technologist, and global strategist known for building impact ventures at the intersection of technology, governance, and equity. He is currently a strategic advisor at MIT, where he collaborates across departments such as the MIT Media Lab and Martin Trust Center. Mr. Dixon has served as a policy strategist to President John Mahama of Ghana, worked with the U.S. Department of Energy on distributed energy infrastructure, and led multi-million-dollar public-private partnerships with organizations like GE Healthcare, USAID, and UNICEF.\n\nMr. Dixon is the founder of SolarFi, a social enterprise that builds portable solar-powered infrastructure for clinics, schools, and underserved communities across Africa. Under his leadership, SolarFi was awarded major U.S. government contracts and featured by MIT and the UN. He has also advised on diplomatic and philanthropic partnerships.\n\nFairwAI is Mr. Dixon’s most urgent venture yet. Inspired by lived experiences of racial bias and systemic discrimination in global travel, hiring, and healthcare systems, he founded FairwAI to reframe fairness as a compliance and safety issue, not a corporate DEI trend. Antonio brings a rare combination of field-tested grit, institutional access, tech, diplomacy, and global coalition to ensure accountability becomes enforceable.\n\nDr. John Cooley – Technical Advisor\n\nRole: Leads FairwAI’s technical architecture, AI compliance engine, and research partnerships.\n\nBio: Dr. John Cooley is a renowned technologist and serial entrepreneur who holds five degrees from MIT: B.S. in Electrical Engineering, B.S. in Physics, M.S. in Electrical Engineering, an Engineer’s Degree, and a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering. He earned the David Adler Memorial Thesis Prize and the Morris Joseph Levin Award, recognizing his groundbreaking work in engineering and systems design. John was the CTO and later CEO of Nanoramic Laboratories, where he led the company to raise $44M+ in capital and developed cutting-edge battery and nanotechnology solutions. With 15+ years of experience at the frontier of hardware-software integration and AI systems, John brings a rare blend of research rigor and venture-scale execution. He now advises FairwAI on tech architecture, compliance logic, and academic research integration across MIT and international institutions.\n\nDr. Niousha Roshani – Social Systems Strategist\n\nRole: Co-leads FairwAI’s strategy, focusing on culturally responsive AI, equity frameworks, and global engagement.\n\nBio: Dr. Niousha Roshani is a leading voice in the intersection of AI, social justice, and public interest technology. She is a former Fellow at the Berkman Klein Center at Harvard University and co-founder of the Center for Democracy Development and Rule of Law at Stanford University. With a background spanning the UN system, Latin American human rights movements, and Stanford’s impact tech community, Niousha brings a transnational lens to algorithmic fairness and ethical design. Her expertise ensures FairwAI builds tools that not only detect discrimination—but empower communities and institutions to address it systemically. Based in Brazil, she anchors our Global South partnerships and pilots. Brazil is the last country in the western hemisphere to abolish slavery.\n\nDr. Ryan Chin – Strategic Advisor, Urban Tech & Mobility Systems\n\nRole: Ryan advises FairwAI on systems architecture, urban integration, and commercial strategy. He brings expertise in AI-driven mobility, sensor networks, and resilient infrastructure to inform how FairwAI scales across physical environments like hotels, hospitals, and cities.\n\nBio:\n\nDr. Ryan Chin is a globally recognized expert in smart cities, urban mobility, and sustainable design systems. He co-founded Optimus Ride, a leading autonomous vehicle company spun out of MIT, where he served as CEO and led the development of self-driving tech for campuses, cities, and business districts. Prior to that, Ryan was Managing Director of the City Science Initiative at the MIT Media Lab, where he pioneered AI-integrated mobility systems and urban computing platforms.\n\nRyan holds a Ph.D. and two Master\'s degrees from MIT in Media Arts and Sciences and Architecture. A serial entrepreneur and systems thinker, Ryan has advised Fortune 100 companies, U.S. government agencies, and international city governments on emerging technologies, sustainability, and mobility innovation. He is a frequent keynote speaker at Davos, Smart City Expo, and the UN.\n\nAt FairwAI, Ryan supports us with building out our advisory team and the integration of computer vision, IoT, and AI fairness protocols into real-world infrastructure, ensuring our platform is adaptable, sensor-compatible, and aligned with the future of ethical urban technology.\n\nMike Rinella – Government Affairs, Financial Strategy\n\nRole: Shapes FairwAI’s public policy strategy, unions to get ivolved, government, and compliance market integration.\n\nBio: Mike Rinella brings decades of experience in public finance, state governance, and strategic planning. He served as a senior advisor to two Governors of New York, including Governor Mario Cuomo, where he worked on economic development, energy regulation, and state-level policy reform. He was also Director of Strategic Planning at SolarFi, helping guide federal partnerships and compliance infrastructure for renewable energy deployments. A graduate of Harvard Kennedy School (’86), Mike is instrumental in crafting FairwAI’s pathways to adoption by Attorneys General, state legislatures, and procurement agencies. He also helps navigate our positioning with foundation-aligned capital like PRIs and MRIs.\n\nCarson Smuts – IoT & Hardware Integration Advisor (MIT Media Lab)\n\nRole: Advises on spatial sensing, IoT systems, and architecture for real-world monitoring.\n\nBio: Carson Smuts is a Senior Research Scientist at the MIT Media Lab’s City Science Group, where he has spent over a decade developing sensor platforms, digital twins, and hardware systems that interact with real-world environments. He co-created the CityScope urban simulation platform and led the design of MIT’s Environmental Sensing Infrastructure, a foundational piece of the lab’s smart city research. Trained as an architect at Columbia University, Carson transitioned into full-stack engineering with a passion for embedding fairness into built environments. He guides FairwAI’s integration with CCTV, IoT sensors, and spatial computing to power real-time bias detection in travel, healthcare, and hiring.\n\nDr. Taj Ahmad Eldridge – Strategic Advisor, Capital & Climate Justice\n\nRole: Taj advises FairwAI on capital formation, social impact investment strategy, and ESG-aligned growth. He brings deep expertise in climate finance, racial equity, and fund structuring—ensuring FairwAI’s monetization models and funding pathways align with both mission and market.\n\nBio:\n\nTaj Ahmad Eldridge is a leading voice in climate justice investing and equitable capital innovation. A former Senior Director of Investment at the Los Angeles Cleantech Incubator (LACI), Taj has helped deploy hundreds of millions of dollars toward sustainable technologies and underrepresented founders. He is currently Managing Partner at Include Ventures, where he builds investment vehicles that close wealth gaps and accelerate climate solutions—particularly in communities historically excluded from capital access.\n\nWith 20+ years of experience in banking, venture capital, and fund management, Taj has advised funds and institutions including the Ford Foundation, MacArthur Foundation, Elemental Excelerator, and Capria Ventures. He is also a Senior Advisor to Jobs for the Future (JFF) and a board member of multiple national investment networks and ESG platforms.\n\nTaj’s unique strength lies in combining climate policy, community wealth-building, and financial engineering to drive systems-level impact. As an advisor to FairwAI, he supports efforts to build revenue models rooted in risk mitigation, government accountability, and regulatory tech—while helping ensure capital raised aligns with the venture’s vision of equity-first compliance.\n\nLegal partners:\n\nBaker Botts and Lowenstein Sandler\n\nThe Role\n\nWe’re seeking a sharp, curious, and mission-aligned Data Analyst Intern to support our core technical work in bias detection. You’ll help uncover patterns of discrimination in real-world datasets—from hospitality reviews to consumer feedback across industries.\n\nThis internship is ideal for students or early-career professionals interested in data science, AI fairness, and social impact analytics.\n\nWhat You’ll Work On\n\nAnalyze public review data\n\nDetect racial, gender, or cultural bias in language, ratings, and location trends\n\nSupport the development of whats going on for hospitality brands\n\nCollaborate on prototyping data dashboards and explainability features\n\nDocument findings with clarity and ethical nuance\n\nWhat You Bring\n• Experience with Python (especially pandas, basic scraping, or NLP) Computer vision would be a bonus\n• Comfort working with messy/unstructured datasets\n• Strong communication skills (verbal or written — Loom optional)\n• Passion for justice, fairness, or the intersection of AI and society\n\nBonus: Experience in data storytelling, visualization, or social science research\n\nWhat You’ll Gain\n• Real-world experience at the intersection of data science and ethics\n• Direct mentorship from advisors at MIT and top-tier tech/policy institutions\n• Portfolio-ready projects tackling algorithmic discrimination\n• Flexible, remote-first work with global scope\n\nNote: Selected applicants will be invited to complete a short technical screening challenge before moving forward.\n\nWe are currently operating in stealth with key global partners.\n\nPay attention:\n\nWe’re excited to see how you think. If you choose to use AI tools to help structure or brainstorm, that’s fine — but we’re not looking for polished fluff or regurgitated answers. We’re looking for your voice, your logic, and your lens\n\nThis is an unpaid internship however you may apply for scholarships or school credit or use it for a capstone project. The goal is that once funding is available to hire the interns that perform well.\n\nTop-performing interns will be:\n\nMay be referred to graduate fellowships or full-time impact AI roles.\n\nEligible for future paid positions with FairwAI or its nonprofit arm if funding is available.\n\nSupported in publishing or presenting findings at tech and policy forums.\n\nYou will aslo receive the FairwAI Vanguard Certificate for participation. This should help you with future employment and education.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'fairwai,mit,capital,advisor,global,compliance,ai,tech,bio,ryan,fairness,dr,integration,systems,policy,infrastructure,mr,brings,urban,mr dixon,taj,partnerships,dixon,public,research'),(426,'jsearch','kCPY6Z7NX6a2CMkCAAAAAA==','GCP Data Analyst – BigQuery (Canada) – Canada – Toronto / Canada – Vancouver / Canada – Calgary','Rackspace',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/analyst-bigquery-gcp-vancouver-at-rackspace','About the Role\n\nWe’re seeking a GCP Data Analyst with deep expertise in BigQuery, strong SQL and Python skills, and a sharp analytical mindset to support both data validation initiatives and ongoing analytics work. This role is ideal for someone who can navigate large datasets, build robust queries, and identify inconsistencies with precision and insight.\n\nThe analyst will work across a variety of data workflows, from validating metrics during system migrations to supporting day-to-day data analysis and reporting needs. You’ll leverage advanced BigQuery features—such as authorized views, materialized views, UDFs, partitioning strategies, and time series analysis—to ensure data integrity and surface meaningful insights. Comfort working in Python with data frames and relevant packages is also essential, particularly for tasks involving data manipulation, anomaly detection, or prototyping workflows.\n\nA solid understanding of data engineering fundamentals and GCP infrastructure is important, as is the ability to read and interpret code in Java or Scala when collaborating with engineering teammates. Familiarity with Airflow (Composer) will help you understand orchestration logic, though this won’t be a core responsibility. Experience with BigQuery ML, anomaly detection frameworks, or Vertex AI is a plus.\n\nKey Responsibilities:-\n• Write, optimize, and execute complex SQL queries in BigQuery to validate data accuracy, identify inconsistencies, and support analytics and reporting.\n• Analyze large datasets to assess data quality, compare trends across systems, and surface anomalies or unexpected behaviors.\n• Utilize advanced BigQuery features such as authorized views, materialized views, UDFs, partitioned tables, and joins to support scalable, high-performance analysis.\n• Use Python (including data frames and relevant libraries) for exploratory analysis, data manipulation, and supporting validation workflows.\n• Support time series analysis and, where applicable, anomaly detection using SQL or Python-based approaches.\n• Assist with load/transform validation to ensure reliability and accuracy in data pipelines.\n• Collaborate with engineering teams to understand data pipelines, with basic ability to read and interpret Java or Scala code when needed.\n• Perform side-by-side comparisons of data across systems to ensure consistency during and after migrations.\n• Maintain basic familiarity with orchestration tools such as Airflow (Composer) to follow pipeline logic and collaborate effectively with engineering.\n• Work within the GCP environment, leveraging cloud tools and services to support analysis, troubleshoot issues, and navigate cloud-based workflows.\n• Clearly communicate analytical findings and data quality issues to cross-functional stakeholders to support decision-making.\n\nQualifications:-\n• Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Engineering, or a related field.\n• 5+ years of experience in data analyst or analytics engineering roles with strong BigQuery, SQL, and Python skills.\n• 5+ years of experience building and operating solutions on Google Cloud Platform (GCP).\n• Strong ability to write and optimize SQL queries to validate data, analyze trends, and detect inconsistencies.\n• Proficient in Python, including use of data frames and common analytical libraries.\n• Experience with advanced BigQuery features such as authorized views, materialized views, UDFs, partitions, and time series analysis.\n• Strong analytical skills and experience validating data across systems during migrations and ongoing operations.\n• Basic ability to read and understand Java or Scala code to support engineering collaboration.\n• Familiarity with Airflow (Cloud Composer) to interpret and trace data pipeline workflows.\n\nNice to have:-\n• Familiarity with Looker or other BI tools for metric validation and reporting support.\n• BigQuery ML and Vertex AI\n• Basic familiarity with legacy systems such as Oozie or Pig for reading existing scripts.\n\nMust have’s:-\n• Proficiency in SQL, BigQuery, and Python\n• Advanced SQL skills in BigQuery for complex data validation, anomaly detection, and trend analysis.\n• Experience comparing datasets across systems\n• Proven ability to identify and investigate data discrepancies across platforms.\n• Strong analytical intuition to sense-check metrics and flag issues that may not trigger formal alerts.\n• Ability to perform side-by-side metric and trend comparisons to confirm post-migration accuracy.\n• Skilled in root cause analysis using SQL, domain expertise, and supporting context.\n• Effective communicator who can document findings and share insights with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.\n• Familiarity with time series analysis to detect unexpected shifts, drops, or spikes in metrics.\n• Ability to follow structured validation processes while proactively identifying workflow improvements.\n\nTravel:-\n• As per business requirements\n\nThe following information is required by pay transparency legislation in the following states: CA, CO, HI, NY, and WA. This information applies only to individuals working in these states.\n\n· The anticipated starting pay range for Colorado is: $ 143,700 – $ 210,760\n\n· The anticipated starting pay range for the states of Hawaii and New York (not including NYC) is: $ 153,000 – $ 224,400\n\n· The anticipated starting pay range for California, New York City and Washington is: $ 167,400 – $ 245,520\n\nUnless already included in the posted pay range and based on eligibility, the role may include variable compensation in the form of bonus, commissions, or other discretionary payments. These discretionary payments are based on company and/or individual performance and may change at any time. Actual compensation is influenced by a wide array of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, licenses and certifications, and specific work location. Information on https://rackspace.jobs/benefits offered is here.\n\n#LI-VM1\n\nAbout Rackspace Technology\n\nWe are the multicloud solutions experts. We combine our expertise with the world’s leading technologies — across applications, data and security — to deliver end-to-end solutions. We have a proven record of advising customers based on their business challenges, designing solutions that scale, building and managing those solutions, and optimizing returns into the future. Named a best place to work, year after year according to Fortune, Forbes and Glassdoor, we attract and develop world-class talent. Join us on our mission to embrace technology, empower customers and deliver the future.\n\nMore on Rackspace Technology\n\nThough we’re all different, Rackers thrive through our connection to a central goal: to be a valued member of a winning team on an inspiring mission. We bring our whole selves to work every day. And we embrace the notion that unique perspectives fuel innovation and enable us to best serve our customers and communities around the globe. We welcome you to apply today and want you to know that we are committed to offering equal employment opportunity without regard to age, color, disability, gender reassignment or identity or expression, genetic information, marital or civil partner status, pregnancy or maternity status, military or veteran status, nationality, ethnic or national origin, race, religion or belief, sexual orientation, or any legally protected characteristic. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'bigquery,data,views,engineering,gcp,validation,analysis,anomaly detection,range,anomaly,series,pay range,series analysis,time series,pay,workflows,canada,detection,cloud,sql,airflow,authorized views,advanced bigquery,migrations,udfs'),(427,'jsearch','pPVliQhkNMgp3gPHAAAAAA==','Data Entry Analyst (Typist)   Remote','The Elite Job',NULL,'GB',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/7942/data-entry-analyst-typist-%E2%80%93-remote','Job Summary:\n\nThe Elite Job is seeking a meticulous and highly organized Data Entry Analyst (Typist) to join our dynamic team on a remote basis. In this role, you will be responsible for inputting, updating, and maintaining data across various platforms to support our operational and strategic goals. The ideal candidate will have exceptional typing skills, a keen eye for detail, and the ability to work independently while adhering to deadlines.\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n• * Accurately enter data from various sources into our databases and systems.\n• * Review and verify data for completeness and correctness, ensuring high standards of data quality.\n• * Perform routine data audits to identify and rectify inconsistencies or errors.\n• * Maintain and update data records in compliance with company policies and data protection regulations.\n• * Generate and provide reports as required to support departmental and organizational objectives.\n• * Collaborate with team members and other departments to address data-related issues and provide solutions.\n• * Manage time efficiently to handle multiple data entry tasks and meet deadlines.\n• * Assist with other administrative tasks as needed, including document preparation and file management.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications:\n• * Exceptional typing speed and accuracy with a focus on detail.\n• * Proficiency in data entry software and Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word, etc.).\n• * Strong organizational skills and ability to manage multiple tasks simultaneously.\n• * Excellent written and verbal communication skills.\n• * Ability to work independently with minimal supervision.\n• * Strong problem-solving skills and a proactive approach to identifying and addressing issues.\n• Experience:\n• * Previous experience in a data entry or administrative role is preferred.\n• * Familiarity with data management systems and software.\n• * Experience working remotely and managing time effectively in a virtual environment.\n• Working Hours:\n• * This is a full-time remote position.\n• * Standard working hours are Monday to Friday, 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM (local time of the employee), with flexibility based on project needs.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:\n• * Knowledge of data entry best practices and data management techniques.\n• * Ability to handle sensitive information with confidentiality and integrity.\n• * Strong analytical skills with attention to detail and accuracy.\n• * Capacity to adapt to new technologies and tools as needed.\n• * Effective interpersonal skills to communicate with team members and other stakeholders.\n• Benefits:\n• * Competitive salary and performance-based bonuses.\n• * Flexible remote working arrangements.\n• * Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance plans.\n• * Retirement savings plan with company match.\n• * Paid time off and holidays.\n• * Professional development opportunities and career growth potential.\n• * Access to a supportive and collaborative team environment.\n• Why Join Us:\n\nAt The Elite Job, we pride ourselves on creating a positive and inclusive work environment where employees are valued and encouraged to excel. As a Data Entry Analyst (Typist) with us, you will have the opportunity to work remotely while being part of a forward-thinking company that values innovation and integrity. Join us to be a part of a team dedicated to excellence and growth.\n\nHow to Apply:\n\nInterested candidates should submit their resume and a cover letter outlining their relevant experience and skills to us. Please include Data Entry Analyst (Typist) � Remote Application in the subject line. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','data entry,data,entry,entry analyst,analyst typist,typist,skills,time,tasks,exceptional typing,typing,administrative,typist remote,remote,team members,needed,handle,data various,team,exceptional,software,members,ability,working,management'),(428,'jsearch','sDFC9T-uuO9wlbl1AAAAAA==','Data Analytics Intern (Remote)','The Elite Job',NULL,'NG',0,'https://www.theelitejob.com/job/3911/data-analytics-intern-remote','At The Elite Job, we recognize the invaluable role that data plays in driving strategic decisions. As a Data Analytics Intern, you will have the opportunity to contribute to our data-driven culture, working remotely with a team of industry experts and professionals. This internship is designed for individuals passionate about data analytics, eager to gain hands-on experience in a dynamic and forward-thinking organization.\n\nResponsibilities:\n• * Collaborate with cross-functional teams to gather and analyze data requirements.\n• * Assist in the development and implementation of data analytics strategies.\n• * Contribute to the design and maintenance of data models and databases.\n• * Generate actionable insights through data interpretation and visualization.\n• * Support in the identification of trends and patterns to inform business decisions.\n• Required Skills:\n• * Proficient in data analysis tools such as [mention specific tools/software].\n• * Solid understanding of statistical concepts and data modeling techniques.\n• * Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills.\n• * Strong communication skills to convey complex findings in a clear and concise manner.\n• * Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a remote setting.\n• * Eagerness to learn and adapt to new technologies and methodologies.\n• Qualifications:\n• * Pursuing a degree in Printing or equivalent practical experience.\n• * Previous exposure to data analytics through coursework or projects.\n• * Familiarity with MS Office.\n• How to Apply:\n\nIf you are a passionate individual ready to embark on a journey in the dynamic field of data analytics, we invite you to apply for the Data Analytics Intern position at The Elite Job. Please submit your resume, a cover letter detailing your interest and relevant experience, and any relevant project portfolios to us.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','data,data analytics,analytics,analytics intern,intern,passionate,contribute,elite job,dynamic,elite,skills,individual ready,invite apply,decisions required,invite,professionals internship,decisions data,practical experience,practical,office apply,opportunity contribute,qualifications pursuing,databases generate,data plays,internship designed'),(429,'jsearch','Avu8L-tkfI-GObfnAAAAAA==','Remote AI Data Analyst: Insights, Dashboards & AI','PulseMediaNL',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/info_technology/5082636462/e/','Position: Remote AI Data Analyst: Insights, Dashboards & AI Support\nPulse\n\nMedia\n\nNL is looking for a detail-oriented AI Data Analyst to support data-driven decisions within a remote team. The role involves analyzing large datasets, translating data into actionable insights, and collaborating with various teams on AI initiatives. Candidates should have 2-4 years of relevant experience, proficiency in tools like SQL and Python, and strong communication skills. Join a collaborative team focused on innovation and flexibility while contributing to impactful AI projects.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'ai,ai data,insights dashboards,dashboards ai,analyst insights,remote ai,data,remote,data analyst,insights,insights collaborating,decisions remote,impactful ai,focused innovation,flexibility contributing,collaborating various,proficiency tools,initiatives candidates,python strong,contributing impactful,join collaborative,like sql,involves analyzing,projects 18808,datasets translating'),(430,'jsearch','kWMNORTEKsvXsEQFAAAAAA==','Business Excellence - Reports Analyst','Sagility (Jamaica) Limited',NULL,'JM',0,'https://sagility.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/Sagility/job/Business-Excellence---Reports-Analyst_REQ-024423','Sagility combines industry-leading technology and transformation-driven BPM services with decades of healthcare domain expertise to help clients draw closer to their members. The company optimizes the entire member/patient experience through service offerings for clinical, case management, member engagement, provider solutions, payment integrity, claims cost containment, and analytics. Sagility has more than 25,000 employees across 5 countries. Job title: Business Excellence - Reports Analyst Job Description: JOB DESCRIPTION Reports Analyst is responsible in ensuring that all routine reports are sent based on timelines, obtain pertinent data from all relevant departments, and compile and sanitize the information before proceeding to data analysis. Is responsible to collect and analyze the data, help drive critical business decisions by designing reports, analyzing metrics, study trends and data patterns and communicate the findings and provide recommendation to Operations, Quality and Training Team DATA MANAGEMENT • Collaborate with cross-functional teams to understand business needs and requirements for reporting and analysis • Collect data by partnering with WFM, Training and Operations • Ensure that the data are sanitized before proceeding to analysis. Develop and implement data quality checks to ensure accuracy and consistency of data • Develop, design and maintain dashboard in an easy-to-comprehend format • Create and maintain reports and dashboards to track key performance indicators (KPIs) and identify trends and patterns • Identify opportunities for process improvement and automation to increase the efficiency and effectiveness of reporting • Stay up-to-date with industry trends and best practices in reporting and analytics REPORTING • Interpret data and provide recommendation for business decisions. Communicate findings and insights to stakeholders through presentations and written reports • Circulate routine reports on timely basis without missed ESSENTIAL SKILLS • Analytical and problem-solving skills • Present data and articulate self well • Consistently demonstrate sound judgment • Rapidly get to the root cause of issues • Design appropriate analysis to support the team in implementing analysis • Provide effective communication and feedback to staff • Consistently demonstrate sound judgment • BPO experience is an advantage The above statements are intended to indicate the general nature and level of work being performed by employees within this classification. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required of employees assigned to this job. Employees in this job may perform other duties as assigned. Location: Kingston, MJS Industrial ParkJamaica Sagility combines industry-leading technology and transformation-driven BPM services with decades of healthcare domain expertise to help clients draw closer to their members. The company optimizes the entire member/patient experience through service offerings for clinical, case management, member engagement, provider solutions, payment integrity, claims cost containment, and analytics. Sagility has more than 25,000 employees across 5 countries. Already keen? Discover your next role with Sagility, a great place to work.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'sagility,reports,employees,data,member,reports analyst,reporting,job,analysis,sagility combines,sagility 25,experience service,job description,excellence reports,routine reports,entire member,help clients,entire,services decades,engagement provider,service offerings,proceeding,optimizes entire,optimizes,employees countries'),(431,'jsearch','Y0K93M8uK_4eRtcUAAAAAA==','Hiring Fresher Data Analyst Trainee','The Elite Job',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/9128/hiring-fresher-data-analyst-trainee','Job Summary\n\nThe Elite Job is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Fresher Data Analyst Trainee to join our dynamic team. In this entry-level position, you will gain hands-on experience in data analysis, interpretation, and visualization while supporting various departments in making data-driven decisions. You will play a crucial role in helping the company harness the power of data to drive strategic initiatives and enhance operational efficiency.\nKey Responsibilities\n• * Assist in collecting, processing, and analyzing large datasets from various sources.\n• * Develop and maintain reports and dashboards to visualize key performance indicators (KPIs).\n• * Collaborate with team members to identify data trends, patterns, and anomalies.\n• * Support data cleaning and transformation processes to ensure data integrity and accuracy.\n• * Participate in team meetings to present findings and contribute to data-driven discussions.\n• * Assist in creating documentation and presentations for stakeholder communications.\n• * Stay updated with industry trends and tools to enhance data analysis capabilities.\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• * Bachelors degree in Data Science, Mathematics, Statistics, Computer Science, or a related field.\n• * Basic knowledge of data analysis tools such as Excel, SQL, or Python.\n• * Familiarity with data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI) is a plus.\n• * Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with attention to detail.\n• * Excellent communication skills, both verbal and written.\n• * Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment.\n• * A proactive attitude and willingness to learn.\n• Experience\n• * This is an entry-level position; no prior experience is required.\n• * Internships or academic projects related to data analysis are a plus.\n• Working Hours\n• * Full-time position: 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM, Monday to Friday.\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• * Strong numerical and analytical aptitude.\n• * Basic understanding of statistics and data analysis principles.\n• * Ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines.\n• * Adaptability and openness to learning new tools and technologies.\n• * Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.\n• Benefits\n• * Competitive salary and performance-based incentives.\n• * Comprehensive training and mentorship program.\n• * Opportunities for career growth and advancement within the company.\n• * Health and wellness benefits.\n• * Paid time off and holidays.\n• * A collaborative and supportive work environment.\n• Why Join The Elite Job?\n\nAt The Elite Job, we believe in investing in our employees and fostering a culture of continuous learning and development. As a Fresher Data Analyst Trainee, you will have the opportunity to work alongside experienced professionals, gain valuable insights into the data analytics field, and contribute to impactful projects. Join us to kickstart your career in data analysis and make a difference in a fast-paced, innovative environment.\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are passionate about data and eager to begin your career in analytics, we would love to hear from you! Please submit your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest in the position to us.',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','data,analyst trainee,fresher,fresher data,data analysis,trainee,analysis,job,level position,enhance,career,elite job,elite,skills,position,00,entry level,skills attention,tools,team,contribute,basic,gain,learning,join'),(432,'jsearch','evj54yLqWySWWkcQAAAAAA==','Data Analyst; Entry​/Junior','Gestionamos.col',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/info_technology/5080584067/e/','Position: Data Analyst (Entry / Junior）\n\nRole Description\n\nThis is a full-time hybrid role for an Entry/Junior Data Analyst based in Singapore River, with opportunities for partial remote work. The Data Analyst will be responsible for analyzing and interpreting data, creating reports, supporting data-driven decision-making processes, and identifying trends and patterns. The role also involves data modeling, preparing visual representations, and collaborating with teams to improve workflows and insights.\nQualifications\n• Strong analytical skills and proficiency in data analytics\n• Foundational knowledge of statistics and capability in data modeling\n• Clear and effective communication skills, both verbal and written, to present complex data in an understandable manner\n• Familiarity with data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI) and basic coding knowledge (e.g., Python, SQL) is a plus\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Data Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or a related field\n• Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a hybrid work environment\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'data,entry junior,junior,analyst entry,entry,hybrid,data analyst,data modeling,analyst,modeling,statistics,work,preparing visual,data creating,interpreting data,based singapore,partial remote,data understandable,plus bachelor,partial,capability data,knowledge python,modeling preparing,position data,opportunities partial'),(433,'jsearch','nCzdhKeNgmMQDF-uAAAAAA==','[Remote] Senior Data Analyst (SQL. Power BI)','Jobs via Dice',NULL,NULL,0,'https://fresherjobss.com/job/remote-senior-data-analyst-sql-power-bi/','Jobs via Dice is seeking an experienced and results-driven Senior Data Analyst to join our remote analytics team. In this role, you will play a critical part in transforming complex datasets into meaningful insights that support strategic business decisions. You will work closely with leadership, product, operations, and engineering teams to design scalable reporting solutions and advanced dashboards.\n\nThis position is ideal for a highly analytical professional with strong SQL expertise, deep experience in Power BI, and the ability to communicate insights clearly to both technical and non-technical stakeholders—all while working in a fully remote environment.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Analyze large and complex datasets to identify trends, patterns, and business opportunities.\n• Design, develop, and maintain interactive dashboards and reports using Power BI.\n• Write optimized SQL queries to extract, transform, and validate data from multiple data sources.\n• Partner with stakeholders to understand business requirements and translate them into analytical solutions.\n• Define, track, and monitor key performance indicators (KPIs) across departments.\n• Ensure data accuracy, consistency, and integrity across reporting systems.\n• Automate reporting processes to improve efficiency and scalability.\n• Present findings, insights, and recommendations to senior management in a clear and actionable manner.\n• Support data governance, documentation, and best practices for analytics workflows.\n• Mentor junior analysts and contribute to building a strong analytics culture.\n\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n• Bachelor’s degree in Data Analytics, Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Business, or a related field.\n• Advanced proficiency in SQL for querying and managing large datasets.\n• Strong hands-on experience with Power BI, including DAX, data modeling, and dashboard design.\n• Solid understanding of data warehousing concepts and relational databases.\n• Experience working with multiple data sources (cloud databases, APIs, flat files, etc.).\n• Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills.\n• Excellent communication and presentation abilities.\n• Ability to work independently in a remote environment and manage multiple priorities.\n\nExperience\n• 5+ years of professional experience in data analysis, business intelligence, or analytics roles.\n• Proven experience delivering insights that influence business strategy and decision-making.\n• Prior experience working in a remote or distributed team environment is a plus.\n\nWorking Hours\n• Full-time, remote position\n• Standard business hours aligned with team and stakeholder needs\n• Flexible scheduling within agreed-upon time zones\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• Strong knowledge of data visualization best practices and storytelling with data.\n• Ability to translate complex data into simple, actionable insights.\n• High attention to detail with a commitment to data accuracy and quality.\n• Strong organizational and time-management skills.\n• Ability to collaborate effectively across cross-functional teams.\n• Continuous learner with a passion for analytics tools and emerging technologies.\n\nBenefits\n• Competitive salary based on experience and market standards.\n• Fully remote work environment with flexible scheduling.\n• Comprehensive health, wellness, and insurance benefits.\n• Paid time off, holidays, and wellness days.\n• Professional development and upskilling opportunities.\n• Supportive and inclusive work culture.\n• Opportunity to work on impactful, data-driven projects.\n\nWhy Join Jobs via Dice\n\nAt Jobs via Dice, we connect top talent with meaningful opportunities while embracing innovation, flexibility, and growth. Joining our team means working in a collaborative, forward-thinking environment where your insights directly influence business outcomes. As a Senior Data Analyst, you’ll have the autonomy, tools, and support to make a real impact—without compromising work-life balance.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates should apply through the Jobs via Dice platform by submitting an updated resume highlighting relevant experience in SQL and Power BI. Qualified candidates will be contacted for further steps in the hiring process.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'HOUR',NULL,'data,dice,jobs dice,senior,senior data,business,experience,remote,jobs,analytics,power bi,power,insights,bi,strong,environment,work,design,influence business,fully,scheduling,sql power,experience power,fully remote,flexible scheduling'),(434,'jsearch','dxZu1iiCP-M_U3waAAAAAA==','Entry Level business analyst jobs for freshers','Progressive Technology',NULL,'PH',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/14959/entry-level-business-analyst-jobs-for-freshers','Job Summary\n\nProgressive Technology is seeking enthusiastic and detail-oriented recent graduates to join our growing team as Entry-Level Business Analysts. This role is an ideal opportunity for freshers passionate about business processes, data analysis, and digital transformation. As an Entry-Level Business Analyst, you will work alongside seasoned professionals to analyze business needs, recommend solutions, and support project implementation that enhances efficiency and decision-making across the organization.\nKey Responsibilities\n• *\n\nAssist in gathering and documenting business requirements through meetings, interviews, and workshops\n• *\n\nAnalyze business processes and identify areas for improvement\n• *\n\nSupport the creation of functional specifications and reports\n• *\n\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams including IT, project managers, and stakeholders\n• *\n\nAssist in developing and testing business solutions or systems\n• *\n\nCreate process flow diagrams, use case documents, and data analysis reports\n• *\n\nMonitor project performance and support tracking of KPIs and metrics\n• *\n\nSupport in quality assurance and user acceptance testing (UAT)\n• *\n\nHelp with preparing presentations and status reports for stakeholders\n• Required Skills and Qualifications\n• *\n\nBachelors degree in Business Administration, Information Technology, Economics, Statistics, or a related field\n• *\n\nStrong analytical and problem-solving skills\n• *\n\nBasic understanding of business processes and data analysis\n• *\n\nProficiency in Microsoft Excel, Word, and PowerPoint\n• *\n\nFamiliarity with tools like Tableau, Power BI, or SQL is a plus\n• *\n\nExcellent written and verbal communication skills\n• *\n\nEagerness to learn and contribute in a fast-paced environment\n• Experience\n• *\n\nExperience Level: No prior professional experience required\n• *\n\nInternships or academic projects related to business analysis, data, or systems are an added advantage\n• Working Hours\n• *\n\nFull-time: 40 hours per week\n• *\n\nFlexible working hours with core collaboration time between 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM (Monday to Friday)\n• *\n\nRemote and hybrid roles are subject to manager and project requirements\n• Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• *\n\nStrong attention to detail and organizational skills\n• *\n\nAbility to work independently and within a team\n• *\n\nAbility to interpret and analyze complex data sets\n• *\n\nStrong aptitude for learning new tools, techniques, and technologies\n• *\n\nWillingness to receive and act upon feedback for continuous improvement\n• *\n\nCustomer-centric mindset and a proactive approach to problem-solving\n• Benefits\n• *\n\nCompetitive entry-level salary\n• *\n\nFlexible working arrangements (remote/hybrid options)\n• *\n\nOn-the-job training and continuous learning opportunities\n• *\n\nMentorship programs with experienced Business Analysts\n• *\n\nPerformance-based growth and promotion opportunities\n• *\n\nPaid time off, sick leaves, and public holidays\n• *\n\nHealth insurance and wellness benefits\n• *\n\nAccess to internal certification programs and workshops\n• Why Join Progressive Technology?\n\nAt Progressive Technology, we believe in investing in talent from day one. We foster a culture of innovation, learning, and collaboration. You will be empowered to take initiative, work on impactful projects, and grow your career in a nurturing environment. If you are looking to launch your business analysis career with an organization that values diversity, forward-thinking, and development—this is the place for you.\nHow to Apply\n\nTo apply for this position, please follow these steps:\n• Prepare an updated resume highlighting your education and any relevant projects or internships.\n• *\n\nWrite a brief cover letter explaining why you are interested in the role.\n• *\n\nSubmit your application through our careers page\n• *\n\nAlternatively, email your resume and cover letter to us with the subject line: Application for Entry-Level Business Analyst\n•',NULL,20.00,30.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','business,level business,entry level,level,entry,progressive technology,progressive,business analyst,business processes,project,technology,analysis,learning,testing,workshops,analyze business,remote hybrid,business analysis,business analysts,freshers,hybrid,processes data,skills,internships,flexible working'),(435,'jsearch','M0dStWNrpUCtP5spAAAAAA==','Software Developer (Montego Bay)','Segoso',NULL,'JM',0,'https://www.caribbeanjobs.com/Software-Developer-Montego-Bay-Job-231435.aspx','Description We are seeking to hire a Software Developer to join our team! As a Software, you will be asked to build high-performing web applications using numerous Angular software best practices. You will also be responsible for developing Net Core APIs. The ideal candidate should have extensive experience in the Microsoft stack, with a strong emphasis on .NET Core, Web API development, and various other technologies. Experience in proficiency in working with teams across multiple time zones. Requirements Required: · Bachelor’s/Master’s degree in computer science or Information technology · At least 3-5+ years of experience in coding using .NET C# Preferred: · A keen eye for detail · Strong communication skills · Knowledge of Front End and Back End Development · Experience with hosting in Azure · Any professional certifications · Azure DevOps Technical Skills and Relevant Technologies: · Experience in .NET Core · Proficiency in using Rest APIs · SQL servers o Stored Procedures o Tables o Triggers o ..etc. o Angular 18 or Above o Typescript o UI/UX Design Soft Skills and Cultural Fit: · Strong organizational skills and the ability to prioritize tasks effectively · Willingness to learn and adapt to new processes and technologies · Positive attitude and a proactive approach to problem-solving · Ability to work independently as well as part of a team',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'net,core,net core,experience,technologies experience,software,skills,technologies,using,apis,strong,web,software developer,developer,ability,end,angular,bachelor master,working teams,ability prioritize,attitude proactive,azure professional,attitude,approach problem,cultural fit'),(436,'jsearch','52wJKwMBnVveakCUAAAAAA==','Experienced Software Developer','ItelBPO','Montego Bay','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/experienced-software-developer/','About Company\n\nItelBPO is a leading global BPO (Business Process Outsourcing) provider, specializing in customer experience management, technical support, and back-office solutions. With a robust presence across the Caribbean, Latin America, and North America, ItelBPO is renowned for its innovative approach to customer interaction, leveraging cutting-edge technology and a people-first culture to deliver exceptional results. We believe that a great customer experience starts with a great employee experience. Our vibrant, dynamic, and diverse teams are at the heart of our success, driving growth and pushing boundaries in a rapidly evolving industry. As we continue our rapid expansion, our commitment to technological excellence and digital transformation is paramount, making our IT department a critical pillar of our global operations. Joining ItelBPO means becoming part of a forward-thinking organization where your contributions directly impact global client success and internal operational efficiency.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a seasoned Software Developer eager to make a significant impact within a rapidly growing global organization? ItelBPO is seeking a highly skilled and experienced Software Developer to join our innovative technology team in Ironshore, Montego Bay. This is an exciting opportunity for a professional with a proven track record in designing, developing, and deploying robust software solutions that power our complex BPO operations and enhance client services.\n\nIn this role, you will be instrumental in the full software development lifecycle, from conceptualization and design to testing, deployment, and ongoing maintenance. You will work closely with cross-functional teams, including operations, product management, and other IT specialists, to understand business requirements and translate them into scalable and efficient software applications. We are looking for someone who thrives in a collaborative environment, possesses strong problem-solving abilities, and is passionate about delivering high-quality code. Your work will directly contribute to streamlining our processes, enhancing our customer interaction platforms, and building bespoke tools that give ItelBPO a competitive edge. If you\'re ready to tackle challenging projects, mentor junior developers, and drive technological innovation, we encourage you to apply and help us shape the future of BPO.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain robust and scalable software solutions primarily using .NET (C#) and related technologies.\n• Collaborate with business analysts, product owners, and other stakeholders to gather and refine software requirements.\n• Write clean, efficient, well-documented, and high-quality code adhering to best practices and coding standards.\n• Participate in code reviews, providing constructive feedback and ensuring code quality, security, and performance.\n• Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing software to improve functionality, performance, and user experience.\n• Develop and maintain APIs and integrations with third-party systems, ensuring seamless data flow and communication.\n• Contribute to the continuous improvement of software development processes, tools, and methodologies.\n• Mentor junior developers, sharing knowledge and fostering a collaborative learning environment.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.\n• 4+ years of professional experience in software development.\n• Proficiency in C# and the .NET framework (.NET Core, .NET 6/7/8).\n• Strong experience with ASP.NET MVC/Web API for building web applications and services.\n• Solid understanding of relational databases, particularly SQL Server, including T-SQL and database design.\n• Experience with front-end technologies such as JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, and modern JavaScript frameworks (e.g., React, Angular, Vue.js).\n• Familiarity with version control systems, especially Git.\n• Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced environment.\n• Excellent problem-solving, analytical, and communication skills.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Master\'s degree in a relevant technical field.\n• Experience with cloud platforms (Azure, AWS, GCP) and services.\n• Knowledge of DevOps practices and tools (CI/CD pipelines, Docker, Kubernetes).\n• Familiarity with Agile development methodologies (Scrum, Kanban).\n• Experience with message queuing systems (e.g., RabbitMQ, Kafka).\n• Certifications in Microsoft technologies (e.g., Azure Developer Associate).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance bonuses.\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and vision insurance.\n• Paid time off and public holidays.\n• Opportunities for professional development and continuous learning.\n• Dynamic and inclusive work environment.\n• Modern office facilities in a convenient location.\n• Employee wellness programs and team-building activities.\n• Career advancement opportunities within a rapidly expanding global company.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to submit their application online by clicking on the link below. Please ensure your resume highlights your relevant experience and technical skills. Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted for an interview.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'software,itelbpo,global,experience,customer,net,bpo,rapidly,code,developer,operations,development,experienced software,interaction,great,quality code,customer experience,customer interaction,america,environment,building,software developer,work,technological,maintain'),(440,'jsearch','lodcXHZ0uzvyxzECAAAAAA==','Junior Cloud Technician – Flexible Hours','Sagicor Group Jamaica Limited','Kingston','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/junior-cloud-technician-flexible-hours/','About Company\n\nSagicor Group Jamaica Limited is a leading financial services conglomerate with a rich history of over 180 years, operating in Jamaica and across the Caribbean. We are committed to improving the lives of people in the communities we serve through innovative financial solutions in life and health insurance, annuities, pensions, and banking. At Sagicor, we believe in fostering a dynamic and supportive work environment where our team members can thrive and contribute to our mission of delivering excellence. We are constantly evolving our technology infrastructure to stay ahead, embracing cloud solutions to enhance efficiency, security, and scalability for our vast array of services. Joining Sagicor means becoming part of a team dedicated to innovation, integrity, and client success.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a technology enthusiast with a foundational understanding of cloud concepts, eager to launch your career in a dynamic, forward-thinking environment? Sagicor Group Jamaica is seeking a highly motivated and detail-oriented Junior Cloud Technician to join our growing IT infrastructure team. This exciting full-time role, offering flexible hours to help you balance work and life commitments, is based in our Kingston operations and provides a unique opportunity to gain hands-on experience with cutting-edge cloud technologies.\n\nAs a Junior Cloud Technician, you will play a crucial role in supporting the day-to-day operations and maintenance of our cloud-based systems and services. You will work closely with senior cloud engineers and architects, assisting with deployment, monitoring, troubleshooting, and optimization tasks. This position is ideal for individuals who are passionate about learning, possess strong problem-solving skills, and are ready to contribute to the stability and performance of our critical financial systems. You\'ll be exposed to various cloud platforms and tools, providing a fantastic learning ground for your professional development. We value initiative and a proactive approach to continuous improvement. If you\'re looking for an entry point into the lucrative and fast-evolving world of cloud technology with a company that truly invests in its people, this is the opportunity for you.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist in the deployment, configuration, and maintenance of cloud infrastructure components on platforms such as AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.\n• Monitor cloud system performance, availability, and security using various monitoring tools and respond to alerts in a timely manner.\n• Perform routine system checks, backups, and recovery procedures to ensure data integrity and business continuity.\n• Provide first-level support for cloud-related incidents and service requests, escalating complex issues to senior technicians.\n• Collaborate with other IT teams to resolve technical issues and implement new cloud solutions.\n• Document cloud configurations, operational procedures, and troubleshooting steps.\n• Participate in ongoing training and professional development to stay current with cloud technologies and best practices.\n• Contribute to the continuous improvement of cloud operations and services.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Basic understanding of cloud computing concepts (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS)\n• Familiarity with operating systems (Windows Server, Linux)\n• Strong problem-solving and analytical skills\n• Excellent communication and teamwork abilities\n• Ability to work independently and manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment\n• Foundational knowledge of networking principles (TCP/IP, DNS, firewalls)\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Associate\'s or Bachelor\'s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related field\n• Entry-level cloud certification (e.g., AWS Cloud Practitioner, Azure Fundamentals)\n• Experience with scripting languages (e.g., PowerShell, Python, Bash)\n• Exposure to virtualization technologies (e.g., VMware, Hyper-V)\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Competitive salary and performance-based incentives\n• Comprehensive health, dental, and life insurance benefits\n• Flexible working hours to promote work-life balance\n• Opportunities for professional growth and career advancement\n• Access to training programs and industry certifications\n• Generous paid time off and holiday schedule\n• Modern and collaborative work environment\n• Employee wellness programs\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates are invited to apply directly through our official careers portal. Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and cover letter. Ensure your application clearly highlights your relevant skills and experience. We thank all applicants for their interest; however, only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'cloud,sagicor,based,technician,junior cloud,infrastructure,cloud technician,life,work,financial,flexible,jamaica,hours,operations,flexible hours,foundational,concepts,monitoring,sagicor group,understanding cloud,troubleshooting,maintenance cloud,day,entry,cloud technologies'),(441,'jsearch','Q70VI0NJF8gbHcu2AAAAAA==','Software QA Specialist – Part-Time','National Commercial Bank Jamaica Limited (NCB)','Kingston','JM',0,'https://career.zycto.com/jobs/software-qa-specialist-part-time/','About Company\n\nNational Commercial Bank Jamaica Limited (NCB) is the largest financial group in Jamaica, offering a comprehensive suite of banking, wealth management, and insurance services. With a rich history spanning over 180 years, NCB is deeply committed to leveraging technology to innovate and enhance the financial experience for its customers. We pride ourselves on fostering a culture of excellence, continuous learning, and digital transformation. At NCB, we believe in empowering our employees to make a significant impact, contributing to our mission of putting our customers first and driving the economic growth of Jamaica. Join our dynamic team and be a part of an organization that is shaping the future of finance in the Caribbean.\n\nJob Description\n\nAre you a meticulous problem-solver with a passion for ensuring software quality? Do you thrive in a fast-paced environment where precision is paramount? National Commercial Bank Jamaica Limited (NCB) is seeking a dedicated and detail-oriented Part-Time Software QA Specialist to join our innovative technology team. In this pivotal role, you will play a crucial part in maintaining the high standards of our digital banking platforms and internal systems, directly impacting the seamless financial experiences of millions of Jamaicans.\n\nAs a Part-Time Software QA Specialist, you will be instrumental in the end-to-end quality assurance lifecycle. You will meticulously review requirements, design robust test cases, execute comprehensive testing, and identify and document defects with clarity and precision. This role offers the flexibility of part-time engagement, making it ideal for individuals looking to balance professional growth with other commitments, while still making a significant contribution to a leading financial institution. You will collaborate closely with developers, product owners, and other QA team members to ensure our software solutions are not only functional but also reliable, secure, and user-friendly. Your keen eye for detail and commitment to quality will directly contribute to safeguarding the integrity of our financial services and enhancing our customers\' trust. We are looking for someone who is proactive, analytical, and eager to contribute their expertise to a team that values innovation and excellence. If you are ready to apply your QA skills to complex, high-impact projects within the financial technology sector, we encourage you to apply and help us build the future of banking.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Develop, execute, and maintain comprehensive test plans and test cases for new and existing software features.\n• Perform various types of testing, including functional, regression, integration, and user acceptance testing (UAT).\n• Identify, document, and track software defects and inconsistencies using defect tracking systems, ensuring clear and concise reporting.\n• Collaborate closely with development teams to ensure defects are understood, prioritized, and resolved efficiently.\n• Participate in requirements and design reviews, providing constructive feedback from a quality assurance perspective.\n• Contribute to the continuous improvement of QA processes and methodologies.\n• Assist in the creation and maintenance of automated test scripts, where applicable.\n• Provide regular updates on testing progress and defect status to team leads and project managers.\n\nRequired Skills\n• Minimum of 18 months of experience in software quality assurance or testing.\n• Proficiency in creating detailed test plans, test cases, and test reports.\n• Strong understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) and QA methodologies.\n• Experience with defect tracking tools (e.g., JIRA, Azure DevOps).\n• Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills with a keen eye for detail.\n• Strong communication skills, both written and verbal, for effective collaboration.\n• Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a dynamic environment.\n• Basic knowledge of SQL for database validation.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n• Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field.\n• ISTQB certification or equivalent.\n• Experience with test automation frameworks and tools (e.g., Selenium, Cypress).\n• Familiarity with Agile/Scrum development methodologies.\n• Prior experience in the financial services industry.\n• Experience testing mobile applications (iOS/Android).\n\nPerks & Benefits\n• Flexible part-time working hours.\n• Opportunity to work with cutting-edge financial technology.\n• Professional development and learning opportunities.\n• Collaborative and supportive team environment.\n• Impactful work contributing to Jamaica\'s leading financial institution.\n• Employee wellness programs.\n• Access to a comprehensive internal training library.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nIf you are a driven and detail-oriented individual eager to contribute your QA expertise to a leading financial institution, we invite you to apply! Please click on the application link below to submit your resume and cover letter. We look forward to reviewing your application.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'MONTH',NULL,'financial,qa,test,software,ncb,jamaica,testing,test cases,software qa,cases,customers,defects,quality assurance,specialist,institution,qa specialist,defect,financial institution,assurance,team,quality,experience,banking,leading financial,technology'),(444,'jsearch','oLRRUF-iV-OyA6PUAAAAAA==','Junior API Integration Specialist (Hotel Systems)','Hotel Res Bot',NULL,NULL,0,'https://landing.jobs/at/hotel-res-bot/junior-api-integration-specialist-hotel-systems','Description\n\nWe are looking for a Junior API Integration Specialist (Hotel Systems) to join Hotel Res Bot, a fully remote SaaS company building automation for hotel communications and operations.\n\nThis is not a standard API role. Hotel technology is highly fragmented, and external systems (especially PMS platforms, booking engines, and payment providers) are often inconsistent, poorly documented, and designed with assumptions about hotel operations that are not always clearly specified.\n\nA core part of this job is working in that reality: understanding how hotel systems actually behave in production, not just how they are described in documentation. This often requires testing, experimentation, and reverse-engineering system behaviour when APIs are incomplete or contradictory.\n\nYou will work directly with hotel APIs and use Postman to test, validate, and debug real-world workflows such as reservations, availability (ARI), rate plans, restrictions, and group blocks.\n\nYour output will be structured, implementation-ready tasks for engineers.\n\nResponsibilities:\n• Analyse and interpret hotel system API documentation (often incomplete, inconsistent, or misleading in practice)\n• Work hands-on with PMS, booking engine, and payment provider APIs in real-world conditions\n• Build, test, and debug API requests using Postman\n• Reverse-engineer API behaviour when documentation does not match real system behaviour\n• Validate hotel workflows through APIs, including:\n• Reservations (create, modify, cancel, including edge cases and vendor-specific behaviour)\n• Availability, Rates & Inventory (ARI logic across inconsistent implementations)\n• Room types and rate plans (often not standardized across systems)\n• Restrictions (min/max stay, closed dates, allotments)\n• Group blocks and allocation logic (frequently under-documented)\n• Guest, company, and travel agency profiles\n• Guarantee, payment, and cancellation rules (varies significantly by system)\n• Identify gaps between hotel operational reality and API documentation\n• Work with logs and API responses to debug integration issues\n• Translate findings into clear, structured GitLab tasks for developers\n• Collaborate with engineering on unclear or ambiguous integration behaviour\n• Occasionally support troubleshooting calls with PMS providers when documentation is insufficient\n• Maintain internal documentation of real-world system behaviour vs documented behaviour\n\nRequirements\n\nWe are looking for someone with hotel operations experience, structured thinking, and the ability to work confidently in ambiguous technical environments.\n\nYou do not need to be a developer, but you must be comfortable working in systems where:\n• documentation is incomplete or incorrect\n• behaviour differs between vendors\n• and the only reliable truth is what the system does when tested\n\nRequired experience:\n• At least 1 year in hotel operations (front desk, reservations, revenue, or systems roles)\n• Strong understanding of PMS systems and real hotel workflows\n• Practical exposure to reservations, rates, availability, and booking logic\n• Experience with at least one hotel system (PMS or similar)\n\nNice to have\n• Basic understanding of REST APIs (request/response, endpoints, payloads)\n• Ability to construct and modify JSON (and/or XML) payloads\n• Understanding of authentication methods (API keys, OAuth, tokens)\n• Comfort working with systems that do not behave exactly as documented\n• Independent problem-solving in ambiguous technical environments\n• Strong written communication in English\n• Ability to work in a scrappy, fast-moving environment without full specifications\n\nPerks\n\nFully remote position (work from anywhere) Flexible working hours with high autonomy Direct access to engineering and product teams (no heavy hierarchy) High ownership over your work and integrations Strong learning environment in both hotel systems and API integrations Opportunity to grow into:\n• Technical Product roles\n• Advanced integration specialist roles\n• Backend development (Go) if desired\n\nCompany-provided equipment (laptop and necessary tools) Startup environment with fast decision-making and low bureaucracy\n\nRemote details\n\nIf you schedule an appointment, you should attend it, but otherwise you define your working hours.\n\nSkills\n\nRequired: Postman, Analytical Skills, Hotel Operation / Systems, API, JSON, XML, OAuth, Communication Skills',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'YEAR',NULL,'hotel,behaviour,systems,api,pms,documentation,work,hotel systems,operations,documented,reservations,real,integration,working,apis,debug,structured,ambiguous,roles,specialist,workflows,booking,incomplete,payment,hotel operations'),(445,'jsearch','b_YLysY9_hoTetnwAAAAAA==','Backend Intern – Java, Spring Boot, APIs','CodeCrafters',NULL,'US',0,'https://theelitejob.com/us/job/1144/Backend-Intern-%E2%80%93-Java%2C-Spring-Boot%2C-APIs','Job Summary\n\nCodeCrafters is seeking a motivated Backend Intern with a strong interest in backend development using Java, Spring Boot, and APIs. This internship offers an excellent opportunity to gain real-world experience in designing, developing, and optimizing backend systems that support modern applications. You will work closely with our engineering team to build scalable solutions, ensure system reliability, and learn industry best practices while contributing to meaningful projects.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n• Assist in designing, developing, and maintaining backend services using Java and Spring Boot.\n• Support in creating and integrating RESTful APIs for various applications.\n• Collaborate with frontend developers to ensure seamless integration between systems.\n• Participate in code reviews, testing, and debugging to ensure high-quality software delivery.\n• Research, document, and suggest improvements for system performance and scalability.\n• Work with databases (SQL/NoSQL) to manage and optimize data storage solutions.\n• Contribute to technical documentation for future reference and project handovers.\n\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n• Strong understanding of Core Java and Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts.\n• Familiarity with Spring Boot framework and API development.\n• Basic knowledge of RESTful web services and HTTP protocols.\n• Understanding of databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL, or MongoDB).\n• Problem-solving mindset with eagerness to learn and adapt.\n• Good communication skills and ability to work in a collaborative environment.\n\nExperience\n• No prior professional experience required; final-year students or recent graduates in Computer Science, IT, or related fields are encouraged to apply.\n• Prior academic projects, internships, or personal coding projects using Java/Spring Boot will be considered an advantage.\n\nWorking Hours\n• Flexible working hours with an expectation of 20–30 hours per week for part-time interns or full-time 40 hours per week depending on availability.\n• Remote/Hybrid opportunities may be available based on project requirements.\n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n• Knowledge of version control systems (Git/GitHub).\n• Ability to quickly grasp new technologies and frameworks.\n• Strong debugging and analytical skills.\n• Team-oriented with a proactive learning approach.\n• Attention to detail and ability to follow clean coding practices.\n\nBenefits\n• Hands-on exposure to enterprise-level backend systems.\n• Mentorship from experienced software engineers.\n• Opportunity to work on live projects impacting real clients.\n• Internship certificate upon successful completion.\n• Potential for pre-placement offer (PPO) based on performance.\n• Flexible work environment encouraging innovation and growth.\n\nWhy Join CodeCrafters?\n\nAt CodeCrafters, we believe in nurturing young talent and providing them with the tools to excel in the tech industry. As an intern, you’ll gain practical experience, collaborate with industry experts, and enhance your technical skills in a supportive and innovative workplace. This is more than just an internship—it’s the first step towards building a successful career in backend development.\n\nHow to Apply\n\nInterested candidates can apply by sending their updated resume and a brief cover letter highlighting relevant skills or projects to us. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for a technical assessment and virtual interview.',NULL,10.00,20.00,NULL,'HOUR','details','boot,spring boot,spring,java,java spring,projects,skills,backend,work,codecrafters,using java,ensure,internship,industry,intern,experience,systems,hours,apply,knowledge,backend systems,oriented,week,software,gain'),(455,'jsearch','a04qa5_we8T1vmogAAAAAA==','Middle Backend Developer (Node.js) – Wrocław, Kielce, Szczecin or remotely','MasterBorn',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/wroclaw-szczecin-backend-developer-kielce-at-masterborn-up2draftex-19032025103416','We are looking for skillful Backend Developers to join one of our teams working with US clients – referrals from the high-end American IT market.\n\nOur tech stack is built around React, React Native, Nodejs, TypeScript and Python. We are working with startups in their early stages (MVPs), which makes the job full of diverse and exciting challenges while crafting innovative solutions.\n\nEnjoy the flexibility of working within the Polish time zone and collaborate with clients from diverse industries such as FinTech, SportsTech, MedTech, and many others.\n\nSalary: PLN 10.000 – 16.000 + VAT (B2B)\n• Required skills: 2+ years of commercial experience in Nodejs, SQL and NoSQL DBs, knowledge of JS frameworks (e.g Express.js, NestJS), experience in TypeScript, SOLID and KISS, knowledge about design and architecture patterns, knows how and why Docker and GitHub Actions works, basic usage of AWS services, English B2, Polish C1\n• Offer: B2B/UZL, paid days off, 100% remote (or hybrid/onsite – as you prefer), Polish time zone, flexible hours, full-time position, long-term contract, Scrum Teams\n• Perks and Benefits: +6 000 PLN / year training budget, budget for health insurance and sports, Mentoring Program, individual Career Path, and more\n• Tools you’ll use: Apple MacBook Pro, Slack, GSuite, GitHub, Jira, Coda, Miro\n\nYour future tasks and duties:\n• Writing readable and easy to maintain JS/TS code with OOP flavor\n• Writing documentation for delivered code\n• Code review of other developers in the team\n• Direct involvement with design and modification of basic DB structures\n• Propose improvements and share proactive ideas/solutions with the team to enhance the team’s work processes\n• Share insights with the team to diagnose issues and focus on solutions\n• Actively participate in project discussions\n• Listen to the client’s needs and, after consulting the team, suggest solutions\n• Support less experienced team members\n\nAbout you – Tech skills & Experience:\n• 2+ years of commercial experience in Nodejs\n• Good experience with at least one Nodejs backend framework (e.g. Express.js, NestJS, Fastify, etc) – you know most of its basic APIs/features, worked on at least 1-2 projects involving such technologies\n• Good understanding of JS (at least ES 2018), its pros and flaws, used Classes and follows recent additions/functionalities, loves to get deeper with knowledge and know-how\n• Potentially worked with NoSQL databases and/or in-memory databases and utilized them as a data store\n• Worked with SQL databases (integration-wise and as a basic design skill) with ORM or query builder tool (ie. Prisma, Knex)\n\nAbout you – Soft Skills:\n• English level B2 – to cooperate with American clients\n• Polish level C1 – to communicate easily within the team\n• Open-minded to new challenges (e.g. different frameworks)\n• Understand the significance of MVP and prioritize the pursuit of excellence and high-quality outcomes, even amid tight project timelines.\n• Communicate with the team to efficiently translate business complexities (user stories/tasks) into solutions (results/estimations)\n• Staying on top with trends/news, sharing them, teaching others and aiming for best quality solutions\n• Strong problem-solving abilities to diagnose issues, suggest solutions, and make decisions based on project requirements.\n\nNice to have:\n• Worked in Agile/Scrum on a daily basis consisting of people with similar skills and monitoring code quality on a daily basis\n• Basic experience with AWS – used some services in specific cases\n• Basic experience with Docker – know how to prepare and debug the environment and connect things up to work locally\n• Worked in the very beginning of the product development/creation stage\n• Understand the significance of MVP and aim to deliver top-notch results, even amid tight project timelines\n\nMeaningful projects, top-notch experts and value-driven workplace\n\nSound good?\n\nApply now!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'basic,worked,solutions,polish,team,000,experience nodejs,know,nodejs,experience,project,good,js,code,clients,diagnose issues,time zone,significance mvp,significance,pln,basic experience,used,c1,suggest solutions,suggest'),(456,'jsearch','JnXMFKCw7-2qJE9jAAAAAA==','Full-Stack Developer – Node.JS – Biassono, Italy / Milan, Italy','Docebo',NULL,NULL,0,'https://up2staff.com/developer-node-biassono-italy-milan-at-docebo','The Full-Stack Developer at Docebo plays a key role in developing and maintaining our SaaS solutions for learning management systems and corporate training. This mid-level role involves working with a variety of technologies, including Nodejs, Angular, and AWS CDK, to build scalable, stable, and high-performing applications. The developer will collaborate closely with System and Platform Engineers and Software Architects to ensure smooth integration, continuous delivery, and infrastructure scalability. The successful candidate will be joining the Learning Analytics team, contributing to the development of Docebo Learn Data. In addition to managing the pipelines functional to the development of the Product Roadmap, a critical focus will be on reducing technical debt and supporting rapid development cycles.\n\nReports to: Analytics Engineering Manager\n\nLocation: Hybrid Biassono/Milan, Italy\n\nTo help our teams work together effectively, this role requires you to be located in Italy.\n• Develop and maintain: Build and enhance full-stack applications using Nodejs, TypeScript, JavaScript, Angular 14+, HTML, and CSS to ensure robust and scalable software solutions\n• Implement best practices: Utilise trunk-based development, continuous integration, and continuous delivery methodologies to streamline development processes and minimise downtime\n• Collaborate with DevOps: Work closely with DevOps to ensure seamless deployment, monitoring, and scaling of serverless and containerised applications\n• Address technical debt: Proactively identify and refactor legacy code or outdated frameworks to reduce technical debt, improving overall codebase quality\n• Optimise infrastructure: Leverage Infrastructure as Code (IaC) frameworks, particularly AWS CDK, to automate and optimise infrastructure deployment and management\n• Ensure scalability: Contribute to the design and implementation of scalable solutions that can handle increased user loads and expand as the business grows\n• Contribute to architecture discussions: Engage with software architects to influence and guide the architectural direction, ensuring alignment with best practices and future-proofing the platform\n\nEducation and Experience:\n• 3-5 years of experience in full-stack development, with a strong focus on SaaS applications\n• Proficient in Nodejs, TypeScript, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, and Angular 14+ frameworks\n• Experience with Trunk-Based Development, Continuous Integration, and Continuous Delivery practices\n• Practical knowledge of serverless and containerised applications, with a focus on AWS services\n• Experience with Infrastructure as Code frameworks, particularly AWS CDK\n• Familiarity with DevOps practices and collaboration with DevOps teams\n• Strong problem-solving skills, with the ability to address technical debt and optimise for scalability\n\nTo excel in this role, the Full-Stack Developer should possess a solid understanding of both front-end and back-end technologies, with particular expertise in Angular, Nodejs, and AWS. They should be adept at working in fast-paced environments with evolving priorities, maintaining a focus on delivering high-quality, scalable code. Collaboration and communication are key, as this role involves working closely with cross-functional teams. A successful candidate will be proactive in addressing technical debt and improving the codebase, all while ensuring that the infrastructure is stable and scalable.\n\nDocebo is focused on nurturing a culture of inclusivity that ensures every employee feels valued and respected. We are dedicated to helping every team member succeed and bring their unique perspectives to the team!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'infrastructure,technical debt,debt,italy,development,angular,scalable,continuous,applications,integration continuous,continuous delivery,optimise,aws cdk,closely,cdk,docebo,nodejs,technical,role,stack,aws,focus,devops,ensure,stack developer'),(457,'jsearch','Xzfz2y_KdnWGCVQsAAAAAA==','Remote Senior Full-Stack Engineer — React, Node, GraphQL','FullRemoteTalent',NULL,NULL,0,'https://www.learn4good.com/jobs/online_remote/software_development/5065897368/e/','Full Remote Talent is seeking a full-stack developer in Dubai to design and ship internal platforms and a new CRM dashboard. You will collaborate with the design and product teams while owning features from inception to completion. The ideal candidate has over 5 years of experience with React and Node.js, Graph\n\nQL knowledge, and a foundational understanding of AWS services. The company supports remote work within EMEA and offers a learning budget for career growth.\n#J-18808-Ljbffr',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'react node,remote,stack,react,product teams,features inception,engineer react,senior stack,emea offers,ql knowledge,supports remote,supports,ql,teams owning,learning budget,emea,dubai design,node graphql,company supports,developer dubai,design ship,talent seeking,remote talent,remote senior,design product'),(458,'jsearch','iyugPJ8N3xaTHTsnAAAAAA==','Node.js Backend Architect â€“ Microservices & Cloud Ops','GradeBuzz',NULL,'IN',0,'https://theelitejob.com/job/20222/node.js-backend-architect-ae%E2%80%9C-microservices-cloud-ops','Job Summary\n\r\n\n\r\nGradeBuzz is seeking a highly skilled and visionary Node.js Backend Architect to lead the design, development, and optimization of scalable backend systems. This role focuses on building robust microservices architectures and managing cloud-native operations. The ideal candidate will play a critical role in shaping the technical direction of our platform, ensuring high performance, reliability, and security across all backend services.\n\r\n\n\r\nKey Responsibilities\n\r\n\n\r\nArchitect and design scalable, high-performance backend systems using Node.js and microservices architecture.\n\r\n\n\r\nLead the migration of monolithic systems to microservices-based distributed systems.\n\r\n\n\r\nDevelop and maintain RESTful and GraphQL APIs.\n\r\n\n\r\nOversee cloud infrastructure (AWS/Azure/GCP) and ensure optimal deployment strategies.\n\r\n\n\r\nImplement CI/CD pipelines for efficient and automated deployments.\n\r\n\n\r\nEnsure system reliability, security, and compliance with industry standards.\n\r\n\n\r\nCollaborate with frontend teams, DevOps engineers, and product managers.\n\r\n\n\r\nOptimize database performance (SQL/NoSQL) and ensure data integrity.\n\r\n\n\r\nMonitor system performance and troubleshoot production issues.\n\r\n\n\r\nMentor and guide backend developers, promoting best coding practices.\n\r\n\n\r\nRequired Skills and Qualifications\n\r\n\n\r\nStrong expertise in Node.js and backend development frameworks (Express.js, NestJS).\n\r\n\n\r\nProven experience in microservices architecture and distributed systems.\n\r\n\n\r\nHands-on experience with cloud platforms like AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud.\n\r\n\n\r\nProficiency in containerization tools such as Docker and Kubernetes.\n\r\n\n\r\nExperience with CI/CD tools (Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI).\n\r\n\n\r\nStrong knowledge of databases like MongoDB, PostgreSQL, or MySQL.\n\r\n\n\r\nUnderstanding of API security, authentication (OAuth, JWT), and encryption.\n\r\n\n\r\nFamiliarity with message brokers (Kafka, RabbitMQ).\n\r\n\n\r\nExcellent problem-solving and system design skills.\n\r\n\n\r\nExperience\n\r\n\n\r\n8+ years of experience in backend development.\n\r\n\n\r\n3+ years of experience in architectural roles or technical leadership.\n\r\n\n\r\nProven track record of building scalable, production-grade systems.\n\r\n\n\r\nExperience working in Agile/Scrum environments.\n\r\n\n\r\nWorking Hours\n\r\n\n\r\nFull-time position\n\r\n\n\r\nFlexible working hours with overlap for team collaboration\n\r\n\n\r\nRemote or hybrid work model (depending on project requirements)\n\r\n\n\r\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n\r\n\n\r\nStrong analytical and critical thinking abilities\n\r\n\n\r\nAbility to design fault-tolerant and highly available systems\n\r\n\n\r\nExcellent communication and leadership skills\n\r\n\n\r\nDeep understanding of system scalability and performance tuning\n\r\n\n\r\nAbility to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment\n\r\n\n\r\nStrong documentation and technical writing skills\n\r\n\n\r\nBenefits\n\r\n\n\r\nCompetitive salary package\n\r\n\n\r\nRemote work flexibility\n\r\n\n\r\nHealth insurance and wellness programs\n\r\n\n\r\nPaid time off and holidays\n\r\n\n\r\nLearning and development opportunities\n\r\n\n\r\nAccess to latest tools and technologies\n\r\n\n\r\nPerformance-based bonuses\n\r\n\n\r\nWhy Join GradeBuzz?\n\r\n\n\r\nAt GradeBuzz, you will be part of an innovative and fast-growing organization that values technology excellence and continuous learning. You will have the opportunity to work on cutting-edge projects, influence architectural decisions, and collaborate with top talent. We foster a culture of ownership, creativity, and growth, empowering you to make a real impact.\n\r\n\n\r\nHow to Apply\n\r\n\n\r\nInterested candidates can apply by submitting their updated resume along with a portfolio of relevant projects. Include a brief cover letter highlighting your experience in backend architecture, microservices, and cloud operations. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for technical discussions and interviews.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'backend,cloud,microservices,systems,performance,experience,security,gradebuzz,js backend,architect,ci,technical,tools,skills,js,reliability security,operations,aws azure,leadership,backend architect,backend systems,microservices cloud,scalable,ensure,design');
